msgid "Django version 0.95 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte leagan 0.95 Django"

msgid "Welcome to the Django 0.95 release."
msgstr "Fáilte go dtí an eisiúint Django 0.95."

msgid ""
"This represents a significant advance in Django development since the 0.91 "
"release in January 2006. The details of every change in this release would "
"be too extensive to list in full, but a summary is presented below."
msgstr ""
"Is é seo dul chun cinn suntasach i bhforbairt Django ó scaoileadh 0.91 i mí "
"Eanáir 2006. Bheadh sonraí gach athrú sa eisiúint seo ró-fhairsing le "
"liostáil go hiomlán, ach cuirtear achoimre i láthair thíos."

msgid "Suitability and API stability"
msgstr "Oiriúnacht agus cobhsaíocht API"

msgid ""
"This release is intended to provide a stable reference point for developers "
"wanting to work on production-level applications that use Django."
msgstr ""
"Tá an scaoileadh seo beartaithe chun pointe tagartha cobhsaí a sholáthar "
"d'fhorbróirí ar mian leo oibriú ar fheidhmchláir ar leibhéal táirgthe a "
"úsáideann Django."

msgid ""
"However, it's not the 1.0 release, and we'll be introducing further changes "
"before 1.0. For a clear look at which areas of the framework will change "
"(and which ones will *not* change) before 1.0, see the ``api-stability.txt`` "
"file, which lives in the docs/ directory of the distribution."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, ní hé an scaoileadh 1.0 é, agus beimid ag tabhairt isteach "
"athruithe breise roimh 1.0. Le haghaidh léargas soiléir ar cé na réimsí den "
"chreat a athróidh (agus cé na cinn* nach n-athróidh) roimh 1.0, féach an "
"comhad `api-stability.txt`, a chónaíonn i ndocs/ eolaire an dáileacháin."

msgid ""
"You may have a need to use some of the features that are marked as \"subject "
"to API change\" in that document, but that's OK with us as long as it's OK "
"with you, and as long as you understand APIs may change in the future."
msgstr ""
"B'fhéidir go mbeidh gá duit cuid de na gnéithe atá marcáilte mar “faoi réir "
"athraithe API” a úsáid sa doiciméad sin, ach tá sé sin ceart go leor linn "
"fad is atá sé ceart go leor leat, agus chomh fada agus a thuigeann tú "
"d'fhéadfadh APIs athrú amach anseo."

msgid ""
"Fortunately, most of Django's core APIs won't be changing before version "
"1.0. There likely won't be as big of a change between 0.95 and 1.0 versions "
"as there was between 0.91 and 0.95."
msgstr ""
"Ar ámharaí an tsaoil, ní bheidh an chuid is mó de chroí-APIs Django ag athrú "
"roimh leagan 1.0. Is dócha nach mbeidh athrú chomh mór idir leaganacha 0.95 "
"agus 1.0 agus a bhí idir 0.91 agus 0.95."

msgid "Changes and new features"
msgstr "Athruithe agus gnéithe nua"

msgid ""
"The major changes in this release (for developers currently using the 0.91 "
"release) are a result of merging the 'magic-removal' branch of development. "
"This branch removed a number of constraints in the way Django code had to be "
"written that were a consequence of decisions made in the early days of "
"Django, prior to its open-source release. It's now possible to write more "
"natural, Pythonic code that works as expected, and there's less \"black "
"magic\" happening behind the scenes."
msgstr ""
"Tá na hathruithe móra sa scaoileadh seo (d'fhorbróirí a úsáideann an "
"scaoileadh 0.91 faoi láthair) mar thoradh ar an mbrainse forbartha 'bainte "
"draíochta' a chumasc. Bhain an brainse seo roinnt srianta ar an mbealach a "
"bhí le cód Django a scríobh a bhí mar thoradh ar chinntí a rinneadh i "
"laethanta tosaigh Django, sula scaoileadh é foinse oscailte. Is féidir anois "
"cód Pythonic níos nádúrtha a scríobh a oibríonn mar a bhíothas ag súil leis, "
"agus tá níos lú “draíochta dubh” ag tarlú taobh thiar de na radhairc."

msgid ""
"Aside from that, another main theme of this release is a dramatic increase "
"in usability. We've made countless improvements in error messages, "
"documentation, etc., to improve developers' quality of life."
msgstr ""
"Seachas sin, is é príomhthéama eile den scaoileadh seo méadú suntasach ar "
"inúsáidteacht. Tá feabhsuithe gan áireamh déanta againn ar theachtaireachtaí "
"earráide, doiciméadú, srl., Chun cáilíocht beatha forbróirí a fheabhsú."

msgid "The new features and changes introduced in 0.95 include:"
msgstr "I measc na ngnéithe agus na hathruithe nua a tugadh isteach i 0.95 tá:"

msgid ""
"Django now uses a more consistent and natural filtering interface for "
"retrieving objects from the database."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann Django comhéadan scagtha níos comhsheasmhach agus nádúrtha anois "
"chun rudaí a aisghabháil ón mbunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"User-defined models, functions and constants now appear in the module "
"namespace they were defined in. (Previously everything was magically "
"transferred to the ``django.models.*`` namespace.)"
msgstr ""
"Tá samhlacha, feidhmeanna agus comhshainneacha sainmhínithe ag an úsáideoir "
"le feiceáil anois sa spás ainmneacha modúl a sainmhíníodh (Roimhe seo "
"aistríodh gach rud go draíochta chuig an spás ainmneacha "
"``django.models.*``.)"

msgid ""
"Some optional applications, such as the FlatPage, Sites and Redirects apps, "
"have been decoupled and moved into ``django.contrib``. If you don't want to "
"use these applications, you no longer have to install their database tables."
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh roinnt feidhmchlár roghnacha, mar shampla na feidhmchláir FlatPage, "
"Sites and Restricts, dícheangailte agus aistrithe go ``django.contrib ``. "
"Mura dteastaíonn uait na feidhmchláir seo a úsáid, ní gá duit a dtáblaí "
"bunachar sonraí a shuiteáil a thuilleadh."

msgid "Django now has support for managing database transactions."
msgstr ""
"Tá tacaíocht ag Django anois chun idirbhearta bunachar sonraí a bhainistiú."

msgid ""
"We've added the ability to write custom authentication and authorization "
"backends for authenticating users against alternate systems, such as LDAP."
msgstr ""
"Chuireamar an cumas cúltaca saincheaptha fíordheimhnithe agus údaraithe a "
"scríobh chun úsáideoirí a fhíordheimhniú i gcoinne córais mhalartacha, mar "
"LDAP."

msgid ""
"We've made it easier to add custom table-level functions to models, through "
"a new \"Manager\" API."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé déanta againn níos éasca feidhmeanna saincheaptha ar leibhéal tábla a "
"chur le samhlacha, trí API “Bainisteoir” nua."

msgid ""
"It's now possible to use Django without a database. This simply means that "
"the framework no longer requires you to have a working database set up just "
"to serve dynamic pages. In other words, you can just use URLconfs/views on "
"their own. Previously, the framework required that a database be configured, "
"regardless of whether you actually used it."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir anois Django a úsáid gan bunachar sonraí. Ciallaíonn sé seo ach "
"nach n-éilíonn an creat a thuilleadh go mbeidh bunachar sonraí oibre ar bun "
"agat ach chun leathanaigh dinimiciúla a sheirbheáil. Is é sin le rá, ní "
"féidir leat ach URLConfs/tuairimí a úsáid leo féin. Roimhe seo, theastaigh "
"an creat go ndéanfaí bunachar sonraí a chumrú, is cuma an n-úsáid tú é i "
"ndáiríre."

msgid ""
"It's now more explicit and natural to override ``save()`` and ``delete()`` "
"methods on models, rather than needing to hook into the ``pre_save()`` and "
"``post_save()`` method hooks."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé níos soiléire agus níos nádúrtha anois modhanna ``save () ``agus "
"``delete ()`` a shárú ar mhúnlaí, seachas gá a chur isteach sna crúcaí modh "
"``pre_save () ``agus ``post_save ()``."

msgid ""
"Individual pieces of the framework now can be configured without requiring "
"the setting of an environment variable. This permits use of, for example, "
"the Django templating system inside other applications."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir píosaí aonair den chreat a chumrú anois gan athróg comhshaoil a "
"shocrú a bheith ag teastáil. Ceadaíonn sé seo úsáid, mar shampla, an córas "
"teimpléireachta Django taobh istigh d'fheidhmchláir eile."

msgid ""
"More and more parts of the framework have been internationalized, as we've "
"expanded internationalization (i18n) support. The Django codebase, including "
"code and templates, has now been translated, at least in part, into 31 "
"languages. From Arabic to Chinese to Hungarian to Welsh, it is now possible "
"to use Django's admin site in your native language."
msgstr ""
"Tá níos mó agus níos mó codanna den chreat idirnáisiúnta, de réir mar a "
"leathnaíomar tacaíocht idirnáisiúnaithe (i18n). Tá an cód Django, lena n-"
"áirítear cód agus teimpléid, aistrithe anois, go páirteach ar a laghad, go "
"31 teanga. Ó Araibis go Sínis go Ungáiris go Breataine, is féidir anois "
"suíomh riaracháin Django a úsáid i do theanga dhúchais."

msgid ""
"The number of changes required to port from 0.91-compatible code to the 0.95 "
"code base are significant in some cases. However, they are, for the most "
"part, reasonably routine and only need to be done once. A list of the "
"necessary changes is described in the `Removing The Magic`_ wiki page. There "
"is also an easy checklist_ for reference when undertaking the porting "
"operation."
msgstr ""
"Tá líon na n-athruithe a theastaíonn don chalafort ó chód comhoiriúnach 0.91 "
"go bonn cód 0.95 suntasach i gcásanna áirithe. Mar sin féin, is gnáthamh "
"réasúnta iad, den chuid is mó agus ní gá iad a dhéanamh ach uair amháin. Tá "
"cur síos ar liosta de na hathruithe riachtanacha sa leathanach wiki "
"`Removing The Magic `_. Tá seicliosta éasca ann freisin le haghaidh tagartha "
"agus an oibríocht iompair á ndéanamh agat."

msgid "Problem reports and getting help"
msgstr "Tuairiscí fadhbanna agus cúnamh"

msgid ""
"Need help resolving a problem with Django? The documentation in the "
"distribution is also available :doc:`online </index>` at the `Django "
"website`_. The :doc:`FAQ </faq/index>` document is especially recommended, "
"as it contains a number of issues that come up time and again."
msgstr ""
"Teastaíonn cabhair uait fadhb a réiteach le Django? Tá an doiciméadú sa "
"dáileadh ar fáil freisin: doc: `ar líne `ag `suíomh gréasáin Dj</index> ango "
"`_. Moltar an doiciméad:doc: `FAQ` go </faq/index> háirithe, toisc go bhfuil "
"roinnt saincheisteanna ann a thagann chun cinn arís agus arís eile."

msgid ""
"For more personalized help, the `django-users`_ mailing list is a very "
"active list, with more than 2,000 subscribers who can help you solve any "
"sort of Django problem. We recommend you search the archives first, though, "
"because many common questions appear with some regularity, and any "
"particular problem may already have been answered."
msgstr ""
"Le cabhair níos pearsanta a fháil, is liosta an-ghníomhach é an liosta "
"seoltaí `django-users`_, le níos mó ná 2,000 síntiúsóir ar féidir leo cabhrú "
"leat aon fhadhb Django a réiteach. Molaimid duit na cartlanna a chuardach ar "
"dtús, áfach, mar go mbíonn go leor ceisteanna coitianta le feiceáil go "
"rialta, agus seans go bhfuil aon fhadhb ar leith freagraithe cheana féin."

msgid ""
"Finally, for those who prefer the more immediate feedback offered by IRC, "
"there's a ``#django`` channel on ``irc.libera.chat`` that is regularly "
"populated by Django users and developers from around the world. Friendly "
"people are usually available at any hour of the day -- to help, or just to "
"chat."
msgstr ""
"Faoi dheireadh, dóibh siúd ar fearr leo an t-aiseolas níos láithreach a "
"thairgeann IRC, tá cainéal ``#django`` ar `irc.libera.chat`` atá daonra go "
"rialta ag úsáideoirí agus forbróirí Django ó gach cearn den domhan. De "
"ghnáth bíonn daoine cairdiúla ar fáil ag uair ar bith den lá - chun cabhrú, "
"nó díreach chun comhrá a dhéanamh."

msgid "Thanks for using Django!"
msgstr "Go raibh maith agat as Django a úsáid!"

msgid "The Django Team July 2006"
msgstr "Foireann Django Iúil 2006"

msgid "Django version 0.96 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte leagan 0.96 Django"

msgid "Welcome to Django 0.96!"
msgstr "Fáilte go dtí Django 0.96!"

msgid ""
"The primary goal for 0.96 is a cleanup and stabilization of the features "
"introduced in 0.95. There have been a few small `backwards-incompatible "
"changes`_ since 0.95, but the upgrade process should be fairly simple and "
"should not require major changes to existing applications."
msgstr ""
"Is é an príomhsprioc do 0.96 ná glanadh agus cobhsú na ngnéithe a tugadh "
"isteach i 0.95. Rinneadh cúpla athrú beag “neamh-chomhoiriúnach ar chúl” _ ó "
"0.95, ach ba chóir go mbeadh an próiseas uasghrádaithe simplí go leor agus "
"níor cheart go mbeadh athruithe móra ag teastáil ó iarratais atá ann cheana."

msgid ""
"However, we're also releasing 0.96 now because we have a set of backwards-"
"incompatible changes scheduled for the near future. Once completed, they "
"will involve some code changes for application developers, so we recommend "
"that you stick with Django 0.96 until the next official release; then you'll "
"be able to upgrade in one step instead of needing to make incremental "
"changes to keep up with the development version of Django."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, táimid ag scaoileadh 0.96 anois freisin toisc go bhfuil sraith "
"athruithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha ar chúl againn sceidealta go luath amach "
"anseo. Nuair a bheidh sé críochnaithe, beidh roinnt athruithe cód i gceist "
"acu d'fhorbróirí feidhmchláir, mar sin molaimid duit cloí le Django 0.96 go "
"dtí an chéad eisiúint oifigiúil eile; ansin beidh tú in ann uasghrádú a "
"dhéanamh i gcéim amháin in ionad go gá athruithe incréideacha a dhéanamh "
"chun coinneáil suas leis an leagan forbartha de Django."

msgid "Backwards-incompatible changes"
msgstr "Athruithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha ar ais"

msgid ""
"The following changes may require you to update your code when you switch "
"from 0.95 to 0.96:"
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh go n-éilíonn na hathruithe seo a leanas ort do chód a nuashonrú "
"nuair a aistríonn tú ó 0.95 go 0.96:"

msgid "``MySQLdb`` version requirement"
msgstr "Riachtanas leagan ``MySQLDB``"

msgid ""
"Due to a bug in older versions of the ``MySQLdb`` Python module (which "
"Django uses to connect to MySQL databases), Django's MySQL backend now "
"requires version 1.2.1p2 or higher of ``MySQLdb``, and will raise exceptions "
"if you attempt to use an older version."
msgstr ""
"Mar gheall ar fhabht i leaganacha níos sine den mhodúl Python ``MySQLDB`` (a "
"úsáideann Django chun nascadh le bunachair sonraí MySQL), teastaíonn cúltaca "
"MySQL Django leagan 1.2.1p2 nó níos airde de ``MySQLDB`` anois, agus ardóidh "
"sé eisceachtaí má dhéanann tú iarracht leagan níos sine a úsáid."

msgid ""
"If you're currently unable to upgrade your copy of ``MySQLdb`` to meet this "
"requirement, a separate, backwards-compatible backend, called \"mysql_old\", "
"has been added to Django. To use this backend, change the "
"``DATABASE_ENGINE`` setting in your Django settings file from this::"
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil tú in ann faoi láthair do chóip de `MySQLDB`` a uasghrádú chun "
"an riachtanas seo a chomhlíonadh, cuireadh cúltaca ar leithligh, "
"comhoiriúnach le cúl, ar a dtugtar “mysql_old”, le Django. Chun an cúltaca "
"seo a úsáid, athraigh an socrú ``DATABASE_ENGINE`` i do chomhad socruithe "
"Django as seo:"

msgid "to this::"
msgstr "chuige seo:"

msgid ""
"However, we strongly encourage MySQL users to upgrade to a more recent "
"version of ``MySQLdb`` as soon as possible, The \"mysql_old\" backend is "
"provided only to ease this transition, and is considered deprecated; aside "
"from any necessary security fixes, it will not be actively maintained, and "
"it will be removed in a future release of Django."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, molaimid go láidir úsáideoirí MySQL uasghrádú go leagan níos "
"déanaí de `MySQLDB`` a luaithe is féidir, Ní sholáthraítear an cúltaca "
"“mysql_old” ach chun an t-aistriú seo a mhaolú, agus meastar go bhfuil sé "
"díluaite; seachas aon socruithe slándála riachtanacha, ní chothabharfar é go "
"gníomhach, agus bainfear é i scaoileadh amach anseo de Django."

msgid ""
"Also, note that some features, like the new ``DATABASE_OPTIONS`` setting "
"(see the :doc:`databases documentation </ref/databases>` for details), are "
"only available on the \"mysql\" backend, and will not be made available for "
"\"mysql_old\"."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara freisin nach bhfuil roinnt gnéithe, cosúil leis an socrú "
"nua ``DATABASE_OPTIONS` (féach na:doc: `doiciméadú bunachair sonraí` </ref/"
"databases> le haghaidh sonraí), ar fáil ach ar an gcúltaca “mysql”, agus ní "
"chuirfear ar fáil do “mysql_old”."

msgid "Database constraint names changed"
msgstr "Athraigh ainmneacha srianta bunachar sonraí"

msgid ""
"The format of the constraint names Django generates for foreign key "
"references have changed slightly. These names are generally only used when "
"it is not possible to put the reference directly on the affected column, so "
"they are not always visible."
msgstr ""
"Tá athrú beagán tagtha ar fhormáid na n-ainmneacha srianta a ghineann Django "
"le haghaidh tagairtí eachtracha. De ghnáth ní úsáidtear na hainmneacha seo "
"ach nuair nach féidir an tagairt a chur go díreach ar an gcolún atá buailte, "
"mar sin ní bhíonn siad le feiceáil i gcónaí."

msgid ""
"The effect of this change is that running ``manage.py reset`` and similar "
"commands against an existing database may generate SQL with the new form of "
"constraint name, while the database itself contains constraints named in the "
"old form; this will cause the database server to raise an error message "
"about modifying nonexistent constraints."
msgstr ""
"Is é éifeacht an athraithe seo ná go bhféadfadh orduithe `manage.py reset`` "
"agus orduithe comhchosúla i gcoinne bunachar sonraí atá ann cheana SQL a "
"ghiniúint leis an bhfoirm nua ainm srianta, agus tá srianta ainmnithe sa "
"seanfhoirm sa bhunachar sonraí féin; cuirfidh sé seo teachtaireacht earráide "
"a ardú faoi srianta nach bhfuil ann a mhodhnú."

msgid "If you need to work around this, there are two methods available:"
msgstr "Más gá duit oibriú timpeall air seo, tá dhá mhodh ar fáil:"

msgid ""
"Redirect the output of ``manage.py`` to a file, and edit the generated SQL "
"to use the correct constraint names before executing it."
msgstr ""
"Aischur `manage.py`` a atreorú chuig comhad, agus cuir an SQL a ghintear in "
"eagar chun na hainmneacha srianta cearta a úsáid sula ndéantar é a chur i "
"bhfeidhm."

msgid ""
"Examine the output of ``manage.py sqlall`` to see the new-style constraint "
"names, and use that as a guide to rename existing constraints in your "
"database."
msgstr ""
"Scrúdaigh aschur ``manage.py sqlall`` chun na hainmneacha srianta stíl nua a "
"fheiceáil, agus bain úsáid as sin mar threoir chun srianta atá ann cheana i "
"do bhunachar sonraí a athainmniú."

msgid "Name changes in ``manage.py``"
msgstr "Athruithe ainm i `manage.py``"

msgid ""
"A few of the options to ``manage.py`` have changed with the addition of "
"fixture support:"
msgstr ""
"Tá roinnt de na roghanna chun `manage.py`` athraithe le tacaíocht daingneáin "
"a chur leis:"

msgid ""
"There are new ``dumpdata`` and ``loaddata`` commands which, as you might "
"expect, will dump and load data to/from the database. These commands can "
"operate against any of Django's supported serialization formats."
msgstr ""
"Tá orduithe nua ``dumpdata`` agus `loaddata`` a dhéanfaidh, mar a bheifeá ag "
"súil leis, sonraí a dhumpáil agus a luchtú chuig/ón mbunachar sonraí. Is "
"féidir leis na horduithe seo oibriú i gcoinne aon cheann de na formáidí "
"sraitheachaithe a fhaigheann tacaíocht ó Django."

msgid ""
"The ``sqlinitialdata`` command has been renamed to ``sqlcustom`` to "
"emphasize that ``loaddata`` should be used for data (and ``sqlcustom`` for "
"other custom SQL -- views, stored procedures, etc.)."
msgstr ""
"Athainmníodh an t-ordú `sqlinitialdata`` go `sqlcustom`` chun béim a leagan "
"ar chóir `loaddata`` a úsáid le haghaidh sonraí (agus ``sqlcustom`` le "
"haghaidh tuairimí saincheaptha eile SQL --, nósanna imeachta stóráilte, "
"srl.)."

msgid "The vestigial ``install`` command has been removed. Use ``syncdb``."
msgstr "Baineadh an t-ordú vestigial ``install``. Úsáid ``syncdb``."

msgid "Backslash escaping changed"
msgstr "Athraíodh éalú cúltaca"

msgid ""
"The Django database API now escapes backslashes given as query parameters. "
"If you have any database API code that matches backslashes, and it was "
"working before (despite the lack of escaping), you'll have to change your "
"code to \"unescape\" the slashes one level."
msgstr ""
"Éalaíonn API bunachar sonraí Django anois cúltaca a thugtar mar "
"pharaiméadair fiosrúcháin. Má tá aon chód API bunachar sonraí agat a "
"mheaitseálann le backslashes, agus go raibh sé ag obair roimhe seo (in "
"ainneoin an easpa éalaithe), beidh ort do chód a athrú chun na slashes a "
"“díéalú” leibhéal amháin."

msgid "For example, this used to work::"
msgstr "Mar shampla, úsáidtear é seo chun oibriú:"

msgid "The above is now incorrect, and should be rewritten as::"
msgstr "Tá an méid thuas mícheart anois, agus ba chóir é a athscríobh mar:"

msgid "Removed ENABLE_PSYCO setting"
msgstr "Bainte socrú ENABLE_PSYCO"

msgid ""
"The ``ENABLE_PSYCO`` setting no longer exists. If your settings file "
"includes ``ENABLE_PSYCO`` it will have no effect; to use Psyco_, we "
"recommend writing a middleware class to activate it."
msgstr ""
"Níl an socrú `ENABLE_PSYCO`` ann a thuilleadh. Má chuimsíonn do chomhad "
"socruithe ``ENABLE_PSYCO`` ní bheidh aon éifeacht aige; chun Psyco_ a úsáid, "
"molaimid rang middleware a scríobh chun é a ghníomhachtú."

msgid "What's new in 0.96?"
msgstr "Cad atá nua i 0.96?"

msgid ""
"This revision represents over a thousand source commits and over four "
"hundred bug fixes, so we can't possibly catalog all the changes. Here, we "
"describe the most notable changes in this release."
msgstr ""
"Léiríonn an t-athbhreithniú seo os cionn míle tiomantas foinse agus os cionn "
"ceithre chéad socruithe fabht, mar sin ní féidir linn na hathruithe go léir "
"a chataló Anseo, déanaimid cur síos ar na hathruithe is suntasaí sa eisiúint "
"seo."

msgid "New forms library"
msgstr "Leabharlann foirmeacha nua saor in aisce"

msgid ""
"``django.newforms`` is Django's new form-handling library. It's a "
"replacement for ``django.forms``, the old form/manipulator/validation "
"framework.  Both APIs are available in 0.96, but over the next two releases "
"we plan to switch completely to the new forms system, and deprecate and "
"remove the old system."
msgstr ""
"Is é ``django.newforms`` leabharlann láimhseála foirmeacha nua Django. Is "
"athsholáthar é do `django.forms``, an sean-chreat foirme/ionramhálaí/"
"bailíochtaithe. Tá an dá API ar fáil i 0.96, ach thar an dá eisiúint eile tá "
"sé beartaithe againn aistriú go hiomlán chuig an gcóras foirmeacha nua, agus "
"an seanchóras a dhíchur agus a bhaint."

msgid "There are three elements to this transition:"
msgstr "Tá trí ghné leis an aistriú seo:"

msgid ""
"We've copied the current ``django.forms`` to ``django.oldforms``. This "
"allows you to upgrade your code *now* rather than waiting for the backwards-"
"incompatible change and rushing to fix your code after the fact.  Just "
"change your import statements like this::"
msgstr ""
"Tá an `django.forms`` reatha cóipeáilte againn go ``django.oldforms``. "
"Ligeann sé seo duit do chód a uasghrádú a uasghrádú anois* seachas fanacht "
"leis an athrú neamh-chomhoiriúnach ar chúl agus dul i do chód a shocrú tar "
"éis na fírinne. Níl ort ach do ráitis iompórtála a athrú mar seo:"

msgid ""
"The next official release of Django will move the current "
"``django.newforms`` to ``django.forms``. This will be a backwards-"
"incompatible change, and anyone still using the old version of "
"``django.forms`` at that time will need to change their import statements as "
"described above."
msgstr ""
"Bogfaidh an chéad eisiúint oifigiúil eile de Django an ``django.newforms`` "
"reatha go ``django.forms``. Is athrú comhoiriúnach ar chúl é seo, agus beidh "
"ar aon duine atá fós ag úsáid an seanleagan de ``django.forms`` ag an am sin "
"a ráitis iompórtála a athrú mar a thuairiscítear thuas."

msgid "The next release after that will completely remove ``django.oldforms``."
msgstr ""
"Bainfidh an chéad eisiúint eile ina dhiaidh sin ``django.oldforms`` go "
"hiomlán."

msgid ""
"Although the ``newforms`` library will continue to evolve, it's ready for "
"use for most common cases. We recommend that anyone new to form handling "
"skip the old forms system and start with the new."
msgstr ""
"Cé go leanfaidh an leabharlann ``newfoirme`` ag forbairt, tá sé réidh le "
"húsáid don chuid is mó de na cásanna coitianta. Molaimid do dhuine ar bith "
"atá nua chun láimhseáil foirme an seanchóras foirmeacha a scipeáil agus tosú "
"leis an nua."

msgid ""
"For more information about ``django.newforms``, read the :doc:`newforms "
"documentation </topics/forms/index>`."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise faoi `django.newforms``, léigh an:doc: "
"`newforms documentation</topics/forms/index> `."

msgid "URLconf improvements"
msgstr "Feabhsuithe URLConf"

msgid ""
"You can now use any callable as the callback in URLconfs (previously, only "
"strings that referred to callables were allowed). This allows a much more "
"natural use of URLconfs. For example, this URLconf::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat aon ghlaoch a úsáid anois mar an glaonna aisghlaonna in "
"URLConfs (roimhe seo, ní cheadaíodh ach teaghráin a thagraíonn do ghlaonna). "
"Ligeann sé seo úsáid i bhfad níos nádúrtha de URLConfs. Mar shampla, an "
"URLConf seo:"

msgid "can now be rewritten as::"
msgstr "is féidir é a athscríobh anois mar:"

msgid ""
"One useful application of this can be seen when using decorators; this "
"change allows you to apply decorators to views *in your URLconf*. Thus, you "
"can make a generic view require login very easily::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir cur i bhfeidhm úsáideach amháin de seo a fheiceáil agus "
"maisitheoirí á úsáid agat; ligeann an t-athrú seo duit maisitheoirí a chur i "
"bhfeidhm ar thuairim* i do URLConf*. Dá bhrí sin, is féidir leat dearcadh "
"cineálach a dhéanamh logáil isteach go héasca::"

msgid ""
"Note that both syntaxes (strings and callables) are valid, and will continue "
"to be valid for the foreseeable future."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go bhfuil an dá syntax (teaghráin agus glaonna) bailí, "
"agus go leanfaidh siad bailí go dtí amach anseo."

msgid "The test framework"
msgstr "An creat tástála"

msgid ""
"Django now includes a test framework so you can start transmuting fear into "
"boredom (with apologies to Kent Beck). You can write tests based "
"on :mod:`doctest` or :mod:`unittest` and test your views with a simple test "
"client."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn Django creat tástála anois ionas gur féidir leat tosú ag athrú "
"eagla go leamh (le leithscéal le Kent Beck). Is féidir leat tástálacha a "
"scríobh bunaithe ar:mod: `doctest` nó: mod: `unittest` agus do thuairimí a "
"thástáil le cliant tástála simplí."

msgid ""
"There is also new support for \"fixtures\" -- initial data, stored in any of "
"the supported :doc:`serialization formats </topics/serialization>`, that "
"will be loaded into your database at the start of your tests. This makes "
"testing with real data much easier."
msgstr ""
"Tá tacaíocht nua ann freisin do “daingneáin” - sonraí tosaigh, a stóráiltear "
"in aon cheann de na foirmeacha sraith a thacaítear: doc:, a luchtálfar "
"isteach i </topics/serialization> do bhunachar sonraí ag tús do thástálacha. "
"Déanann sé seo tástáil le fíor-shonraí i bhfad níos éasca."

msgid ""
"See :doc:`the testing documentation </topics/testing/index>` for the full "
"details."
msgstr ""
"Féach: doc: `an doiciméadú tástála` le haghaidh na sonraí iomlá</topics/"
"testing/index> na."

msgid "Improvements to the admin interface"
msgstr "Feabhsuithe ar an gcomhéadan riaracháin"

msgid ""
"A small change, but a very nice one: dedicated views for adding and updating "
"users have been added to the admin interface, so you no longer need to worry "
"about working with hashed passwords in the admin."
msgstr ""
"Athrú beag, ach ceann an-deas: cuireadh tuairimí tiomnaithe chun úsáideoirí "
"a chur leis agus a nuashonrú leis an gcomhéadan riaracháin, mar sin ní gá "
"duit a bheith buartha a thuilleadh faoi oibriú le pasfhocail hashaithe sa "
"riarachán."

msgid "Thanks"
msgstr "Go raibh maith agat"

msgid ""
"Since 0.95, a number of people have stepped forward and taken a major new "
"role in Django's development. We'd like to thank these people for all their "
"hard work:"
msgstr ""
"Ó 0.95 ó shin, tá roinnt daoine tar éis dul ar aghaidh agus glacadh ról mór "
"nua i bhforbairt Django. Ba mhaith linn buíochas a ghabháil leis na daoine "
"seo as a gcuid oibre crua go léir:"

msgid ""
"Russell Keith-Magee and Malcolm Tredinnick for their major code "
"contributions. This release wouldn't have been possible without them."
msgstr ""
"Russell Keith-Magee agus Malcolm Tredinnick as a gcuid mór-ranníocaíochtaí "
"cód. Ní bheadh an scaoileadh seo indéanta gan iad."

msgid ""
"Our new release manager, James Bennett, for his work in getting out 0.95.1, "
"0.96, and (hopefully) future release."
msgstr ""
"Ár mbainisteoir scaoilte nua, James Bennett, as a chuid oibre maidir le "
"0.95.1, 0.96, agus (tá súil agam) scaoileadh amach anseo a fháil amach anseo."

msgid ""
"Our ticket managers Chris Beaven (aka SmileyChris), Simon Greenhill, Michael "
"Radziej, and Gary Wilson. They agreed to take on the monumental task of "
"wrangling our tickets into nicely cataloged submission. Figuring out what to "
"work on is now about a million times easier; thanks again, guys."
msgstr ""
"Ár mbainisteoirí ticéad Chris Beaven (aka SmileyChris), Simon Greenhill, "
"Michael Radziej, agus Gary Wilson. D'aontaigh siad glacadh leis an tasc "
"iontach ár dticéid a chur isteach i aighneacht chatalógaithe go deas. Tá sé "
"thart ar milliún uair níos éasca anois a fháil amach cad atá le bheith ag "
"obair air; go raibh maith agat arís, daoine."

msgid ""
"Everyone who submitted a bug report, patch or ticket comment. We can't "
"possibly thank everyone by name -- over 200 developers submitted patches "
"that went into 0.96 -- but everyone who's contributed to Django is listed "
"in :source:`AUTHORS`."
msgstr ""
"Gach duine a chuir tuarascáil fabht, paiste nó trácht ticéad isteach. Ní "
"féidir linn buíochas a ghabháil le gach duine de réir ainm - chuir os cionn "
"200 forbróirí paistí isteach a chuaigh isteach i 0.96 - ach tá gach duine a "
"chuir le Django liostaithe in:source: `AUTHORS`."

msgid "Django 1.0 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.0"

msgid "Welcome to Django 1.0!"
msgstr "Fáilte go dtí Django 1.0!"

msgid ""
"We've been looking forward to this moment for over three years, and it's "
"finally here. Django 1.0 represents the largest milestone in Django's "
"development to date: a web framework that a group of perfectionists can "
"truly be proud of."
msgstr ""
"Táimid ag tnúth leis an nóiméad seo le breis agus trí bliana, agus tá sé "
"anseo ar deireadh. Is ionann Django 1.0 an chloch mhíle is mó i bhforbairt "
"Django go dtí seo: creat gréasáin ar féidir le grúpa foirfeachtóirí a bheith "
"bródúil as."

msgid ""
"Django 1.0 represents over three years of community development as an Open "
"Source project. Django's received contributions from hundreds of developers, "
"been translated into fifty languages, and today is used by developers on "
"every continent and in every kind of job."
msgstr ""
"Léiríonn Django 1.0 breis agus trí bliana d'fhorbairt phobail mar "
"thionscadal Foinse Oscailte. Fuair Django ranníocaíochtaí ó na céadta "
"forbróirí, aistrigh siad go caoga teanga, agus inniu úsáideann forbróirí é "
"ar gach mór-roinn agus i ngach cineál poist."

msgid ""
"An interesting historical note: when Django was first released in July 2005, "
"the initial released version of Django came from an internal repository at "
"revision number 8825. Django 1.0 represents revision 8961 of our public "
"repository. It seems fitting that our 1.0 release comes at the moment where "
"community contributions overtake those made privately."
msgstr ""
"Nóta stairiúil suimiúil: nuair a eisíodh Django den chéad uair i mí Iúil "
"2005, tháinig an chéad leagan eisithe de Django ó stór inmheánach ag uimhir "
"athbhreithnithe 8825. Léiríonn Django 1.0 athbhreithniú 8961 ar ár stór "
"poiblí. Dealraíonn sé go bhfuil sé oiriúnach go dtagann ár n-eisiúint 1.0 "
"faoi láthair nuair a sháraíonn ranníocaíochtaí pobail na ranníocaíochtaí a "
"dhéantar go príobháideach."

msgid "Stability and forwards-compatibility"
msgstr "Cobhsaíocht agus comhoiriúnacht"

msgid ""
"The release of Django 1.0 comes with a promise of API stability and forwards-"
"compatibility. In a nutshell, this means that code you develop against "
"Django 1.0 will continue to work against 1.1 unchanged, and you should need "
"to make only minor changes for any 1.X release."
msgstr ""
"Tagann scaoileadh Django 1.0 le gealltanas cobhsaíocht API agus "
"comhoiriúnacht seolta. Go hachomair, ciallaíonn sé seo go leanfaidh an cód a "
"fhorbraíonn tú i gcoinne Django 1.0 ag obair i gcoinne 1.1 gan athrú, agus "
"níor cheart duit ach mionathruithe a dhéanamh d'aon scaoileadh 1.X."

msgid ""
"See the :doc:`API stability guide </misc/api-stability>` for full details."
msgstr ""
"Féach an:doc: `Treoir chobhsaíochta API` le haghaidh sonraí iom</misc/api-"
"stability> lána."

msgid ""
"Django 1.0 has a number of backwards-incompatible changes from Django 0.96. "
"If you have apps written against Django 0.96 that you need to port, see our "
"detailed porting guide:"
msgstr ""
"Tá roinnt athruithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha ag Django 1.0 ó Django 0.96. Má tá "
"aipeanna scríofa agat i gcoinne Django 0.96 a chaithfidh tú a chalafoirt, "
"féach ár dtreoir iompair mionsonraithe:"

msgid ""
"A complete list of backwards-incompatible changes can be found at https://"
"code.djangoproject.com/wiki/BackwardsIncompatibleChanges."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir liosta iomlán d'athruithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha ar chúl a fháil ag "
"https://code.djangoproject.com/wiki/BackwardsIncompatibleChanges."

msgid "What's new in Django 1.0"
msgstr "Cad atá nua i Django 1.0"

msgid "A *lot*!"
msgstr "A* mór*!"

msgid ""
"Since Django 0.96, we've made over 4,000 code commits, fixed more than 2,000 "
"bugs, and edited, added, or removed around 350,000 lines of code. We've also "
"added 40,000 lines of new documentation, and greatly improved what was "
"already there."
msgstr ""
"Ó Django 0.96, rinneamar os cionn 4,000 tiomantas cód, shocraigh muid níos "
"mó ná 2,000 fabht, agus thart ar 350,000 líne cód in eagar, a chur leis nó a "
"bhaint againn. Chuireamar 40,000 líne de dhoiciméadú nua leis freisin, agus "
"feabhsaigh muid go mór an méid a bhí ann cheana féin."

msgid ""
"In fact, new documentation is one of our favorite features of Django 1.0, so "
"we might as well start there. First, there's a new documentation site:"
msgstr ""
"Déanta na fírinne, tá cáipéisíocht nua ar cheann de na gnéithe is fearr linn "
"de Django 1.0, mar sin d'fhéadfaimis tosú ansin chomh maith. Ar dtús, tá "
"suíomh doiciméadaithe nua ann:"

msgid "https://docs.djangoproject.com/"
msgstr "https://docs.djangoproject.com/"

msgid ""
"The documentation has been greatly improved, cleaned up, and generally made "
"awesome. There's now dedicated search, indexes, and more."
msgstr ""
"Tá an doiciméadú feabhsaithe go mór, glanadh suas, agus go ginearálta déanta "
"uamhnach. Tá cuardach tiomnaithe anois, innéacsanna, agus go leor eile ann."

msgid ""
"We can't possibly document everything that's new in 1.0, but the "
"documentation will be your definitive guide. Anywhere you see something like:"
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir linn gach rud atá nua i 1.0 a dhoiciméadú, ach beidh an doiciméadú "
"mar do threoir chinntitheach. Áit ar bith a fheiceann tú rud mar:"

msgid "This feature is new in Django 1.0"
msgstr "Tá an ghné seo nua i Django 1.0"

msgid "You'll know that you're looking at something new or changed."
msgstr ""
"Beidh a fhios agat go bhfuil tú ag féachaint ar rud éigin nua nó athraithe."

msgid "The other major highlights of Django 1.0 are:"
msgstr "Is iad na príomhbhuaicphointí eile de Django 1.0 ná:"

msgid "Refactored admin application"
msgstr "Feidhmchlár riaracháin athchóirithe"

msgid ""
"The Django administrative interface (``django.contrib.admin``) has been "
"completely refactored; admin definitions are now completely decoupled from "
"model definitions (no more ``class Admin`` declaration in models!), "
"rewritten to use Django's new form-handling library (introduced in the 0.96 "
"release as ``django.newforms``, and now available as simply "
"``django.forms``) and redesigned with extensibility and customization in "
"mind. Full documentation for the admin application is available online in "
"the official Django documentation:"
msgstr ""
"Tá comhéadan riaracháin Django (`django.contrib.admin ``) athchóirithe go "
"hiomlán; tá sainmhínithe riaracháin dícheangailte go hiomlán anois ó "
"shainmhínithe samhlacha (gan aon dearbhú ``aicme Riaracháin`` níos mó i "
"samhlacha!) , athscríofa chun leabharlann láimhseála foirme nua Django a "
"úsáid (a tugadh isteach sa eisiúint 0.96 mar ``django.newforms``, agus atá "
"ar fáil anois mar `django.forms``) agus a athdhearadh le leathaitheacht agus "
"saincheaptha san áireamh. Tá cáipéisíocht iomlán don iarratas riaracháin ar "
"fáil ar líne i ndoiciméadú oifigiúil Django:"

msgid "See the :doc:`admin reference </ref/contrib/admin/index>` for details"
msgstr ""
"Féach na:doc: `tagairt admin `le haghaidh sonraí </ref/contrib/admin/index>"

msgid "Improved Unicode handling"
msgstr "Láimhseáil Unicode feabhsaithe"

msgid ""
"Django's internals have been refactored to use Unicode throughout; this "
"drastically simplifies the task of dealing with non-Western-European content "
"and data in Django. Additionally, utility functions have been provided to "
"ease interoperability with third-party libraries and systems which may or "
"may not handle Unicode gracefully. Details are available in Django's Unicode-"
"handling documentation."
msgstr ""
"Athraíodh inmheánacha Django chun Unicode a úsáid ar fud; déanann sé seo an "
"tasc déileáil le hábhar agus sonraí neamh-Iarthar-Eorpach i Django a "
"shimpliú go mór. Ina theannta sin, cuireadh feidhmeanna fóntais ar fáil chun "
"idir-inoibritheacht a mhaolú le leabharlanna agus córais tríú páirtí a "
"d'fhéadfadh Unicode a láimhseáil Tá sonraí ar fáil i ndoiciméadú láimhseála "
"Unicode Django."

msgid "See :doc:`/ref/unicode`."
msgstr "Féach: doc: `/ref/unicode`."

msgid "An improved ORM"
msgstr "ORM feabhsaithe"

msgid ""
"Django's object-relational mapper -- the component which provides the "
"mapping between Django model classes and your database, and which mediates "
"your database queries -- has been dramatically improved by a massive "
"refactoring. For most users of Django this is backwards-compatible; the "
"public-facing API for database querying underwent a few minor changes, but "
"most of the updates took place in the ORM's internals. A guide to the "
"changes, including backwards-incompatible modifications and mentions of new "
"features opened up by this refactoring, is `available on the Django wiki`__."
msgstr ""
"Feabhsaíodh léarscáil réad-choibhneasta Django - an chomhpháirt a "
"sholáthraíonn an mapáil idir ranganna samhail Django agus do bhunachar "
"sonraí, agus a idirghabhálann do cheisteanna bunachar sonraí - trí "
"athfhorthóiriú ollmhór. Maidir le formhór na n-úsáideoirí Django tá sé seo "
"comhoiriúnach le cúlra; rinneadh cúpla beag athrú ar an API atá ag tabhairt "
"aghaidh an phobail le haghaidh fiosrúcháin bunachar sonraí, ach tharla an "
"chuid is mó de na nuashonruithe i ndáileanna inmheánacha an ORM. Tá treoir "
"maidir leis na hathruithe, lena n-áirítear modhnuithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha "
"ar chúl agus luaitheanna ar ghnéithe nua a osclaíodh leis an athfhabhtú seo, "
"ar fáil ar an Django wiki`__."

msgid "Automatic escaping of template variables"
msgstr "Éalú uathoibríoch athróga teimplé"

msgid ""
"To provide improved security against cross-site scripting (XSS) "
"vulnerabilities, Django's template system now automatically escapes the "
"output of variables. This behavior is configurable, and allows both "
"variables and larger template constructs to be marked as safe (requiring no "
"escaping) or unsafe (requiring escaping). A full guide to this feature is in "
"the documentation for the :ttag:`autoescape` tag."
msgstr ""
"Chun slándáil fheabhsaithe a sholáthar i gcoinne leochaileachtaí scripteála "
"tras-láithreáin (XSS), éalaíonn córas teimpléad Django anois as aschur "
"athróg go huathoibríoch. Tá an t-iompar seo inchumraithe, agus ligeann sé "
"athróga agus tógáil teimpléad níos mó a mharcáil mar shábháilte (gan éalú ag "
"éalú) nó neamhshábháilte (ag éalú ag teastáil). Tá treoir iomlán ar an ngné "
"seo sa dhoiciméadú don chlib: ttag: `autoescape`."

msgid "``django.contrib.gis`` (GeoDjango)"
msgstr "``django.contrib.gis`` (GeodJango)"

msgid ""
"A project over a year in the making, this adds world-class GIS (`Geographic "
"Information Systems`_) support to Django, in the form of a ``contrib`` "
"application. Its documentation is currently being maintained externally, and "
"will be merged into the main Django documentation shortly. Huge thanks go to "
"Justin Bronn, Jeremy Dunck, Brett Hoerner and Travis Pinney for their "
"efforts in creating and completing this feature."
msgstr ""
"Tionscadal breis agus bliain atá á dhéanamh, cuireann sé seo tacaíocht GIS "
"den scoth (`Córais Faisnéise Geografacha `_) do Django, i bhfoirm iarratais "
"``contrib``. Tá a dhoiciméadú á chothabháil go seachtrach faoi láthair, agus "
"cumasófar é sa phríomhdhoiciméadú Django go luath. Gabhann buíochas ollmhóra "
"le Justin Bronn, Jeremy Dunck, Brett Hoerner agus Travis Pinney as a n-"
"iarrachtaí chun an ghné seo a chruthú agus a chríochnú."

msgid "See :doc:`GeoDjango </ref/contrib/gis/index>` for details."
msgstr "Féach: doc: `GeodJango` le haghaidh sonraí </ref/contrib/gis/index>."

msgid "Pluggable file storage"
msgstr "Stóráil comhaid inphlugáilte"

msgid ""
"Django's built-in ``FileField`` and ``ImageField`` now can take advantage of "
"pluggable file-storage backends, allowing extensive customization of where "
"and how uploaded files get stored by Django. For details, see :doc:`the "
"files documentation </topics/files>`; big thanks go to Marty Alchin for "
"putting in the hard work to get this completed."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le ``Filefield` agus ``ImageField` ionsuite Django anois leas a "
"bhaint as cúltaca stórála comhad inphlugáilte, rud a ligeann saincheapadh "
"fairsing ar an áit agus conas a stóráilíonn Django comhaid uaslódáilte. Le "
"haghaidh sonraí, féach:doc: `doiciméadú na gcomhaid`; bu</topics/files> "
"íochas mór le Marty Alchin as an obair chrua a chur isteach chun é seo a "
"chur i gcrích."

msgid "Jython compatibility"
msgstr "Comhoiriúnacht Jython"

msgid ""
"Thanks to a lot of work from Leo Soto during a Google Summer of Code "
"project, Django's codebase has been refactored to remove incompatibilities "
"with `Jython`_, an implementation of Python written in Java, which runs "
"Python code on the Java Virtual Machine. Django is now compatible with the "
"forthcoming Jython 2.5 release."
msgstr ""
"A bhuíochas le go leor oibre ó Leo Soto le linn tionscadail Google Summer of "
"Code, rinneadh athbhreithniú cód Django chun neamhoiriúnachtaí a bhaint le "
"`Jython`_, cur i bhfeidhm Python scríofa i Java, a ritheann cód Python ar an "
"Meaisín Fíorúil Java. Tá Django comhoiriúnach anois leis an eisiúint Jython "
"2.5 atá le teacht."

msgid "Generic relations in forms and admin"
msgstr "Caidrimh chineálach i bhfoirmeacha agus"

msgid ""
"Classes are now included in ``django.contrib.contenttypes`` which can be "
"used to support generic relations in both the admin interface and in end-"
"user forms. See :ref:`the documentation for generic relations <generic-"
"relations>` for details."
msgstr ""
"Tá ranganna san áireamh anois in ``django.contrib.contenttypes`` ar féidir a "
"úsáid chun tacú le caidreamh cineálach sa chomhéadan riaracháin agus i "
"bhfoirmeacha úsáideora deiridh araon. Féach: tagairt: `an doiciméadú maidir "
"le caidreamh cineálach <generic-relations>`le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid "``INSERT``/``UPDATE`` distinction"
msgstr "``Cuir isteach ````/``UPDATE`` idirdhealú"

msgid ""
"Although Django's default behavior of having a model's ``save()`` method "
"automatically determine whether to perform an ``INSERT`` or an ``UPDATE`` at "
"the SQL level is suitable for the majority of cases, there are occasional "
"situations where forcing one or the other is useful. As a result, models can "
"now support an additional parameter to ``save()`` which can force a specific "
"operation."
msgstr ""
"Cé go bhfuil iompar réamhshocraithe Django maidir le modh ``save () "
"``samhail a chinneann go huathoibríoch an gcaithfear ``INSERT`` nó `UPDATE`` "
"a dhéanamh ag leibhéal SQL oiriúnach do fhormhór na gcásanna, bíonn cásanna "
"ó am go chéile ann ina bhfuil úsáideach ceann amháin nó an ceann eile a chur "
"i bhfeidhm. Mar thoradh air sin, is féidir le samhlacha tacú anois le "
"paraiméadar breise chun ``sábháil () ``ar féidir leo oibríocht shonrach a "
"chur i bhfeidhm."

msgid "See :ref:`ref-models-force-insert` for details."
msgstr "Féach: ref: `ref-models-force-insert` le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid "Split ``CacheMiddleware``"
msgstr "Scoilt ``Cachemiddleware``"

msgid ""
"Django's ``CacheMiddleware`` has been split into three classes: "
"``CacheMiddleware`` itself still exists and retains all of its previous "
"functionality, but it is now built from two separate middleware classes "
"which handle the two parts of caching (inserting into and reading from the "
"cache) separately, offering additional flexibility for situations where "
"combining these functions into a single middleware posed problems."
msgstr ""
"Tá “Cachemiddleware” Django roinnte ina thrí rang: “Cachemiddleware” féin "
"ann fós agus coinníonn a fheidhmiúlacht go léir roimhe seo, ach tá sé tógtha "
"anois ó dhá rang lár ar leithligh a láimhseálann an dá chuid de chaching "
"(cur isteach sa taisce agus léamh as) fadhbanna."

msgid ""
"Full details, including updated notes on appropriate use, are in :doc:`the "
"caching documentation </topics/cache>`."
msgstr ""
"Tá sonraí iomlána, lena n-áirítear nótaí nuashonraithe maidir le húsáid "
"chuí, in:doc: `an doiciméadú caching '</topics/cache>."

msgid "Refactored ``django.contrib.comments``"
msgstr "Athchóirithe ``django.contrib.comments``"

msgid ""
"As part of a Google Summer of Code project, Thejaswi Puthraya carried out a "
"major rewrite and refactoring of Django's bundled comment system, greatly "
"increasing its flexibility and customizability."
msgstr ""
"Mar chuid de thionscadal Google Summer of Code, rinne Thejaswi Puthraya "
"athscríobh agus athfhabhtú mór ar chóras tráchtaireachta cuachta Django, ag "
"méadú go mór a sholúbthacht agus a inshaincheapthacht."

msgid "Removal of deprecated features"
msgstr "Gnéithe díscothaithe a bhaint"

msgid ""
"A number of features and methods which had previously been marked as "
"deprecated, and which were scheduled for removal prior to the 1.0 release, "
"are no longer present in Django. These include imports of the form library "
"from ``django.newforms`` (now located simply at ``django.forms``), the "
"``form_for_model`` and ``form_for_instance`` helper functions (which have "
"been replaced by ``ModelForm``) and a number of deprecated features which "
"were replaced by the dispatcher, file-uploading and file-storage refactoring "
"introduced in the Django 1.0 alpha releases."
msgstr ""
"Níl roinnt gnéithe agus modhanna a marcáilíodh roimhe seo mar dhíluaite, "
"agus a bhí sceidealta le fáil roimh an scaoileadh 1.0, i láthair a "
"thuilleadh i Django. Ina measc seo tá allmhairí leabharlann na foirme ó "
"`django.newforms`` (atá suite anois ag `django.forms``), feidhmeanna cúntóra "
"``form_for_model`` agus ``form_for_instance`` (a cuireadh `ModelForm 'in "
"ionad' ModelForm ') agus roinnt gnéithe lasctha a cuireadh in ionad an "
"seoltóir, comhad a uaslódáil athfhabhtú stórála a tugadh isteach sna "
"eisiúintí alfa Django 1.0."

msgid "Known issues"
msgstr "Saincheisteanna aitheanta"

msgid ""
"We've done our best to make Django 1.0 as solid as possible, but "
"unfortunately there are a couple of issues that we know about in the release."
msgstr ""
"Rinneamar ár ndícheall chun Django 1.0 a dhéanamh chomh láidir agus is "
"féidir, ach ar an drochuair tá cúpla saincheist ann a bhfuil a fhios againn "
"faoi sa scaoileadh."

msgid "Multi-table model inheritance with ``to_field``"
msgstr "Oidhreacht samhail il-tábla le ``to_field`"

msgid ""
"If you're using :ref:`multiple table model inheritance <multi-table-"
"inheritance>`, be aware of this caveat: child models using a custom "
"``parent_link`` and ``to_field`` will cause database integrity errors. A set "
"of models like the following are **not valid**::"
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag baint úsáidea:ref: `oidhreacht samhail iolracha tábla <multi-"
"table-inheritance>`, bí ar an eolas faoin rabhadh seo: beidh earráidí sláine "
"bunachar sonraí ina chúis le samhlacha leanaí a úsáideann saincheaptha "
"``parent_link`` agus ``to_field``. Níl sraith samhlacha mar na nithe seo a "
"leanas bailí**:"

msgid "This bug will be fixed in the next release of Django."
msgstr "Socrófar an fabht seo sa chéad eisiúint eile de Django."

msgid "Caveats with support of certain databases"
msgstr "Rabhadh le tacaíocht ó bhunachar sonraí áirithe"

msgid ""
"Django attempts to support as many features as possible on all database "
"backends. However, not all database backends are alike, and in particular "
"many of the supported database differ greatly from version to version. It's "
"a good idea to checkout our :doc:`notes on supported database </ref/"
"databases>`:"
msgstr ""
"Déanann Django iarracht tacaíocht a thabhairt don oiread gnéithe agus is "
"féidir ar gach inneall bunachar sonraí. Mar sin féin, níl na haiséilí "
"bunachar sonraí go léir mar a chéile, agus go háirithe go bhfuil difríocht "
"mhór idir go leor den bhunachar sonraí tacaithe ó leagan go leagan. Is "
"smaoineamh maith é ár nótaí :doc:`a sheiceáil amach ar bhunachar sonraí "
"tacaithe </ref/databases>`:"

msgid ":ref:`mysql-notes`"
msgstr ":ref: `mysql-nótaí `"

msgid ":ref:`sqlite-notes`"
msgstr ":ref: `sqlite-notes`"

msgid ":ref:`oracle-notes`"
msgstr ":ref: `oracle-notes`"

msgid "Porting your apps from Django 0.96 to 1.0"
msgstr "Do chuid aipeanna a iompar ó Django 0.96 go 1.0"

msgid "Django 1.0 breaks compatibility with 0.96 in some areas."
msgstr "Briseann Django 1.0 comhoiriúnacht le 0.96 i roinnt réimsí."

msgid ""
"This guide will help you port 0.96 projects and apps to 1.0. The first part "
"of this document includes the common changes needed to run with 1.0. If "
"after going through the first part your code still breaks, check the section "
"`Less-common Changes`_ for a list of a bunch of less-common compatibility "
"issues."
msgstr ""
"Cuideoidh an treoir seo leat tionscadal agus feidhmchláir 0.96 a phort go "
"1.0. Cuimsíonn an chéad chuid den doiciméad seo na hathruithe coitianta a "
"theastaíonn chun reáchtáil le 1.0. Má bhriseann do chód fós tar éis dul tríd "
"an gcéad chuid, seiceáil an chuid `Athruithe Lú Coitianta `_ le haghaidh "
"liosta de dornán saincheisteanna comhoiriúnachta nach bhfuil chomh coitianta."

msgid ""
"The :doc:`1.0 release notes </releases/1.0>`. That document explains the new "
"features in 1.0 more deeply; the porting guide is more concerned with "
"helping you quickly update your code."
msgstr ""
"Nótaí scaoileadh: Doc: `1.0 </releases/1.0>. Míníonn an doiciméad sin na "
"gnéithe nua i 1.0 níos doimhne; tá baint níos mó ag an treoir iompair le "
"cabhrú leat do chód a nuashonrú go tapa."

msgid "Common changes"
msgstr "Athruithe coitianta"

msgid ""
"This section describes the changes between 0.96 and 1.0 that most users will "
"need to make."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an chuid seo cur síos ar na hathruithe idir 0.96 agus 1.0 a "
"chaithfidh mórchuid na n-úsáideoirí a dhéanamh."

msgid "Use Unicode"
msgstr "Úsáid Unicode"

msgid ""
"Change string literals (``'foo'``) into Unicode literals (``u'foo'``). "
"Django now uses Unicode strings throughout. In most places, raw strings will "
"continue to work, but updating to use Unicode literals will prevent some "
"obscure problems."
msgstr ""
"Athraigh litríochtaí teaghrán (``'foo'``) go litríochtaí Unicode "
"(``u'foo'``). Úsáideann Django teaghráin Unicode anois ar fud. I bhformhór "
"na n-áiteanna, leanfaidh teaghráin amh ag obair, ach cuirfidh nuashonrú chun "
"litríochtaí Unicode a úsáid cosc ar roinnt fadhbanna doiléire."

msgid "See :doc:`/ref/unicode` for full details."
msgstr "Féach: doc: `/ref/unicode` le haghaidh sonraí iomlána."

msgid "Models"
msgstr "Samhla"

msgid "Common changes to your models file:"
msgstr "Athruithe coitianta ar do chomhad samhlacha:"

msgid "Rename ``maxlength`` to ``max_length``"
msgstr "Athainmnigh ``maxlength ``go ``max_long``"

msgid ""
"Rename your ``maxlength`` argument to ``max_length`` (this was changed to be "
"consistent with form fields):"
msgstr ""
"Athainmnigh d'argóint ``maxlength ``go `max_length`` (athraíodh é seo chun a "
"bheith comhsheasmhach le réimsí foirme):"

msgid "Replace ``__str__`` with ``__unicode__``"
msgstr "Cuir ``__unicode__`` in ionad ``__str__``"

msgid ""
"Replace your model's ``__str__`` function with a ``__unicode__`` method, and "
"make sure you `use Unicode`_ (``u'foo'``) in that method."
msgstr ""
"Cuir modh ``__unicode__`` feidhm ``__str__`` do mhúnla, agus déan cinnte go "
"n-úsáideann tú Unicode`_ (``u'foo'``) sa mhodh sin."

msgid "Remove ``prepopulated_from``"
msgstr "Bain ``prepopulated_from``"

msgid ""
"Remove the ``prepopulated_from`` argument on model fields. It's no longer "
"valid and has been moved to the ``ModelAdmin`` class in ``admin.py``. See "
"`the admin`_, below, for more details about changes to the admin."
msgstr ""
"Bain an argóint ``prepopulated_from`` ar réimsí samhail. Níl sé bailí a "
"thuilleadh agus aistríodh é go dtí an rang ``ModelAdmin`` i `admin.py``. "
"Féach `an riarachán `_, thíos, le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí faoi athruithe "
"ar an riarachán."

msgid "Remove ``core``"
msgstr "Bain ``core ``"

msgid ""
"Remove the ``core`` argument from your model fields. It is no longer "
"necessary, since the equivalent functionality (part of :ref:`inline editing "
"<admin-inlines>`) is handled differently by the admin interface now. You "
"don't have to worry about inline editing until you get to `the admin`_ "
"section, below. For now, remove all references to ``core``."
msgstr ""
"Bain an argóint ``core ``ó do réimsí samhail. Níl sé riachtanach a "
"thuilleadh, ós rud é go láimhseálann an comhéadan riaracháin an "
"fheidhmiúlacht chomhionann (cuid de: ref: `eagarthóireacht inlíne <admin-"
"inlines>`) go difriúil anois. Ní gá duit a bheith buartha faoi "
"eagarthóireacht inlíne go dtí go sroicheann tú chuig an rannán `an "
"riaracháin `_, thíos. Go dtí seo, bain na tagairtí go léir do `core``."

msgid "Replace ``class Admin:`` with ``admin.py``"
msgstr "Cuir “admin” in ionad ``class Admin:`` le `admin.py``"

msgid ""
"Remove all your inner ``class Admin`` declarations from your models. They "
"won't break anything if you leave them, but they also won't do anything. To "
"register apps with the admin you'll move those declarations to an "
"``admin.py`` file; see `the admin`_ below for more details."
msgstr ""
"Bain do dhearbhuithe inmheánacha ``aicme Riaracháin ``ó do mhúnlaí. Ní "
"bhriseoidh siad aon rud má fhágann tú iad, ach ní dhéanfaidh siad aon rud "
"freisin. Chun aipeanna a chlárú leis an riarachán aistrfidh tú na "
"dearbhuithe sin chuig comhad `admin.py`; féach `an riarachán `_ thíos le "
"haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid ""
"A contributor to djangosnippets__ has written a script that'll `scan your "
"models.py and generate a corresponding admin.py`__."
msgstr ""
"Tá script scríofa ag ranníocóir le djangosnippets__ a dhéanfaidh `scanadh do "
"models.py agus a ghinneoidh admin.py`__ comhfhreagrach."

msgid "Example"
msgstr "Sampla"

msgid ""
"Below is an example ``models.py`` file with all the changes you'll need to "
"make:"
msgstr ""
"Seo thíos sampla comhad ``models.py`` leis na hathruithe go léir a "
"chaithfidh tú a dhéanamh:"

msgid "Old (0.96) ``models.py``::"
msgstr "Sean (0.96) ``models.py``::"

msgid "New (1.0) ``models.py``::"
msgstr "Nua (1.0) ``models.py``:"

msgid "New (1.0) ``admin.py``::"
msgstr "Nua (1.0) ``admin.py``:"

msgid "The Admin"
msgstr "An Riarachán"

msgid ""
"One of the biggest changes in 1.0 is the new admin. The Django "
"administrative interface (``django.contrib.admin``) has been completely "
"refactored; admin definitions are now completely decoupled from model "
"definitions, the framework has been rewritten to use Django's new form-"
"handling library and redesigned with extensibility and customization in mind."
msgstr ""
"Ceann de na hathruithe is mó i 1.0 is é an riarachán nua. Tá comhéadan "
"riaracháin Django (`django.contrib.admin ``) athchóirithe go hiomlán; tá "
"sainmhínithe riaracháin dícheangailte go hiomlán anois ó shainmhínithe "
"samhail, athscríobhadh an creat chun leabharlann láimhseála foirm nua Django "
"a úsáid agus athdhearadh le leathaitheacht agus saincheaptha san áireamh."

msgid ""
"Practically, this means you'll need to rewrite all of your ``class Admin`` "
"declarations. You've already seen in `models`_ above how to replace your "
"``class Admin`` with an ``admin.site.register()`` call in an ``admin.py`` "
"file. Below are some more details on how to rewrite that ``Admin`` "
"declaration into the new syntax."
msgstr ""
"Go praiticiúil, ciallaíonn sé seo go mbeidh ort gach ceann de do "
"dhearbhuithe ```Riarachán aicme ``a athscríobh. Chonaic tú cheana féin i "
"`samhlacha `_ thuas conas glao ``admin.site.register () ``a chur in ionad do "
"``admin aicme`` admin ```. Seo thíos roinnt sonraí níos mó maidir le conas "
"an dearbhú ``Riarach`` sin a athscríobh isteach sa chomhréir nua."

msgid "Use new inline syntax"
msgstr "Úsáid comhréir inlíne nua"

msgid ""
"The new ``edit_inline`` options have all been moved to ``admin.py``. Here's "
"an example:"
msgstr ""
"Tá na roghanna nua ``edit_inline`` aistrithe go léir chuig `admin.py``. Seo "
"sampla:"

msgid "Old (0.96)::"
msgstr "Sean (0.96)::"

msgid "New (1.0)::"
msgstr "Nua (1.0)::"

msgid "See :ref:`admin-inlines` for more details."
msgstr "Féach: ref: `admin-inlines` le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid "Simplify ``fields``, or use ``fieldsets``"
msgstr "``réimsí ``a shimpliú, nó bain úsáid as ``fieldsets``"

msgid ""
"The old ``fields`` syntax was quite confusing, and has been simplified. The "
"old syntax still works, but you'll need to use ``fieldsets`` instead."
msgstr ""
"Bhí an sean-chomhpháirtíocht ``réimsí `mearbhall go leor, agus tá sé "
"simplithe. Oibríonn an sean-chomhréir fós, ach beidh ort ``fieldsets`` a "
"úsáid ina ionad."

msgid ""
"More detailed information about the changes and the reasons behind them can "
"be found on the `NewformsAdminBranch wiki page`__"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir faisnéis níos mionsonraithe faoi na hathruithe agus na cúiseanna "
"atá taobh thiar leo a fháil ar an leathanach wiki `NewFormsAdminbranch `__"

msgid ""
"The new admin comes with a ton of new features; you can read about them in "
"the :doc:`admin documentation </ref/contrib/admin/index>`."
msgstr ""
"Tagann an riarachán nua le tonna gnéithe nua; is féidir leat léamh fúthu "
"in:doc: `doiciméadú riaracháin `</ref/contrib/admin/index>."

msgid "URLs"
msgstr "URLanna"

msgid "Update your root ``urls.py``"
msgstr "Nuashonraigh do fhréamh ``urls.py``"

msgid ""
"If you're using the admin site, you need to update your root ``urls.py``."
msgstr ""
"Má tá an suíomh riaracháin á úsáid agat, ní mór duit do fhréamh ``urls.py` a "
"nuashonrú."

msgid "Old (0.96) ``urls.py``::"
msgstr "Sean (0.96) ``urls.py``::"

msgid "New (1.0) ``urls.py``::"
msgstr "Nua (1.0) ``urls.py``:"

msgid "Views"
msgstr "Radharcanna"

msgid "Use ``django.forms`` instead of ``newforms``"
msgstr "Úsáid ``django.forms`` in ionad ``newforms``"

msgid ""
"Replace ``django.newforms`` with ``django.forms`` -- Django 1.0 renamed the "
"``newforms`` module (introduced in 0.96) to plain old ``forms``. The "
"``oldforms`` module was also removed."
msgstr ""
"Cuir `django.newforms`` in ionad `django.forms`` - Athainmníodh Django 1.0 "
"an modúl ``newforms`` (tugadh isteach i 0.96) go sean-`foirme`` simplí. "
"Baineadh an modúl `oldforms` freisin."

msgid ""
"If you're already using the ``newforms`` library, and you used our "
"recommended ``import`` statement syntax, all you have to do is change your "
"import statements."
msgstr ""
"Má tá leabharlann ``newforms` á úsáid agat cheana féin, agus má d'úsáid tú "
"ár gcomhréiteach ráiteas ``allmhairiúch` a mholtar, níl le déanamh agat ach "
"do ráitis iompórtála a athrú."

msgid "Old::"
msgstr "Sean::"

msgid "New::"
msgstr "Nua::"

msgid ""
"If you're using the old forms system (formerly known as ``django.forms`` and "
"``django.oldforms``), you'll have to rewrite your forms. A good place to "
"start is the :doc:`forms documentation </topics/forms/index>`"
msgstr ""
"Má tá an seanchóras foirmeacha á n-úsáid agat (ar a django.forms`` agus "
"`django.oldforms`` roimhe seo), beidh ort d'fhoirmeacha a athscríobh. Áit "
"mhaith le tosú ná: doc: `foirmeacha doiciméadúcháin `</topics/forms/index>"

msgid "Handle uploaded files using the new API"
msgstr "Láimhseáil comhaid uaslódáilte ag úsáid an API"

msgid ""
"Replace use of uploaded files -- that is, entries in ``request.FILES`` -- as "
"simple dictionaries with the "
"new :class:`~django.core.files.uploadedfile.UploadedFile`. The old "
"dictionary syntax no longer works."
msgstr ""
"Cuir úsáid comhaid uaslódáilte - is é sin, iontrálacha i ``Request.Files`` "
"-- mar fhoclóirí simplí leis an nua:class: "
"`~django.core.files.uploadedfile.uploadedfile`. Ní oibríonn comhréir an sean-"
"fhoclóra a thuilleadh."

msgid "Thus, in a view like::"
msgstr "Dá bhrí sin, i radharc mar:"

msgid "...you'd need to make the following changes:"
msgstr "... bheadh ort na hathruithe seo a leanas a dhéanamh:"

msgid "Old (0.96)"
msgstr "Sean (0.96)"

msgid "New (1.0)"
msgstr "Nua (1.0)"

msgid "``f['content']``"
msgstr "``f ['ábhar'] ``"

msgid "``f.read()``"
msgstr "``f.read () ``"

msgid "``f['filename']``"
msgstr "``f ['ainm comhad'] ``"

msgid "``f.name``"
msgstr "``f.ainm``"

msgid "``f['content-type']``"
msgstr "``f ['cineál ábhair'] ``"

msgid "``f.content_type``"
msgstr "``f.cineál_content``"

msgid "Work with file fields using the new API"
msgstr "Oibrigh le réimsí comhad ag baint úsáide as an API nua"

msgid ""
"The internal implementation of :class:`django.db.models.FileField` have "
"changed. A visible result of this is that the way you access special "
"attributes (URL, filename, image size, etc.) of these model fields has "
"changed. You will need to make the following changes, assuming your "
"model's :class:`~django.db.models.FileField` is called ``myfile``:"
msgstr ""
"Tá athrú tagtha ar chur i bhfeidhm inmheán:class: "
"`Django.db.Models.FileField`. Toradh infheicthe air seo ná go bhfuil athrú "
"tagtha ar an mbealach a rochtain agat ar thréithe speisialta (URL, ainm "
"comhaid, méid íomhá, srl.) na réimsí samhail seo. Beidh ort na hathruithe "
"seo a leanas a dhéanamh, ag glacadh leis ar do mhúnla 's:class: "
"`~django.db.models.filefield` tugtar ``myfile``:"

msgid "``myfile.get_content_filename()``"
msgstr "``myfile.get_content_filename () ``"

msgid "``myfile.content.path``"
msgstr "``myfile.content.path``"

msgid "``myfile.get_content_url()``"
msgstr "``myfile.get_content_url () ``"

msgid "``myfile.content.url``"
msgstr "``myfile.content.url ``"

msgid "``myfile.get_content_size()``"
msgstr "``myfile.get_content_size () ``"

msgid "``myfile.content.size``"
msgstr "``myfile.content.size``"

msgid "``myfile.save_content_file()``"
msgstr "``myfile.save_content_file () ``"

msgid "``myfile.content.save()``"
msgstr "``myfile.content.save () ``"

msgid "``myfile.get_content_width()``"
msgstr "``myfile.get_content_width () ``"

msgid "``myfile.content.width``"
msgstr "``myfile.content.width``"

msgid "``myfile.get_content_height()``"
msgstr "``myfile.get_content_height () ``"

msgid "``myfile.content.height``"
msgstr "``myfile.content.height``"

msgid ""
"Note that the ``width`` and ``height`` attributes only make sense "
"for :class:`~django.db.models.ImageField` fields. More details can be found "
"in the :doc:`model API </ref/models/fields>` documentation."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara nach bhfuil ciall ar na tréithe ``leithead`` agus "
"``airde`` ach do réimsí: `class: `~django.db.models.imagefield`. Is féidir "
"tuilleadh sonraí a fháil sna cáipéiséisíocht: doc: `model API` </ref/models/"
"fields>."

msgid "Use ``Paginator`` instead of ``ObjectPaginator``"
msgstr "Úsáid ``Paginator`` in ionad ``ObjectPaginator``"

msgid ""
"The ``ObjectPaginator`` in 0.96 has been removed and replaced with an "
"improved version, :class:`django.core.paginator.Paginator`."
msgstr ""
"Baineadh an `ObjectPaginator`` i 0.96 agus cuireadh leagan feabhsaithe ina "
"ionad, :class: `django.core.paginator.paginator`."

msgid "Templates"
msgstr "Teimpléid"

msgid "Learn to love autoescaping"
msgstr "Foghlaim grá a bhaint as autoescaping"

msgid ""
"By default, the template system now automatically HTML-escapes the output of "
"every variable. To learn more, see :ref:`automatic-html-escaping`."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, éalaíonn an córas teimpléid HTML-go huathoibríoch "
"anois aschur gach athróg. Chun tuilleadh a fhoghlaim, féach:ref: `automatic-"
"html-escaping`."

msgid ""
"To disable auto-escaping for an individual variable, use the :tfilter:`safe` "
"filter:"
msgstr ""
"Chun éalú uathoibríoch a dhíchumasú le haghaidh athróg aonair, bain úsáid as "
"an scagair:tfilter: `safe`:"

msgid ""
"To disable auto-escaping for an entire template, wrap the template (or just "
"a particular section of the template) in the :ttag:`autoescape` tag:"
msgstr ""
"Chun éalú uathoibríoch a dhíchumasú le haghaidh teimpléad iomlán, fillte an "
"teimpléad (nó díreach cuid áirithe den teimpléad) sa chlibe:ttag: "
"`autoescape`:"

msgid "Less-common changes"
msgstr "Athruithe nach bhfuil chomh coitianta"

msgid ""
"The following changes are smaller, more localized changes. They should only "
"affect more advanced users, but it's probably worth reading through the list "
"and checking your code for these things."
msgstr ""
"Is athruithe níos lú, níos logánaithe iad na hathruithe seo a leanas. Níor "
"cheart dóibh dul i bhfeidhm ach ar úsáideoirí níos airde, ach is dócha gur "
"fiú léamh tríd an liosta agus do chód a sheiceáil le haghaidh na rudaí seo."

msgid "Signals"
msgstr "Comharthaí"

msgid "Add ``**kwargs`` to any registered signal handlers."
msgstr "Cuir `**kwargs ``le haon láimhseálaithe comhartha cláraithe."

msgid ""
"Connect, disconnect, and send signals via methods on "
"the :class:`~django.dispatch.Signal` object instead of through module "
"methods in ``django.dispatch.dispatcher``."
msgstr ""
"Ceangail, dícheangail agus seol comharthaí trí mhodhanna ar an réad: class: "
"`~django.dispch.signal` in ionad trí mhodhanna modúl i "
"`django.expedich.expedicher``."

msgid ""
"Remove any use of the ``Anonymous`` and ``Any`` sender options; they no "
"longer exist. You can still receive signals sent by any sender by using "
"``sender=None``"
msgstr ""
"Bain aon úsáid de na roghanna seoltóra ``Anainm`` agus ```Aon ````` ``` `` "
"`` `` `` `` `` `` `` `` ` Is féidir leat comharthaí a sheolann aon seoltóir "
"a fháil fós trí úsáid a bhaint as ``seoltóir = none``"

msgid ""
"Make any custom signals you've declared into instances "
"of :class:`django.dispatch.Signal` instead of anonymous objects."
msgstr ""
"Déan aon chomharthaí saincheaptha a dhearbhaigh tú i gcásanna de:class: "
"`Django.Dispatch.Signal` in ionad rudaí gan ainm."

msgid "Here's quick summary of the code changes you'll need to make:"
msgstr "Seo achoimre tapa ar na hathruithe cód a chaithfidh tú a dhéanamh:"

msgid "``def callback(sender)``"
msgstr "``def glaonna aisghairm (seoltóir) ``"

msgid "``def callback(sender, **kwargs)``"
msgstr "``def glaonna aisghairm (seoltóir, **kwargs) ``"

msgid "``sig = object()``"
msgstr "``sig = réad () ``"

msgid "``sig = django.dispatch.Signal()``"
msgstr "``sig = django.expedich.signal () ``"

msgid "``dispatcher.connect(callback, sig)``"
msgstr "``expedicher.connect (glaoch ar ais, sig) ``"

msgid "``sig.connect(callback)``"
msgstr "``sig.connect (glaoch ar ais) ``"

msgid "``dispatcher.send(sig, sender)``"
msgstr "``expedicher.send (sig, seoltóir) ``"

msgid "``sig.send(sender)``"
msgstr "``sig.send (seoltóir) ``"

msgid "``dispatcher.connect(callback, sig, sender=Any)``"
msgstr "``expedicher.connect (glaoch ar ais, sig, seoltóir = aon) ``"

msgid "``sig.connect(callback, sender=None)``"
msgstr "``sig.connect (glaoch ar ais, Seoltóir = níl aon duine) ``"

msgid "Comments"
msgstr "Tuairimí"

msgid ""
"If you were using Django 0.96's ``django.contrib.comments`` app, you'll need "
"to upgrade to the new comments app introduced in 1.0. See the upgrade guide "
"for details."
msgstr ""
"Má bhí tú ag úsáid aip ``django.contrib.comments` Django 0.96, beidh ort "
"uasghrádú a dhéanamh chuig an aip tráchtanna nua a tugadh isteach i 1.0. "
"Féach an treoir uasghrádaithe le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid "Template tags"
msgstr "Clibeanna teimpléid"

msgid ":ttag:`spaceless` tag"
msgstr ":ttag: clib `gan spás`"

msgid ""
"The ``spaceless`` template tag now removes *all* spaces between HTML tags, "
"instead of preserving a single space."
msgstr ""
"Baineann an chlib teimpléad ``spacel`` anois spásanna uach* idir clibeanna "
"HTML, in ionad spás amháin a chaomhnú."

msgid "Local flavors"
msgstr "Blasanna áitiúla"

msgid "U.S. local flavor"
msgstr "Blas áitiúil na SA"

msgid ""
"``django.contrib.localflavor.usa`` has been renamed to "
"``django.contrib.localflavor.us``. This change was made to match the naming "
"scheme of other local flavors. To migrate your code, all you need to do is "
"change the imports."
msgstr ""
"Athainmníodh ``django.contrib.localflavor.usa ``go "
"`django.contrib.localflavor.us``. Rinneadh an t-athrú seo chun scéim "
"ainmniúcháin blasanna áitiúla eile a mheaitseáil. Chun do chód a aistriú, "
"níl le déanamh agat ach na hallmhairí a athrú."

msgid "Sessions"
msgstr "Seisiúin"

msgid "Getting a new session key"
msgstr "Eochair seisiúin nua a fháil"

msgid ""
"``SessionBase.get_new_session_key()`` has been renamed to "
"``_get_new_session_key()``. ``get_new_session_object()`` no longer exists."
msgstr ""
"Athainmníodh ``SessionBase.get_new_session_key () ``go "
"``_get_new_session_key ()``. ``get_new_session_object () ``níl ann a "
"thuilleadh."

msgid "Fixtures"
msgstr "Daingneáin"

msgid "Loading a row no longer calls ``save()``"
msgstr "Ní ghlaonn sé ar `save () ``a thuilleadh ag luchtú sraitheanna"

msgid ""
"Previously, loading a row automatically ran the model's ``save()`` method. "
"This is no longer the case, so any fields (for example: timestamps) that "
"were auto-populated by a ``save()`` now need explicit values in any fixture."
msgstr ""
"Roimhe seo, rith an tsraith a luchtú go huathoibríoch modh ``save () ``an "
"tsamhail. Níl sé seo amhlaidh a thuilleadh, mar sin teastaíonn luachanna "
"follasacha in aon daingneán anois ó aon réimsí (mar shampla: stampaí ama) a "
"rinneadh go huathoibríoch ag `save () `."

msgid "Settings"
msgstr "Socruithe"

msgid "Better exceptions"
msgstr "Eisceachtaí níos fearr"

msgid ""
"The old :exc:`EnvironmentError` has split into an :exc:`ImportError` when "
"Django fails to find the settings module and a :exc:`RuntimeError` when you "
"try to reconfigure settings after having already used them."
msgstr ""
"Tá an sean:exc: `EnvironmentError` roinnte ina an:exc: `ImportError` nuair a "
"theipeann ar Django an modúl socruithe a aimsiú agus a:exc: `RuntimeError` "
"nuair a dhéanann tú iarracht socruithe a athchumrú tar éis iad a úsáid "
"cheana féin."

msgid ":setting:`LOGIN_URL` has moved"
msgstr ":setting: `LOGIN_URL` tar éis bogadh"

msgid ""
"The :setting:`LOGIN_URL` constant moved from ``django.contrib.auth`` into "
"the ``settings`` module. Instead of using ``from django.contrib.auth import "
"LOGIN_URL`` refer to :setting:`settings.LOGIN_URL <LOGIN_URL>`."
msgstr ""
"Bhog an: setting: `LOGIN_URL` tairiseach ó ``django.contrib.auth`` isteach "
"sa modúl ``socruithe ``. <LOGIN_URL>In ionad ``from django.contrib.auth "
"allmhairiú LOGIN_URL`` a úsáid féach to:setting: `Settings.login_url `."

msgid ":setting:`APPEND_SLASH` behavior has been updated"
msgstr ":setting: Nuashonraíodh iompar `APPEND_SLASH`"

msgid ""
"In 0.96, if a URL didn't end in a slash or have a period in the final "
"component of its path, and :setting:`APPEND_SLASH` was True, Django would "
"redirect to the same URL, but with a slash appended to the end. Now, Django "
"checks to see whether the pattern without the trailing slash would be "
"matched by something in your URL patterns. If so, no redirection takes "
"place, because it is assumed you deliberately wanted to catch that pattern."
msgstr ""
"I 0.96, mura raibh deireadh le URL i slash nó mura raibh tréimhse aige sa "
"chomhpháirt dheiridh dá chonair, agus:setting: 'APPEND_SLASH` Fíor, "
"atreoródh Django chuig an URL céanna, ach le slash curtha leis an deireadh. "
"Anois, seiceálann Django chun a fheiceáil an mbeadh rud éigin i do phatrúin "
"URL comhoiriúnach leis an bpatrún gan an slash rianaithe. Más ea, ní "
"dhéantar aon athatreorú, toisc go nglactar leis go raibh tú ag iarraidh an "
"patrún sin a ghabháil d'aon ghnó."

msgid ""
"For most people, this won't require any changes. Some people, though, have "
"URL patterns that look like this::"
msgstr ""
"Maidir le formhór na ndaoine, ní bheidh aon athruithe ag teastáil ó seo. Mar "
"sin féin, tá patrúin URL ag daoine áirithe a bhfuil cuma seo orthu:"

msgid ""
"Previously, those patterns would have been redirected to have a trailing "
"slash. If you always want a slash on such URLs, rewrite the pattern as::"
msgstr ""
"Roimhe seo, bheadh na patrúin sin a atreorú chun slasc rianaithe a bheith "
"acu. Más mian leat slash i gcónaí ar URLanna den sórt sin, athscríobh an "
"patrún mar:"

msgid "Smaller model changes"
msgstr "Athruithe samhail níos lú"

msgid "Different exception from ``get()``"
msgstr "Eisceacht difriúil ó ``get () ``"

msgid ""
"Managers now return a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.MultipleObjectsReturned` "
"exception instead of :exc:`AssertionError`:"
msgstr ""
"Tugann bainisteoirí ar ais anois eisceacht a:exc: "
"`~Django.Core.Exceptions.MultipleObjectsReturned` in ionad:exc: "
"`AssertionError`:"

msgid "``LazyDate`` has been fired"
msgstr "Scaoileadh ``LazyDate``"

msgid "The ``LazyDate`` helper class no longer exists."
msgstr "Níl an rang cúntóra ``LazyDate`` ann a thuilleadh."

msgid ""
"Default field values and query arguments can both be callable objects, so "
"instances of ``LazyDate`` can be replaced with a reference to "
"``datetime.datetime.now``:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir luachanna réamhshocraithe réimse agus argóintí fiosrúcháin a "
"bheith ina rudaí inghlaonta, mar sin is féidir tagairt do "
"`datetime.datetime.now`` a chur in ionad cásanna ``LazyDate``:"

msgid "``DecimalField`` is new, and ``FloatField`` is now a proper float"
msgstr ""
"Tá ``Decimalfield`` nua, agus is snámhphointe ceart anois é ``Floatfield``"

msgid ""
"If you forget to make this change, you will see errors about ``FloatField`` "
"not taking a ``max_digits`` attribute in ``__init__``, because the new "
"``FloatField`` takes no precision-related arguments."
msgstr ""
"Má dhéanann tú dearmad an t-athrú seo a dhéanamh, feicfidh tú earráidí faoi "
"``Floatfield`` gan tréith ``max_digits`` a ghlacadh i ``__init__``, toisc "
"nach nglacann an ``Floatfield`` nua aon argóintí a bhaineann le cruinneas."

msgid ""
"If you're using MySQL or PostgreSQL, no further changes are needed. The "
"database column types for ``DecimalField`` are the same as for the old "
"``FloatField``."
msgstr ""
"Má tá MySQL nó PostgreSQL á úsáid agat, níl aon athruithe breise ag "
"teastáil. Tá na cineálacha colún bunachar sonraí le haghaidh "
"``Decimalfield`` mar an gcéanna leis an sean-``Floatfield``."

msgid ""
"If you're using SQLite, you need to force the database to view the "
"appropriate columns as decimal types, rather than floats. To do this, you'll "
"need to reload your data. Do this after you have made the change to using "
"``DecimalField`` in your code and updated the Django code."
msgstr ""
"Má tá SQLite á úsáid agat, ní mór duit an bunachar sonraí a chur i bhfeidhm "
"ar na colúin chuí mar chineálacha deachúil, seachas snámha. Chun seo a "
"dhéanamh, beidh ort do chuid sonraí a athluchtú. Déan é seo tar éis duit an "
"t-athrú a dhéanamh ar `Decimalfield` a úsáid i do chód agus an cód Django a "
"nuashonrú."

msgid "**Back up your database first!**"
msgstr "** Cuir cúltaca ar do bhunachar sonraí ar dtús! **"

msgid ""
"For SQLite, this means making a copy of the single file that stores the "
"database (the name of that file is the ``DATABASE_NAME`` in your "
"``settings.py`` file)."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le SQLite, ciallaíonn sé seo cóip a dhéanamh den chomhad aonair a "
"stóráilíonn an bunachar sonraí (is é ainm an chomhaid sin an "
"`DATABASE_NAME`` i do chomhad ``settings.py``)."

msgid ""
"To upgrade each application to use a ``DecimalField``, you can do the "
"following, replacing ``<app>`` in the code below with each app's name:"
msgstr ""
"Chun gach feidhmchlár a uasghrádú chun ``Decimalfield` a úsáid, is féidir "
"leat an méid seo a leanas a dhéanamh, agus ainm gach aip in ionad ```sa chód "
"th <app>íos:"

msgid "Notes:"
msgstr "Nótaí:"

msgid ""
"It's important that you remember to use XML format in the first step of this "
"process. We are exploiting a feature of the XML data dumps that makes "
"porting floats to decimals with SQLite possible."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé tábhachtach go gcuimhneoidh tú formáid XML a úsáid sa chéad chéim den "
"phróiseas seo. Táimid ag baint leas as gné de na dumpaí sonraí XML a fhágann "
"gur féidir snámha a iompar go deachmhálacha le SQLite."

msgid ""
"In the second step you will be asked to confirm that you are prepared to "
"lose the data for the application(s) in question. Say yes; we'll restore "
"this data in the third step."
msgstr ""
"Sa dara céim iarrfar ort a dhearbhú go bhfuil tú ullmhaithe chun na sonraí a "
"chailleadh don iarratas (í) atá i gceist. Abair tá; cuirfimid na sonraí seo "
"ar ais sa tríú céim."

msgid ""
"``DecimalField`` is not used in any of the apps shipped with Django prior to "
"this change being made, so you do not need to worry about performing this "
"procedure for any of the standard Django models."
msgstr ""
"Ní úsáidtear ``Decimalfield`` in aon cheann de na feidhmchláir a sheoltar le "
"Django sula ndéantar an t-athrú seo, mar sin ní gá duit a bheith buartha "
"faoin nós imeachta seo a dhéanamh d'aon cheann de na samhlacha caighdeánacha "
"Django."

msgid ""
"If something goes wrong in the above process, just copy your backed up "
"database file over the original file and start again."
msgstr ""
"Má théann rud éigin mícheart sa phróiseas thuas, níl le déanamh ach cóipeáil "
"do bhunachar sonraí cúltaca thar an mbunchomhad agus tosú arís."

msgid "Internationalization"
msgstr "Idirnáisiúnú"

msgid ":func:`django.views.i18n.set_language` now requires a POST request"
msgstr ":func: Éilíonn `django.views.i18n.set_language` iarratas POST anois"

msgid ""
"Previously, a GET request was used. The old behavior meant that state (the "
"locale used to display the site) could be changed by a GET request, which is "
"against the HTTP specification's recommendations. Code calling this view "
"must ensure that a POST request is now made, instead of a GET. This means "
"you can no longer use a link to access the view, but must use a form "
"submission of some kind (e.g. a button)."
msgstr ""
"Roimhe seo, úsáideadh iarratas GET. Chiallaigh an sean-iompar go bhféadfaí "
"stát (an áitiúil a úsáidtear chun an suíomh a thaispeáint) a athrú trí "
"iarratas GET, atá i gcoinne moltaí na sonraíochta HTTP. Caithfidh an cód a "
"ghlaonn an dearcadh seo a chinntiú go ndéantar iarratas POST anois, in ionad "
"GET. Ciallaíonn sé seo nach féidir leat nasc a úsáid a thuilleadh chun "
"rochtain a fháil ar an radharc, ach caithfidh tú aighneacht foirme de "
"chineál éigin a úsáid (m.sh. cnaipe)."

msgid "``_()`` is no longer in builtins"
msgstr "Níl `_ () ``i dtógáin a thuilleadh"

msgid ""
"``_()`` (the callable object whose name is a single underscore) is no longer "
"monkeypatched into builtins -- that is, it's no longer available magically "
"in every module."
msgstr ""
"Ní dhéantar `_ () ``(an réad inghlaonta a bhfuil a ainm béim amháin aige) a "
"thuilleadh isteach i dtógáin - is é sin, níl sé ar fáil go draíochta i ngach "
"modúl a thuilleadh."

msgid ""
"If you were previously relying on ``_()`` always being present, you should "
"now explicitly import ``ugettext`` or ``ugettext_lazy``, if appropriate, and "
"alias it to ``_`` yourself::"
msgstr ""
"Má bhí tú ag brath roimhe seo ar `_ () ``a bheith i láthair i gcónaí, ba "
"cheart duit ``ugettext`` nó ``ugettext_lazy`` a iompórtáil go sainráite "
"anois, más cuí, agus é a ainmhairiú chuig `_`` duit féin:"

msgid "HTTP request/response objects"
msgstr "Réadanna iarrata/freagartha HTTP"

msgid "Dictionary access to ``HttpRequest``"
msgstr "Rochtain ar an bhfoclóir ar `HttpRequest``"

msgid ""
"``HttpRequest`` objects no longer directly support dictionary-style access; "
"previously, both ``GET`` and ``POST`` data were directly available on the "
"``HttpRequest`` object (e.g., you could check for a piece of form data by "
"using ``if 'some_form_key' in request`` or by reading "
"``request['some_form_key']``. This is no longer supported; if you need "
"access to the combined ``GET`` and ``POST`` data, use ``request.REQUEST`` "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"Ní thacaíonn rudaí `HttpRequest`` le rochtain ar stíl fhoclóra a thuilleadh; "
"roimhe seo, bhí sonraí ``GET`` agus `POST ``ar fáil go díreach ar an réad "
"`HttpRequest`` (m.sh., d'fhéadfá píosa sonraí foirme a sheiceáil trí `if "
"'some_form_key' a úsáid in iarrat`` nó trí `request ['some_form_key']. Ní "
"thacaítear leis seo a thuilleadh; má theastaíonn rochtain uait ar na sonraí "
"comhcheangailte ``GET`` agus `POST ``, bain úsáid as ``Request.request`` ina "
"ionad."

msgid ""
"It is strongly suggested, however, that you always explicitly look in the "
"appropriate dictionary for the type of request you expect to receive "
"(``request.GET`` or ``request.POST``); relying on the combined "
"``request.REQUEST`` dictionary can mask the origin of incoming data."
msgstr ""
"Moltar go láidir, áfach, go bhféachann tú go sainráite sa fhoclóir cuí i "
"gcónaí don chineál iarratais a bhfuil súil agat a fháil (``Request.Get`` nó "
"``Request.Post``); ag brath ar an bhfoclóir comhcheangailte "
"``request.request`` is féidir bunús na sonraí atá ag teacht isteach a masc."

msgid "Accessing ``HTTPResponse`` headers"
msgstr "Rochtain a fháil ar cheanntásca `HttpResponse``"

msgid ""
"``django.http.HttpResponse.headers`` has been renamed to ``_headers`` "
"and :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse` now supports containment checking "
"directly. So use ``if header in response:`` instead of ``if header in "
"response.headers:``."
msgstr ""
"Athainmníodh ``Django.http.httpResponse.Headers`` go ``_headers`` "
"agus:class: `~django.http.http.httpResponse` tacaíonn anois le seiceáil "
"srianta go díreach. Mar sin bain úsáid as `if ceannteideal mar fhreagra: "
"``in ionad ``if ceannteideal i freagra.heads:``."

msgid "Generic relations"
msgstr "Caidreamh cineálach"

msgid "Generic relations have been moved out of core"
msgstr "Tá caidreamh cineálach aistrithe as croílár"

msgid ""
"The generic relation classes -- ``GenericForeignKey`` and "
"``GenericRelation`` -- have moved into "
"the :mod:`django.contrib.contenttypes` module."
msgstr ""
"Tá na ranganna caidrimh chineálach -- `GenericForeignKey`` agus "
"`GenericRelation` -- tar éis bogadh isteach sa mhodúl:mod: "
"`django.contrib.contenttypes`."

msgid "Testing"
msgstr "Tástáil"

msgid ":meth:`django.test.Client.login` has changed"
msgstr ":meth: Tá athrú tagtha ag `django.test.client.login`"

msgid "Management commands"
msgstr "Orduithe bainistíochta"

msgid "Running management commands from your code"
msgstr "Orduithe bainistíochta a rith ó do chód"

msgid ":mod:`django.core.management` has been greatly refactored."
msgstr ":mod: Rinneadh athbhreithniú go mór ar `django.core.management`."

msgid ""
"Calls to management services in your code now need to use ``call_command``. "
"For example, if you have some test code that calls flush and load_data::"
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh glaonna chuig seirbhísí bainistíochta i do chód ``call_command ``a "
"úsáid anois. Mar shampla, má tá cód tástála éigin agat a ghlaonn flush agus "
"load_data::"

msgid "...you'll need to change this code to read::"
msgstr "... beidh ort an cód seo a athrú chun léamh:"

msgid "Subcommands must now precede options"
msgstr "Caithfidh fo-orduithe a bheith roimh roghanna anois"

msgid ""
"``django-admin.py`` and ``manage.py`` now require subcommands to precede "
"options. So:"
msgstr ""
"Éilíonn ``django-admin.py`` agus `manage.py`` fo-orduithe anois chun roimh "
"roghanna. Mar sin:"

msgid "...no longer works and should be changed to:"
msgstr "... ní oibríonn sé a thuilleadh agus ba chóir é a athrú go:"

msgid "Syndication"
msgstr "Sindeacáitiú"

msgid "``Feed.__init__`` has changed"
msgstr "``Beathú. __init__`` tá athrú tagtha"

msgid ""
"The ``__init__()`` method of the syndication framework's ``Feed`` class now "
"takes an ``HttpRequest`` object as its second parameter, instead of the "
"feed's URL. This allows the syndication framework to work without requiring "
"the sites framework. This only affects code that subclasses ``Feed`` and "
"overrides the ``__init__()`` method, and code that calls ``Feed.__init__()`` "
"directly."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an modh ``__init__ () ``de rang ``Feed`` chreat shiondícithe réad "
"``HttpRequest`` anois mar a dara paraiméadar, in ionad URL an bheatha. "
"Ligeann sé seo don chreat siondicíochta oibriú gan creat na suíomhanna a "
"bheith ag teastáil. Ní théann sé seo ach ar an gcód a dhéanann fo-aicmí "
"``Feed ``agus a sháraíonn an modh ``__init__ ()``, agus an cód a ghlaonn "
"``Feed. __init__ () ``go díreach."

msgid "Data structures"
msgstr "Struchtúir sonraí"

msgid "``SortedDictFromList`` is gone"
msgstr "Tá ``Sorteddictfromlist`` imithe"

msgid ""
"``django.newforms.forms.SortedDictFromList`` was removed. "
"``django.utils.datastructures.SortedDict`` can now be instantiated with a "
"sequence of tuples."
msgstr ""
"Baineadh ``django.newforms.forms.sorteddictfromlist``. Is féidir "
"``Django.Utils.DataStructures.SortedDict`` a ionchasadh anois le seicheamh "
"tuples."

msgid "To update your code:"
msgstr "Chun do chód a nuashonrú:"

msgid ""
"Use ``django.utils.datastructures.SortedDict`` wherever you were using "
"``django.newforms.forms.SortedDictFromList``."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid ``Django.Utils.DataStructures.SortedDict`` cibé áit a raibh tú ag "
"úsáid ``Django.NewForms.Forms.SortedDictFromList``."

msgid ""
"Because ``django.utils.datastructures.SortedDict.copy`` doesn't return a "
"deepcopy as ``SortedDictFromList.copy()`` did, you will need to update your "
"code if you were relying on a deepcopy. Do this by using ``copy.deepcopy`` "
"directly."
msgstr ""
"Toisc nach dtugann `Django.utils.DataStructures.SortedDict.copy`` doimhchóip "
"ar ais mar a rinne ``SortedDictFromList.copy () `, beidh ort do chód a "
"nuashonrú má bhí tú ag brath ar dhoimhchóip. Déan é seo trí `copy.deepcopy`` "
"a úsáid go díreach."

