msgid "Django 1.0.1 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoileadh Django 1.0.1"

msgid "Welcome to Django 1.0.1!"
msgstr "Fáilte go dtí Django 1.0.1!"

msgid ""
"This is the first \"bugfix\" release in the Django 1.0 series, improving the "
"stability and performance of the Django 1.0 codebase. As such, Django 1.0.1 "
"contains no new features (and, pursuant to :doc:`our compatibility policy </"
"misc/api-stability/>`, maintains backwards compatibility with Django 1.0), "
"but does contain a number of fixes and other improvements. Django 1.0.1 is a "
"recommended upgrade for any development or deployment currently using or "
"targeting Django 1.0."
msgstr ""
"Is é seo an chéad eisiúint “bugfix” sa tsraith Django 1.0, ag feabhsú "
"cobhsaíocht agus feidhmíocht an chódbhuntáiste Django 1.0. Dá bhrí sin, níl "
"aon ghnéithe nua ag Django 1.0.1 (agus, de bhun: doc: `ár mbeartas "
"comhoiriúnachta `, coinníonn com</misc/api-stability/> hoiriúnacht ar ais le "
"Django 1.0), ach tá roinnt socruithe agus feabhsuithe eile ann. Is uasghrádú "
"molta é Django 1.0.1 d'aon fhorbairt nó imscaradh a úsáideann nó ag díriú ar "
"Django 1.0 faoi láthair."

msgid "Fixes and improvements in Django 1.0.1"
msgstr "Deartuithe agus feabhsuithe i Django 1.0.1"

msgid ""
"Django 1.0.1 contains over two hundred fixes to the original Django 1.0 "
"codebase; full details of every fix are available in `the history of the "
"1.0.X branch`_, but here are some of the highlights:"
msgstr ""
"Tá os cionn dhá chéad ceartú ag Django 1.0.1 ar an gclóid bunaidh Django "
"1.0; tá sonraí iomlána faoi gach socrú ar fáil i `stair an bhrainse 1.0.X`_, "
"ach seo cuid de na buaicphointí:"

msgid ""
"Several fixes in ``django.contrib.comments``, pertaining to RSS feeds of "
"comments, default ordering of comments and the XHTML and "
"internationalization of the default templates for comments."
msgstr ""
"Roinnt socruithe i ``django.contrib.comments``, a bhaineann le fothaí "
"tuairimí RSS, ordú réamhshocraithe tuairimí agus XHTML agus idirnáisiúnú na "
"dteimpléid réamhshocraithe le haghaidh tuairimí."

msgid ""
"Multiple fixes for Django's support of Oracle databases, including "
"pagination support for GIS QuerySets, more efficient slicing of results and "
"improved introspection of existing databases."
msgstr ""
"Socruithe iolracha do thacaíocht Django do bhunachair sonraí Oracle, lena n-"
"áirítear tacaíocht leathanaigh do QuerySets GIS, slisnú níos éifeachtaí "
"torthaí agus ionchúrsáil fheabhsaithe ar bhunachar sonraí atá ann cheana."

msgid ""
"Several fixes for query support in the Django object-relational mapper, "
"including repeated setting and resetting of ordering and fixes for working "
"with ``INSERT``-only queries."
msgstr ""
"Roinnt socruithe le haghaidh tacaíochta ceisteanna i léarscáil réad gaolmhar "
"Django, lena n-áirítear socrú agus athshocrú arís agus athshocrú ordú agus "
"socruithe chun oibriú le ceisteanna ``Ionsáil ``amháin."

msgid "Multiple fixes for inline forms in formsets."
msgstr "Socruithe iolracha d'fhoirmeacha inlíne i bhfoirmeacha."

msgid ""
"Multiple fixes for ``unique`` and ``unique_together`` model constraints in "
"automatically-generated forms."
msgstr ""
"Socruithe iolracha le haghaidh srianta samhail ``unique`` agus "
"``unique_together ``i bhfoirmeacha a ghintear go huathoibríoch."

msgid ""
"Fixed support for custom callable ``upload_to`` declarations when handling "
"file uploads through automatically-generated forms."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíocht sheasta le haghaidh dearbhuithe saincheaptha ``upload_` inghlaonta "
"agus uaslódálacha comhaid á láimhseáil trí fhoirmeacha a ghintear go "
"huathoibríoch."

msgid ""
"Fixed support for sorting an admin change list based on a callable "
"attributes in ``list_display``."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíocht sheasta chun liosta athraithe riaracháin a shórtáil bunaithe ar "
"thréithe inghlaonta i `list_display``."

msgid ""
"A fix to the application of autoescaping for literal strings passed to the "
"``join`` template filter. Previously, literal strings passed to ``join`` "
"were automatically escaped, contrary to :ref:`the documented behavior for "
"autoescaping and literal strings <string-literals-and-automatic-escaping>`. "
"Literal strings passed to ``join`` are no longer automatically escaped, "
"meaning you must now manually escape them; this is an incompatibility if you "
"were relying on this bug, but not if you were relying on escaping behaving "
"as documented."
msgstr ""
"Socrú ar chur i bhfeidhm uathoibríoch le haghaidh teaghráin litriúla a "
"chuirtear chuig an scagaire teimpléad ``join`. <string-literals-and-"
"automatic-escaping>Roimhe seo, éaladh go huathoibríoch na teaghráin "
"liteartha a chuirtear chuig ``comhpháirtíoch`, i gcoinne na:ref: `an t-"
"iompar doiciméadaithe le haghaidh autoescaping agus teaghráin litriúla `. Ní "
"éalaíonn teaghráin litriúla a chuirtear chuig ``comhpháirti`` go "
"huathoibríoch a thuilleadh, rud a chiallaíonn go gcaithfidh tú éalú de láimh "
"anois; is neamhchomhoiriúnacht é seo má bhí tú ag brath ar an fabht seo, ach "
"ní dá raibh tú ag brath ar iompar éalaithe mar a dhoiciméadaithe."

msgid ""
"Improved and expanded translation files for many of the languages Django "
"supports by default."
msgstr ""
"Comhaid aistriúcháin feabhsaithe agus leathnaithe do go leor de na teangacha "
"a dtacaíonn Django leo de réir réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"And as always, a large number of improvements to Django's documentation, "
"including both corrections to existing documents and expanded and new "
"documentation."
msgstr ""
"Agus mar i gcónaí, líon mór feabhsuithe ar dhoiciméadú Django, lena n-"
"áirítear ceartúcháin ar dhoiciméid atá ann cheana agus doiciméadú "
"leathnaithe agus nua."

msgid "Django 1.0.2 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.0.2"

msgid "Welcome to Django 1.0.2!"
msgstr "Fáilte go Django 1.0.2!"

msgid ""
"This is the second \"bugfix\" release in the Django 1.0 series, improving "
"the stability and performance of the Django 1.0 codebase. As such, Django "
"1.0.2 contains no new features (and, pursuant to :doc:`our compatibility "
"policy </misc/api-stability>`, maintains backwards compatibility with Django "
"1.0.0), but does contain a number of fixes and other improvements. Django "
"1.0.2 is a recommended upgrade for any development or deployment currently "
"using or targeting Django 1.0."
msgstr ""
"Is é seo an dara scaoileadh “bugfix” sa tsraith Django 1.0, ag feabhsú "
"cobhsaíocht agus feidhmíocht an chódabhais Django 1.0. Dá bhrí sin, níl aon "
"ghnéithe nua ag Django 1.0.2 (agus, de bhun: doc: `ár mbeartas "
"comhoiriúnachtachta `, coimeádann comhoiriúnach</misc/api-stability> t ar "
"ais le Django 1.0.0), ach tá roinnt socruithe agus feabhsuithe eile ann. Is "
"uasghrádú molta é Django 1.0.2 d'aon fhorbairt nó imscaradh a úsáideann nó "
"ag díriú ar Django 1.0 faoi láthair."

msgid "Fixes and improvements in Django 1.0.2"
msgstr "Deartuithe agus feabhsuithe i Django 1.0.2"

msgid ""
"The primary reason behind this release is to remedy an issue in the recently-"
"released Django 1.0.1; the packaging scripts used for Django 1.0.1 omitted "
"some directories from the final release package, including one directory "
"required by ``django.contrib.gis`` and part of Django's unit-test suite."
msgstr ""
"Is é an príomhchúis atá taobh thiar den scaoileadh seo ná saincheist sa "
"Django 1.0.1 a eisíodh le déanaí a leigheas; d'fhág na scripteanna "
"pacáistithe a úsáidtear do Django 1.0.1 roinnt eolairí ón bpacáiste scaoilte "
"deiridh, lena n-áirítear eolaire amháin a theastaíonn ag "
"``django.contrib.gis`` agus cuid de shraith tástála aonaid Django."

msgid ""
"Django 1.0.2 contains updated packaging scripts, and the release package "
"contains the directories omitted from Django 1.0.1. As such, this release "
"contains all of the fixes and improvements from Django 1.0.1; see :doc:`the "
"Django 1.0.1 release notes </releases/1.0.1>` for details."
msgstr ""
"Tá scripteanna pacáistithe nuashonraithe i Django 1.0.2, agus tá na heolairí "
"a fhágtar as Django 1.0.1 sa phacáiste scaoilte. Mar sin, tá na socruithe "
"agus na feabhsuithe go léir ó Django 1.0.1 sa eisiúint seo; féach: doc: "
"`nótaí scaoilte Django 1.0.1 </releases/1.0.1> le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid "Additionally, in the period since Django 1.0.1 was released:"
msgstr "Ina theannta sin, sa tréimhse ó scaoileadh Django 1.0.1:"

msgid "Updated Hebrew and Danish translations have been added."
msgstr "Tá aistriúcháin nuashonraithe Eabhrais agus Danmhairgis curtha leis."

msgid ""
"The default ``__repr__`` method of Django models has been made more robust "
"in the face of bad Unicode data coming from the ``__unicode__`` method; "
"rather than raise an exception in such cases, ``repr()`` will now contain "
"the string \"[Bad Unicode data]\" in place of the invalid Unicode."
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh an modh réamhshocraithe ``__repr__`` de mhúnlaí Django níos láidre "
"i bhfianaise droch-shonraí Unicode a thagann ón modh ``__unicode__``; "
"seachas eisceacht a ardú i gcásanna den sórt sin, beidh an teaghrán “[Bad "
"Unicode data]” anois in ionad an Unicode neamhbhailí."

msgid ""
"A bug involving the interaction of Django's ``SafeUnicode`` class and the "
"MySQL adapter has been resolved; ``SafeUnicode`` instances (generated, for "
"example, by template rendering) can now be assigned to model attributes and "
"saved to MySQL without requiring an explicit intermediate cast to "
"``unicode``."
msgstr ""
"Réiteadh fabht a bhaineann le hidirghníomhaíocht rang ``SafeUnicode`` Django "
"agus an cuibheoir MySQL; is féidir cásanna ``SafeUnicode`` (a ghintear, mar "
"shampla, trí rindreáil teimpléad) a shannadh anois do thréithe samhail agus "
"a shábháil go MySQL gan teilgthe idirmheánach follasach a theastaíonn go "
"`unicode``."

msgid ""
"A bug affecting filtering on a nullable ``DateField`` in SQLite has been "
"resolved."
msgstr ""
"Réitíodh fabht a théann i bhfeidhm ar scagadh ar ``Datefield`` neamhnaithe i "
"SQLite."

msgid ""
"Several updates and improvements have been made to Django's documentation."
msgstr "Rinneadh roinnt nuashonruithe agus feabhsuithe ar dhoiciméadú Django."

msgid "Django 1.1 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.1"

msgid "July 29, 2009"
msgstr "29 Iúil, 2009"

msgid "Welcome to Django 1.1!"
msgstr "Fáilte go dtí Django 1.1!"

msgid ""
"Django 1.1 includes a number of nifty :ref:`new features <whats-new-1.1>`, "
"lots of bug fixes, and an easy upgrade path from Django 1.0."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn Django 1.1 roinnt nifty:ref: `gnéithe nua <whats-new-1.1>`, go "
"leor socruithe fabht, agus cosán uasghrádaithe éasca ó Django 1.0."

msgid "Backwards-incompatible changes in 1.1"
msgstr "Athruithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha ar chúl i 1.1"

msgid ""
"Django has a policy of :doc:`API stability </misc/api-stability>`. This "
"means that, in general, code you develop against Django 1.0 should continue "
"to work against 1.1 unchanged. However, we do sometimes make backwards-"
"incompatible changes if they're necessary to resolve bugs, and there are a "
"handful of such (minor) changes between Django 1.0 and Django 1.1."
msgstr ""
"Tá beartas ag Django de:doc: `Cobhsaíocht API` </misc/api-stability>. "
"Ciallaíonn sé seo gur chóir go leanfadh cód a fhorbraíonn tú i gcoinne "
"Django 1.0 ag obair i gcoinne 1.1 gan athrú. Mar sin féin, déanaimid "
"athruithe neamhchomhoiriúnacha ar chúl uaireanta má tá siad riachtanach chun "
"fabhtanna a réiteach, agus tá dornán athruithe den sórt sin (mion) idir "
"Django 1.0 agus Django 1.1."

msgid ""
"Before upgrading to Django 1.1 you should double-check that the following "
"changes don't impact you, and upgrade your code if they do."
msgstr ""
"Sula n-uasghrádú a dhéanamh go Django 1.1 ba chóir duit seiceáil faoi dhó "
"nach mbíonn tionchar ag na hathruithe seo a leanas ort, agus do chód a "
"uasghrádú má dhéanann siad."

msgid "Changes to constraint names"
msgstr "Athruithe ar ainmneacha srianta"

msgid ""
"Django 1.1 modifies the method used to generate database constraint names so "
"that names are consistent regardless of machine word size. This change is "
"backwards incompatible for some users."
msgstr ""
"Athraíonn Django 1.1 an modh a úsáidtear chun ainmneacha srianta bunachar "
"sonraí a ghiniúint ionas go mbeidh ainmneacha comhsheasmhach beag beann ar "
"mhéid focal Níl an t-athrú seo ag teacht ar ais do roinnt úsáideoirí."

msgid ""
"If you are using a 32-bit platform, you're off the hook; you'll observe no "
"differences as a result of this change."
msgstr ""
"Má tá ardán 32-giotán á úsáid agat, tá tú as an crúca; ní bhreathnóidh tú "
"aon difríochtaí mar thoradh ar an athrú seo."

msgid ""
"However, **users on 64-bit platforms may experience some problems** using "
"the ``reset`` management command. Prior to this change, 64-bit platforms "
"would generate a 64-bit, 16 character digest in the constraint name; for "
"example:"
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, d'fhéadfadh go mbeadh roinnt fadhbanna** ag úsáideoirí ar "
"ardáin 64-giotán** ag baint úsáide as an ordú bainistíochta ``athshocraí` "
"Roimh an athrú seo, ginearfadh ardáin 64-giotán díleá 64-giotán, 16 "
"charachtar san ainm srianta; mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"Following this change, all platforms, regardless of word size, will generate "
"a 32-bit, 8 character digest in the constraint name; for example:"
msgstr ""
"Tar éis an athraithe seo, ginfidh gach ardán, beag beann ar mhéid an "
"fhocail, díleá 32-giotán, 8 charachtar san ainm srianta; mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"As a result of this change, you will not be able to use the ``reset`` "
"management command on any table made by a 64-bit machine. This is because "
"the new generated name will not match the historically generated name; as a "
"result, the SQL constructed by the reset command will be invalid."
msgstr ""
"Mar thoradh ar an athrú seo, ní bheidh tú in ann an t-ordú bainistíochta "
"``reset ``a úsáid ar aon tábla a dhéanann meaisín 64-giotán. Tá sé seo toisc "
"nach n-oireann an t-ainm nua a ghintear leis an ainm a ghintear go "
"stairiúil; mar thoradh air sin, beidh an SQL a thógtar leis an ordú "
"athshocraithe neamhbhailí."

msgid ""
"If you need to reset an application that was created with 64-bit "
"constraints, you will need to manually drop the old constraint prior to "
"invoking ``reset``."
msgstr ""
"Más gá duit feidhmchlár a cruthaíodh le srianta 64-giotán a athshocrú, beidh "
"ort an sean-srian a scaoileadh de láimh sula n-iarrtar ar ``athshocraí`."

msgid "Test cases are now run in a transaction"
msgstr "Déantar cásanna tástála a reáchtáil anois in idirbheart"

msgid ""
"Django 1.1 runs tests inside a transaction, allowing better test performance "
"(see `test performance improvements`_ for details)."
msgstr ""
"Ritheann Django 1.1 tástálacha taobh istigh d'idirbheart, rud a cheadaíonn "
"feidhmíocht tástála níos fearr (féach `feabhsuithe feidhmíochta tástála`_ le "
"haghaidh sonraí)."

msgid ""
"This change is slightly backwards incompatible if existing tests need to "
"test transactional behavior, if they rely on invalid assumptions about the "
"test environment, or if they require a specific test case ordering."
msgstr ""
"Tá an t-athrú seo beagán ar gcúl neamh-chomhoiriúnach más gá do thástálacha "
"atá ann cheana iompar idirbheartaíochta a thástáil, má bhíonn siad ag brath "
"ar thoimhdí neamhbhailí faoin timpeallacht tástála, nó má theastaíonn ordú "
"cás tástála sonrach uathu."

msgid ""
"For these cases, :class:`~django.test.TransactionTestCase` can be used "
"instead. This is a just a quick fix to get around test case errors revealed "
"by the new rollback approach; in the long-term tests should be rewritten to "
"correct the test case."
msgstr ""
"Maidir leis na cásanna seo, is féidir :class: "
"`~django.test.transactionTestCase` a úsáid ina ionad. Níl anseo ach socrú "
"tapa chun timpeall ar earráidí cásanna tástála a nochtann an cur chuige "
"athiompaithe nua; sna tástálacha fadtéarmacha ba cheart iad a athscríobh "
"chun an cás tástála a cheartú."

msgid "Removed ``SetRemoteAddrFromForwardedFor`` middleware"
msgstr "Bainte ``SetRemoteAddrfromForWardedFor`` middleware"

msgid ""
"For convenience, Django 1.0 included an optional middleware class -- "
"``django.middleware.http.SetRemoteAddrFromForwardedFor`` -- which updated "
"the value of ``REMOTE_ADDR`` based on the HTTP ``X-Forwarded-For`` header "
"commonly set by some proxy configurations."
msgstr ""
"Ar mhaithe le áisiúlacht, chuimsíonn Django 1.0 rang roghnach middleware - "
"``Django.middleware.http.setRemoteAddrFromForwardedFor`` - a nuashonraigh "
"luach ``REMOTE_ADDR`` bunaithe ar an gceannteideal HTTP ``X-Forwarded-For`` "
"a shocraíonn go coitianta ag roinnt cumraíochtaí seachfhreastalaí."

msgid ""
"It has been demonstrated that this mechanism cannot be made reliable enough "
"for general-purpose use, and that (despite documentation to the contrary) "
"its inclusion in Django may lead application developers to assume that the "
"value of ``REMOTE_ADDR`` is \"safe\" or in some way reliable as a source of "
"authentication."
msgstr ""
"Léiríodh nach féidir an meicníocht seo a dhéanamh iontaofa go leor le húsáid "
"ghinearálta, agus go bhféadfadh forbróirí feidhmchláir glacadh leis go "
"bhfuil luach `REMOTE_ADDR` “sábháilte” nó iontaofa ar bhealach éigin "
"iontaofa mar fhoinse fíordheimhnithe."

msgid ""
"While not directly a security issue, we've decided to remove this middleware "
"with the Django 1.1 release. It has been replaced with a class that does "
"nothing other than raise a ``DeprecationWarning``."
msgstr ""
"Cé nach saincheist slándála é go díreach, shocraigh muid an middleware seo a "
"bhaint leis an scaoileadh Django 1.1. Cuireadh rang a chur in ionad air nach "
"ndéanann aon rud seachas ``DeprecationWarning`` a ardú."

msgid "If you've been relying on this middleware, the easiest upgrade path is:"
msgstr ""
"Má bhí tú ag brath ar an meán-earraí seo, is é an cosán uasghrádaithe is "
"éasca:"

msgid "Examine `the code as it existed before it was removed`__."
msgstr "Scrúdaigh `an cód mar a bhí ann sula mbainíodh é `__."

msgid ""
"Verify that it works correctly with your upstream proxy, modifying it to "
"support your particular proxy (if necessary)."
msgstr ""
"Deimhnigh go n-oibríonn sé i gceart le do sheachfhreastalaí "
"réamhtheachtacha, agus modhnaigh é chun tacú le do sheachfhreastalaí ar "
"leith (más gá)."

msgid ""
"Introduce your modified version of ``SetRemoteAddrFromForwardedFor`` as a "
"piece of middleware in your own project."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair isteach do leagan modhnaithe de ``SetRemoteAdDrFromForWardedFor`` "
"mar phíosa meán-earraí i do thionscadal féin."

msgid "Names of uploaded files are available later"
msgstr "Tá ainmneacha na gcomhaid uaslódáilte ar fáil"

msgid ""
"In Django 1.0, files uploaded and stored in a model's :class:`FileField` "
"were saved to disk before the model was saved to the database. This meant "
"that the actual file name assigned to the file was available before saving. "
"For example, it was available in a model's pre-save signal handler."
msgstr ""
"I Django 1.0, sábháladh comhaid a uaslódáil agus a stóráiltear i "
"samhail:class: `FileField` ar dhiosca sula sábháladh an tsamhail ar an "
"mbunachar sonraí. Chiallaigh sé seo go raibh ainm iarbhír an chomhaid a "
"shanntar don chomhad ar fáil sula sábháladh é. Mar shampla, bhí sé ar fáil i "
"láimhseálaí comhartha réamhshábhála samhail."

msgid ""
"In Django 1.1 the file is saved as part of saving the model in the database, "
"so the actual file name used on disk cannot be relied on until *after* the "
"model has been saved."
msgstr ""
"I Django 1.1 sábháltar an comhad mar chuid den tsamhail a shábháil sa "
"bhunachar sonraí, mar sin ní féidir brath ar an ainm comhaid iarbhír a "
"úsáidtear ar dhiosca go dt* go ndéantar an tsamhail a shábháil."

msgid "Changes to how model formsets are saved"
msgstr "Athruithe ar an gcaoi a sábháltar foirmeacha samhail"

msgid ""
"In Django 1.1, :class:`~django.forms.models.BaseModelFormSet` now calls "
"``ModelForm.save()``."
msgstr ""
"I Django 1.1, glaonn: class: `~Django.Forms.Models.BaseModelFormSet` anois "
"``ModelForm.save () ``."

msgid ""
"This is backwards-incompatible if you were modifying ``self.initial`` in a "
"model formset's ``__init__``, or if you relied on the internal "
"``_total_form_count`` or ``_initial_form_count`` attributes of BaseFormSet. "
"Those attributes are now public methods."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé seo comhoiriúnach ar ais má bhí tú ag modhnú ``self.initial`` i "
"``__init__`` foirmset samhail, nó má bhraith tú ar na tréithe inmheánacha "
"``_total_form_count`` nó ``_initial_form_count`` de BaseFormSet. Is modhanna "
"poiblí iad na tréithe sin anois."

msgid "Fixed the ``join`` filter's escaping behavior"
msgstr "Socraigh iompar éalaithe an scagaire ``comhoiriúnaí`"

msgid ""
"The :tfilter:`join` filter no longer escapes the literal value that is "
"passed in for the connector."
msgstr ""
"Ní éalaíonn an scagaire: TFilter: `join` an luach liteartha a chuirtear "
"isteach don chónascaire a thuilleadh."

msgid ""
"This is backwards incompatible for the special situation of the literal "
"string containing one of the five special HTML characters. Thus, if you were "
"writing ``{{ foo|join:\"&\" }}``, you now have to write ``{{ foo|join:\"&amp;"
"\" }}``."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé seo comhoiriúnach ar chúl do staid speisialta an teaghrán litriúil ina "
"bhfuil ceann de na cúig charachtar HTML speisialta. Mar sin, má bhí tú ag "
"scríobh ``{{foo|join: \"&”}}``, caithfidh tú anois ``{{foo|join: \"&”}}`` a "
"scríobh."

msgid ""
"The previous behavior was a bug and contrary to what was documented and "
"expected."
msgstr ""
"Ba fabht an t-iompar roimhe seo agus contrártha leis an méid a "
"doiciméadaíodh agus a raibh súil leis."

msgid "Permanent redirects and the ``redirect_to()`` generic view"
msgstr "Athreoruithe buana agus an radharc cineálach ``redirect_to () ``"

msgid ""
"Django 1.1 adds a ``permanent`` argument to the "
"``django.views.generic.simple.redirect_to()`` view. This is technically "
"backwards-incompatible if you were using the ``redirect_to`` view with a "
"format-string key called 'permanent', which is highly unlikely."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann Django 1.1 argóint ``permanent`` leis an radharc "
"``django.views.generic.simple.redirect_to () ``. Tá sé seo comhoiriúnach go "
"teicniúil ar ais má bhí tú ag úsáid an radharc ``redirect_to` le eochair "
"teaghrán formáide ar a dtugtar 'buan', rud nach dócha go mór."

msgid "Features deprecated in 1.1"
msgstr "Gnéithe atá díscríofa i 1.1"

msgid "One feature has been marked as deprecated in Django 1.1:"
msgstr "Tá gné amháin marcáilte mar dhíscríofa i Django 1.1:"

msgid ""
"You should no longer use ``AdminSite.root()`` to register that admin views. "
"That is, if your URLconf contains the line::"
msgstr ""
"Níor chóir duit `Adminsite.root () `a úsáid a thuilleadh chun na tuairimí "
"riaracháin sin a chlárú. Is é sin, má tá an líne i do URLConf:"

msgid "You should change it to read::"
msgstr "Ba chóir duit é a athrú chun léamh:"

msgid ""
"You should begin to remove use of this feature from your code immediately."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir duit tosú ag úsáid an ghné seo a bhaint as do chód láithreach."

msgid ""
"``AdminSite.root`` will raise a ``PendingDeprecationWarning`` if used in "
"Django 1.1. This warning is hidden by default. In Django 1.2, this warning "
"will be upgraded to a ``DeprecationWarning``, which will be displayed "
"loudly. Django 1.3 will remove ``AdminSite.root()`` entirely."
msgstr ""
"Ardóidh ``adminsite.root`` ``PendingDeprecationWarning`` má úsáidtear é i "
"Django 1.1. Tá an rabhadh seo i bhfolach de réir réamhshocrú. I Django 1.2, "
"déanfar an rabhadh seo a uasghrádú go ``DeprecationWarning``, a thaispeánfar "
"go hard. Bainfidh Django 1.3 ``adminsite.root () ``go hiomlán."

msgid ""
"For more details on our deprecation policies and strategy, see :doc:`/"
"internals/release-process`."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí faoinár mbeartais agus straitéis díghabhála, "
"féach:doc: `/internals/release-process`."

msgid "What's new in Django 1.1"
msgstr "Cad atá nua i Django 1.1"

msgid ""
"Quite a bit: since Django 1.0, we've made 1,290 code commits, fixed 1,206 "
"bugs, and added roughly 10,000 lines of documentation."
msgstr ""
"Go leor: ó Django 1.0, rinneamar 1,290 tiomantas cód, shocraigh muid 1,206 "
"fabht, agus chuireamar thart ar 10,000 líne doiciméadaithe leis."

msgid "The major new features in Django 1.1 are:"
msgstr "Is iad na príomhghnéithe nua i Django 1.1:"

msgid "ORM improvements"
msgstr "Feabhsuithe ORM"

msgid ""
"Two major enhancements have been added to Django's object-relational mapper "
"(ORM): aggregate support, and query expressions."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh dhá mhórfheabhsú le mapálaí réad-choibhneasta (ORM) Django: "
"tacaíocht chomhiomlán, agus nathanna fiosrúcháin."

msgid "Aggregate support"
msgstr "Tacaíocht chomhiomlán"

msgid ""
"It's now possible to run SQL aggregate queries (i.e. ``COUNT()``, ``MAX()``, "
"``MIN()``, etc.) from within Django's ORM. You can choose to either return "
"the results of the aggregate directly, or else annotate the objects in "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet` with the results of the "
"aggregate query."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir anois ceisteanna comhiomlána SQL a reáchtáil (ie ``COUNT () ``, "
"`MAX ()``, ``MIN () ``, srl.) ó laistigh de ORM Django. Is féidir leat a "
"roghnú torthaí an chomhiomlán a thabhairt ar ais go díreach, nó anótáil a "
"dhéanamh ar na rudaí in a:class: `~django.db.models.query.queryset` le "
"torthaí an cheistiúcháin chomhiomlán."

msgid ""
"This feature is available as "
"new :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.aggregate` "
"and :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.annotate` methods, and is "
"covered in detail in :doc:`the ORM aggregation documentation </topics/db/"
"aggregation>`."
msgstr ""
"Tá an ghné seo ar fáil mar mhodhanna nua:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.aggregate` agus:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.queryset.annotate`, agus tá sé clúdaithe go mion in:doc: "
"`an doiciméadú comhiomlán</topics/db/aggregation> aithe ORM`."

msgid "Query expressions"
msgstr "Nathanna fiosraithe"

msgid ""
"Queries can now refer to another field on the query and can traverse "
"relationships to refer to fields on related models. This is implemented in "
"the new :class:`~django.db.models.F` object; for full details, including "
"examples, consult the :class:`F expressions documentation "
"<django.db.models.F>`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le ceisteanna tagairt a dhéanamh anois do réimse eile ar an gceist "
"agus is féidir leo caidrimh a thrasú chun tagairt a dhéanamh do réimsí ar "
"mhúnlaí <django.db.models.F>Cuirtear é seo i bhfeidhm sa réad nua:class: "
"`~django.db.Models.f`; le haghaidh sonraí iomlána, lena n-áirítear samplaí, "
"téigh i gcomhairle la:class: `F expressions doiciméadach`."

msgid "Model improvements"
msgstr "Feabhsuithe samhail"

msgid "A number of features have been added to Django's model layer:"
msgstr "Cuireadh roinnt gnéithe le ciseal samhail Django:"

msgid "\"Unmanaged\" models"
msgstr "Múnlaí “neamh-bhainistithe”"

msgid ""
"You can now control whether or not Django manages the life-cycle of the "
"database tables for a model using the :attr:`~Options.managed` model option. "
"This defaults to ``True``, meaning that Django will create the appropriate "
"database tables in ``syncdb`` and remove them as part of the ``reset`` "
"command. That is, Django *manages* the database table's lifecycle."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat rialú anois cibé an mbainistíonn Django saolré na dtáblaí "
"bunachar sonraí do mhúnla ag baint úsáide as an rogha samhail: attr: "
"`~Options.managed`. Réamhshocraíonn sé seo go ``True``, rud a chiallaíonn go "
"gcruthóidh Django na táblaí bunachar sonraí cuí i `syncdb`` agus bainfidh sé "
"iad mar chuid den ordú ``reset``. Is é sin, bainistíonn Django* saolré an "
"tábla bunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"If you set this to ``False``, however, no database table creating or "
"deletion will be automatically performed for this model. This is useful if "
"the model represents an existing table or a database view that has been "
"created by some other means."
msgstr ""
"Má shocraíonn tú é seo go `False`, áfach, ní dhéanfar aon tábla bunachar "
"sonraí a chruthú nó a scriosadh go huathoibríoch don tsamhail seo. Tá sé seo "
"úsáideach má léiríonn an tsamhail tábla atá ann cheana nó dearcadh bunachar "
"sonraí a cruthaíodh ar bhealach éigin eile."

msgid ""
"For more details, see the documentation for the :attr:`~Options.managed` "
"option."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí, féach an doiciméadú don rogha: attr: "
"`~Options.managed`."

msgid "Proxy models"
msgstr "Múnlaí proxy"

msgid ""
"You can now create :ref:`proxy models <proxy-models>`: subclasses of "
"existing models that only add Python-level (rather than database-level) "
"behavior and aren't represented by a new table. That is, the new model is a "
"*proxy* for some underlying model, which stores all the real data."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat anois:ref: `seachfsamhlacha <proxy-models>`a chruthú anois: "
"fo-aicmí de mhúnlaí atá ann cheana nach gcuireann ach iompar ar leibhéal "
"Python (seachas leibhéal bunachar sonraí) agus nach léiríonn tábla nua iad. "
"Is é sin, is *proxy* é an tsamhail nua do roinnt samhail bhunúsach, a "
"stóráilíonn na sonraí fíor go léir."

msgid ""
"All the details can be found in the :ref:`proxy models documentation <proxy-"
"models>`. This feature is similar on the surface to unmanaged models, so the "
"documentation has an explanation of :ref:`how proxy models differ from "
"unmanaged models <proxy-vs-unmanaged-models>`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir na sonraí go léir a fháil sa :ref:`doiciméadú samhlacha "
"seachfhreastalaí <seachfhreastalaí-samhlacha>`. Tá an ghné seo cosúil ar an "
"dromchla le samhlacha neamhbhainistithe, agus mar sin tá míniú sa "
"cháipéisíocht ar :tag:`conas a dhifríonn samhlacha seachfhreastalaí ó "
"mhúnlaí neamhbhainistithe <proxy-vs-unmanaged-models>`."

msgid "Deferred fields"
msgstr "Réimsí iarchurtha"

msgid ""
"In some complex situations, your models might contain fields which could "
"contain a lot of data (for example, large text fields), or require expensive "
"processing to convert them to Python objects. If you know you don't need "
"those particular fields, you can now tell Django not to retrieve them from "
"the database."
msgstr ""
"I roinnt cásanna casta, d'fhéadfadh réimsí a bheith i do mhúnlaí a "
"d'fhéadfadh go leor sonraí a bheith ann (mar shampla, réimsí móra téacs), nó "
"a dteastaíonn próiseáil daor ag teastáil chun iad a thiontú go rudaí Python. "
"Má tá a fhios agat nach dteastaíonn na réimsí áirithe sin uait, is féidir "
"leat a rá anois do Django gan iad a aisghabháil ón mbunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"You'll do this with the new queryset "
"methods :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.defer` "
"and :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.only`."
msgstr ""
"Déanfaidh tú é seo leis na modhanna nua Queryset: meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.defer` agus:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.only`."

msgid "Testing improvements"
msgstr "Feabhsuithe tástála"

msgid ""
"A few notable improvements have been made to the :doc:`testing framework </"
"topics/testing/index>`."
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh roinnt feabhsuithe suntasacha ar: doc: `creat tástála</topics/"
"testing/index> '."

msgid "Test performance improvements"
msgstr "Feabhsúcháin feidhmíochta"

msgid ""
"Tests written using Django's :doc:`testing framework </topics/testing/"
"index>` now run dramatically faster (as much as 10 times faster in many "
"cases)."
msgstr ""
"Ritheann tástálacha atá scríofa ag baint úsáide as Django: Doc: `creat "
"tástála` go mór </topics/testing/index> níos gasta anois (chomh hard le 10 n-"
"uaire níos gasta i go leor cásanna)."

msgid ""
"This was accomplished through the introduction of transaction-based tests: "
"when using :class:`django.test.TestCase`, your tests will now be run in a "
"transaction which is rolled back when finished, instead of by flushing and "
"re-populating the database. This results in an immense speedup for most "
"types of unit tests. See the documentation for :class:`TestCase` "
"and :class:`TransactionTestCase` for a full description, and some important "
"notes on database support."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh i gcrích é seo trí thástálacha bunaithe ar idirbhearta a thabhairt "
"isteach: nuair a úsáidtear: class: `django.test.testcase`, reáchtálfar do "
"thástálacha anois in idirbheart a rolltar ar ais nuair a bheidh "
"críochnaithe, in ionad tríd an mbunachar sonraí a shruthlú agus a "
"athlíonadh. Mar thoradh air seo tá luas ollmhór ag an gcuid is mó de na "
"cineálacha tástálacha aonaid. Féach an doiciméadú le haghaidh: class: "
"`TestCase` agus:class: `TransactionTestCase` le haghaidh tuairisc iomlán, "
"agus roinnt nótaí tábhachtacha maidir le tacaíocht bunachar sonraí."

msgid "Test client improvements"
msgstr "Tástáil feabhsuithe cliant"

msgid ""
"A couple of small -- but highly useful -- improvements have been made to the "
"test client:"
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh cúpla feabhsúcháin bheaga - ach an-úsáideach - ar an gcliant "
"tástála:"

msgid ""
"The test :class:`Client` now can automatically follow redirects with the "
"``follow`` argument to :meth:`Client.get` and :meth:`Client.post`. This "
"makes testing views that issue redirects simpler."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leis an tástála:class: `Client` anois atreoruithe a leanúint go "
"huathoibríoch leis an argóint ``follow`` chuig:meth: `Client.get` agus:meth: "
"`Client.post`. Déanann sé seo tuairimí tástála a eisíonn atreoruithe níos "
"simplí."

msgid ""
"It's now easier to get at the template context in the response returned the "
"test client: you'll simply access the context as ``request.context[key]``. "
"The old way, which treats ``request.context`` as a list of contexts, one for "
"each rendered template in the inheritance chain, is still available if you "
"need it."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé níos éasca anois teacht ar chomhthéacs an teimpléid sa fhreagra a thug "
"an cliant tástála ar ais: ní bheidh tú ach rochtain ar an gcomhthéacs mar "
"``request.context [key] ``. Tá an seanbhealach, a dhéileálann le "
"``request.context`` mar liosta comhthéacsanna, ceann amháin do gach "
"teimpléad rindreáilte sa slabhra oidhreachta, ar fáil fós má theastaíonn sé "
"uait."

msgid "New admin features"
msgstr "Gnéithe nua riaracháin"

msgid ""
"Django 1.1 adds a couple of nifty new features to Django's admin interface:"
msgstr ""
"Cuireann Django 1.1 cúpla gné nua iontach le comhéadan riaracháin Django:"

msgid "Editable fields on the change list"
msgstr "Réimsí in-eagarthóireachta ar an liosta athraithe"

msgid ""
"You can now make fields editable on the admin list views via the "
"new :ref:`list_editable <admin-list-editable>` admin option. These fields "
"will show up as form widgets on the list pages, and can be edited and saved "
"in bulk."
msgstr ""
"<admin-list-editable>Is féidir leat réimsí a chur in eagar anois ar "
"thuairimí an liosta riaracháin tríd an rogha riaracháin nua:ref: "
"`list_editable `admin. Taispeánfar na réimsí seo mar ghuirléidí foirme ar na "
"leathanaigh liosta, agus is féidir iad a chur in eagar agus a shábháil ar an "
"mórchóir."

msgid "Admin \"actions\""
msgstr "“Gníomhartha” Riaracháin"

msgid ""
"You can now define :doc:`admin actions </ref/contrib/admin/actions>` that "
"can perform some action to a group of models in bulk. Users will be able to "
"select objects on the change list page and then apply these bulk actions to "
"all selected objects."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat a shainiú anois :doc: `gníomhaíochtaí admin </ref/contrib/"
"admin/actions>` ar féidir leo gníomh éigin a dhéanamh do ghrúpa samhlacha ar "
"an mórchóir. Beidh úsáideoirí in ann oibiachtaí a roghnú ar leathanach an "
"liosta athruithe agus ansin na gníomhartha toirtiúla seo a chur i bhfeidhm "
"ar gach réad roghnaithe."

msgid ""
"Django ships with one pre-defined admin action to delete a group of objects "
"in one fell swoop."
msgstr ""
"Seolann Django le gníomh riaracháin réamhshainithe amháin chun grúpa rudaí a "
"scriosadh i gcás amháin."

msgid "Conditional view processing"
msgstr "Próiseáil amharc coinníoll"

msgid ""
"Django now has much better support for :doc:`conditional view processing </"
"topics/conditional-view-processing>` using the standard ``ETag`` and ``Last-"
"Modified`` HTTP headers. This means you can now easily short-circuit view "
"processing by testing less-expensive conditions. For many views this can "
"lead to a serious improvement in speed and reduction in bandwidth."
msgstr ""
"Tá tacaíocht i bhfad níos fearr ag Django anois do :doc:`próiseáil amhairc "
"choinníollach </topics/conditional-view-processing>` ag baint úsáide as na "
"ceanntásca caighdeánacha ``ETag`` agus ``Last-Adified`` HTTP. Ciallaíonn sé "
"seo gur féidir leat próiseáil amhairc ghearrchiorcaid a phróiseáil go héasca "
"trí choinníollacha nach bhfuil chomh daor sin a thástáil. I gcás go leor "
"tuairimí is féidir go dtiocfadh feabhas mór ar luas agus laghdú ar "
"bandaleithead dá bharr."

msgid "URL namespaces"
msgstr "Spásanna ainmneacha URL"

msgid ""
"Django 1.1 improves :ref:`named URL patterns <naming-url-patterns>` with the "
"introduction of URL \"namespaces.\""
msgstr ""
"Feabhsaíonn Django 1.1: ref: `patrúin URL ainmnithe <naming-url-"
"patterns>`trí URL “spais ainmneacha” a thabhairt isteach."

msgid ""
"In short, this feature allows the same group of URLs, from the same "
"application, to be included in a Django URLConf multiple times, with varying "
"(and potentially nested) named prefixes which will be used when performing "
"reverse resolution. In other words, reusable applications like Django's "
"admin interface may be registered multiple times without URL conflicts."
msgstr ""
"I mbeagán focal, ceadaíonn an ghné seo an grúpa céanna URLanna, ón "
"bhfeidhmchlár céanna, a áireamh i URLConf Django arís agus arís eile, le "
"réamhfhoirmeacha ainmnithe éagsúla (agus a d'fhéadfadh a bheith neadaithe) a "
"úsáidfear agus réiteach droim á dhéanamh. Is é sin le rá, féadfar "
"feidhmchláir in-athúsáidte mar chomhéadan riaracháin Django a chlárú arís "
"agus arís eile gan coinbhleachtaí URL."

msgid ""
"For full details, see :ref:`the documentation on defining URL namespaces "
"<topics-http-defining-url-namespaces>`."
msgstr ""
"<topics-http-defining-url-namespaces>Le haghaidh sonraí iomlána, féach:ref: "
"`an doiciméadú maidir le spaisí ainmneacha URL a shainiú `."

msgid "GeoDjango"
msgstr "GeodJango"

msgid ""
"In Django 1.1, :doc:`GeoDjango </ref/contrib/gis/index>` (i.e. "
"``django.contrib.gis``) has several new features:"
msgstr ""
"I Django 1.1, :doc: `GeodJango` (ie ``django.contrib.gis`` </ref/contrib/gis/"
"index>) tá roinnt gnéithe nua:"

msgid ""
"Support for SpatiaLite_ -- a spatial database for SQLite -- as a spatial "
"backend."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíocht do Spatialite_ - bunachar sonraí spásúil do SQLite - mar chúltaca "
"spásúil."

msgid ""
"Geographic aggregates (``Collect``, ``Extent``, ``MakeLine``, ``Union``) and "
"``F`` expressions."
msgstr ""
"Comhiomláin gheografacha (``Collect``, `Extent``, ``Makeline``, ``Union``) "
"agus abairtí ``F``."

msgid ""
"New ``GeoQuerySet`` methods: ``collect``, ``geojson``, and ``snap_to_grid``."
msgstr ""
"Modhanna nua ``GeoquerySet``: ``baili``, `geojson``, agus ``snap_to_grid``."

msgid "A new list interface methods for ``GEOSGeometry`` objects."
msgstr "Modhanna comhéadan liosta nua le haghaidh rudaí ``Geosgeoimetry'."

msgid "For more details, see the GeoDjango documentation."
msgstr "Le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí, féach an doiciméadú GeodJango."

msgid "Other improvements"
msgstr "Feabhsuithe eile"

msgid "Other new features and changes introduced since Django 1.0 include:"
msgstr ""
"I measc na ngnéithe agus athruithe nua eile a tugadh isteach ó Django 1.0 tá:"

msgid ""
"The :doc:`CSRF protection middleware </ref/csrf>` has been split into two "
"classes -- ``CsrfViewMiddleware`` checks incoming requests, and "
"``CsrfResponseMiddleware`` processes outgoing responses. The combined "
"``CsrfMiddleware`` class (which does both) remains for backwards-"
"compatibility, but using the split classes is now recommended in order to "
"allow fine-grained control of when and where the CSRF processing takes place."
msgstr ""
"Tá an: Doc: “Meán-earraí cosanta CSRF” roinnte ina dhá rang -- "
"“CSRFViewMiddleware” seiceálann iarratais atá ag teacht isteach, agus "
"próiseálann ``CSRFresponsemiddleware` </ref/csrf> freagraí amach. Tá an rang "
"comhcheangailte `CSRFmiddleware` (a dhéanann an dá cheann) fós le haghaidh "
"comhoiriúnacht ar ais, ach moltar anois na ranganna scoilte a úsáid chun "
"rialú mionghráin a cheadú ar cathain agus cá háit a dtarlaíonn an próiseáil "
"CSRF."

msgid ""
"``reverse()`` and code which uses it (e.g., the ``{% url %}`` template tag) "
"now works with URLs in Django's administrative site, provided that the admin "
"URLs are set up via ``include(admin.site.urls)`` (sending admin requests to "
"the ``admin.site.root`` view still works, but URLs in the admin will not be "
"\"reversible\" when configured this way)."
msgstr ""
"Oibríonn ``reverse () ``agus cód a úsáideann é (m.sh., clib teimpléad`` {% "
"url%} ``) anois le URLanna i láithreán riaracháin Django, ar choinníoll go "
"bhfuil URLanna riaracháin curtha ar bun trí `include (admin.site.urls)`` "
"(iarratais riaracháin a sheoladh chuig an radharc `admin.site.root`` fós ag "
"obair, ach ní chumraítear URLanna sa admin nuair a bheidh” ar an mbealach "
"seo)."

msgid ""
"The ``include()`` function in Django URLconf modules can now accept "
"sequences of URL patterns (generated by ``patterns()``) in addition to "
"module names."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leis an bhfeidhm ``include () `i modúil Django URLConf glacadh "
"anois le seicheamh patrúin URL (a ghintear ag ``patrúin ()`) i dteannta "
"ainmneacha modúl."

msgid ""
"Instances of Django forms (see :doc:`the forms overview </topics/forms/"
"index>`) now have two additional methods, ``hidden_fields()`` and "
"``visible_fields()``, which return the list of hidden -- i.e., ``<input "
"type=\"hidden\">`` -- and visible fields on the form, respectively."
msgstr ""
"</topics/forms/index> <input type=\"hidden\">Tá dhá mhodh breise ag cásanna "
"foirmeacha Django (féach:doc: `forbhreathnú ar na foirmeach`) anois, "
"``hidden_fields () ``agus ``feice_fields ()``, a thugann liosta na réimsí i "
"bhfolach - ie, ```` - agus réimsí infheicthe ar an bhfoirm, faoi seach."

msgid ""
"The ``redirect_to`` generic view now accepts an additional keyword argument "
"``permanent``. If ``permanent`` is ``True``, the view will emit an HTTP "
"permanent redirect (status code 301). If ``False``, the view will emit an "
"HTTP temporary redirect (status code 302)."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an dearcadh cineálach ``redirect_to`` anois le argóint eochairfhocal "
"breise ``permanent``. Más é ```buan`` `True``, astóidh an dearcadh atreorú "
"buan HTTP (cód stádais 301). Má tá ``False``, astóidh an dearcadh atreorú "
"sealadach HTTP (cód stádais 302)."

msgid ""
"A new database lookup type -- ``week_day`` -- has been added for "
"``DateField`` and ``DateTimeField``. This type of lookup accepts a number "
"between 1 (Sunday) and 7 (Saturday), and returns objects where the field "
"value matches that day of the week. See :ref:`the full list of lookup types "
"<field-lookups>` for details."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh cineál nua cuardaigh bunachar sonraí - ``week_day`` -- le haghaidh "
"``DateField`` agus ``DateTimeField``. Glacann an cineál cuardaigh seo le "
"huimhir idir 1 (Dé Domhnaigh) agus 7 (Dé Sathairn), agus filleann sé rudaí "
"ina n-oireann luach an réimse leis an lá sin den tseachtain. <field-"
"lookups>Féach: tagairt: `liosta iomlán na gcineálacha cuardaigh `le haghaidh "
"sonraí."

msgid ""
"The ``{% for %}`` tag in Django's template language now accepts an optional "
"``{% empty %}`` clause, to be displayed when ``{% for %}`` is asked to loop "
"over an empty sequence. See :doc:`the list of built-in template tags </ref/"
"templates/builtins>` for examples of this."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an chlib ``{% le haghaidh %}`` i dteanga teimpléid Django anois le "
"clásal roghnach ``{ % folamh %}``, a thaispeánfar nuair a iarrtar ar ``{% do "
"%}`` lúbadh thar fholamh seicheamh. Féach :doc:`an liosta de na clibeanna "
"teimpléid ionsuite </ref/templates/builtins>` le haghaidh samplaí de seo."

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`dumpdata` management command now accepts individual model "
"names as arguments, allowing you to export the data just from particular "
"models."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an t-ordú bainistíochta: DJadmin: `dumpdata` le hainmneacha samhail "
"aonair mar argóintí anois, rud a ligeann duit na sonraí a onnmhairiú díreach "
"ó mhúnlaí áirithe."

msgid ""
"There's a new :tfilter:`safeseq` template filter which works just "
"like :tfilter:`safe` for lists, marking each item in the list as safe."
msgstr ""
"Tá scagaire teimpléad nua: tfilter: `safeseq` ann a oibríonn díreach "
"cosúil:tfilter: `sábháilte` le haghaidh liostaí, ag marcáil gach mír sa "
"liosta mar shábháilte."

msgid ""
":doc:`Cache backends </topics/cache>` now support ``incr()`` and ``decr()`` "
"commands to increment and decrement the value of a cache key. On cache "
"backends that support atomic increment/decrement -- most notably, the "
"memcached backend -- these operations will be atomic, and quite fast."
msgstr ""
":doc: Tacaíonn `cúltaca taiscéala` anois le </topics/cache> horduithe ``incr "
"() ``agus ``decr ()`` chun luach eochair taisce a mhéadú agus a laghdú. "
"Maidir le cúltaca taisce a thacaíonn le fhás/laghdú adamhach - go háirithe, "
"an cúltaca memcached - beidh na hoibríochtaí seo adamhacha, agus go tapa go "
"leor."

msgid ""
"Django now can :doc:`easily delegate authentication to the web server </"
"howto/auth-remote-user>` via a new authentication backend that supports the "
"standard ``REMOTE_USER`` environment variable used for this purpose."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le Django anois:doc: `fíordheimhniú a tharmligean go héasca chuig "
"an bhfreastalaí gréasán' trí chúltaca fíordheimhnithe nua a thacaíonn leis "
"an athróg comhshaoil caighdeánach `REMOTE_USER` </howto/auth-remote-user> a "
"úsáidtear chun na críche seo."

msgid ""
"There's a new :func:`django.shortcuts.redirect` function that makes it "
"easier to issue redirects given an object, a view name, or a URL."
msgstr ""
"Tá feidhm nua:func: `django.shortcuts.redirect` ann a fhágann go bhfuil sé "
"níos éasca athatreoruithe a eisiúint mar gheall ar réad, ainm amharc, nó URL."

msgid ""
"The ``postgresql_psycopg2`` backend now supports :ref:`native PostgreSQL "
"autocommit <postgresql-notes>`. This is an advanced, PostgreSQL-specific "
"feature, that can make certain read-heavy applications a good deal faster."
msgstr ""
"<postgresql-notes>Tacaíonn an cúltaca ``postgresql_psycopg2`` anois:ref: "
"`autocommit PostgreSQL dúchas`. Is gné chun cinn é seo, atá sonrach le "
"PostgreSQL, ar féidir leis feidhmchláir áirithe troma léitheoireachta a "
"dhéanamh níos gasta."

msgid "What's next?"
msgstr "Cad atá romhainn?"

msgid ""
"We'll take a short break, and then work on Django 1.2 will begin -- no rest "
"for the weary! If you'd like to help, discussion of Django development, "
"including progress toward the 1.2 release, takes place daily on the |django-"
"developers| mailing list and in the ``#django-dev`` IRC channel on "
"``irc.libera.chat``. Feel free to join the discussions!"
msgstr ""
"Glacfaimid sos gairid, agus ansin tosóidh an obair ar Django 1.2 - gan aon "
"scíth do dhaoine atá tuirseach! Más mian leat cabhrú, bíonn plé ar fhorbairt "
"Django, lena n-áirítear dul chun cinn i dtreo an eisiúint 1.2, ar an liosta "
"seoltaí |django-developers| agus sa chainéal IRC ``#django -dev`` ar "
"`irc.libera.chat``. Bíodh leisce ort páirt a ghlacadh sna plé!"

msgid ""
"Django's online documentation also includes pointers on how to contribute to "
"Django:"
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn cáipéisíocht ar líne Django leideanna freisin maidir le conas cur "
"le Django:"

msgid ":doc:`How to contribute to Django </internals/contributing/index>`"
msgstr ":doc: `Conas cur le Django</internals/contributing/index> `"

msgid ""
"Contributions on any level -- developing code, writing documentation or "
"simply triaging tickets and helping to test proposed bugfixes -- are always "
"welcome and appreciated."
msgstr ""
"Fáiltítear i gcónaí roimh ranníocaíochtaí ar aon leibhéal – cód a fhorbairt, "
"doiciméadú a scríobh nó ticéid a thriaisteáil agus cabhrú le ceartúcháin "
"bheartaithe a thástáil – agus is mór againn i gcónaí iad."

msgid "And that's the way it is."
msgstr "Agus sin an bealach atá sé."

msgid "Django 1.1.2 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.1.2"

msgid "Welcome to Django 1.1.2!"
msgstr "Fáilte go dtí Django 1.1.2!"

msgid ""
"This is the second \"bugfix\" release in the Django 1.1 series, improving "
"the stability and performance of the Django 1.1 codebase."
msgstr ""
"Is é seo an dara scaoileadh “bugfix” sa tsraith Django 1.1, ag feabhsú "
"cobhsaíocht agus feidhmíocht an chódabhais Django 1.1."

msgid ""
"Django 1.1.2 maintains backwards compatibility with Django 1.1.0, but "
"contain a number of fixes and other improvements. Django 1.1.2 is a "
"recommended upgrade for any development or deployment currently using or "
"targeting Django 1.1."
msgstr ""
"Coinníonn Django 1.1.2 comhoiriúnacht ar ais le Django 1.1.0, ach tá roinnt "
"socruithe agus feabhsuithe eile ann. Is uasghrádú molta é Django 1.1.2 d'aon "
"fhorbairt nó imscaradh a úsáideann nó ag díriú ar Django 1.1 faoi láthair."

msgid ""
"For full details on the new features, backwards incompatibilities, and "
"deprecated features in the 1.1 branch, see the :doc:`/releases/1.1`."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh sonraí iomlána faoi na gnéithe nua, na neamhoiriúnachtaí ar ais, "
"agus na gnéithe lasmuigh sa bhrainse 1.1, féach an:doc: `/releases/1.1`."

msgid "Backwards-incompatible changes in 1.1.2"
msgstr "Athruithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha ar chúl i 1.1.2"

msgid "Test runner exit status code"
msgstr "Cód stádais imeachta an reathóra tástála"

msgid ""
"The exit status code of the test runners (``tests/runtests.py`` and ``python "
"manage.py test``) no longer represents the number of failed tests, since a "
"failure of 256 or more tests resulted in a wrong exit status code.  The exit "
"status code for the test runner is now 0 for success (no failing tests) and "
"1 for any number of test failures.  If needed, the number of test failures "
"can be found at the end of the test runner's output."
msgstr ""
"Ní léiríonn cód stádas imeachta na riteadóirí tástála (`tests/runtests.py`` "
"agus ``python manage.py test ``) líon na dtástálacha theip a thuilleadh, ós "
"rud é go raibh cód stádais imeachta mícheart mar thoradh ar theip 256 "
"tástáil nó níos mó. Is é an cód stádais imeachta don rádálaí tástála anois 0 "
"le haghaidh rath (gan aon tástálacha teip) agus 1 le haghaidh aon líon "
"teipeanna tástála. Más gá, is féidir líon na dteipeanna tástála a fháil ag "
"deireadh aschur an rádálaí tástála."

msgid "Cookie encoding"
msgstr "Ionchódú fianán"

msgid ""
"To fix bugs with cookies in Internet Explorer, Safari, and possibly other "
"browsers, our encoding of cookie values was changed so that the characters "
"comma and semi-colon are treated as non-safe characters, and are therefore "
"encoded as ``\\054`` and ``\\073`` respectively.  This could produce "
"backwards incompatibilities, especially if you are storing comma or semi-"
"colon in cookies and have JavaScript code that parses and manipulates cookie "
"values client-side."
msgstr ""
"Chun fabhtanna a shocrú le fianáin in Internet Explorer, Safari, agus "
"b'fhéidir brabhsálaithe eile, athraíodh ár n-ionchódú luachanna fianán ionas "
"go ndéileálfar leis na carachtair coma agus leath-colon mar charachtair "
"neamh-shábháilte, agus dá bhrí sin ionchódú iad mar ``\\ 054`` agus``\\ "
"073`` faoi seach. D'fhéadfadh sé seo neamhoiriúnachtaí ar ais a bheith mar "
"thoradh air, go háirithe má tá camóg nó leath-colon á stóráil agat i "
"bhfianáin agus má tá cód JavaScript agat a pháirsíonn agus a ionramhlaigh "
"luachanna fianán taobh an chliaint."

msgid "One new feature"
msgstr "Gné nua amháin"

msgid ""
"Ordinarily, a point release would not include new features, but in the case "
"of Django 1.1.2, we have made an exception to this rule. Django 1.2 (the "
"next major release of Django) will contain a feature that will improve "
"protection against Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF) attacks. This feature "
"requires the use of a new :ttag:`csrf_token` template tag in all forms that "
"Django renders."
msgstr ""
"De ghnáth, ní chuimsíodh gnéithe nua i scaoileadh pointe, ach i gcás Django "
"1.1.2, tá eisceacht déanta againn ón riail seo. Beidh gné i Django 1.2 (an "
"chéad scaoileadh mór eile de Django) a fheabhsóidh cosaint i gcoinne "
"ionsaithe Fhorbhósáide Iarratas Tras-Láithreáin (CSRF). Éilíonn an ghné seo "
"clib teimpléad nua: ttag: `csrf_token` a úsáid i ngach foirm a dhéanann "
"Django."

msgid ""
"To make it easier to support both 1.1.X and 1.2.X versions of Django with "
"the same templates, we have decided to introduce the :ttag:`csrf_token` "
"template tag to the 1.1.X branch. In the 1.1.X branch, :ttag:`csrf_token` "
"does nothing - it has no effect on templates or form processing. However, it "
"means that the same template will work with Django 1.2."
msgstr ""
"Chun é a dhéanamh níos éasca tacú le leaganacha 1.1.X agus 1.2.X de Django "
"leis na teimpléid chéanna, shocraigh muid an chlib teimpléad:ttag: "
"`csrf_token` a thabhairt isteach chuig an mbrainse 1.1.X. Sa bhrainse 1.1.X, "
"ní dhéanann :ttag: `csrf_token` aon rud - níl aon éifeacht aige ar "
"theimpléid ná ar phróiseáil foirme. Ciallaíonn sé, áfach, go n-oibreoidh an "
"teimpléad céanna le Django 1.2."

msgid "Django 1.1.3 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.1.3"

msgid "Welcome to Django 1.1.3!"
msgstr "Fáilte go Django 1.1.3!"

msgid ""
"This is the third \"bugfix\" release in the Django 1.1 series, improving the "
"stability and performance of the Django 1.1 codebase."
msgstr ""
"Is é seo an tríú scaoileadh “bugfix” sa tsraith Django 1.1, ag feabhsú "
"cobhsaíocht agus feidhmíocht an chódabhsa Django 1.1."

msgid ""
"With one exception, Django 1.1.3 maintains backwards compatibility with "
"Django 1.1.2. It also contains a number of fixes and other improvements. "
"Django 1.1.2 is a recommended upgrade for any development or deployment "
"currently using or targeting Django 1.1."
msgstr ""
"Le haon eisceacht amháin, coimeádann Django 1.1.3 comhoiriúnacht ar ais le "
"Django 1.1.2. Tá roinnt socruithe agus feabhsuithe eile ann freisin. Is "
"uasghrádú molta é Django 1.1.2 d'aon fhorbairt nó imscaradh a úsáideann nó "
"ag díriú ar Django 1.1 faoi láthair."

msgid "Backwards incompatible changes"
msgstr "Athruithe neamhoiriúnacha ar ais"

msgid "Restricted filters in admin interface"
msgstr "Scagairí srianta i gcomhéadan admin"

msgid ""
"The Django administrative interface, ``django.contrib.admin``, supports "
"filtering of displayed lists of objects by fields on the corresponding "
"models, including across database-level relationships. This is implemented "
"by passing lookup arguments in the querystring portion of the URL, and "
"options on the ModelAdmin class allow developers to specify particular "
"fields or relationships which will generate automatic links for filtering."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn comhéadan riaracháin Django, ``django.contrib.admin ``, le scagadh "
"liostaí a thaispeántar rudaí de réir réimsí ar na samhlacha comhfhreagracha, "
"lena n-áirítear thar chaidrimh ar leibhéal bunachar sonraí. Cuirtear é seo i "
"bhfeidhm trí argóintí cuardaigh a rith sa chuid ceisteanna den URL, agus "
"tugann roghanna ar an rang ModelAdmin deis d'fhorbróirí réimsí nó caidrimh "
"áirithe a shonrú a ghinfidh naisc uathoibríoch le haghaidh scagadh."

msgid ""
"One historically-undocumented and -unofficially-supported feature has been "
"the ability for a user with sufficient knowledge of a model's structure and "
"the format of these lookup arguments to invent useful new filters on the fly "
"by manipulating the querystring."
msgstr ""
"Gné amháin neamhdhoiciméadaithe ó thaobh stairiúil agus neamhoifigiúil ná an "
"cumas d'úsáideoir a bhfuil eolas leordhóthanach aige ar struchtúr samhail "
"agus ar fhormáid na n-argóintí cuardaigh seo scagairí nua úsáideacha a "
"chumadh ar an eitilt tríd an sreang ceisteanna a ionramháil."

msgid ""
"However, it has been demonstrated that this can be abused to gain access to "
"information outside of an admin user's permissions; for example, an attacker "
"with access to the admin and sufficient knowledge of model structure and "
"relations could construct query strings which -- with repeated use of "
"regular-expression lookups supported by the Django database API -- expose "
"sensitive information such as users' password hashes."
msgstr ""
"Taispeánadh, áfach, gur féidir é seo a mhí-úsáid chun rochtain a fháil ar "
"fhaisnéis lasmuigh de cheadanna úsáideora riaracháin; mar shampla, "
"d'fhéadfadh ionsaitheoir a bhfuil rochtain aige ar an riarachán agus eolas "
"leordhóthanach ar struchtúr agus caidreamh samhail teaghráin cheisteanna a "
"nochtadh - le luacháin rialta le API bunachar sonraí Django."

msgid ""
"To remedy this, ``django.contrib.admin`` will now validate that querystring "
"lookup arguments either specify only fields on the model being viewed, or "
"cross relations which have been explicitly allowed by the application "
"developer using the preexisting mechanism mentioned above. This is backwards-"
"incompatible for any users relying on the prior ability to insert arbitrary "
"lookups."
msgstr ""
"Chun é seo a leigheas, bailíochnóidh ``django.contrib.admin ``anois go "
"sonraíonn argóintí cuardaigh ceisteanna ach réimsí ar an tsamhail atá á "
"fheiceáil, nó traschaidrimh a cheadaigh an forbróir feidhmchláir go "
"sainráite ag baint úsáide as an meicníocht atá ann cheana a luaitear thuas. "
"Tá sé seo comhoiriúnach le cúl d'úsáideoirí ar bith ag brath ar an gcumas "
"roimhe seo cuardaigh treallach a chur isteach."

msgid "Django 1.1.4 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.1.4"

msgid "Welcome to Django 1.1.4!"
msgstr "Fáilte go Django 1.1.4!"

msgid ""
"This is the fourth \"bugfix\" release in the Django 1.1 series, improving "
"the stability and performance of the Django 1.1 codebase."
msgstr ""
"Is é seo an ceathrú scaoileadh “bugfix” sa tsraith Django 1.1, ag feabhsú "
"cobhsaíocht agus feidhmíocht an chódabhais Django 1.1."

msgid ""
"With one exception, Django 1.1.4 maintains backwards compatibility with "
"Django 1.1.3. It also contains a number of fixes and other improvements. "
"Django 1.1.4 is a recommended upgrade for any development or deployment "
"currently using or targeting Django 1.1."
msgstr ""
"Le haon eisceacht amháin, coimeádann Django 1.1.4 comhoiriúnacht ar ais le "
"Django 1.1.3. Tá roinnt socruithe agus feabhsuithe eile ann freisin. Is "
"uasghrádú molta é Django 1.1.4 d'aon fhorbairt nó imscaradh a úsáideann nó "
"ag díriú ar Django 1.1 faoi láthair."

msgid "CSRF exception for AJAX requests"
msgstr "Eisceacht CSRF d'iarratais AJAX"

msgid ""
"Django includes a CSRF-protection mechanism, which makes use of a token "
"inserted into outgoing forms. Middleware then checks for the token's "
"presence on form submission, and validates it."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn Django meicníocht cosanta CSRF, a úsáideann comhartha a cuireadh "
"isteach i bhfoirmeacha amach. Seiceálann Middleware ansin ar láithreacht an "
"chomhartha ar aighneacht foirme, agus bailíochtaíonn sé í."

msgid ""
"Prior to Django 1.2.5, our CSRF protection made an exception for AJAX "
"requests, on the following basis:"
msgstr ""
"Roimh Django 1.2.5, rinne ár gcosaint CSRF eisceacht d'iarratais AJAX, ar an "
"mbonn seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"Many AJAX toolkits add an X-Requested-With header when using XMLHttpRequest."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann go leor trealamh uirlisí AJAX ceanntásc X-Iarrtha leis agus "
"XMLHttpRequest á n-úsáid agat."

msgid "Browsers have strict same-origin policies regarding XMLHttpRequest."
msgstr ""
"Tá beartais dhian den bhunús céanna ag brabhsálaí maidir le XMLHttpRequest."

msgid ""
"In the context of a browser, the only way that a custom header of this "
"nature can be added is with XMLHttpRequest."
msgstr ""
"I gcomhthéacs brabhsálaí, is é an t-aon bhealach is féidir ceannteideal "
"saincheaptha den chineál seo a chur leis ná le XMLHttpRequest."

msgid ""
"Therefore, for ease of use, we did not apply CSRF checks to requests that "
"appeared to be AJAX on the basis of the X-Requested-With header. The Ruby on "
"Rails web framework had a similar exemption."
msgstr ""
"Dá bhrí sin, ar mhaithe le héasca le húsáid, níor chuireamar seiceálacha "
"CSRF i bhfeidhm ar iarratais a bhí ar an gcosúil gur AJAX iad ar bhonn an "
"cheanntásc X-Requested-With. Bhí díolúine den chineál céanna ag creat "
"gréasáin Ruby on Rails."

msgid ""
"Recently, engineers at Google made members of the Ruby on Rails development "
"team aware of a combination of browser plugins and redirects which can allow "
"an attacker to provide custom HTTP headers on a request to any website. This "
"can allow a forged request to appear to be an AJAX request, thereby "
"defeating CSRF protection which trusts the same-origin nature of AJAX "
"requests."
msgstr ""
"Le déanaí, chuir innealtóirí ag Google ar an eolas ar bhaill d'fhoireann "
"forbartha Ruby on Rails faoi mheascán de bhreiseáin agus atreoruithe "
"brabhsálaí a fhéadann ligean d'ionsaitheoir ceanntásca saincheaptha HTTP a "
"sholáthar ar iarratas ar aon láithreán gréasáin. Féadann sé seo ligean gur "
"iarratas brionnaithe gur iarratas AJAX é, agus ar an gcaoi sin ruaig ar "
"chosaint CSRF a bhfuil muinín aige ar an nádúr céanna tionscnaimh iarratais "
"AJAX."

msgid ""
"Michael Koziarski of the Rails team brought this to our attention, and we "
"were able to produce a proof-of-concept demonstrating the same vulnerability "
"in Django's CSRF handling."
msgstr ""
"Thug Michael Koziarski ó fhoireann na Rails aird air seo, agus bhí muid in "
"ann cruthúnas coincheap a tháirgeadh ag taispeáint an leochaileacht chéanna "
"i láimhseáil CSRF Django."

msgid ""
"To remedy this, Django will now apply full CSRF validation to all requests, "
"regardless of apparent AJAX origin. This is technically backwards-"
"incompatible, but the security risks have been judged to outweigh the "
"compatibility concerns in this case."
msgstr ""
"Chun é seo a leigheas, cuirfidh Django bailíochtú iomlán CSRF i bhfeidhm "
"anois ar gach iarratas, beag beann ar bhunús AJAX dealraitheach. Tá sé seo "
"chomhoiriúnach go teicniúil le cúl, ach measadh go bhfuil na rioscaí "
"slándála níos mó ná na hábhair imní comhoiriúnachta sa chás seo."

msgid ""
"Additionally, Django will now accept the CSRF token in the custom HTTP "
"header X-CSRFTOKEN, as well as in the form submission itself, for ease of "
"use with popular JavaScript toolkits which allow insertion of custom headers "
"into all AJAX requests."
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, glacfaidh Django leis an gcomhartha CSRF anois sa "
"cheannteideal saincheaptha HTTP X-CSRFTOKEN, chomh maith leis an aighneacht "
"foirme féin, le haghaidh éasca le húsáid le feistí uirlisí móréilimh "
"JavaScript a cheadaíonn ceannteidil saincheaptha a chur isteach i ngach "
"iarratas AJAX."

msgid ""
"Please see the :ref:`CSRF docs for example jQuery code <csrf-ajax>` that "
"demonstrates this technique, ensuring that you are looking at the "
"documentation for your version of Django, as the exact code necessary is "
"different for some older versions of Django."
msgstr ""
"Féach le do thoil an:ref: `CSRF docs mar shampla cód jQuery <csrf-ajax>`a "
"léiríonn an teicníc seo, ag cinntiú go bhfuil tú ag féachaint ar an "
"doiciméadú do leagan de Django, toisc go bhfuil an cód cruinn riachtanach "
"difriúil do roinnt leaganacha níos sine de Django."

msgid "Django 1.10 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.10"

msgid "*August 1, 2016*"
msgstr "*1 Lúnasa, 2016*"

msgid "Welcome to Django 1.10!"
msgstr "Fáilte go Django 1.10!"

msgid ""
"These release notes cover the :ref:`new features <whats-new-1.10>`, as well "
"as some :ref:`backwards incompatible changes <backwards-incompatible-1.10>` "
"you'll want to be aware of when upgrading from Django 1.9 or older versions. "
"We've :ref:`dropped some features <removed-features-1.10>` that have reached "
"the end of their deprecation cycle, and we've :ref:`begun the deprecation "
"process for some features <deprecated-features-1.10>`."
msgstr ""
"Clúdaíonn na nótaí scaoilte seo na:ref: `gnéithe nua <whats-new-1.10>`, "
"chomh maith le roinnt athruithe: ref: `athruithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha ar "
"chúl<backwards-incompatible-1.10>` a mbeidh tú ag iarraidh a bheith ar an "
"eolas fúthu agus tú ag uasghrádú ó Django 1.9 nó leaganacha níos sine. "
"<deprecated-features-1.10>Chuireamar: Ref: `thit roinnt <removed-"
"features-1.10>gnéithe `a bhfuil deireadh a dtimthriall díghníomhaíochta "
"bainte amach acu, agus chuireamaire:ref: `thosaigh muid ar an bpróiseas "
"díghníomhaíochta do roinnt gnéithe`."

msgid ""
"See the :doc:`/howto/upgrade-version` guide if you're updating an existing "
"project."
msgstr ""
"Féach an treoir:doc: `/howto/upgrade-leagan` má tá tionscadal atá ann cheana "
"á nuashonrú agat."

msgid "Python compatibility"
msgstr "Comhoiriúnacht Python"

msgid ""
"Like Django 1.9, Django 1.10 requires Python 2.7, 3.4, or 3.5. We **highly "
"recommend** and only officially support the latest release of each series."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le Django 1.9, teastaíonn Python 2.7, 3.4, nó 3.5 ó Django 1.10. "
"Molaimid** go hard** agus ní thacaímid go hoifigiúil ach leis an scaoileadh "
"is déanaí de gach sraith."

msgid "What's new in Django 1.10"
msgstr "Cad atá nua i Django 1.10"

msgid "Full text search for PostgreSQL"
msgstr "Cuardach téacs iomlán do PostgreSQL"

msgid ""
"``django.contrib.postgres`` now includes a :doc:`collection of database "
"functions </ref/contrib/postgres/search>` to allow the use of the full text "
"search engine. You can search across multiple fields in your relational "
"database, combine the searches with other lookups, use different language "
"configurations and weightings, and rank the results by relevance."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn ``django.contrib.postgres`` anois :doc:`cnuasach feidhmeanna "
"bunachar sonraí </ref/contrib/postgres/search>` chun úsáid an innill "
"chuardaigh téacs iomlán a cheadú. Is féidir leat cuardach a dhéanamh thar "
"réimsí iolracha i do bhunachar sonraí coibhneasta, cuardaigh a chomhcheangal "
"le cuardaigh eile, cumraíochtaí agus ualuithe éagsúla teanga a úsáid, agus "
"na torthaí a rangú de réir ábharthacht."

msgid ""
"It also now includes trigram support, using the :lookup:`trigram_similar` "
"lookup, and the :class:`~django.contrib.postgres.search.TrigramSimilarity` "
"and :class:`~django.contrib.postgres.search.TrigramDistance` expressions."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn sé tacaíocht trigram anois, ag baint úsáide as an lorgaí:lookup: "
"`trigram_similar`, agus na:class: "
"`~django.contrib.postgres.search.trigramsimilarity` agus:class: "
"`~django.contrib.postgres.search.trigramdistance`."

msgid "New-style middleware"
msgstr "Meán-earraí nua i stíl"

msgid ""
":doc:`A new style of middleware is introduced </topics/http/middleware>` to "
"solve the lack of strict request/response layering of the old-style of "
"middleware described in `DEP 0005 <https://github.com/django/deps/blob/main/"
"final/0005-improved-middleware.rst>`_. You'll need to :ref:`adapt old, "
"custom middleware <upgrading-middleware>` and switch from the "
"``MIDDLEWARE_CLASSES`` setting to the new :setting:`MIDDLEWARE` setting to "
"take advantage of the improvements."
msgstr ""
"</topics/http/middleware> < https://github.com/django/deps/blob/main/final/"
"0005-improved-middleware.rst>:doc: “Cuirtear isteach stíl nua de mheán-"
"earraí” chun an easpa docht iarrata/freagartha a réiteach ar sheanstíl "
"mheánearraí a thuairiscítear in `DEP 0005`_. Beidh ort: ref: `sean-mheán-"
"earraí saincheaptha a oiriúnú `agus aistriú ón socrú ``MIDDLEWARE <upgrading-"
"middleware>_CLASSES`` go dtí an socrú nua:setting: `MIDDLEWARE` chun leas a "
"bhaint as na feabhsuithe."

msgid "Official support for Unicode usernames"
msgstr "Tacaíocht oifigiúil d'ainmneacha úsáideora Unicode"

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User` model in "
"``django.contrib.auth`` originally only accepted ASCII letters and numbers "
"in usernames. Although it wasn't a deliberate choice, Unicode characters "
"have always been accepted when using Python 3."
msgstr ""
"Ní ghlac an tsamhail:class: `~django.contrib.auth.models.user` i "
"``django.contrib.auth`` ar dtús litreacha agus uimhreacha ASCII in "
"ainmneacha úsáideora. Cé nach rogha d'aon ghnó a bhí ann, glacadh le "
"carachtair Unicode i gcónaí agus Python 3 á úsáid agat."

msgid ""
"The username validator now explicitly accepts Unicode characters by default "
"on Python 3 only."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an bailíochtóir ainm úsáideora go sainráite anois le carachtair "
"Unicode de réir réamhshocraithe ar Python 3 amháin."

msgid ""
"Custom user models may use the "
"new :class:`~django.contrib.auth.validators.ASCIIUsernameValidator` "
"or :class:`~django.contrib.auth.validators.UnicodeUsernameValidator`."
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh samhlacha úsáideora saincheaptha an nua:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.validators.asciiUserNameValidator` nó: class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.validators.unicodeUserNameValidator` a úsáid."

msgid "Minor features"
msgstr "Mionghnéithe"

msgid ":mod:`django.contrib.admin`"
msgstr ":mod: `django.contrib.admin `"

msgid ""
"For sites running on a subpath, the default :attr:`URL for the \"View site\" "
"link <django.contrib.admin.AdminSite.site_url>` at the top of each admin "
"page will now point to ``request.META['SCRIPT_NAME']`` if set, instead of ``/"
"``."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le suíomhanna atá ag rith ar fho-chosán, déanfaidh an "
"réamhshocraithe:attr: `URL don nasc “Féach ar an láithreán” "
"<django.contrib.admin.AdminSite.site_url>`ag barr gach leathanach riaracháin "
"ag díriú anois ar ``request.meta ['SCRIPT_NAME'] ``má tá sé socraithe, in "
"ionad ``/``."

msgid ""
"The success message that appears after adding or editing an object now "
"contains a link to the object's change form."
msgstr ""
"Tá nasc anois le foirm athraithe an réada sa teachtaireacht rathúlachta atá "
"le feiceáil tar éis réad a chur leis nó a chur in eagar."

msgid ""
"All inline JavaScript is removed so you can enable the ``Content-Security-"
"Policy`` HTTP header if you wish."
msgstr ""
"Baintear gach JavaScript inlíne ionas gur féidir leat an ceannteideal HTTP "
"``Content-Security-Policy`` a chumasú más mian leat."

msgid ""
"The new :attr:`InlineModelAdmin.classes "
"<django.contrib.admin.InlineModelAdmin.classes>` attribute allows specifying "
"classes on inline fieldsets. Inlines with a ``collapse`` class will be "
"initially collapsed and their header will have a small \"show\" link."
msgstr ""
"<django.contrib.admin.InlineModelAdmin.classes>Ceadaíonn an tréith nua:attr: "
"`InlineModelAdmin.classes `aicmí a shonrú ar thacainní réimsí inlíne. "
"Titeofar ar dtús na línte a bhfuil rang ``fallse`` acu agus beidh nasc beag "
"“seó” ag a gceanntásc."

msgid ""
"If a user doesn't have the add permission, the ``object-tools`` block on a "
"model's changelist will now be rendered (without the add button). This makes "
"it easier to add custom tools in this case."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil an cead breise ag úsáideoir, déanfar an bloc `réad-uirlisí ``ar "
"liosta athraithe samhail a léiriú anois (gan an cnaipe leis). Fágann sé seo "
"go bhfuil sé níos éasca uirlisí saincheaptha a chur leis sa chás seo."

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.contrib.admin.models.LogEntry` model now stores change "
"messages in a JSON structure so that the message can be dynamically "
"translated using the current active language. A new "
"``LogEntry.get_change_message()`` method is now the preferred way of "
"retrieving the change message."
msgstr ""
"Stórálann an tsamhail:Class: `~django.contrib.admin.models.logentry` "
"teachtaireachtaí athraithe i struchtúr JSON anois ionas gur féidir an "
"teachtaireacht a aistriú go dinimiciúil ag baint úsáide as an teanga "
"ghníomhach reatha. Is é modh nua ``Logentry.get_change_message () ``an "
"bealach is fearr anois chun an teachtaireacht athraithe a aisghabháil."

msgid ""
"Selected objects for fields in ``ModelAdmin.raw_id_fields`` now have a link "
"to object's change form."
msgstr ""
"Tá nasc anois ag rudaí roghnaithe do réimsí i `ModelAdmin.raw_id_fields`` le "
"foirm athraithe réad anois."

msgid ""
"Added \"No date\" and \"Has date\" choices for ``DateFieldListFilter`` if "
"the field is nullable."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh roghanna “Gan dáta” agus “Tá dáta aige” le haghaidh "
"``DateFieldListFilter`` má tá an réimse neamhnaithe."

msgid ""
"The jQuery library embedded in the admin is upgraded from version 2.1.4 to "
"2.2.3."
msgstr ""
"Déantar an leabharlann jQuery atá leabaithe sa riarachán a uasghrádú ó "
"leagan 2.1.4 go 2.2.3."

msgid ":mod:`django.contrib.auth`"
msgstr ":mod: `django.contrib.auth`"

msgid ""
"Added support for the :ref:`Argon2 password hash <argon2_usage>`. It's "
"recommended over PBKDF2, however, it's not the default as it requires a "
"third-party library."
msgstr ""
"<argon2_usage>Tacaíocht bhreise don: ref: `hash pasfhocal Argon2 `. Moltar é "
"thar PBKDF2, áfach, ní hé an réamhshocrú toisc go dteastaíonn leabharlann "
"tríú páirtí uaidh."

msgid ""
"The default iteration count for the PBKDF2 password hasher has been "
"increased by 25%. This backwards compatible change will not affect users who "
"have subclassed ``django.contrib.auth.hashers.PBKDF2PasswordHasher`` to "
"change the default value."
msgstr ""
"Méadaíodh 25% an líon athraithe réamhshocraithe don hasher pasfhocal PBKDF2. "
"Ní dhéanfaidh an t-athrú comhoiriúnach ar chúl difear d'úsáideoirí a bhfuil "
"fo-aicmithe ag ``Django.contrib.auth.hashers.pbkdf2PasswordHasher`` chun an "
"luach réamhshocraithe a athrú."

msgid ""
"The ``django.contrib.auth.views.logout()`` view sends \"no-cache\" headers "
"to prevent an issue where Safari caches redirects and prevents a user from "
"being able to log out."
msgstr ""
"Seolann an radharc ``django.contrib.auth.views.logout () ``ceanntásca “no-"
"cache” chun saincheist a chosc ina ndéanann Safari ceascanna a atreorú agus "
"cuireann sé cosc ar úsáideoir a bheith in ann logáil amach."

msgid ""
"Added the optional ``backend`` argument to :func:`django.contrib.auth.login` "
"to allow using it without credentials."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an argóint roghnach ``backend`` chuig: func: "
"`django.contrib.auth.login` chun ligean é a úsáid gan dhintiúir."

msgid ""
"The new :setting:`LOGOUT_REDIRECT_URL` setting controls the redirect of the "
"``django.contrib.auth.views.logout()`` view, if the view doesn't get a "
"``next_page`` argument."
msgstr ""
"Rialaíonn an socrú nua:setting: `LOGOUT_REDIRECT_URL` athreorú an amharc "
"``django.contrib.auth.views.logout () `, mura bhfaigheann an dearcadh "
"argóint ``next_page``."

msgid ""
"The new ``redirect_authenticated_user`` parameter for the "
"``django.contrib.auth.views.login()`` view allows redirecting authenticated "
"users visiting the login page."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an paraiméadar nua ``redirect_autenticated_user`` don amharc "
"``django.contrib.auth.views.login () ``úsáideoirí fíordheimhnithe a thugann "
"cuairt ar an leathanach logála isteach a atreorú."

msgid ""
"The new :class:`~django.contrib.auth.backends.AllowAllUsersModelBackend` "
"and :class:`~django.contrib.auth.backends.AllowAllUsersRemoteUserBackend` "
"ignore the value of ``User.is_active``, "
"while :class:`~django.contrib.auth.backends.ModelBackend` "
"and :class:`~django.contrib.auth.backends.RemoteUserBackend` now reject "
"inactive users."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an nua:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.backends.allowAllUsersModelBackend` agus:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.backends.allowAllUsersRemoteUserBackend` neamhaird ar "
"luach ``User.is_Active``, agus: class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.backends.modelBackend` :class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.backends.remoteUserBackend` diúltú úsáideoirí "
"neamhghníomhacha anois."

msgid ":mod:`django.contrib.gis`"
msgstr ":mod: `django.contrib.gis`"

msgid ""
":ref:`Distance lookups <distance-lookups>` now accept expressions as the "
"distance value parameter."
msgstr ""
":ref: “Cuardaigh achair” glacann anois <distance-lookups>le nathanna mar "
"pharaiméadar luach achair."

msgid ""
"The new :attr:`GEOSGeometry.unary_union "
"<django.contrib.gis.geos.GEOSGeometry.unary_union>` property computes the "
"union of all the elements of this geometry."
msgstr ""
"Ríomhaíonn an maoin nua:attr: `Geosgeometry.unary_union "
"<django.contrib.gis.geos.GEOSGeometry.unary_union>`aontas eilimintí uile an "
"geoiméadra seo."

msgid ""
"Added the :meth:`GEOSGeometry.covers() "
"<django.contrib.gis.geos.GEOSGeometry.covers>` binary predicate."
msgstr ""
"<django.contrib.gis.geos.GEOSGeometry.covers>Cuireadh an predicate dénártha: "
"meth: `Geosgeometry.covers () `leis."

msgid ""
"Added the :meth:`GDALBand.statistics() "
"<django.contrib.gis.gdal.GDALBand.statistics>` method "
"and :attr:`~django.contrib.gis.gdal.GDALBand.mean` "
"and :attr:`~django.contrib.gis.gdal.GDALBand.std` attributes."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an modh: meth: `GdalBand.Statistics () `agus:attr: "
"`~django.contrib.gis.gdal.gdalband.mean` agus:attr: "
"`~django.contrib.gis.gdal.gdalband.st "
"<django.contrib.gis.gdal.GDALBand.statistics>d` tréithe."

msgid ""
"Added support for the :class:`~django.contrib.gis.db.models.MakeLine` "
"aggregate and :class:`~django.contrib.gis.db.models.functions.GeoHash` "
"function on SpatiaLite."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíocht bhreise don chomhiomlán: aicme: "
"`~django.contrib.gis.db.models.makeline` agus:class: "
"`~django.contrib.gis.db.models.functions.geohash` feidhm ar Spatialite."

msgid ""
"Added support for "
"the :class:`~django.contrib.gis.db.models.functions.Difference`, :class:`~django.contrib.gis.db.models.functions.Intersection`, "
"and :class:`~django.contrib.gis.db.models.functions.SymDifference` functions "
"on MySQL."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíocht bhreise don: class: "
"`~django.contrib.gis.db.models.functions.difference`, :class: "
"`~django.contrib.gis.db.models.functions.intersection`, agus:class: "
"`~django.contrib.gis.db.models.functions.symdifference` feidhmeanna ar MySQL."

msgid "Added support for instantiating empty GEOS geometries."
msgstr "Tacaíocht bhreise chun geoiméadraí folamh GEOS a chur ar aghaidh."

msgid ""
"The new :attr:`~django.contrib.gis.geos.WKTWriter.trim` "
"and :attr:`~django.contrib.gis.geos.WKTWriter.precision` properties "
"of :class:`~django.contrib.gis.geos.WKTWriter` allow controlling output of "
"the fractional part of the coordinates in WKT."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn an nua:attr: `~django.contrib.gis.geos.wktwriter.trim` agus:attr: "
"`~django.contrib.gis.geos.wktWriter.Precision` airíonna de:class: "
"`~django.contrib.gis.geos.wktWriter` rialú aschur an chuid codánach de na "
"comhordanáidí i WKT."

msgid ""
"Added the :attr:`LineString.closed "
"<django.contrib.gis.geos.LineString.closed>` "
"and :attr:`MultiLineString.closed "
"<django.contrib.gis.geos.MultiLineString.closed>` properties."
msgstr ""
"<django.contrib.gis.geos.LineString.closed><django.contrib.gis.geos.MultiLineString.closed>Cuireadh "
"airíonna: attr: `Linestring.closed `agus:attr: `MultilineString.Closed` leis."

msgid ""
"The :doc:`GeoJSON serializer </ref/contrib/gis/serializers>` now outputs the "
"primary key of objects in the ``properties`` dictionary if specific fields "
"aren't specified."
msgstr ""
"Aisíonn an:doc: `GeoJSON serializer` an príomh-eochair na rudaí sa fhoclóir "
"``</ref/contrib/gis/serializers> airíonna`` mura sonraítear réimsí ar leith."

msgid ""
"The ability to replicate input data on the :meth:`GDALBand.data() "
"<django.contrib.gis.gdal.GDALBand.data>` method was added. Band data can now "
"be updated with repeated values efficiently."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an cumas sonraí ionchuir a mhacasamhlú ar an "
"modh :meth:`GDALBand.data() <django.contrib.gis.gdal.GDALBand.data>`. Is "
"féidir sonraí banna a nuashonrú anois le luachanna arís agus arís eile go "
"héifeachtach."

msgid ""
"Added database "
"functions :class:`~django.contrib.gis.db.models.functions.IsValid` "
"and :class:`~django.contrib.gis.db.models.functions.MakeValid`, as well as "
"the :lookup:`isvalid` lookup, all for PostGIS. This allows filtering and "
"repairing invalid geometries on the database side."
msgstr ""
"Feidhmeanna bunachar sonraí "
"breise :aicme:`~django.contrib.gis.db.models.functions.IsValid` "
"agus :rang:`~django.contrib.gis.db.models.functions.MakeValid`, chomh maith "
"leis an :lookup: cuardach `isvalid`, go léir le haghaidh PostGIS. Ligeann sé "
"seo céimseataí neamhbhailí ar thaobh an bhunachair shonraí a scagadh agus a "
"dheisiú."

msgid ""
"Added raster support for all :doc:`spatial lookups </ref/contrib/gis/"
"geoquerysets>`."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh tacaíocht raster leis do gach duine: doc: `cuardach spásúil` </ref/"
"contrib/gis/geoquerysets>."

msgid ":mod:`django.contrib.postgres`"
msgstr ":mod: `django.contrib.postgres`"

msgid ""
"For convenience, :class:`~django.contrib.postgres.fields.HStoreField` now "
"casts its keys and values to strings."
msgstr ""
"Ar mhaithe le áisiúlacht, caitheann :class: "
"`~django.contrib.postgres.fields.hStorefield` anois a heochracha agus a "
"luachanna chuig teaghráin."

msgid ":mod:`django.contrib.sessions`"
msgstr ":mod: `django.contrib.sessions`"

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`clearsessions` management command now removes file-based "
"sessions."
msgstr ""
"Baineann an t-ordú bainistíochta: DJadmin: `clearsessions` seisiúin "
"comhadbhunaithe anois."

msgid ":mod:`django.contrib.sites`"
msgstr ":mod: `django.contrib.sites`"

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.contrib.sites.models.Site` model now "
"supports :ref:`natural keys <topics-serialization-natural-keys>`."
msgstr ""
"<topics-serialization-natural-keys>Tacaíonn an tsamhail: Class: "
"`~django.contrib.sites.models.site` anois:ref: `eochracha nádúrtha `."

msgid ":mod:`django.contrib.staticfiles`"
msgstr ":mod: `django.contrib.staticfiles`"

msgid ""
"The :ttag:`static` template tag now uses ``django.contrib.staticfiles`` if "
"it's in ``INSTALLED_APPS``. This is especially useful for third-party apps "
"which can now always use ``{% load static %}`` (instead of ``{% load "
"staticfiles %}`` or ``{% load static from staticfiles %}``) and not worry "
"about whether or not the ``staticfiles`` app is installed."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann an chlib teimpléad:ttag: `static` ``django.contrib.staticfiles`` "
"anois má tá sé i ``INSTALLED_APPS``. Tá sé seo úsáideach go háirithe "
"d'aipeanna tríú páirtí ar féidir leo ``{% load static%} `a úsáid anois i "
"gcónaí (in ionad`` {% load staticfiles%} ``nó`` {% load static from "
"staticfiles%} ``) agus gan a bheith buartha faoi cibé an bhfuil an aip "
"`staticfiles`` suiteáilte nó nach bhfuil."

msgid ""
"You can :ref:`more easily customize <customize-staticfiles-ignore-patterns>` "
"the ``collectstatic --ignore`` option with a custom ``AppConfig``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat:ref: ``a shaincheapadh níos éasca `an rogha`` <customize-"
"staticfiles-ignore-patterns>collectstatic --ignore`` le `AppConfig`` "
"saincheaptha."

msgid "Cache"
msgstr "Cache"

msgid "The file-based cache backend now uses the highest pickling protocol."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann an cúltaca taisce comhbhunaithe anois an prótacal picling is airde."

msgid "CSRF"
msgstr "CSRF"

msgid ""
"The default :setting:`CSRF_FAILURE_VIEW`, ``views.csrf.csrf_failure()`` now "
"accepts an optional ``template_name`` parameter, defaulting to "
"``'403_csrf.html'``, to control the template used to render the page."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an réamhshocraithe:setting: `CSRF_FAILURE_VIEW`, "
"``views.csrf.csrf_fail () `anois le paraiméadar roghnach ``template_name``, "
"ag réamhshocrú go ``403_csrf.html'`, chun an teimpléad a úsáidtear chun an "
"leathanach a rinneadh a rialú."

msgid ""
"To protect against `BREACH`_ attacks, the CSRF protection mechanism now "
"changes the form token value on every request (while keeping an invariant "
"secret which can be used to validate the different tokens)."
msgstr ""
"Chun cosaint a dhéanamh i gcoinne ionsaithe `BREACH`_, athraíonn an "
"mheicníocht cosanta CSRF luach an chomhartha foirme anois ar gach iarratas "
"(agus rún inathraithe á choinneáil ar féidir a úsáid chun na comharthaí "
"éagsúla a bhailíochtú)."

msgid "Database backends"
msgstr "Cúltaca bunachar sonraí"

msgid "Temporal data subtraction was unified on all backends."
msgstr "Aontaíodh gearradh sonraí ama ar gach cúltaca."

msgid ""
"If the database supports it, backends can set "
"``DatabaseFeatures.can_return_ids_from_bulk_insert=True`` and implement "
"``DatabaseOperations.fetch_returned_insert_ids()`` to set primary keys on "
"objects created using ``QuerySet.bulk_create()``."
msgstr ""
"Má thacaíonn an bunachar sonraí leis, is féidir le cúltaca "
"``databaseFeatures.can_return_ids_from_bulk_insert=true`` a shocrú agus "
"``DatabaseOperations.fetch_returned_insert_ids ()`` a chur i bhfeidhm chun "
"eochracha bunscoile a shocrú ar rudaí a cruthaíodh ag baint úsáide as "
"`querySet.bulk_create () `."

msgid ""
"Added keyword arguments to the ``as_sql()`` methods of various expressions "
"(``Func``, ``When``, ``Case``, and ``OrderBy``) to allow database backends "
"to customize them without mutating ``self``, which isn't safe when using "
"different database backends. See the ``arg_joiner`` and ``**extra_context`` "
"parameters of :meth:`Func.as_sql() <django.db.models.Func.as_sql>` for an "
"example."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh argóintí eochairfhocal leis na modhanna ``as_sql () ``de nathanna "
"éagsúla (`Func``, `When``, `Case ``, agus `Orderby``) chun ligean do "
"chúltaca bunachar sonraí iad a shaincheapadh gan ``féin`` a athrú, rud nach "
"bhfuil sábháilte agus cúltaca bunachar sonraí éagsúla á úsáid. "
"<django.db.models.Func.as_sql>Féach na paraiméadair `arg_joiner`` agus "
"``**extra_context`` de:meth: `Func.as_sql () `mar shampla."

msgid "File Storage"
msgstr "Stóráil Comhad"

msgid ""
"Storage backends now present a timezone-aware API with new "
"methods :meth:`~django.core.files.storage.Storage.get_accessed_time`, :meth:`~django.core.files.storage.Storage.get_created_time`, "
"and :meth:`~django.core.files.storage.Storage.get_modified_time`. They "
"return a timezone-aware ``datetime`` if :setting:`USE_TZ` is ``True`` and a "
"naive ``datetime`` in the local timezone otherwise."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann cúltaca stórála API atá ar an eolas ag crios ama anois le modhanna "
"nua: meth: `~django.core.files.storage.storage.get_accessed_time`, :meth: "
"`~django.core.files.storage.storage.get_created_time`, agus:meth: "
"`~django.core.files.storage.get_get_get_get_geT_Am_athraithe'. Tugann siad "
"`datetime`` atá ar an eolas faoi chrios ama más rud é: socrú: ```True`` é "
"`USE_TZ` agus `datetime`` naif sa chrios ama áitiúil ar shlí eile."

msgid ""
"The new :meth:`Storage.generate_filename() "
"<django.core.files.storage.Storage.generate_filename>` method makes it "
"easier to implement custom storages that don't use the ``os.path`` calls "
"previously in :class:`~django.db.models.FileField`."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an modh nua:meth: `Storage.generate_filename () "
"<django.core.files.storage.Storage.generate_filename>`níos éasca stórais "
"saincheaptha a chur i bhfeidhm nach n-úsáideann na glaonna ``os.path`` "
"roimhe seo in:class: `~Django.db.Models.FileField`."

msgid "Forms"
msgstr "Foirmeacha"

msgid ""
"Form and widget ``Media`` is now served "
"using :mod:`django.contrib.staticfiles` if installed."
msgstr ""
"Freastalaítear foirm agus giuirléid ``Meáin ``anois ag baint úsáide as: mod: "
"`django.contrib.staticfiles` má tá sé suiteáilte."

msgid ""
"The ``<input>`` tag rendered by :class:`~django.forms.CharField` now "
"includes a ``minlength`` attribute if the field has a ``min_length``."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn an chlib <input>```a rinneadh ag:class: `~django.forms.charfield` "
"tréith ``minlength`` anois má tá ``min_length ``sa réimse."

msgid ""
"Required form fields now have the ``required`` HTML attribute. Set the "
"new :attr:`Form.use_required_attribute "
"<django.forms.Form.use_required_attribute>` attribute to ``False`` to "
"disable it. The ``required`` attribute isn't included on forms of formsets "
"because the browser validation may not be correct when adding and deleting "
"formsets."
msgstr ""
"Tá an tréith HTML “riachtanach” ag réimsí foirme riachtanacha anois. "
"<django.forms.Form.use_required_attribute>Socraigh an tréith nua:attr: "
"`Form.use_required_attribute` le ``False`` chun é a dhíchumasú. Ní chuirtear "
"an tréith “riachtanach” san áireamh ar fhoirmeacha foirmeacha mar b'fhéidir "
"nach mbeidh bailíochtú an bhrabhsálaí ceart agus foirmeacha á gcur leis agus "
"á scriosadh."

msgid "Generic Views"
msgstr "Tuairimí cineálacha"

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.views.generic.base.View` class can now be imported from "
"``django.views``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an rang:class: `~django.views.generic.base.view` a allmhairiú "
"anois ó ``django.views``."

msgid ""
"The :func:`~django.conf.urls.i18n.i18n_patterns` helper function can now be "
"used in a root URLConf specified using :attr:`request.urlconf "
"<django.http.HttpRequest.urlconf>`."
msgstr ""
"<django.http.HttpRequest.urlconf>Is féidir an fheidhm chúntóirí:func: "
"`~django.conf.urls.i18n.i18n_patterns` a úsáid anois i bhfréimhe URLConf a "
"shonraítear ag baint úsáide as: attr: `request.urlconf `."

msgid ""
"By setting the new ``prefix_default_language`` parameter "
"for :func:`~django.conf.urls.i18n.i18n_patterns` to ``False``, you can allow "
"accessing the default language without a URL prefix."
msgstr ""
"Trí an pharaiméadar nua ``prefix_default_language`` a shocrú fao:func: "
"`~django.conf.urls.i18n.i18n_patterns` go `False``, is féidir leat rochtain "
"a fháil ar an teanga réamhshocraithe gan réimír URL a cheadú."

msgid ""
":func:`~django.views.i18n.set_language` now returns a 204 status code (No "
"Content) for AJAX requests when there is no ``next`` parameter in ``POST`` "
"or ``GET``."
msgstr ""
":func: `~django.views.i18n.set_language` filleann cód stádais 204 (Gan "
"Ábhar) anois d'iarratais AJAX nuair nach bhfuil aon pharaiméadar ``next "
"``ann i `POST`` nó `GET``."

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.views.i18n.JavaScriptCatalog` "
"and :class:`~django.views.i18n.JSONCatalog` class-based views supersede the "
"deprecated ``javascript_catalog()`` and ``json_catalog()`` function-based "
"views. The new views are almost equivalent to the old ones except that by "
"default the new views collect all JavaScript strings in the ``djangojs`` "
"translation domain from all installed apps rather than only the JavaScript "
"strings from :setting:`LOCALE_PATHS`."
msgstr ""
"Is ionad tuairimí ranga-bhunaithe: `~Django.Views.I18N.JavaScriptCatalog` "
"agus:class: `~django.views.i18N.jsonCatalog` na tuairimí bunaithe ar fheidhm "
"“javascript_catalog () ``agus ``json_catalog () `. Tá na tuairimí nua "
"beagnach comhionann leis na seanchúin ach amháin go mbailíonn na tuairimí "
"nua gach teaghrán JavaScript i bhfearann aistriúcháin ``djangojs ``ó gach "
"aip suiteáilte seachas na teaghráin JavaScript ó:setting: `LOCALE_PATHS`."

msgid "Management Commands"
msgstr "Orduithe Bainistíochta"

msgid ""
":func:`~django.core.management.call_command` now returns the value returned "
"from the ``command.handle()`` method."
msgstr ""
":func: `~django.core.management.call_command` filleann anois an luach ar ais "
"ón modh ``command.handle () ``."

msgid ""
"The new :option:`check --fail-level` option allows specifying the message "
"level that will cause the command to exit with a non-zero status."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an rogha nua:option: `check --fail-level` leibhéal na "
"teachtaireachta a shonrú a fhágfaidh go n-imeoidh an t-ordú le stádas neamh-"
"nialas."

msgid ""
"The new :option:`makemigrations --check` option makes the command exit with "
"a non-zero status when model changes without migrations are detected."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an rogha nua:option: `makemigrations --check` imeacht an t-ordú le "
"stádas neamh-nialas nuair a bhraitear athruithe samhail gan imirce."

msgid ""
":djadmin:`makemigrations` now displays the path to the migration files that "
"it generates."
msgstr ""
":djadmin: Taispeánann `makemigrations` anois an cosán chuig na comhaid "
"imirce a ghineann sé."

msgid ""
"The :option:`shell --interface` option now accepts ``python`` to force use "
"of the \"plain\" Python interpreter."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an roghna:option: `shell --interface` anois le ``python`` chun an "
"ateangaire Python “simplí” a úsáid a chur i bhfeidhm."

msgid ""
"The new :option:`shell --command` option lets you run a command as Django "
"and exit, instead of opening the interactive shell."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an rogha nua:option: `shell --command` duit ordú a reáchtáil mar "
"Django agus imeacht, in ionad an bhlaosc idirghníomhach a oscailt."

msgid ""
"Added a warning to :djadmin:`dumpdata` if a proxy model is specified (which "
"results in no output) without its concrete parent."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh rabhadh chuig: djadmin: `dumpdata` má shonraítear samhail "
"seachfhreastalaí (nach bhfuil aon aschur mar thoradh air sin) gan a "
"thuismitheoir nithiúil."

msgid ""
"The new :attr:`BaseCommand.requires_migrations_checks "
"<django.core.management.BaseCommand.requires_migrations_checks>` attribute "
"may be set to ``True`` if you want your command to print a warning, "
"like :djadmin:`runserver` does, if the set of migrations on disk don't match "
"the migrations in the database."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an tréith nua:attr: `BaseCommand.requires_migrations_checks` a "
"shocrú go "
"``<django.core.management.BaseCommand.requires_migrations_checks>True`` más "
"mian leat d'ordú rabhadh a phriontáil, cosúil:djadmin: `runserver`, mura n-"
"oireann an tacar imirce ar an diosca leis na himirce sa bhunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"To assist with testing, :func:`~django.core.management.call_command` now "
"accepts a command object as the first argument."
msgstr ""
"Chun cabhrú le tástáil, glacann: func: "
"`~django.core.management.call_command` anois le réad ordaithe mar an chéad "
"argóint."

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`shell` command supports tab completion on systems using "
"``libedit``, e.g. macOS."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn an t-ordú: Djadmin: `shell` le críochnú cluaisín ar chórais a "
"úsáideann ``libedit``, m.sh. macOS."

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`inspectdb` command lets you choose what tables should be "
"inspected by specifying their names as arguments."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an t-ordú: DJAdmin: `inspectdb` duit na táblaí ba chóir a iniúchadh "
"a roghnú trína n-ainmneacha a shonrú mar argóintí."

msgid "Migrations"
msgstr "Imirce"

msgid "Added support for serialization of ``enum.Enum`` objects."
msgstr "Tacaíocht bhreise le haghaidh sraitheadh rudaí ``Enum.enum``."

msgid ""
"Added the ``elidable`` argument to "
"the :class:`~django.db.migrations.operations.RunSQL` "
"and :class:`~django.db.migrations.operations.RunPython` operations to allow "
"them to be removed when squashing migrations."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an argóint ``elidable`` leis na hoibríochtaí: :class: "
"`~django.db.migrations.operations.runsql` agus:class: "
"`~django.db.migrations.operations.runpython` chun ligean iad a bhaint agus "
"imirce á scrúdú."

msgid ""
"Added support for :ref:`non-atomic migrations <non-atomic-migrations>` by "
"setting the ``atomic`` attribute on a ``Migration``."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíocht bhreise le haghaidh: ref: `imirce neamh-adamhaíoch` tríd an tréith "
"``atomic` <non-atomic-migrations>`a shocrú ar ``Imirce``."

msgid ""
"The ``migrate`` and ``makemigrations`` commands now :ref:`check for a "
"consistent migration history <migration-history-consistency>`. If they find "
"some unapplied dependencies of an applied migration, "
"``InconsistentMigrationHistory`` is raised."
msgstr ""
"<migration-history-consistency>Na horduithe ``imirce`` agus "
"`makemigrations`` anois:ref: `seiceáil stair chomhsheasmhach imirce `. Má "
"aimsíonn siad roinnt spleáchais neamhfheidhmeacha ar imirce feidhmithe, "
"ardaítear ``InconsistentImmigrationHistory``."

msgid ""
"The :func:`~django.db.models.signals.pre_migrate` "
"and :func:`~django.db.models.signals.post_migrate` signals now dispatch "
"their migration ``plan`` and ``apps``."
msgstr ""
"Seolann na comharthaí: Func: `~django.db.models.signals.pre_migrate` "
"agus:func: `~django.db.models.signals.post_migrate` a n-imirce `plean`` agus "
"``apps`` anois."

msgid ""
"Reverse foreign keys from proxy models are now propagated to their concrete "
"class. The reverse relation attached by "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey` pointing to a proxy model is now "
"accessible as a descriptor on the proxied model class and may be referenced "
"in queryset filtering."
msgstr ""
"Déantar eochracha eachtracha droim ó mhúnlaí seachfhreastalaí a iomadú anois "
"Tá an gaol droim atá ceangailte ag a:class: `~Django.db.Models.ForeignKey` "
"ag díriú ar mhúnla seachfhreastalaí inrochtana anois mar thuairiscitheoir ar "
"an rang samhail seachfhreastaithe agus féadfar tagairt a thabhairt dó i "
"scagadh tacar fiosrúcháin."

msgid ""
"The new :meth:`Field.rel_db_type() <django.db.models.Field.rel_db_type>` "
"method returns the database column data type for fields such as "
"``ForeignKey`` and ``OneToOneField`` that point to another field."
msgstr ""
"Tugann an modh nua:meth: `Field.rel_DB_type () "
"<django.db.models.Field.rel_db_type>`cineál sonraí colún bunachar sonraí do "
"réimsí mar `ForeignKey`` agus ``OneTooneField`` a thugann pointe chuig "
"réimse eile."

msgid ""
"The :attr:`~django.db.models.Func.arity` class attribute is added "
"to :class:`~django.db.models.Func`. This attribute can be used to set the "
"number of arguments the function accepts."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear tréith aicme:attr: `~django.db.models.func.arity` leis a:class: "
"`~django.db.models.func`. Is féidir an tréith seo a úsáid chun líon na n-"
"argóintí a ghlacann an fheidhm a shocrú."

msgid ""
"Added :class:`~django.db.models.BigAutoField` which acts much like "
"an :class:`~django.db.models.AutoField` except that it is guaranteed to fit "
"numbers from ``1`` to ``9223372036854775807``."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh leis: Class: `~Django.db.Models.BigAutoField` a fheidhmíonn cosúil "
"leis an:class: `~django.db.models.autofield` ach amháin go bhfuil sé "
"ráthaithe go n-oirfidh sé uimhreacha ó ``1`` go `9223372036854775807``."

msgid ""
":meth:`QuerySet.in_bulk() <django.db.models.query.QuerySet.in_bulk>` may be "
"called without any arguments to return all objects in the queryset."
msgstr ""
":meth: Is féidir `queryset.in_bulk () "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.in_bulk>`a ghlaoch gan aon argóintí chun "
"gach rud sa tacar ceisteanna a thabhairt ar ais."

msgid ""
":attr:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey.related_query_name` now supports app "
"label and class interpolation using the ``'%(app_label)s'`` and ``'%"
"(class)s'`` strings."
msgstr ""
":attr: `~Django.db.Models.ForeignKey.Related_Query_Name` tacaíonn anois le "
"lipéad aip agus idirghabháil aicme ag baint úsáide as na teaghráin ``'% "
"(app_label) s'`` agus ```% (class) s'``."

msgid "Allowed overriding model fields inherited from abstract base classes."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaítear sár-réimsí samhla a fuarthas le hoidhreacht ó bhunaicmí teibí."

msgid ""
"The :func:`~django.db.models.prefetch_related_objects` function is now a "
"public API."
msgstr ""
"Is API poiblí anois é an fheidhm:func: "
"`~django.db.models.prefetch_related_objects`."

msgid ""
":meth:`QuerySet.bulk_create() <django.db.models.query.QuerySet.bulk_create>` "
"sets the primary key on objects when using PostgreSQL."
msgstr ""
":meth: Socraíonn `querySet.bulk_create () "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.bulk_create>`an príomh-eochair ar rudaí "
"agus PostgreSQL á úsáid agat."

msgid "Added the :class:`~django.db.models.functions.Cast` database function."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh feidhm bunachar sonraí: class: `~django.db.models.functions.cast` "
"leis."

msgid ""
"A proxy model may now inherit multiple proxy models that share a common non-"
"abstract parent class."
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh samhail seachfhreastalaí teacht le hoidhreacht anois ar mhúnlaí "
"seachfhreastalaí iolracha a roinneann aicme tuismitheora neamhtheibí "
"coitianta."

msgid ""
"Added :class:`~django.db.models.functions.Extract` functions to extract "
"datetime components as integers, such as year and hour."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh leis: Class: `~Django.db.Models.Functions.Extract` feidhmeanna chun "
"comhpháirteanna dáta-ama a bhaint mar shláimhreacha, mar shampla bliain agus "
"uair an chloig."

msgid ""
"Added :class:`~django.db.models.functions.Trunc` functions to truncate a "
"date or datetime to a significant component. They enable queries like sales-"
"per-day or sales-per-hour."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh leis: Class: `~Django.db.Models.Functions.Trunc` feidhmíonn dáta nó "
"dáta-am a ghearradh go comhpháirt shuntasach. Cumasaíonn siad ceisteanna mar "
"dhíolacháin in aghaidh an lae nó díolacháin in aghaidh na huaire."

msgid ""
"``Model.__init__()`` now sets values of virtual fields from its keyword "
"arguments."
msgstr ""
"``Samhail. Socraíonn __init__ () ``luachanna réimsí fíorúla anois óna "
"argóintí eochairfhocal."

msgid ""
"The new :attr:`Meta.base_manager_name "
"<django.db.models.Options.base_manager_name>` "
"and :attr:`Meta.default_manager_name "
"<django.db.models.Options.default_manager_name>` options allow controlling "
"the :attr:`~django.db.models.Model._base_manager` "
"and :attr:`~django.db.models.Model._default_manager`, respectively."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.Options.default_manager_name>Ceadaíonn na roghanna "
"nua:attr: `Meta.Base_Manager_name `agus:attr: "
"`Meta.Default_Manager_name<django.db.models.Options.base_manager_name>` an: "
"attr: `~django.db.models.model a rialú. _base_manager` agus:attr: "
"`~Django.db.Models.Model. _default_manager`, faoi seach."

msgid "Requests and Responses"
msgstr "Iarrataí agus Freagraí"

msgid "Added ``request.user`` to the debug view."
msgstr "Cuireadh ``request.user`` leis an radharc dífhabhtaithe."

msgid ""
"Added :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse` "
"methods :meth:`~django.http.HttpResponse.readable()` "
"and :meth:`~django.http.HttpResponse.seekable()` to make an instance a "
"stream-like object and allow wrapping it with :py:class:`io.TextIOWrapper`."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh leis: Class: `~django.http.httpResponse` modh:meth: "
"`~django.http.http.HttpResponse.readable () `agus:meth: "
"`~django.http.httpResponse.seekable ()` chun sampla a dhéanamh ina réad "
"cosúil le sruth agus ligean é a fhilleadh le:py:class: `IO.TextioWrapper`."

msgid ""
"Added the :attr:`HttpRequest.content_type "
"<django.http.HttpRequest.content_type>` "
"and :attr:`~django.http.HttpRequest.content_params` attributes which are "
"parsed from the ``CONTENT_TYPE`` header."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh na tréithe: attr: `HttpRequest.content_type `agus:attr: "
"`~django.http.httpRequest.content_params` a pháirsítear ón gceannteideal "
"``CONTENT_TY <django.http.HttpRequest.content_type>PE``."

msgid ""
"The parser for ``request.COOKIES`` is simplified to better match the "
"behavior of browsers. ``request.COOKIES`` may now contain cookies that are "
"invalid according to :rfc:`6265` but are possible to set via "
"``document.cookie``."
msgstr ""
"Déantar an parser do ``Request.cookies`` a shimpliú chun iompar brabhsálaí a "
"mheaitseáil níos fearr. D'fhéadfadh go mbeadh fianáin anois ag "
"`request.cookies`` atá neamhbhailí de réir: rfc: `6265` ach is féidir iad a "
"shocrú trí `document.cookie``."

msgid "Serialization"
msgstr "Sraitheadh"

msgid ""
"The ``django.core.serializers.json.DjangoJSONEncoder`` now knows how to "
"serialize lazy strings, typically used for translatable content."
msgstr ""
"Tá a fhios ag an `django.core.serializers.json.djangojsonEncoder`` anois "
"conas teaghráin leisciúil a shraitheadh, a úsáidtear de ghnáth le haghaidh "
"ábhar inaistrithe."

msgid ""
"Added the ``autoescape`` option to "
"the :class:`~django.template.backends.django.DjangoTemplates` backend and "
"the :class:`~django.template.Engine` class."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an rogha ``autoescape`` leis an:class: "
"`~django.template.backends.django.djangoTemplates` cúltaca agus an "
"ranga:class: `~django.template.engine`."

msgid ""
"Added the ``is`` and ``is not`` comparison operators to the :ttag:`if` tag."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh na hoibreoirí comparáide ``is ``agus ``níl`` leis an gclibe:ttag: "
"`if `."

msgid ""
"Allowed :tfilter:`dictsort` to order a list of lists by an element at a "
"specified index."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaí:TFilter: `dictsort` liosta liostaí a ordú de réir eilimint ag innéacs "
"sonraithe."

msgid ""
"The :func:`~django.template.context_processors.debug` context processor "
"contains queries for all database aliases instead of only the default alias."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn an próiseálaí comhthéacs: Func: "
"`~django.template.context_processors.debug` ceisteanna maidir le gach ainm "
"bunachar sonraí in ionad an ailias réamhshocraithe amháin."

msgid ""
"Added relative path support for string arguments of the :ttag:`extends` "
"and :ttag:`include` template tags."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh tacaíocht coibhneasta coibhneasta le haghaidh argóintí teaghráin de "
"chlibeanna teimpléad: ttag: `extends` agus:ttag: `include`."

msgid "Tests"
msgstr "Tástálacha"

msgid ""
"To better catch bugs, :class:`~django.test.TestCase` now checks deferrable "
"database constraints at the end of each test."
msgstr ""
"Chun fabhtanna a ghabháil níos fearr, seiceálann: class: "
"`~django.test.testcase` srianta bunachar sonraí in-iarchurraithe anois ag "
"deireadh gach tástála."

msgid ""
"Tests and test cases can be :ref:`marked with tags <topics-tagging-tests>` "
"and run selectively with the new :option:`test --tag` and :option:`test --"
"exclude-tag` options."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le tástálacha agus cásanna tástála a bheith: ref: `marcáilte le "
"clibeanna <topics-tagging-tests>`agus rith go roghnach leis na roghanna "
"nua:option: `test --tag` agus:option: `test --exclude-tag`."

msgid ""
"You can now login and use sessions with the test client even "
"if :mod:`django.contrib.sessions` is not in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat logáil isteach anois agus seisiúin a úsáid leis an gcliant "
"tástála fiú mura bhfuil: mod: `django.contrib.sessions` in:setting: "
"`INSTALLED_APPS`."

msgid ""
"An addition in :func:`django.setup()` allows URL resolving that happens "
"outside of the request/response cycle (e.g. in management commands and "
"standalone scripts) to take :setting:`FORCE_SCRIPT_NAME` into account when "
"it is set."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn breise in:func: `django.setup () `réiteach URL a tharlaíonn "
"lasmuigh den timthriall iarrata/freagartha (m.sh. in orduithe bainistíochta "
"agus scripteanna neamhspleácha): socrú: `FORCE_SCRIPT_NAME` a chur san "
"áireamh nuair a shocraítear é."

msgid "Validators"
msgstr "Bailíochtóirí"

msgid ""
":class:`~django.core.validators.URLValidator` now limits the length of "
"domain name labels to 63 characters and the total length of domain names to "
"253 characters per :rfc:`1034`."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.core.validators.urlvalidator` teorann anois fad na lipéid "
"ainm fearainn go 63 carachtar agus fad iomlán na n-ainmneacha fearainn go "
"253 carachtar per:rfc: `1034`."

msgid ""
":func:`~django.core.validators.int_list_validator` now accepts an optional "
"``allow_negative`` boolean parameter, defaulting to ``False``, to allow "
"negative integers."
msgstr ""
":func: Glacann `~django.core.validators.int_list_validator` anois le "
"paraiméadar boolean roghnach ``allow_negative``, ag réamhshocrú go "
"``False``, chun sláimhreacha diúltacha a cheadú."

msgid "Backwards incompatible changes in 1.10"
msgstr "Athruithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha ar ais i 1.10"

msgid ""
"In addition to the changes outlined in this section, be sure to review "
"the :ref:`removed-features-1.10` for the features that have reached the end "
"of their deprecation cycle and therefore been removed. If you haven't "
"updated your code within the deprecation timeline for a given feature, its "
"removal may appear as a backwards incompatible change."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith leis na hathruithe a leagtar amach sa chuid seo, déan cinnte "
"athbhreithniú a dhéanamh ar:ref: `removed-features-1.10` do na gnéithe a "
"shroich deireadh a dtimthriall díghabhála agus dá bhrí sin baineadh. Mura "
"ndearna tú do chód a nuashonrú laistigh den amlíne díscoilte do ghné ar "
"leith, d'fhéadfadh go mbeadh sé a bhaint mar athrú neamh-chomhoiriúnach ar "
"chúl."

msgid "Database backend API"
msgstr "API cúltaca bunachar sonraí"

msgid ""
"GIS's ``AreaField`` uses an unspecified underlying numeric type that could "
"in practice be any numeric Python type. ``decimal.Decimal`` values retrieved "
"from the database are now converted to ``float`` to make it easier to "
"combine them with values used by the GIS libraries."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann “Areafield” GIS cineál uimhriúil bunúsach neamhshonraithe a "
"d'fhéadfadh a bheith i gcleachtas aon chineál uimhriúil Python. Déantar "
"luachanna ``Decimal.Decimal`` a aisghabháiltear ón mbunachar sonraí a "
"thiontú anois go ``float`` chun go mbeidh sé níos éasca iad a chomhcheangal "
"le luachanna a úsáideann na leabharlanna GIS."

msgid ""
"In order to enable temporal subtraction you must set the "
"``supports_temporal_subtraction`` database feature flag to ``True`` and "
"implement the ``DatabaseOperations.subtract_temporals()`` method. This "
"method should return the SQL and parameters required to compute the "
"difference in microseconds between the ``lhs`` and ``rhs`` arguments in the "
"datatype used to store :class:`~django.db.models.DurationField`."
msgstr ""
"D'fhonn gearradh ama a chumasú ní mór duit bratach gné bunachar sonraí "
"``supports_temporal_subtraction`` a shocrú go ``True`` agus an modh "
"``DatabaseOperations.subtract_temporals ()`` a chur i bhfeidhm. Ba cheart "
"don mhodh seo an SQL agus na paraiméadair a theastaíonn chun an difríocht i "
"micreasoicind idir na hargóintí `lhs`` agus `rhs`` a ríomh sa chineál sonraí "
"a úsáidtear chun stóráil:class: `~Django.db.Models.DurationField` a ríomh."

msgid ""
"``select_related()`` prohibits non-relational fields for nested relations"
msgstr ""
"Cuireann ``select_related () `cosc ar réimsí neamhghaolmhara do chaidreamh "
"neadaithe"

msgid ""
"Django 1.8 added validation for non-relational fields in "
"``select_related()``:"
msgstr ""
"Chuir Django 1.8 bailíochtú le haghaidh réimsí neamhghaolmhara i "
"``select_related () ``:"

msgid "But it didn't prohibit nested non-relation fields as it does now:"
msgstr ""
"Ach níor chuir sé cosc ar réimsí neamhghaolmhara neadaithe mar a dhéanann sé "
"anois:"

msgid ""
"``_meta.get_fields()`` returns consistent reverse fields for proxy models"
msgstr ""
"Tugann ``_meta.get_fields () ``réimsí comhsheasmhacha droim ar ais do "
"mhúnlaí seachfhreastalaí"

msgid ""
"Before Django 1.10, the :meth:`~django.db.models.options.Options.get_fields` "
"method returned different reverse fields when called on a proxy model "
"compared to its proxied concrete class. This inconsistency was fixed by "
"returning the full set of fields pointing to a concrete class or one of its "
"proxies in both cases."
msgstr ""
"Roimh Django 1.10, chuir an modh: meth: "
"`~django.db.models.options.options.get_fields` réimsí droim éagsúla ar ais "
"nuair a ghlaoigh sé ar mhúnla seachfhreastalaí i gcomparáid lena aicme "
"coincréite seachfhála. Socraíodh an neamhréireacht seo tríd an tsraith "
"iomlán réimsí a thabhairt ar ais ag díriú ar aicme coincréite nó ar cheann "
"dá sheirbhísí sa dá chás."

msgid ""
":attr:`AbstractUser.username <django.contrib.auth.models.User.username>` "
"``max_length`` increased to 150"
msgstr ""
"<django.contrib.auth.models.User.username>:attr: `Abstractuser.username "
"```max_length ``méadaithe go 150"

msgid ""
"A migration for :attr:`django.contrib.auth.models.User.username` is "
"included. If you have a custom user model inheriting from ``AbstractUser``, "
"you'll need to generate and apply a database migration for your user model."
msgstr ""
"Tá imirce le haghaidh: attr: `django.contrib.auth.models.user.userName` san "
"áireamh. Má tá samhail úsáideora saincheaptha agat ag oidhreacht ó "
"``AbstractUser`, beidh ort imirce bunachar sonraí a ghiniúint agus a chur i "
"bhfeidhm do do mhúnla úsáideora."

msgid ""
"We considered an increase to 254 characters to more easily allow the use of "
"email addresses (which are limited to 254 characters) as usernames but "
"rejected it due to a MySQL limitation.  When using the ``utf8mb4`` encoding "
"(recommended for proper Unicode support), MySQL can only create unique "
"indexes with 191 characters by default. Therefore, if you need a longer "
"length, please use a custom user model."
msgstr ""
"Bhreathnaigh muid méadú go 254 carachtar chun seoltaí ríomhphoist a úsáid "
"níos éasca (atá teoranta do 254 carachtar) mar ainmneacha úsáideora ach "
"dhiúltaigh muid é mar gheall ar theorannú MySQL. Agus an ionchódú `utf8mb4` "
"á úsáid agat (moltar le haghaidh tacaíochta ceart Unicode), ní féidir le "
"MySQL ach innéacsanna uathúla a chruthú le 191 carachtar de réir "
"réamhshocraithe. Dá bhrí sin, má theastaíonn fad níos faide uait, bain úsáid "
"as samhail úsáideora saincheaptha."

msgid ""
"If you want to preserve the 30 character limit for usernames, use a custom "
"form when creating a user or changing usernames::"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat an teorainn 30 carachtar d'ainmneacha úsáideora a chaomhnú, "
"bain úsáid as foirm saincheaptha agus úsáideoir á chruthú agat nó agus "
"ainmneacha úsáideora á athrú agat:"

msgid ""
"If you wish to keep this restriction in the admin, set "
"``UserAdmin.add_form`` to use this form::"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat an srian seo a choinneáil sa riarachán, socraigh "
"``UserAdmin.Add_Form ``chun an fhoirm seo a úsáid:"

msgid "Dropped support for PostgreSQL 9.1"
msgstr "Tacaíocht titim do PostgreSQL 9.1"

msgid ""
"Upstream support for PostgreSQL 9.1 ends in September 2016. As a "
"consequence, Django 1.10 sets PostgreSQL 9.2 as the minimum version it "
"officially supports."
msgstr ""
"Críochnaíonn tacaíocht suas srutha do PostgreSQL 9.1 i Meán Fómhair 2016. "
"Mar thoradh air sin, leagann Django 1.10 PostgreSQL 9.2 mar an leagan íosta "
"a thacaíonn sé go hoifigiúil."

msgid "``runserver`` output goes through logging"
msgstr "Téann aschur ``runserver ``trí logáil"

msgid ""
"Request and response handling of the ``runserver`` command is sent to "
"the :ref:`django-server-logger` logger instead of to ``sys.stderr``. If you "
"disable Django's logging configuration or override it with your own, you'll "
"need to add the appropriate logging configuration if you want to see that "
"output::"
msgstr ""
"Seoltar láimhseáil iarratais agus freagartha an ordaithe ``runserver`` chuig "
"an logger:ref: `django-server-logger` in ionad chuig `sys.stderr``. Má "
"dhíchumraíonn tú cumraíocht logála Django nó má dhíchumraíonn tú é le do "
"chuid féin, beidh ort an chumraíocht logála cuí a chur leis más mian leat an "
"t-aschur sin a fheiceáil:"

msgid "``auth.CustomUser`` and ``auth.ExtensionUser`` test models were removed"
msgstr ""
"Baineadh samhlacha tástála `Auth.CustomUser`` agus ``Auth.ExtensionUser``"

msgid ""
"Since the introduction of migrations for the contrib apps in Django 1.8, the "
"tables of these custom user test models were not created anymore making them "
"unusable in a testing context."
msgstr ""
"Ó tugadh isteach imirce do na feidhmchláir contrib i Django 1.8, níor "
"cruthaíodh táblaí na samhlacha tástála úsáideora saincheaptha seo a "
"thuilleadh rud a fhágann go bhfuil siad neamhúsáidte i gcomhthéacs tástála."

msgid ""
"Apps registry is no longer auto-populated when unpickling models outside of "
"Django"
msgstr ""
"Ní dhéantar clárlann apps go huathoibríoch a thuilleadh nuair a dhíphictear "
"samhlacha lasmuigh"

msgid ""
"The apps registry is no longer auto-populated when unpickling models. This "
"was added in Django 1.7.2 as an attempt to allow unpickling models outside "
"of Django, such as in an RQ worker, without calling ``django.setup()``, but "
"it creates the possibility of a deadlock. To adapt your code in the case of "
"RQ, you can `provide your own worker script <https://python-rq.org/docs/"
"workers/>`_ that calls ``django.setup()``."
msgstr ""
"Níl clárlann na n-aipeanna daonra go huathoibríoch a thuilleadh agus "
"samhlacha á Cuireadh é seo leis i Django 1.7.2 mar iarracht samhlacha "
"neamhphicilte a cheadú lasmuigh de Django, mar shampla in oibrí RQ, gan "
"glaoch ar ``django.setup () `, ach cruthaíonn sé an fhéidearthacht go mbeadh "
"caoileadh ann. Chun do chód a oiriúnú i gcás RQ, is féidir leat `scriptúr "
"oibrí féin a sholáthar `_ a ghlaonn ``django.setup (< https://python-rq.org/"
"docs/workers/>) ``."

msgid "Removed null assignment check for non-null foreign key fields"
msgstr ""
"Seiceáil sannadh neall bainte le haghaidh príomhréimsí eachtracha neamh-"

msgid ""
"In older versions, assigning ``None`` to a non-nullable ``ForeignKey`` or "
"``OneToOneField`` raised ``ValueError('Cannot assign None: \"model.field\" "
"does not allow null values.')``. For consistency with other model fields "
"which don't have a similar check, this check is removed."
msgstr ""
"I leaganacha níos sine, a shannadh ``None`` do `ForeignKey`` neamh-neamh-"
"neamhrialaithe nó ``OneTooneField`` ardaithe ``ValueError ('Ní féidir Aon a "
"shannadh: ní cheadaíonn “model.field” luachanna null. ') ``. Le haghaidh "
"comhsheasmhachta le réimsí samhlacha eile nach bhfuil seiceáil den chineál "
"céanna acu, baintear an seiceáil seo."

msgid ""
"Removed weak password hashers from the default ``PASSWORD_HASHERS`` setting"
msgstr ""
"Bainte hashers pasfhocal lag ón socrú réamhshocraithe ``PASSWORD_HASHERS``"

msgid ""
"Django 0.90 stored passwords as unsalted MD5. Django 0.91 added support for "
"salted SHA1 with automatic upgrade of passwords when a user logs in. Django "
"1.4 added PBKDF2 as the default password hasher."
msgstr ""
"Stóráilte pasfhocail Django 0.90 mar MD5 neamh-shailte. Chuir Django 0.91 "
"tacaíocht le haghaidh SHA1 saillte le pasfhocail a uasghrádú uathoibríoch "
"nuair a logálann úsáideoir isteach. Chuir Django 1.4 PBKDF2 leis mar an "
"hasher pasfhocal réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"If you have an old Django project with MD5 or SHA1 (even salted) encoded "
"passwords, be aware that these can be cracked fairly easily with today's "
"hardware. To make Django users acknowledge continued use of weak hashers, "
"the following hashers are removed from the "
"default :setting:`PASSWORD_HASHERS` setting:"
msgstr ""

msgid "``\"django.contrib.auth.hashers.SHA1PasswordHasher\"``"
msgstr ""

msgid "``\"django.contrib.auth.hashers.MD5PasswordHasher\"``"
msgstr ""

msgid "``\"django.contrib.auth.hashers.UnsaltedSHA1PasswordHasher\"``"
msgstr ""

msgid "``\"django.contrib.auth.hashers.UnsaltedMD5PasswordHasher\"``"
msgstr ""

msgid "``\"django.contrib.auth.hashers.CryptPasswordHasher\"``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Consider using a :ref:`wrapped password hasher <wrapping-password-hashers>` "
"to strengthen the hashes in your database. If that's not feasible, add "
"the :setting:`PASSWORD_HASHERS` setting to your project and add back any "
"hashers that you need."
msgstr ""
"Smaoinigh ar a:ref: `phasfhocal fillte hasher <wrapping-password-hashers>`a "
"úsáid chun na hashes i do bhunachar sonraí a neartú. Mura bhfuil sé sin "
"indéanta, cuir an socrú:setting: `PASSWORD_HASHERS` le do thionscadal agus "
"cuir aon hashers a theastaíonn uait ar ais."

msgid ""
"You can check if your database has any of the removed hashers like this::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat a sheiceáil an bhfuil aon cheann de na hashers bainte mar seo "
"ag do bhunachar sonraí:"

msgid ""
"``Field.get_prep_lookup()`` and ``Field.get_db_prep_lookup()`` methods are "
"removed"
msgstr ""
"Baintear modhanna ``Field.get_prep_lookup () ``agus "
"``Field.get_db_prep_lookup ()``"

msgid ""
"If you have a custom field that implements either of these methods, register "
"a custom lookup for it. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Má tá réimse saincheaptha agat a chuireann ceachtar de na modhanna seo i "
"bhfeidhm, cláraigh cuardach saincheaptha dó. Mar shampla::"

msgid "Support for SpatiaLite < 3.0 and GEOS < 3.3 is dropped."
msgstr "Titear tacaíocht do SpatiaLite <3.0 agus GEOS <3.3."

msgid ""
"The ``add_postgis_srs()`` backwards compatibility alias for "
"``django.contrib.gis.utils.add_srs_entry()`` is removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear an ailias comhoiriúnachta ``add_postgis_srs () ``ar chúl do "
"`django.contrib.gis.utils.add_srs_entry ()``."

msgid ""
"On Oracle/GIS, the :class:`~django.contrib.gis.db.models.functions.Area` "
"aggregate function now returns a ``float`` instead of ``decimal.Decimal``. "
"(It's still wrapped in a measure of square meters.)"
msgstr ""
"Ar Oracle/GIS, filleann an fheidhm chomhiomlán:: class: "
"`~django.contrib.gis.db.Models.Functions.Area` ``float`` anois in ionad "
"``Decimal.Decimal``. (Tá sé fós fillte i dtomhas méadar cearnach.)"

msgid ""
"The default :class:`~django.contrib.gis.geos.GEOSGeometry` representation "
"(WKT output) is trimmed by default. That is, instead of ``POINT "
"(23.0000000000000000 5.5000000000000000)``, you'll get ``POINT (23 5.5)``."
msgstr ""
"Déantar an ionadaíocht réamhshocraithe: class: "
"`~django.contrib.gis.geos.geosgeometry` (aschur WKT) a ghearradh de réir "
"réamhshocraithe. Is é sin, in ionad ``POINT (23.0000000000000000 "
"5.5000000000000000) ``, gheobhaidh tú ``POINT (23 5.5)``."

msgid ""
"Maximum size of a request body and the number of GET/POST parameters is "
"limited"
msgstr ""
"Tá uasmhéid comhlachta iarratais agus líon na bparaiméadair GET/POST teoranta"

msgid ""
"Two new settings help mitigate denial-of-service attacks via large requests:"
msgstr ""
"Cuidíonn dhá shocrú nua le hionsaithe diúltaithe seirbhíse a mhaolú trí "
"iarratais mhóra:"

msgid ""
":setting:`DATA_UPLOAD_MAX_MEMORY_SIZE` limits the size that a request body "
"may be. File uploads don't count toward this limit."
msgstr ""
":setting: `DATA_UPLOAD_MAX_MEMORY_SIZE` teorainn leis an méid a d'fhéadfadh "
"comhlacht iarratais a bheith. Ní chomhaireann uaslódálacha comhad i dtreo an "
"teorainn seo."

msgid ""
":setting:`DATA_UPLOAD_MAX_NUMBER_FIELDS` limits the number of GET/POST "
"parameters that are parsed."
msgstr ""
":setting: `DATA_UPLOAD_MAX_NUMBER_FIELDS` teorainn le líon na bparaiméadair "
"GET/POST a pháirsítear."

msgid ""
"Applications that receive unusually large form posts may need to tune these "
"settings."
msgstr ""
"Seans go mbeidh ar iarratais a fhaigheann postanna foirmeacha neamhghnácha "
"móra na socruithe seo a choigeartú."

msgid "Miscellaneous"
msgstr "Ilghnéitheach"

msgid ""
"The ``repr()`` of a ``QuerySet`` is wrapped in ``<QuerySet >`` to "
"disambiguate it from a plain list when debugging."
msgstr ""
"<QuerySet >Tá an `repr () ``de `QuerySet`` fillte i`` ``chun é a dhíbhriú ó "
"liosta simplí agus é á dífhabhtú."

msgid ""
"``utils.version.get_version()`` returns :pep:`440` compliant release "
"candidate versions (e.g. '1.10rc1' instead of '1.10c1')."
msgstr ""
"``utils.version.get_version () `filleadh: pep: leaganacha iarrthóirí "
"scaoilte comhlíontacha `440` (m.sh. '1.10rc1' in ionad '1.10c1')."

msgid ""
"CSRF token values are now required to be strings of 64 alphanumerics; values "
"of 32 alphanumerics, as set by older versions of Django by default, are "
"automatically replaced by strings of 64 characters. Other values are "
"considered invalid. This should only affect developers or users who replace "
"these tokens."
msgstr ""
"Ceanglaítear anois gur teaghráin de 64 alfa-uimhriúla iad luachanna "
"dearbháin CSRF; cuirtear teaghráin de 64 carachtar in ionad luachanna 32 "
"alfa-uimhriúla, mar atá socraithe ag leaganacha níos sine de Django de réir "
"réamhshocraithe. Meastar luachanna eile a bheith neamhbhailí. Níor cheart go "
"ndéanfadh sé seo difear ach d’fhorbróirí nó d’úsáideoirí a athsholáthróidh "
"na comharthaí seo."

msgid ""
"The ``LOGOUT_URL`` setting is removed as Django hasn't made use of it since "
"pre-1.0. If you use it in your project, you can add it to your project's "
"settings. The default value was ``'/accounts/logout/'``."
msgstr ""
"Baintear an socrú ``LOGOUT_URL` toisc nár bhain Django úsáid as ó roimh 1.0. "
"Má úsáideann tú é i do thionscadal, is féidir leat é a chur le socruithe do "
"thionscadail. Ba é an luach réamhshocraithe ná ``'/cuntais/logáil/'``."

msgid ""
"Objects with a ``close()`` method such as files and generators passed "
"to :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse` are now closed immediately instead of "
"when the WSGI server calls ``close()`` on the response."
msgstr ""
"Tá rudaí le modh ``close () ``mar chomhaid agus gineadóirí a chuirtear "
"chuig: class: `~django.http.httpResponse` dúnta anois láithreach in ionad "
"nuair a ghlaonn an freastalaí WSGI ``close ()`` ar an bhfreagra."

msgid ""
"A redundant ``transaction.atomic()`` call in ``QuerySet.update_or_create()`` "
"is removed. This may affect query counts tested by "
"``TransactionTestCase.assertNumQueries()``."
msgstr ""
"Baintear glao iomarcach ``transaction.atomic () ``i "
"`QuerySet.Update_or_create ()``. D'fhéadfadh sé seo dul i bhfeidhm ar "
"chomhaireamh ceisteanna a ndearnadh tástáil ag "
"``TransactionTestCase.assertNumQueries () ``."

msgid ""
"Support for ``skip_validation`` in ``BaseCommand.execute(**options)`` is "
"removed. Use ``skip_checks`` (added in Django 1.7) instead."
msgstr ""
"Baintear tacaíocht do `skip_validation`` i ``BaseCommand.execute "
"(**roghanna) ``. Úsáid ``skip_checks`` (cuireadh i Django 1.7) ina ionad."

msgid ""
":djadmin:`loaddata` now raises a ``CommandError`` instead of showing a "
"warning when the specified fixture file is not found."
msgstr ""
": djadmin: Ardaíonn `loaddata` ``CommandError`` anois in ionad rabhadh a "
"thaispeáint nuair nach bhfaightear an comhad daingneáin sonraithe."

msgid ""
"Instead of directly accessing the ``LogEntry.change_message`` attribute, "
"it's now better to call the ``LogEntry.get_change_message()`` method which "
"will provide the message in the current language."
msgstr ""
"In ionad rochtain a fháil go díreach ar an tréith "
"``Logentry.change_message``, is fearr anois glaoch ar an modh "
"``Logentry.get_change_message () ``a sholáthróidh an teachtaireacht sa "
"teanga reatha."

msgid ""
"The default error views now raise ``TemplateDoesNotExist`` if a nonexistent "
"``template_name`` is specified."
msgstr ""
"Ardaíonn na tuairimí earráide réamhshocraithe ``TemplateDoesNotExist`` anois "
"má shonraítear ``template_name`` nach bhfuil ann."

msgid ""
"The unused ``choices`` keyword argument of the ``Select`` and "
"``SelectMultiple`` widgets' ``render()`` method is removed. The ``choices`` "
"argument of the ``render_options()`` method is also removed, making "
"``selected_choices`` the first argument."
msgstr ""
"Baintear an argóint eochairfhocal ``roghnaí` neamhúsáidte den mhodh "
"``Relect`` agus ``SelectMultiple`` `render () ``giuirléidí ``Render ()``. "
"Baintear an argóint ``roghna`` den mhodh ``render_options () ``freisin, rud "
"a fhágann go bhfuil `roghnaí_roghnaithe`` an chéad argóint."

msgid ""
"Tests that violate deferrable database constraints will now error when run "
"on a database that supports deferrable constraints."
msgstr ""
"Déanfaidh tástálacha a sháraíonn srianta bunachar sonraí in-iarchurtha "
"earráid anois nuair a reáchtáiltear iad ar bhunachar sonraí a thacaíonn le "
"srianta in-iarchurtha."

msgid ""
"Built-in management commands now use indexing of keys in ``options``, e.g. "
"``options['verbosity']``, instead of ``options.get()`` and no longer perform "
"any type coercion. This could be a problem if you're calling commands using "
"``Command.execute()`` (which bypasses the argument parser that sets a "
"default value) instead of :func:`~django.core.management.call_command`. "
"Instead of calling ``Command.execute()``, pass the command object as the "
"first argument to ``call_command()``."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann orduithe bainistíochta ionsuite anois innéacsú eochracha i "
"“roghanna”, m.sh. ``options ['verbosity'] ``, in ionad ``options.get ()`` "
"agus ní dhéanann siad aon chineál comhéigeantach a thuilleadh. D'fhéadfadh "
"sé seo a bheith ina fhadhb má tá tú ag glaoch orduithe ag baint úsáide as "
"``Command.execute () ``(a sheachnaíonn an parser argóint a leagann luach "
"réamhshocraithe) in ionad:func: `~django.core.management.call_command`. In "
"ionad glaoch ar ``Command.execute () ``, pas an réad ordaithe mar an chéad "
"argóint chuig ``call_command ()``."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.contrib.auth.backends.ModelBackend` "
"and :class:`~django.contrib.auth.backends.RemoteUserBackend` now reject "
"inactive users. This means that inactive users can't login and will be "
"logged out if they are switched from ``is_active=True`` to ``False``. If you "
"need the previous behavior, use the "
"new :class:`~django.contrib.auth.backends.AllowAllUsersModelBackend` "
"or :class:`~django.contrib.auth.backends.AllowAllUsersRemoteUserBackend` "
"in :setting:`AUTHENTICATION_BACKENDS` instead."
msgstr ""
"Diúltaíonn: `~django.contrib.auth.backends.modelBackend` agus:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.backends.remoteUserBackend` úsáideoirí "
"neamhghníomhacha anois. Ciallaíonn sé seo nach féidir le húsáideoirí "
"neamhghníomhacha logáil isteach agus logálfar amach iad má aistrítear iad ó "
"``is_active=true`` go ``False``. Má theastaíonn an t-iompar roimhe seo uait, "
"bain úsáid as an nua:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.backends.allowAllUsersModelBackend` nó:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.backends.allowAllUsersRemoteUserBackend` in:setting: "
"`AUTHENTICATION_BACKENDS` ina ionad."

msgid ""
"In light of the previous change, the test "
"client's :meth:`~django.test.Client.login()` method no longer always rejects "
"inactive users but instead delegates this decision to the authentication "
"backend. :meth:`~django.test.Client.force_login()` also delegates the "
"decision to the authentication backend, so if you're using the default "
"backends, you need to use an active user."
msgstr ""
"I bhfianaise an athrú roimhe seo, ní dhiúltaíonn modh na cliant tástála: "
"meth: `~django.test.client.login () `úsáideoirí neamhghníomhacha a "
"thuilleadh ach ina ionad sin tarlacadh an cinneadh seo chuig an gcúltaca "
"fíordheimhnithe. :meth: `~django.test.client.force_login () `tarmhairigh an "
"cinneadh chuig an gcúltaca fíordheimhnithe freisin, mar sin má tá na cúltaca "
"réamhshocraithe á úsáid agat, ní mór duit úsáideoir gníomhach a úsáid."

msgid ""
":func:`django.views.i18n.set_language` may now return a 204 status code for "
"AJAX requests."
msgstr ""
":func: Féadfaidh `django.views.i18n.set_language` cód stádais 204 a "
"thabhairt ar ais anois le haghaidh iarratais AJAX."

msgid ""
"The ``base_field`` attribute "
"of :class:`~django.contrib.postgres.fields.RangeField` is now a type of "
"field, not an instance of a field.  If you have created a custom subclass "
"of :class:`~django.contrib.postgres.fields.RangeField`, you should change "
"the ``base_field`` attribute."
msgstr ""
"Is cineál réimse é an tréith ``base_field`` de:class: "
"`~django.contrib.postgres.fields.rangefield` anois, ní sampla de réimse. Má "
"chruthaigh tú fo-aicme saincheaptha de:class: "
"`~django.contrib.postgres.fields.rangefield`, ba cheart duit an tréith "
"``base_field`` a athrú."

msgid ""
"Middleware classes are now initialized when the server starts rather than "
"during the first request."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear ranganna Middleware a thionscnamh anois nuair a thosaíonn an "
"freastalaí seachas le linn na chéad iarratais."

msgid ""
"If you override ``is_authenticated()`` or ``is_anonymous()`` in a custom "
"user model, you must convert them to attributes or properties as described "
"in :ref:`the deprecation note <user-is-auth-anon-deprecation>`."
msgstr ""
"<user-is-auth-anon-deprecation>Má sháraitheann tú ``is_autentifikated () "
"``nó ``is_anonymné ()`` i samhail úsáideora saincheaptha, ní mór duit iad a "
"thiontú go tréithe nó airíonna mar a thuairiscítear in:ref: `an nóta "
"dímheasa `."

msgid ""
"When using :attr:`ModelAdmin.save_as=True "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.save_as>`, the \"Save as new\" button now "
"redirects to the change view for the new object instead of to the model's "
"changelist. If you need the previous behavior, set the "
"new :attr:`ModelAdmin.save_as_continue "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.save_as_continue>` attribute to ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a úsáidtear: attr: `ModelAdmin.save_ "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.save_as>as = True `, atreoraíonn an cnaipe "
"“Sábháil mar nua” anois chuig an radharc athraithe don réad nua in ionad "
"chuig liosta athraithe an tsamhail. "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.save_as_continue>Má theastaíonn an t-iompar "
"roimhe seo uait, socraigh an tréith nua:attr: `ModelAdmin.save_as_continue "
"`do `False``."

msgid ""
"Required form fields now have the ``required`` HTML attribute. Set "
"the :attr:`Form.use_required_attribute "
"<django.forms.Form.use_required_attribute>` attribute to ``False`` to "
"disable it. You could also add the ``novalidate`` attribute to ``<form>`` if "
"you don't want browser validation. To disable the ``required`` attribute on "
"custom widgets, override the :meth:`Widget.use_required_attribute() "
"<django.forms.Widget.use_required_attribute>` method."
msgstr ""
"Tá an tréith HTML “riachtanach” ag réimsí foirme riachtanacha anois. "
"<django.forms.Form.use_required_attribute>Socraigh an tréith: attr: "
"`Form.USE_Required_Attribute `le `False`` chun é a dhíchumasú. D'fhéadfá an "
"tréith ``novalidate`` a chur le ```` mura dteastaíonn bailíochtú brabhsála "
"<form>í uait. <django.forms.Widget.use_required_attribute>Chun an tréith "
"``riachtan`` a dhíchumasú ar ghuirléidí saincheaptha, athsháraigh an "
"modh:meth: `Widget.USE_REQUIRED_ATTRIBUTE () `."

msgid ""
"The WSGI handler no longer removes content of responses from ``HEAD`` "
"requests or responses with a ``status_code`` of 100-199, 204, or 304. Most "
"web servers already implement this behavior. Responses retrieved using the "
"Django test client continue to have these \"response fixes\" applied."
msgstr ""
"Ní bhaineann an láimhseálaí WSGI ábhar na bhfreagraí a thuilleadh ó "
"iarratais nó freagraí ``HEAD` le ``status_code`` de 100-199, 204, nó 304. "
"Cuireann an chuid is mó de na freastalaithe gréasáin an t-iompar seo Leanann "
"na “socruithe freagartha” seo i bhfeidhm ag freagraí a aisghabhadh ag úsáid "
"cliant tástála Django."

msgid ""
"``Model.__init__()`` now receives ``django.db.models.DEFERRED`` as the value "
"of deferred fields."
msgstr ""
"``Samhail. Faigheann __init__ () ```Django.db.Models.Deferred`` anois mar "
"luach na réimsí iarchurtha."

msgid ""
"The ``Model._deferred`` attribute is removed as dynamic model classes when "
"using ``QuerySet.defer()`` and ``only()`` is removed."
msgstr ""
"An ``Samhail. Baintear tréith _athraingthe ``mar aicmí samhail dinimiciúla "
"nuair a úsáidtear ``querySet.Defer ()`` agus ``only () ``baintear."

msgid ""
":meth:`Storage.save() <django.core.files.storage.Storage.save>` no longer "
"replaces ``'\\'`` with ``'/'``. This behavior is moved "
"to :class:`~django.core.files.storage.FileSystemStorage` since this is a "
"storage specific implementation detail. Any Windows user with a custom "
"storage implementation that relies on this behavior will need to implement "
"it in the custom storage's ``save()`` method."
msgstr ""
":meth: Ní chuireann `Storage.save () "
"<django.core.files.storage.Storage.save>`in ionad ``'\\ '`a thuilleadh le "
"``'/'``. Bogtar an t-iompar seo chuig: class: "
"`~django.core.files.storage.fileSystemStorage` ós rud é gur mionsonraí cur "
"chun feidhme stórála sonrach é seo. Beidh ar aon úsáideoir Windows le cur i "
"bhfeidhm stórála saincheaptha atá ag brath ar an iompar seo é a chur i "
"bhfeidhm i modh `save () `an stórála saincheaptha."

msgid ""
"Private :class:`~django.db.models.FileField` methods "
"``get_directory_name()`` and ``get_filename()`` are no longer called (and "
"are now deprecated) which is a backwards incompatible change for users "
"overriding those methods on custom fields. To adapt such code, override "
"``FileField.generate_filename()`` or :meth:`Storage.generate_filename() "
"<django.core.files.storage.Storage.generate_filename>` instead. It might be "
"possible to use :attr:`~django.db.models.FileField.upload_to` also."
msgstr ""
"Príobháideach:Class: `~django.db.models.filefield` ní thuilleadh ar "
"mhodhanna ``get_directory_name () ``agus `get_filename ()`` a thuilleadh "
"(agus tá siad curtha anois) ar athrú neamh-chomhoiriúnach é d'úsáideoirí a "
"sháraíonn na modhanna sin ar réimsí saincheaptha. "
"<django.core.files.storage.Storage.generate_filename>Chun an cód den sórt "
"sin a oiriúnú, déan `filefield.generate_filename () ```nó: meth: "
"`Storage.generate_filename ()` ina ionad. B'fhéidir go mbeadh sé indéanta a "
"úsáid:attr: `~django.db.models.filefield.upload_to` freisin."

msgid ""
"The subject of mail sent by ``AdminEmailHandler`` is no longer truncated at "
"989 characters. If you were counting on a limited length, truncate the "
"subject yourself."
msgstr ""
"Ní ghearrtar ábhar an phoist a sheolann ``AdminEmailHandler`` ag 989 "
"carachtar a thuilleadh. Má bhí tú ag brath ar fad teoranta, déan an t-ábhar "
"a ghearradh ort féin."

msgid ""
"Private expressions ``django.db.models.expressions.Date`` and ``DateTime`` "
"are removed. The new :class:`~django.db.models.functions.Trunc` expressions "
"provide the same functionality."
msgstr ""
"Baintear abairtí príobháideacha ``Django.db.Models.Expressions.Date`` agus "
"`DateTime``. Soláthraíonn na nathanna nua:class: "
"`~django.db.models.functions.trunc` an fheidhmiúlacht chéanna."

msgid ""
"The ``_base_manager`` and ``_default_manager`` attributes are removed from "
"model instances. They remain accessible on the model class."
msgstr ""
"Baintear na tréithe ``_base_manager`` agus ``_default_manager`` ó chásanna "
"samhail. Tá siad inrochtana ar an rang samhail."

msgid ""
"Accessing a deleted field on a model instance, e.g. after ``del obj.field``, "
"reloads the field's value instead of raising ``AttributeError``."
msgstr ""
"Ag rochtain a fháil ar réimse scriosta ar shampla samhail, m.sh. tar éis "
"``del obj.field``, luach an réimse a athluchtú in ionad ``AttributeError`` a "
"ardú."

msgid ""
"If you subclass ``AbstractBaseUser`` and override ``clean()``, be sure it "
"calls ``super()``. :meth:`.AbstractBaseUser.normalize_username` is called in "
"a new :meth:`.AbstractBaseUser.clean` method."
msgstr ""
"Má dhéanann tú fo-aicme ``AbstractBaseUser`` agus má sháraíonn tú ``clean () "
"``, bí cinnte go nglacann sé ``super ()``. :meth: Glaítear "
"`.AbstractBaseUser.Normalize_UserName` i modh nua:meth: "
"`.AbstractBaseUser.clean`."

msgid ""
"Private API ``django.forms.models.model_to_dict()`` returns a queryset "
"rather than a list of primary keys for ``ManyToManyField``\\s."
msgstr ""
"Tugann API príobháideach ``django.forms.models.model_to_dict () ``tacar "
"fiosrúcháin seachas liosta de na príomheochracha do ``ManyTomanyField``\\ s."

msgid ""
"If ``django.contrib.staticfiles`` is installed, the :ttag:`static`  template "
"tag uses the ``staticfiles`` storage to construct the URL rather than simply "
"joining the value with ``STATIC_ROOT``. The new approach encodes the URL, "
"which could be backwards-incompatible in cases such as including a fragment "
"in a path, e.g. ``{% static 'img.svg#fragment' %}``, since the ``#`` is "
"encoded as ``%23``. To adapt, move the fragment outside the template tag: "
"``{% static 'img.svg' %}#fragment``."
msgstr ""
"Má tá `django.contrib.staticfiles`` suiteáilte, úsáideann an clib "
"teimpléad:ttag: `static` an stóráil ``staticfiles`` chun an URL a thógáil "
"seachas an luach a cheangal le `STATIC_ROOT``. Ionchódaíonn an cur chuige "
"nua an URL, a d'fhéadfadh a bheith comhoiriúnach ar chúl i gcásanna amhail "
"blúire a áireamh i gcosán, m.sh. ``{% static 'img.svg #fragment'%} `, ós rud "
"é go bhfuil an `#`` ionchódaithe mar `%23``. Chun oiriúnú, bog an blúire "
"lasmuigh den chlib teimpléad: ``{% static 'img.svg'%} #fragment``."

msgid ""
"When ``USE_L10N`` is ``True``, localization is now applied for "
"the :tfilter:`date` and :tfilter:`time` filters when no format string is "
"specified. The ``DATE_FORMAT`` and ``TIME_FORMAT`` specifiers from the "
"active locale are used instead of the settings of the same name."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhíonn ``USE_L10N`` ``True``, cuirtear logánú i bhfeidhm anois ar na "
"scagairí:tfilter: `dáta` agus:tfilter: `time` nuair nach sonraítear aon "
"teaghrán formáide. Úsáidtear na sonraitheoirí ``DATE_FORMAT`` agus "
"``TIME_FORMAT`` ón áitear gníomhach in ionad na socruithe den ainm céanna."

msgid "Features deprecated in 1.10"
msgstr "Gnéithe atá díscríofa i 1.10"

msgid "Direct assignment to a reverse foreign key or many-to-many relation"
msgstr "Sannadh díreach le heochair eachtrach droim nó gaol go leor"

msgid "Instead of assigning related objects using direct assignment:"
msgstr "In ionad rudaí gaolmhara a shannadh ag úsáid sannadh díreach:"

msgid ""
"Use the :meth:`~django.db.models.fields.related.RelatedManager.set` method "
"added in Django 1.9:"
msgstr ""
"Úsáid an modh: meth: `~django.db.models.fields.related.relatedManager.set` "
"curtha leis i Django 1.9:"

msgid ""
"This prevents confusion about an assignment resulting in an implicit save."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann sé seo cosc ar mhearbhall faoi shannadh mar thoradh ar shábháil "
"intuigthe."

msgid "Non-timezone-aware :class:`~django.core.files.storage.Storage` API"
msgstr "Neamh-Time-Area: Class: `~django.core.files.storage.storage` API"

msgid ""
"The old, non-timezone-aware methods ``accessed_time()``, ``created_time()``, "
"and ``modified_time()`` are deprecated in favor of the new ``get_*_time()`` "
"methods."
msgstr ""
"Tá na sean-mhodhanna, neamh-eolach ar chrios ama ``accsed_time () ``, "
"`created_time ()``, agus `modified_time () ``, `modhnaithe () ``a dhíchur i "
