"iomlán:doc: </ref/contrib/syndication>."

msgid "Technical message IDs"
msgstr "ID teachtaireachta teicniúla"

msgid ""
"Up to version 1.1 Django used technical message IDs to provide localizers "
"the possibility to translate date and time formats. They were "
"translatable :term:`translation strings <translation string>` that could be "
"recognized because they were all upper case (for "
"example :setting:`DATETIME_FORMAT`, :setting:`DATE_FORMAT`, :setting:`TIME_FORMAT`). "
"They have been deprecated in favor of the new :doc:`/topics/i18n/formatting` "
"infrastructure that allows localizers to specify that information in a "
"``formats.py`` file in the corresponding ``django/conf/locale/<locale name>/"
"`` directory."
msgstr ""
"Suas le leagan 1.1 D'úsáid Django IDanna teachtaireachta teicniúla chun an "
"fhéidearthacht a sholáthar do logálaithe formáidí dáta agus ama a aistriú. "
"Bhí siad <translation string>inaistrithe: téarma: `teaghráin aistriúcháin `a "
"d'fhéadfaí a aithint toisc gur uachtarchás iad uile (mar shampla:setting: "
"`DATETIME_FORMAT`, :setting: `DATE_FORMAT`, :setting: `TIME_FORMAT`). "
"<locale name>Tá siad curtha i bhfabhar an bonneagar nua:doc: `/topics/i18n/"
"formatting` a ligeann do logálaithe an fhaisnéis sin a shonrú i gcomhad "
"``formats.py`` san eolaire comhfhreagrach ``django/conf/locale/ ``."

msgid ""
"To allow support for multiple databases, the GeoDjango database internals "
"were changed substantially.  The largest backwards-incompatible change is "
"that the module ``django.contrib.gis.db.backend`` was renamed "
"to :mod:`django.contrib.gis.db.backends`, where the full-"
"fledged :ref:`spatial database backends <spatial-backends>` now exist.  The "
"following sections provide information on the most-popular APIs that were "
"affected by these changes."
msgstr ""
"Chun tacaíocht a cheadú do iliomad bunachair sonraí, athraíodh inmheánacha "
"bunachar sonraí GeodJango go suntasach. <spatial-backends>Is é an t-athrú is "
"mó atá neamhchomhoiriúnach ar ais ná go n-athainmníodh an modúl "
"``django.contrib.gis.gis.db.backend`` u:mod: "
"`django.contrib.gis.db.backends`, áit a bhfuil na cúltaca bunachar sonraí "
"lán-fheadged:ref: `spásúil ann anois. Soláthraíonn na hailt seo a leanas "
"faisnéis faoi na APIs is mó éilimh orthu a raibh tionchar ag na hathruithe "
"seo orthu."

msgid "``SpatialBackend``"
msgstr "``SpatialBackend``"

msgid ""
"Prior to the creation of the separate spatial backends, the "
"``django.contrib.gis.db.backend.SpatialBackend`` object was provided as an "
"abstraction to introspect on the capabilities of the spatial database.  All "
"of the attributes and routines provided by ``SpatialBackend`` are now a part "
"of the ``ops`` attribute of the database backend."
msgstr ""
"Sula cruthaíodh na cúltaca spásúla ar leithligh, cuireadh an réad "
"``Django.contrib.gis.db.backend.spatialBackend ``ar fáil mar teibí chun "
"iniúchadh a dhéanamh ar chumais an bhunachar sonraí spásúil. Tá na tréithe "
"agus na gnáthaimh go léir a sholáthraíonn ``SpatialBackend`` anois mar chuid "
"de thréith ``ops`` de chúlcheann an bhunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"The old module ``django.contrib.gis.db.backend`` is still provided for "
"backwards-compatibility access to a ``SpatialBackend`` object, which is just "
"an alias to the ``ops`` module of the *default* spatial database connection."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear an sean-mhodúl ``django.contrib.gis.db.backend`` fós ar fáil le "
"haghaidh rochtain comhoiriúnachta cúil ar réad ``SpatialBackend``, nach "
"bhfuil ach ainm ar an modúl ``ops`` den nasc bunachar sonraí "
"spásúil*default*."

msgid ""
"Users that were relying on undocumented modules and objects within "
"``django.contrib.gis.db.backend``, rather the abstractions provided by "
"``SpatialBackend``, are required to modify their code. For example, the "
"following import which would work in 1.1 and below::"
msgstr ""
"Ceanglaítear ar úsáideoirí a bhí ag brath ar mhodúil agus ar rudaí "
"neamhdhoiciméadaithe laistigh de ``django.contrib.gis.db.backend``, seachas "
"na teibí a sholáthraíonn ``SpatialBackend`, a gcód a mhodhnú. Mar shampla, "
"an t-allmhairiú seo a leanas a oibreodh in 1.1 agus thíos:"

msgid "Would need to be changed::"
msgstr "Bheadh gá é a athrú::"

msgid "``SpatialRefSys`` and ``GeometryColumns`` models"
msgstr "Samhlacha ``SpatialRefsys`` agus ``GeometryColumns``"

msgid ""
"In previous versions of GeoDjango, :mod:`django.contrib.gis.db.models` had "
"``SpatialRefSys`` and ``GeometryColumns`` models for querying the OGC "
"spatial metadata tables ``spatial_ref_sys`` and ``geometry_columns``, "
"respectively."
msgstr ""
"I leaganacha roimhe seo de GeodJango, bhí: mod: "
"`django.contrib.gis.db.models` samhlacha ``spatialRefsys` agus "
"``GeometryColumns`` chun táblaí meiteashonraí spásúla OGC "
"``spatial_ref_sys`` agus ``geometry_columns`` a cheistiú, faoi seach."

msgid ""
"While these aliases are still provided, they are only for the *default* "
"database connection and exist only if the default connection is using a "
"supported spatial database backend."
msgstr ""
"Cé go gcuirtear na hainmneacha seo ar fáil fós, níl siad ach don nasc "
"bunachar sonraí *réamhshocraithe* agus níl ann ach má tá an nasc "
"réamhshocraithe ag úsáid cúltaca bunachar sonraí spásúil tacaithe."

msgid ""
"Because the table structure of the OGC spatial metadata tables differs "
"across spatial databases, the ``SpatialRefSys`` and ``GeometryColumns`` "
"models can no longer be associated with the ``gis`` application name.  Thus, "
"no models will be returned when using the ``get_models`` method in the "
"following example:"
msgstr ""
"Toisc go bhfuil struchtúr tábla táblaí meiteashonraí spásúla OGC difriúil ar "
"fud bunachair sonraí spásúla, ní féidir na samhlacha ``SpatialRefsys` agus "
"`GeometryColumns` a bheith bainteach le hainm an fheidhmchláir ``gis ``a "
"thuilleadh. Dá bhrí sin, ní thabharfar aon mhúnlaí ar ais nuair a úsáidtear "
"an modh ``get_models`` sa sampla seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"To get the correct ``SpatialRefSys`` and ``GeometryColumns`` for your "
"spatial database use the methods provided by the spatial backend:"
msgstr ""
"Chun na `SpatialRefsys`` agus ``GeometryColumns`` ceart a fháil do do "
"bhunachar sonraí spásúil bain úsáid as na modhanna a sholáthraíonn an "
"cúltaca spásúil:"

msgid ""
"When using the models returned from the ``spatial_ref_sys()`` and "
"``geometry_columns()`` method, you'll still need to use the correct database "
"alias when querying on the non-default connection. In other words, to ensure "
"that the models in the example above use the correct database::"
msgstr ""
"Agus na samhlacha a chuirtear ar ais ón modh ``spatial_ref_sys () ``agus "
"``geometry_columns () `á úsáid, beidh ort fós an ailias ceart bunachar "
"sonraí a úsáid agus tú ag fiosrú ar an nasc neamh-réamhshocraithe. Is é sin "
"le rá, chun a chinntiú go n-úsáideann na samhlacha sa sampla thuas an "
"bunachar sonraí ceart:"

msgid "Language code ``no``"
msgstr "Cód teanga ``no``"

msgid ""
"The currently used language code for Norwegian Bokmål ``no`` is being "
"replaced by the more common language code ``nb``."
msgstr ""
"Tá an cód teanga níos coitianta ``nb`` á chur in ionad an cód teanga a "
"úsáidtear faoi láthair do Bokmål na hIorua ``no ``."

msgid "Function-based template loaders"
msgstr "Luchtaitheoirí teimpléad bunaithe"

msgid ""
"Django 1.2 changes the template loading mechanism to use a class-based "
"approach. Old style function-based template loaders will still work, but "
"should be updated to use the new class-based template loaders."
msgstr ""
"Athraíonn Django 1.2 an meicníocht lódála teimpléid chun cur chuige rang-"
"bhunaithe a úsáid. Beidh lódairí teimpléid sean-stíl bunaithe ar fheidhm fós "
"ag obair, ach ba cheart iad a nuashonrú chun na lódairí teimpléid "
"rangbhunaithe nua a úsáid."

msgid "Django 1.2.1 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.2.1"

msgid ""
"Django 1.2.1 was released almost immediately after 1.2.0 to correct two "
"small bugs: one was in the documentation packaging script, the other was "
"a :ticket:`bug <13560>` that affected datetime form field widgets when "
"localization was enabled."
msgstr ""
"Scaoileadh Django 1.2.1 beagnach díreach tar éis 1.2.0 chun dhá fhabhta "
"beaga a cheartú: bhí ceann amháin sa script pacáistithe doiciméadaithe, ba é "
"an ceann eile a:ticket: `bug <13560>`a chuir isteach i ngiuirléidí réimse "
"foirm dáta nuair a cumasaíodh logánú."

msgid "Django 1.2.2 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.2.2"

msgid "Welcome to Django 1.2.2!"
msgstr "Fáilte go Django 1.2.2!"

msgid ""
"This is the second \"bugfix\" release in the Django 1.2 series, improving "
"the stability and performance of the Django 1.2 codebase."
msgstr ""
"Is é seo an dara scaoileadh “bugfix” sa tsraith Django 1.2, ag feabhsú "
"cobhsaíocht agus feidhmíocht an chódabhais Django 1.2."

msgid ""
"Django 1.2.2 maintains backwards compatibility with Django 1.2.1, but "
"contain a number of fixes and other improvements. Django 1.2.2 is a "
"recommended upgrade for any development or deployment currently using or "
"targeting Django 1.2."
msgstr ""
"Coinníonn Django 1.2.2 comhoiriúnacht ar ais le Django 1.2.1, ach tá roinnt "
"socruithe agus feabhsuithe eile ann. Is uasghrádú molta é Django 1.2.2 d'aon "
"fhorbairt nó imscaradh a úsáideann nó ag díriú ar Django 1.2 faoi láthair."

msgid ""
"For full details on the new features, backwards incompatibilities, and "
"deprecated features in the 1.2 branch, see the :doc:`/releases/1.2`."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh sonraí iomlána faoi na gnéithe nua, neamhoiriúnachtaí ar ais, "
"agus gnéithe lasmuigh sa bhrainse 1.2, féach an:doc: `/releases/1.2`."

msgid ""
"Ordinarily, a point release would not include new features, but in the case "
"of Django 1.2.2, we have made an exception to this rule."
msgstr ""
"De ghnáth, ní chuimsíodh gnéithe nua i scaoileadh pointe, ach i gcás Django "
"1.2.2, tá eisceacht déanta againn ón riail seo."

msgid ""
"In order to test a bug fix that forms part of the 1.2.2 release, it was "
"necessary to add a feature -- the ``enforce_csrf_checks`` flag -- to "
"the :ref:`test client <test-client>`. This flag forces the test client to "
"perform full CSRF checks on forms. The default behavior of the test client "
"hasn't changed, but if you want to do CSRF checks with the test client, it "
"is now possible to do so."
msgstr ""
"<test-client>D'fhonn socrú fabht atá mar chuid den scaoileadh 1.2.2 a "
"thástáil, bhí sé riachtanach gné - an bhratach ``exec_csrf_checks`` -- a "
"chur leis an:ref: `cliant tástála`. Cuireann an bratach seo iallach ar an "
"gcliant tástála seiceálacha iomlán CSRF a dhéanamh ar fhoirmeacha. Níor "
"athraigh iompar réamhshocraithe an chliaint tástála, ach más mian leat "
"seiceálacha CSRF a dhéanamh leis an gcliant tástála, is féidir é sin a "
"dhéanamh anois."

msgid "Django 1.2.3 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.2.3"

msgid ""
"Django 1.2.3 fixed a couple of release problems in the 1.2.2 release and was "
"released two days after 1.2.2."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh Django 1.2.3 cúpla fadhb scaoilte sa scaoileadh 1.2.2 agus "
"scaoileadh é dhá lá tar éis 1.2.2."

msgid "This release corrects the following problems:"
msgstr "Ceartaíonn an eisiúint seo na fadhbanna seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"The :commit:`patch <7f84657b6b2243cc787bdb9f296710c8d13ad0bd>` applied for "
"the security issue covered in Django 1.2.2 caused issues with non-ASCII "
"responses using CSRF tokens."
msgstr ""
"Ba chúis leis an: commit: `patch "
"<7f84657b6b2243cc787bdb9f296710c8d13ad0bd>`a chuir isteach ar an saincheist "
"slándála atá clúdaithe i Django 1.2.2 saincheisteanna le freagraí neamh-"
"ASCII ag baint úsáide as comharthaí CSRF."

msgid ""
"The patch also caused issues with some forms, most notably the user-editing "
"forms in the Django administrative interface."
msgstr ""
"Chuir an paiste saincheisteanna le roinnt foirmeacha freisin, go háirithe na "
"foirmeacha eagarthóireachta úsáideora i gcomhéadan riaracháin Django."

msgid "The packaging manifest did not contain the full list of required files."
msgstr "Ní raibh liosta iomlán na gcomhaid riachtanacha sa léiriú pacáistithe."

msgid "Django 1.2.4 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.2.4"

msgid "Welcome to Django 1.2.4!"
msgstr "Fáilte go Django 1.2.4!"

msgid ""
"This is the fourth \"bugfix\" release in the Django 1.2 series, improving "
"the stability and performance of the Django 1.2 codebase."
msgstr ""
"Is é seo an ceathrú scaoileadh “bugfix” sa tsraith Django 1.2, ag feabhsú "
"cobhsaíocht agus feidhmíocht an chódabhais Django 1.2."

msgid ""
"With one exception, Django 1.2.4 maintains backwards compatibility with "
"Django 1.2.3. It also contains a number of fixes and other improvements. "
"Django 1.2.4 is a recommended upgrade for any development or deployment "
"currently using or targeting Django 1.2."
msgstr ""
"Le haon eisceacht amháin, coimeádann Django 1.2.4 comhoiriúnacht ar ais le "
"Django 1.2.3. Tá roinnt socruithe agus feabhsuithe eile ann freisin. Is "
"uasghrádú molta é Django 1.2.4 d'aon fhorbairt nó imscaradh a úsáideann nó "
"ag díriú ar Django 1.2 faoi láthair."

msgid ""
"Ordinarily, a point release would not include new features, but in the case "
"of Django 1.2.4, we have made an exception to this rule."
msgstr ""
"De ghnáth, ní chuimsíodh gnéithe nua i scaoileadh pointe, ach i gcás Django "
"1.2.4, tá eisceacht déanta againn ón riail seo."

msgid ""
"One of the bugs fixed in Django 1.2.4 involves a set of circumstances "
"whereby a running a test suite on a multiple database configuration could "
"cause the original source database (i.e., the actual production database) to "
"be dropped, causing catastrophic loss of data. In order to provide a fix for "
"this problem, it was necessary to introduce a new setting "
"-- :setting:`TEST_DEPENDENCIES` -- that allows you to define any creation "
"order dependencies in your database configuration."
msgstr ""
"Is éard atá i gceann de na fabhtanna a shocraítear i Django 1.2.4 tá sraith "
"imthosca trína bhféadfadh sraith tástála a reáchtáil ar chumraíocht iolrach "
"bunachar sonraí a bheith ina chúis leis an mbunachar sonraí bunaidh (ie, an "
"bunachar sonraí táirgeachta iarbhír) a thit, rud a chruthaíonn cailliúint "
"D'fhonn socrú a sholáthar don fhadhb seo, bhí sé riachtanach socrú nua a "
"thabhairt isteach --:setting: `TEST_DEPENDENCIES` - a ligeann duit aon "
"spleáchais ordú cruthaithe a shainiú i do chumraíocht bunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"Most users -- even users with multiple-database configurations -- need not "
"be concerned about the data loss bug, or the manual configuration "
"of :setting:`TEST_DEPENDENCIES`. See the :ticket:`original problem report "
"<14415>` documentation on :ref:`controlling the creation order of test "
"databases <topics-testing-creation-dependencies>` for details."
msgstr ""
"Ní gá go mbeadh imní ar chuid is mó d'úsáideoirí - fiú úsáideoirí a bhfuil "
"cumraíochtaí ilbhunachar sonraí acu - faoin bhfabht caillteanais sonraí, nó "
"faoi chumraíocht láimhe de:setting: `TEST_DEPENDENCIES`. <topics-testing-"
"creation-dependencies>Féach an doiciméadú:ticket: `tuarascáil bunaidh "
"fadhban <14415>na` ar:ref: `ord cruthaithe bunachar sonraí tástála a rialú "
"`le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid ""
"The function-based :setting:`TEST_RUNNER` previously used to execute the "
"GeoDjango test suite, ``django.contrib.gis.tests.run_gis_tests``, was "
"finally deprecated in favor of a class-based test runner, "
"``django.contrib.gis.tests.GeoDjangoTestSuiteRunner``, added in this release."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an feidhm-bhunaithe:setting: `TEST_RUNNER` roimhe seo chun an "
"tsraith tástála GeodJango a fhorghníomhú, "
"``django.contrib.gis.tests.run_gis_tests``, i bhfabhar reathnóir tástála "
"rang-bhunaithe, ``django.contrib.gis.tests.geodjangoTestSuiterunner``, "
"curtha leis sa eisiúint seo."

msgid ""
"In addition, the GeoDjango test suite is now included when :ref:`running the "
"Django test suite <running-unit-tests>` with ``runtests.py`` and "
"using :ref:`spatial database backends <spatial-backends>`."
msgstr ""
"<spatial-backends>Ina theannta sin, tá an tsraith tástála GeodJango san "
"áireamh anois nuair a bhíonn: ref: `ag rith an tsraith tástála Django `le "
"``runtests.py`` agus ag baint úsáid:ref: <running-unit-tests>`cúltaca "
"bunachar sonraí spásúla`."

msgid "Django 1.2.5 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.2.5"

msgid "Welcome to Django 1.2.5!"
msgstr "Fáilte go Django 1.2.5!"

msgid ""
"This is the fifth \"bugfix\" release in the Django 1.2 series, improving the "
"stability and performance of the Django 1.2 codebase."
msgstr ""
"Is é seo an cúigiú scaoileadh “bugfix” sa tsraith Django 1.2, ag feabhsú "
"cobhsaíocht agus feidhmíocht an chódabhais Django 1.2."

msgid ""
"With four exceptions, Django 1.2.5 maintains backwards compatibility with "
"Django 1.2.4. It also contains a number of fixes and other improvements. "
"Django 1.2.5 is a recommended upgrade for any development or deployment "
"currently using or targeting Django 1.2."
msgstr ""
"Le ceithre eisceacht, coimeádann Django 1.2.5 comhoiriúnacht ar ais le "
"Django 1.2.4. Tá roinnt socruithe agus feabhsuithe eile ann freisin. Is "
"uasghrádú molta é Django 1.2.5 d'aon fhorbairt nó imscaradh a úsáideann nó "
"ag díriú ar Django 1.2 faoi láthair."

msgid "FileField no longer deletes files"
msgstr "Ní scriosann FileField comhaid a thuilleadh"

msgid ""
"In earlier Django versions, when a model instance containing "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.FileField` was "
"deleted, :class:`~django.db.models.FileField` took it upon itself to also "
"delete the file from the backend storage. This opened the door to several "
"potentially serious data-loss scenarios, including rolled-back transactions "
"and fields on different models referencing the same file. In Django "
"1.2.5, :class:`~django.db.models.FileField` will never delete files from the "
"backend storage. If you need cleanup of orphaned files, you'll need to "
"handle it yourself (for instance, with a custom management command that can "
"be run manually or scheduled to run periodically via e.g. cron)."
msgstr ""
"I leaganacha Django níos luaithe, nuair a scriosadh samhail samhail ina "
"raibh a:class: `~django.db.models.filefield`, ghlac: :class: "
"`~django.db.models.filefield` leis an gcomhad a scriosadh ón stóráil cúltaca "
"freisin. D'oscail sé seo an doras do roinnt cásanna caillteanais sonraí "
"tromchúiseacha a d'fhéadfadh a bheith ann, lena n-áirítear idirbhearta "
"rollta ar ais agus réimsí ar mhúnlaí éagsúla a thag I Django 1.2.5, ní "
"scriosfaidh: class: `~Django.db.Models.FileField` comhaid ón stóráil cúltaca "
"riamh. Más gá duit comhaid dílleachta a ghlanadh, beidh ort é a láimhseáil "
"tú féin (mar shampla, le ordú bainistíochta saincheaptha is féidir a "
"reáchtáil de láimh nó a sceidealú le rith go tréimhsiúil trí e.g. cron)."

msgid "Use of custom SQL to load initial data in tests"
msgstr "Úsáid SQL saincheaptha chun sonraí tosaigh a luchtú i dtástálacha"

msgid ""
"Django provides a custom SQL hooks as a way to inject hand-crafted SQL into "
"the database synchronization process. One of the possible uses for this "
"custom SQL is to insert data into your database. If your custom SQL contains "
"``INSERT`` statements, those insertions will be performed every time your "
"database is synchronized. This includes the synchronization of any test "
"databases that are created when you run a test suite."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Django crúcaí SQL saincheaptha mar bhealach chun SQL "
"lámhdhéanta a instealladh isteach sa phróiseas sioncrónaithe bunachar sonraí "
"Ceann de na húsáidí féideartha don SQL saincheaptha seo ná sonraí a chur "
"isteach i do bhunachar sonraí. Má tá ráitis ``INSERT`` i do SQL "
"saincheaptha, déanfar na cuireadh isteach sin gach uair a dhéanfar do "
"bhunachar sonraí a shioncronú. Áirítear leis seo sioncrónú aon bhunachar "
"sonraí tástála a chruthaítear nuair a reáchtáil tú sraith tástála."

msgid ""
"However, in the process of testing the Django 1.3, it was discovered that "
"this feature has never completely worked as advertised. When using database "
"backends that don't support transactions, or when using a "
"TransactionTestCase, data that has been inserted using custom SQL will not "
"be visible during the testing process."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, sa phróiseas chun an Django 1.3 a thástáil, fuarthas amach nár "
"oibrigh an ghné seo riamh go hiomlán mar a fógraíodh. Agus cúltaca bunachar "
"sonraí á úsáid nach dtacaíonn le hidirbhearta, nó nuair a bhíonn "
"TransactionTestCase á úsáid agat, ní bheidh sonraí a cuireadh isteach ag "
"úsáid SQL saincheaptha le feiceáil le linn an phróisis tástála."

msgid ""
"Unfortunately, there was no way to rectify this problem without introducing "
"a backwards incompatibility. Rather than leave SQL-inserted initial data in "
"an uncertain state, Django now enforces the policy that data inserted by "
"custom SQL will *not* be visible during testing."
msgstr ""
"Ar an drochuair, ní raibh aon bhealach ann chun an fhadhb seo a cheartú gan "
"neamhoiriúnacht ar ais a thabhairt isteach. Seachas sonraí tosaigh a "
"cuireadh isteach ag SQL a fhágáil i stát neamhchinnte, cuireann Django i "
"bhfeidhm anois an beartas nach mbeidh sonraí a cuireadh isteach ag SQL "
"saincheaptaí* le feiceáil le linn na tástála."

msgid ""
"This change only affects the testing process. You can still use custom SQL "
"to load data into your production database as part of the ``syncdb`` "
"process. If you require data to exist during test conditions, you should "
"either insert it using :ref:`test fixtures <topics-testing-fixtures>`, or "
"using the ``setUp()`` method of your test case."
msgstr ""
"Ní théann an t-athrú seo ach ar an bpróiseas tástála Is féidir leat SQL "
"saincheaptha a úsáid fós chun sonraí a luchtú isteach i do bhunachar sonraí "
"táirgeachta mar chuid den phróiseas `syncdb`. Má theastaíonn uait go mbeidh "
"sonraí ann le linn coinníollacha tástála, ba cheart duit iad a chur isteach "
"ag baint úsáide as: ref: `daingneáin tástá <topics-testing-fixtures>la `, nó "
"ag baint úsáide as an modh ``Setup ()` de do cháis tástála."

msgid "ModelAdmin.lookup_allowed signature changed"
msgstr "ModelAdmin.lookup_Allowed síniú athraithe"

msgid ""
"Django 1.2.4 introduced a method ``lookup_allowed`` on ``ModelAdmin``, to "
"cope with a security issue (changeset :commit:`[15033] "
"<85207a245bf09fdebe486b4c7bbcb65300f2a693>`). Although this method was never "
"documented, it seems some people have overridden ``lookup_allowed``, "
"especially to cope with regressions introduced by that changeset. While the "
"method is still undocumented and not marked as stable, it may be helpful to "
"know that the signature of this function has changed."
msgstr ""
"<85207a245bf09fdebe486b4c7bbcb65300f2a693>Thug Django 1.2.4 modh "
"``lookup_allowed` isteach ar ``ModelAdmin``, chun déileáil le saincheist "
"slándála (changeset:commit: `[15033]`). Cé nach ndearnadh an modh seo "
"doiciméadaithe riamh, is cosúil go bhfuil daoine áirithe tar éis "
"`lookup_allowed` a shárú, go háirithe chun déileáil le haischéimnithe a thug "
"isteach ag an athrú sin. Cé go bhfuil an modh fós gan doiciméadú agus nach "
"bhfuil sé marcáilte mar chobhsaí, b'fhéidir go mbeadh sé cabhrach a fháil "
"amach go bhfuil síniú na feidhme seo athraithe."

msgid "Django 1.2.6 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.2.6"

msgid "*September 9, 2011*"
msgstr "*9 Meán Fómhair, 2011*"

msgid "Welcome to Django 1.2.6!"
msgstr "Fáilte go Django 1.2.6!"

msgid ""
"This is the sixth bugfix/security release in the Django 1.2 series, fixing "
"several security issues present in Django 1.2.5.  Django 1.2.6 is a "
"recommended upgrade for all users of any Django release in the 1.2.X series."
msgstr ""
"Is é seo an séú scaoileadh bugfix/slándála sa tsraith Django 1.2, ag socrú "
"roinnt saincheisteanna slándála atá i láthair i Django 1.2.5. Is uasghrádú "
"molta é Django 1.2.6 d'úsáideoir uile d'aon scaoileadh Django sa tsraith "
"1.2.X."

msgid ""
"For a full list of issues addressed in this release, see the `security "
"advisory`_."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh liosta iomlán na saincheisteanna a thugtar aghaidh orthu sa "
"eisiúint seo, féach an `comhairleoireacht slándála`_."

msgid "Django 1.2.7 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.2.7"

msgid "*September 10, 2011*"
msgstr "*10 Meán Fómhair, 2011*"

msgid "Welcome to Django 1.2.7!"
msgstr "Fáilte go Django 1.2.7!"

msgid ""
"This is the seventh bugfix/security release in the Django 1.2 series. It "
"replaces Django 1.2.6 due to problems with the 1.2.6 release tarball. Django "
"1.2.7 is a recommended upgrade for all users of any Django release in the "
"1.2.X series."
msgstr ""
"Is é seo an seachtú eisiúint bugfix/slándála sa tsraith Django 1.2. Cuireann "
"sé in ionad Django 1.2.6 mar gheall ar fhadhbanna leis an tarball scaoilte "
"1.2.6. Is uasghrádú molta é Django 1.2.7 d'úsáideoir uile d'aon scaoileadh "
"Django sa tsraith 1.2.X."

msgid "For more information, see the `release advisory`_."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise, féach an `comhairleoireacht scaoileacha`_."

msgid "Django 1.3 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoileadh Django 1.3"

msgid "*March 23, 2011*"
msgstr "*23 Márta, 2011*"

msgid "Welcome to Django 1.3!"
msgstr "Fáilte go dtí Django 1.3!"

msgid ""
"Nearly a year in the making, Django 1.3 includes quite a few :ref:`new "
"features <whats-new-1.3>` and plenty of bug fixes and improvements to "
"existing features. These release notes cover the new features in 1.3, as "
"well as some :ref:`backwards-incompatible changes <backwards-incompatible-"
"changes-1.3>` you'll want to be aware of when upgrading from Django 1.2 or "
"older versions."
msgstr ""
"Beagnach bliain ag déanamh, cuimsíonn Django 1.3 beagán go leor: ref: "
"`gnéithe nua' agus neart socruithe fabht agus fe <whats-new-1.3>abhsúcháin "
"ar ghnéithe atá ann cheana. Clúdaíonn na nótaí scaoilte seo na gnéithe nua i "
"1.3, chomh maith le roinnt: ref: `athruithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha <backwards-"
"incompatible-changes-1.3>'a mbeidh tú ag iarraidh a bheith ar an eolas fúthu "
"agus tú ag uasghrádú ó Django 1.2 nó leaganacha níos sine."

msgid ""
"Django 1.3's focus has mostly been on resolving smaller, long-standing "
"feature requests, but that hasn't prevented a few fairly significant new "
"features from landing, including:"
msgstr ""
"Bhí fócas Django 1.3 den chuid is mó ar iarratais gné níos lú fadtéarmach a "
"réiteach, ach níor chuir sé sin cosc ar chúpla gné nua réasúnta suntasach ó "
"thúrlann, lena n-áirítear:"

msgid "A framework for writing `class-based views`_."
msgstr "Creat chun 'tuairimí rangbhunaithe '_ a scríobh."

msgid "Built-in support for `using Python's logging facilities`_."
msgstr "Tacaíocht ionsuite chun `saoráidí logála Python a úsáid `_."

msgid "Contrib support for `easy handling of static files`_."
msgstr "Tacaíocht Contrib do `láimhseáil éasca comhaid statacha `_."

msgid ""
"Django's testing framework now supports (and ships with a copy of) `the "
"unittest2 library`_."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn creat tástála Django anois le “leabharlann unittest2” (agus seolann "
"sé le cóip de)."

msgid ""
"Wherever possible, new features are introduced in a backwards-compatible "
"manner per :doc:`our API stability policy </misc/api-stability>` policy. As "
"a result of this policy, Django 1.3 :ref:`begins the deprecation process for "
"some features <deprecated-features-1.3>`."
msgstr ""
"Cibé áit is féidir, tugtar gnéithe nua isteach ar bhealach atá comhoiriúnach "
"le cúl: doc: 'ár mbeartas cobhsaíochta API</misc/api-stability> '. "
"<deprecated-features-1.3>Mar thoradh ar an mbeartas seo, dtosaíonn Django "
"1.3:ref: `an próiseas díghabhála do roinnt gnéithe `."

msgid ""
"The release of Django 1.2 was notable for having the first shift in Django's "
"Python compatibility policy; prior to Django 1.2, Django supported any 2.x "
"version of Python from 2.3 up. As of Django 1.2, the minimum requirement was "
"raised to Python 2.4."
msgstr ""
"Bhí scaoileadh Django 1.2 suntasach as an chéad athrú a bheith aige i "
"mbeartas comhoiriúnachta Python Django; roimh Django 1.2, thacaigh Django le "
"haon leagan 2.x de Python ó 2.3 suas. Amhail Django 1.2, ardaíodh an "
"riachtanas íosta go Python 2.4."

msgid ""
"Django 1.3 continues to support Python 2.4, but will be the final Django "
"release series to do so; beginning with Django 1.4, the minimum supported "
"Python version will be 2.5. A document outlining our full timeline for "
"deprecating Python 2.x and moving to Python 3.x will be published shortly "
"after the release of Django 1.3."
msgstr ""
"Leanann Django 1.3 ag tacú le Python 2.4, ach is é an tsraith scaoileadh "
"Django deiridh é sin a dhéanamh; ag tosú le Django 1.4, is é 2.5 an leagan "
"Python íosta a thacaítear. Foilseofar doiciméad ina leagtar amach ár n-"
"amlíne iomlán chun Python 2.x a dhíspreagadh agus bogadh go Python 3.x go "
"gairid tar éis Django 1.3 a scaoileadh."

msgid "What's new in Django 1.3"
msgstr "Cad atá nua i Django 1.3"

msgid "Class-based views"
msgstr "Tuairimí rang-bhunaithe"

msgid ""
"Django 1.3 adds a framework that allows you to use a class as a view. This "
"means you can compose a view out of a collection of methods that can be "
"subclassed and overridden to provide common views of data without having to "
"write too much code."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann Django 1.3 creat leis a ligeann duit rang a úsáid mar radharc. "
"Ciallaíonn sé seo gur féidir leat radharc a chumadh as bailiúchán modhanna "
"is féidir iad a fho-aicmiú agus a shárú chun tuairimí coitianta ar shonraí a "
"sholáthar gan an iomarca cód a scríobh."

msgid ""
"Analogs of all the old function-based generic views have been provided, "
"along with a completely generic view base class that can be used as the "
"basis for reusable applications that can be easily extended."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh analógacha de na sean-radhairc chineálacha bunaithe ar fheidhm ar "
"fáil, mar aon le rang bonn radharc go hiomlán cineálach is féidir a úsáid "
"mar bhunús d'iarratais in-athúsáidte is féidir a leathnú go héasca."

msgid ""
"See :doc:`the documentation on class-based generic views</topics/class-based-"
"views/index>` for more details. There is also a document to help you "
"`convert your function-based generic views to class-based views <https://"
"raw.githubusercontent.com/django/django/"
"ea9dc9f4b03ae034c1dc080730422dda7a9c2e47/docs/topics/generic-views-"
"migration.txt>`_."
msgstr ""
"Féach: Doc: `an doiciméadú ar tuairimí cineálacha rang-bhunaithe 'le "
"haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí .</topics/class-based-views/index> < https://"
"raw.githubusercontent.com/django/django/"
"ea9dc9f4b03ae034c1dc080730422dda7a9c2e47/docs/topics/generic-views-"
"migration.txt>Tá doiciméad ann freisin chun cabhrú leat `do thuairimí "
"cineálacha feidhmiúbhunaithe a thiontú go tuairimí rang-bhunaithe `_."

msgid "Logging"
msgstr "Logáil"

msgid ""
"Django 1.3 adds framework-level support for Python's ``logging`` module.  "
"This means you can now easily configure and control logging as part of your "
"Django project. A number of logging handlers and logging calls have been "
"added to Django's own code as well -- most notably, the error emails sent on "
"an HTTP 500 server error are now handled as a logging activity. "
"See :doc:`the documentation on Django's logging interface </topics/logging>` "
"for more details."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann Django 1.3 tacaíocht ar leibhéal an chreata leis do mhodúl "
"``logála`` Python. Ciallaíonn sé seo gur féidir leat logáil a chumrú agus a "
"rialú go héasca anois mar chuid de do thionscadal Django. Cuireadh roinnt "
"láimhseálaithe logála agus glaonna logála le cód Django féin freisin - go "
"háirithe, déantar na ríomhphoist earráide a sheoltar ar earráid freastalaí "
"HTTP 500 a láimhseáil mar ghníomhaíocht logála anois. Féach :doc:`an "
"doiciméadú ar chomhéadan logála Django </topics/logging>` le haghaidh "
"tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid "Extended static files handling"
msgstr "Láimhseáil comhaid statacha sínte"

msgid ""
"Django 1.3 ships with a new contrib app -- ``django.contrib.staticfiles`` -- "
"to help developers handle the static media files (images, CSS, JavaScript, "
"etc.) that are needed to render a complete web page."
msgstr ""
"Seolann Django 1.3 le aip contrib nua - ``django.contrib.staticfiles`` - "
"chun cabhrú le forbróirí na comhaid meán statacha (íomhánna, CSS, "
"JavaScript, srl.) atá riachtanach chun leathanach gréasáin iomlán a "
"láimhseáil."

msgid ""
"In previous versions of Django, it was common to place static assets "
"in :setting:`MEDIA_ROOT` along with user-uploaded files, and serve them both "
"at :setting:`MEDIA_URL`. Part of the purpose of introducing the "
"``staticfiles`` app is to make it easier to keep static files separate from "
"user-uploaded files. Static assets should now go in ``static/`` "
"subdirectories of your apps or in other static assets directories listed "
"in :setting:`STATICFILES_DIRS`, and will be served at :setting:`STATIC_URL`."
msgstr ""
"I leaganacha roimhe seo de Django, bhí sé coitianta sócmhainní statacha a "
"chur in:setting: `MEDIA_ROOT` mar aon le comhaid uaslódáilte ón úsáideoir, "
"agus iad araon a sheirbheáil ag: socrú: `MEDIA_URL`. Cuid den chuspóir a "
"bhaineann leis an aip `staticfiles` a thabhairt isteach ná é a dhéanamh níos "
"éasca comhaid statacha a choinneáil ar leithligh ó chomhaid uaslódáilte ón "
"úsáideoir. Ba chóir sócmhainní statacha dul anois i bhfo-eolairí `statach/`` "
"d'aipeanna nó in eolairí sócmhainní statacha eile atá liostaithe in:setting: "
"`STATICFILES_DIRS`, agus seirbheálfar iad ag: socrú: `STATIC_URL`."

msgid ""
"See the :doc:`reference documentation of the app </ref/contrib/staticfiles>` "
"for more details or learn how to :doc:`manage static files </howto/static-"
"files/index>`."
msgstr ""
"Féach na:doc: `doiciméadú tagartha an aipe` le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí nó "
"fo</ref/contrib/staticfiles> ghlaim conas:doc: `comhaid statacha a "
"bhainistiú </howto/static-files/index> '."

msgid "``unittest2`` support"
msgstr "Tacaíocht ``unittest2``"

msgid ""
"Python 2.7 introduced some major changes to the ``unittest`` library, adding "
"some extremely useful features. To ensure that every Django project can "
"benefit from these new features, Django ships with a copy "
"of :pypi:`unittest2`, a copy of the Python 2.7 ``unittest`` library, "
"backported for Python 2.4 compatibility."
msgstr ""
"Thug Python 2.7 roinnt athruithe móra isteach ar an leabharlann ``unittest "
"``, ag cur roinnt gnéithe thar a bheith úsáideach leis. Chun a chinntiú gur "
"féidir le gach tionscadal Django leas a bhaint as na gnéithe nua seo, "
"seolann Django cóip de:pypi: `unittest2`, cóip de leabharlann Python 2.7 "
"`unittest ``, cúltaca le haghaidh comhoiriúnacht Python 2.4."

msgid ""
"To access this library, Django provides the ``django.utils.unittest`` module "
"alias. If you are using Python 2.7, or you have installed ``unittest2`` "
"locally, Django will map the alias to the installed version of the "
"``unittest`` library. Otherwise, Django will use its own bundled version of "
"``unittest2``."
msgstr ""
"Chun rochtain a fháil ar an leabharlann seo, soláthraíonn Django ailias "
"modúl ``django.utils.unittest``. Má tá Python 2.7 á úsáid agat, nó má tá "
"`unittest2`` suiteáilte agat go háitiúil, déanfaidh Django an t-ainm a "
"mhapáil chuig an leagan suiteáilte den leabharlann ``unittest``. Seachas "
"sin, úsáidfidh Django a leagan cuacail féin de ``unittest2`."

msgid "To take advantage of this alias, simply use::"
msgstr "Chun leas a bhaint as an ailias seo, bain úsáid as:"

msgid "wherever you would have historically used::"
msgstr "cibé áit a bheadh úsáid agat go stairiúil:"

msgid ""
"If you want to continue to use the base ``unittest`` library, you can -- you "
"just won't get any of the nice new ``unittest2`` features."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat leanúint ar aghaidh ag úsáid an leabharlann “unittest” bonn, "
"is féidir leat - ní gheobhaidh tú aon cheann de na gnéithe deasa nua "
"``unittest2`."

msgid "Transaction context managers"
msgstr "Bainisteoirí comhthéacs i"

msgid ""
"Users of Python 2.5 and above may now use transaction management functions "
"as context managers. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh úsáideoirí Python 2.5 agus níos airde feidhmeanna bainistíochta "
"idirbheart a úsáid anois mar bhainisteoirí comhthéacs. Mar shampla::"

msgid "Configurable delete-cascade"
msgstr "Cascade-scriosadh cumraithe"

msgid ""
":class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey` "
"and :class:`~django.db.models.OneToOneField` now accept "
"an :attr:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey.on_delete` argument to customize "
"behavior when the referenced object is deleted. Previously, deletes were "
"always cascaded; available alternatives now include set null, set default, "
"set to any value, protect, or do nothing."
msgstr ""
":class: `~Django.db.Models.ForeignKey` agus:class: "
"`~django.db.models.onetoonefield` glacann anois le argóint: attr: "
"`~django.db.models.foreignKey.on_delete` chun iompar a shaincheapadh nuair a "
"scriostar an réad tagartha. Roimhe seo, rinneadh scriosadh i gcónaí; tá "
"roghanna eile atá ar fáil anois tá neall a shocrú, socraigh réamhshocrú, "
"socraithe ar aon luach, cosaint nó aon rud a dhéanamh."

msgid ""
"For more information, see the :attr:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey.on_delete` "
"documentation."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise, féach an doiciméadach:attr: "
"`~django.db.models.foreignkey.on_delete`."

msgid "Contextual markers and comments for translatable strings"
msgstr "Marcóirí agus tuairimí comhthéacsúla le haghaidh teaghráin inai"

msgid ""
"For translation strings with ambiguous meaning, you can now use the "
"``pgettext`` function to specify the context of the string."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le teaghráin aistriúcháin a bhfuil brí débhríoch acu, is féidir leat "
"an fheidhm `pgettext`` a úsáid anois chun comhthéacs an teaghráin a shonrú."

msgid ""
"And if you just want to add some information for translators, you can also "
"add special translator comments in the source."
msgstr ""
"Agus mura dteastaíonn uait ach roinnt faisnéise a chur leis d'aistritheoirí, "
"is féidir leat tráchtanna aistritheora speisialta a chur san fhoinse freisin."

msgid ""
"For more information, see :ref:`contextual-markers` and :ref:`translator-"
"comments`."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise, féach:ref: `contextual-markers` agus:ref: "
"`translator-comments`."

msgid "Improvements to built-in template tags"
msgstr "Feabhsuithe ar chlib teimpléad ionsuite"

msgid ""
"A number of improvements have been made to Django's built-in template tags:"
msgstr "Rinneadh roinnt feabhsuithe ar chlibeanna teimpléad ionsuite Django:"

msgid ""
"The :ttag:`include` tag now accepts a ``with`` option, allowing you to "
"specify context variables to the included template"
msgstr ""
"Glacann an clibe:ttag: `include` anois le rogha ``with`,,, ag ligean duit "
"athróga comhthéacs a shonrú don teimpléad san áireamh"

msgid ""
"The :ttag:`include` tag now accepts an ``only`` option, allowing you to "
"exclude the current context from the included context"
msgstr ""
"Glacann an clibe:ttag: `include` anois le rogha ``amháin ``, rud a ligeann "
"duit an comhthéacs reatha a eisiamh ón gcomhthéacs san áireamh"

msgid ""
"The :ttag:`with` tag now allows you to define multiple context variables in "
"a single :ttag:`with` block."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an clibe:ttag: `with` duit anois ilathróga comhthéacs a shainiú i "
"mbloc aonair: ttag: `with`."

msgid ""
"The :ttag:`load` tag now accepts a ``from`` argument, allowing you to load a "
"single tag or filter from a library."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an clibe:ttag: `load anois le argóint ``ó ``, rud a ligeann duit "
"clib amháin nó scagaire a luchtú ó leabharlann."

msgid "TemplateResponse"
msgstr "TeimpléadFreagra"

msgid ""
"It can sometimes be beneficial to allow decorators or middleware to modify a "
"response *after* it has been constructed by the view. For example, you may "
"want to change the template that is used, or put additional data into the "
"context."
msgstr ""
"Uaireanta d'fhéadfadh sé a bheith tairbheach ligean do mhaisitheoirí nó "
"earraí lárnacha freagra a mhodhnó* tar éis dó* é a thógáil ag an dearcadh. "
"Mar shampla, b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat an teimpléad a úsáidtear a athrú, nó "
"sonraí breise a chur sa chomhthéacs."

msgid ""
"However, you can't (easily) modify the content of a "
"basic :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse` after it has been constructed. To "
"overcome this limitation, Django 1.3 adds a "
"new :class:`~django.template.response.TemplateResponse` class. Unlike "
"basic :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse` "
"objects, :class:`~django.template.response.TemplateResponse` objects retain "
"the details of the template and context that was provided by the view to "
"compute the response. The final output of the response is not computed until "
"it is needed, later in the response process."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, ní féidir leat ábhar bunús:class: `~django.http.httpResponse` "
"a mhodhnú (go héasca) tar éis é a thógáil. Chun an teorannú seo a shárú, "
"cuireann Django 1.3 rang nua:class: "
"`~Django.Template.Response.TemplateResponse` leis. Murab ionann agus "
"bunús:class: `~django.http.httpResponse` rudaí, :class: "
"`~Django.Template.Response.TemplateResponse` coinníonn rudaí sonraí an "
"teimpléad agus an chomhthéacs a chuir an dearcadh ar fáil chun an freagra a "
"ríomh. Ní ríomhtar aschur deiridh an fhreagra go dtí go mbeidh sé ag "
"teastáil, níos déanaí sa phróiseas freagartha."

msgid ""
"For more details, see the :doc:`documentation </ref/template-response>` on "
"the :class:`~django.template.response.TemplateResponse` class."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí, féach ar an :doc:`doiciméadúchán </ref/"
"template-response>` ar "
"an :class:`~django.template.response.TemplateResponse` rang."

msgid "Caching changes"
msgstr "Athruithe Caching"

msgid ""
"Django 1.3 sees the introduction of several improvements to the Django's "
"caching infrastructure."
msgstr ""
"Feiceann Django 1.3 tugtar isteach roinnt feabhsuithe ar bhonneagar caching "
"an Django."

msgid ""
"Firstly, Django now supports multiple named caches. In the same way that "
"Django 1.2 introduced support for multiple database connections, Django 1.3 "
"allows you to use the new :setting:`CACHES` setting to define multiple named "
"cache connections."
msgstr ""
"Ar dtús, tacaíonn Django anois le cúscáin ainmnithe iolracha. Ar an mbealach "
"céanna a thug Django 1.2 tacaíocht isteach do naisc iolracha bunachar "
"sonraí, tugann Django 1.3 deis duit an socrú nua:setting: `CACHES` a úsáid "
"chun naisc taisce iolracha ainmnithe a shainiú."

msgid ""
"Secondly, :ref:`versioning <cache_versioning>`, :ref:`site-wide prefixing "
"<cache_key_prefixing>` and :ref:`transformation <cache_key_transformation>` "
"have been added to the cache API."
msgstr ""
"<cache_key_transformation>Ar an dara dul síos, cuireadh :ref: `leagan "
"<cache_versioning>`, :ref: `réamhshocrú ar fud an láithreáin` agus "
"<cache_key_prefixing>:ref: `claochlú `leis an API taisce."

msgid ""
"Thirdly, :ref:`cache key creation <using-vary-headers>` has been updated to "
"take the request query string into account on ``GET`` requests."
msgstr ""
"Ar an tríú dul síos, nuashonraí <using-vary-headers>odh :ref: `cruthú "
"eochair taiscéalaí` chun an teaghrán fiosrúcháin iarratais a chur san "
"áireamh ar iarratais ``GET``."

msgid ""
"Finally, support for pylibmc_ has been added to the memcached cache backend."
msgstr ""
"Faoi dheireadh, cuireadh tacaíocht do pylibmc_ leis an gcúltaca taisce "
"memcached."

msgid ""
"For more details, see the :doc:`documentation on caching in Django</topics/"
"cache>`."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí, féach an:doc: `doiciméadú maidir le caching in "
"Django`</topics/cache>."

msgid "Permissions for inactive users"
msgstr "Ceadanna d'úsáideoirí neamhriach"

msgid ""
"If you provide a custom auth backend with ``supports_inactive_user`` set to "
"``True``, an inactive ``User`` instance will check the backend for "
"permissions.  This is useful for further centralizing the permission "
"handling. See the :doc:`authentication docs </topics/auth/index>` for more "
"details."
msgstr ""
"Má sholáthraíonn tú cúltaca saincheaptha auth le ``supports_inactive_user`` "
"socraithe go ``True``, seiceálfaidh sampla neamhghníomhach ``Úsáideoir ``an "
"cúltaca le haghaidh ceadanna. Tá sé seo úsáideach chun an láimhseáil "
"ceadanna a lárú tuilleadh. Féach na:doc: `doiciméid fíordheimhniúcháin` le "
"haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí </topics/auth/index>."

msgid ""
"The GeoDjango test suite is now included when :ref:`running the Django test "
"suite <running-unit-tests>` with ``runtests.py`` when using :ref:`spatial "
"database backends <spatial-backends>`."
msgstr ""
"<spatial-backends>Tá an tsraith tástála GeodJango san áireamh anois nuair: "
"ref: `ag rith an tsraith tástála Django `le ``runtests.py`` nuair a "
"úsáidtear: ref: <running-unit-tests>`cúltaca bunachar sonraí spásúla`."

msgid ":setting:`MEDIA_URL` and :setting:`STATIC_URL` must end in a slash"
msgstr ""
":setting: `MEDIA_URL` agus:setting: `STATIC_URL` caithfidh deireadh a chur "
"le slasc"

msgid ""
"Previously, the :setting:`MEDIA_URL` setting only required a trailing slash "
"if it contained a suffix beyond the domain name."
msgstr ""
"Roimhe seo, ní theastaigh le socrú: socrú: `MEDIA_URL` ach amháin má bhí "
"iarmhír ann níos faide ná an ainm fearainn."

msgid ""
"A trailing slash is now *required* for :setting:`MEDIA_URL` and the "
"new :setting:`STATIC_URL` setting as long as it is not blank. This ensures "
"there is a consistent way to combine paths in templates."
msgstr ""
"Tá slais leantach ag teastáil * anois * le haghaidh :setting:`MEDIA_URL` "
"agus an socrú nua ::`STATIC_URL` chomh fada agus nach bhfuil sé bán. "
"Cinntíonn sé seo go bhfuil bealach comhsheasmhach ann chun cosáin a "
"chomhcheangal i dteimpléid."

msgid ""
"Project settings which provide either of both settings without a trailing "
"slash will now raise a ``PendingDeprecationWarning``."
msgstr ""
"Ardóidh socruithe tionscadail a sholáthraíonn ceachtar den dá shocrú gan "
"slasc rianaithe ``PendingDeprecationWarning`` anois."

msgid ""
"In Django 1.4 this same condition will raise ``DeprecationWarning``, and in "
"Django 1.5 will raise an ``ImproperlyConfigured`` exception."
msgstr ""
"I Django 1.4 ardóidh an coinníoll céanna seo ``DeprecationWarning``, agus i "
"Django 1.5 ardóidh sé eisceacht ``ImproperlyConfigurred``."

msgid "Everything else"
msgstr "Gach rud eile"

msgid ""
"Django :doc:`1.1 <1.1>` and :doc:`1.2 <1.2>` added lots of big ticket items "
"to Django, like multiple-database support, model validation, and a session-"
"based messages framework. However, this focus on big features came at the "
"cost of lots of smaller features."
msgstr ""
"Chuir Django:doc: `1.1 <1.1>`agus:doc: `1.2<1.2>` go leor earraí ticéad móra "
"le Django, cosúil le tacaíocht ilbhunachar sonraí, bailíochtú samhail, agus "
"creat teachtaireachtaí bunaithe ar sheisiún. Mar sin féin, tháinig an fócas "
"seo ar ghnéithe móra ar chostas go leor gnéithe níos lú."

msgid ""
"To compensate for this, the focus of the Django 1.3 development process has "
"been on adding lots of smaller, long standing feature requests. These "
"include:"
msgstr ""
"Chun cúiteamh air seo, bhí fócas an phróisis forbartha Django 1.3 ar go leor "
"iarratais gné níos lú, fada a chur leis. Ina measc seo tá:"

msgid ""
"Improved tools for accessing and manipulating the "
"current :class:`~django.contrib.sites.models.Site` object in :doc:`the sites "
"framework </ref/contrib/sites>`."
msgstr ""
"Uirlisí feabhsaithe chun an réad reatha: class: "
"`~django.contrib.sites.models.site` a rochtain agus a ionramháil in:doc: "
"`creat </ref/contrib/sites> na láithreáin ghréamh`."

msgid "A :class:`~django.test.RequestFactory` for mocking requests in tests."
msgstr ""
"A: Aicme: `~ Django.Test.RequestFactory` chun iarratais a mheaitseáil i "
"dtástálacha."

msgid ""
"A new test assertion "
"-- :meth:`~django.test.TransactionTestCase.assertNumQueries` -- making it "
"easier to test the database activity associated with a view."
msgstr ""
"Dearbhú tástála nua --:meth: "
"`~django.test.transactionTestCase.assertNumqueries` - rud a fhágann go "
"bhfuil sé níos éasca gníomhaíocht an bhunachar sonraí a bhaineann le radharc "
"a thástáil."

msgid ""
"Support for lookups spanning relations in "
"admin's :attr:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.list_filter`."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíocht do chuardaigh a chuimsíonn caidreamh i admin 's:attr: "
"`~django.contrib.admin.modeladmin.list_filter`."

msgid "Support for HttpOnly_ cookies."
msgstr "Tacaíocht do fhianáin HTTPOnly_."

msgid ""
":func:`~django.core.mail.mail_admins` "
"and :func:`~django.core.mail.mail_managers` now support easily attaching "
"HTML content to messages."
msgstr ""

msgid ":class:`~django.core.mail.EmailMessage` now supports CC's."
msgstr ":class: `~django.core.mail.emailMessage` tacaíonn anois le CC."

msgid ""
"Error emails now include more of the detail and formatting of the debug "
"server error page."
msgstr ""
"Áiríonn ríomhphoist earráide anois níos mó sonraí agus formáidiú leathanach "
"earráide an fhreastalaí dífhabhtaithe."

msgid ""
":meth:`~django.template.Library.simple_tag` now accepts a ``takes_context`` "
"argument, making it easier to write simple template tags that require access "
"to template context."
msgstr ""
":meth: `~django.template.library.simple_tag` glacann anois le argóint "
"``takes_context``, rud a fhágann go bhfuil sé níos éasca clibeanna teimpléad "
"simplí a scríobh a éilíonn rochtain ar chomhthéacs teimpléad."

msgid ""
"A new :meth:`~django.shortcuts.render()` shortcut -- an alternative to "
"``django.shortcuts.render_to_response()`` providing "
"a :class:`~django.template.RequestContext` by default."
msgstr ""
"Aicearra nua:meth: `~django.shortcuts.render () `- rogha eile seachas "
"``django.shortcuts.render_to_response () ``ag soláthar a:class: "
"`~django.template.requestContext` de réir réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"Support for combining :class:`F expressions <django.db.models.F>` with "
"``timedelta`` values when retrieving or updating database values."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíocht chun: aicme: abairtí `F `a chomhcheangal le luachanna` "
"<django.db.models.F>`timedelta` agus luachanna bunachar sonraí á aisghabháil "
"nó ag nuashonrú."

msgid "Backwards-incompatible changes in 1.3"
msgstr "Athruithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha ar chúl i 1.3"

msgid "CSRF validation now applies to AJAX requests"
msgstr "Baineann bailíochtú CSRF anois le hiarratais AJAX"

msgid ""
"Prior to Django 1.2.5, Django's CSRF-prevention system exempted AJAX "
"requests from CSRF verification; due to `security issues`_ reported to us, "
"however, *all* requests are now subjected to CSRF verification. "
"Consult :doc:`the Django CSRF documentation </ref/csrf>` for details on how "
"to handle CSRF verification in AJAX requests."
msgstr ""
"Roimh Django 1.2.5, dhíolmhaigh córas cosc CSRF Django iarratais AJAX ó "
"fhíorú CSRF; mar gheall ar `saincheisteanna slándála`_ a thuairiscíodh "
"dúinn, áfach, * uil* iarratais faoi réir fíorú CSRF anois. Téigh i "
"gcomhairl:doc: `an doiciméadú Django CSRF` le haghaidh sonraí maidir le "
"conas fíorú CSRF a láim</ref/csrf> hseáil in iarratais AJAX."

msgid ""
"Prior to Django 1.2.5, the Django administrative interface allowed filtering "
"on any model field or relation -- not just those specified in "
"``list_filter`` -- via query string manipulation. Due to security issues "
"reported to us, however, query string lookup arguments in the admin must be "
"for fields or relations specified in ``list_filter`` or ``date_hierarchy``."
msgstr ""
"Roimh Django 1.2.5, cheadaigh comhéadan riaracháin Django scagadh ar aon "
"réimse samhail nó gaol - ní amháin iad siúd a shonraítear i “list_filter” - "
"trí ionramháil sreangán fiosrúcháin. Mar gheall ar shaincheisteanna slándála "
"a tuairiscíodh dúinn, áfach, ní mór argóintí cuardaigh sreangán fiosrúcháin "
"sa riarachán a bheith le haghaidh réimsí nó caidrimh a shonraítear i "
"``list_filter`` nó ``date_hierarchy``."

msgid "Deleting a model doesn't delete associated files"
msgstr "Ní scriosann tú samhail comhaid ghaolmhara"

msgid ""
"In earlier Django versions, when a model instance containing "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.FileField` was "
"deleted, :class:`~django.db.models.FileField` took it upon itself to also "
"delete the file from the backend storage. This opened the door to several "
"data-loss scenarios, including rolled-back transactions and fields on "
"different models referencing the same file. In Django 1.3, when a model is "
"deleted the :class:`~django.db.models.FileField`’s ``delete()`` method won't "
"be called. If you need cleanup of orphaned files, you'll need to handle it "
"yourself (for instance, with a custom management command that can be run "
"manually or scheduled to run periodically via e.g. cron)."
msgstr ""
"I leaganacha Django níos luaithe, nuair a scriosadh samhail samhail ina "
"raibh a:class: `~django.db.models.filefield`, ghlac: :class: "
"`~django.db.models.filefield` leis an gcomhad a scriosadh ón stóráil cúltaca "
"freisin. D'oscail sé seo an doras do roinnt cásanna caillteanais sonraí, "
"lena n-áirítear idirbhearta rollta siar agus réimsí ar mhúnlaí éagsúla ag "
"tagairt don chomhad céanna. I Django 1.3, nuair a scriostar samhail ní "
"ghlaofar modh ``delete () ``ag: `class: `~Django.db.Models.FileField`. Más "
"gá duit comhaid dílleachta a ghlanadh, beidh ort é a láimhseáil tú féin (mar "
"shampla, le ordú bainistíochta saincheaptha is féidir a reáchtáil de láimh "
"nó a sceidealú le rith go tréimhsiúil trí e.g. cron)."

msgid "PasswordInput default rendering behavior"
msgstr "PasswordIompar rindreála réamhshocraithe Cuir isteach"

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.forms.PasswordInput` form widget, intended for use with "
"form fields which represent passwords, accepts a boolean keyword argument "
"``render_value`` indicating whether to send its data back to the browser "
"when displaying a submitted form with errors. Prior to Django 1.3, this "
"argument defaulted to ``True``, meaning that the submitted password would be "
"sent back to the browser as part of the form. Developers who wished to add a "
"bit of additional security by excluding that value from the redisplayed form "
"could instantiate a :class:`~django.forms.PasswordInput` passing "
"``render_value=False`` ."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an giuirléid fhoirme:class: `~django.forms.passwordInput`, atá "
"beartaithe le húsáid le réimsí foirme a léiríonn pasfhocail, le hargóint "
"eochairfhocal boolean ``render_value`` a léiríonn an gcuid sonraí a sheoladh "
"ar ais chuig an mbrabhsálaí nuair a thaispeántar foirm le hearráidí. Roimh "
"Django 1.3, réamhshocraigh an argóint seo go “True”, rud a chiallaíonn go "
"gcuirfí an pasfhocal curtha isteach ar ais chuig an mbrabhsálaí mar chuid "
"den fhoirm. D'fhéadfadh forbróirí a raibh siad ag iarraidh beagán slándála "
"breise a chur leis tríd an luach sin a eisiamh ón bhfoirm athléirithe a:: "
"class: `~django.forms.passwordInput` ag dul ``Render_Value=False``."

msgid ""
"Due to the sensitive nature of passwords, however, Django 1.3 takes this "
"step automatically; the default value of ``render_value`` is now ``False``, "
"and developers who want the password value returned to the browser on a "
"submission with errors (the previous behavior) must now explicitly indicate "
"this. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Mar gheall ar nádúr íogair na bhpasfhocail, áfach, glacann Django 1.3 an "
"chéim seo go huathoibríoch; is é “False” anois luach réamhshocraithe "
"``render_value``, agus ní mór d'fhorbróirí atá ag iarraidh an luach "
"pasfhocal a thabhairt ar ais chuig an bhbrabhsálaí ar aighneacht le "
"hearráidí (an t-iompar roimhe seo) anois. Mar shampla::"

msgid "Clearable default widget for FileField"
msgstr "Giuirléid réamhshocraithe inghlanaithe do FileField"

msgid ""
"Django 1.3 now includes a :class:`~django.forms.ClearableFileInput` form "
"widget in addition to :class:`~django.forms.FileInput`. "
"``ClearableFileInput`` renders with a checkbox to clear the field's value "
"(if the field has a value and is not required); ``FileInput`` provided no "
"means for clearing an existing file from a ``FileField``."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn Django 1.3 anois a: class: `~django.forms.clearaableFileInput` "
"giuirléid fhoirme i dteann:class: `~django.forms.fileInput`. Tugann "
"``ClearableFileInput`` bosca seiceála chun luach an réimse a ghlanadh (mura "
"bhfuil luach ag an réimse agus mura bhfuil sé riachtanach); ní sholáthraíodh "
"`FileInput`` aon bhealach chun comhad atá ann cheana a ghlanadh ó "
"`fileField`."

msgid ""
"``ClearableFileInput`` is now the default widget for a ``FileField``, so "
"existing forms including ``FileField`` without assigning a custom widget "
"will need to account for the possible extra checkbox in the rendered form "
"output."
msgstr ""
"Is é ``ClearableFileInput`` an giuirléid réamhshocraithe anois do "
"`FileField``, mar sin caithfidh foirmeacha atá ann cheana lena n-áirítear "
"``FileField`` gan giuirléid saincheaptha a shannadh cuntas a thabhairt ar an "
"mbosca seiceála breise féideartha san aschur foirme rindreáilte."

msgid ""
"To return to the previous rendering (without the ability to clear the "
"``FileField``), use the ``FileInput`` widget in place of "
"``ClearableFileInput``. For instance, in a ``ModelForm`` for a hypothetical "
"``Document`` model with a ``FileField`` named ``document``::"
msgstr ""
"Chun filleadh ar an rindreáil roimhe seo (gan an cumas an `FileField` a "
"ghlanadh), bain úsáid as an giuirléid ``FileInput`` in ionad "
"``ClearableFileInput``. Mar shampla, i `Modelfhoirme`` do mhúnla "
"hipitéiseach ``Doiciméad`` le `FileField`` darb ainm ``doiciméad``:"

msgid "New index on database session table"
msgstr "Innéacs nua ar thábla seisiún bunachar sonraí"

msgid ""
"Prior to Django 1.3, the database table used by the database backend for "
"the :doc:`sessions </topics/http/sessions>` app had no index on the "
"``expire_date`` column. As a result, date-based queries on the session table "
"-- such as the query that is needed to purge old sessions -- would be very "
"slow if there were lots of sessions."
msgstr ""
"Roimh Django 1.3, ní raibh aon innéacs ag an tábla bunachar sonraí a "
"úsáideann cúltaca an bhunachar sonraí don aip: doc: `seisiús` ar an gcolún "
"`expire_date` </topics/http/sessions>. Mar thoradh air sin, bheadh "
"ceisteanna dáta-bhunaithe ar an tábla seisiúin - mar an cheist atá ag "
"teastáil chun sean-sheisiúin a ghlanadh - an-mhall dá mbeadh go leor "
"seisiúin ann."

msgid ""
"If you have an existing project that is using the database session backend, "
"you don't have to do anything to accommodate this change. However, you may "
"get a significant performance boost if you manually add the new index to the "
"session table. The SQL that will add the index can be found by running the "
"``sqlindexes`` admin command:"
msgstr ""
"Má tá tionscadal ann cheana agat atá ag úsáid cúltaca seisiúin bunachar "
"sonraí, ní gá duit aon rud a dhéanamh chun freastal ar an athrú seo. Mar sin "
"féin, b'fhéidir go bhfaighidh tú borradh suntasach feidhmíochta má chuireann "
"tú an t-innéacs nua de láimh leis an tábla seisiúin. Is féidir an SQL a "
"chuirfidh an t-innéacs a fháil tríd an ordú riaracháin `sqlindexes`` a "
"reáchtáil:"

msgid "No more naughty words"
msgstr "Níl níos mó focail dhánna"

msgid ""
"Django has historically provided (and enforced) a list of profanities. The "
"comments app has enforced this list of profanities, preventing people from "
"submitting comments that contained one of those profanities."
msgstr ""
"Chuir Django liosta de bhróbanna ar fáil (agus a fhorfheidhmiú) go "
"stairiúil. Chuir an aip tráchtanna an liosta seo de bhráchtanna i bhfeidhm, "
"ag cosc ar dhaoine tuairimí a chur isteach ina raibh ceann de na díobhálacha "
"sin."

msgid ""
"Unfortunately, the technique used to implement this profanities list was "
"woefully naive, and prone to the `Scunthorpe problem`_. Improving the built-"
"in filter to fix this problem would require significant effort, and since "
"natural language processing isn't the normal domain of a web framework, we "
"have \"fixed\" the problem by making the list of prohibited words an empty "
"list."
msgstr ""
"Ar an drochuair, bhí an teicníc a úsáidtear chun an liosta dochtúireachtaí "
"seo a chur i bhfeidhm go hiomlán, agus seans go mbeadh an “fadhb Scunthorpe” "
"_ ann. Bheadh iarracht shuntasach ag teastáil leis an scagaire ionsuite a "
"fheabhsú chun an fhadhb seo a shocrú, agus ós rud é nach é próiseáil teanga "
"nádúrtha gnáthfhearann chreat gréasáin, tá an fhadhb “socraithe” againn trí "
"liosta folamh a dhéanamh ar liosta na bhfocal toirmiscthe."

msgid ""
"If you want to restore the old behavior, simply put a ``PROFANITIES_LIST`` "
"setting in your settings file that includes the words that you want to "
"prohibit (see the :commit:`commit that implemented this change "
"<edd767d2612d891a906268cf590571f541dd164f>` if you want to see the list of "
"words that was historically prohibited). However, if avoiding profanities is "
"important to you, you would be well advised to seek out a better, less naive "
"approach to the problem."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat an sean-iompar a chur ar ais, ní gá ach socrú "
"``PROFANITIES_LIST`` a chur i do chomhad socruithe a chuimsíonn na focail ar "
"mhaith leat a thoirmeasc (féach na:commit: `commit: `commit a chuir an t-"
"athrú seo i bhfeidhm <edd767d2612d891a906268cf590571f541dd164f>`más mian "
"leat an liosta focal a fheiceáil a bhí toirmiscthe go stairiúil). Mar sin "
"féin, má tá sé tábhachtach duit dífhabhachtaí a sheachaint, mholfaí duit cur "
"chuige níos fearr, chomh naif a lorg maidir leis an bhfadhb."

msgid "Localflavor changes"
msgstr "Athruithe Localflavour"

msgid ""
"Django 1.3 introduces the following backwards-incompatible changes to local "
"flavors:"
msgstr ""
"Tugann Django 1.3 na hathruithe seo a leanas isteach ar bhlasanna áitiúla "
"nach bhfuil comhoiriúnach ar gcúl:"

msgid ""
"Canada (ca) -- The province \"Newfoundland and Labrador\" has had its "
"province code updated to \"NL\", rather than the older \"NF\". In addition, "
"the Yukon Territory has had its province code corrected to \"YT\", instead "
"of \"YK\"."
msgstr ""
"Ceanada (ca) - Tá a chód cúige nuashonraithe go “NL” sa chúige “Newfoundland "
"and Labrador”, seachas an “NF” níos sine. Ina theannta sin, tá a chód cúige "
"ceartaithe ag Críoch Yukon go “YT”, in ionad “YK”."

msgid ""
"Indonesia (id) -- The province \"Nanggroe Aceh Darussalam (NAD)\" has been "
"removed from the province list in favor of the new official designation "
"\"Aceh (ACE)\"."
msgstr ""
"An Indinéis (id) - Baineadh an cúige “Nanggroe Aceh Darussalam (NAD)” as "
"liosta na gcúige i bhfabhar an ainmniú oifigiúil nua “Aceh (ACE)”."

msgid ""
"United States of America (us) -- The list of \"states\" used by "
"``USStateField`` has expanded to include Armed Forces postal codes. This is "
"backwards-incompatible if you were relying on ``USStateField`` not including "
"them."
msgstr ""
"Stáit Aontaithe Mheiriceá (US) - Leathnaigh liosta na “stáit” a úsáideann "
"``UsStatefield` chun cóid poist na bhFórsaí Armtha a áireamh. Tá sé seo "
"comhoiriúnach ar chúl má bhí tú ag brath ar ``UsStateField`` gan iad san "
"áireamh."

msgid "FormSet updates"
msgstr "Nuashonruithe FormSet"

msgid ""
"In Django 1.3 ``FormSet`` creation behavior is modified slightly. "
"Historically the class didn't make a distinction between not being passed "
"data and being passed empty dictionary. This was inconsistent with behavior "
"in other parts of the framework. Starting with 1.3 if you pass in empty "
"dictionary the ``FormSet`` will raise a ``ValidationError``."
msgstr ""
"I Django 1.3 athraítear iompar cruthaithe ``FormSet ``beagán. Go stairiúil "
"níor rinne an rang idirdhealú idir gan sonraí a rith agus foclóir folamh a "
"rith. Bhí sé seo neamhréidh le hiompar i gcodanna eile den chreat. Ag tosú "
"le 1.3 má théann tú i bhfoclóir folamh ardóidh an ``FormSet`` "
"``ValidationError``."

msgid "For example with a ``FormSet``:"
msgstr "Mar shampla le ``FormSet``:"

msgid "the following code will raise a ``ValidationError``:"
msgstr "ardóidh an cód seo a leanas ``Error Validation``:"

msgid ""
"if you need to instantiate an empty ``FormSet``, don't pass in the data or "
"use ``None``:"
msgstr ""
"más gá duit ``FormSet`` folamh a chur isteach, ná cuir isteach sna sonraí nó "
"bain úsáid as ``None``:"

msgid "Callables in templates"
msgstr "Glaonna i dteimpléid"

msgid ""
"Previously, a callable in a template would only be called automatically as "
"part of the variable resolution process if it was retrieved via attribute "
"lookup. This was an inconsistency that could result in confusing and "
"unhelpful behavior:"
msgstr ""
"Roimhe seo, ní ghlaofaí glaoch inghlaonta i dteimpléad go huathoibríoch mar "
"chuid den phróiseas réitigh athraitheach ach dá n-aisghairfí é trí chuardach "
"tréithe. Neamhréireacht a bhí ann a d'fhéadfadh iompar mearbhall agus "
"neamhchabhrach a bheith mar thoradh air:"

msgid ""
"This has been resolved in Django 1.3 - the result in both cases will be "
"``u'Joe Bloggs'``. Although the previous behavior was not useful for a "
"template language designed for web designers, and was never deliberately "
"supported, it is possible that some templates may be broken by this change."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé seo réitithe i Django 1.3 - is é `U'Joe Bloggs'`` an toradh sa dá "
"chás. Cé nach raibh an t-iompar roimhe seo úsáideach do theanga teimpléid a "
"dearthaíodh do dhearthóirí gréasáin, agus nár tacaíodh d'aon ghnó riamh, is "
"féidir go bhféadfadh roinnt teimpléid a bhriseadh leis an athrú seo."

msgid "Changed priority of translation loading"
msgstr "Tosaíocht athraithe ar luchtú aistriú"

msgid ""
"Work has been done to simplify, rationalize and properly document the "
"algorithm used by Django at runtime to build translations from the different "
"translations found on disk, namely:"
msgstr ""
"Tá obair déanta chun an t-algartam a úsáideann Django ag am rite a shimpliú, "
"a chuíchóiriú agus a dhoiciméadú i gceart chun aistriúcháin a chruthú ó na "
"haistriúcháin éagsúla a fhaightear ar diosca, mar atá:"

msgid ""
"For translatable literals found in Python code and templates (``'django'`` "
"gettext domain):"
msgstr ""
"Maidir le litríochtaí inaistrithe a fhaightear i gcód Python agus teimpléid "
"(fearann gettext ```django'``):"

msgid ""
"Priorities of translations included with applications listed in "
"the :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` setting were changed. To provide a behavior "
"consistent with other parts of Django that also use such setting (templates, "
"etc.) now, when building the translation that will be made available, the "
"apps listed first have higher precedence than the ones listed later."
msgstr ""
"Athraíodh tosaíochtaí na n-aistriúcháin san áireamh le feidhmchláir atá "
"liostaithe sa socrú: `INSTALLED_APPS`. Chun iompar a sholáthar atá "
"comhsheasmhach le codanna eile de Django a úsáideann socrú den sórt sin "
"(teimpléid, srl.) Anois, agus an t-aistriúchán a chuirfear ar fáil á "
"dtógáil, tá tosaíocht níos airde ag na feidhmchláir atá liostaithe ar dtús "
"ná na cinn atá liostaithe níos déanaí."

msgid ""
"Now it is possible to override the translations shipped with applications by "
"using the :setting:`LOCALE_PATHS` setting whose translations have now higher "
"precedence than the translations of :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` applications. "
"The relative priority among the values listed in this setting has also been "
"modified so the paths listed first have higher precedence than the ones "
"listed later."
msgstr ""
"Anois is féidir na haistriúcháin a sheoltar le feidhmchláir a shárú trí "
"úsáid a bhaint as an socrú :setting:`LOCALE_PATHS` a bhfuil tosaíocht níos "
"airde anois ag a n-aistriúcháin ná na haistriúcháin ar "
"fheidhmchláir :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`. Athraíodh an tosaíocht choibhneasta "
"i measc na luachanna atá liostaithe sa socrú seo freisin ionas go mbeidh "
"tosaíocht níos airde ag na cosáin a liostaítear ar dtús ná na cinn a "
"liostaítear níos déanaí."

msgid ""
"The ``locale`` subdirectory of the directory containing the settings, that "
"usually coincides with and is known as the *project directory* is being "
"deprecated in this release as a source of translations. (the precedence of "
"these translations is intermediate between applications "
"and :setting:`LOCALE_PATHS` translations). See the `corresponding deprecated "
"features section`_ of this document."
msgstr ""
"Tá fo-eolaire ``áitiúil ```den eolaire ina bhfuil na socruithe, a théann i "
"gcomhthráth leis agus ar a dtugtar an *stiúrthóireacht tionscadaile* de "
"ghnáth á ndíchur san eisiúint seo mar fhoinse aistriúcháin. (tá tosaíocht na "
"n-aistriúcháin seo idirmheánach idir iarratais agus:setting: `LOCALE_PATHS` "
"aistriúcháin). Féach ar an rannán `gnéithe luasghabháilte comhfhreagr`_ den "
"doiciméad seo."

msgid ""
"For translatable literals found in JavaScript code (``'djangojs'`` gettext "
"domain):"
msgstr ""
"Maidir le litríochtaí inaistrithe a fhaightear i gcód JavaScript (fearann "
"``djangojs'`` gettext):"

msgid ""
"Similarly to the ``'django'`` domain translations: Overriding of "
"translations shipped with applications by using the :setting:`LOCALE_PATHS` "
"setting is now possible for this domain too. These translations have higher "
"precedence than the translations of Python packages passed to the "
"``javascript_catalog()`` view. Paths listed first have higher precedence "
"than the ones listed later."
msgstr ""
"Mar an gcéanna leis na haistriúcháin fearainn ``'django'``: Is féidir "
"aistriúcháin a sheoltar le feidhmchláir a shárú trí úsáid a bhaint as an "
"socrú :setting:`LOCALE_PATHS` don fhearann ​​seo freisin. Tá tosaíocht níos "
"airde ag na haistriúcháin seo ná na haistriúcháin ar phacáistí Python a "
"cuireadh ar aghaidh chuig an radharc ``javascript_catalog()``. Tá tosaíocht "
"níos airde ag na cosáin a liostaítear ar dtús ná na cinn a liostaítear níos "
"déanaí."

msgid ""
"Translations under the ``locale`` subdirectory of the *project directory* "
"have never been taken in account for JavaScript translations and remain in "
"the same situation considering the deprecation of such location."
msgstr ""
"Níor cuireadh aistriúcháin faoi fho-eolaire ``áitiúil ``den *stiúrthóir "
"tionscadal* san áireamh riamh le haghaidh aistriúcháin JavaScript agus "
"fanann siad sa chás céanna ag smaoineamh ar an suíomh sin a dhíscaoileadh."

msgid "Transaction management"
msgstr "Bainistíocht idirbheart"

msgid ""
"When using managed transactions -- that is, anything but the default "
"autocommit mode -- it is important when a transaction is marked as "
"\"dirty\". Dirty transactions are committed by the ``commit_on_success`` "
"decorator or the ``django.middleware.transaction.TransactionMiddleware``, "
"and ``commit_manually`` forces them to be closed explicitly; clean "
"transactions \"get a pass\", which means they are usually rolled back at the "
"end of a request when the connection is closed."
msgstr ""
"Agus idirbhearta bainistithe á úsáid agat - is é sin, rud ar bith ach an "
"modh réamhshocraithe uathchomhartha - tá sé tábhachtach nuair a bhíonn "
"idirbheart marcáilte mar “salach”. Déanann an maisitheoir "
"``commit_on_success`` nó an "
"`django.middleware.transaction.transactionMiddleware` idirbhearta salacha, "
"agus cuireann ``commit_manually`` iallach orthu a dhúnadh go sainráite; "
"idirbhearta glan “faigheann pas”, rud a chiallaíonn go ndéantar iad a "
"rolladh ar ais ag deireadh iarratais nuair a dhúntar an nasc."

msgid ""
"Until Django 1.3, transactions were only marked dirty when Django was aware "
"of a modifying operation performed in them; that is, either some model was "
"saved, some bulk update or delete was performed, or the user explicitly "
"called ``transaction.set_dirty()``. In Django 1.3, a transaction is marked "
"dirty when *any* database operation is performed."
msgstr ""
"Go dtí Django 1.3, ní mharcáladh idirbhearta salach ach nuair a bhí Django "
"ar an eolas faoi oibríocht mhodhnaithe a rinneadh iontu; is é sin, sábháladh "
"samhail éigin, rinneadh roinnt nuashonrú nó scriosadh mórchóir, nó tugtar go "
"sainráite ar an úsáideoir ``transaction.set_dirty () `. I Django 1.3, "
"déantar idirbheart salach a mharcáil nuair a dhéantar oibríocht bunachar "
"sonraí *aon n*."

msgid ""
"As a result of this change, you no longer need to set a transaction dirty "
"explicitly when you execute raw SQL or use a data-modifying ``SELECT``. "
"However, you *do* need to explicitly close any read-only transactions that "
"are being managed using ``commit_manually()``. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Mar thoradh ar an athrú seo, ní gá duit idirbheart salach a shocrú go "
"sainráite a thuilleadh nuair a fhorghníomhaíonn tú SQL amh nó nuair a "
"úsáideann tú “SELECT” a mhodhnú sonraí. Mar sin féin, ní mór duit* aon "
"idirbhearta léite amháin atá á bhainistiú ag baint úsáide as `commit_manual "
"() `a dhúnadh go sainráite. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"Prior to Django 1.3, this would work without error. However, under Django "
"1.3, this will raise "
"a :class:`~django.db.transaction.TransactionManagementError` because the "
"read operation that retrieves the ``MyObject`` instance leaves the "
"transaction in a dirty state."
msgstr ""
"Roimh Django 1.3, oibreodh sé seo gan earráid. Mar sin féin, faoi Django "
"1.3, ardóidh sé seo a:class: "
"`~django.db.transaction.transactionManagementError` toisc go bhfágann an "
"oibríocht léite a aisghabhann an cás ``Myobject`` an idirbheart i stát "
"salach."

msgid "No password reset for inactive users"
msgstr "Gan athshocrú pasfhocal d'úsáideoirí neamhghní"

msgid ""
"Prior to Django 1.3, inactive users were able to request a password reset "
"email and reset their password. In Django 1.3 inactive users will receive "
"the same message as a nonexistent account."
msgstr ""
"Roimh Django 1.3, bhí úsáideoirí neamhghníomhacha in ann ríomhphost "
"athshocraithe pasfhocal a iarraidh agus a bhfocal faire a athshocrú. I "
"Django 1.3 gheobhaidh úsáideoirí neamhghníomhacha an teachtaireacht chéanna "
"le cuntas nach bhfuil ann."

msgid "Password reset view now accepts ``from_email``"
msgstr "Glacann amharc athshocraithe pasfhocal anois le ``from_email``"

msgid ""
"The ``django.contrib.auth.views.password_reset()`` view now accepts a "
"``from_email`` parameter, which is passed to the ``password_reset_form``’s "
"``save()`` method as a keyword argument. If you are using this view with a "
"custom password reset form, then you will need to ensure your form's "
"``save()`` method accepts this keyword argument."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an radharc ``django.contrib.auth.views.password_reset () ``anois le "
"paraiméadar ``from_email``, a chuirtear chuig modh ``save () "
"``password_reset_form`` mar argóint eochairfhocal. Má tá an dearcadh seo á "
"úsáid agat le foirm athshocraithe pasfhocal saincheaptha, ansin beidh ort a "
"chinntiú go nglacann modh ``save () `d'fhoirm leis an argóint eochairfhocal "
"seo."

msgid "Features deprecated in 1.3"
msgstr "Gnéithe atá díscríofa i 1.3"

msgid ""
"Django 1.3 deprecates some features from earlier releases. These features "
"are still supported, but will be gradually phased out over the next few "
"release cycles."
msgstr ""
"Déanann Django 1.3 roinnt gnéithe a dhíspreagadh ó eisiúintí níos luaithe. "
"Tacaítear leis na gnéithe seo fós, ach déanfar iad a dhíchur de réir a "
"chéile thar na cúpla timthriall scaoilte amach romhainn."

msgid ""
"Code taking advantage of any of the features below will raise a "
"``PendingDeprecationWarning`` in Django 1.3. This warning will be silent by "
"default, but may be turned on using Python's :mod:`warnings` module, or by "
"running Python with a ``-Wd`` or ``-Wall`` flag."
msgstr ""
"Ardóidh an cód a bhaineann leas as aon cheann de na gnéithe thíos "
"``PendingDeprecationWarning`` i Django 1.3. Beidh an rabhadh seo ciúin de "
"réir réamhshocraithe, ach féadfar é a chasadh air ag baint úsáide as modúl "
"Python: MOD: `rabhaigh`, nó trí Python a reáchtáil le bratach ``-Wd`` nó ``-"
"Wall``."

msgid ""
"In Django 1.4, these warnings will become a ``DeprecationWarning``, which is "
"*not* silent. In Django 1.5 support for these features will be removed "
"entirely."
msgstr ""
"I Django 1.4, beidh na rabhaidh seo ina `DeprecationWarning``, ar* níl* "
"ciúin. I Django 1.5 bainfear tacaíocht do na gnéithe seo go hiomlán."

msgid ""
"For more details, see the documentation :doc:`Django's release process </"
"internals/release-process>` and our :doc:`deprecation timeline </internals/"
"deprecation>`."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí, féach an doiciméadúis:doc: `Próiseas "
"scaoileadh Django` agus inn:doc: `líne ama díphróiseálaí` </internals/"
"release-process> </internals/deprecation>."

msgid "``mod_python`` support"
msgstr "Tacaíocht ``mod_python``"

msgid ""
"The ``mod_python`` library has not had a release since 2007 or a commit "
"since 2008. The Apache Foundation board voted to remove ``mod_python`` from "
"the set of active projects in its version control repositories, and its lead "
"developer has shifted all of his efforts toward the lighter, slimmer, more "
"stable, and more flexible ``mod_wsgi`` backend."
msgstr ""
"Níl scaoileadh ag an leabharlann `mod_python`` ó 2007 ná tiomantas ó 2008. "
"Vótáil bord Fondúireachta Apache ``mod_python`` a bhaint as an tsraith "
"tionscadal gníomhacha ina stórais rialaithe leaganacha, agus tá a "
"phríomhfhorbróir tar éis a chuid iarrachtaí go léir a aistriú i dtreo an "
"cúltaca `mod_wsgi` níos éadroime, níos cobhsaí agus níos solúbtha."

msgid ""
"If you are currently using the ``mod_python`` request handler, you should "
"redeploy your Django projects using another request handler. :doc:`mod_wsgi "
"</howto/deployment/wsgi/modwsgi>` is the request handler recommended by the "
"Django project, but FastCGI is also supported. Support for ``mod_python`` "
"deployment will be removed in Django 1.5."
msgstr ""
"Má tá an láimhseálaí iarratais `mod_python`` á úsáid agat faoi láthair, ba "
"cheart duit do thionscadail Django a athúsáid ag baint úsáide as láimhseálaí "
"iarratais eile. :doc: Is é `mod_wsgi` an láimhseálaí iarrat</howto/"
"deployment/wsgi/modwsgi> ais a mhol tionscadal Django, ach tacaítear le "
"FastCGI freisin. Bainfear tacaíocht d'imscaradh `mod_python`` i Django 1.5."

msgid "Function-based generic views"
msgstr "Tuairimí cineálacha ar fheidhm"

msgid ""
"As a result of the introduction of class-based generic views, the function-"
"based generic views provided by Django have been deprecated. The following "
"modules and the views they contain have been deprecated:"
msgstr ""
"Mar thoradh ar tuairimí cineálacha aicmbunaithe a thabhairt isteach, tá na "
"tuairimí cineálacha bunaithe ar fheidhm a sholáthraíonn Django a chuir "
"isteach. Rinneadh na modúil seo a leanas agus na tuairimí atá iontu a "
"dhíchur:"

msgid "``django.views.generic.create_update``"
msgstr "``django.views.generic.create_nuashonraithe``"

msgid "``django.views.generic.date_based``"
msgstr "``django.views.generic.date_based``"

msgid "``django.views.generic.list_detail``"
msgstr "``django.views.generic.list_details ``"

msgid "``django.views.generic.simple``"
msgstr "``django.views.generic.simpl``"

msgid "Test client response ``template`` attribute"
msgstr "Tástáil freagra cliant ``teimpléad` tréith"

msgid ""
"Django's :ref:`test client <test-client>` "
"returns :class:`~django.test.Response` objects annotated with extra testing "
"information. In Django versions prior to 1.3, this included a ``template`` "
"attribute containing information about templates rendered in generating the "
"response: either None, a single :class:`~django.template.Template` object, "
"or a list of :class:`~django.template.Template` objects. This inconsistency "
"in return values (sometimes a list, sometimes not) made the attribute "
"difficult to work with."
msgstr ""
"Tugann :tag:`cliant tástála <test-client>` ag Django ar "
"ais :class:`~django.test.Response` réada anótáilte le faisnéis tástála "
"breise. I leaganacha Django roimh 1.3, chuimsigh sé seo aitreabúid "
"``teimpléad`` ina raibh faisnéis faoi theimpléid a tugadh chun an freagra a "
"ghiniúint: ceachtar Dada, réad :class:`~django.template.Template` amháin, nó "
"liosta de :class :`~django.template.Template` réada. Mar gheall ar an "
"neamhréireacht seo sna luachanna tuairisceáin (uaireanta liosta, uaireanta "
"ní raibh) ba dheacair oibriú leis an tréith."

msgid ""
"In Django 1.3 the ``template`` attribute is deprecated in favor of a "
"new :attr:`~django.test.Response.templates` attribute, which is always a "
"list, even if it has only a single element or no elements."
msgstr ""
"I Django 1.3 tá an tréith ``template`` a dhíchur i bhfabhar nua:attr: "
"`~django.test.response.templates` tréith, atá i gcónaí ina liosta, fiú mura "
"bhfuil ach eilimint amháin nó gan aon eilimintí aige."

msgid "``DjangoTestRunner``"
msgstr "``Djangotestrunner``"

msgid ""
"As a result of the introduction of support for ``unittest2``, the features "
"of ``django.test.simple.DjangoTestRunner`` (including fail-fast and Ctrl-C "
"test termination) have been made redundant. In view of this redundancy, "
"``DjangoTestRunner`` has been turned into an empty placeholder class, and "
"will be removed entirely in Django 1.5."
msgstr ""
"Mar thoradh ar thacaíocht a thabhairt isteach do `unittest2`, rinneadh "
"gnéithe ``Django.Test.Simple.DjangoTestRunner`` (lena n-áirítear "
"foirceannadh tástála teip tapa agus Ctrl-C) iomarcach. Mar gheall ar an "
"iomarcaíocht seo, rinneadh ``Djangotestrunner`` a iompú ina rang sealbhóra "
"áit folamh, agus bainfear é go hiomlán i Django 1.5."

msgid "Changes to ``url`` and ``ssi``"
msgstr "Athruithe ar ``url ``agus ``ssi``"

msgid ""
"Most template tags will allow you to pass in either constants or variables "
"as arguments -- for example:"
msgstr ""
"Ligfidh an chuid is mó de na clibeanna teimpléad duit comhsheasmhainní nó "
"athróga a rith isteach mar argóintí - mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"allows you to specify a base template as a constant, but if you have a "
"context variable ``templ`` that contains the value ``base.html``:"
msgstr ""
"ligeann duit teimpléad bonn a shonrú mar thairiseach, ach má tá athróg "
"comhthéacs agat ``templ`` ina bhfuil an luach ``base.html``:"

msgid "is also legal."
msgstr "tá sé dlíthiúil freisin."

msgid ""
"However, due to an accident of history, the ``url`` and ``ssi`` are "
"different. These tags use the second, quoteless syntax, but interpret the "
"argument as a constant. This means it isn't possible to use a context "
"variable as the target of a ``url`` and ``ssi`` tag."
msgstr ""
"Mar gheall ar thimpiste staire, áfach, tá an `url ``agus `ssi`` difriúil. "
"Úsáideann na clibeanna seo an dara comhréir gan chóta, ach léirmhíníonn an "
"argóint mar thrasuach. Ciallaíonn sé seo nach féidir athróg comhthéacs a "
"úsáid mar sprioc chlib ``url ``agus `ssi``."

msgid ""
"Django 1.3 marks the start of the process to correct this historical "
"accident. Django 1.3 adds a new template library -- ``future`` -- that "
"provides alternate implementations of the ``url`` and ``ssi`` template tags. "
"This ``future`` library implement behavior that makes the handling of the "
"first argument consistent with the handling of all other variables. So, an "
"existing template that contains:"
msgstr ""
"Marcann Django 1.3 tús an phróisis chun an timpiste stairiúil seo a cheartú. "
"Cuireann Django 1.3 leabharlann teimpléad nua leis - ``todhcha`` - a "
"sholáthraíonn cur i bhfeidhm malartacha ar na clibeanna teimpléad ``url "
"``agus `ssi``. Cuireann an leabharlann “todhchaí” seo iompar i bhfeidhm a "
"fhágann go bhfuil láimhseáil an chéad argóint comhsheasmhach le láimhseáil "
"gach athróg eile. Mar sin, teimpléad atá ann cheana ina bhfuil:"

msgid "should be replaced with:"
msgstr "ba chóir iad a chur in ionad:"

msgid ""
"The tags implementing the old behavior have been deprecated, and in Django "
"1.5, the old behavior will be replaced with the new behavior. To ensure "
"compatibility with future versions of Django, existing templates should be "
"modified to use the new ``future`` libraries and syntax."
msgstr ""
"Tá na clibeanna a chuireann an sean-iompar i bhfeidhm imithe i léig, agus i "
"Django 1.5, cuirfear an t-iompar nua in ionad an tseaniompar. Chun "
"comhoiriúnacht le leaganacha amach anseo de Django a chinntiú, ba cheart na "
"teimpléid atá ann cheana a mhodhnú chun na leabharlanna agus an chomhréir "
"nua ``todhchaí`` a úsáid."

msgid "Changes to the login methods of the admin"
msgstr "Athruithe ar na modhanna logála isteach an riaracháin"

msgid ""
"In previous version the admin app defined login methods in multiple "
"locations and ignored the almost identical implementation in the already "
"used auth app. A side effect of this duplication was the missing adoption of "
"the changes made in :commit:`r12634 "
"<c8015052d935a99a5c8f96434b2d0cd16d8a4e14>` to support a broader set of "
"characters for usernames."
msgstr ""
"Sa leagan roimhe seo shainigh an aip riaracháin modhanna logála isteach in "
"áiteanna éagsúla agus rinne sé neamhaird ar an gcur i bhfeidhm beagnach "
"comhionann san aip auth Ba é fo-éifeacht a bhaineann leis an dúbailt seo ná "
"glacadh in easnamh na hathruithe a rinneadh in:commit: `r12634 "
"<c8015052d935a99a5c8f96434b2d0cd16d8a4e14>`chun tacú le tacú le sraith "
"carachtair níos leithne d'ainmneacha úsáideora."

msgid ""
"This release refactors the admin's login mechanism to use a subclass of "
"the :class:`~django.contrib.auth.forms.AuthenticationForm` instead of a "
"manual form validation. The previously undocumented method "
"``'django.contrib.admin.sites.AdminSite.display_login_form'`` has been "
"removed in favor of a new :attr:`~django.contrib.admin.AdminSite.login_form` "
"attribute."
msgstr ""
"Athraíonn an scaoileadh seo meicníocht logála isteach an riaracháin chun fo-"
"aicme den: class: `~django.contrib.auth.forms.AuthenticationForm` a úsáid in "
"ionad bailíochtú foirme láimhe. Baineadh an modh neamhdhoiciméadaithe roimhe "
"seo ``Django.contrib.admin.sites.adminsite.display_login_form'`` i bhfabhar "
"tréith nua:attr: `~django.contrib.admin.admin.adminsite.login_form`."

msgid "``reset`` and ``sqlreset`` management commands"
msgstr "Orduithe bainistíochta ``reset`` agus `sqlreset ``"

msgid ""
"Those commands have been deprecated. The ``flush`` and ``sqlflush`` commands "
"can be used to delete everything. You can also use ALTER TABLE or DROP TABLE "
"statements manually."
msgstr ""
"Tá na horduithe sin díscríofa. Is féidir na horduithe ``flush ``agus "
"`sqlflush`` a úsáid chun gach rud a scriosadh. Is féidir leat ráitis ALTER "
"TABLE nó DROP TABLE a úsáid de láimh freisin."

msgid ""
"The function-based :setting:`TEST_RUNNER` previously used to execute the "
"GeoDjango test suite, ``django.contrib.gis.tests.run_gis_tests``, was "
"deprecated for the class-based runner, "
"``django.contrib.gis.tests.GeoDjangoTestSuiteRunner``."
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh an feidhm-bhunaithe:setting: `TEST_RUNNER` a úsáideadh roimhe seo "
"chun an tsraith tástála GeodJango a fhorghníomhú, "
"``django.contrib.gis.tests.run_gis_tests``, cuirtear as an riteoir rang-"
"bhunaithe, `Django.contrib.gis.tests.geodjangoTestSuiterunner``."

msgid ""
"Previously, calling :meth:`~django.contrib.gis.geos.GEOSGeometry.transform` "
"would silently do nothing when GDAL wasn't available.  Now, "
"a :class:`~django.contrib.gis.geos.GEOSException` is properly raised to "
"indicate possible faulty application code.  A warning is now raised "
"if :meth:`~django.contrib.gis.geos.GEOSGeometry.transform` is called when "
"the SRID of the geometry is less than 0 or ``None``."
msgstr ""
"Roimhe seo, ní dhéanfadh glaoch ar :meth: "
"`~django.contrib.gis.geos.geosgeometry.transform` rud ar bith go ciúin nuair "
"nach raibh GDAL ar fáil. Anois, a: aicme: "
"`~django.contrib.gis.geos.geosException` a ardaítear i gceart chun cód "
"iarratais lochtach féideartha a léiriú. Ardaítear rabhadh anois má thugtar: "
"meth: `~django.contrib.gis.geos.geosgeometry.transform` nuair a bhíonn SRID "
"an geoiméadair níos lú ná 0 nó ``None ``."

msgid "``CZBirthNumberField.clean``"
msgstr "``CZBirthNumberField.Clean``"

msgid ""
"Previously this field's ``clean()`` method accepted a second, gender, "
"argument which allowed stronger validation checks to be made, however since "
"this argument could never actually be passed from the Django form machinery "
"it is now pending deprecation."
msgstr ""
"Roimhe seo ghlac modh ``glan () ``réimse seo leis an dara argóint inscne, a "
"cheadaigh seiceálacha bailíochtaithe níos láidre a dhéanamh, ach ós rud é "
"nach bhféadfaí an argóint seo a rith riamh ón innealra foirme Django tá sé "
"ar feitheamh ar dhíscaoileadh."

msgid "``CompatCookie``"
msgstr "``CompatCookie``"

msgid ""
"Previously, ``django.http`` exposed an undocumented ``CompatCookie`` class, "
"which was a bugfix wrapper around the standard library ``SimpleCookie``. As "
"the fixes are moving upstream, this is now deprecated - you should use "
"``from django.http import SimpleCookie`` instead."
msgstr ""
"Roimhe seo, nocht ``django.http`` aicme ``CompatCookie`` "
"neamhdhoiciméadaithe, a bhí ina fillteán bugfix timpeall an leabharlainne "
"caighdeánach ``Simplecookie``. De réir mar a bhíonn na socruithe ag "
"gluaiseacht suas an sruth, tá sé seo níos luaithe anois - ba cheart duit "
"``from django.http allmhairiú SimpleCookie ``a úsáid ina ionad."

msgid "Loading of *project-level* translations"
msgstr "Aistriúcháin*leibhéal tionscadla* a luchtú"

msgid ""
"This release of Django starts the deprecation process for inclusion of "
"translations located under the so-called *project path* in the translation "
"building process performed at runtime. The :setting:`LOCALE_PATHS` setting "
"can be used for the same task by adding the filesystem path to a ``locale`` "
"directory containing project-level translations to the value of that setting."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann an scaoileadh seo de Django tús leis an bpróiseas díréitithe chun "
"aistriúcháin atá lonnaithe faoin mbealán* tionscadail mar a thugtar air a "
"chuimsiú sa phróiseas tógála aistriúchá Is féidir an socrú: SETTING: "
"`LOCALE_PATHS` a úsáid don tasc céanna trí chonair an chórais chomhaid a "
"chur le eolaire ``locale`` ina bhfuil aistriúcháin ar leibhéal tionscadail "
"chuig luach an socraithe sin."

msgid "Rationale for this decision:"
msgstr "Réasúnaíocht don chinneadh seo:"

msgid ""
"The *project path* has always been a loosely defined concept (actually, the "
"directory used for locating project-level translations is the directory "
"containing the settings module) and there has been a shift in other parts of "
"the framework to stop using it as a reference for location of assets at "
"runtime."
msgstr ""
"Is coincheap sainithe go scaoilte a bhí san *bealach tionscadal* i gcónaí (i "
"ndáiríre, is é an t-eolaire a úsáidtear chun aistriúcháin ar leibhéal "
"tionscadail a aimsiú an eolaire ina bhfuil an modúl socruithe ann) agus tá "
"athrú ann i gcodanna eile den chreat chun stop a úsáid mar thagairt do "
"shuíomh sócmhainní ag rith."

msgid ""
"Detection of the ``locale`` subdirectory tends to fail when the deployment "
"scenario is more complex than the basic one. e.g. it fails when the settings "
"module is a directory (ticket #10765)."
msgstr ""
"Is gnách go dteipeann ar an bhfo-eolaire ``áitiúil ``a bhrath nuair a bhíonn "
"an cás imscartha níos casta ná an ceann bunúsach. m.sh. teipeann air nuair "
"is eolaire é an modúl socruithe (ticéad #10765)."

msgid ""
"There are potential strange development- and deployment-time problems like "
"the fact that the ``project_dir/locale/`` subdir can generate spurious error "
"messages when the project directory is added to the Python path (``manage.py "
"runserver`` does this) and then it clashes with the equally named standard "
"library module, this is a typical warning message:"
msgstr ""
"Tá fadhbanna aisteach forbartha agus ama imscartha ann mar an bhfíric gur "
"féidir leis an subdir ``project_dir/locale/`` teachtaireachtaí earráide "
"bréige a ghiniúint nuair a chuirtear eolaire an tionscadail le cosán Python "
"(`manage.py runserver ``déanann é seo) agus ansin comhraíonn sé leis an "
"modúl leabharlainne caighdeánach, is teachtaireacht rabhaidh tipiciúil é seo:"

msgid ""
"This location wasn't included in the translation building process for "
"JavaScript literals. This deprecation removes such inconsistency."
msgstr ""
"Níor cuireadh an suíomh seo san áireamh sa phróiseas tógála aistriúcháin do "
"litríochtaí JavaScript. Cuireann an diúltú seo deireadh leis an "
"míchomhsheasmhacht sin."

msgid "``PermWrapper`` moved to ``django.contrib.auth.context_processors``"
msgstr ""
"``PermWrapper`` bogadh chuig ``django.contrib.auth.context_processors``"

msgid ""
"In Django 1.2, we began the process of changing the location of the ``auth`` "
"context processor from ``django.core.context_processors`` to "
"``django.contrib.auth.context_processors``. However, the ``PermWrapper`` "
"support class was mistakenly omitted from that migration. In Django 1.3, the "
"``PermWrapper`` class has also been moved to "
"``django.contrib.auth.context_processors``, along with the "
"``PermLookupDict`` support class. The new classes are functionally identical "
"to their old versions; only the module location has changed."
msgstr ""
"I Django 1.2, thosaíomar an próiseas chun suíomh an phróiseálaí comhthéacs "
"``auth`` a athrú ó ``django.core.context_processors`` go "
"`django.contrib.auth.context_processors``. Mar sin féin, fágadh an rang "
"tacaíochta `PermWrapper`` ón imirce sin faoi dhearmad. I Django 1.3, "
"aistríodh an rang ``PermWrapper`` chuig "
"``django.contrib.auth.context_processors``, chomh maith leis an rang "
"tacaíochta `PermlookUpdict``. Tá na ranganna nua comhionann go feidhmiúil "
"lena seanleaganacha; níor athraigh ach suíomh an mhodúil."

msgid "Removal of ``XMLField``"
msgstr "“XMLField” a bhaint"

msgid ""
"When Django was first released, Django included an ``XMLField`` that "
"performed automatic XML validation for any field input. However, this "
"validation function hasn't been performed since the introduction of "
"``newforms``, prior to the 1.0 release. As a result, ``XMLField`` as "
"currently implemented is functionally indistinguishable from a "
"simple :class:`~django.db.models.TextField`."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a scaoileadh Django den chéad uair, chuimsíonn Django ``XMLField`` a "
"rinne bailíochtú XML uathoibríoch d'aon ionchur réimse. Mar sin féin, níor "
"rinneadh an fheidhm bailíochtaithe seo ó tugadh isteach ``newforms`, roimh "
"an scaoileadh 1.0. Mar thoradh air sin, tá ``XMLField`` mar a chuirtear i "
"bhfeidhm faoi láthair neamh-idirdhealaithe go feidhmiúil ó shimple:class: "
"`~django.db.models.textfield`."

msgid ""
"For this reason, Django 1.3 has fast-tracked the deprecation of ``XMLField`` "
"-- instead of a two-release deprecation, ``XMLField`` will be removed "
"entirely in Django 1.4."
msgstr ""
"Ar an gcúis seo, tá Django 1.3 tar éis diúsceitheadh ``XMLField`` a rianú go "
"tapa - in ionad dí-eisiúint dhá scaoileadh, bainfear ``XMLField`` go hiomlán "
"i Django 1.4."

msgid ""
"It's easy to update your code to accommodate this change -- just replace all "
"uses of ``XMLField`` with ``TextField``, and remove the ``schema_path`` "
"keyword argument (if it is specified)."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé éasca do chód a nuashonrú chun freastal ar an athrú seo - ní gá ach "
"gach úsáid de ``XMLField` a chur in ionad ``Textfield`, agus bain an argóint "
"eochairfhocal ``schema_path`` (má shonraítear é)."

msgid "Django 1.3.1 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.3.1"

msgid "Welcome to Django 1.3.1!"
msgstr "Fáilte go Django 1.3.1!"

msgid ""
"This is the first security release in the Django 1.3 series, fixing several "
"security issues in Django 1.3.  Django 1.3.1 is a recommended upgrade for "
"all users of Django 1.3."
msgstr ""
"Is é seo an chéad eisiúint slándála sa tsraith Django 1.3, ag socraithe "
"roinnt saincheisteanna slándála i Django 1.3. Is uasghrádú molta é Django "
"1.3.1 do gach úsáideoir de Django 1.3."

msgid "Django 1.3.2 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.3.2"

msgid "*July 30, 2012*"
msgstr "*30 Iúil, 2012*"

msgid ""
"This is the second security release in the Django 1.3 series, fixing several "
"security issues in Django 1.3. Django 1.3.2 is a recommended upgrade for all "
"users of Django 1.3."
msgstr ""
"Is é seo an dara eisiúint slándála sa tsraith Django 1.3, ag socraithe "
"roinnt saincheisteanna slándála i Django 1.3. Is uasghrádú molta é Django "
"1.3.2 do gach úsáideoir Django 1.3."

msgid "Django 1.3.3 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.3.3"

msgid "*August 1, 2012*"
msgstr "*1 Lúnasa, 2012*"

msgid ""
"Following Monday's security release of :doc:`Django 1.3.2 </releases/"
"1.3.2>`, we began receiving reports that one of the fixes applied was "
"breaking Python 2.4 compatibility for Django 1.3. Since Python 2.4 is a "
"supported Python version for that release series, this release fixes "
"compatibility with Python 2.4."
msgstr ""
"Tar éis scaoileadh slándála Dé Luain :doc:`Django 1.3.2 </releases/1.3.2>`, "
"thosaigh muid ag fáil tuairiscí go raibh ceann de na réitigh a cuireadh i "
"bhfeidhm ag briseadh comhoiriúnacht Python 2.4 do Django 1.3. Ós rud é gur "
"leagan Python tacaithe é Python 2.4 don tsraith scaoileadh sin, socraíonn an "
"scaoileadh seo comhoiriúnacht le Python 2.4."

msgid "Django 1.3.4 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.3.4"

msgid "*October 17, 2012*"
msgstr "*Deireadh Fómhair 17, 2012*"

msgid "This is the fourth release in the Django 1.3 series."
msgstr "Is é seo an ceathrú eisiúint sa tsraith Django 1.3."

msgid "Host header poisoning"
msgstr "Nimhiú ceanntásc óstá"

msgid ""
"Some parts of Django -- independent of end-user-written applications -- make "
"use of full URLs, including domain name, which are generated from the HTTP "
"Host header. Some attacks against this are beyond Django's ability to "
"control, and require the web server to be properly configured; Django's "
"documentation has for some time contained notes advising users on such "
"configuration."
msgstr ""
"Baineann roinnt codanna de Django - neamhspleách ar fheidhmchláir scríofa ag "
"an úsáideoir deiridh - úsáid as URLanna iomlána, lena n-áirítear ainm "
"fearainn, a ghintear ó cheanntásc Óstach HTTP. Tá roinnt ionsaithe i gcoinne "
"seo thar chumas Django rialú, agus éilíonn siad go ndéanfar an freastalaí "
"gréasáin a chumrú i gceart; le tamall tá nótaí i ndoiciméadú Django ag "
"comhairle le húsáideoirí maidir le cumraíocht den sórt sin."

msgid ""
"Django's own built-in parsing of the Host header is, however, still "
"vulnerable, as was reported to us recently. The Host header parsing in "
"Django 1.3.3 and Django 1.4.1 -- specifically, "
"``django.http.HttpRequest.get_host()`` -- was incorrectly handling username/"
"password information in the header. Thus, for example, the following Host "
"header would be accepted by Django when running on ``validsite.com``:"
msgstr ""
"Tá parsáil ionsuite Django féin ar cheanntásc an Óstach fós leochaileach, "
"mar a tuairiscíodh dúinn le déanaí. Bhí an ceanntásc Óstach ag paráil i "
"Django 1.3.3 agus Django 1.4.1 - go sonrach, "
"``Django.http.HTTPrequest.get_host () ``-- ag láimhseáil faisnéis ainm "
"úsáideora/pasfhocal sa cheanntásc go mícheart. Dá bhrí sin, mar shampla, "
"glacfadh Django leis an gceannteideal Óstach seo a leanas agus é ag rith ar "
"`validsite.com``:"

msgid ""
"Using this, an attacker can cause parts of Django -- particularly the "
"password-reset mechanism -- to generate and display arbitrary URLs to users."
msgstr ""
"Agus é seo á úsáid, féadfaidh ionsaitheoir a chur faoi deara codanna de "
"Django -- go háirithe an mheicníocht um athshocrú pasfhocail -- URLanna "
"treallach a ghiniúint agus a thaispeáint d'úsáideoirí."

msgid ""
"To remedy this, the parsing in ``HttpRequest.get_host()`` is being modified; "
"Host headers which contain potentially dangerous content (such as username/"
"password pairs) now raise the "
"exception :exc:`django.core.exceptions.SuspiciousOperation`."
msgstr ""
"Chun é seo a leigheas, tá an parsáil in `HttpRequest.get_host () `á mhodhnú; "
"Ardaíonn ceannteidil óstach ina bhfuil ábhar a d'fhéadfadh a bheith "
"contúirteach (amhail péirí ainm úsáideora/pasfhocal) an eisceacht anois: "
"exc: `Django.Core.Exceptions.SuspiciousOperation`."

msgid ""
"Details of this issue were initially posted online as a `security advisory`_."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh sonraí faoin tsaincheist seo ar líne ar dtús mar “comhairleoir "
"slándála”."

msgid "Django 1.3.5 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.3.5"

msgid "*December 10, 2012*"
msgstr "*10 Nollaig, 2012*"

msgid ""
"Django 1.3.5 addresses two security issues present in previous Django "
"releases in the 1.3 series."
msgstr ""
"Tugann Django 1.3.5 aghaidh ar dhá shaincheist slándála i láthair in "
"eisiúintí Django roimhe seo sa tsraith 1.3."

msgid ""
"Please be aware that this security release is slightly different from "
"previous ones. Both issues addressed here have been dealt with in prior "
"security updates to Django. In one case, we have received ongoing reports of "
"problems, and in the other we've chosen to take further steps to tighten up "
"Django's code in response to independent discovery of potential problems "
"from multiple sources."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go bhfuil an eisiúint slándála seo beagán difriúil ó na "
"cinn roimhe seo. Déileáladh leis an dá shaincheist a ndearnadh aghaidh orthu "
"anseo i nuashonruithe slándála roimhe seo I gcás amháin, tá tuairiscí "
"leanúnacha faighte againn ar fhadhbanna, agus sa chás eile roghnaigh muid "
"céimeanna breise a ghlacadh chun cód Django a dhaingniú mar fhreagairt ar "
"fhadhbanna féideartha go neamhspleách ó fhoinsí iolracha."

msgid ""
"Several earlier Django security releases focused on the issue of poisoning "
"the HTTP Host header, causing Django to generate URLs pointing to arbitrary, "
"potentially-malicious domains."
msgstr ""
"Dhírigh roinnt eisiúintí slándála Django níos luaithe ar an gceist maidir le "
"nimhiú ceanntásc an Óstríomhaire HTTP, rud a fhágann gur ghin Django URLanna "
"a dhírigh ar fhearainn treallacha a d’fhéadfadh a bheith mailíseach."

msgid ""
"In response to further input received and reports of continuing issues "
"following the previous release, we're taking additional steps to tighten "
"Host header validation. Rather than attempt to accommodate all features HTTP "
"supports here, Django's Host header validation attempts to support a "
"smaller, but far more common, subset:"
msgstr ""
"Mar fhreagra ar ionchur breise a fuarthas agus tuairiscí faoi "
"shaincheisteanna leanúnacha tar éis an eisiúint roimhe seo, táimid ag "
"glacadh céimeanna breise chun bailíochtú ceann Seachas iarracht a dhéanamh "
"freastal ar na gnéithe go léir a thacaíonn HTTP anseo, déanann bailíochtú "
"ceanntásc Óstach Django tacú le fo-thacar níos lú, ach i bhfad níos "
"coitianta:"

msgid ""
"Hostnames must consist of characters ``[A-Za-z0-9]`` plus hyphen ('-') or "
"dot ('.')."
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh carachtair ``[a-Za-Z0-9] `móide hiphen ('-') nó ponc ('.') a "
"bheith comhdhéanta d'ainmneacha óstach."

msgid "IP addresses -- both IPv4 and IPv6 -- are permitted."
msgstr "Ceadaítear seoltaí IP - IPv4 agus IPv6 araon."

msgid "Port, if specified, is numeric."
msgstr "Tá calafort, má shonraítear é, uimhriúil."

msgid ""
"Any deviation from this will now be rejected, raising the "
"exception :exc:`django.core.exceptions.SuspiciousOperation`."
msgstr ""
"Diúltófar aon diall ó seo anois, ag ardú an eisceacht:exc: "
"`Django.Core.Exceptions.SuspiciousOperation`."

msgid "Redirect poisoning"
msgstr "Nimhiú a atreorú"

msgid ""
"Also following up on a previous issue: in July of this year, we made changes "
"to Django's HTTP redirect classes, performing additional validation of the "
"scheme of the URL to redirect to (since, both within Django's own supplied "
"applications and many third-party applications, accepting a user-supplied "
"redirect target is a common pattern)."
msgstr ""
"Ag leanúint ar shaincheist roimhe seo freisin: i mí Iúil na bliana seo, "
"rinneamar athruithe ar ranganna atreoraithe HTTP Django, ag déanamh "
"bailíochtú breise ar scéim an URL chun a atreorú chuig (ós rud é, laistigh "
"d'iarratais soláthraithe Django féin agus go leor iarratais tríú páirtí, is "
"patrún coitianta é glacadh le sprioc atreoraithe a sholáthraíonn an "
"úsáideoir)."

msgid ""
"Since then, two independent audits of the code turned up further potential "
"problems. So, similar to the Host-header issue, we are taking steps to "
"provide tighter validation in response to reported problems (primarily with "
"third-party applications, but to a certain extent also within Django "
"itself). This comes in two parts:"
msgstr ""
"Ó shin i leith, chuir dhá iniúchadh neamhspleách ar an gcód fadhbanna "
"féideartha breise. Mar sin, cosúil leis an gceist Ceannteideal Óstach, "
"táimid ag glacadh céimeanna chun bailíochtú níos déine a sholáthar mar "
"fhreagra ar fhadhbanna tuairiscithe (go príomha le feidhmchláir tríú páirtí, "
"ach go pointe áirithe laistigh de Django féin Tagann sé seo i dhá chuid:"

msgid ""
"1. A new utility function, ``django.utils.http.is_safe_url``, is added; this "
"function takes a URL and a hostname, and checks that the URL is either "
"relative, or if absolute matches the supplied hostname. This function is "
"intended for use whenever user-supplied redirect targets are accepted, to "
"ensure that such redirects cannot lead to arbitrary third-party sites."
msgstr ""
"1. Cuirtear feidhm fóntais nua, `` django.utils.http.is_safe_url``, leis; "
"glacann an fheidhm seo URL agus óstainm, agus seiceálann sé go bhfuil an URL "
"coibhneasta, nó má thagann leis an óstainm a soláthraíodh. Tá an fheidhm seo "
"beartaithe lena húsáid aon uair a ghlactar le spriocanna atreoraithe arna "
"soláthar ag an úsáideoir, lena chinntiú nach féidir le hathsheolaidh dá "
"leithéid teacht chuig suíomhanna treallacha tríú páirtí."

msgid ""
"2. All of Django's own built-in views -- primarily in the authentication "
"system -- which allow user-supplied redirect targets now use ``is_safe_url`` "
"to validate the supplied URL."
msgstr ""
"2. Úsáideann tuairimí ionsuite go léir Django féin - go príomha sa chóras "
"fíordheimhnithe - a ligeann spriocanna atreoraithe a sholáthraítear don "
"úsáideoir ``is_safe_url ``anois chun an URL a sholáthraítear a bhailíochtú."

msgid "Django 1.3.6 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.3.6"

msgid "*February 19, 2013*"
msgstr "*19 Feabhra, 2013*"

msgid ""
"Django 1.3.6 fixes four security issues present in previous Django releases "
"in the 1.3 series."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.3.6 ceithre shaincheist slándála atá i láthair in "
"eisiúintí Django roimhe seo sa tsraith 1.3."

msgid "This is the sixth bugfix/security release in the Django 1.3 series."
msgstr "Is é seo an séú scaoileadh bugfix/slándála sa tsraith Django 1.3."

msgid ""
"Some parts of Django -- independent of end-user-written applications -- make "
"use of full URLs, including domain name, which are generated from the HTTP "
"Host header. Django's documentation has for some time contained notes "
"advising users on how to configure web servers to ensure that only valid "
"Host headers can reach the Django application. However, it has been reported "
"to us that even with the recommended web server configurations there are "
"still techniques available for tricking many common web servers into "
"supplying the application with an incorrect and possibly malicious Host "
"header."
msgstr ""
"Baineann roinnt codanna de Django - neamhspleách ar fheidhmchláir scríofa ag "
"an úsáideoir deiridh - úsáid as URLanna iomlána, lena n-áirítear ainm "
"fearainn, a ghintear ó cheanntásc Óstach HTTP. Tá nótaí i ndoiciméadú Django "
"le tamall a thugann comhairle le húsáideoirí maidir le conas freastalaithe "
"gréasáin a chumrú chun a chinntiú nach féidir ach ceanntásca bailí Óstach "
"feidhmchlár Django a bhaint amach. Mar sin féin, tuairiscíodh dúinn go "
"bhfuil teicnící ar fáil fós fiú leis na cumraíochtaí freastalaí gréasáin "
"molta chun go leor freastalaithe gréasáin coitianta a mhealladh chun "
"ceannteideal Óstach mícheart agus b'fhéidir mailíseach a sholáthar don "
"fheidhmchlár."

msgid ""
"For this reason, Django 1.3.6 adds a new setting, ``ALLOWED_HOSTS``, which "
"should contain an explicit list of valid host/domain names for this site. A "
"request with a Host header not matching an entry in this list will raise "
"``SuspiciousOperation`` if ``request.get_host()`` is called. For full "
"details see the documentation for the :setting:`ALLOWED_HOSTS` setting."
msgstr ""
"Ar an gcúis seo, cuireann Django 1.3.6 socrú nua leis, `ALLOWED_HOSTS`, ar "
"chóir go mbeadh liosta sainráite d'ainmneacha bailí óstaí/fearainn don "
"láithreán seo. Ardóidh iarratas le ceanntásc Óstach nach bhfuil iontráil sa "
"liosta seo ag teacht ar ```ConsumciousOperation`` má thugtar "
"``request.get_host () ``. Le haghaidh sonraí iomlána féach an doiciméadú don "
"socrú: setting: `ALLOWED_HOSTS`."

msgid ""
"The default value for this setting in Django 1.3.6 is ``['*']`` (matching "
"any host), for backwards-compatibility, but we strongly encourage all sites "
"to set a more restrictive value."
msgstr ""
"Is é an luach réamhshocraithe don socrú seo i Django 1.3.6 ná ``['*']`` (aon "
"óstach a mheaitseáil), le haghaidh comhoiriúnacht ar ais, ach molaimid go "
"láidir gach suíomh luach níos srianta a shocrú."

msgid ""
"This host validation is disabled when ``DEBUG`` is ``True`` or when running "
"tests."
msgstr ""
"Déantar an bailíochtú óstach seo a dhíchumasú nuair a bhíonn `DEBUG` "
"``True`` nó nuair a bhíonn tástálacha á reáchtáil."

msgid "XML deserialization"
msgstr "Dísheerialú XML"

msgid ""
"The XML parser in the Python standard library is vulnerable to a number of "
"attacks via external entities and entity expansion. Django uses this parser "
"for deserializing XML-formatted database fixtures. The fixture deserializer "
"is not intended for use with untrusted data, but in order to err on the side "
"of safety in Django 1.3.6 the XML deserializer refuses to parse an XML "
"document with a DTD (DOCTYPE definition), which closes off these attack "
"avenues."
msgstr ""
"Tá an parser XML i leabharlann caighdeánach Python leochaileach do roinnt "
"ionsaithe trí eintitis sheachtracha agus leathnú eintiteas. Úsáideann Django "
"an parser seo chun daingneáin bunachar sonraí formáidithe XML a dhísherialú. "
"Níl an deserializer daingneáin beartaithe le húsáid le sonraí neamhiontaofa, "
"ach d'fhonn earráid a dhéanamh ar thaobh na sábháilteachta i Django 1.3.6 "
"diúltaíonn an deserializer XML doiciméad XML a pharsáil le DTD (sainmhíniú "
"DOCTYPE), a dhúnann na bealaí ionsaithe seo."

msgid ""
"These issues in the Python standard library are CVE-2013-1664 and "
"CVE-2013-1665. More information available `from the Python security team`_."
msgstr ""
"Is iad na saincheisteanna seo i leabharlann caighdeánach Python ná "
"CVE-2013-1664 agus CVE-2013-1665. Tuilleadh faisnéise ar fáil `ó fhoireann "
"slándála Python`_."

msgid ""
"Django's XML serializer does not create documents with a DTD, so this should "
"not cause any issues with the typical round-trip from ``dumpdata`` to "
"``loaddata``, but if you feed your own XML documents to the ``loaddata`` "
"management command, you will need to ensure they do not contain a DTD."
msgstr ""
"Ní chruthaíonn serializer XML Django doiciméid le DTD, mar sin níor cheart "
"go gcuirfeadh sé seo aon fhadhbanna leis an turas babhta tipiciúil ó "
"`dumpdata` go `loaddata`, ach má bheathaíonn tú do dhoiciméid XML féin don "
"ordú bainistíochta `loaddata ``, beidh ort a chinntiú nach bhfuil DTD iontu."

msgid "Formset memory exhaustion"
msgstr "Ídiú cuimhne Formset"

msgid ""
"Previous versions of Django did not validate or limit the form-count data "
"provided by the client in a formset's management form, making it possible to "
"exhaust a server's available memory by forcing it to create very large "
"numbers of forms."
msgstr ""
"Níor ndearna leaganacha roimhe seo de Django na sonraí comhaireamh "
"foirmeacha a sholáthraíonn an cliant i bhfoirm bhainistíochta foirmeacha a "
"bhailíochtú ná teorainn, rud a fhág gur féidir cuimhne freastalaí atá ar "
"fáil a shícheadadh trí iallach air líon an-mhór foirmeacha a chruthú."

msgid ""
"In Django 1.3.6, all formsets have a strictly-enforced maximum number of "
"forms (1000 by default, though it can be set higher via the ``max_num`` "
"formset factory argument)."
msgstr ""
"I Django 1.3.6, tá uaslíon foirmeacha a fhorfheidhmithe go docht ag gach "
"tacar foirme (1000 de réir réamhshocraithe, cé gur féidir é a shocrú níos "
"airde tríd an argóint monarcha foirmset ``max_num``)."

msgid "Admin history view information leakage"
msgstr "Féach ar stair an riaracháin sceitheadh"

msgid ""
"In previous versions of Django, an admin user without change permission on a "
"model could still view the Unicode representation of instances via their "
"admin history log. Django 1.3.6 now limits the admin history log view for an "
"object to users with change permission for that model."
msgstr ""
"I leaganacha roimhe seo de Django, d'fhéadfadh úsáideoir riaracháin gan cead "
"athraithe ar mhúnla léiriú Unicode ar chásanna a fheiceáil fós trína log "
"stair riaracháin. Cuireann Django 1.3.6 teorainn anois ar an radharc log "
"stair riaracháin do réad d'úsáideoirí a bhfuil cead athraithe acu don "
"tsamhail sin."

msgid "Django 1.3.7 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.3.7"

msgid "*February 20, 2013*"
msgstr "*20 Feabhra, 2013*"

msgid ""
"Django 1.3.7 corrects a packaging problem with yesterday's :doc:`1.3.6 "
"release </releases/1.3.6>`."
msgstr ""
"Ceartaíonn Django 1.3.7 fadhb pacáistithe le :doc: `1.3.6 scaoileadh </"
"releases/1.3.6>`."

msgid ""
"The release contained stray ``.pyc`` files that caused \"bad magic number\" "
"errors when running with some versions of Python. This releases corrects "
"this, and also fixes a bad documentation link in the project template "
"``settings.py`` file generated by ``manage.py startproject``."
msgstr ""
"Bhí comhaid `.pyc`` straiteach sa eisiúint a bhí ina chúis le hearráidí "
"“droch-uimhir draíochta” agus iad ag rith le roinnt leaganacha de Python. "
"Ceartaíonn sé seo é seo, agus socraíonn sé droch-nasc doiciméadaithe i "
"gcomhad teimpléad an tionscadail `settings.py`` a ghineann `manage.py "
"startproject``."

msgid "Django 1.4 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.4"

msgid "*March 23, 2012*"
msgstr "*23 Márta, 2012*"

msgid "Welcome to Django 1.4!"
msgstr "Fáilte go dtí Django 1.4!"

msgid ""
"These release notes cover the :ref:`new features <whats-new-1.4>`, as well "
"as some :ref:`backwards incompatible changes <backwards-incompatible-1.4>` "
"you'll want to be aware of when upgrading from Django 1.3 or older versions. "
"We've also dropped some features, which are detailed in :ref:`our "
"deprecation plan <deprecation-removed-in-1.4>`, and we've :ref:`begun the "
"deprecation process for some features <deprecated-features-1.4>`."
msgstr ""
"Clúdaíonn na nótaí scaoilte seo na:ref: `gnéithe nua <whats-new-1.4>`, chomh "
"maith le roinnt athruithe: ref: `athruithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha ar "
"chúl<backwards-incompatible-1.4>` a mbeidh tú ag iarraidh a bheith ar an "
"eolas fúthu agus tú ag uasghrádú ó Django 1.3 nó leaganacha níos sine. "
"<deprecated-features-1.4>Tá roinnt gnéithe titim againn freisin, atá "
"mionsonraithe in:ref: `ár bplean díghabhála <deprecation-removed-in-1.4>`, "
"agus chuireamaire:ref: `tús leis an bpróiseas díghabhála do roinnt gnéithe`."

msgid ""
"The biggest new feature in Django 1.4 is `support for time zones`_ when "
"handling date/times. When enabled, this Django will store date/times in UTC, "
"use timezone-aware objects internally, and translate them to users' local "
"timezones for display."
msgstr ""
"Is é an ghné nua is mó i Django 1.4 ná `tacaíocht do chriosanna ama `_ agus "
"dáta/amanna á láimhseáil. Nuair a bheidh sé cumasaithe, stóráilfidh an "
"Django seo dáta/amanna in UTC, úsáidfidh sé rudaí atá ar an eolas faoi "
"chrios ama go hinmheánach, agus aistrfidh siad iad chuig criosanna ama "
"áitiúla úsáideoirí le taispeáint."

msgid ""
"If you're upgrading an existing project to Django 1.4, switching to the "
"timezone aware mode may take some care: the new mode disallows some rather "
"sloppy behavior that used to be accepted. We encourage anyone who's "
"upgrading to check out the :ref:`timezone migration guide <time-zones-"
"migration-guide>` and the :ref:`timezone FAQ <time-zones-faq>` for useful "
"pointers."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag uasghrádú ar thionscadal atá ann cheana go Django 1.4, "
"d'fhéadfadh go mbeadh cúram ag aistriú go dtí an modh feasach ar an gcrios "
"ama: ní cheadaíonn an modh nua roinnt iompar sách lasc a nglacíodh leis. "
"<time-zones-faq>Molaimid do dhuine ar bith atá ag uasghrádú chun seiceáil ar "
"an: ref: `treoir imirce crios ama `agus an:ref: `Ceisteanna Coitianta Time-"
"zone<time-zones-migration-guide>` le haghaidh leideanna úsáideacha."

msgid "Other notable new features in Django 1.4 include:"
msgstr "I measc na ngnéithe nua suntasacha eile i Django 1.4 tá:"

msgid ""
"A number of ORM improvements, including `SELECT FOR UPDATE support`_, the "
"ability to `bulk insert <#model-objects-bulk-create-in-the-orm>`_ large "
"datasets for improved performance, and `QuerySet.prefetch_related`_, a "
"method to batch-load related objects in areas "
"where :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.select_related` doesn't work."
msgstr ""
"Roinnt feabhsuithe ORM, lena n-áirítear `SELECT FOR UPDATE taca`_, an cumas "
"`mórchóir <#model-objects-bulk-create-in-the-orm>`_ tacair mhóra sonraí le "
"haghaidh feidhmíochta feabhsaithe, agus `QuerySet.prefetch_related`_, modh "
"chun rudaí gaolmhara a luchtú i réimsí ina nd:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.queryset.select.select.queryset.select.select.Ní oibríonn "
"_related`."

msgid ""
"Some nice security additions, including `improved password hashing`_ "
"(featuring PBKDF2_ and bcrypt_ support), new `tools for cryptographic "
"signing`_, several `CSRF improvements`_, and `simple clickjacking "
"protection`_."
msgstr ""
"Roinnt breiseanna slándála deas, lena n-áirítear `hashing pasfhocal "
"feabhsaithe`_ (ina bhfuil tacaíocht PBKDF2_ agus bcrypt_), `uirlisí nua le "
"haghaidh síniú cripteagrafac`_, roinnt feabhsuithe CSRF `_, agus `cosaint "
"clickjacking simplí`_."

msgid ""
"An `updated default project layout and manage.py`_ that removes the "
"\"magic\" from prior versions. And for those who don't like the new layout, "
"you can use `custom project and app templates`_ instead!"
msgstr ""
"'leagan amach tionscadail réamhshocraithe nuashonraithe agus manage.py`_ a "
"bhaineann an “draíocht” ó leaganacha roimhe seo. Agus dóibh siúd nach "
"dtaitníonn an leagan amach nua dóibh, is féidir leat `teimpléid tionscadail "
"agus aipeanna saincheapaithe`_ a úsáid ina ionad sin!"

msgid "`Support for in-browser testing frameworks`_ (like Selenium_)."
msgstr ""
"`Tacaíocht do chreataí tástála in-bhrabhsálaí `_ (cosúil le Selenium_)."

msgid "... and a whole lot more; `see below <#what-s-new-in-django-1-4>`_!"
msgstr "... agus go leor eile; `féach thíos <#what-s-new-in-django-1-4>`_!"

msgid ""
"Wherever possible we try to introduce new features in a backwards-compatible "
"manner per :doc:`our API stability policy </misc/api-stability>` policy. "
"However, as with previous releases, Django 1.4 ships with some "
"minor :ref:`backwards incompatible changes <backwards-incompatible-1.4>`; "
"people upgrading from previous versions of Django should read that list "
"carefully."
msgstr ""
"Nuair is féidir déanaimid iarracht gnéithe nua a thabhairt isteach ar "
"bhealach atá comhoiriúnach ar gcúl de réir :doc:`ár mbeartas cobhsaíochta "
"API </misc/api-stability>`. Mar a tharla le heisiúintí roimhe seo, áfach, "
"long Django 1.4 le roinnt mionathruithe :tag:`ar gcúl athruithe neamh-"
"chomhoiriúnacha <backwards-incompatible-1.4>`; ba chóir do dhaoine atá ag "
"uasghrádú ó leaganacha níos sine de Django an liosta sin a léamh go cúramach."

msgid ""
"Django 1.4 has dropped support for Python 2.4. Python 2.5 is now the minimum "
"required Python version. Django is tested and supported on Python 2.5, 2.6 "
"and 2.7."
msgstr ""
"Tá tacaíocht do Python 2.4 titim ag Django 1.4. Is é Python 2.5 anois an "
"leagan Python íosta riachtanach. Déantar tástáil agus tacaítear le Django ar "
"Python 2.5, 2.6 agus 2.7."

msgid ""
"This change should affect only a small number of Django users, as most "
"operating-system vendors today are shipping Python 2.5 or newer as their "
"default version. If you're still using Python 2.4, however, you'll need to "
"stick to Django 1.3 until you can upgrade. Per :doc:`our support policy </"
"internals/release-process>`, Django 1.3 will continue to receive security "
"support until the release of Django 1.5."
msgstr ""
"Níor cheart go mbíonn tionchar ag an athrú seo ach ar líon beag úsáideoirí "
"Django, mar tá formhór na ndíoltóirí córais oibriúcháin inniu ag seoladh "
"Python 2.5 nó níos nuaí mar a leagan réamhshoc Má tá Python 2.4 á úsáid agat "
"fós, áfach, beidh ort cloí le Django 1.3 go dtí gur féidir leat uasghrádú a "
"dhéanamh. Per:doc: `ár mbeartas tacaíochta ', leanfaidh </internals/release-"
"process> Django 1.3 ag fáil tacaíochta slándála go dtí go scaoilfear Django "
"1.5."

msgid ""
"Django does not support Python 3.x at this time. At some point before the "
"release of Django 1.4, we plan to publish a document outlining our full "
"timeline for deprecating Python 2.x and moving to Python 3.x."
msgstr ""
"Ní thacaíonn Django le Python 3.x ag an am seo. Ag pointe éigin roimh "
"scaoileadh Django 1.4, tá sé beartaithe againn doiciméad a fhoilsiú ina "
"leagtar amach ár n-amlíne iomlán chun Python 2.x a dhíspreagadh agus bogadh "
"go Python 3.x."

msgid "What's new in Django 1.4"
msgstr "Cad atá nua i Django 1.4"

msgid "Support for time zones"
msgstr "Tacaíocht do chriosanna ama"

msgid ""
"In previous versions, Django used \"naive\" date/times (that is, date/times "
"without an associated time zone), leaving it up to each developer to "
"interpret what a given date/time \"really means\". This can cause all sorts "
"of subtle timezone-related bugs."
msgstr ""
"I leaganacha roimhe seo, d’úsáid Django dáta/amanna “naive” (is é sin, dáta/"
"amanna gan crios ama gaolmhar), rud a fhágann gur faoi gach forbróir é a "
"léirmhíniú cad a chiallaíonn dáta/am tugtha “i ndáiríre”. Is féidir leis seo "
"a bheith ina chúis le gach cineál fabhtanna subtle a bhaineann le crios ama."

msgid ""
"In Django 1.4, you can now switch Django into a more correct, time-zone "
"aware mode. In this mode, Django stores date and  time information in UTC in "
"the database, uses time-zone-aware datetime objects internally and "
"translates them to the end user's time zone in templates and forms. Reasons "
"for using this feature include:"
msgstr ""
"I Django 1.4, is féidir leat Django a aistriú go modh níos ceart, atá "
"feasach ar chrios ama anois. Sa mhodh seo, stóráilíonn Django faisnéis dáta "
"agus ama i UTC sa bhunachar sonraí, úsáideann sé rudaí dáta-ama atá ar an "
"eolas ó chrios ama go hinmheánach agus aistríonn sé iad go crios ama an "
"úsáideora deiridh i dteimpléid agus i bhfoirmeacha. I measc na gcúiseanna "
"chun an ghné seo a úsáid tá:"

msgid "Customizing date and time display for users around the world."
msgstr ""
"Taispeántas dáta agus ama a shaincheapadh d'úsáideoirí ar fud an domhain."

msgid ""
"Storing datetimes in UTC for database portability and interoperability. "
"(This argument doesn't apply to PostgreSQL, because it already stores "
"timestamps with time zone information in Django 1.3.)"
msgstr ""
"Dáta a stóráil in UTC le haghaidh iniomparthacht bunachar sonraí agus idir-"
"inoibritheacht (Ní bhaineann an argóint seo le PostgreSQL, toisc go "
"stórálann sé stampaí ama cheana féin le faisnéis chrios ama i Django 1.3.)"

msgid "Avoiding data corruption problems around DST transitions."
msgstr "Fadhbanna éillithe sonraí a sheachaint ar aistrithe DST."

msgid ""
"Time zone support is enabled by default in new projects created "
"with :djadmin:`startproject`. If you want to use this feature in an existing "
"project, read the :ref:`migration guide <time-zones-migration-guide>`. If "
"you encounter problems, there's a helpful :ref:`FAQ <time-zones-faq>`."
msgstr ""
"Cumasaítear tacaíocht crios ama de réir réamhshocraithe i dtionscadail nua a "
"cruthaíodh le:djadmin: `startproject`. <time-zones-migration-guide>Más mian "
"leat an ghné seo a úsáid i dtionscadal atá ann cheana, léigh an:ref: `treoir "
"imirce``. <time-zones-faq>Má bhíonn fadhbanna agat, tá cabhrach ann: ref: "
"`Ceisteanna Coitianta `."

msgid "Support for in-browser testing frameworks"
msgstr "Tacaíocht do chreataí tástála in-bhrabhsála"

msgid ""
"Django 1.4 supports integration with in-browser testing frameworks like "
"Selenium_. The new :class:`django.test.LiveServerTestCase` base class lets "
"you test the interactions between your site's front and back ends more "
"comprehensively. See "
"the :class:`documentation<django.test.LiveServerTestCase>` for more details "
"and concrete examples."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn Django 1.4 le comhtháthú le creataí tástála in-bhrabhsálaí cosúil "
"le Selenium_. Ligeann an rang bonn nua:class: "
"`django.test.liveservertestcase` duit na hidirghníomhaíochtaí idir foircinn "
"tosaigh agus cúl do shuíomh a thástáil níos cuimsitheach. Féach an:class: "
"`doiciméadú <django.test.LiveServerTestCase>`le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí "
"agus samplaí nithiúla."

msgid "Updated default project layout and ``manage.py``"
msgstr ""
"Leagan amach tionscadail réamhshocraithe nuashonraithe agus `manage.py``"

msgid ""
"Django 1.4 ships with an updated default project layout and ``manage.py`` "
"file for the :djadmin:`startproject` management command. These fix some "
"issues with the previous ``manage.py`` handling of Python import paths that "
"caused double imports, trouble moving from development to deployment, and "
"other difficult-to-debug path issues."
msgstr ""
"Seoltar Django 1.4 le leagan amach réamhshocraithe tionscadail nuashonraithe "
"agus comhad ``manage.py`` don ordú bainistíochta : djadmin: `startproject`. "
"Réitíonn siad seo roinnt fadhbanna leis an láimhseáil ``manage.py`` roimhe "
"seo ar chonairí allmhairithe Python a d'eascair allmhairí dúbailte, "
"deacracht ag bogadh ó fhorbairt go himscaradh, agus saincheisteanna cosáin "
"eile a bhí deacair le dífhabhtú."

msgid ""
"The previous ``manage.py`` called functions that are now deprecated, and "
"thus projects upgrading to Django 1.4 should update their ``manage.py``. "
"(The old-style ``manage.py`` will continue to work as before until Django "
"1.6. In 1.5 it will raise ``DeprecationWarning``)."
msgstr ""
"Tugadh na `manage.py` roimhe seo ar fheidhmeanna atá díscoite anois, agus dá "
"bhrí sin ba cheart do thionscadail a uasghrádú go Django 1.4 a “manage.py” a "
"nuashonrú. (Leanfaidh an sean-stíl `manage.py`` ag obair mar a bhí roimhe "
"seo go dtí Django 1.6. I 1.5 ardóidh sé ``DeprecationWarning``)."

msgid "The new recommended ``manage.py`` file should look like this::"
msgstr "Ba chóir go mbeadh cuma seo ar an gcomhad nua `manage.py` a mholtar:"

msgid ""
"``{{ project_name }}`` should be replaced with the Python package name of "
"the actual project."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir ainm pacáiste Python an tionscadail iarbhír a chur in ionad "
"``{{project_name}}``."

msgid ""
"If settings, URLconfs and apps within the project are imported or referenced "
"using the project name prefix (e.g. ``myproject.settings``, ``ROOT_URLCONF = "
"\"myproject.urls\"``, etc.), the new ``manage.py`` will need to be moved one "
"directory up, so it is outside the project package rather than adjacent to "
"``settings.py`` and ``urls.py``."
msgstr ""
"Má iompórtáiltear nó má dhéantar socruithe, URLConfs agus aipeanna laistigh "
"den tionscadal ag úsáid réimír ainm an tionscadail (m.sh. "
"``myproject.settings``, `ROOT_URLCONF = “myproject.urls\"`, srl.), ní mór an "
"`manage.py` nua a aistriú suas, mar sin tá sé lasmuigh den phacáiste "
"tionscadail seachas in aice le `settings.py`` `agus ``urls.py``."

msgid "For instance, with the following layout:"
msgstr "Mar shampla, leis an leagan amach seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"You could import ``mysite.settings``, ``mysite.urls``, and ``mysite.myapp``, "
"but not ``settings``, ``urls``, or ``myapp`` as top-level modules."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfá ``mysite.settings``, `mysite.urls``, agus `mysite.myapp`` a "
"iompórtáil, ach ní ``settings``, ``urls``, nó `myapp`` mar mhodúil "
"barrleibhéil."

msgid ""
"Anything imported as a top-level module can be placed adjacent to the new "
"``manage.py``. For instance, to decouple ``myapp`` from the project module "
"and import it as just ``myapp``, place it outside the ``mysite/`` directory:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir aon rud a allmhairítear mar mhodúl barrleibhéil a chur in aice "
"leis an `manage.py` nua. Mar shampla, chun `myapp`` a dhícheangal ón modúl "
"tionscadail agus é a iompórtáil mar `myapp``, cuir lasmuigh den eolaire "
"``mysite/`` é:"

msgid ""
"If the same code is imported inconsistently (some places with the project "
"prefix, some places without it), the imports will need to be cleaned up when "
"switching to the new ``manage.py``."
msgstr ""
"Má iompórtar an cód céanna go neamhchomhsheasmhach (áiteanna áirithe le "
"réimír an tionscadail, áiteanna áirithe gan é), beidh gá na hallmhairí a "
"ghlanadh agus iad ag aistriú chuig an `manage.py` nua."

msgid "Custom project and app templates"
msgstr "Teimpléid tionscadail agus aip saincheaptha"

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`startapp` and :djadmin:`startproject` management commands now "
"have a ``--template`` option for specifying a path or URL to a custom app or "
"project template."
msgstr ""
"Tá rogha ``--teimpléad ``anois ag na horduithe bainistíochta: djadmin: "
"`startapp` agus:djadmin: `startproject` chun cosán nó URL a shonrú chuig aip "
"saincheaptha nó teimpléad tionscadail."

msgid ""
"For example, Django will use the ``/path/to/my_project_template`` directory "
"when you run the following command:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, úsáidfidh Django an eolaire ``/path/to/my_project_template`` "
"nuair a ritheann tú an t-ordú seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"You can also now provide a destination directory as the second argument to "
"both :djadmin:`startapp` and :djadmin:`startproject`:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat eolaire ceann scríbe a sholáthar anois mar an dara argóint "
"chuig an dá cheann:djadmin: `startapp` agus:djadmin: `startproject`:"

msgid ""
"For more information, see the :djadmin:`startapp` "
"and :djadmin:`startproject` documentation."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise, féach an doiciméad:djadmin: `startapp` "
"agus:djadmin: `startproject`."

msgid "Improved WSGI support"
msgstr "Tacaíocht WSGI feabhsaithe"

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`startproject` management command now adds a :file:`wsgi.py` "
"module to the initial project layout, containing a simple WSGI application "
"that can be used for :doc:`deploying with WSGI app servers</howto/deployment/"
"wsgi/index>`."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann an t-ordú bainistíochta: DJADmin: `startproject` modúl a:file: "
"`wsgi.py` anois le leagan amach tosaigh an tionscadail, ina bhfuil "
"feidhmchlár simplí WSGI is féidir a úsáid le haghaidh: doc: `imscaradh le "
"freastalaithe aipeanna</howto/deployment/wsgi/index> WSGI'."

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`built-in development server<runserver>` now supports using an "
"externally-defined WSGI callable, which makes it possible to run "
"``runserver`` with the same WSGI configuration that is used for deployment. "
"The new :setting:`WSGI_APPLICATION` setting lets you configure which WSGI "
"callable :djadmin:`runserver` uses."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn <runserver>an: DJAdmin: “freastalaí forbartha ionsuite” anois le "
"glaoch WSGI atá sainmhínithe go seachtrach a úsáid, rud a fhágann gur féidir "
"``runserver` a reáchtáil leis an gcumraíocht WSGI céanna a úsáidtear le "
"haghaidh imscaradh. Ligeann an socrú nua:setting: `WSGI_APPLICATION` duit a "
"chumrú a úsáideann WSGI callable:djadmin: `runserver`."

msgid ""
"(The ``runfcgi`` management command also internally wraps the WSGI callable "
"configured via :setting:`WSGI_APPLICATION`.)"
msgstr ""
"(Cumhdaíonn an t-ordú bainistíochta ``runfcgi` go hinmheánach an WSGI "
"cumraithe inghlaonta trí:setting: `WSGI_APPLICATION`.)"

msgid "``SELECT FOR UPDATE`` support"
msgstr "Tacaíocht ``ROGHNAIGH LE HAGHAIDH NUASHONRÚ ``"

msgid ""
"Django 1.4 includes a :meth:`QuerySet.select_for_update() "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.select_for_update>` method, which generates "
"a ``SELECT ... FOR UPDATE`` SQL query. This will lock rows until the end of "
"the transaction, meaning other transactions cannot modify or delete rows "
"matched by a ``FOR UPDATE`` query."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.select_for_update>Cuimsíonn Django 1.4 modh "
"a:meth: `QuerySet.Select_for_Update () `, a ghineann ``SELECT... LE HAGHAIDH "
"NUASHONRÚ ``fiosrúchán SQL. Glasálfaidh sé seo sraitheanna go dtí deireadh "
"an idirbheart, rud a chiallaíonn nach féidir le hidirbhearta eile "
"sraitheanna a mheaitseáil le ceist `FOR UPDATE`` a mhodhnú nó a scriosadh."

msgid ""
"For more details, see the documentation "
"for :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.select_for_update`."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí, féach an doiciméadú le haghaidh: meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.select_for_update`."

msgid "``Model.objects.bulk_create`` in the ORM"
msgstr "``Model.objects.bulk_create`` sa ORM"

msgid ""
"This method lets you create multiple objects more efficiently. It can result "
"in significant performance increases if you have many objects."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an modh seo duit rudaí iomadúla a chruthú níos éifeachtaí "
"D'fhéadfadh méaduithe suntasacha feidhmíochta a bheith mar thoradh air má tá "
"go leor rudaí agat."

msgid ""
"Django makes use of this internally, meaning some operations (such as "
"database setup for test suites) have seen a performance benefit as a result."
msgstr ""
"Baineann Django úsáid as seo go hinmheánach, rud a chiallaíonn go bhfaca "
"sochar feidhmíochta roinnt oibríochtaí (mar shampla socrú bunachar sonraí do "
"shraith tástála) mar thoradh air sin."

msgid ""
"See the :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.bulk_create` docs for more "
"information."
msgstr ""
"Féach na docs: meth: `~django.db.models.query.queryset.bulk_create` le "
"haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise."

msgid "``QuerySet.prefetch_related``"
msgstr "``QuerySet.Prefetch_Related``"

msgid ""
"Similar to :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.select_related` but with "
"a different strategy and broader "
"scope, :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.prefetch_related` has been "
"added to :class:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet`. This method returns a "
"new ``QuerySet`` that will prefetch each of the specified related lookups in "
"a single batch as soon as the query begins to be evaluated. Unlike "
"``select_related``, it does the joins in Python, not in the database, and "
"supports many-to-many relationships, ``GenericForeignKey`` and more. This "
"allows you to fix a very common performance problem in which your code ends "
"up doing O(n) database queries (or worse) if objects on your primary "
"``QuerySet`` each have many related objects that you also need to fetch."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le:meth: `~django.db.models.query.queryset.select_related` ach le "
"straitéis dhifriúil agus raon feidhme níos leithne, cuireadh :meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.prefetch_related` chuirte:class: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset`. Tugann an modh seo ``QuerySet`` nua ar "
"ais a fhaighfidh gach ceann de na cuardaigh ghaolmhara sonraithe i mbaisc "
"amháin a luaithe a thosaíonn an cheist á mheas. Murab ionann agus "
"``select_related``, déanann sé na páirtí i Python, ní sa bhunachar sonraí, "
"agus tacaíonn sé le caidrimh go leor, `GenericForeignKey`` agus go leor "
"eile. Ligeann sé seo duit fadhb feidhmíochta an-choitianta a shocrú ina "
"gcríochnaíonn do chód ag déanamh ceisteanna bunachar sonraí O (n) (nó níos "
"measa) má tá go leor rudaí gaolmhara ag rudaí ar do phríomh-`QuerySet` gach "
"ceann acu a chaithfidh tú a fháil freisin."

msgid "Improved password hashing"
msgstr "Hashing pasfhocal feabhsaithe"

msgid ""
"Django's auth system (``django.contrib.auth``) stores passwords using a one-"
"way algorithm. Django 1.3 uses the SHA1_ algorithm, but increasing processor "
"speeds and theoretical attacks have revealed that SHA1 isn't as secure as "
"we'd like. Thus, Django 1.4 introduces a new password storage system: by "
"default Django now uses the PBKDF2_ algorithm (as recommended by NIST_). You "
"can also easily choose a different algorithm (including the popular bcrypt_ "
"algorithm). For more details, see :ref:`auth_password_storage`."
msgstr ""
"Stórálann córas auth Django (``django.contrib.auth``) pasfhocail ag baint "
"úsáide as algartam aon-bhealaigh. Úsáideann Django 1.3 an algartam SHA1_, "
"ach léirigh luasanna próiseálaí agus ionsaithe teoiriciúla ag méadú nach "
"bhfuil SHA1 chomh slán agus is mian linn. Dá bhrí sin, tugann Django 1.4 "
"córas nua stórála pasfhocal isteach: de réir réamhshocraithe úsáideann "
"Django anois algartam PBKDF2_ (mar a mhol NIST_). Is féidir leat algartam "
"difriúil a roghnú go héasca freisin (lena n-áirítear an algartam bcrypt_ "
"coitianta). Le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí, féach:ref: `auth_password_storage`."

msgid "HTML5 doctype"
msgstr "HTML5 doctype"

msgid ""
"We've switched the admin and other bundled templates to use the HTML5 "
"doctype. While Django will be careful to maintain compatibility with older "
"browsers, this change means that you can use any HTML5 features you need in "
"admin pages without having to lose HTML validity or override the provided "
"templates to change the doctype."
msgstr ""
"Tá an riarachán agus teimpléid cuachta eile tar éis aistriú againn chun an "
"doctype HTML5 a úsáid. Cé go mbeidh Django cúramach comhoiriúnacht le "
"brabhsálaithe níos sine a choinneáil, ciallaíonn an t-athrú seo gur féidir "
"leat aon ghnéithe HTML5 a theastaíonn uait a úsáid i leathanaigh riaracháin "
"gan bailíocht HTML a chailleadh nó na teimpléid a chuirtear ar fáil chun an "
"doctype a athrú."

msgid "List filters in admin interface"
msgstr "Liostaigh scagairí i gcomhéadan admin"

msgid ""
"Prior to Django 1.4, the :mod:`~django.contrib.admin` app let you specify "
"change list filters by specifying a field lookup, but it didn't allow you to "
"create custom filters. This has been rectified with a simple API (previously "
"used internally and known as \"FilterSpec\"). For more details, see the "
"documentation for :attr:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.list_filter`."
msgstr ""
"Roimh Django 1.4, lig an aip: mod: `~django.contrib.admin duit scagairí "
"liosta athraithe a shonrú trí chuardach réimse a shonrú, ach níor chead sé "
"duit scagairí saincheaptha a chruthú. Ceartaíodh é seo le API simplí (a "
"úsáidtear go hinmheánach roimhe seo agus ar a dtugtar “FilterSpec”). Le "
"haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí, féach an doiciméadú le haghaidh: attr: "
"`~django.contrib.admin.modeladmin.list_filter`."

msgid "Multiple sort in admin interface"
msgstr "Sórtáil iolrach i gcomhéadan admin"

msgid ""
"The admin change list now supports sorting on multiple columns. It respects "
"all elements of the :attr:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.ordering` "
"attribute, and sorting on multiple columns by clicking on headers is "
"designed to mimic the behavior of desktop GUIs. We also added "
"a :meth:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.get_ordering` method for "
"specifying the ordering dynamically (i.e., depending on the request)."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn an liosta athraithe riaracháin anois le sórtáil ar iliomad colún Tá "
"meas aige ar gach gné den tréith: attr: "
"`~django.contrib.admin.modelAdmin.Ordering`, agus tá sórtáil ar iliomad "
"colúin trí chliceáil ar cheanntásca deartha chun aithris a dhéanamh ar "
"iompar GUIanna deisce. Chuireamar modh a:meth: "
"`~django.contrib.admin.modeladmin.get_ordering` freisin chun an t-ordú a "
"shonrú go dinimiciúil (ie, ag brath ar an iarratas)."

msgid "New ``ModelAdmin`` methods"
msgstr "Modhanna nua ``ModelAdmin``"

msgid ""
"We added a :meth:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.save_related` method "
"to :mod:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin` to ease customization of how "
"related objects are saved in the admin."
msgstr ""
"Chuireamar modh a:meth: `~django.contrib.admin.modeladmin.save_related` "
"leis: mod: `~django.contrib.admin.modelAdmin` chun saincheapadh a éascú ar "
"an gcaoi a shábháiltear rudaí gaolmhara sa riarachán."

msgid ""
"Two other new :class:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin` "
"methods, :meth:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.get_list_display` "
"and :meth:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.get_list_display_links` enable "
"dynamic customization of fields and links displayed on the admin change list."
msgstr ""
"Cumasaíonn dhá mhodh nua eile: `~django.contrib.admin.modelAdmin`, :meth: "
"`~django.contrib.admin.modeladmin.get_list_display` agus:meth: "
"`~django.contrib.admin.modeladmin.get_list_display_links` saincheapadh "
"dinimiciúil réimsí agus naisc a thaispeántar ar an liosta athraithe admin."

msgid "Admin inlines respect user permissions"
msgstr "Meas ar línte riaracháin ceadanna úsáideora"

msgid ""
"Admin inlines now only allow those actions for which the user has "
"permission. For ``ManyToMany`` relationships with an auto-created "
"intermediate model (which does not have its own permissions), the change "
"permission for the related model determines if the user has the permission "
"to add, change or delete relationships."
msgstr ""
"Ní cheadaíonn inlínte riaracháin anois ach na gníomhartha sin a bhfuil cead "
"ag an úsáideoir dóibh. Maidir le caidrimh ``ManyTomany` le samhail "
"idirmheánach a chruthaítear go huathoibríoch (nach bhfuil a cheadanna féin "
"aige), cinneann an cead athraithe don tsamhail ghaolmhar an bhfuil cead ag "
"an úsáideoir caidrimh a chur leis, a athrú nó a scriosadh."

msgid "Tools for cryptographic signing"
msgstr "Uirlisí le haghaidh síniú cripteagrafach"

msgid ""
"Django 1.4 adds both a low-level API for signing values and a high-level API "
"for setting and reading signed cookies, one of the most common uses of "
"signing in web applications."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann Django 1.4 API leibhéal íseal le haghaidh luachanna a shíniú agus "
"API ardleibhéil chun fianáin sínithe a shocrú agus a léamh, ceann de na "
"húsáidí is coitianta a bhaineann le síniú feidhmchláir ghréasáin."

msgid ""
"See the :doc:`cryptographic signing </topics/signing>` docs for more "
"information."
msgstr ""
"Féach na doiciméid :doc:`síniú cripteagrafach </topics/signing>` le haghaidh "
"tuilleadh eolais."

msgid "Cookie-based session backend"
msgstr "Cúlcheann seisiúin bunaithe ar fhianán"

msgid ""
"Django 1.4 introduces a cookie-based session backend that uses the tools "
"for :doc:`cryptographic signing </topics/signing>` to store the session data "
"in the client's browser."
msgstr ""
"Tugann Django 1.4 inneall seisiún fianán-bhunaithe isteach a úsáideann na "
"huirlisí le haghaidh :doc: `síniú cripteagrafach </topics/signing>` chun "
"sonraí an tseisiúin a stóráil i mbrabhsálaí an chliaint."

msgid ""
"Session data is signed and validated by the server, but it's not encrypted. "
"This means a user can view any data stored in the session but cannot change "
"it. Please read the documentation for further clarification before using "
"this backend."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an freastalaí sonraí an tseisiúin a shíniú agus a bhailíochtú, ach "
"níl siad criptithe. Ciallaíonn sé seo gur féidir le húsáideoir féachaint ar "
"aon sonraí atá stóráilte sa seisiún ach nach féidir leo é a athrú. Léigh na "
"doiciméid le haghaidh soiléirithe breise le do thoil roimh úsáid a bhaint as "
"an inneall seo."

msgid ""
"See the :ref:`cookie-based session backend <cookie-session-backend>` docs "
"for more information."
msgstr ""
"<cookie-session-backend>Féach na doiciméad:ref: `cúltaca seisiúin bunaithe "
"ar fianáin `le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise."

msgid "New form wizard"
msgstr "Draoi foirm nua"

msgid ""
"The previous ``FormWizard`` from ``django.contrib.formtools`` has been "
"replaced with a new implementation based on the class-based views introduced "
"in Django 1.3. It features a pluggable storage API and doesn't require the "
"wizard to pass around hidden fields for every previous step."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh cur i bhfeidhm nua in ionad an `FormWizard` roimhe seo ó "
"`django.contrib.formtools`` bunaithe ar na tuairimí ranga-bhunaithe a tugadh "
"isteach i Django 1.3. Tá API stórála in-phlugáilte aige agus ní éilíonn sé "
"ar an draoi dul timpeall réimsí i bhfolach do gach céim roimhe seo."

msgid ""
"Django 1.4 ships with a session-based storage backend and a cookie-based "
"storage backend. The latter uses the tools for :doc:`cryptographic signing </"
"topics/signing>` also introduced in Django 1.4 to store the wizard's state "
"in the user's cookies."
msgstr ""
"Seolann Django 1.4 le cúltaca stórála bunaithe ar sheisiún agus cúltaca "
"stórála bunaithe ar fhianán. Úsáideann an dara ceann na huirlisí le "
"haghaidh: doc: `síniú cripteagrafach' a tugadh isteach i Django 1.4 freisin "
"chun staid an draoi a stóráil i bhfi</topics/signing> anáin an úsáideora."

msgid "``reverse_lazy``"
msgstr "```reverse_lazy``"

msgid ""
"A lazily evaluated version of ``reverse()`` was added to allow using URL "
"reversals before the project's URLconf gets loaded."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh leagan meastóireachta go leisciúil de ``reverse () ``chun ligean "
"aisiompú URL a úsáid sula luchtaítear URLConf an tionscadail."

msgid "Translating URL patterns"
msgstr "Patrúin URL a aistriú"

msgid ""
"Django can now look for a language prefix in the URLpattern when using the "
"new :func:`~django.conf.urls.i18n.i18n_patterns` helper function. It's also "
"now possible to define translatable URL patterns using "
"``django.utils.translation.ugettext_lazy()``. See :ref:`url-"
"internationalization` for more information about the language prefix and how "
"to internationalize URL patterns."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le Django réimír teanga a lorg anois sa URLPattern agus an fheidhm "
"chúntóra nua:func: `~django.conf.urls.i18n.i18n_patterns` á úsáid agat. Is "
"féidir anois patrúin URL inaistrithe a shainiú ag baint úsáide as "
"``django.utils.translation.ugettext_lazy () ``. Féach:ref: `url-"
"idirnáisiúnach` le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise faoin réimír teanga agus "
"conas patrúin URL a idirnáisiúnú."

msgid ""
"Contextual translation support for ``{% trans %}`` and ``{% blocktrans %}``"
msgstr ""
"Tacaíocht aistriúcháin chomhthéacsúil do ``{% trans%}`` agus ``{% "
"blocktrans%}``"

msgid ""
"The :ref:`contextual translation<contextual-markers>` support introduced in "
"Django 1.3 via the ``pgettext`` function has been extended to "
"the :ttag:`trans` and :ttag:`blocktrans` template tags using the new "
"``context`` keyword."
msgstr ""
"Leathnaíodh an taca <contextual-markers>íocht: Ref: `aistriúchán "
"comhthéacsúil `a tugadh isteach i Django 1.3 tríd an bhfeidhm ``pgettext`` "
"chuig clibeanna teimpléad:ttag: `trans` agus:ttag: `blocktrans` ag baint "
"úsáide as an eochairfhocal nua ``context``."

msgid "Customizable ``SingleObjectMixin`` URLConf kwargs"
msgstr "UrlConf kwargs inúsáidte ``SingleObjectMixin``"

msgid ""
"Two new "
"attributes, :attr:`pk_url_kwarg<django.views.generic.detail.SingleObjectMixin.pk_url_kwarg>` "
"and :attr:`slug_url_kwarg<django.views.generic.detail.SingleObjectMixin.slug_url_kwarg>`, "
"have been added to :class:`~django.views.generic.detail.SingleObjectMixin` "
"to enable the customization of URLconf keyword arguments used for single "
"object generic views."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh dhá thréith nua, :attr: `pk_url_kwarg `agus:attr:` "
"<django.views.generic.detail.SingleObjectMixin.pk_url_kwarg>slug_url_kwarg "
"`, la:class: `~django.views.generic.detail.singleObjectMixin` chun "
"saincheapadh argóintí eochairfhocal URLConf a úsáidtear le haghaidh tuairimí "
"cineálacha réad aonair a chumas "
"<django.views.generic.detail.SingleObjectMixin.slug_url_kwarg>ú."

msgid "Assignment template tags"
msgstr "Clibeanna teimpléad sannadh"

msgid ""
"A new ``assignment_tag`` helper function was added to ``template.Library`` "
"to ease the creation of template tags that store data in a specified context "
"variable."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh feidhm chúntóra nua ``assignment_tag`` le `Template.Library`` chun "
"clibeanna teimpléad a stóráil sonraí in athróg comhthéacs sonraithe a éascú."

msgid "``*args`` and ``**kwargs`` support for template tag helper functions"
msgstr ""
"Tacaíocht ``*args`` agus ``**kwargs ``d'fheidhmeanna cúntóra clibeanna "
"teimpléad"

msgid ""
"The :ref:`simple_tag<howto-custom-template-tags-simple-"
"tags>`, :ref:`inclusion_tag <howto-custom-template-tags-inclusion-tags>` and "
"newly introduced ``assignment_tag`` template helper functions may now accept "
"any number of positional or keyword arguments. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh na feidhmeanna cúntóra teimpléad:ref: `simple_tag <howto-custom-"
"template-tags-simple-tags>`, :ref: `inclusion_tag` agus feidhmeanna cúntóra "
"teimpléad ``<howto-custom-template-tags-inclusion-tags>assignment_tag`` nua-"
"tugadh isteach glacadh anois le haon líon argóintí seasaimh nó "
"eochairfhocal. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"Then, in the template, any number of arguments may be passed to the template "
"tag. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Ansin, sa teimpléad, féadfar aon líon argóintí a chur chuig an gclib "
"teimpléid. Mar shampla:"

msgid "No wrapping of exceptions in ``TEMPLATE_DEBUG`` mode"
msgstr "Gan aon eisceachtaí a fhilleadh i mód ``TEMPLATE_DEBUG`"

msgid ""
"In previous versions of Django, whenever the ``TEMPLATE_DEBUG`` setting was "
"``True``, any exception raised during template rendering (even exceptions "
"unrelated to template syntax) were wrapped in ``TemplateSyntaxError`` and re-"
"raised. This was done in order to provide detailed template source location "
"information in the debug 500 page."
msgstr ""
"I leaganacha roimhe seo de Django, aon uair a bhí an socrú ``TEMPLATE_DEBUG` "
"``True``, filleadh in `TemplateSyntaxError`` aon eisceacht a ardaíodh le "
"linn rindreáil teimpléad (fiú eisceachtaí nach mbaineann le comhréiteach "
"teimpléad) agus ath-ardaíodh. Rinneadh é seo d'fhonn faisnéis mhionsonraithe "
"suíomh foinse teimpléad a sholáthar ar an leathanach dífhabhtú 500."

msgid ""
"In Django 1.4, exceptions are no longer wrapped. Instead, the original "
"exception is annotated with the source information. This means that catching "
"exceptions from template rendering is now consistent regardless of the value "
"of ``TEMPLATE_DEBUG``, and there's no need to catch and unwrap "
"``TemplateSyntaxError`` in order to catch other errors."
msgstr ""
"I Django 1.4, níl eisceachtaí fillte a thuilleadh. Ina áit sin, tá an "
"eisceacht bhunaidh anótáilte leis an bhfaisnéis fhoinse. Ciallaíonn sé seo "
"go bhfuil eisceachtaí a ghabháil ó rindreáil teimpléid comhsheasmhach anois "
"beag beann ar luach ``TEMPLATE_DEBUG`, agus ní gá ``TemplateSyntaxError`` a "
"ghabháil agus a dhífhilleadh d'fhonn earráidí eile a ghabháil."

msgid "``truncatechars`` template filter"
msgstr "scagaire teimpléad ``truncatechars``"

msgid ""
"This new filter truncates a string to be no longer than the specified number "
"of characters. Truncated strings end with a translatable ellipsis sequence "
"(\"...\"). See the documentation for :tfilter:`truncatechars` for more "
"details."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an scagaire nua seo sreang a ghearradh nach mbeidh níos faide ná an "
"líon sonraithe carachtair. Críochnaíonn teaghráin ghearrtha le seicheamh "
"ellipsis inaistrithe (“...”). Féach an doiciméadú le haghaidh: tfilter: "
"`truncatechars` le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid "``static`` template tag"
msgstr "Clib teimpléad ``static`"

msgid ""
"The :mod:`staticfiles<django.contrib.staticfiles>` contrib app has a new "
"``static`` template tag to refer to files saved with the "
"``STATICFILES_STORAGE`` storage backend. It uses the storage backend's "
"``url`` method and therefore supports advanced features such "
"as :ref:`serving files from a cloud service<staticfiles-from-cdn>`."
msgstr ""
"<django.contrib.staticfiles>Tá clib teimpléad nua ``static`` ag an aip "
"contrib `staticfiles `chun tagairt a dhéanamh do chomhaid a shábháiltear "
"leis an gcúltaca stórála ``STATICFILES_STORAGE``. <staticfiles-from-"
"cdn>Úsáideann sé modh ``url ``an chúltaca stórála agus dá bhrí sin tacaíonn "
"sé le gnéithe chun cinn mar: ref: `comhaid a sheirbheáil ó sheirbhís scamall "
"`."

msgid "``CachedStaticFilesStorage`` storage backend"
msgstr "Cúlcheann stórála ``CachedStaticFilesStorage``"

msgid ""
"The :mod:`staticfiles<django.contrib.staticfiles>` contrib app now has a "
"``django.contrib.staticfiles.storage.CachedStaticFilesStorage`` backend that "
"caches the files it saves (when running the :djadmin:`collectstatic` "
"management command) by appending the MD5 hash of the file's content to the "
"filename. For example, the file ``css/styles.css`` would also be saved as "
"``css/styles.55e7cbb9ba48.css``"
msgstr ""
"<django.contrib.staticfiles>Tá cúltaca "
"``django.contrib.staticfiles.storage.cachedStaticFilesStorage`` ag an aip "
"contrib `staticfiles `anois a choscann na comhaid a shábhálann sé (agus an t-"
"ordú bainistíochta: djadmin: `collectstatic` á rith) trí hash MD5 d'ábhar an "
"chomhaid a chur leis an ainm comhaid. Mar shampla, sábhálfaí an comhad ``css/"
"styles.css`` mar `css/styles.55e7cbb9ba48.css``"

msgid "Simple clickjacking protection"
msgstr "Cosaint clickjacking simplí"

msgid ""
"We've added a middleware to provide easy protection against `clickjacking "
"<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clickjacking>`_ using the ``X-Frame-Options`` "
"header. It's not enabled by default for backwards compatibility reasons, but "
"you'll almost certainly want to :doc:`enable it </ref/clickjacking/>` to "
"help plug that security hole for browsers that support the header."
msgstr ""
"Chuireamar lárearraí leis chun cosaint éasca a sholáthar in aghaidh "
"`clickjacking <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clickjacking>`_ ag baint úsáide "
"as an gceanntásc ``X-Frame-Options``. Níl sé cumasaithe de réir "
"réamhshocraithe ar chúiseanna comhoiriúnachta ar gcúl, ach is cinnte go "
"mbeidh tú ag iarraidh :doc: `a chumasú </ref/clickjacking/>` chun cabhrú "
"leis an bpoll slándála sin a phlugáil le haghaidh brabhsálaithe a thacaíonn "
"leis an gceanntásc."

msgid "CSRF improvements"
msgstr "Feabhsuithe CSRF"

msgid ""
"We've made various improvements to our CSRF features, including "
"the :func:`~django.views.decorators.csrf.ensure_csrf_cookie` decorator, "
"which can help with AJAX-heavy sites; protection for PUT and DELETE "
"requests; and the :setting:`CSRF_COOKIE_SECURE` "
"and :setting:`CSRF_COOKIE_PATH` settings, which can improve the security and "
"usefulness of CSRF protection. See the :doc:`CSRF docs </ref/csrf>` for more "
"information."
msgstr ""
"Tá feabhsuithe éagsúla déanta againn ar ár ngnéithe CSRF, lena n-áirítear "
"maisitheoir: func: `~django.views.decorators.csrf.ensure_csrf_cookie, ar "
"féidir leo cabhrú le suíomhanna Ajax-heavy; cosaint d'iarratais PUT agus "
"DELETE; agus an:setting: `CSRF_COOKIE_PATH`, socruithe is féidir le slándáil "
"agus úsáideacht cosanta CSRF a fheabhsú. Féach na:doc: `CSRF docs` le "
"haghaidh tuilleadh eolais </ref/csrf>."

msgid "Error report filtering"
msgstr "Scagadh tuairisc earráide"

msgid ""
"We added two function "
"decorators, :func:`~django.views.decorators.debug.sensitive_variables` "
"and :func:`~django.views.decorators.debug.sensitive_post_parameters`, to "
"allow designating the local variables and POST parameters that may contain "
"sensitive information and should be filtered out of error reports."
msgstr ""
"Chuireamar dhá mhaisitheoir feidhm leis, :func: "
"`~django.views.decorators.debug.sensitive_variables` agus:func: "
"`~django.views.decorators.debug.sensitive_post_parameters`, chun na hathróga "
"áitiúla agus paraiméadair POST a dheimhniú a d'fhéadfadh faisnéis íogair a "
"bheith ann agus ba chóir iad a scagadh as tuarascálacha earráide."

msgid ""
"All POST parameters are now systematically filtered out of error reports for "
"certain views (``login``, ``password_reset_confirm``, ``password_change`` "
"and ``add_view`` in :mod:`django.contrib.auth.views`, as well as "
"``user_change_password`` in the admin app) to prevent the leaking of "
"sensitive information such as user passwords."
msgstr ""
"Déantar gach paraiméadar POST a scagadh go córasach anois as tuarascálacha "
"earráide le haghaidh tuairimí áirithe (``login``, `password_reset_confirm``, "
"`password_change`` agus ``add_view`` in:mod: `django.contrib.auth.views`, "
"chomh maith le ``user_change_password`` san aip admin) chun faisnéis íogair "
"a chosc mar shampla pasfhocail úsáideora."

msgid ""
"You can override or customize the default filtering by writing "
"a :ref:`custom filter<custom-error-reports>`. For more information see the "
"docs on :ref:`Filtering error reports<filtering-error-reports>`."
msgstr ""
"<custom-error-reports>Is féidir leat an scagadh réamhshocraithe a shárú nó a "
"shaincheapadh trí scríobh a:ref: `scagaire saincheapaithe`. <filtering-error-"
"reports>Le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise féach na doiciméid ar:ref: "
"`Tuarascálacha earráide scagtha `."

msgid "Extended IPv6 support"
msgstr "Tacaíocht leathnaithe IPv6"

msgid ""
"Django 1.4 can now better handle IPv6 addresses with the "
"new :class:`~django.db.models.GenericIPAddressField` model "
"field, :class:`~django.forms.GenericIPAddressField` form field and the "
"validators :data:`~django.core.validators.validate_ipv46_address` "
"and :data:`~django.core.validators.validate_ipv6_address`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le Django 1.4 seoltaí IPv6 a láimhseáil níos fearr anois leis an "
"réimse múnla nua:class: `~django.db.models.genericipAddressField`, :class: "
"`~django.forms.genericipAddressField` agus na bailíoróir:data: "
"`~django.core.validators.validate_ipv46_address` agus:data: "
"`~django.core.validators.validate_ipv46_address` agus:data: "
"`~django.core.validators.validate_ipv46_address` agus:data: "
"`~django.djan.go.core.validators.validate_ipv6_seolads`."

msgid "HTML comparisons in tests"
msgstr "Comparáidí HTML i dtástálacha"

msgid ""
"The base classes in :mod:`django.test` now have some helpers to compare HTML "
"without tripping over irrelevant differences in whitespace, argument quoting/"
"ordering and closing of self-closing tags. You can either compare HTML "
"directly with the new :meth:`~django.test.SimpleTestCase.assertHTMLEqual` "
"and :meth:`~django.test.SimpleTestCase.assertHTMLNotEqual` assertions, or "
"use the ``html=True`` flag "
"with :meth:`~django.test.SimpleTestCase.assertContains` "
"and :meth:`~django.test.SimpleTestCase.assertNotContains` to test whether "
"the client's response contains a given HTML fragment. See "
"the :ref:`assertions documentation <assertions>` for more."
msgstr ""
"Tá roinnt cúntóirí anois ag na bunaicmí in:mod: `django.test` chun HTML a "
"chur i gcomparáid gan difríochtaí neamhábhartha i spás bán, luach/ordú "
"argóintí agus dúnadh clibeanna féin-dhúnadh. Is féidir leat HTML a chur i "
"gcomparáid go díreach leis na dearbhóidí nua:meth: "
"`~django.test.simpletestCase.asserthtmlequal` agus:meth: "
"`~django.test.simpletestcase.asserthtmlNoteQual`, nó an bhratach "
"`html=True`` a úsáid le:meth: "
"`~django.test.simpletestCase.AssertAssertAssertAssertAssertAssertAssertAssertX "
"`agus:meth: `~django.test.simpletestCase.assertNotContains` chun tástáil a "
"dhéanamh an bhfuil blúir HTML ar leith i bhfreagra an chliaint. "
"<assertions>Féach doiciméadach:ref: `dearbhóireachtaí `le haghaidh tuilleadh "
"eolais."

msgid "Two new date format strings"
msgstr "Dhá teaghráin formáid dáta nua"

msgid ""
"Two new :tfilter:`date` formats were added for use in template filters, "
"template tags and :doc:`/topics/i18n/formatting`:"
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh dhá fhormáid nua: tfilter: `dáta` le húsáid i scagairí teimpléad, "
"clibeanna teimpléad agus:doc: `/topics/i18n/formatting`:"

msgid "``e`` -- the name of the timezone of the given datetime object"
msgstr "``e`` - ainm an chrios ama den réad dáta-ama tugtha"

msgid "``o`` -- the ISO 8601 year number"
msgstr "```-- uimhir na bliana ISO 8601"

msgid ""
"Please make sure to update your :ref:`custom format files <custom-format-"
"files>` if they contain either ``e`` or ``o`` in a format string. For "
"example a Spanish localization format previously only escaped the ``d`` "
"format character::"
msgstr ""
"Déan cinnte do thoil do chuid comhad formáid saincheaptha a nuashonrú má "
"<custom-format-files>tá `e`` nó ```i sreang formáide iontu. Mar shampla ní "
"éalaigh formáid logánaithe na Spáinne roimhe seo ach an carachtar formáide "
"`d``:"

msgid "But now it needs to also escape ``e`` and ``o``::"
msgstr "Ach anois caithfidh sé éalú freisin ``e`` agus ````:"

msgid "For more information, see the :tfilter:`date` documentation."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise, féach an doiciméadach:tfilter: `date`."

msgid "Django 1.4 also includes several smaller improvements worth noting:"
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn Django 1.4 roinnt feabhsuithe níos lú ar fiú a thabhairt faoi "
"deara:"

msgid ""
"A more usable stacktrace in the technical 500 page. Frames in the stack "
"trace that reference Django's framework code are dimmed out, while frames in "
"application code are slightly emphasized. This change makes it easier to "
"scan a stacktrace for issues in application code."
msgstr ""
"Stacktrace níos inúsáidte ar an leathanach teicniúil 500. Déantar frámaí sa "
"rian cruach a thagann tagairt do chód creat Django a laghdú amach, agus "
"cuirtear béim beagán ar fhrámaí sa chód feidhmchláir. Fágann an t-athrú seo "
"go bhfuil sé níos éasca stacktrace a scanadh le haghaidh saincheisteanna i "
"gcód feidhmchláir."

msgid ":doc:`Tablespace support </topics/db/tablespaces>` in PostgreSQL."
msgstr ":doc:`Tacaíocht tablespace </topics/db/tablespaces>` in PostgreSQL."

msgid "Customizable names for :meth:`~django.template.Library.simple_tag`."
msgstr ""
"Ainmneacha inoiriúnaithe le haghaidh: meth: "
"`~django.template.library.simple_tag`."

msgid ""
"In the documentation, a helpful :doc:`security overview </topics/security>` "
"page."
msgstr ""
"Sa doiciméadú, leathanach cabhrach: doc: `léirmheas slándála' </topics/"
"security>."

msgid ""
"The ``django.contrib.auth.models.check_password`` function has been moved to "
"the :mod:`django.contrib.auth.hashers` module. Importing it from the old "
"location will still work, but you should update your imports."
msgstr ""
"Tá an fheidhm ``django.contrib.auth.models.check_password`` aistrithe chuig "
"an modúl:mod: `django.contrib.auth.hashers`. Oibreoidh é a iompórtáil ón "
"sean-áit fós, ach ba cheart duit d'allmhairí a nuashonrú."

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`collectstatic` management command now has a ``--clear`` option "
"to delete all files at the destination before copying or linking the static "
"files."
msgstr ""
"Tá rogha ``--clear`` anois ag an ordú bainistíochta: DjaDmin: "
"`collectstatic` chun gach comhad ag an gceann scríbe a scriosadh sula "
"ndéanfar na comhaid statacha a chóipeáil nó a nascadh."

msgid ""
"It's now possible to load fixtures containing forward references when using "
"MySQL with the InnoDB database engine."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir anois daingneáin ina bhfuil tagairtí tosaigh a luchtú agus MySQL á "
"n-úsáid agat le hinneall bunachar sonraí InnoDB."

msgid ""
"A new 403 response handler has been added as "
"``'django.views.defaults.permission_denied'``. You can set your own handler "
"by setting the value of :data:`django.conf.urls.handler403`. See the "
"documentation about :ref:`the 403 (HTTP Forbidden) "
"view<http_forbidden_view>` for more information."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh láimhseálaí nua 403 freagra leis mar "
"``'django.views.defaults.permission_denied'`. Is féidir leat do láimhseálaí "
"féin a shocrú trí luach: data: `django.conf.urls.handler403` a shocrú. Féach "
"an doiciméadú fao:ref: `the 403 (HTTP Forbidden) view "
"<http_forbidden_view>`le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise."

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`makemessages` command uses a new and more accurate "
"lexer, :pypi:`JsLex <jslex>`, for extracting translatable strings from "
"JavaScript files."
msgstr ""
"<jslex>Úsáideann an ordú:djaDmin: `makemessages` foclóir nua agus níos "
"cruinne, :pypi: `JSLEX `, chun teaghráin inaistrithe a bhaint as comhaid "
"JavaScript."

msgid ""
"The :ttag:`trans` template tag now takes an optional ``as`` argument to be "
"able to retrieve a translation string without displaying it but setting a "
"template context variable instead."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an chlib teimpléad:ttag: `trans` argóint roghnach `as ``anois chun a "
"bheith in ann teaghrán aistriúcháin a aisghabháil gan é a thaispeáint ach "
"athróg comhthéacs teimpléad a shocrú ina ionad."

msgid "The :ttag:`if` template tag now supports ``{% elif %}`` clauses."
msgstr "Tacaíonn an clib teimpléad:ttag: `if `anois le clásail ``{% elif%}``."

msgid ""
"If your Django app is behind a proxy, you might find the "
"new :setting:`SECURE_PROXY_SSL_HEADER` setting useful. It solves the problem "
"of your proxy \"eating\" the fact that a request came in via HTTPS. But only "
"use this setting if you know what you're doing."
msgstr ""
"Má tá d'aip Django taobh thiar de sheachfhreastalaí, b'fhéidir go mbeadh an "
"socrú nua:setting: `SECURE_PROXY_SSL_HEADER` úsáideach duit. Réitíonn sé an "
"fhadhb a bhaineann le do sheachfhreastalaí “ag ithe” an bhfíric gur tháinig "
"iarratas isteach trí HTTPS. Ach bain úsáid as an socrú seo ach má tá a fhios "
"agat cad atá á dhéanamh agat."

msgid ""
"A new, plain-text, version of the HTTP 500 status code internal error page "
"served when :setting:`DEBUG` is ``True`` is now sent to the client when "
"Django detects that the request has originated in JavaScript code. "
"(``is_ajax()`` is used for this.)"
msgstr ""
"Seoltar leagan nua, simple-théacs, den leathanach earráide inmheánach cód "
"stádais HTTP 500 nuair a sheirbheáltar nuair:socrú: “Debug” ``True`` chuig "
"an gcliant anois nuair a bhraitheann Django gur tháinig an t-iarratas i gcód "
"JavaScript. (Úsáidtear ``is_ajax () ``chuige seo.)"

msgid ""
"Like its HTML counterpart, it contains a collection of different pieces of "
"information about the state of the application."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil lena mhacasamhail HTML, tá bailiúchán píosaí éagsúla faisnéise ann "
"faoi staid an fheidhmchláir."

msgid ""
"This should make it easier to read when debugging interaction with client-"
"side JavaScript."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh sé seo níos éasca léamh agus idirghníomhaíocht á "
"dhifhabhtú le JavaScript taobh an chliaint."

msgid "Added the :option:`makemessages --no-location` option."
msgstr "Cuireadh an rogha: rogha: `makemessages --no-location` leis."

msgid ""
"Changed the ``locmem`` cache backend to use ``pickle.HIGHEST_PROTOCOL`` for "
"better compatibility with the other cache backends."
msgstr ""
"Athraigh cúltaca taisce ``locmem`` chun ``pickle.highest_protocol`` a úsáid "
"chun comhoiriúnacht níos fearr leis na cúltaca taisce eile."

msgid ""
"Added support in the ORM for generating ``SELECT`` queries containing "
"``DISTINCT ON``."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíocht bhreise san ORM chun ceisteanna ``SELECT`` a ghiniúint ina bhfuil "
"``DISTINCT ON``."

msgid ""
"The ``distinct()`` ``QuerySet`` method now accepts an optional list of model "
"field names. If specified, then the ``DISTINCT`` statement is limited to "
"these fields. This is only supported in PostgreSQL."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an modh ``different () ```QuerySet`` anois le liosta roghnach "
"d'ainmneacha réimse samhail. Má shonraítear é, ansin tá an ráiteas "
"``DISTINCT`` teoranta do na réimsí seo. Ní thacaítear leis seo ach i "
"PostgreSQL."

msgid ""
"For more details, see the documentation "
"for :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.distinct`."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí, féach an doiciméadú le haghaidh: meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.Distinct`."

msgid ""
"The admin login page will add a password reset link if you include a URL "
"with the name ``'admin_password_reset'`` in your ``urls.py``, so plugging in "
"the built-in password reset mechanism and making it available is now much "
"easier. For details, see :ref:`auth_password_reset`."
msgstr ""
"Cuirfidh an leathanach logála isteach riaracháin nasc athshocraithe "
"pasfhocal má chuireann tú URL leis an ainm ``admin_password_reset'` i do "
"`urls.py``, mar sin tá sé i bhfad níos éasca anois an mheicníocht "
"athshocraithe pasfhocal ionsuite a phlugáil isteach agus é a chur ar fáil. "
"Le haghaidh sonraí, féach:ref: `auth_password_reset`."

msgid ""
"The MySQL database backend can now make use of the savepoint feature "
"implemented by MySQL version 5.0.3 or newer with the InnoDB storage engine."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le cúltaca bunachar sonraí MySQL úsáid a bhaint as an ngné "
"savepoint a chuirtear i bhfeidhm ag leagan MySQL 5.0.3 nó níos nuaí leis an "
"inneall stórála InnoDB."

msgid ""
"It's now possible to pass initial values to the model forms that are part of "
"both model formsets and inline model formsets as returned from factory "
"functions ``modelformset_factory`` and ``inlineformset_factory`` "
"respectively just like with regular formsets. However, initial values only "
"apply to extra forms, i.e. those which are not bound to an existing model "
"instance."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir anois luachanna tosaigh a chur chuig na foirmeacha samhail atá mar "
"chuid de fhoirmeacha samhail agus foirmeacha samhail inlíne araon mar a "
"thugtar ar ais ó fheidhmeanna monarchan `modelformset_factory`` agus "
"``inlineformset_factory`` faoi seach díreach mar atá le foirmeacha rialta. "
"Mar sin féin, ní bhaineann luachanna tosaigh ach le foirmeacha breise, i.e. "
"iad siúd nach bhfuil ceangailte le samhail shampla atá ann cheana."

msgid ""
"The sitemaps framework can now handle HTTPS links using the "
"new :attr:`Sitemap.protocol <django.contrib.sitemaps.Sitemap.protocol>` "
"class attribute."
msgstr ""
"<django.contrib.sitemaps.Sitemap.protocol>Is féidir leis an creat "
"léarscáileanna láithreáin naisc HTTPS a láimhseáil anois ag baint úsáide as "
"an tréith aicme nua:attr: `SiteMap.protocol `."

msgid ""
"A new :class:`django.test.SimpleTestCase` subclass "
"of :class:`unittest.TestCase` that's lighter "
"than :class:`django.test.TestCase` and company. It can be useful in tests "
"that don't need to hit a database. See :ref:`testcase_hierarchy_diagram`."
msgstr ""
"Fo-aicme nua:class: `Django.Test.SimpleTestCase` de:class: "
"`UnitTest.TestCase` atá níos éadroime ná: Class: `Django.Test.TestCase` agus "
"cuideachta. Is féidir leis a bheith úsáideach i dtástálacha nach gá bunachar "
"sonraí a bhualadh. Féach:ref: `testcase_hierarchy_diagram `."

msgid "Backwards incompatible changes in 1.4"
msgstr "Athruithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha ar ais i 1.4"

msgid "SECRET_KEY setting is required"
msgstr "Tá socrú SECRET_KEY ag teastáil"

msgid ""
"Running Django with an empty or known :setting:`SECRET_KEY` disables many of "
"Django's security protections and can lead to remote-code-execution "
"vulnerabilities. No Django site should ever be run without "
"a :setting:`SECRET_KEY`."
msgstr ""
"Déanann rith Django le socrú folamh nó eol:setting: `SECRET_KEY` a "
"dhíchumasú go leor de chosaintí slándála Django agus d'fhéadfadh "
"leochaileachtaí iargúlta a fhorghníomhú cód a bheith mar thoradh air. Níor "
"chóir aon suíomh Django a reáchtáil riamh gan a: socrú: `SECRET_KEY`."

msgid ""
"In Django 1.4, starting Django with an empty :setting:`SECRET_KEY` will "
"raise a ``DeprecationWarning``. In Django 1.5, it will raise an exception "
"and Django will refuse to start. This is slightly accelerated from the usual "
"deprecation path due to the severity of the consequences of running Django "
"with no :setting:`SECRET_KEY`."
msgstr ""
"I Django 1.4, ag tosú Django le folamh: setting: `SECRET_KEY` ardóidh "
"``DeprecationWarning``. I Django 1.5, ardóidh sé eisceacht agus diúltóidh "
"Django tosú. Déantar é seo a luasghéarú beagán ón ngnáthchosán mar gheall ar "
"dhéine na n-iarmhairtí a bhaineann le Django a reáchtáil le no:setting: "
"`SECRET_KEY`."

msgid "``django.contrib.admin``"
msgstr "``django.contrib.admin ``"

msgid ""
"The included administration app ``django.contrib.admin`` has for a long time "
"shipped with a default set of static files such as JavaScript, images and "
"stylesheets. Django 1.3 added a new contrib app "
"``django.contrib.staticfiles`` to handle such files in a generic way and "
"defined conventions for static files included in apps."
msgstr ""
"Tá an aip riaracháin san áireamh ``django.contrib.admin ``seolta le fada le "
"tacar réamhshocraithe comhaid statacha mar JavaScript, íomhánna agus bileoga "
"stíle. Chuir Django 1.3 aip contrib nua ``django.contrib.staticfiles`` leis "
"chun comhaid den sórt sin a láimhseáil ar bhealach cineálach agus "
"sainmhínigh coinbhinsiúin do chomhaid statacha atá san áireamh in aipeanna."

msgid ""
"Starting in Django 1.4, the admin's static files also follow this "
"convention, to make the files easier to deploy. In previous versions of "
"Django, it was also common to define an ``ADMIN_MEDIA_PREFIX`` setting to "
"point to the URL where the admin's static files live on a web server. This "
"setting has now been deprecated and replaced by the more general "
"setting :setting:`STATIC_URL`. Django will now expect to find the admin "
"static files under the URL ``<STATIC_URL>/admin/``."
msgstr ""
"Ag tosú i Django 1.4, leanann comhaid statacha an riaracháin an coinbhinsiún "
"seo freisin, chun na comhaid a dhéanamh níos éasca a imscaradh. I leaganacha "
"roimhe seo de Django, bhí sé coitianta freisin socrú ``ADMIN_MEDIA_PREFIX "
"``a shainiú chun díriú ar an URL ina gcónaíonn comhaid statacha an "
"riaracháin ar fhreastalaí gréasáin. Tá an socrú seo caite anois agus tá an "
"socrú níos ginearálta:setting: `STATIC_URL` ina ionad. Beidh Django ag súil "
"anois go bhfaighidh tú na comhaid statacha riaracháin faoin URL "
"``<STATIC_URL>/admin/``."

msgid ""
"If you've previously used a URL path for ``ADMIN_MEDIA_PREFIX`` (e.g. ``/"
"media/``) simply make sure :setting:`STATIC_URL` and :setting:`STATIC_ROOT` "
"are configured and your web server serves those files correctly. The "
"development server continues to serve the admin files just like before. Read "
"the :doc:`static files howto </howto/static-files/index>` for more details."
msgstr ""
"Má d'úsáid tú conair URL do ``ADMIN_MEDIA_PREFIX`` roimhe seo (m.sh. ``/ "
"meáin/``) déan cinnte go bhfuil :an socrú:`STATIC_URL` agus : "
"socrú:`STATIC_ROOT` cumraithe agus go bhfreastalaíonn do fhreastalaí "
"gréasáin ar na comhaid sin i gceart. Leanann an freastalaí forbartha ag "
"freastal ar na comhaid riaracháin díreach mar a bhí roimhe seo. Léigh "
"an :doc:`comhaid statacha howto </howto/static-files/index>` le haghaidh "
"tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid ""
"If your ``ADMIN_MEDIA_PREFIX`` is set to a specific domain (e.g. ``http://"
"media.example.com/admin/``), make sure to also set "
"your :setting:`STATIC_URL` setting to the correct URL -- for example, "
"``http://media.example.com/``."
msgstr ""
"Má tá do `ADMIN_MEDIA_PREFIX`` socraithe ar fearann ar leith (m.sh. ``http://"
"media.example.com/admin/``), déan cinnte do shuíomh: `STATIC_URL` a shocrú "
"go dtí an URL ceart - mar shampla, ``http://media.example.com/``."

msgid ""
"If you're implicitly relying on the path of the admin static files within "
"Django's source code, you'll need to update that path. The files were moved "
"from :file:`django/contrib/admin/media/` to :file:`django/contrib/admin/"
"static/admin/`."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag brath go hiontach ar chonair na gcomhaid statacha riaracháin "
"laistigh de chód foinse Django, beidh ort an cosán sin a nuashonrú. Bogadh "
"na comhaid ó:file: `django/contrib/admin/media/` chuig: file: `django/"
"contrib/admin/static/admin/`."

msgid "Supported browsers for the admin"
msgstr "Brabhsálaithe tacaithe don riarachán"

msgid ""
"Django hasn't had a clear policy on which browsers are supported by the "
"admin app. Our new policy formalizes existing practices: `YUI's A-grade`_ "
"browsers should provide a fully-functional admin experience, with the "
"notable exception of Internet Explorer 6, which is no longer supported."
msgstr ""
"Ní raibh beartas soiléir ag Django maidir leis na brabhsálaithe a thacaíonn "
"an aip riaracháin. Déanann ár mbeartas nua cleachtais atá ann cheana a "
"fhoirmiú: Ba chóir go gcuirfeadh brabhsálaí YUI a Grád A eispéireas "
"riaracháin lánfheidhmiúil a sholáthar, seachas suntasach Internet Explorer "
"6, nach dtacaítear leis a thuilleadh."

msgid ""
"Released over 10 years ago, IE6 imposes many limitations on modern web "
"development. The practical implications of this policy are that contributors "
"are free to improve the admin without consideration for these limitations."
msgstr ""
"Scaoilte breis agus 10 mbliana ó shin, cuireann IE6 go leor teorainneacha ar "
"fhorbairt gréasáin nua-aimsear Is iad impleachtaí praiticiúla an bheartais "
"seo ná go bhfuil saor ó rannpháirtithe an riarachán a fheabhsú gan breithniú "
"ar na teorainneacha seo."

msgid ""
"This new policy **has no impact** on sites you develop using Django. It only "
"applies to the Django admin. Feel free to develop apps compatible with any "
"range of browsers."
msgstr ""
"Níl aon tionchar ag an mbeartas nua seo **ar shuíomhanna a fhorbraíonn tú ag "
"úsáid Django. Ní bhaineann sé ach leis an riarthóir Django. Thig leat "
"aipeanna a fhorbairt atá comhoiriúnach le haon raon brabhsálaithe."

msgid "Removed admin icons"
msgstr "Deilbhíní riaracháin bainte"

msgid ""
"As part of an effort to improve the performance and usability of the admin's "
"change-list sorting interface and :attr:`horizontal "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.filter_horizontal>` and :attr:`vertical "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.filter_vertical>` \"filter\" widgets, some "
"icon files were removed and grouped into two sprite files."
msgstr ""
"Mar chuid d'iarracht feidhmíocht agus inúsáidteacht comhéadan sórtála liosta "
"athraithe an riaracháin a fheabhsú agus:attr: `cothrománach `agus:attr: giu "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.filter_horizontal>irléidí "
"`ingearach<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.filter_vertical>` “scagaire”, "
"baineadh roinnt comhad deilbhín agus grúpaíodh ina dhá chomhad sprite."

msgid ""
"Specifically: ``selector-add.gif``, ``selector-addall.gif``, ``selector-"
"remove.gif``, ``selector-removeall.gif``, ``selector_stacked-add.gif`` and "
"``selector_stacked-remove.gif`` were combined into ``selector-icons.gif``; "
"and ``arrow-up.gif`` and ``arrow-down.gif`` were combined into ``sorting-"
"icons.gif``."
msgstr ""
"Go sonrach: 'selector-add.gif``, `selector-addall.gif``, `selector-"
"remove.gif``, `selector-removeall.gif``, `selector_stacked-add.gif`` agus "
"``selector_stacked-remove.gif``, `selector_stacked-remove.gif`` i `selector-"
"icons.gif``; agus ``Cuireadh `arrow-up.gif`` agus ``arrow-down.gif`` le "
"chéile ina ``sorting-icons.gif``."

msgid ""
"If you used those icons to customize the admin, then you'll need to replace "
"them with your own icons or get the files from a previous release."
msgstr ""
"Má d'úsáid tú na deilbhíní sin chun an riarachán a shaincheapadh, ansin "
"beidh ort do dheilbhíní féin a chur in ionad iad nó na comhaid a fháil ó "
"scaoileadh roimhe seo."

msgid "CSS class names in admin forms"
msgstr "Ainmneacha ranga CSS i bhfoirmeacha riaracháin"

msgid ""
"To avoid conflicts with other common CSS class names (e.g. \"button\"), we "
"added a prefix (\"field-\") to all CSS class names automatically generated "
"from the form field names in the main admin forms, stacked inline forms and "
"tabular inline cells. You'll need to take that prefix into account in your "
"custom style sheets or JavaScript files if you previously used plain field "
"names as selectors for custom styles or JavaScript transformations."
msgstr ""
"Chun coinbhleachtaí le hainmneacha ranga CSS coitianta eile (m.sh. “cnaipe”) "
"a sheachaint, chuireamar réimír (“field-”) le gach ainm ranga CSS a ghintear "
"go huathoibríoch ó ainmneacha réimse na bhfoirme sna príomhfhoirmeacha "
"riaracháin, foirmeacha inlíne cruachta agus cealla inlíne táblaí. Beidh ort "
"an réimír sin a chur san áireamh i do bhileoga stíl saincheaptha nó i "
"gcomhaid JavaScript má d'úsáid tú ainmneacha réimse simplí roimhe seo mar "
"roghnóirí do stíleanna saincheaptha nó claochlú JavaScript."

msgid "Compatibility with old signed data"
msgstr "Comhoiriúnacht le sean-sonraí síni"

msgid ""
"Django 1.3 changed the cryptographic signing mechanisms used in a number of "
"places in Django. While Django 1.3 kept fallbacks that would accept hashes "
"produced by the previous methods, these fallbacks are removed in Django 1.4."
msgstr ""
"D'athraigh Django 1.3 na meicníochtaí sínithe cripteagrafacha a úsáidtear i "
"roinnt áiteanna i Django. Cé gur choinnigh Django 1.3 bacainní a ghlacfadh "
"le hashes a tháirgtear ag na modhanna roimhe seo, baintear na fallbacks seo "
"i Django 1.4."

msgid ""
"So, if you upgrade to Django 1.4 directly from 1.2 or earlier, you may lose/"
"invalidate certain pieces of data that have been cryptographically signed "
"using an old method. To avoid this, use Django 1.3 first for a period of "
"time to allow the signed data to expire naturally. The affected parts are "
"detailed below, with 1) the consequences of ignoring this advice and 2) the "
"amount of time you need to run Django 1.3 for the data to expire or become "
"irrelevant."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin, má dhéanann tú uasghrádú go Django 1.4 go díreach ó 1.2 nó níos "
"luaithe, féadfaidh tú píosaí áirithe sonraí a síníodh go cripteagrafach a "
"chailltear/neamhbhailí ag baint úsáide as sean-mhodh. Chun é seo a "
"sheachaint, bain úsáid as Django 1.3 ar dtús ar feadh tréimhse ama chun "
"ligean do na sonraí sínithe dul in éag go nádúrtha. Tá na codanna atá "
"buailte mionsonraithe thíos, le 1) na hiarmhairtí a bhaineann le neamhaird a "
"dhéanamh ar an gcomhairle seo agus 2) an méid ama a theastaíonn uait chun "
"Django 1.3 a rith chun na sonraí dul in éag nó go mbeidh siad neamhábhartha."

msgid "``contrib.sessions`` data integrity check"
msgstr "Seiceáil sláine sonraí ``contrib.sessions``"

msgid ""
"Consequences: The user will be logged out, and session data will be lost."
msgstr ""
"Iarmhairtí: Déanfar an t-úsáideoir logáil amach, agus caillfear sonraí "
"seisiúin."

msgid "Time period: Defined by :setting:`SESSION_COOKIE_AGE`."
msgstr "Tréimhse ama: Sainmhínithe ag:setting: `SESSION_COOKIE_AGE`."

msgid "``contrib.auth`` password reset hash"
msgstr "Hash athshocraithe pasfhocal ``contrib.auth``"

msgid ""
"Consequences: Password reset links from before the upgrade will not work."
msgstr ""
"Iarmhairtí: Ní oibreoidh naisc athshocraithe pasfhocal ó roimh an uasghrádú."

msgid "Time period: Defined by ``PASSWORD_RESET_TIMEOUT_DAYS``."
msgstr "Tréimhse ama: Sainmhínithe ag ``PASSWORD_RESET_TIMEOUT_DAYS``."

msgid ""
"Form-related hashes: these have a much shorter lifetime and are relevant "
"only for the short window where a user might fill in a form generated by the "
"pre-upgrade Django instance and try to submit it to the upgraded Django "
"instance:"
msgstr ""
"Hais a bhaineann le foirmeacha: tá saolré i bhfad níos giorra acu seo agus "
"níl siad ábhartha ach amháin don fhuinneog ghairid ina bhféadfadh úsáideoir "
"foirm arna giniúint ag an gcás Django réamh-uasghrádaithe a líonadh agus "
"iarracht a dhéanamh í a chur isteach sa chás uasghrádaithe Django:"

msgid "``contrib.comments`` form security hash"
msgstr "Foirm hash slándála ``contrib.comments``"

msgid ""
"Consequences: The user will see the validation error \"Security hash failed."
"\""
msgstr ""
"Iarmhairtí: Feicfidh an t-úsáideoir an earráid bailíochtaithe “Theip ar hash "
"slándála.”"

msgid ""
"Time period: The amount of time you expect users to take filling out comment "
"forms."
msgstr ""
"Tréimhse ama: An méid ama a bhfuil tú ag súil go dtógfaidh úsáideoirí "
"foirmeacha tráchta a líonadh."

msgid "``FormWizard`` security hash"
msgstr "Hash slándála ``FormWizard``"

msgid ""
"Consequences: The user will see an error about the form having expired and "
"will be sent back to the first page of the wizard, losing the data entered "
"so far."
msgstr ""
"Iarmhairtí: Feicfidh an t-úsáideoir earráid faoin bhfoirm atá in éag agus "
"seolfar ar ais chuig an gcéad leathanach den draoi, ag cailleadh na sonraí a "
"iontráiltear go dtí seo."

msgid ""
"Time period: The amount of time you expect users to take filling out the "
"affected forms."
msgstr ""
"Tréimhse ama: An méid ama a bhfuil tú ag súil go dtógfaidh úsáideoirí na "
"foirmeacha atá buailte ag líonadh."

msgid "CSRF check"
msgstr "Seiceáil CSRF"

msgid ""
"Note: This is actually a Django 1.1 fallback, not Django 1.2, and it applies "
"only if you're upgrading from 1.1."
msgstr ""
"Nóta: Is fallback Django 1.1 é seo i ndáiríre, ní Django 1.2, agus ní "
"bhaineann sé ach amháin má tá tú ag uasghrádú ó 1.1."

msgid ""
"Consequences: The user will see a 403 error with any CSRF-protected POST "
"form."
msgstr ""
"Iarmhairtí: Feicfidh an t-úsáideoir earráid 403 le haon fhoirm POST faoi "
"chosaint CSRF."

msgid ""
"Time period: The amount of time you expect user to take filling out such "
"forms."
msgstr ""
"Tréimhse ama: An méid ama a bhfuil súil agat leis an úsáideoir a ghlacadh "
"chun foirmeacha den sórt sin a líonadh."

msgid "``contrib.auth`` user password hash-upgrade sequence"
msgstr "Seicheamh uasghrádaithe pasfhocal úsáideora ``contrib.auth``"

msgid ""
"Consequences: Each user's password will be updated to a stronger password "
"hash when it's written to the database in 1.4. This means that if you "
"upgrade to 1.4 and then need to downgrade to 1.3, version 1.3 won't be able "
"to read the updated passwords."
msgstr ""
"Iarmhairtí: Déanfar pasfhocal gach úsáideora a nuashonrú go hash pasfhocal "
"níos láidre nuair a bheidh sé scríofa chuig an mbunachar sonraí i 1.4. "
"Ciallaíonn sé seo má dhéanann tú uasghrádú go 1.4 agus ansin caithfidh tú "
"íosghrádú go 1.3, ní bheidh leagan 1.3 in ann na pasfhocail nuashonraithe a "
"léamh."

msgid ""
"Remedy: Set :setting:`PASSWORD_HASHERS` to use your original password "
"hashing when you initially upgrade to 1.4. After you confirm your app works "
"well with Django 1.4 and you won't have to roll back to 1.3, enable the new "
"password hashes."
msgstr ""
"Leigheas: Socraigh: Socrú: `PASSWORD_HASHERS` chun do hashing pasfhocal "
"bunaidh a úsáid nuair a dhéanann tú uasghrádú ar dtús go 1.4. Tar éis duit a "
"dhearbhú go n-oibríonn d'aip go maith le Django 1.4 agus ní bheidh ort "
"rolladh ar ais go 1.3, cumasaigh na hashes pasfhocal nua."

msgid "``django.contrib.flatpages``"
msgstr "``django.contrib.flatpages``"

msgid ""
"Starting in 1.4, "
"the :class:`~django.contrib.flatpages.middleware.FlatpageFallbackMiddleware` "
"only adds a trailing slash and redirects if the resulting URL refers to an "
"existing flatpage. For example, requesting ``/notaflatpageoravalidurl`` in a "
"previous version would redirect to ``/notaflatpageoravalidurl/``, which "
"would subsequently raise a 404. Requesting ``/notaflatpageoravalidurl`` now "
"will immediately raise a 404."
msgstr ""
"Ag tosú i 1.4, ní chuireann an:class: "
"`~django.contrib.flatpages.middleware.flatPageFallBackMiddleware` ach slash "
"rianaithe agus atreoraíonn sé má thagraíonn an URL mar thoradh air sin do "
"leathanach cothrom atá ann cheana. Mar shampla, iarraidh ``/"
"notaflatpageoravalidurl`` i leagan roimhe seo, atreoródh sé chuig ``/"
"notaflatpageoravalidurl/``, a d'ardódh 404 ina dhiaidh sin. Ag iarraidh ``/"
"notaflatpageoravalidurl`` anois ardófar 404 láithreach."

msgid ""
"Also, redirects returned by flatpages are now permanent (with 301 status "
"code), to match the behavior "
"of :class:`~django.middleware.common.CommonMiddleware`."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith leis sin, tá athatreoruithe ar ais ag flatpages buan anois (le "
"301 cód stádais), chun iompraíocht: class: "
"`~django.middleware.common.commonMiddleware` a mheaitseáil."

msgid ""
"Serialization of :class:`~datetime.datetime` and :class:`~datetime.time`"
msgstr "Sraitheadh de:class: `~datetime.datetime` agus:class: `~datetime.time`"

msgid ""
"As a consequence of time-zone support, and according to the ECMA-262 "
"specification, we made changes to the JSON serializer:"
msgstr ""
"Mar thoradh ar thacaíocht crios ama, agus de réir sonraíocht ECMA-262, "
"rinneamar athruithe ar an serializer JSON:"

msgid ""
"It includes the time zone for aware datetime objects. It raises an exception "
"for aware time objects."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn sé an crios ama le haghaidh rudaí dáta-am feasacha. Ardaíonn sé "
"eisceacht maidir le rudaí ama feasacha."

msgid ""
"It includes milliseconds for datetime and time objects. There is still some "
"precision loss, because Python stores microseconds (6 digits) and JSON only "
"supports milliseconds (3 digits). However, it's better than discarding "
"microseconds entirely."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn sé milleasoicind le haghaidh rudaí dáta agus ama. Tá roinnt "
"caillteanas cruinneas ann fós, toisc go stórálann Python micrea-soicind (6 "
"dhigit) agus ní thacaíonn JSON ach le milleasoicind (3 dhigit). Mar sin "
"féin, tá sé níos fearr ná microsoicind a dhiúscairt go hiomlán."

msgid ""
"We changed the XML serializer to use the ISO8601 format for datetimes. The "
"letter ``T`` is used to separate the date part from the time part, instead "
"of a space. Time zone information is included in the ``[+-]HH:MM`` format."
msgstr ""
"D'athraíomar an serializer XML chun an formáid ISO8601 a úsáid le haghaidh "
"dáta-amanna. Úsáidtear an litir `T ``chun an chuid dáta a scaradh ón gcuid "
"ama, in ionad spás. Tá faisnéis crios ama san áireamh sa fhormáid ``[+-] "
"HH:MM``."

msgid ""
"Though the serializers now use these new formats when creating fixtures, "
"they can still load fixtures that use the old format."
msgstr ""
"Cé go n-úsáideann na sraitheoirí na formáidí nua seo anois agus iad ag "
"cruthú daingneáin, is féidir leo daingneáin a úsáideann an seanfhormáid a "
"luchtú fós."

msgid "``supports_timezone`` changed to ``False`` for SQLite"
msgstr "Athraíodh ``supports_timezone`` go ``False`` do SQLite"

msgid ""
"The database feature ``supports_timezone`` used to be ``True`` for SQLite. "
"Indeed, if you saved an aware datetime object, SQLite stored a string that "
"included an UTC offset. However, this offset was ignored when loading the "
"value back from the database, which could corrupt the data."
msgstr ""
"Ba é ``True`` an ghné bhunachar sonraí ``supports_timezone`` do SQLite. Go "
"deimhin, má shábháil tú réad am dáta feasach, stóráil SQLite teaghrán a "
"chuimsigh fritháireamh UTC. Mar sin féin, rinneadh neamhaird den "
"fhritháireamh seo agus an luach á luchtú ar ais ón mbunachar sonraí, rud a "
"d'fhéadfadh na sonraí a éilliú."

msgid ""
"In the context of time-zone support, this flag was changed to ``False``, and "
"datetimes are now stored without time-zone information in SQLite. "
"When :setting:`USE_TZ` is ``False``, if you attempt to save an aware "
"datetime object, Django raises an exception."
msgstr ""
"I gcomhthéacs tacaíochta crios ama, athraíodh an bratach seo go `False`, "
"agus stóráiltear amanna dáta anois gan faisnéis crios ama i SQLite. Nuair: "
"Setting: Is é `USE_TZ` `False``, má dhéanann tú iarracht réad dáta-ama "
"feasach a shábháil, ardaíonn Django eisceacht."

msgid "``MySQLdb``-specific exceptions"
msgstr "``MySQLDB``-eisceachtaí sonracha"

msgid ""
"The MySQL backend historically has raised ``MySQLdb.OperationalError`` when "
"a query triggered an exception. We've fixed this bug, and we now "
"raise :exc:`django.db.DatabaseError` instead. If you were testing for "
"``MySQLdb.OperationalError``, you'll need to update your ``except`` clauses."
msgstr ""
"D'ardaigh cúltaca MySQL go stairiúil ``MySQLDB.OperationalError`` nuair a "
"spreag ceist eisceacht. Tá an fabht seo socraithe againn, agus argaimid "
"anois:exc: `django.db.databaseError` ina ionad. Má bhí tú ag tástáil le "
"haghaidh `MySQLDB.OperationalError``, beidh ort do chlásal ```except` a "
"nuashonrú."

msgid "Database connection's thread-locality"
msgstr "Suíomh snáithe nasc bunachar sonraí"

msgid ""
"``DatabaseWrapper`` objects (i.e. the connection objects referenced by "
"``django.db.connection`` and ``django.db.connections[\"some_alias\"]``) used "
"to be thread-local. They are now global objects in order to be potentially "
"shared between multiple threads. While the individual connection objects are "
"now global, the ``django.db.connections`` dictionary referencing those "
"objects is still thread-local. Therefore if you just use the ORM or "
"``DatabaseWrapper.cursor()`` then the behavior is still the same as before. "
"Note, however, that ``django.db.connection`` does not directly reference the "
"default ``DatabaseWrapper`` object anymore and is now a proxy to access that "
"object's attributes. If you need to access the actual ``DatabaseWrapper`` "
"object, use ``django.db.connections[DEFAULT_DB_ALIAS]`` instead."
msgstr ""
"Bhí rudaí `DatabaseWrapper`` (ie na rudaí nasc dá dtagraíonn "
"``django.db.connection`` agus ``django.db.connexions [\"some_alias\"] ``) a "
"bhí snáith-áitiúil. Is rudaí domhanda iad anois d'fhonn iad a roinnt idir "
"snáitheanna iolracha. Cé go bhfuil na rudaí ceangail aonair domhanda anois, "
"tá an foclóir ``django.db.connections` a thagraíonn na rudaí sin fós snáithe "
"áitiúil. Dá bhrí sin mura n-úsáideann tú ach an ORM nó "
"``DatabaseWrapper.cursor ()`` ansin tá an t-iompar fós mar an gcéanna le "
"roimhe seo. Tabhair faoi deara, áfach, nach dtagraíonn "
"`django.db.connection`` go díreach don réad réamhshocraithe "
"``DatabaseWrapper`` níos mó agus gur seachfhreastalaí é anois chun rochtain "
"a fháil ar thréithe an réada sin. Más gá duit rochtain a fháil ar an réad "
"iarbhír ``DatabaseWrapper``, bain úsáid as ``django.db.connexions "
"[DEFAULT_DB_ALIAS]`` ina ionad."

msgid ""
"As part of this change, all underlying SQLite connections are now enabled "
"for potential thread-sharing (by passing the ``check_same_thread=False`` "
"attribute to ``pysqlite``). ``DatabaseWrapper`` however preserves the "
"previous behavior by disabling thread-sharing by default, so this does not "
"affect any existing code that purely relies on the ORM or on "
"``DatabaseWrapper.cursor()``."
msgstr ""
"Mar chuid den athrú seo, cumasaítear gach nasc bunúsach SQLite anois le "
"haghaidh comhroinnt snáithe féideartha (tríd an tréith "
"``Check_SAME_Thread=False`` a rith le ``pysqlite ``). Caomhníonn "
"``DatabaseWrapper`` an t-iompar roimhe seo, áfach, trí chomhroinnt snáithe a "
"dhíchumasú de réir réamhshocraithe, mar sin ní dhéanann sé difear d'aon chód "
"atá ann cheana atá ag brath amháin ar an ORM nó ar`` DatabaseWrapper.cursor "
"() ``."

msgid ""
"Finally, while it's now possible to pass connections between threads, Django "
"doesn't make any effort to synchronize access to the underlying backend. "
"Concurrency behavior is defined by the underlying backend implementation. "
"Check their documentation for details."
msgstr ""
"Faoi dheireadh, cé go bhfuil sé indéanta anois naisc a rith idir "
"snáitheanna, ní dhéanann Django aon iarracht rochtain ar an gcúltaca "
"bunúsach a shioncronú. Sainmhínítear iompar comhréireachta ag an gcur chun "
"feidhme cúltaca bunúsach. Seiceáil a gcáipéisíocht le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid "``COMMENTS_BANNED_USERS_GROUP`` setting"
msgstr "Socrú ``COMMENTS_BANNED_USERS_GROUP``"

msgid ""
"Django's comments has historically supported excluding the comments of a "
"special user group, but we've never documented the feature properly and "
"didn't enforce the exclusion in other parts of the app such as the template "
"tags. To fix this problem, we removed the code from the feed class."
msgstr ""
"Tacaigh tuairimí Django go stairiúil le tuairimí grúpa úsáideoirí speisialta "
"a eisiamh, ach níor dhoiciméadaíomar an ghné riamh i gceart agus níor "
"fhorfheidhmigh muid an eisiamh i gcodanna eile den aip mar na clibeanna "
"teimpléid. Chun an fhadhb seo a shocrú, bhain muid an cód ón rang beatha."

msgid ""
"If you rely on the feature and want to restore the old behavior, use a "
"custom comment model manager to exclude the user group, like this::"
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag brath ar an ngné agus má theastaíonn uait an sean-iompar a chur "
"ar ais, bain úsáid as bainisteoir samhail tráchta saincheaptha chun an grúpa "
"úsáideoirí a eisiamh, mar seo:"

msgid ""
"Save this model manager in your custom comment app (e.g., in "
"``my_comments_app/managers.py``) and add it your custom comment app model::"
msgstr ""
"Sábháil an bainisteoir samhail seo i d'aip tráchta saincheaptha (m.sh., i "
"`my_comments_app/managers.py``) agus cuir do mhúnla aip trácht saincheaptha "
"leis::"

msgid "``IGNORABLE_404_STARTS`` and ``IGNORABLE_404_ENDS`` settings"
msgstr "Socruithe ```IGNORABLE_404_STARTS`` agus ``IGNORABLE_404_ENDS``"

msgid ""
"Until Django 1.3, it was possible to exclude some URLs from "
"Django's :doc:`404 error reporting</howto/error-reporting>` by adding "
"prefixes to ``IGNORABLE_404_STARTS`` and suffixes to ``IGNORABLE_404_ENDS``."
msgstr ""
"Go dtí Django 1.3, bhí sé in ann roinnt URLanna a eisiamh ó Django's:doc: "
"`404 tuairisciú earráid` trí réamhréamhacha a chur le "
"``IGNORABLE_404_STARTS`` agus iarmhairtí le ``IGNORABLE_404_ENDS``</howto/"
"error-reporting>."

msgid ""
"In Django 1.4, these two settings are superseded "
"by :setting:`IGNORABLE_404_URLS`, which is a list of compiled regular "
"expressions. Django won't send an email for 404 errors on URLs that match "
"any of them."
msgstr ""
"I Django 1.4, cuirtear an dá shocrú seo in ionad:setting: "
"`IGNORABLE_404_URLS`, ar liosta de nathanna rialta tiomsaithe é. Ní "
"sheolfaidh Django ríomhphost le haghaidh earráidí 404 ar URLanna a "
"mheaitseálann le haon cheann acu."

msgid ""
"Furthermore, the previous settings had some rather arbitrary default values::"
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, bhí roinnt luachanna réamhshocraithe a bhí sách treallach "
"ag na socruithe roimhe seo::"

msgid ""
"It's not Django's role to decide if your website has a legacy ``/cgi-bin/`` "
"section or a ``favicon.ico``. As a consequence, the default values "
"of :setting:`IGNORABLE_404_URLS`, ``IGNORABLE_404_STARTS``, and "
"``IGNORABLE_404_ENDS`` are all now empty."
msgstr ""
"Ní ról Django é cinneadh a dhéanamh an bhfuil rannán ``/cgi-bin/`` "
"oidhreachta nó ``favicon.ic` ag do shuíomh Gréasáin. Mar thoradh air sin, tá "
"na luachanna réamhshocraithe de:setting: `IGNORABLE_404_URLS`, "
"``IGNORABLE_404_STARTS``, agus ``IGNORABLE_404_ENDS`` folamh anois."

msgid ""
"If you have customized ``IGNORABLE_404_STARTS`` or ``IGNORABLE_404_ENDS``, "
"or if you want to keep the old default value, you should add the following "
"lines in your settings file::"
msgstr ""
"Má tá ``IGNORABLE_404_STARTS`` nó ``IGNORABLE_404_ENDS`` saincheaptha agat, "
"nó más mian leat an seanluach réamhshocraithe a choinneáil, ba cheart duit "
"na línte seo a leanas a chur i do chomhad socruithe:"

msgid ""
"Don't forget to escape characters that have a special meaning in a regular "
"expression, such as periods."
msgstr ""
"Ná déan dearmad éalú le carachtair a bhfuil brí speisialta acu i léiriú "
"rialta, mar shampla tréimhsí."

msgid "CSRF protection extended to PUT and DELETE"
msgstr "Leathnaithe cosaint CSRF go PUT agus DELETE"

msgid ""
"Previously, Django's :doc:`CSRF protection </ref/csrf/>` provided protection "
"only against POST requests. Since use of PUT and DELETE methods in AJAX "
"applications is becoming more common, we now protect all methods not defined "
"as safe by :rfc:`2616` -- i.e., we exempt GET, HEAD, OPTIONS and TRACE, and "
"we enforce protection on everything else."
msgstr ""
"Roimhe seo, thug Django's:doc: `Cosaint CSRF `cosaint ar fáil ach amháin i "
"gcoinne iarratais POST. </ref/csrf/> Ós rud é go bhfuil úsáid modhanna PUT "
"agus DELETE i bhfeidhmchláir AJAX ag éirí níos coitianta, déanaimid cosaint "
"anois gach modh nach bhfuil sainmhínithe mar shábháilte ag: rfc: `2616` - "
"ie, déanaimid díolmhaithe GET, HEAD, OPTIONS agus TRACE, agus cuirimid "
"cosaint i bhfeidhm ar gach rud eile."

msgid ""
"If you're using PUT or DELETE methods in AJAX applications, please see "
"the :ref:`instructions about using AJAX and CSRF <csrf-ajax>`."
msgstr ""
"<csrf-ajax>Má tá modhanna PUT nó DELETE á úsáid agat in iarratais AJAX, "
"féach le do thoil: ref: `treoracha maidir le AJAX agus CSRF a úsáid `."

msgid "Password reset view now accepts ``subject_template_name``"
msgstr ""
"Glacann amharc athshocraithe pasfhocal anois le ``subject_template_name``"

msgid ""
"The ``password_reset`` view in ``django.contrib.auth`` now accepts a "
"``subject_template_name`` parameter, which is passed to the password save "
"form as a keyword argument. If you are using this view with a custom "
"password reset form, then you will need to ensure your form's ``save()`` "
"method accepts this keyword argument."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an radharc ``password_reset`` i `django.contrib.auth`` anois le "
"paraiméadar ``subject_template_name``, a chuirtear chuig an bhfoirm sábhála "
"pasfhocal mar argóint eochairfhocal. Má tá an dearcadh seo á úsáid agat le "
"foirm athshocraithe pasfhocal saincheaptha, ansin beidh ort a chinntiú go "
"nglacann modh ``save () `d'fhoirm leis an argóint eochairfhocal seo."

msgid "``django.core.template_loaders``"
msgstr "``django.core.template_loaders``"

msgid ""
"This was an alias to ``django.template.loader`` since 2005, and we've "
"removed it without emitting a warning due to the length of the deprecation. "
"If your code still referenced this, please use ``django.template.loader`` "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"Ba ailias é seo ar ``django.template.loader`` ó 2005, agus tá sé bainte "
"againn gan rabhadh a astú mar gheall ar fhad an díghníomhaíochta. Má "
"thagraíonn do chód seo fós, bain úsáid as ``django.template.loader`` ina "
"ionad."

msgid "``django.db.models.fields.URLField.verify_exists``"
msgstr "``Django.db.models.fields.urlfield.verify_exists``"

msgid ""
"This functionality has been removed due to intractable performance and "
"security issues. Any existing usage of ``verify_exists`` should be removed."
msgstr ""
"Baineadh an fheidhmiúlacht seo mar gheall ar shaincheisteanna feidhmíochta "
"agus slándála nach féidir Ba chóir aon úsáid atá ann cheana de "
"`verify_exists`` a bhaint."

msgid "``django.core.files.storage.Storage.open``"
msgstr "``Django.core.files.storage.storage.open``"

msgid ""
"The ``open`` method of the base Storage class used to take an obscure "
"parameter ``mixin`` that allowed you to dynamically change the base classes "
"of the returned file object. This has been removed. In the rare case you "
"relied on the ``mixin`` parameter, you can easily achieve the same by "
"overriding the ``open`` method, like this::"
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear an modh `oscailte`` den rang Stórála bonn chun paraiméadar doiléir "
"``mixin`` a thógáil a ligean duit bunaicmí an réada comhaid a fhilleadh a "
"athrú go dinimiciúil. Tá sé seo bainte. Sa chás annamh a bhraith tú ar an "
"bparaiméadar ``mixin``, is féidir leat an rud céanna a bhaint amach go "
"héasca tríd an modh `oscailt ``a shárú, mar seo:"

msgid "YAML deserializer now uses ``yaml.safe_load``"
msgstr "Úsáideann deserializer YAML anois ``yaml.safe_load ``"

msgid ""
"``yaml.load`` is able to construct any Python object, which may trigger "
"arbitrary code execution if you process a YAML document that comes from an "
"untrusted source. This feature isn't necessary for Django's YAML "
"deserializer, whose primary use is to load fixtures consisting of simple "
"objects. Even though fixtures are trusted data, the YAML deserializer now "
"uses ``yaml.safe_load`` for additional security."
msgstr ""
"Tá ``yaml.load`` in ann aon réad Python a thógáil, a d'fhéadfadh forghníomhú "
"cód treallach a spreagadh má phróiseálann tú doiciméad YAML a thagann ó "
"fhoinse neamhiontaofa. Níl an ghné seo riachtanach le haghaidh deserializer "
"YAML Django, a bpríomhúsáid ná daingneáin atá comhdhéanta de rudaí simplí a "
"luchtú. Cé gur sonraí iontaofa iad daingneáin, úsáideann an deserializer "
"YAML anois ``yaml.safe_load ``le haghaidh slándála breise."

msgid "Session cookies now have the ``httponly`` flag by default"
msgstr ""
"Tá an bratach `httponly` ag fianáin seisiúin anois de réir réamhshocraithe"

msgid ""
"Session cookies now include the ``httponly`` attribute by default to help "
"reduce the impact of potential XSS attacks. As a consequence of this change, "
"session cookie data, including ``sessionid``, is no longer accessible from "
"JavaScript in many browsers. For strict backwards compatibility, use "
"``SESSION_COOKIE_HTTPONLY = False`` in your settings file."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn fianáin seisiúin an tréith `httponly` anois de réir "
"réamhshocraithe chun cabhrú le tionchar ionsaithe féideartha XSS a laghdú. "
"Mar thoradh ar an athrú seo, níl sonraí fianán seisiúin, lena n-áirítear "
"``sessionid`, inrochtana a thuilleadh ó JavaScript i go leor brabhsálaithe. "
"Le haghaidh comhoiriúnacht dhian ar chúl, bain úsáid as "
"``SESSION_COOKIE_HTTPONLY = False`` i do chomhad socruithe."

msgid "The :tfilter:`urlize` filter no longer escapes every URL"
msgstr "Ní éalaíonn an scagair:tFilter: `urlize` gach URL a thuilleadh"

msgid ""
"When a URL contains a ``%xx`` sequence, where ``xx`` are two hexadecimal "
"digits, :tfilter:`urlize` now assumes that the URL is already escaped and "
"doesn't apply URL escaping again. This is wrong for URLs whose unquoted form "
"contains a ``%xx`` sequence, but such URLs are very unlikely to happen in "
"the wild, because they would confuse browsers too."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhíonn seicheamh ``%xx`` i URL, áit a bhfuil dhá dhigit "
"heicseachadúil iad ``xx``, glacann: tfilter: `urlize` anois go bhfuil an URL "
"éalaithe cheana féin agus nach gcuireann sé URL ag éalú arís. Tá sé seo "
"mícheart do URLanna a bhfuil seicheamh ``%xx`` ag a bhfoirm neamh-luaite, "
"ach ní dócha go dtarlóidh URLanna den sórt sin san fhiáin, toisc go "
"ndéanfadh siad mearbhall ar bhrabhsálaithe freisin."

msgid "``assertTemplateUsed`` and ``assertTemplateNotUsed`` as context manager"
msgstr ""
"``AssertTemplateUsed`` agus ``AssertTemplateNoTused`` mar bhainisteoir "
"comhthéacs"

msgid ""
"It's now possible to check whether a template was used within a block of "
"code with :meth:`~django.test.SimpleTestCase.assertTemplateUsed` "
"and :meth:`~django.test.SimpleTestCase.assertTemplateNotUsed`. And they can "
"be used as a context manager::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir anois a sheiceáil an úsáideadh teimpléad laistigh de bhloc cód le: "
"meth: `~django.test.simpletestcase.assertTemplateUsed` agus:meth: "
"`~django.test.simpletestcase.assertTemplateNotUsed`. Agus is féidir iad a "
"úsáid mar bhainisteoir comhthéacs::"

msgid "See the :ref:`assertion documentation<assertions>` for more."
msgstr ""
"<assertions>Féach in:ref: `dearbhú doiciméadú `le haghaidh tuilleadh eolais."

msgid "Database connections after running the test suite"
msgstr "Naisc bhunachar sonraí tar éis an tsraith tástála"

msgid ""
"The default test runner no longer restores the database connections after "
"tests' execution. This prevents the production database from being exposed "
"to potential threads that would still be running and attempting to create "
"new connections."
msgstr ""
"Ní dhéanfaidh an reathaí tástála réamhshocraithe na naisc bhunachar sonraí a "
"athchóiriú a thuilleadh tar éis na tástálacha a chur i gcrích. Cuireann sé "
"seo cosc ​​ar an mbunachar sonraí táirgeachta a bheith faoi lé snáitheanna "
"féideartha a bheadh ​​fós ar siúl agus iarracht a dhéanamh naisc nua a chruthú."

msgid ""
"If your code relied on connections to the production database being created "
"after tests' execution, then you can restore the previous behavior by "
"subclassing ``DjangoTestRunner`` and overriding its ``teardown_databases()`` "
"method."
msgstr ""
"Má bhí do chód ag brath ar naisc leis an mbunachar sonraí táirgeachta atá á "
"chruthú tar éis tástálacha a fhorghníomhú, ansin is féidir leat an t-iompar "
"roimhe seo a chur ar ais trí “DjangoTestRunner” a fho-aicmiú agus a mhodh "
"`teardown_databases () `a shárú."

msgid "Output of :djadmin:`manage.py help <help>`"
msgstr "<help>Aschur de:djadmin: `cabhair manage.py `"

msgid ""
":djadmin:`manage.py help <help>` now groups available commands by "
"application. If you depended on the output of this command -- if you parsed "
"it, for example -- then you'll need to update your code. To get a list of "
"all available management commands in a script, use :djadmin:`manage.py help "
"--commands <help>` instead."
msgstr ""
": djadmin: `manage.py cabhair <help>`grúpaíonn orduithe atá ar fáil anois de "
"réir feidhmchláir. Má bhí tú ag brath ar aschur an ordaithe seo - má "
"dhéantar é a pháirseáil, mar shampla - ansin beidh ort do chód a nuashonrú. "
"<help>Chun liosta de na horduithe bainistíochta go léir atá ar fáil a fháil "
"i script, bain úsáid as: djadmin: `manage.py help --orders `ina ionad."

msgid "``extends`` template tag"
msgstr "Clib teimpléad ``leathnaíon`"

msgid ""
"Previously, the :ttag:`extends` tag used a buggy method of parsing "
"arguments, which could lead to it erroneously considering an argument as a "
"string literal when it wasn't. It now uses ``parser.compile_filter``, like "
"other tags."
msgstr ""
"Roimhe seo, d'úsáid an clibe:ttag: `extens` modh buggy chun argóintí a "
"pháirseáil, rud a d'fhéadfadh a bheith mar thoradh air go bhféadfadh sé "
"argóint a mheas go míearrach mar shreang litriúil nuair nach raibh sé. "
"Úsáideann sé anois ``parser.compile_filter``, cosúil le clibeanna eile."

msgid ""
"The internals of the tag aren't part of the official stable API, but in the "
"interests of full disclosure, the ``ExtendsNode.__init__`` definition has "
"changed, which may break any custom tags that use this class."
msgstr ""
"Níl inmheánacha an chlib mar chuid den API cobhsaí oifigiúil, ach ar mhaithe "
"le nochtadh iomlán, an `ExtendsNode. Tá athrú tagtha ar an sainmhíniú "
"__init__``, rud a d'fhéadfadh aon chlibeanna saincheaptha a úsáideann an "
"rang seo a bhriseadh."

msgid "Loading some incomplete fixtures no longer works"
msgstr "Ní oibríonn luchtú roinnt daingneáin neamhiom"

msgid ""
"Prior to 1.4, a default value was inserted for fixture objects that were "
"missing a specific date or datetime value when auto_now or auto_now_add was "
"set for the field. This was something that should not have worked, and in "
"1.4 loading such incomplete fixtures will fail. Because fixtures are a raw "
"import, they should explicitly specify all field values, regardless of field "
"options on the model."
msgstr ""
"Roimh 1.4, cuireadh luach réamhshocraithe isteach le haghaidh réada "
"daingneáin a raibh dáta nó dáta dáta ar leith in easnamh orthu nuair a "
"socraíodh auto_now nó auto_now_add don réimse. Ba rud é seo nár cheart a "
"bheith ag obair, agus i 1.4 theipfidh ar lódáil daingneáin neamhiomlána den "
"sórt sin. Toisc gur allmhairí amh iad daingneáin, ba cheart go sonrófaí go "
"sainráite iad na luachanna réimse uile, beag beann ar na roghanna allamuigh "
"ar an tsamhail."

msgid "Development Server Multithreading"
msgstr "Multithreading Freastalaí Forbartha"

msgid ""
"The development server is now is multithreaded by default. Use "
"the :option:`runserver --nothreading` option to disable the use of threading "
"in the development server:"
msgstr ""
"Tá an freastalaí forbartha ilshreathaithe anois de réir réamhshocraithe. "
"Úsáid an rogha:option: `runserver --nothreading` chun úsáid snáithe a "
"dhíchumasú sa fhreastalaí forbartha:"

msgid "Attributes disabled in markdown when safe mode set"
msgstr "Díchumasaithe tréithe i marcáil nuair a shocraítear modh sábhá"

msgid ""
"Prior to Django 1.4, attributes were included in any markdown output "
"regardless of safe mode setting of the filter. With version > 2.1 of the "
"Python-Markdown library, an enable_attributes option was added. When the "
"safe argument is passed to the markdown filter, both the ``safe_mode=True`` "
"and ``enable_attributes=False`` options are set. If using a version of the "
"Python-Markdown library less than 2.1, a warning is issued that the output "
"is insecure."
msgstr ""
"Roimh Django 1.4, cuireadh tréithe san áireamh in aon aschur marcála beag "
"beann ar shuíomh modh sábháilte an scagaire. Le leagan> 2.1 de leabharlann "
"Python-Markdown, cuireadh rogha enable_attributs leis. Nuair a chuirtear an "
"argóint sábháilte chuig an scagaire marcdown, socraítear na roghanna "
"``safe_mode=true`` agus ``enable_attributes=false ``araon. Má úsáideann tú "
"leagan de leabharlann Python-Markdown níos lú ná 2.1, eisítear rabhadh go "
"bhfuil an t-aschur neamhchinnte."

msgid "FormMixin get_initial returns an instance-specific dictionary"
msgstr "Filleann FormMixin get_initial foclóir sonrach don eocht"

msgid ""
"In Django 1.3, the ``get_initial`` method of "
"the :class:`django.views.generic.edit.FormMixin` class was returning the "
"class ``initial`` dictionary. This has been fixed to return a copy of this "
"dictionary, so form instances can modify their initial data without messing "
"with the class variable."
msgstr ""
"I Django 1.3, bhí an modh ``get_initial`` den range:class: "
"`django.views.generic.edit.formMixin` ag tabhairt ar ais an bhfoclóir ranga "
"``initial``. Socraíodh é seo chun cóip den fhoclóir seo a thabhairt ar ais, "
"mar sin is féidir le cásanna foirme a gcuid sonraí tosaigh a mhodhnú gan dul "
"isteach leis an athróg aicme."

msgid "Features deprecated in 1.4"
msgstr "Gnéithe atá díscríofa i 1.4"

msgid "Old styles of calling ``cache_page`` decorator"
msgstr "Seanstíleanna chun glaoch ar ``cache_page`` maisitheoir"

msgid ""
"Some legacy ways of "
"calling :func:`~django.views.decorators.cache.cache_page` have been "
"deprecated. Please see the documentation for the correct way to use this "
"decorator."
msgstr ""
"Tá roinnt bealaí oidhreachta chun glaoch a ghlao:func: "
"`~django.views.decorators.cache.cache_page` a dhíchur. Féach an doiciméadú "
"le do thoil maidir leis an mbealach ceart chun an maisitheoir seo a úsáid."

msgid "Support for PostgreSQL versions older than 8.2"
msgstr "Tacaíocht do leaganacha PostgreSQL níos sine ná 8.2"

msgid ""
"Django 1.3 dropped support for PostgreSQL versions older than 8.0, and we "
"suggested using a more recent version because of performance improvements "
"and, more importantly, the end of upstream support periods for 8.0 and 8.1 "
"was near (November 2010)."
msgstr ""
"Thit Django 1.3 tacaíocht do leaganacha PostgreSQL níos sine ná 8.0, agus "
"mholamar leagan níos déanaí a úsáid mar gheall ar fheabhsuithe feidhmíochta "
"agus, níos tábhachtaí fós, bhí deireadh na dtréimhsí tacaíochta suas sruth "
"do 8.0 agus 8.1 gar (Samhain 2010)."

msgid ""
"Django 1.4 takes that policy further and sets 8.2 as the minimum PostgreSQL "
"version it officially supports."
msgstr ""
"Tógann Django 1.4 an beartas sin níos faide agus leagann sé 8.2 mar an "
"leagan íosta PostgreSQL a thacaíonn sé go hoifigiúil."

msgid "Request exceptions are now always logged"
msgstr "Déantar eisceachtaí iarratais logáilte anois i"

msgid ""
"When we added :doc:`logging support </topics/logging/>` in Django in 1.3, "
"the admin error email support was moved into "
"the :class:`django.utils.log.AdminEmailHandler`, attached to the "
"``'django.request'`` logger. In order to maintain the established behavior "
"of error emails, the ``'django.request'`` logger was called only "
"when :setting:`DEBUG` was ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a chuireamar leis: doc: `tacaíocht logaithe' i Django i 1.3, aistríodh "
"an tacaíocht ríomhphoist earráid riaracháin isteach in:class: "
"`django.utils.log.adminemailHandler` </topics/logging/>, ceangailte leis an "
"logger ``'django.request'`. D'fhonn iompar seanbhunaithe ríomhphoist "
"earráide a choinneáil, níor glaoíodh ar an logálaí ``'django.request'` ach "
"nuair:setting: `DEBUG` `False``."

msgid ""
"To increase the flexibility of error logging for requests, the "
"``'django.request'`` logger is now called regardless of the value "
"of :setting:`DEBUG`, and the default settings file for new projects now "
"includes a separate filter attached "
"to :class:`django.utils.log.AdminEmailHandler` to prevent admin error emails "
"in ``DEBUG`` mode::"
msgstr ""
"Chun solúbthacht logála earráide le haghaidh iarratais a mhéadú, tugtar an "
"logálaí ``django.request'` anois beann ar an luach de:setting: `DEBUG`, agus "
"tá an comhad socruithe réamhshocraithe do thionscadail nua anois scagaire ar "
"leithligh ceangailte la:class: `Django.utils.log.adminemailHandler` chun "
"ríomhphoist earráide riaracháin a chosc i mód `DEBUG`:"

msgid ""
"If your project was created prior to this change, your :setting:`LOGGING` "
"setting will not include this new filter. In order to maintain backwards-"
"compatibility, Django will detect that your ``'mail_admins'`` handler "
"configuration includes no ``'filters'`` section and will automatically add "
"this filter for you and issue a pending-deprecation warning. This will "
"become a deprecation warning in Django 1.5, and in Django 1.6 the backwards-"
"compatibility shim will be removed entirely."
msgstr ""
"Má cruthaíodh do thionscadal roimh an athrú seo, ní chuimsíonn do shuíomh: "
"'LOGGING' an scagaire nua seo. D'fhonn comhoiriúnacht cúil a choinneáil, "
"braithfidh Django nach bhfuil aon chuid ```filters' ``i do chumraíocht "
"láimhseála ```mail_admins'` agus cuirfidh sé an scagaire seo duit go "
"huathoibríoch agus eiseoidh sé rabhadh dí-dhíothaithe. Beidh sé seo ina "
"rabhadh diúltaithe i Django 1.5, agus i Django 1.6 bainfear an shim "
"comhoiriúnachta cúil go hiomlán."

msgid ""
"The existence of any ``'filters'`` key under the ``'mail_admins'`` handler "
"will disable this backward-compatibility shim and deprecation warning."
msgstr ""
"Díchumasóidh aon eochair ``'filters'`` faoin láimhseálaí ```mail_admins'` an "
"rabhadh shiam comhoiriúnachta cúil seo agus díghníomhú."

msgid "``django.conf.urls.defaults``"
msgstr "``django.conf.urls.defaults``"

msgid ""
"Until Django 1.3, the ``include()``, ``patterns()``, and ``url()`` "
"functions, plus :data:`~django.conf.urls.handler404` "
"and :data:`~django.conf.urls.handler500` were located in a "
"``django.conf.urls.defaults`` module."
msgstr ""
"Go dtí Django 1.3, bhí na feidhmeanna ``include () ``, `patrons ()``, agus "
"``url () ``, móis:data: `~django.conf.urls.handler404` agus:data: "
"`~django.conf.urls.deftsaults`` lonnaithe i modúl "
"``django.conf.urls.deftsaults``."

msgid "In Django 1.4, they live in :mod:`django.conf.urls`."
msgstr "I Django 1.4, tá siad ina gcónaí in:mod: `django.conf.urls`."

msgid "``django.contrib.databrowse``"
msgstr "``django.contrib.databrowse``"

msgid ""
"Databrowse has not seen active development for some time, and this does not "
"show any sign of changing. There had been a suggestion for a `GSOC project`_ "
"to integrate the functionality of databrowse into the admin, but no progress "
"was made. While Databrowse has been deprecated, an enhancement of "
"``django.contrib.admin`` providing a similar feature set is still possible."
msgstr ""
"Níor chonaic Databrowse forbairt ghníomhach le tamall anuas, agus ní "
"thaispeánann sé seo aon chomhartha athraithe. Bhí moladh ann maidir le "
"`tionscadal GSOC `_ chun feidhmiúlacht databrowse a chomhtháthú sa "
"riarachán, ach níor rinneadh aon dul chun cinn. Cé go bhfuil Databrowse "
"imithe, is féidir feabhsú ar ``django.contrib.admin ``a sholáthraíonn tacar "
"gné den chineál céanna fós."

msgid ""
"The code that powers Databrowse is licensed under the same terms as Django "
"itself, so it's available to be adopted by an individual or group as a third-"
"party project."
msgstr ""
"Tá an cód a chumhachtaíonn Databrowse ceadúnaithe faoi na téarmaí céanna le "
"Django féin, mar sin tá sé ar fáil le duine aonair nó grúpa é a ghlacadh mar "
"thionscadal tríú páirtí."

msgid "``django.core.management.setup_environ``"
msgstr "``django.core.bainist.setup_environment ``"

msgid ""
"This function temporarily modified ``sys.path`` in order to make the parent "
"\"project\" directory importable under the old flat :djadmin:`startproject` "
"layout. This function is now deprecated, as its path workarounds are no "
"longer needed with the new ``manage.py`` and default project layout."
msgstr ""
"Athraigh an fheidhm seo ``sys.path`` go sealadach d'fhonn an t-eolaire "
"tuismitheora “tionscadal” a dhéanamh in-iompórtáilte faoin sean-leagan amach "
"flat:djadmin: `startproject`. Tá an fheidhm seo imithe anois, mar ní "
"theastaíonn a réamhshocruithe cosáin a thuilleadh leis an `manage.py` nua "
"agus leagan amach tionscadail réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"This function was never documented or part of the public API, but it was "
"widely recommended for use in setting up a \"Django environment\" for a user "
"script. These uses should be replaced by setting "
"the :envvar:`DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE` environment variable or "
"using :func:`django.conf.settings.configure`."
msgstr ""
"Níor doiciméadaíodh an fheidhm seo riamh ná mar chuid den API poiblí, ach "
"moladh go forleathan é le húsáid chun “timpeallacht Django” a bhunú do "
"script úsáideora. Ba chóir na húsáidí seo a chur in ionad trí athróg "
"timpeallachta: envvar: `DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE` a shocrú nó úsáid: func: "
"`django.conf.settings.configure`."

msgid "``django.core.management.execute_manager``"
msgstr "``django.core.bainistéireach.execute_manager``"

msgid ""
"This function was previously used by ``manage.py`` to execute a management "
"command. It is identical to "
"``django.core.management.execute_from_command_line``, except that it first "
"calls ``setup_environ``, which is now deprecated. As such, "
"``execute_manager`` is also deprecated; ``execute_from_command_line`` can be "
"used instead. Neither of these functions is documented as part of the public "
"API, but a deprecation path is needed due to use in existing ``manage.py`` "
"files."
msgstr ""
"D'úsáid `manage.py`` an fheidhm seo roimhe seo chun ordú bainistíochta a "
"fhorghníomhú. Tá sé comhionann le "
"``django.core.management.execute_from_command_line``, ach amháin go nglaonn "
"sé ar ``setup_environment ``ar dtús, atá díscoite anois. Dá bhrí sin, tá "
"`execute_manager`` díluanta freisin; is féidir ``execute_from_command_line`` "
"a úsáid ina ionad. Níl aon cheann de na feidhmeanna seo a dhoiciméadú mar "
"chuid den API poiblí, ach teastaíonn cosán díréireachta mar gheall ar úsáid "
"i gcomhaid `manage.py` atá ann cheana."

msgid "``is_safe`` and ``needs_autoescape`` attributes of template filters"
msgstr "``is_safe`` agus ``needs_autoescape`` tréithe scagairí teimpléad"

msgid ""
"Two flags, ``is_safe`` and ``needs_autoescape``, define how each template "
"filter interacts with Django's auto-escaping behavior. They used to be "
"attributes of the filter function::"
msgstr ""
"Sainmhíníonn dhá bhratach, ``is_safe`` agus ``needs_autoescape``, conas a "
"idirghníomhaíonn gach scagaire teimpléad le hiompar éalaithe uathoibríoch "
"Django. Ba ghnách iad a bheith ina thréithe den fheidhm scagaire::"

msgid ""
"However, this technique caused some problems in combination with decorators, "
"especially :func:`@stringfilter "
"<django.template.defaultfilters.stringfilter>`. Now, the flags are keyword "
"arguments of :meth:`@register.filter <django.template.Library.filter>`::"
msgstr ""
"<django.template.defaultfilters.stringfilter>Mar sin féin, ba chúis leis an "
"teicníc seo roinnt fadhbanna i dteannta le maisitheoirí, go háirithe: func: "
"`@stringfilter`. <django.template.Library.filter>Anois, is argóintí "
"eochairfhocal iad na bratacha de:meth: `@register .filter`:"

msgid ""
"See :ref:`filters and auto-escaping <filters-auto-escaping>` for more "
"information."
msgstr ""
"<filters-auto-escaping>Féach: tagairt: `scagairí agus éalú uathoibríoch `le "
"haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise."

msgid "Wildcard expansion of application names in ``INSTALLED_APPS``"
msgstr "Leathnú cárta fiáin ar ainmneacha iarratais i ``INSTALLED_APPS``"

msgid ""
"Until Django 1.3, :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` accepted wildcards in "
"application names, like ``django.contrib.*``. The expansion was performed by "
"a filesystem-based implementation of ``from <package> import *``. "
"Unfortunately, this can't be done reliably."
msgstr ""
"Go dtí Django 1.3, ghlac: `INSTALLED_APPS` le cártaí fiáine in ainmneacha "
"iarratais, cosúil le ``django.contrib.*``. <package>Rinneadh an leathnú trí "
"chur i bhfeidhm bunaithe ar chóras comhaid “ó allmhairiú*”. Ar an drochuair, "
"ní féidir é seo a dhéanamh go hiontaofa."

msgid ""
"This behavior was never documented. Since it is unpythonic, it was removed "
"in Django 1.4. If you relied on it, you must edit your settings file to list "
"all your applications explicitly."
msgstr ""
"Ní dhoiciméadaíodh an t-iompar seo riamh. Ós rud é go bhfuil sé "
"neamhpythonic, baineadh é i Django 1.4. Má bhraith tú air, ní mór duit do "
"chomhad socruithe a chur in eagar chun d'iarratais go léir a liostáil go "
"sainráite."

msgid "``HttpRequest.raw_post_data`` renamed to ``HttpRequest.body``"
msgstr "Athainmnigh ``HttpRequest.Raw_Post_Data`` go ``HttpRequest.body``"

msgid ""
"This attribute was confusingly named ``HttpRequest.raw_post_data``, but it "
"actually provided the body of the HTTP request. It's been renamed to "
"``HttpRequest.body``, and ``HttpRequest.raw_post_data`` has been deprecated."
msgstr ""
"Ainmníodh an tréith seo go mearbhall ``HttpRequest.raw_post_data ``, ach "
"chuir sé ar fáil i ndáiríre corp an iarratais HTTP. Athainmníodh é go "
"`HttpRequest.body ``, agus tá ``HttpRequest.Raw_Post_Data`` díluaite."

msgid ""
"``django.contrib.sitemaps`` bug fix with potential performance implications"
msgstr ""
"Socrú fabht ``django.contrib.sitemaps ``le himpleachtaí feidhmíochta "
"féideartha"

msgid ""
"In previous versions, ``Paginator`` objects used in sitemap classes were "
"cached, which could result in stale site maps. We've removed the caching, so "
"each request to a site map now creates a new Paginator object and calls "
"the :attr:`~django.contrib.sitemaps.Sitemap.items()` method of "
"the :class:`~django.contrib.sitemaps.Sitemap` subclass. Depending on what "
"your ``items()`` method is doing, this may have a negative performance "
"impact. To mitigate the performance impact, consider using the :doc:`caching "
"framework </topics/cache>` within your ``Sitemap`` subclass."
msgstr ""
"I leaganacha roimhe seo, rinneadh réada ``Paginator`` a úsáideadh i ranganna "
"léarscáileanna suímh a thaisceadh, rud a d'fhéadfadh seanléarscáileanna "
"láithreáin a bheith mar thoradh air. Bhaineamar an taisceadh as, mar sin "
"cruthaíonn gach iarratas chuig léarscáil an tsuímh réad Paginator nua agus "
"glaonn sé an modh :attr:`~django.contrib.sitemaps.Sitemap.items()` "
"den :class:`~django. ranníoc.mapaí láithreáin.fo-aicme léarscáil an "
"láithreáin`. Ag brath ar a bhfuil á dhéanamh ag do mhodh ``míreanna()``, "
"d'fhéadfadh tionchar diúltach a bheith aige seo ar fheidhmíocht. Chun an "
"tionchar feidhmíochta a mhaolú, smaoinigh ar an :doc:`creat taisce </topics/"
"cache>` a úsáid laistigh d'fho-aicme ``Mapa Láithreáin``."

msgid "Versions of Python-Markdown earlier than 2.1"
msgstr "Leaganacha de Python-Markdown níos luaithe ná 2.1"

msgid ""
"Versions of Python-Markdown earlier than 2.1 do not support the option to "
"disable attributes. As a security issue, earlier versions of this library "
"will not be supported by the markup contrib app in 1.5 under an accelerated "
"deprecation timeline."
msgstr ""
"Ní thacaíonn leaganacha de Python-Markdown níos luaithe ná 2.1 leis an rogha "
"tréithe a dhíchumasú. Mar shaincheist slándála, ní thacóidh an aip contrib "
"marcála le leaganacha níos luaithe den leabharlann seo i 1.5 faoi amlíne "
"díscrúdaithe luathaithe."

msgid "Django 1.4.1 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.4.1"

msgid ""
"This is the first security release in the Django 1.4 series, fixing several "
"security issues in Django 1.4. Django 1.4.1 is a recommended upgrade for all "
"users of Django 1.4."
msgstr ""
"Is é seo an chéad eisiúint slándála sa tsraith Django 1.4, ag socraithe "
"roinnt saincheisteanna slándála i Django 1.4. Is uasghrádú molta é Django "
"1.4.1 do gach úsáideoir de Django 1.4."

msgid "Django 1.4.10 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.4.10"

msgid "*November 6, 2013*"
msgstr "*6 Samhain, 2013*"

msgid "Django 1.4.10 fixes a Python-compatibility bug in the 1.4 series."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.4.10 fabht comhoiriúnachta Python sa tsraith 1.4."

msgid ""
"Django 1.4.9 inadvertently introduced issues with Python 2.5 compatibility. "
"Django 1.4.10 restores Python 2.5 compatibility. This was issue #21362 in "
"Django's Trac."
msgstr ""
"Thug Django 1.4.9 saincheisteanna isteach le comhoiriúnacht Python 2.5. "
"Athchruthaíonn Django 1.4.10 comhoiriúnacht Python 2.5. Ba é seo ceist "
"#21362 i Django's Trac."

msgid "Django 1.4.11 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.4.11"

msgid "*April 21, 2014*"
msgstr "*21 Aibreán, 2014*"

msgid ""
"Django 1.4.11 fixes three security issues in 1.4.10. Additionally, Django's "
"vendored version of six, ``django.utils.six``, has been upgraded to the "
"latest release (1.6.1)."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.4.11 trí shaincheist slándála i 1.4.10. Ina theannta sin, "
"tá leagan díolta Django de sé, ``django.utils.six ``, uasghrádaithe go dtí "
"an eisiúint is déanaí (1.6.1)."

msgid "Unexpected code execution using ``reverse()``"
msgstr "Forghníomhú cód gan choinne ag baint úsáide as ``reverse () ``"

msgid ""
"Django's URL handling is based on a mapping of regex patterns (representing "
"the URLs) to callable views, and Django's own processing consists of "
"matching a requested URL against those patterns to determine the appropriate "
"view to invoke."
msgstr ""
"Tá láimhseáil URL Django bunaithe ar mhapáil patrúin regex (a léiríonn na "
"URLanna) le tuairimí inghlaonta, agus is éard atá i bpróiseáil Django féin "
"URL iarrtha a mheaitseáil i gcoinne na patrúin sin chun an dearcadh cuí le "
"glaoch a chinneadh."

msgid ""
"Django also provides a convenience function -- ``reverse()`` -- which "
"performs this process in the opposite direction. The ``reverse()`` function "
"takes information about a view and returns a URL which would invoke that "
"view. Use of ``reverse()`` is encouraged for application developers, as the "
"output of ``reverse()`` is always based on the current URL patterns, meaning "
"developers do not need to change other code when making changes to URLs."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Django feidhm áisiúlachta freisin - ``reverse () ``- a dhéanann "
"an próiseas seo sa treo eile. Tógann an fheidhm ``reverse () ``faisnéis faoi "
"radharc agus filleann URL ar ais a chuirfeadh an dearcadh sin. Spreagtar "
"úsáid ``reverse () ``d'fhorbróirí feidhmchláir, toisc go mbíonn aschur "
"``reverse ()`` bunaithe i gcónaí ar na patrúin URL reatha, rud a chiallaíonn "
"nach gá d'fhorbróirí cód eile a athrú agus athruithe á dhéanamh ar URLanna."

msgid ""
"One argument signature for ``reverse()`` is to pass a dotted Python path to "
"the desired view. In this situation, Django will import the module indicated "
"by that dotted path as part of generating the resulting URL. If such a "
"module has import-time side effects, those side effects will occur."
msgstr ""
"Síniú argóint amháin le haghaidh ``reverse () ``ná cosán poncaí Python a "
"rith chuig an radharc atá ag teastáil. Sa chás seo, iompórtálfaidh Django an "
"modúl a léirítear leis an gcosán poncaigh sin mar chuid den URL mar thoradh "
"air a ghiniúint. Má tá fo-iarsmaí ama allmhairithe ag modúl den sórt sin, "
"tarlóidh na fo-iarsmaí sin."

msgid ""
"Thus it is possible for an attacker to cause unexpected code execution, "
"given the following conditions:"
msgstr ""
"Mar sin is féidir le hionsaitheoir cód a fhorghníomhú gan choinne, i "
"bhfianaise na gcoinníollacha seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"One or more views are present which construct a URL based on user input "
"(commonly, a \"next\" parameter in a querystring indicating where to "
"redirect upon successful completion of an action)."
msgstr ""
"Tá tuairimí amháin nó níos mó i láthair a thógann URL bunaithe ar ionchur "
"úsáideora (de ghnáth, paraiméadar “eile” eile i sreang fiosrúcháin a "
"léiríonn cá háit le hathatreorú nuair a bheidh gníomh críochnaithe go "
"rathúil)."

msgid ""
"One or more modules are known to an attacker to exist on the server's Python "
"import path, which perform code execution with side effects on importing."
msgstr ""
"Tá modúl amháin nó níos mó ar eolas ag ionsaitheoir ar chonair allmhairithe "
"Python an fhreastalaí, a dhéanann forghníomhú cód le fo-iarsmaí ar "
"allmhairiú."

msgid ""
"To remedy this, ``reverse()`` will now only accept and import dotted paths "
"based on the view-containing modules listed in the project's :doc:`URL "
"pattern configuration </topics/http/urls>`, so as to ensure that only "
"modules the developer intended to be imported in this fashion can or will be "
"imported."
msgstr ""
"Chun é seo a leigheas, ní ghlacfaidh `reverse () ``anois ach cosáin ponctha "
"agus a allmhairiú bunaithe ar na modúil ina bhfuil radharc atá liostaithe sa "
"tionscadal:doc: `Cumraíocht patrún URL` </topics/http/urls>, chun a chinntiú "
"nach féidir nó nach ndéanfar ach modúil an forbróir atá beartaithe a "
"allmhairiú ar an mbealach seo."

msgid "Caching of anonymous pages could reveal CSRF token"
msgstr "D'fhéadfadh taiscéáil leathanaigh gan ainm comhartha CSRF a nochtadh"

msgid ""
"Django includes both a :doc:`caching framework </topics/cache>` and a system "
"for :doc:`preventing cross-site request forgery (CSRF) attacks </ref/csrf/"
">`. The CSRF-protection system is based on a random nonce sent to the client "
"in a cookie which must be sent by the client on future requests and, in "
"forms, a hidden value which must be submitted back with the form."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn Django araon a:doc: `creat caching 'agus córas le haghaidh: doc: "
"`ionsaithe bréagaithe </topics/cache> iarratais tras-láithreáin (CSRF) a "
"chos</ref/csrf/> c'. Tá an córas cosanta CSRF bunaithe ar nonce randamach a "
"sheoltar chuig an gcliant i bhfianán a chaithfidh an cliant a sheoladh ar "
"iarratais amach anseo agus, i bhfoirmeacha, luach i bhfolach a chaithfear a "
"chur isteach ar ais leis an bhfoirm."

msgid ""
"The caching framework includes an option to cache responses to anonymous "
"(i.e., unauthenticated) clients."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn an creat taiscéála rogha chun freagraí a thaisceadh ar chliaint "
"gan ainm (ie, neamhfhíordheimhnithe)."

msgid ""
"When the first anonymous request to a given page is by a client which did "
"not have a CSRF cookie, the cache framework will also cache the CSRF cookie "
"and serve the same nonce to other anonymous clients who do not have a CSRF "
"cookie. This can allow an attacker to obtain a valid CSRF cookie value and "
"perform attacks which bypass the check for the cookie."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhíonn cliant nach raibh fianán CSRF aige an chéad iarratas gan ainm "
"chuig leathanach ar leathanach ar leathanach ar leith, déanfaidh an creat "
"taisce an fianán CSRF a thaisceadh freisin agus seirbheálfaidh an nóiméad "
"céanna do chliaint gan ainm eile nach bhfuil fianán CSRF acu. Féadann sé seo "
"ligean d'ionsaitheoir luach bailí fianán CSRF a fháil agus ionsaithe a "
"dhéanamh a sheachnóidh an seiceáil don fhianán."

msgid ""
"To remedy this, the caching framework will no longer cache such responses. "
"The heuristic for this will be:"
msgstr ""
"Chun é seo a leigheas, ní dhéanfaidh an creat taiscéála freagraí den sórt "
"sin a thuilleadh. Is é an heuristic seo ná:"

msgid "If the incoming request did not submit any cookies, and"
msgstr "Mura gcuirfeadh aon fhianáin isteach san iarratas isteach, agus"

msgid "If the response did send one or more cookies, and"
msgstr "Má chuir an freagra fianán amháin nó níos mó, agus"

msgid ""
"If the ``Vary: Cookie`` header is set on the response, then the response "
"will not be cached."
msgstr ""
"Má shocraítear an ceannteideal ``Vary: Cookie`` ar an bhfreagra, ansin ní "
"chuirfear an freagra a chosc."

msgid "MySQL typecasting"
msgstr "Cineál MySQL"

msgid ""
"The MySQL database is known to \"typecast\" on certain queries; for example, "
"when querying a table which contains string values, but using a query which "
"filters based on an integer value, MySQL will first silently coerce the "
"strings to integers and return a result based on that."
msgstr ""
"Is eol go bhfuil bunachar sonraí MySQL “typecast” ar cheisteanna áirithe; "
"mar shampla, nuair a fhiosraítear tábla ina bhfuil luachanna teaghráin, ach "
"ag baint úsáide as ceist a scagairíonn bunaithe ar luach sláimhreacha, "
"cuirfidh MySQL na teaghráin go sláimhreacha ar dtús agus toradh a thabhairt "
"ar ais bunaithe air sin."

msgid ""
"If a query is performed without first converting values to the appropriate "
"type, this can produce unexpected results, similar to what would occur if "
"the query itself had been manipulated."
msgstr ""
"Má dhéantar ceist gan luachanna a thiontú go dtí an cineál cuí ar dtús, "
"féadfaidh sé seo torthaí gan choinne a thabhairt, cosúil leis an méid a "
"tharlódh dá ndéanfaí an cheist féin a ionramháil."

msgid ""
"Django's model field classes are aware of their own types and most such "
"classes perform explicit conversion of query arguments to the correct "
"database-level type before querying. However, three model field classes did "
"not correctly convert their arguments:"
msgstr ""
"Tá ranganna réimse samhail Django ar an eolas faoina gcineálacha féin agus "
"déanann mórchuid na ranganna den sórt sin comhshó follasach argóintí "
"fiosrúcháin go dtí an cineál ceart ar leibhéal bunachar sonraí Mar sin féin, "
"níor thiontaigh trí rang réimse samhail a gcuid argóintí i gceart:"

msgid ":class:`~django.db.models.FilePathField`"
msgstr ":class: `~django.db.models.filePathfield`"

msgid ":class:`~django.db.models.GenericIPAddressField`"
msgstr ":class: `~django.db.models.genericipAddressField`"

msgid "``IPAddressField``"
msgstr "``Ipaddressfield``"

msgid ""
"These three fields have been updated to convert their arguments to the "
"correct types before querying."
msgstr ""
"Nuashonraíodh na trí réimse seo chun a n-argóintí a thiontú go dtí na "
"cineálacha cearta sula gcuirtear ceisteanna orthu."

msgid ""
"Additionally, developers of custom model fields are now warned via "
"documentation to ensure their custom field classes will perform appropriate "
"type conversions, and users of the :meth:`raw() "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.raw>` and :meth:`extra() "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.extra>` query methods -- which allow the "
"developer to supply raw SQL or SQL fragments -- will be advised to ensure "
"they perform appropriate manual type conversions prior to executing queries."
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, tugtar rabhadh anois trí dhoiciméadú chun a chinntiú go "
"ndéanfaidh a ranganna réimse saincheaptha tiontaithe cineál cuí, agus molfar "
"d'úsáideoirí mod "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.raw><django.db.models.query.QuerySet.extra>hanna "
"fiosrúcháin: meth: `raw () `agus:meth: `extra ()` - a ligeann don fhorbróir "
"blúirí SQL nó SQL a chinntiú go ndéanann siad comhshó láimhe."

msgid "Django 1.4.12 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.4.12"

msgid "*April 28, 2014*"
msgstr "*Aibreán 28, 2014*"

msgid "Django 1.4.12 fixes a regression in the 1.4.11 security release."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.4.12 aischéimniú sa scaoileadh slándála 1.4.11."

msgid ""
"Restored the ability to ``reverse()`` views created "
"using :func:`functools.partial()` (:ticket:`22486`)."
msgstr ""
"Athchóirigh sé an cumas tuairimí ``reverse () ``a cruthaíodh ag baint "
"úsáid:func: `functools.parcial () `(:ticket: `22486`)."

msgid "Django 1.4.13 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.4.13"

msgid "*May 14, 2014*"
msgstr "*Bealtaine 14, 2014*"

msgid "Django 1.4.13 fixes two security issues in 1.4.12."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.4.13 dhá shaincheist slándála i 1.4.12."

msgid "Caches may incorrectly be allowed to store and serve private data"
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfaí cead a thabhairt do chaisceanna sonraí príobháideacha a stóráil "
"agus a"

msgid ""
"In certain situations, Django may allow caches to store private data related "
"to a particular session and then serve that data to requests with a "
"different session, or no session at all. This can lead to information "
"disclosure and can be a vector for cache poisoning."
msgstr ""
"I gcásanna áirithe, féadfaidh Django cead a thabhairt do caches sonraí "
"príobháideacha a bhaineann le seisiún áirithe a stóráil agus ansin na sonraí "
"sin a sheirbheáil ar iarratais le seisiún difriúil, nó gan aon seisiún ar "
"bith. D'fhéadfadh nochtadh faisnéise a bheith mar thoradh air seo agus "
"d'fhéadfadh sé a bheith ina veicteoir le haghaidh nimhiú taisce."

msgid ""
"When using Django sessions, Django will set a ``Vary: Cookie`` header to "
"ensure caches do not serve cached data to requests from other sessions. "
"However, older versions of Internet Explorer (most likely only Internet "
"Explorer 6, and Internet Explorer 7 if run on Windows XP or Windows Server "
"2003) are unable to handle the ``Vary`` header in combination with many "
"content types. Therefore, Django would remove the header if the request was "
"made by Internet Explorer."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhíonn seisiúin Django á úsáid agat, socraíonn Django ceanntásc "
"``Vary: Cookie` chun a chinntiú nach bhfreastalaíonn caches sonraí "
"taisceáilte d'iarratais ó sheisiúin eile. Mar sin féin, níl leaganacha níos "
"sine de Internet Explorer (is dóichí nach bhfuil ach Internet Explorer 6, "
"agus Internet Explorer 7 má reáchtáiltear ar Windows XP nó Windows Server "
"2003) in ann an ceannteideal ``Vary`` a láimhseáil i gcomhcheangal le go "
"leor cineálacha ábhair. Dá bhrí sin, bainfeadh Django an ceanntásc dá "
"ndéanfadh Internet Explorer an t-iarraidh."

msgid ""
"To remedy this, the special behavior for these older Internet Explorer "
"versions has been removed, and the ``Vary`` header is no longer stripped "
"from the response. In addition, modifications to the ``Cache-Control`` "
"header for all Internet Explorer requests with a ``Content-Disposition`` "
"header have also been removed as they were found to have similar issues."
msgstr ""
"Chun é seo a leigheas, baineadh an t-iompar speisialta do na leaganacha níos "
"sine Internet Explorer seo, agus ní dhéantar an ceanntásc `Vary` a bhaint as "
"an bhfreagra a thuilleadh. Ina theannta sin, baineadh modhnuithe ar an "
"gceanntásc ``Cache-Control` do gach iarratas Internet Explorer le "
"ceannteideal ``Content-Disposition` toisc gur fuarthas go raibh "
"saincheisteanna comhchosúla acu."

msgid "Malformed redirect URLs from user input not correctly validated"
msgstr ""
"URLanna atreoraithe mífheidhmithe ó ionchur úsáideora nach bhfuil bailíochtú "
"i gceart"

msgid ""
"The validation for redirects did not correctly validate some malformed URLs, "
"which are accepted by some browsers. This allows a user to be redirected to "
"an unsafe URL unexpectedly."
msgstr ""
"Níor bhailíochnaigh an bailíochtú le haghaidh atreoruithe roinnt URLanna "
"mífhoirmithe i gceart, a nglacann roinnt brabhsálaithe leo. Ligeann sé seo "
"úsáideoir a atreorú chuig URL neamhshábháilte gan choinne."

msgid ""
"Django relies on user input in some cases (e.g. "
"``django.contrib.auth.views.login()``, ``django.contrib.comments``, "
"and :doc:`i18n </topics/i18n/index>`) to redirect the user to an \"on "
"success\" URL. The security checks for these redirects (namely "
"``django.utils.http.is_safe_url()``) did not correctly validate some "
"malformed URLs, such as ``http:\\\\\\\\\\\\djangoproject.com``, which are "
"accepted by some browsers with more liberal URL parsing."
msgstr ""
"Braitheann Django ar ionchur úsáideora i roinnt cásanna (m.sh. "
"``django.contrib.auth.views.login () ``, ``django.contrib.comments``, "
"agus:doc: `i18n`) chun an t-úsáideoir a atreorú chuig URL “ar rath </topics/"
"i18n/index>”. Níor bhailíodh na seiceálacha slándála do na haatreoruithe seo "
"(eadhon ``django.utils.http.is_safe_url () ``) roinnt URLanna "
"míchfhoirmithe, mar shampla ``http:\\\\\\\\\\\\ djangoproject.com``, a "
"ghlacann roinnt brabhsálaithe le parsáil URL níos liobrálacha."

msgid ""
"To remedy this, the validation in ``is_safe_url()`` has been tightened to be "
"able to handle and correctly validate these malformed URLs."
msgstr ""
"Chun é seo a leigheas, rinneadh an bailíochtú in ``is_safe_url () ``níos "
"doichte chun a bheith in ann na URLanna míchfhoirmithe seo a láimhseáil agus "
"a bhailíochtú i gceart."

msgid "Django 1.4.14 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.4.14"

msgid "*August 20, 2014*"
msgstr "*20 Lúnasa, 2014*"

msgid "Django 1.4.14 fixes several security issues in 1.4.13."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.4.14 roinnt saincheisteanna slándála i 1.4.13."

msgid "``reverse()`` could generate URLs pointing to other hosts"
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh ``reverse () ``URLanna a ghiniúint ag díriú chuig óstach eile"

msgid ""
"In certain situations, URL reversing could generate scheme-relative URLs  "
"(URLs starting with two slashes), which could unexpectedly redirect a user  "
"to a different host. An attacker could exploit this, for example, by "
"redirecting users to a phishing site designed to ask for user's passwords."
msgstr ""
"I gcásanna áirithe, d'fhéadfadh aisiompú URLanna URLanna a bhaineann le "
"scéim a ghiniúint (URLanna ag tosú le dhá slashes), rud a d'fhéadfadh "
"úsáideoir a atreorú chuig óstach difriúil gan choinne. D'fhéadfadh "
"ionsaitheoir leas a bhaint as seo, mar shampla, trí úsáideoirí a atreorú "
"chuig suíomh fiasc atá deartha chun pasfhocail úsáideora a iarraidh."

msgid ""
"To remedy this, URL reversing now ensures that no URL starts with two "
"slashes (//), replacing the second slash with its URL encoded counterpart "
"(%2F). This approach ensures that semantics stay the same, while making the "
"URL relative to the domain and not to the scheme."
msgstr ""
"Chun é seo a leigheas, cinntíonn aisiompú URL anois nach dtosaíonn aon URL "
"le dhá slashes (//), ag cur a mhacasamhail ionchódaithe URL (%2F) in ionad "
"an dara slash. Cinntíonn an cur chuige seo go bhfanann séimeantaic mar an "
"gcéanna, agus an URL á ndéanamh i gcoibhneas leis an bhfearann agus ní leis "
"an scéim."

msgid "File upload denial-of-service"
msgstr "Diúltú seirbhíse a uaslódáil comhad"

msgid ""
"Before this release, Django's file upload handing in its default "
"configuration may degrade to producing a huge number of ``os.stat()`` system "
"calls when a duplicate filename is uploaded. Since ``stat()`` may invoke IO, "
"this may produce a huge data-dependent slowdown that slowly worsens over "
"time. The net result is that given enough time, a user with the ability to "
"upload files can cause poor performance in the upload handler, eventually "
"causing it to become very slow simply by uploading 0-byte files. At this "
"point, even a slow network connection and few HTTP requests would be all "
"that is necessary to make a site unavailable."
msgstr ""
"Roimh an scaoileadh seo, féadfaidh uaslódáil comhad Django ina chumraíocht "
"réamhshocraithe a dhíghrádú chun líon mór glaonna chórais `os.stat () `a "
"tháirgeadh nuair a uaslódálfar ainm comhaid dúblach. Ós rud é go bhféadfadh "
"``stat () ``IO a ghairm, d'fhéadfadh sé seo moilliú ollmhór atá ag brath ar "
"shonraí a tháirgeann in olcas go mall le himeacht ama. Is é an toradh glan "
"ná gur féidir le húsáideoir a bhfuil sé de chumas comhaid a uaslódáil droch-"
"fheidhmíocht sa láimhseálaí uaslódála mar thoradh ar dóthain ama, rud a "
"fhágann go mbeidh sé an-mhall sa deireadh ach trí chomhaid 0-byte a "
"uaslódáil. Ag an bpointe seo, ní bheadh fiú nasc líonra mall agus mórán "
"iarratais HTTP riachtanach chun suíomh a chur ar fáil."

msgid ""
"We've remedied the issue by changing the algorithm for generating file names "
"if a file with the uploaded name already "
"exists. :meth:`Storage.get_available_name() "
"<django.core.files.storage.Storage.get_available_name>` now appends an "
"underscore plus a random 7 character alphanumeric string (e.g. "
"``\"_x3a1gho\"``), rather than iterating through an underscore followed by a "
"number (e.g. ``\"_1\"``, ``\"_2\"``, etc.)."
msgstr ""
"Rinneamar an cheist a leigheas tríd an algartam a athrú chun ainmneacha "
"comhaid a ghiniúint má tá comhad leis an ainm uaslódáilte ann cheana "
"féin. :meth: Cuireann `Storage.get_available_name () "
"<django.core.files.storage.Storage.get_available_name>`béim anois móide "
"sreang alfauméireach randamach 7 charachtar (m.sh. ``\"_x3a1gho\"``), "
"seachas athrá trí bhuscór ina dhiaidh sin uimhir (m.sh. ``\"_1\"``, `_2\"``, "
"srl.)."

msgid "``RemoteUserMiddleware`` session hijacking"
msgstr "Fuadach seisiún ``RemoteUserMiddleWare``"

msgid ""
"When using the :class:`~django.contrib.auth.middleware.RemoteUserMiddleware` "
"and the ``RemoteUserBackend``, a change to the ``REMOTE_USER`` header "
"between requests without an intervening logout could result in the prior "
"user's session being co-opted by the subsequent user. The middleware now "
"logs the user out on a failed login attempt."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a úsáidtear an:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.middleware.remoteUserMiddleware` agus an "
"`RemoteUserBackend``, d'fhéadfadh athrú ar an gceannteideal `REMOTE_USER`` "
"idir iarratais gan logáil isteach idirghabhála go ndéanfadh an t-úsáideoir "
"ina dhiaidh sin comhoghnú seisiún an úsáideora roimhe seo. Déanann an "
"middleware an t-úsáideoir a logáil amach anois ar iarracht logála isteach "
"theip air."

msgid "Data leakage via query string manipulation in ``contrib.admin``"
msgstr ""
"Sceitheadh sonraí trí ionramháil teaghrán fiosrúcháin i ``contrib.admin ``"

msgid ""
"In older versions of Django it was possible to reveal any field's data by "
"modifying the \"popup\" and \"to_field\" parameters of the query string on "
"an admin change form page. For example, requesting a URL like ``/admin/auth/"
"user/?pop=1&t=password`` and viewing the page's HTML allowed viewing the "
"password hash of each user. While the admin requires users to have "
"permissions to view the change form pages in the first place, this could "
"leak data if you rely on users having access to view only certain fields on "
"a model."
msgstr ""
"I leaganacha níos sine de Django bhíothas in ann sonraí aon réimse a "
"nochtadh trí na paraiméadair \"aníos\" agus \"to_field\" den teaghrán "
"fiosrúcháin a mhodhnú ar leathanach foirm athraithe riaracháin. Mar shampla, "
"le URL mar ``/ admin/auth/user/?pop=1&t=password`` agus ag féachaint ar HTML "
"an leathanaigh ceadaíodh féachaint ar hash pasfhocail gach úsáideoir. Cé go "
"n-éilíonn an riarthóir cead a bheith ag úsáideoirí féachaint ar leathanaigh "
"na bhfoirm athraithe ar an gcéad dul síos, d'fhéadfadh sé seo sonraí a "
"sceitheadh ​​​​má tá tú ag brath ar rochtain a bheith ag úsáideoirí chun "
"féachaint ar réimsí áirithe ar shamhail amháin."

msgid ""
"To address the issue, an exception will now be raised if a ``to_field`` "
"value that isn't a related field to a model that has been registered with "
"the admin is specified."
msgstr ""
"Chun aghaidh a thabhairt ar an saincheist, ardófar eisceacht anois má "
"shonraítear luach ``to_field` nach réimse gaolmhar é le samhail atá "
"cláraithe leis an riarachán."

msgid "Django 1.4.15 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.4.15"

msgid "*September 2, 2014*"
msgstr "*Meán Fómhair 2, 2014*"

msgid "Django 1.4.15 fixes a regression in the 1.4.14 security release."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.4.15 aischéimniú sa scaoileadh slándála 1.4.14."

msgid ""
"Allowed inherited and m2m fields to be referenced in the admin "
"(:ticket:`22486`)"
msgstr ""
"Ceadaítear do réimsí oidhreachta agus m2m a thagairt sa riarachán (:ticket: "
"`22486`)"

msgid "Django 1.4.16 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.4.16"

msgid "*October 22, 2014*"
msgstr "*Deireadh Fómhair 22, 2014*"

msgid ""
"Django 1.4.16 fixes a couple regressions in the 1.4.14 security release and "
"a bug preventing the use of some GEOS versions with GeoDjango."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.4.16 cúpla aischéimniú sa scaoileadh slándála 1.4.14 agus "
"fabht a chuireann cosc ar roinnt leaganacha GEOS a úsáid le GeodJango."

msgid ""
"Allowed related many-to-many fields to be referenced in the admin "
"(:ticket:`23604`)."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaítear tagairt a thabhairt do go leor réimsí gaolmhara sa riarachán "
"(:ticket: `23604`)."

msgid "Allowed inline and hidden references to admin fields (:ticket:`23431`)."
msgstr ""
"Tagairtí inlíne agus i bhfolach ceadaithe do réimsí riaracháin (:ticket: "
"`23431`)."

msgid "Fixed parsing of the GEOS version string (:ticket:`20036`)."
msgstr "Parsáil sheasta ar an teaghrán leagan GEOS (: ticéad: `20036`)."

msgid "Django 1.4.17 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.4.17"

msgid "*January 2, 2015*"
msgstr "*2 Eanáir, 2015*"

msgid "Django 1.4.17 fixes a regression in the 1.4.14 security release."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.4.17 aischéimniú sa scaoileadh slándála 1.4.14."

msgid ""
"Additionally, Django's vendored version of six, ``django.utils.six``, has "
"been upgraded to the latest release (1.9.0)."
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, tá leagan díolta Django de sé, ``django.utils.six ``, "
"uasghrádaithe go dtí an eisiúint is déanaí (1.9.0)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression with dynamically generated inlines and allowed field "
"references in the admin (:ticket:`23754`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú le línte a ghintear go dinimiciúil agus tagairtí "
"allamuigh ceadaithe sa riarachán (:ticket: `23754`)."

msgid "Django 1.4.18 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.4.18"

msgid "*January 13, 2015*"
msgstr "*13 Eanáir, 2015*"

msgid ""
"Django 1.4.18 fixes several security issues in 1.4.17 as well as a "
"regression on Python 2.5 in the 1.4.17 release."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.4.18 roinnt saincheisteanna slándála i 1.4.17 chomh maith "
"le aischéimniú ar Python 2.5 sa scaoileadh 1.4.17."

msgid "WSGI header spoofing via underscore/dash conflation"
msgstr "Ceanntásc WSGI trí chomhcheangal fo-scór/dash"

msgid ""
"When HTTP headers are placed into the WSGI environ, they are normalized by "
"converting to uppercase, converting all dashes to underscores, and "
"prepending ``HTTP_``. For instance, a header ``X-Auth-User`` would become "
"``HTTP_X_AUTH_USER`` in the WSGI environ (and thus also in Django's "
"``request.META`` dictionary)."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a chuirtear ceanntásca HTTP isteach sa timpeallacht WSGI, déantar iad "
"a normalú trí thiontú go uachchlitreacha, gach ceann a thiontú go béim, agus "
"`HTTP_`` a réamhfheidhmiú. Mar shampla, bheadh ceannteideal ``X-Auth-User`` "
"ina `HTTP_X_AUTH_USER`` sa timpeallacht WSGI (agus dá bhrí sin freisin i "
"bhfoclóir ``request.meta`` Django)."

msgid ""
"Unfortunately, this means that the WSGI environ cannot distinguish between "
"headers containing dashes and headers containing underscores: ``X-Auth-"
"User`` and ``X-Auth_User`` both become ``HTTP_X_AUTH_USER``. This means that "
"if a header is used in a security-sensitive way (for instance, passing "
"authentication information along from a front-end proxy), even if the proxy "
"carefully strips any incoming value for ``X-Auth-User``, an attacker may be "
"able to provide an ``X-Auth_User`` header (with underscore) and bypass this "
"protection."
msgstr ""
"Ar an drochuair, ciallaíonn sé seo nach féidir leis an timpeallacht WSGI "
"idirdhealú a dhéanamh idir ceanntásca ina bhfuil ceanntáin agus ceanntásca "
"ina bhfuil béim: ``X-Auth-User`` agus ``X-Auth_User`` araon ina "
"``HTTP_X_AUTH_USER``. Ciallaíonn sé seo má úsáidtear ceanntásc ar bhealach "
"íogair ó shlándáil (mar shampla, faisnéis fíordheimhnithe a chur ar "
"sheachfhreastalaí tosaigh), fiú má bhíonn an seachfhreastalaí luach ag "
"teacht isteach ar `X-Auth-User`` go cúramach, d'fhéadfadh go mbeadh "
"ionsaitheoir in ann ceannteideal `X-Auth_User`` a sholáthar agus an chosaint "
"seo."

msgid ""
"In order to prevent such attacks, both Nginx and Apache 2.4+ strip all "
"headers containing underscores from incoming requests by default. Django's "
"built-in development server now does the same. Django's development server "
"is not recommended for production use, but matching the behavior of common "
"production servers reduces the surface area for behavior changes during "
"deployment."
msgstr ""
"D'fhonn ionsaithe den sórt sin a chosc, scriosann Nginx agus Apache 2.4+ "
"gach ceanntásc ina bhfuil béim ó iarratais ag teacht isteach de réir "
"réamhshocraithe. Déanann freastalaí forbartha ionsuite Django an rud céanna "
"anois. Ní mholtar freastalaí forbartha Django le húsáid táirgeachta, ach "
"laghdaíonn meaitseáil iompar freastalaithe táirgeachta coitianta an t-achar "
"dromchla le haghaidh athruithe iompraíochta le linn imscartha."

msgid "Mitigated possible XSS attack via user-supplied redirect URLs"
msgstr ""
"Ionsaí XSS féideartha a mhaolú trí URLanna atreoraithe a sholáthraíonn an "
"úsáide"

msgid ""
"Django relies on user input in some cases (e.g. "
"``django.contrib.auth.views.login()`` and :doc:`i18n </topics/i18n/index>`) "
"to redirect the user to an \"on success\" URL. The security checks for these "
"redirects (namely ``django.utils.http.is_safe_url()``) didn't strip leading "
"whitespace on the tested URL and as such considered URLs like "
"``\\njavascript:...`` safe. If a developer relied on ``is_safe_url()`` to "
"provide safe redirect targets and put such a URL into a link, they could "
"suffer from a XSS attack. This bug doesn't affect Django currently, since we "
"only put this URL into the ``Location`` response header and browsers seem to "
"ignore JavaScript there."
msgstr ""
"Braitheann Django ar ionchur úsáideora i roinnt cásanna (m.sh. "
"``django.contrib.auth.views.login () ``agus:doc: `i18n`) chun an t-úsáideoir "
"a atreorú chuig URL “ar rath”. </topics/i18n/index> Níor scriosadh na "
"seiceálacha slándála do na haatreoruithe seo (eadhon "
"``django.utils.http.is_safe_url () ``) spás bán tosaigh ar an URL tástáilte "
"agus mar sin meastar go bhfuil URLanna mar``\\ n javascript:... ``sábháilte. "
"Má bhí forbróir ag brath ar ``is_safe_url () ``chun spriocanna athsheolta "
"sábháilte a sholáthar agus URL den sórt sin a chur i nasc, d'fhéadfadh siad "
"a bheith ag fulaingt ó ionsaí XSS. Ní chuireann an fabht seo i bhfeidhm ar "
"Django faoi láthair, ós rud é nach gcuirimid an URL seo ach sa cheannteideal "
"freagartha ``Suíomh ``agus is cosúil go ndéanann brabhsálaithe neamhaird ar "
"JavaScript ansin."

msgid "Denial-of-service attack against ``django.views.static.serve``"
msgstr "Ionsaí diúltaithe seirbhíse i gcoinne ``django.views.static.serve``"

msgid ""
"In older versions of Django, the :func:`django.views.static.serve` view read "
"the files it served one line at a time. Therefore, a big file with no "
"newlines would result in memory usage equal to the size of that file. An "
"attacker could exploit this and launch a denial-of-service attack by "
"simultaneously requesting many large files. This view now reads the file in "
"chunks to prevent large memory usage."
msgstr ""
"I leaganacha níos sine de Django, léigh an amharc: func: "
"`django.views.static.serve` na comhaid a d'fhreastail sé líne amháin ag an "
"am. Dá bhrí sin, bheadh úsáid cuimhne cothrom le méid an chomhaid sin mar "
"thoradh ar chomhad mór gan aon línte nua. D'fhéadfadh ionsaitheoir leas a "
"bhaint as seo agus ionsaí diúltaithe seirbhíse a sheoladh trí go leor "
"comhaid mhóra a iarraidh ag Léann an dearcadh seo anois an comhad i gcodanna "
"chun úsáid mór cuimhne a chosc."

msgid ""
"Note, however, that this view has always carried a warning that it is not "
"hardened for production use and should be used only as a development aid. "
"Now may be a good time to audit your project and serve your files in "
"production using a real front-end web server if you are not doing so."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara, áfach, go raibh rabhadh i gcónaí ag an dearcadh seo nach "
"bhfuil sé cruaite le haghaidh úsáide táirgeachta agus gur chóir é a úsáid "
"ach mar chúnamh forbartha. B'fhéidir gur am maith é anois do thionscadal a "
"iniúchadh agus freastal ar do chuid comhad i dtáirgeadh ag baint úsáide as "
"fíor-fhreastalaí gréasáin tosaigh mura bhfuil tú ag déanamh amhlaidh."

msgid ""
"To maintain compatibility with Python 2.5, Django's vendored version of six, "
"``django.utils.six``, has been downgraded to 1.8.0 which is the last version "
"to support Python 2.5."
msgstr ""
"Chun comhoiriúnacht le Python 2.5 a choinneáil, íosghrádaíodh leagan Django "
"de sé, ``django.utils.six``, go 1.8.0 arb é an leagan deireanach chun tacú "
"le Python 2.5."

msgid "Django 1.4.19 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.4.19"

msgid "*January 27, 2015*"
msgstr "*27 Eanáir, 2015*"

msgid "Django 1.4.19 fixes a regression in the 1.4.18 security release."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.4.19 aischéimniú sa scaoileadh slándála 1.4.18."

msgid ""
"``GZipMiddleware`` now supports streaming responses. As part of the 1.4.18 "
"security release, the ``django.views.static.serve()`` function was altered "
"to stream the files it serves. Unfortunately, the ``GZipMiddleware`` "
"consumed the stream prematurely and prevented files from being served "
"properly (:ticket:`24158`)."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn ``GZipMiddleware ``le freagraí sruthú anois. Mar chuid den "
"scaoileadh slándála 1.4.18, athraíodh an fheidhm ``django.views.static.serve "
"() `chun na comhaid a fhreastalaíonn sé a shruthlú. Ar an drochuair, d'ith "
"an `GzipMiddleware`` an sruth roimh am agus chuir sé cosc ar chomhaid a "
"sheirbheáil i gceart (:ticket: `24158`)."

msgid "Django 1.4.2 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.4.2"

msgid "This is the second security release in the Django 1.4 series."
msgstr "Is é seo an dara eisiúint slándála sa tsraith Django 1.4."

msgid ""
"The newly introduced :class:`~django.db.models.GenericIPAddressField` "
"constructor arguments have been adapted to match those of all other model "
"fields. The first two keyword arguments are now verbose_name and name."
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh na hargóintí tógálaí:class: "
"`~django.db.models.genericiPaddressField` nua-tugadh isteach in oiriúint "
"chun iad siúd a bhaineann le gach réimse samhail eile a mheaitseáil. Is é an "
"chéad dá argóint eochairfhocal anois verbose_name agus ainm."

msgid "Other bugfixes and changes"
msgstr "Buigdheisiúcháin agus athruithe eile"

msgid "Subclass HTMLParser only for appropriate Python versions (#18239)."
msgstr "Fo-aicme HTMLParser amháin le haghaidh leaganacha Python cuí (#18239)."

msgid "Added batch_size argument to qs.bulk_create() (#17788)."
msgstr "Cuireadh argóint batch_size leis qs.bulk_create () (#17788)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a small regression in the admin filters where wrongly formatted dates "
"passed as url parameters caused an unhandled ValidationError (#18530)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú beag sna scagairí riaracháin inar chuaigh dátaí "
"formáidithe go mícheart mar pharaiméadair url ba chúis le ValidationError "
"neamhláimhseáilte (#18530)."

msgid ""
"Fixed an endless loop bug when accessing permissions in templates (#18979)"
msgstr ""
"Socraigh fabht lúb gan deireadh agus tú ag rochtain ar cheadanna i "
"dteimpléid (#18979)"

msgid "Fixed some Python 2.5 compatibility issues"
msgstr "Socraigh roinnt saincheisteanna comhoiriúnachta"

msgid ""
"Fixed an issue with quoted filenames in Content-Disposition header (#19006)"
msgstr ""
"Socraigh saincheist le hainmneacha comhaid luaite i gceannteideal "
"Diúspóireacht Ábhar (#19006)"

msgid ""
"Made the context option in ``trans`` and ``blocktrans`` tags accept literals "
"wrapped in single quotes (#18881)."
msgstr ""
"Rinne an rogha comhthéacs i gclibeanna ``trans`` agus `blocktrans`` glacadh "
"le litríochtaí atá fillte i luachana aonair (#18881)."

msgid "Numerous documentation improvements and fixes."
msgstr "Feabhsuithe agus ceartúcháin iomadúla doiciméadúcháin."

msgid "Django 1.4.20 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.4.20"

msgid "*March 18, 2015*"
msgstr "*18 Márta, 2015*"

msgid "Django 1.4.20 fixes one security issue in 1.4.19."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.4.20 saincheist slándála amháin i 1.4.19."

msgid ""
"Django relies on user input in some cases (e.g. "
"``django.contrib.auth.views.login()`` and :doc:`i18n </topics/i18n/index>`) "
"to redirect the user to an \"on success\" URL. The security checks for these "
"redirects (namely ``django.utils.http.is_safe_url()``) accepted URLs with "
"leading control characters and so considered URLs like "
"``\\x08javascript:...`` safe. This issue doesn't affect Django currently, "
"since we only put this URL into the ``Location`` response header and "
"browsers seem to ignore JavaScript there. Browsers we tested also treat URLs "
"prefixed with control characters such as ``%08//example.com`` as relative "
"paths so redirection to an unsafe target isn't a problem either."
msgstr ""
"Braitheann Django ar ionchur úsáideora i roinnt cásanna (m.sh. "
"``django.contrib.auth.views.login () ``agus:doc: `i18n`) chun an t-úsáideoir "
"a atreorú chuig URL “ar rath”. </topics/i18n/index> Ghlac na seiceálacha "
"slándála do na haatreoruithe seo (eadhon ``django.utils.http.is_safe_url () "
"``) le URLanna le príomhcharachtair rialaithe agus mar sin mheas go bhfuil "
"URLanna mar``\\ x08javascript:... ``sábháilte. Ní chuireann an tsaincheist "
"seo i bhfeidhm ar Django faoi láthair, ós rud é nach gcuirimid an URL seo "
"ach sa cheanntásc freagartha ``Suíomh ``agus is cosúil go ndéanann "
"brabhsálaithe neamhaird ar JavaScript ansin. Déileálann brabhsálaithe a "
"ndearna muid tástáil orthu URLanna a réamhshocraithe le carachtair rialaithe "
"mar `%08//example.com`` mar chosáin choibhneasta mar sin ní fadhb í an "
"athatreorú chuig sprioc neamhshábháilte ach an oiread."

msgid ""
"However, if a developer relies on ``is_safe_url()`` to provide safe redirect "
"targets and puts such a URL into a link, they could suffer from an XSS "
"attack as some browsers such as Google Chrome ignore control characters at "
"the start of a URL in an anchor ``href``."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, má bhraitheann forbróir ar ``is_safe_url () ``chun spriocanna "
"athsheolta sábháilte a sholáthar agus go gcuireann siad URL den sórt sin i "
"nasc, d'fhéadfadh ionsaí XSS a bheith ag fulaingt mar roinnt brabhsálaithe "
"mar Google Chrome neamhaird le carachtair rialaithe ag tús URL in ancaire "
"``href``."

msgid "Django 1.4.21 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.4.21"

msgid "*July 8, 2015*"
msgstr "*8 Iúil, 2015*"

msgid "Django 1.4.21 fixes several security issues in 1.4.20."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.4.21 roinnt saincheisteanna slándála i 1.4.20."

msgid "Denial-of-service possibility by filling session store"
msgstr "Féidearthacht seirbhíse a dhiúltú trí siopa seisiúin a"

msgid ""
"In previous versions of Django, the session backends created a new empty "
"record in the session storage anytime ``request.session`` was accessed and "
"there was a session key provided in the request cookies that didn't already "
"have a session record. This could allow an attacker to easily create many "
"new session records simply by sending repeated requests with unknown session "
"keys, potentially filling up the session store or causing other users' "
"session records to be evicted."
msgstr ""
"I leaganacha roimhe seo de Django, chruthaigh na hiasail seisiúin taifead "
"folamh nua sa stóras seisiúin am ar bith a ndearnadh rochtain ar "
"``request.session`` agus cuireadh eochair seisiúin ar fáil sna fianáin "
"iarratais nach raibh taifead seisiúin acu cheana féin. D'fhéadfadh sé seo "
"ligean d'ionsaitheoir go leor taifead seisiúin nua a chruthú go héasca go "
"simplí trí iarratais arís agus arís eile a sheoladh le heochracha seisiúin "
"anaithnid, d'fhéadfadh go líonfadh siad stór an tseisiúin nó go ndéanfaí "
"taifid seisiúin úsáideoirí eile a dhíshealbhú."

msgid ""
"The built-in session backends now create a session record only if the "
"session is actually modified; empty session records are not created. Thus "
"this potential DoS is now only possible if the site chooses to expose a "
"session-modifying view to anonymous users."
msgstr ""
"Ní chruthaíonn na cúltaca seisiúin ionsuite taifead seisiúin anois ach "
"amháin má dhéantar an seisiún a mhodhnú i ndáiríre; ní chruthaítear taifid "
"Dá bhrí sin ní féidir an DoS féideartha seo a dhéanamh anois ach má "
"roghnaíonn an suíomh dearcadh modhnaithe seisiún a nochtadh d'úsáideoirí gan "
"ainm."

msgid ""
"As each built-in session backend was fixed separately (rather than a fix in "
"the core sessions framework), maintainers of third-party session backends "
"should check whether the same vulnerability is present in their backend and "
"correct it if so."
msgstr ""
"Toisc go socraíodh gach cúltaca seisiúin ionsuite ar leithligh (seachas "
"socrú i gcreat croí-sheisiúin), ba cheart do chothabhálaí cúltaca seisiúin "
"tríú páirtí a sheiceáil an bhfuil an leochaileacht chéanna i láthair ina "
"gcúltaca agus é a cheartú más amhlaidh."

msgid "Header injection possibility since validators accept newlines in input"
msgstr ""
"Féidearthacht insteallta ceanntásc ós rud é go nglacann bailíochtóirí lín"

msgid ""
"Some of Django's built-in validators "
"(:class:`~django.core.validators.EmailValidator`, most seriously) didn't "
"prohibit newline characters (due to the usage of ``$`` instead of ``\\Z`` in "
"the regular expressions). If you use values with newlines in HTTP response "
"or email headers, you can suffer from header injection attacks. Django "
"itself isn't vulnerable because :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse` and the "
"mail sending utilities in :mod:`django.core.mail` prohibit newlines in HTTP "
"and SMTP headers, respectively. While the validators have been fixed in "
"Django, if you're creating HTTP responses or email messages in other ways, "
"it's a good idea to ensure that those methods prohibit newlines as well. You "
"might also want to validate that any existing data in your application "
"doesn't contain unexpected newlines."
msgstr ""
"Níor chuir cuid de bhailíochtóirí ionsuite Django (:class: "
"`~django.core.validators.emailValidator`, go dáiríre) cosc ar charachtair "
"líne nua (mar gheall ar úsáid ``$`` in ionad ``\\ Z`` sna nathanna rialta). "
"Má úsáideann tú luachanna le línte nua i gceanntásca freagra HTTP nó "
"ríomhphoist, féadfaidh ionsaithe insteallta ceanntásc a fhulaingt Níl Django "
"féin leochaileach toisc go gcuireann: class: `~django.http.HttpResponse` "
"agus cosc ar na fóntais seolta ríomhphoist in:mod: `django.core.mail` línte "
"nua i gceanntásca HTTP agus SMTP, faoi seach. Cé go bhfuil na bailíochtóirí "
"socraithe i Django, má tá freagraí HTTP nó teachtaireachtaí ríomhphoist á "
"chruthú agat ar bhealaí eile, is smaoineamh maith é a chinntiú go gcuireann "
"na modhanna sin cosc ar líne nua freisin. B'fhéidir gur mhaith leat a "
"bhailíochtú freisin nach bhfuil línte nua gan choinne ag aon sonraí atá ann "
"cheana i d'iarratas."

msgid ""
":func:`~django.core.validators.validate_ipv4_address`, :func:`~django.core.validators.validate_slug`, "
"and :class:`~django.core.validators.URLValidator` and their usage in the "
"corresponding form fields ``GenericIPAddresseField``, ``IPAddressField``, "
"``SlugField``, and ``URLField`` are also affected."
msgstr ""
":func: `~django.core.validators.validate_ipv4_address`, :func: "
"`~django.core.validators.validate_slug`, agus:class: "
"`~django.core.validators.urlvalidator` agus a n-úsáid sna réimsí foirmeacha "
"comhfhreagracha ``GenericipAddresseField``, `iPadsfield` Bíonn tionchar ag "
"Eld``, `Slugfield``, agus ``URLField`` freisin."

msgid ""
"The undocumented, internally unused ``validate_integer()`` function is now "
"stricter as it validates using a regular expression instead of simply "
"casting the value using ``int()`` and checking if an exception was raised."
msgstr ""
"Tá an fheidhm ``validate_integer () ``neamhdhoiciméadaithe, neamhúsáidte go "
"hinmheánach níos déine anois mar a bhailíochnaíonn sé abairt rialta a úsáid "
"in ionad an luach a chaitheamh ag baint úsáide as ``int ()`` agus seiceáil "
"an ardaíodh eisceacht."

msgid "Django 1.4.22 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.4.22"

msgid "*August 18, 2015*"
msgstr "*18 Lúnasa, 2015*"

msgid "Django 1.4.22 fixes a security issue in 1.4.21."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.4.22 saincheist slándála i 1.4.21."

msgid ""
"It also fixes support with pip 7+ by disabling wheel support. Older versions "
"of 1.4 would silently build a broken wheel when installed with those "
"versions of pip."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn sé tacaíocht le pip 7+ freisin trí thacaíocht roth a dhíchumasú. "
"Tógfadh leaganacha níos sine de 1.4 roth briste go ciúin nuair a bhíonn siad "
"suiteáilte leis na leaganacha sin de phíopa."

msgid ""
"Denial-of-service possibility in ``logout()`` view by filling session store"
msgstr ""
"Féidearthacht seirbhíse a dhiúltú i “logáil amach ()” amharc trí stór "
"seisiúin a líonadh"

msgid ""
"Previously, a session could be created when anonymously accessing the "
"``django.contrib.auth.views.logout()`` view (provided it wasn't decorated "
"with :func:`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.login_required` as done in the "
"admin). This could allow an attacker to easily create many new session "
"records by sending repeated requests, potentially filling up the session "
"store or causing other users' session records to be evicted."
msgstr ""
"Roimhe seo, d'fhéadfaí seisiún a chruthú agus rochtain gan ainm ar an "
"radharc ``django.contrib.auth.views.logout()`` (ar choinníoll nach raibh sé "
"maisithe le :func:`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.login_required` mar a "
"dhéantar sa admin). D'fhéadfadh sé seo ligean d'ionsaitheoir go leor taifead "
"seisiúin nua a chruthú go héasca trí iarratais arís agus arís eile a "
"sheoladh, d'fhéadfadh go mbeadh an stór seisiún á líonadh nó go ndéanfaí "
"taifid seisiúin úsáideoirí eile a dhíshealbhú."

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.contrib.sessions.middleware.SessionMiddleware` has been "
"modified to no longer create empty session records, including "
"when :setting:`SESSION_SAVE_EVERY_REQUEST` is active."
msgstr ""
"Athraíodh an: Class: `~django.contrib.sessions.middleware.sessionMiddleware` "
"chun gan taifid seisiúin folamh a chruthú a thuilleadh, lena n-áirítear "
"nuai:setting: `SESSION_SAVE_EVERY_REQUEST` gníomhach."

msgid ""
"Additionally, the ``contrib.sessions.backends.base.SessionBase.flush()`` and "
"``cache_db.SessionStore.flush()`` methods have been modified to avoid "
"creating a new empty session. Maintainers of third-party session backends "
"should check if the same vulnerability is present in their backend and "
"correct it if so."
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, modhnaíodh na modhanna "
"``Contrib.sessions.backends.base.sessionBase.flush () ``agus "
"``Cache_db.sessionStore.flush ()`` chun seisiún folamh nua a chruthú a "
"sheachaint. Ba chóir do chothabhálaí cúltaca seisiúin tríú páirtí a "
"sheiceáil an bhfuil an leochaileacht chéanna i láthair ina gcúltaca agus é a "
"cheartú más amhlaidh."

msgid "Django 1.4.3 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.4.3"

msgid ""
"Django 1.4.3 addresses two security issues present in previous Django "
"releases in the 1.4 series."
msgstr ""
"Tugann Django 1.4.3 aghaidh ar dhá shaincheist slándála i láthair in "
"eisiúintí Django roimhe seo sa tsraith 1.4."

msgid "Django 1.4.4 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.4.4"

msgid ""
"Django 1.4.4 fixes four security issues present in previous Django releases "
"in the 1.4 series, as well as several other bugs and numerous documentation "
"improvements."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.4.4 ceithre shaincheist slándála a bhí i láthair in "
"eisiúintí Django roimhe seo sa tsraith 1.4, chomh maith le roinnt bugs eile "
"agus feabhsuithe iomadúla doiciméadú."

msgid "This is the fourth bugfix/security release in the Django 1.4 series."
msgstr "Is é seo an ceathrú eisiúint bugfix/slándála sa tsraith Django 1.4."

msgid ""
"For this reason, Django 1.4.4 adds a new setting, ``ALLOWED_HOSTS``, "
"containing an explicit list of valid host/domain names for this site. A "
"request with a Host header not matching an entry in this list will raise "
"``SuspiciousOperation`` if ``request.get_host()`` is called. For full "
"details see the documentation for the :setting:`ALLOWED_HOSTS` setting."
msgstr ""
"Ar an gcúis seo, cuireann Django 1.4.4 socrú nua leis, `ALLOWED_HOSTS`, ina "
"bhfuil liosta sainráite d'ainmneacha bailí óstach/fearainn don láithreán "
"seo. Ardóidh iarratas le ceanntásc Óstach nach bhfuil iontráil sa liosta seo "
"ag teacht ar ```ConsumciousOperation`` má thugtar ``request.get_host () ``. "
"Le haghaidh sonraí iomlána féach an doiciméadú don socrú: setting: "
"`ALLOWED_HOSTS`."

msgid ""
"The default value for this setting in Django 1.4.4 is ``['*']`` (matching "
"any host), for backwards-compatibility, but we strongly encourage all sites "
"to set a more restrictive value."
msgstr ""
"Is é an luach réamhshocraithe don socrú seo i Django 1.4.4 ná ``['*']`` (aon "
"óstach a mheaitseáil), le haghaidh comhoiriúnacht ar ais, ach molaimid go "
"láidir gach suíomh luach níos srianta a shocrú."

msgid ""
"The XML parser in the Python standard library is vulnerable to a number of "
"attacks via external entities and entity expansion. Django uses this parser "
"for deserializing XML-formatted database fixtures. This deserializer is not "
"intended for use with untrusted data, but in order to err on the side of "
"safety in Django 1.4.4 the XML deserializer refuses to parse an XML document "
"with a DTD (DOCTYPE definition), which closes off these attack avenues."
msgstr ""
"Tá an parser XML i leabharlann caighdeánach Python leochaileach do roinnt "
"ionsaithe trí eintitis sheachtracha agus leathnú eintiteas. Úsáideann Django "
"an parser seo chun daingneáin bunachar sonraí formáidithe XML a dhísherialú. "
"Níl an deserializer seo beartaithe le húsáid le sonraí neamhiontaofa, ach "
"d'fhonn earráid a dhéanamh ar thaobh na sábháilteachta i Django 1.4.4 "
"diúltaíonn an deserializer XML doiciméad XML a pharsáil le DTD (sainmhíniú "
"DOCTYPE), a dhúnann na bealaí ionsaithe seo."

msgid ""
"In Django 1.4.4, all formsets have a strictly-enforced maximum number of "
"forms (1000 by default, though it can be set higher via the ``max_num`` "
"formset factory argument)."
msgstr ""
"I Django 1.4.4, tá uaslíon foirmeacha a fhorfheidhmithe go docht ag gach "
"tacar foirme (1000 de réir réamhshocraithe, cé gur féidir é a shocrú níos "
"airde tríd an argóint monarcha foirmset ``max_num``)."

msgid ""
"In previous versions of Django, an admin user without change permission on a "
"model could still view the Unicode representation of instances via their "
"admin history log. Django 1.4.4 now limits the admin history log view for an "
"object to users with change permission for that model."
msgstr ""
"I leaganacha roimhe seo de Django, d'fhéadfadh úsáideoir riaracháin gan cead "
"athraithe ar mhúnla léiriú Unicode ar chásanna a fheiceáil fós trína log "
"stair riaracháin. Cuireann Django 1.4.4 teorainn anois ar an radharc log "
"stair riaracháin do réad d'úsáideoirí a bhfuil cead athraithe acu don "
"tsamhail sin."

msgid ""
"Prevented transaction state from leaking from one request to the next "
"(#19707)."
msgstr ""
"Cosc ar stát idirbheart ó sceitheadh ó iarratas amháin go dtí an chéad "
"iarratas eile (#19707)."

msgid "Changed an SQL command syntax to be MySQL 4 compatible (#19702)."
msgstr ""
"Athraigh comhréir ordaithe SQL chun a bheith comhoiriúnach le MySQL 4 "
"(#19702)."

msgid "Added backwards-compatibility with old unsalted MD5 passwords (#18144)."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh comhoiriúnacht ar ais le sean-phasfhocail MD5 neamh-shailte "
"(#18144)."

msgid "Django 1.4.5 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.4.5"

msgid ""
"Django 1.4.5 corrects a packaging problem with yesterday's :doc:`1.4.4 "
"release </releases/1.4.4>`."
msgstr ""
"Ceartaíonn Django 1.4.5 fadhb pacáistithe le :doc:`1.4.4 scaoileadh </"
"releases/1.4.4>`."

msgid "Django 1.4.6 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.4.6"

msgid "*August 13, 2013*"
msgstr "*13 Lúnasa, 2013*"

msgid ""
"Django 1.4.6 fixes one security issue present in previous Django releases in "
"the 1.4 series, as well as one other bug."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.4.6 saincheist slándála amháin atá i láthair in eisiúintí "
"Django roimhe seo sa tsraith 1.4, chomh maith le fabht amháin eile."

msgid "This is the sixth bugfix/security release in the Django 1.4 series."
msgstr "Is é seo an séú scaoileadh bugfix/slándála sa tsraith Django 1.4."

msgid ""
"Django relies on user input in some cases (e.g. "
"``django.contrib.auth.views.login()``, ``django.contrib.comments``, "
"and :doc:`i18n </topics/i18n/index>`) to redirect the user to an \"on "
"success\" URL. The security checks for these redirects (namely "
"``django.utils.http.is_safe_url()``) didn't check if the scheme is "
"``http(s)`` and as such allowed ``javascript:...`` URLs to be entered. If a "
"developer relied on ``is_safe_url()`` to provide safe redirect targets and "
"put such a URL into a link, they could suffer from a XSS attack. This bug "
"doesn't affect Django currently, since we only put this URL into the "
"``Location`` response header and browsers seem to ignore JavaScript there."
msgstr ""
"Braitheann Django ar ionchur úsáideora i roinnt cásanna (m.sh. "
"``django.contrib.auth.views.login () ``, ``django.contrib.comments``, "
"agus:doc: `i18n`) chun an t-úsáideoir a atreorú chuig URL “ar rath </topics/"
"i18n/index>”. Níor sheiceáil na seiceálacha slándála do na haatreoruithe seo "
"(eadhon ``django.utils.http.is_safe_url () ``)``) an bhfuil an scéim ``http "
"(s) ``agus mar sin cheadaíodh URLanna ``javascript:...`` a iontráil. Má bhí "
"forbróir ag brath ar ``is_safe_url () ``chun spriocanna athsheolta sábháilte "
"a sholáthar agus URL den sórt sin a chur i nasc, d'fhéadfadh siad a bheith "
"ag fulaingt ó ionsaí XSS. Ní chuireann an fabht seo i bhfeidhm ar Django "
"faoi láthair, ós rud é nach gcuirimid an URL seo ach sa cheannteideal "
"freagartha ``Suíomh ``agus is cosúil go ndéanann brabhsálaithe neamhaird ar "
"JavaScript ansin."

msgid ""
"Fixed an obscure bug with the :func:`~django.test.override_settings` "
"decorator. If you hit an ``AttributeError: 'Settings' object has no "
"attribute '_original_allowed_hosts'`` exception, it's probably fixed "
"(#20636)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh fabht doiléir leis an maisitheoir: func: "
"`~django.test.override_settings`. Má bhuail tú eisceacht "
"“_original_allowed_hosts'” ag réad ``AttributeError: 'Socruithe', is dócha "
"go bhfuil sé socraithe (#20636)."

msgid "Django 1.4.7 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.4.7"

msgid "*September 10, 2013*"
msgstr "*10 Meán Fómhair, 2013*"

msgid ""
"Django 1.4.7 fixes one security issue present in previous Django releases in "
"the 1.4 series."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.4.7 saincheist slándála amháin atá i láthair in eisiúintí "
"Django roimhe seo sa tsraith 1.4."

msgid "Directory traversal vulnerability in ``ssi`` template tag"
msgstr "Leochaileacht eolaire a thrasnú i gclib teimpléad ``ssi``"

msgid ""
"In previous versions of Django it was possible to bypass the "
"``ALLOWED_INCLUDE_ROOTS`` setting used for security with the ``ssi`` "
"template tag by specifying a relative path that starts with one of the "
"allowed roots. For example, if ``ALLOWED_INCLUDE_ROOTS = (\"/var/www\",)`` "
"the following would be possible:"
msgstr ""
"I leaganacha roimhe seo de Django bhí sé in ann an socrú "
"`ALLOWED_INCLUDE_ROOTS`` a úsáidtear le haghaidh slándála leis an gclib "
"teimpléad ``ssi`` a sheachaint trí chonair choibhneasta a shonrú a thosaíonn "
"le ceann de na fréamhacha ceadaithe. Mar shampla, má tá "
"`ALLOWED_INCLUDE_ROOTS = (“/var/www”,) ``bheadh an méid seo a leanas "
"indéanta:"

msgid ""
"In practice this is not a very common problem, as it would require the "
"template author to put the ``ssi`` file in a user-controlled variable, but "
"it's possible in principle."
msgstr ""
"Go praiticiúil ní fadhb an-choitianta í seo, mar go n-éilfeadh sé ar an údar "
"teimpléid an comhad ``ssi`` a chur in athróg faoi rialú úsáideora, ach is "
"féidir é i bprionsabal."

msgid "Django 1.4.8 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.4.8"

msgid "*September 14, 2013*"
msgstr "*Meán Fómhair 14, 2013*"

msgid ""
"Django 1.4.8 fixes two security issues present in previous Django releases "
"in the 1.4 series."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.4.8 dhá shaincheist slándála atá i láthair in eisiúintí "
"Django roimhe seo sa tsraith 1.4."

msgid "Denial-of-service via password hashers"
msgstr "Diúltú seirbhíse trí hashers pasfhocal"

msgid ""
"In previous versions of Django, no limit was imposed on the plaintext length "
"of a password. This allowed a denial-of-service attack through submission of "
"bogus but extremely large passwords, tying up server resources performing "
"the (expensive, and increasingly expensive with the length of the password) "
"calculation of the corresponding hash."
msgstr ""
"I leaganacha roimhe seo de Django, níor cuireadh aon teorainn ar fad téacs "
"simplí pasfhocal. Ceadaigh sé seo ionsaí seirbhíse a dhiúltú trí phasfhocail "
"bhréagacha ach thar a bheith mór a chur isteach, ag ceangal acmhainní "
"freastalaí ag déanamh ríomh (costasach, agus níos costasaí le fad an "
"phasfhocal) an hash comhfhreagrach."

msgid ""
"As of 1.4.8, Django's authentication framework imposes a 4096-byte limit on "
"passwords and will fail authentication with any submitted password of "
"greater length."
msgstr ""
"Amhail 1.4.8, cuireann creat fíordheimhnithe Django teorainn 4096 beart ar "
"phasfhocail agus teipeann sé ar fhíordheimhniú le haon phasfhocal curtha "
"isteach de fhad níos mó."

msgid ""
"Corrected usage "
"of :func:`~django.views.decorators.debug.sensitive_post_parameters` "
"in :mod:`django.contrib.auth`’s admin"
msgstr ""
"Úsáid cheartaithe de:func: "
"`~django.views.decorators.debug.sensitive_post_parameters` in:mod: admin "
"`django.contrib.auth`"

msgid ""
"The decoration of the ``add_view`` and ``user_change_password`` user admin "
"views with :func:`~django.views.decorators.debug.sensitive_post_parameters` "
"did not include :func:`~django.utils.decorators.method_decorator` (required "
"since the views are methods) resulting in the decorator not being properly "
"applied. This usage has been fixed "
"and :func:`~django.views.decorators.debug.sensitive_post_parameters` will "
"now throw an exception if it's improperly used."
msgstr ""
"Ní raibh maisiú tuairimí riaracháin úsáideora ``add_view`` agus "
"``user_change_password`` le: func: "
"`~django.views.decorators.debug.sensitive_post_parameters`: func: "
"`~django.utils.decorators.method_decorator` (riachtanach ós rud é gur "
"modhanna iad na tuairimí) mar thoradh ar an maisitheoir i bhfeidhm i gceart. "
"Socraíodh an úsáid seo agus caithfidh: func: "
"`~django.views.decorators.debug.sensitive_post_parameters` eisceacht anois "
"má úsáidtear é go míchuí."

msgid "Django 1.4.9 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.4.9"

msgid "*October 23, 2013*"
msgstr "*Deireadh Fómhair 23, 2013*"

msgid ""
"Django 1.4.9 fixes a security-related bug in the 1.4 series and one other "
"data corruption bug."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.4.9 fabht a bhaineann le slándáil sa tsraith 1.4 agus "
"fabht éillithe sonraí amháin eile."

msgid "Readdressed denial-of-service via password hashers"
msgstr "Diúltú seirbhíse léite trí hashers pasfhocal"

msgid ""
"Django 1.4.8 imposes a 4096-byte limit on passwords in order to mitigate a "
"denial-of-service attack through submission of bogus but extremely large "
"passwords. In Django 1.4.9, we've reverted this change and instead improved "
"the speed of our PBKDF2 algorithm by not rehashing the key on every "
"iteration."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann Django 1.4.8 teorainn 4096 beart ar phasfhocail d'fhonn ionsaí "
"diúltaithe seirbhíse a mhaolú trí phasfhocail bhréagacha ach thar a bheith "
"mór a chur isteach. I Django 1.4.9, rinneamar an t-athrú seo ar ais agus ina "
"ionad sin feabhsaigh muid luas ár algartam PBKDF2 trí gan an eochair ar gach "
"athrá a athdhéanamh."

msgid ""
"Fixed a data corruption bug with ``datetime_safe.datetime.combine`` (#21256)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh fabht éillithe sonraí le ``datetime_safe.datetime.combine`` "
"(#21256)."

msgid "Django 1.5 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.5"

msgid "*February 26, 2013*"
msgstr "*26 Feabhra, 2013*"

msgid "Welcome to Django 1.5!"
msgstr "Fáilte go dtí Django 1.5!"

msgid ""
"These release notes cover the :ref:`new features <whats-new-1.5>`, as well "
"as some :ref:`backwards incompatible changes <backwards-incompatible-1.5>` "
"you'll want to be aware of when upgrading from Django 1.4 or older versions. "
"We've also dropped some features, which are detailed in :ref:`our "
"deprecation plan <deprecation-removed-in-1.5>`, and we've :ref:`begun the "
"deprecation process for some features <deprecated-features-1.5>`."
msgstr ""
"Clúdaíonn na nótaí scaoilte seo na:ref: `gnéithe nua <whats-new-1.5>`, chomh "
"maith le roinnt athruithe: ref: `athruithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha ar "
"ais<backwards-incompatible-1.5>` beidh tú ag iarraidh a bheith ar an eolas "
"fúthu agus tú ag uasghrádú ó Django 1.4 nó leaganacha níos sine. <deprecated-"
"features-1.5>Tá roinnt gnéithe titim againn freisin, atá mionsonraithe "
"in:ref: `ár bplean díghabhála <deprecation-removed-in-1.5>`, agus "
"chuireamaire:ref: `tús leis an bpróiseas díghabhála do roinnt gnéithe`."

msgid ""
"The biggest new feature in Django 1.5 is the `configurable User model`_. "
"Before Django 1.5, applications that wanted to use Django's auth framework "
"(:mod:`django.contrib.auth`) were forced to use Django's definition of a "
"\"user\". In Django 1.5, you can now swap out the ``User`` model for one "
"that you write yourself. This could be a simple extension to the existing "
"``User`` model -- for example, you could add a Twitter or Facebook ID field "
"-- or you could completely replace the ``User`` with one totally customized "
"for your site."
msgstr ""
"Is é an ghné nua is mó i Django 1.5 an `samhail Úsáideora inchumraithe`_. "
"Roimh Django 1.5, cuireadh iallach ar iarratais a bhí ag iarraidh creat auth "
"Django a úsáid (:mod: `django.contrib.auth`) sainmhíniú Django ar "
"“úsáideoir” a úsáid. I Django 1.5, is féidir leat an tsamhail ``Úsáideoir "
"``a mhalartú anois le haghaidh ceann a scríobhann tú féin. D'fhéadfadh sé "
"seo a bheith ina síneadh simplí ar an tsamhail ``Úsáideoir ``atá ann cheana "
"- mar shampla, d'fhéadfá réimse ID Twitter nó Facebook a chur leis -- nó "
"d'fhéadfá ceann saincheaptha go hiomlán do do shuíomh a chur in ionad an "
"``Úsáideoir``."

msgid ""
"Django 1.5 is also the first release with `Python 3 support`_! We're "
"labeling this support \"experimental\" because we don't yet consider it "
"production-ready, but everything's in place for you to start porting your "
"apps to Python 3. Our next release, Django 1.6, will support Python 3 "
"without reservations."
msgstr ""
"Is é Django 1.5 an chéad eisiúint freisin le `tacaíocht Python 3`_! Táimid "
"ag lipéadú ar an tacaíocht seo “turgnamhach” toisc nach measaimid go fóill "
"go bhfuil sé réidh le táirgeadh, ach tá gach rud i bhfeidhm duit tosú ag "
"iompar d'aipeanna chuig Python 3. Tacóidh ár gcéad eisiúint eile, Django "
"1.6, le Python 3 gan áirithintí."

msgid "Other notable new features in Django 1.5 include:"
msgstr "I measc na ngnéithe nua suntasacha eile i Django 1.5 tá:"

msgid ""
"`Support for saving a subset of model's fields`_ - :meth:`Model.save() "
"<django.db.models.Model.save()>` now accepts an ``update_fields`` argument, "
"letting you specify which fields are written back to the database when you "
"call ``save()``. This can help in high-concurrency operations, and can "
"improve performance."
msgstr ""
"Glacann `tacaíocht chun fothacar de réimsí an mhúnla a shábháil`_ "
"- :meth:`Model.save() <django.db.models.Model.save()>` anois le argóint `` "
"update_fields``, rud a ligeann duit na réimsí a shonrú scríofa ar ais chuig "
"an mbunachar sonraí nuair a ghlaonn tú ar ``save()``. Is féidir leis seo "
"cabhrú in oibríochtaí ard-concurrency, agus féadann sé feidhmíocht a "
"fheabhsú."

msgid ""
"Better `support for streaming responses <#explicit-streaming-responses>`_ "
"via the new  :class:`~django.http.StreamingHttpResponse` response class."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíocht níos fearr le haghaidh freagraí sruthú <#explicit-streaming-"
"responses>`_ tríd an rang freagartha nua:class: "
"`~django.http.StreamInghttPresponse`."

msgid "`GeoDjango`_ now supports PostGIS 2.0."
msgstr "Tacaíonn `GeodJango`_ anois le PostGIS 2.0."

msgid "... and more; `see below <#what-s-new-in-django-1-5>`_."
msgstr "... agus níos mó; `féach thíos <#what-s-new-in-django-1-5>`_."

msgid ""
"Wherever possible we try to introduce new features in a backwards-compatible "
"manner per :doc:`our API stability policy </misc/api-stability>`. However, "
"as with previous releases, Django 1.5 ships with some minor :ref:`backwards "
"incompatible changes <backwards-incompatible-1.5>`; people upgrading from "
"previous versions of Django should read that list carefully."
msgstr ""
"Nuair is féidir déanaimid iarracht gnéithe nua a thabhairt isteach ar "
"bhealach atá comhoiriúnach siar le :doc:`ár mbeartas cobhsaíochta API </misc/"
"api-stability>`. Mar a bhí le heisiúintí roimhe seo, áfach, long Django 1.5 "
"le roinnt mionathruithe :tag:`ar gcúl athruithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha "
"<backwards-incompatible-1.5>`; ba chóir do dhaoine atá ag uasghrádú ó "
"leaganacha níos sine de Django an liosta sin a léamh go cúramach."

msgid ""
"One deprecated feature worth noting is the shift to \"new-"
"style\" :ttag:`url` tag. Prior to Django 1.3, syntax like ``{% url myview %}"
"`` was interpreted incorrectly (Django considered ``\"myview\"`` to be a "
"literal name of a view, not a template variable named ``myview``). Django "
"1.3 and above introduced the ``{% load url from future %}`` syntax to bring "
"in the corrected behavior where ``myview`` was seen as a variable."
msgstr ""
"Gné scoite amháin is fiú a thabhairt faoi deara ná an t-aistriú go clib "
"“stíl nua”: ttag: `url`. Roimh Django 1.3, léiríníodh comhréir mar ``{% url "
"myview%} `go mícheart (mheas Django gur ainm liteartha radharc é "
"``\"myview\"`, ní athróg teimpléad darb ainm ``myview``). Thug Django 1.3 "
"agus thuas an comhréir ``{% load url ón todhchaí%}`` isteach chun an t-"
"iompar ceartaithe a thabhairt isteach ina bhfeictear ``myview`` mar athróg."

msgid ""
"The upshot of this is that if you are not using ``{% load url from future %}"
"`` in your templates, you'll need to change tags like ``{% url myview %}`` "
"to ``{% url \"myview\" %}``. If you *were* using ``{% load url from future %}"
"`` you can simply remove that line under Django 1.5"
msgstr ""
"Is é an toradh a bhaineann leis seo ná mura bhfuil tú ag úsáid ``{% load url "
"from the future%}`` i do theimpléid, beidh ort clibeanna mar ``{% url "
"myview%}`` a athrú go ``{% url “myview”%}``. Má bhí t** ag baint úsáide as "
"``{% load url ón todhchaí%}`` is féidir leat an líne sin a bhaint faoi "
"Django 1.5"

msgid ""
"Django 1.5 requires Python 2.6.5 or above, though we **highly recommend** "
"Python 2.7.3 or above. Support for Python 2.5 and below has been dropped."
msgstr ""
"Éilíonn Django 1.5 Python 2.6.5 nó os a chionn, cé go molaimid** go hard** "
"Python 2.7.3 nó os a chionn. Tá tacaíocht do Python 2.5 agus thíos titim."

msgid ""
"This change should affect only a small number of Django users, as most "
"operating-system vendors today are shipping Python 2.6 or newer as their "
"default version. If you're still using Python 2.5, however, you'll need to "
"stick to Django 1.4 until you can upgrade your Python version. Per :doc:`our "
"support policy </internals/release-process>`, Django 1.4 will continue to "
"receive security support until the release of Django 1.6."
msgstr ""
"Níor cheart go mbíonn tionchar ag an athrú seo ach ar líon beag úsáideoirí "
"Django, mar tá formhór na ndíoltóirí córais oibriúcháin inniu ag seoladh "
"Python 2.6 nó níos nuaí mar a leagan réamhshoc Má tá Python 2.5 á úsáid agat "
"fós, áfach, beidh ort cloí le Django 1.4 go dtí gur féidir leat do leagan "
"Python a uasghrádú. Per:doc: `ár mbeartas tacaíochta `, leanfaidh </"
"internals/release-process> Django 1.4 ag fáil tacaíochta slándála go dtí go "
"scaoilfear Django 1.6."

msgid ""
"Django 1.5 does not run on a Jython final release, because Jython's latest "
"release doesn't currently support Python 2.6. However, Jython currently does "
"offer an alpha release featuring 2.7 support, and Django 1.5 supports that "
"alpha release."
msgstr ""
"Ní ritheann Django 1.5 ar eisiúint deiridh Jython, toisc nach dtacaíonn an "
"eisiúint is déanaí de Jython le Python 2.6 faoi láthair. Mar sin féin, "
"cuireann Jython scaoileadh alfa ar fáil faoi láthair le tacaíocht 2.7, agus "
"tacaíonn Django 1.5 leis an scaoileadh alfa sin."

msgid "Python 3 support"
msgstr "Tacaíocht Python 3"

msgid ""
"Django 1.5 introduces support for Python 3 - specifically, Python 3.2 and "
"above. This comes in the form of a **single** codebase; you don't need to "
"install a different version of Django on Python 3. This means that you can "
"write applications targeted for just Python 2, just Python 3, or single "
"applications that support both platforms."
msgstr ""
"Tugann Django 1.5 tacaíocht isteach do Python 3 - go sonrach, Python 3.2 "
"agus os a chionn. Tagann sé seo i bhfoirm bonn cód**aonair**; ní gá duit "
"leagan difriúil de Django a shuiteáil ar Python 3. Ciallaíonn sé seo gur "
"féidir leat feidhmchláir a scríobh dírithe ar Python 2 amháin, ach Python 3, "
"nó feidhmchláir aonair a thacaíonn leis an dá ardán."

msgid ""
"However, we're labeling this support \"experimental\" for now: although it's "
"received extensive testing via our automated test suite, it's received very "
"little real-world testing. We've done our best to eliminate bugs, but we "
"can't be sure we covered all possible uses of Django."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, táimid ag lipéadú ar an tacaíocht seo “turgnamhach” anois: cé "
"go bhfuair sé tástáil fhairsing trínár sraith tástála uathoibrithe, níl "
"mórán tástála fíor faighte aige. Rinneamar ár ndícheall chun fabhtanna a "
"dhíchur, ach ní féidir linn a bheith cinnte go gclúdaigh muid gach úsáid "
"féideartha de Django."

msgid ""
"Some features of Django aren't available because they depend on third-party "
"software that hasn't been ported to Python 3 yet, including:"
msgstr ""
"Níl roinnt gnéithe de Django ar fáil toisc go mbraitheann siad ar bhogearraí "
"tríú páirtí nár iompraíodh chuig Python 3 fós, lena n-áirítear:"

msgid "the MySQL database backend (depends on MySQLdb)"
msgstr "cúltaca bunachar sonraí MySQL (ag brath ar MySQLDB)"

msgid ":class:`~django.db.models.ImageField` (depends on PIL)"
msgstr ":class: `~django.db.models.imagefield` (ag brath ar PIL)"

msgid ""
":class:`~django.test.LiveServerTestCase` (depends on Selenium WebDriver)"
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.test.liveservertestcase` (ag brath ar Seiléiniam WebDriver)"

msgid ""
"Further, Django's more than a web framework; it's an ecosystem of pluggable "
"components. At this point, very few third-party applications have been "
"ported to Python 3, so it's unlikely that a real-world application will have "
"all its dependencies satisfied under Python 3."
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, tá níos mó ná creat gréasáin Django; is éiceachóras de "
"chomhpháirteanna inphlugáilte é. Ag an bpointe seo, is beag feidhmchlár tríú "
"páirtí a iompraíodh chuig Python 3, mar sin ní dócha go mbeidh a spleáchas "
"go léir sásta ag feidhmchlár saol fíor faoi Python 3."

msgid ""
"Thus, we're recommending that Django 1.5 not be used in production under "
"Python 3. Instead, use this opportunity to begin porting applications to "
"Python 3. If you're an author of a pluggable component, we encourage you to "
"start porting now."
msgstr ""
"Dá bhrí sin, táimid ag moladh nach n-úsáidfear Django 1.5 i dtáirgeadh faoi "
"Python 3. Ina áit sin, bain úsáid as an deis seo chun feidhmchláir a iompar "
"chuig Python 3. Más údar tú ar chomhpháirt inphlugáilte, molaimid duit tosú "
"ag iompar anois."

msgid ""
"We plan to offer first-class, production-ready support for Python 3 in our "
"next release, Django 1.6."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé beartaithe againn tacaíocht den chéad scoth, réidh le táirgeadh a "
"thairiscint do Python 3 inár gcéad eisiúint eile, Django 1.6."

msgid "What's new in Django 1.5"
msgstr "Cad atá nua i Django 1.5"

msgid "Configurable User model"
msgstr "Múnla Úsáideora inchumraithe"

msgid ""
"In Django 1.5, you can now use your own model as the store for user-related "
"data. If your project needs a username with more than 30 characters, or if "
"you want to store user's names in a format other than first name/last name, "
"or you want to put custom profile information onto your User object, you can "
"now do so."
msgstr ""
"I Django 1.5, is féidir leat do mhúnla féin a úsáid anois mar an siopa le "
"haghaidh sonraí a bhaineann le húsáideoir. Má theastaíonn ainm úsáideora de "
"do thionscadal le níos mó ná 30 carachtar, nó más mian leat ainmneacha "
"úsáideora a stóráil i bhformáid seachas céadainm/ainm deiridh, nó más mian "
"leat faisnéis phróifíle saincheaptha a chur ar do réad Úsáideora, is féidir "
"leat é sin a dhéanamh anois."

msgid ""
"If you have a third-party reusable application that references the User "
"model, you may need to make some changes to the way you reference User "
"instances. You should also document any specific features of the User model "
"that your application relies upon."
msgstr ""
"Má tá feidhmchlár athúsáidte tríú páirtí agat a thagann tagairt don tsamhail "
"Úsáideora, b'fhéidir go mbeidh ort roinnt athruithe a dhéanamh ar an "
"mbealach a thagann tú tagairt do chásanna Ba chóir duit aon ghnéithe "
"sonracha den tsamhail Úsáideora a bhfuil d'iarratas ag brath air a "
"dhoiciméadú freisin."

msgid ""
"See the :ref:`documentation on custom user models <auth-custom-user>` for "
"more details."
msgstr ""
"Féach an:ref: `doiciméadú ar mhúnlaí úsáideora saincheaptha <auth-custom-"
"user>`le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid "Support for saving a subset of model's fields"
msgstr "Tacaíocht chun fo-thacar de réimsí an tsamhail a shábháil"

msgid ""
"The method :meth:`Model.save() <django.db.models.Model.save()>` has a new "
"keyword argument ``update_fields``. By using this argument it is possible to "
"save only a select list of model's fields. This can be useful for "
"performance reasons or when trying to avoid overwriting concurrent changes."
msgstr ""
"Tá argóint nua eochairfhocail ag an modh :meth:`Model.save() "
"<django.db.models.Model.save()>` `` update_fields``. Trí úsáid a bhaint as "
"an argóint seo ní féidir ach liosta roghnaithe de réimsí an mhúnla a "
"shábháil. D’fhéadfadh sé seo a bheith úsáideach ar chúiseanna feidhmíochta "
"nó nuair a dhéantar iarracht athruithe comhthráthacha a fhorscríobh a "
"sheachaint."

msgid ""
"Deferred instances (those loaded by ``.only()`` or ``.defer()``) will "
"automatically save just the loaded fields. If any field is set manually "
"after load, that field will also get updated on save."
msgstr ""
"Sábhálfaidh cásanna iarchurtha (iad siúd a luchtaithe ag ``.only () ``nó "
"``.defer ()``) na réimsí luchtaithe go huathoibríoch. Má shocraítear aon "
"réimse de láimh tar éis an ualaigh, déanfar an réimse sin nuashonrú freisin "
"ar shábháil."

msgid ""
"See the :meth:`Model.save() <django.db.models.Model.save()>` documentation "
"for more details."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.Model.save () >Féach an doiciméadú: meth: `Model.save ()` "
"le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid "Caching of related model instances"
msgstr "Cáscaíocht cásanna samhail ghaolmhara"

msgid ""
"When traversing relations, the ORM will avoid re-fetching objects that were "
"previously loaded. For example, with the tutorial's models:"
msgstr ""
"Agus caidrimh á thrasú, seachnóidh an ORM rudaí a luchtaigh roimhe seo a "
"athghabháil. Mar shampla, le samhlacha an rang teagaisc:"

msgid ""
"In Django 1.5, the third line no longer triggers a new SQL query to fetch "
"``first_choice.poll``; it was set by the second line."
msgstr ""
"I Django 1.5, ní spreagann an tríú líne ceist nua SQL a thuilleadh chun "
"``first_choice.poll`` a fháil; socraíodh é ag an dara líne."

msgid ""
"For one-to-one relationships, both sides can be cached. For many-to-one "
"relationships, only the single side of the relationship can be cached. This "
"is particularly helpful in combination with ``prefetch_related``."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le caidrimh duine le duine, is féidir an dá thaobh a chosc. Maidir le "
"caidrimh go leor, ní féidir ach an taobh amháin den chaidreamh a chosc. Tá "
"sé seo cabhrach go háirithe i dteannta le ``prefetch_related``."

msgid "Explicit support for streaming responses"
msgstr "Tacaíocht shoiléir le haghaidh freagraí sru"

msgid ""
"Before Django 1.5, it was possible to create a streaming response by passing "
"an iterator to :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse`. But this was unreliable: "
"any middleware that accessed the :attr:`~django.http.HttpResponse.content` "
"attribute would consume the iterator prematurely."
msgstr ""
"Roimh Django 1.5, bhí sé indéanta freagra sruthú a chruthú trí athraitheoir "
"a chur chuig: class: `~django.http.httpResponse`. Ach ní raibh sé seo "
"neamhiontaofa: d'ith aon mheán-earraí a rochtain ar thréith: attr: "
"`~django.http.httpResponse.content` an t-athraitheoir roimh am."

msgid ""
"You can now explicitly generate a streaming response with the "
"new :class:`~django.http.StreamingHttpResponse` class. This class exposes "
"a :class:`~django.http.StreamingHttpResponse.streaming_content` attribute "
"which is an iterator."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat freagra sruthú a ghiniúint go sainráite anois leis an rang "
"nua:class: `~django.http.StreamInghttPresponse`. Nochtann an rang seo a: "
"class: `~django.http.StreamInghttPresponse.streaming_content` tréith atá ina "
"athraitheoir."

msgid ""
"Since :class:`~django.http.StreamingHttpResponse` does not have a "
"``content`` attribute, middleware that needs access to the response content "
"must test for streaming responses and behave accordingly."
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é: :class: `~django.http.StreamInghttPresponse` níl tréith "
"``content``, ní mór do mheán-earraí a theastaíonn rochtain uathu ar an ábhar "
"freagartha tástáil a dhéanamh le haghaidh freagraí sruthú agus iompar dá "
"réir sin."

msgid "``{% verbatim %}`` template tag"
msgstr "``{% verbatim%}`` clib teimpléad"

msgid ""
"To make it easier to deal with JavaScript templates which collide with "
"Django's syntax, you can now use the :ttag:`verbatim` block tag to avoid "
"parsing the tag's content."
msgstr ""
"Chun é a dhéanamh níos éasca déileáil le teimpléid JavaScript a imbhuaileann "
"le comhréir Django, is féidir leat an chlib bloc:ttag: `verbatim` a úsáid "
"anois chun ábhar an chlib a pháirseáil a sheachaint."

msgid "Retrieval of ``ContentType`` instances associated with proxy models"
msgstr ""
"Aisghabháil cásanna ``contentType`` a bhaineann le samhlacha seachfhreastalaí"

msgid ""
"The methods :meth:`ContentTypeManager.get_for_model() "
"<django.contrib.contenttypes.models.ContentTypeManager.get_for_model()>` "
"and :meth:`ContentTypeManager.get_for_models() "
"<django.contrib.contenttypes.models.ContentTypeManager.get_for_models()>` "
"have a new keyword argument – respectively ``for_concrete_model`` and "
"``for_concrete_models``. By passing ``False`` using this argument it is now "
"possible to retrieve the :class:`ContentType "
"<django.contrib.contenttypes.models.ContentType>` associated with proxy "
"models."
msgstr ""
"<django.contrib.contenttypes.models.ContentTypeManager.get_for_models () >Tá "
"argóint eochairfhocal nua ag na modhaí:meth: "
"`ContentTypeManager.get_for_Model ()` agus:meth: "
"`ContentTypeManager.get_for_Models ()` faoi seach `for_concrete_model`` agus "
"``for_concrete_models`` "
"<django.contrib.contenttypes.models.ContentTypeManager.get_for_model () >. "
"<django.contrib.contenttypes.models.ContentType>Trí ``False`` a rith ag "
"baint úsáide as an argóint seo is féidir anois an:class: `ContentType` a "
"bhaineann le samhlacha seachfhreastalaí a aisghabháil."

msgid "New ``view`` variable in class-based views context"
msgstr "Athróg nua ```amharc`` i gcomhthéacs tuairimí rang-bhunaithe"

msgid ""
"In all :doc:`generic class-based views </topics/class-based-views/index>` "
"(or any class-based view inheriting from ``ContextMixin``), the context "
"dictionary contains a ``view`` variable that points to the ``View`` instance."
msgstr ""
"I ngach:doc: `tuairimí cineálacha bunaithe ar aicme' (nó aon dearcadh aicme-"
"bhunaithe a fhaigheann oidhreacht ó ``ContextMixin``), tá athróg ``dearcadh "
"``sa bhfoclóir comhthéacs a thugann tuiscint ar an sampla ``View</topics/"
"class-based-views/index> `."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.contrib.gis.geos.LineString` "
"and :class:`~django.contrib.gis.geos.MultiLineString` GEOS objects now "
"support the :meth:`~django.contrib.gis.geos.GEOSGeometry.interpolate()` "
"and :meth:`~django.contrib.gis.geos.GEOSGeometry.project()` methods (so-"
"called linear referencing)."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.contrib.gis.geos.lineString` agus:class: "
"`~django.contrib.gis.geos.multilineString` Tacaíonn rudaí GEOS anois "
"la:meth: `~django.contrib.gis.geos.geosgeometry.interpolate () `agus:meth: "
"`~django.contrib.gis.contrib.gisModhanna geos.geosgeometry.project ()` "
"(tagairt líneach mar a thugtar air)."

msgid ""
"The ``wkb`` and ``hex`` properties "
"of :class:`~django.contrib.gis.geos.GEOSGeometry` objects preserve the Z "
"dimension."
msgstr ""
"Coinníonn na hairíonna ``wkb`` agus ``hex`` de:class: "
"`~django.contrib.gis.geos.geosgeometry` an toise Z."

msgid ""
"Support for PostGIS 2.0 has been added and support for GDAL < 1.5 has been "
"dropped."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh tacaíocht do PostGIS 2.0 leis agus tá tacaíocht do GDAL <1.5 titim."

msgid "New tutorials"
msgstr "Ranganna teagaisc nua"

msgid ""
"Additions to the docs include a revamped :doc:`Tutorial 3</intro/"
"tutorial03>` and a new :doc:`tutorial on testing</intro/tutorial05>`. A new "
"section, \"Advanced Tutorials\", offers :doc:`How to write reusable apps </"
"intro/reusable-apps>` as well as a step-by-step guide for new contributors "
"in :doc:`Writing your first patch for Django </intro/contributing>`."
msgstr ""
"I measc na mbreiseanna leis na doiciméid tá athbhreithnithe: doc: `Teagaisc "
"3` agus nua:doc: `teagaisc ar thástáil`</intro/tutorial03></intro/"
"tutorial05>. Cuireann rannán nua, “Ard-Ranganna Teagaisc”, ar fáil: doc: "
"`Conas aipeanna in-athúsáidte a scríobh `chomh maith le treoir céim ar chéim "
"do rannpháirtithe nua in:doc: `Do chéad phai</intro/reusable-apps> ste a "
"scríobh do </intro/contributing> Django`."

msgid "Django 1.5 also includes several smaller improvements worth noting:"
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn Django 1.5 roinnt feabhsuithe níos lú ar fiú a thabhairt faoi "
"deara:"

msgid ""
"The template engine now interprets ``True``, ``False`` and ``None`` as the "
"corresponding Python objects."
msgstr ""
"Léirmhíníonn an t-inneall teimpléid anois ``True``, `False`` agus ``None`` "
"mar na rudaí Python comhfhreagracha."

msgid ""
":mod:`django.utils.timezone` provides a helper for converting aware "
"datetimes between time zones. See :func:`~django.utils.timezone.localtime`."
msgstr ""
":mod: Soláthraíonn `django.utils.timezone` cúntóir chun dáta feasacha a "
"thiontú idir criosanna ama. Féach: func: `~django.utils.timezone.localtime`."

msgid "The generic views support OPTIONS requests."
msgstr "Tacaíonn na tuairimí cineálacha le hiarratais OPTIONS."

msgid ""
"Management commands do not raise ``SystemExit`` any more when called by code "
"from :func:`~django.core.management.call_command`. Any exception raised by "
"the command (mostly :exc:`~django.core.management.CommandError`) is "
"propagated."
msgstr ""
"Ní ardaíonn orduithe bainistíochta ``SystemExit`` níos mó nuair a ghlaonn "
"siad le cód ó:func: `~django.core.management.call_command`. Déantar aon "
"eisceacht a ardóidh an t-ordú (den chuid is mó: exc: "
"`~django.core.management.commandError`) iomadú."

msgid ""
"Moreover, when you output errors or messages in your custom commands, you "
"should now use ``self.stdout.write('message')`` and "
"``self.stderr.write('error')`` (see the note on :ref:`management commands "
"output <management-commands-output>`)."
msgstr ""
"<management-commands-output>Thairis sin, nuair a aschuireann tú earráidí nó "
"teachtaireachtaí i d'orduithe saincheaptha, ba chóir duit anois "
"``self.stdout.write ('teachtaireacht') ``agus ``self.stderr.write ('error') "
"`a úsáid anois (féach an nóta ar:ref: `aschur orduithe bainistíochta`)."

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`dumpdata` management command outputs one row at a time, "
"preventing out-of-memory errors when dumping large datasets."
msgstr ""
"Aschuireann an t-ordú bainistíochta: DJadmin: `dumpdata` sraith amháin ag an "
"am, ag cosc ar earráidí lasmuigh den chuimhne agus tacair mhóra sonraí á "
"ndúmáil."

msgid ""
"In the localflavor for Canada, ``pq`` was added to the acceptable codes for "
"Quebec. It's an old abbreviation."
msgstr ""
"Sa bhlaor áitiúil do Cheanada, cuireadh `pq`` leis na cóid inghlactha do "
"Quebec. Is sean-ghiorrúchán é."

msgid ""
"The :ref:`receiver <connecting-receiver-functions>` decorator is now able to "
"connect to more than one signal by supplying a list of signals."
msgstr ""
"Tá an maisitheoir: ref: `glacad <connecting-receiver-functions>óir` in ann "
"ceangal anois le níos mó ná comhartha amháin trí liosta comharthaí a "
"sholáthar."

msgid ""
"In the admin, you can now filter users by groups which they are members of."
msgstr ""
"Sa riarachán, is féidir leat úsáideoirí a scagadh anois de réir grúpaí a "
"bhfuil siad ina mbaill díobh."

msgid ""
":meth:`QuerySet.bulk_create() <django.db.models.query.QuerySet.bulk_create>` "
"now has a batch_size argument. By default the batch_size is unlimited except "
"for SQLite where single batch is limited so that 999 parameters per query "
"isn't exceeded."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.bulk_create>:meth: Tá argóint batch_size ag "
"`querySet.bulk_create () `anois. De réir réamhshocraithe tá an batch_size "
"gan teorainn ach amháin SQLite áit a bhfuil baisc aonair teoranta ionas nach "
"sáraítear paraiméadair 999 in aghaidh an cheistiúcháin."

msgid ""
"The :setting:`LOGIN_URL` and :setting:`LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL` settings now also "
"accept view function names and :ref:`named URL patterns <naming-url-"
"patterns>`. This allows you to reduce configuration duplication. More "
"information can be found in "
"the :func:`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.login_required` documentation."
msgstr ""
"<naming-url-patterns>Glacann socruithe an:setting: `LOGIN_URL` agus:setting: "
"`LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL` anois le hainmneacha feidhm amharc agus:ref: `patrúin "
"URL ainmnithe `. Ligeann sé seo duit dúbailt cumraíochta a laghdú. Is féidir "
"tuilleadh faisnéise a fháil sna cáipéisíocht: :func: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.login_required`."

msgid ""
"Django now provides a mod_wsgi :doc:`auth handler </howto/deployment/wsgi/"
"apache-auth>`."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Django anois mod_wsgi :doc:`auth handler </howto/deployment/"
"wsgi/apache-auth>`."

msgid ""
"The :meth:`QuerySet.delete() <django.db.models.query.QuerySet.delete>` "
"and :meth:`Model.delete() <django.db.models.Model.delete()>` can now take "
"fast-path in some cases. The fast-path allows for less queries and less "
"objects fetched into memory. See :meth:`QuerySet.delete() "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.delete>` for details."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.Model.delete () >Is féidir leis an:Meth: `QuerySet.delete "
"() `agus:meth: `Model.delete ()<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.delete>` "
"cosán tapa a ghlacadh anois i roinnt cásanna. Ligeann an cosán tapa níos lú "
"ceisteanna agus níos lú rudaí a thógtar isteach i gcuimhne. "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.delete>Féach: Meth: `QuerySet.delete () `le "
"haghaidh sonraí."

msgid ""
"An instance of ``ResolverMatch`` is stored on the request as "
"``resolver_match``."
msgstr ""
"Stóráiltear sampla de `ResolverMatch`` ar an iarratas mar ``resolver_match``."

msgid ""
"By default, all logging messages reaching the ``django`` logger "
"when :setting:`DEBUG` is ``True`` are sent to the console (unless you "
"redefine the logger in your :setting:`LOGGING` setting)."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, seoltar gach teachtaireacht logála a shroicheann an "
"logálaí ``django`` nuai:socrú: ``DEBUG` ``True`` chuig an gconsól (mura "
"ndéanann tú an logálaí a athshainiú i do shuíomh:: `LOGGING`)."

msgid ""
"When using :class:`~django.template.RequestContext`, it is now possible to "
"look up permissions by using ``{% if 'someapp.someperm' in perms %}`` in "
"templates."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a úsáidtear: class: `~django.template.requestContext`, is féidir anois "
"ceadanna a lorg suas trí ``{% if 'someapp.someperm' i perms%}`` a úsáid i "
"dteimpléid."

msgid ""
"It's not required any more to have ``404.html`` and ``500.html`` templates "
"in the root templates directory. Django will output some basic error "
"messages for both situations when those templates are not found. It's still "
"recommended as good practice to provide those templates in order to present "
"pretty error pages to the user."
msgstr ""
"Ní gá níos mó teimpléid ``404.html`` agus ``500.html`` a bheith san eolaire "
"teimpléid fréimhe. Aschróidh Django roinnt teachtaireachtaí earráide "
"bunúsacha don dá chás nuair nach bhfaightear na teimpléid sin. Moltar fós "
"mar dhea-chleachtas na teimpléid sin a sholáthar d'fhonn leathanaigh "
"earráide deasa a chur i láthair don úsáideoir."

msgid ""
":mod:`django.contrib.auth` provides a new signal that is emitted whenever a "
"user fails to login successfully. "
"See :data:`~django.contrib.auth.signals.user_login_failed`"
msgstr ""
":mod: Soláthraíonn `django.contrib.auth` comhartha nua a astaítear aon uair "
"a theipeann ar úsáideoir logáil isteach go rathúil. Féach: sonraí: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.signals.user_login_failed`"

msgid ""
"The new :option:`loaddata --ignorenonexistent` option ignore data for fields "
"that no longer exist."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an rogha nua:option: `loaddata --ignorenonexistent` neamhaird de "
"shonraí do réimsí nach bhfuil ann a thuilleadh."

msgid ""
":meth:`~django.test.SimpleTestCase.assertXMLEqual` "
"and :meth:`~django.test.SimpleTestCase.assertXMLNotEqual` new assertions "
"allow you to test equality for XML content at a semantic level, without "
"caring for syntax differences (spaces, attribute order, etc.)."
msgstr ""
":meth: `~django.test.simpletestcase.assertxmlequal` agus:meth: "
"`~django.test.simpletestcase.assertxmlNoteQual` deis duit comhionannas a "
"thástáil le haghaidh ábhar XML ar leibhéal séimeantach, gan aire a thabhairt "
"do dhifríochtaí comhréireachta (spásanna, ord tréithe, srl.)."

msgid ""
"RemoteUserMiddleware now forces logout when the REMOTE_USER header "
"disappears during the same browser session."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann RemoteUserMiddleware i bhfeidhm anois logáil amach nuair a imíonn "
"an ceannteideal REMOTE_USER le linn an tseisiúin bhrabhsálaí céanna."

msgid ""
"The :ref:`cache-based session backend <cached-sessions-backend>` can store "
"session data in a non-default cache."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leis an:ref: `cúltaca seisiúin bunaithe ar taisce <cached-sessions-"
"backend>`sonraí seisiúin a stóráil i taisce neamh-réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"Multi-column indexes can now be created on models. Read the "
"``index_together`` documentation for more information."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir innéacsanna il-cholún a chruthú anois ar mhúnlaí. Léigh an "
"doiciméad `index_together ``le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise."

msgid ""
"During Django's logging configuration verbose Deprecation warnings are "
"enabled and warnings are captured into the logging system. Logged warnings "
"are routed through the ``console`` logging handler, which by default "
"requires :setting:`DEBUG` to be True for output to be generated. The result "
"is that DeprecationWarnings should be printed to the console in development "
"environments the way they have been in Python versions < 2.7."
msgstr ""
"Le linn cumraíocht logála Django cumasaítear rabhaidh díphríochta agus "
"gabhtar rabhaidh isteach sa chóras logála. Déantar rabhaidh logáilte a "
"threorú tríd an láimhseálaí logála ``consóla`, a éilíonn de réir "
"réamhshocraithe: socrú: `DEBUG` go mbeidh Fíor chun aschur a ghiniúint. Is é "
"an toradh atá ann ná gur chóir DeprecationWarnings a phriontáil chuig an "
"gconsól i dtimpeallachtaí forbartha mar a bhí siad i leaganacha Python < 2.7."

msgid ""
"The API for :meth:`django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.message_user` method has "
"been modified to accept additional arguments adding capabilities similar "
"to :func:`django.contrib.messages.add_message`. This is useful for "
"generating error messages from admin actions."
msgstr ""
"Athraíodh an modh API "
"do :meth:`django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.message_user` chun glacadh le "
"hargóintí breise a chuireann cumais cosúil "
"le :func:`django.contrib.messages.add_message`. Tá sé seo úsáideach chun "
"teachtaireachtaí earráide a ghiniúint ó ghníomhartha riaracháin."

msgid ""
"The admin's list filters can now be customized per-request thanks to the "
"new :meth:`django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.get_list_filter` method."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir scagairí liosta an riaracháin a shaincheapadh anois in aghaidh "
"iarratais a bhuíochas leis an modh nua: meth: "
"`django.contrib.admin.modeladmin.get_list_filter`."

msgid "Backwards incompatible changes in 1.5"
msgstr "Athruithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha ar ais i 1.5"

msgid ""
"In addition to the changes outlined in this section, be sure to review "
"the :ref:`deprecation plan <deprecation-removed-in-1.5>` for any features "
"that have been removed. If you haven't updated your code within the "
"deprecation timeline for a given feature, its removal may appear as a "
"backwards incompatible change."
msgstr ""
"<deprecation-removed-in-1.5>Chomh maith leis na hathruithe a leagtar amach "
"sa chuid seo, déan cinnte athbhreithniú a dhéanamh ar an:ref: `plean "
"díréachtaithe `le haghaidh aon ghnéithe a baineadh. Mura ndearna tú do chód "
"a nuashonrú laistigh den amlíne díscoilte do ghné ar leith, d'fhéadfadh go "
"mbeadh sé a bhaint mar athrú neamh-chomhoiriúnach ar chúl."

msgid "``ALLOWED_HOSTS`` required in production"
msgstr "``ALLOWED_HOSTS`` ag teastáil i dtáirgeadh"

msgid ""
"The new :setting:`ALLOWED_HOSTS` setting validates the request's ``Host`` "
"header and protects against host-poisoning attacks. This setting is now "
"required whenever :setting:`DEBUG` is ``False``, or "
"else :meth:`django.http.HttpRequest.get_host()` will "
"raise :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.SuspiciousOperation`. For more details "
"see the :setting:`full documentation<ALLOWED_HOSTS>` for the new setting."
msgstr ""
"Bailíonn an socrú nua:setting: `ALLOWED_HOSTS` ceannteideal ``Host` an "
"iarratais agus cosnaíonn sé i gcoinne ionsaithe nimhithe óstach. Tá an socrú "
"seo ag teastáil anois nuair a bhíonn: socrú: `DEBUG` ``False``, nó eile: "
"meth: `django.http.httpRequest.get_host () `ardóidh: exc: "
"`~Django.Core.Exceptions.SuspiciousOperation`. Le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí "
"féach an:setting: `doiciméadú iomlán <ALLOWED_HOSTS>`don suíomh nua."

msgid "Managers on abstract models"
msgstr "Bainisteoirí ar samhlacha teibí"

msgid ""
"Abstract models are able to define a custom manager, and that "
"manager :ref:`will be inherited by any concrete models extending the "
"abstract model <custom-managers-and-inheritance>`. However, if you try to "
"use the abstract model to call a method on the manager, an exception will "
"now be raised. Previously, the call would have been permitted, but would "
"have failed as soon as any database operation was attempted (usually with a "
"\"table does not exist\" error from the database)."
msgstr ""
"<custom-managers-and-inheritance>Tá samhlacha teibí in ann bainisteoir "
"saincheaptha a shainiú, agus beidh an bainisteoir sin: ref: `oidhreacht ag "
"aon mhúnlaí coincréite a leathnaíonn an tsamhail teibí `. Mar sin féin, má "
"dhéanann tú iarracht an tsamhail teibí a úsáid chun modh a ghlaoch ar an "
"mbainisteoir, ardófar eisceacht anois. Roimhe seo, bheadh an glao ceadaithe, "
"ach theip air a luaithe a rinneadh iarracht ar aon oibríocht bunachar sonraí "
"(de ghnáth le earráid “níl tábla ann” ón mbunachar sonraí)."

msgid ""
"If you have functionality on a manager that you have been invoking using the "
"abstract class, you should migrate that logic to a Python ``staticmethod`` "
"or ``classmethod`` on the abstract class."
msgstr ""
"Má tá feidhmiúlacht agat ar bhainisteoir a bhí á ghairm agat ag baint úsáide "
"as an rang teibí, ba cheart duit an loighic sin a aistriú chuig "
"`staticmethod` nó `classmethod`` Python ar an rang teibí."

msgid "Context in year archive class-based views"
msgstr "Tuairimí rangbhunaithe ar chartlann comhthéacs i m"

msgid ""
"For consistency with the other date-based generic "
"views, :class:`~django.views.generic.dates.YearArchiveView` now passes "
"``year`` in the context as a :class:`datetime.date` rather than a string.  "
"If you are using ``{{ year }}`` in your templates, you must replace it with "
"``{{ year|date:\"Y\" }}``."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh comhsheasmhachta leis na tuairimí cineálacha dáta-bhunaithe "
"eile, téann: class: `~django.views.generic.dates.yearArchiveView` ``year "
"``sa chomhthéacs anois mar a:class: `datetime.date` seachas teaghrán. Má tá "
"``{{year}}`` á úsáid agat i do theimpléid, ní mór duit ``{{year|date: \"Y”}}"
"`` a chur in ionad."

msgid ""
"``next_year`` and ``previous_year`` were also added in the context. They are "
"calculated according to ``allow_empty`` and ``allow_future``."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh ``next_year`` agus ``roimh_year`` sa chomhthéacs freisin. Déantar "
"iad a ríomh de réir `allow_empty`` agus `allow_future``."

msgid "Context in year and month archive class-based views"
msgstr "Comhthéacs i dtuairimí rangbhunaithe i gcartlann bliana"

msgid ""
":class:`~django.views.generic.dates.YearArchiveView` "
"and :class:`~django.views.generic.dates.MonthArchiveView` were documented to "
"provide a ``date_list`` sorted in ascending order in the context, like their "
"function-based predecessors, but it actually was in descending order. In "
"1.5, the documented order was restored. You may want to add (or remove) the "
"``reversed`` keyword when you're iterating on ``date_list`` in a template:"
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.views.generic.dates.yearArchiveView` agus:class: "
"`~django.views.generic.dates.monthArchiveView` doiciméadaithe chun "
"`date_list`` a sholáthar in ord ardaitheach sa chomhthéacs, cosúil lena "
"réamhtheachtaí feidhmiúbhunaithe, ach bhí sé i ord íslitheach i ndáiríre. I "
"1.5, rinneadh an t-ordú doiciméadaithe ar ais. B'fhéidir gur mhaith leat an "
"eochairfhocal ``reversed`` a chur leis (nó a bhaint) agus tú ag athrú ar "
"`date_list`` i dteimpléad:"

msgid ""
":class:`~django.views.generic.dates.ArchiveIndexView` still provides a "
"``date_list`` in descending order."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.views.generic.dates.archiveIndexView` soláthraíonn "
"``date_list`` fós in ord íslitheach."

msgid "Context in TemplateView"
msgstr "Comhthéacs i TemplateView"

msgid ""
"For consistency with the design of the other generic "
"views, :class:`~django.views.generic.base.TemplateView` no longer passes a "
"``params`` dictionary into the context, instead passing the variables from "
"the URLconf directly into the context."
msgstr ""
"Le comhsheasmhacht le dearadh na dtuairimí cineálacha eile, ní "
"chuireann :class: `~django.views.generic.base.templateView` foclóir "
"`params`` isteach sa chomhthéacs a thuilleadh, ina ionad sin cuireann na "
"hathróga ón URLConf go díreach isteach sa chomhthéacs."

msgid "Non-form data in HTTP requests"
msgstr "Sonraí neamh-fhoirme in iarratais HTTP"

msgid ""
":attr:`request.POST <django.http.HttpRequest.POST>` will no longer include "
"data posted via HTTP requests with non form-specific content-types in the "
"header. In prior versions, data posted with content-types other "
"than :mimetype:`multipart/form-data` or :mimetype:`application/x-www-form-"
"urlencoded` would still end up represented in the :attr:`request.POST "
"<django.http.HttpRequest.POST>` attribute. Developers wishing to access the "
"raw POST data for these cases, should use the :attr:`request.body "
"<django.http.HttpRequest.body>` attribute instead."
msgstr ""
":attr: Ní chuimsíonn `Request.post <django.http.HttpRequest.POST>`sonraí a "
"phostáiltear trí iarratais HTTP le cineálacha ábhar neamh-shonracha "
"foirmeacha sa cheannteideal a thuilleadh. <django.http.HttpRequest.POST>I "
"leaganacha roimhe seo, bheadh sonraí a phostáiltear le cineálacha ábhair "
"seachas: mimetype: `multipart/form-data` nó: mimetype: `application/x-www-"
"form-urlencoded` ionadaíocht fós sa tréith: attr: `request.post `. "
"<django.http.HttpRequest.body>Ba chóir d'fhorbróirí ar mian leo rochtain a "
"fháil ar na sonraí amh POST do na cásanna seo, an tréith: attr: "
"`request.body `a úsáid ina ionad."

msgid ":data:`~django.core.signals.request_finished` signal"
msgstr ":data: comhartha `~django.core.signals.request_finished`"

msgid ""
"Django used to send the :data:`~django.core.signals.request_finished` signal "
"as soon as the view function returned a response. This interacted badly "
"with :ref:`streaming responses <httpresponse-streaming>` that delay content "
"generation."
msgstr ""
"D'úsáid Django an comhartha: data: `~django.core.signals.request_finished` a "
"sheoladh a luaithe a d'fhill an fheidhm amharc freagra. Idirghníomhaíodh sé "
"seo go dona le: ref: `freagraí sruthú <httpresponse-streaming>`a chuireann "
"moill ar ghiniúint ábhair."

msgid ""
"This signal is now sent after the content is fully consumed by the WSGI "
"gateway. This might be backwards incompatible if you rely on the signal "
"being fired before sending the response content to the client. If you do, "
"you should consider using :doc:`middleware </topics/http/middleware>` "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"Seoltar an comhartha seo anois tar éis an t-ábhar a ithe go hiomlán ag geata "
"WSGI. D'fhéadfadh sé seo a bheith neamhoiriúnach ar ais má bhíonn tú ag "
"brath ar an gcomhartha a dhúnadh sula gcuireann tú an t-ábhar freagartha "
"chuig an g Má dhéanann tú, ba chóir duit smaoineamh ar: doc: `middleware` a "
"úsáid ina ionad </topics/http/middleware>."

msgid ""
"Some WSGI servers and middleware do not always call ``close`` on the "
"response object after handling a request, most notably uWSGI prior to 1.2.6 "
"and Sentry's error reporting middleware up to 2.0.7. In those cases the "
"``request_finished`` signal isn't sent at all. This can result in idle "
"connections to database and memcache servers."
msgstr ""
"Ní ghlaonn roinnt freastalaithe WSGI agus meán-earraí “gar” i gcónaí ar an "
"réad freagartha tar éis iarratas a láimhseáil, go háirithe UWSGI roimh 1.2.6 "
"agus earráid Sentry ag tuairisciú meánghearraí suas le 2.0.7. Sna cásanna "
"sin ní sheoltar an comhartha ``request_finished` ar chor ar bith. "
"D'fhéadfadh naisc díomhaoin a bheith mar thoradh air seo le freastalaithe "
"bunachar sonraí agus memcache."

msgid "OPTIONS, PUT and DELETE requests in the test client"
msgstr "Iarrataí ROGHANNA, PUT agus DELETE sa chliant tástála"

msgid ""
"Unlike GET and POST, these HTTP methods aren't implemented by web browsers. "
"Rather, they're used in APIs, which transfer data in various formats such as "
"JSON or XML. Since such requests may contain arbitrary data, Django doesn't "
"attempt to decode their body."
msgstr ""
"Murab ionann agus GET agus POST, ní chuireann brabhsálaithe gréasáin na "
"modhanna HTTP seo i bhfeidhm. Ina ionad sin, úsáidtear iad in APIanna, a "
"aistríonn sonraí i bhformáidí éagsúla ar nós JSON nó XML. Ós rud é go "
"bhféadfadh sonraí treallacha a bheith sna hiarratais sin, ní dhéanann Django "
"iarracht a gcorp a dhíchódú."

msgid ""
"However, the test client used to build a query string for OPTIONS and DELETE "
"requests like for GET, and a request body for PUT requests like for POST. "
"This encoding was arbitrary and inconsistent with Django's behavior when it "
"receives the requests, so it was removed in Django 1.5."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, d'úsáid an cliant tástála teaghrán fiosrúcháin a thógáil le "
"haghaidh iarratais OPTIONS agus DELETE cosúil le GET, agus comhlacht "
"iarratais d'iarratais PUT cosúil le POST. Bhí an t-ionchódú seo treallach "
"agus neamhréidh le hiompar Django nuair a fhaigheann sé na hiarratais, mar "
"sin baineadh é i Django 1.5."

msgid ""
"If you were using the ``data`` parameter in an OPTIONS or a DELETE request, "
"you must convert it to a query string and append it to the ``path`` "
"parameter."
msgstr ""
"Má bhí an paraiméadar ``sonraí ``á úsáid agat i roghanna nó in iarratas "
"DELETE, ní mór duit é a thiontú go sreang fiosrúcháin agus é a chur leis an "
"bparaiméadar ``path`."

msgid ""
"If you were using the ``data`` parameter in a PUT request without a "
"``content_type``, you must encode your data before passing it to the test "
"client and set the ``content_type`` argument."
msgstr ""
"Má bhí an paraiméadar ``sonraí ``á úsáid agat in iarratas PUT gan "
"``content_type``, ní mór duit do chuid sonraí a ionchódú sula gcuirfidh tú "
"chuig an gcliant tástála iad agus an argóint ``content_type`` a shocrú."

msgid "System version of ``simplejson`` no longer used"
msgstr "Ní úsáidtear leagan an chórais de ``simplejson`` a thuilleadh"

msgid ""
":ref:`As explained below <simplejson-deprecation>`, Django 1.5 deprecates "
"``django.utils.simplejson`` in favor of Python 2.6's built-in :mod:`json` "
"module. In theory, this change is harmless. Unfortunately, because of "
"incompatibilities between versions of ``simplejson``, it may trigger errors "
"in some circumstances."
msgstr ""
":ref: `Mar a mhínítear thíos <simplejson-deprecation>`, déanann Django 1.5 "
"``django.utils.simplejson`` a dhíspreagadh i bhfabhar modúl ionsuite Python "
"2.6: mod: `json`. Go teoiric, tá an t-athrú seo neamhdhíobhálach. Ar an "
"drochuair, mar gheall ar neamhoiriúnachtaí idir leaganacha de `simplejson`, "
"d'fhéadfadh sé earráidí a spreagadh i gcúinsí áirithe."

msgid ""
"JSON-related features in Django 1.4 always used ``django.utils.simplejson``. "
"This module was actually:"
msgstr ""
"Baineann gnéithe a bhaineann le JSON i Django 1.4 úsáid as "
"``django.utils.simplejson`` i gcónaí. Ba é an modúl seo i ndáiríre:"

msgid ""
"A system version of ``simplejson``, if one was available (i.e. ``import "
"simplejson`` works), if it was more recent than Django's built-in copy or it "
"had the C speedups, or"
msgstr ""
"Leagan córais de `simplejson``, má bhí ceann ar fáil (ie oibreacha "
"``allmhairiú simplejson ``), má bhí sé níos déanaí ná cóip ionsuite Django "
"nó má bhí na luasanna C aige, nó"

msgid ""
"The :mod:`json` module from the standard library, if it was available (i.e. "
"Python 2.6 or greater), or"
msgstr ""
"An modúl: mod: `json` ón leabharlann caighdeánach, má bhí sé ar fáil (ie "
"Python 2.6 nó níos mó), nó"

msgid "A built-in copy of version 2.0.7 of ``simplejson``."
msgstr "Cóip ionsuite de leagan 2.0.7 de `simplejson``."

msgid ""
"In Django 1.5, those features use Python's :mod:`json` module, which is "
"based on version 2.0.9 of ``simplejson``."
msgstr ""
"I Django 1.5, úsáideann na gnéithe sin modúl Python: mod: `json`, atá "
"bunaithe ar leagan 2.0.9 de `simplejson`."

msgid ""
"There are no known incompatibilities between Django's copy of version 2.0.7 "
"and Python's copy of version 2.0.9. However, there are some "
"incompatibilities between other versions of ``simplejson``:"
msgstr ""
"Níl aon neamhoiriúnachtaí ar eolas idir cóip Django de leagan 2.0.7 agus "
"cóip Python de leagan 2.0.9. Mar sin féin, tá roinnt neamhoiriúnachtaí idir "
"leaganacha eile de `simplejson``:"

msgid ""
"While the ``simplejson`` API is documented as always returning Unicode "
"strings, the optional C implementation can return a bytestring. This was "
"fixed in Python 2.7."
msgstr ""
"Cé go ndéantar an API `simplejson`` doiciméadaithe mar atá i gcónaí ag "
"filleadh teaghráin Unicode, is féidir leis an gcur i bhfeidhm roghnach C "
"bytestring a thabhairt ar ais. Socraíodh é seo i Python 2.7."

msgid ""
"``simplejson.JSONEncoder`` gained a ``namedtuple_as_object`` keyword "
"argument in version 2.2."
msgstr ""
"Fuair ``simplejson.jsonEncoder`` argóint eochairfhocal "
"``namedtuple_as_object`` i leagan 2.2."

msgid ""
"More information on these incompatibilities is available in :ticket:`ticket "
"#18023 <18023#comment:10>`."
msgstr ""
"<18023 #comment:10>Tá tuilleadh eolais ar na neamhoiriúnachtaí seo ar fáil "
"in:ticéad: `ticéad # 18023`."

msgid ""
"The net result is that, if you have installed ``simplejson`` and your code "
"uses Django's serialization internals directly -- for instance "
"``django.core.serializers.json.DjangoJSONEncoder``, the switch from "
"``simplejson`` to :mod:`json` could break your code. (In general, changes to "
"internals aren't documented; we're making an exception here.)"
msgstr ""
"Is é an toradh glan ná, má tá `simplejson`` suiteáilte agat agus má "
"úsáideann do chód inmheánacha sraitheach Django go díreach - mar shampla "
"``django.core.serializers.json.djangojsonEncoder``, d'fhéadfadh an t-athrú ó "
"`simplejson`` go: mod: `json` do chód a bhriseadh. (Go ginearálta, ní "
"dhoiciméadaítear athruithe ar inmheánacha; táimid ag déanamh eisceacht "
"anseo.)"

msgid ""
"At this point, the maintainers of Django believe that using :mod:`json` from "
"the standard library offers the strongest guarantee of backwards-"
"compatibility. They recommend to use it from now on."
msgstr ""
"Ag an bpointe seo, creideann cothabháirí Django go dtugann úsáid: mod: "
"`json` ón leabharlann caighdeánach an ráthaíocht is láidre maidir le "
"comhoiriúnacht ar ais. Molann siad é a úsáid as seo amach."

msgid "String types of hasher method parameters"
msgstr "Cineálacha teaghrán de pharaiméadair modh hasher"

msgid ""
"If you have written a :ref:`custom password hasher <auth_password_storage>`, "
"your ``encode()``, ``verify()`` or ``safe_summary()`` methods should accept "
"Unicode parameters (``password``, ``salt`` or ``encoded``). If any of the "
"hashing methods need bytestrings, you can use "
"the :func:`~django.utils.encoding.force_bytes` utility to encode the strings."
msgstr ""
"Má scríobh tú a:ref: `pasfhocal saincheaptha hasher "
"<auth_password_storage>`, ba cheart do mhodhanna ``encode () ``, `verify "
"()`` nó ``safe_summary () ``glacadh le paraiméadair Unicode (`pasfhocal``, "
"`salt`` nó ``encoded ``). Má theastaíonn bytestrings ó aon cheann de na "
"modhanna hashing, is féidir leat an fóntais: func: "
"`~django.utils.encoding.force_bytes` a úsáid chun na teaghráin a ionchódú."

msgid "Validation of previous_page_number and next_page_number"
msgstr "Bailíochtú uimhir leathanaigh roimhe seo agus uimhir leathanaigh eile"

msgid ""
"When using :doc:`object pagination </topics/pagination>`, the "
"``previous_page_number()`` and ``next_page_number()`` methods of "
"the :class:`~django.core.paginator.Page` object did not check if the "
"returned number was inside the existing page range. It does check it now and "
"raises an :exc:`~django.core.paginator.InvalidPage` exception when the "
"number is either too low or too high."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a úsáideadh: doc: `leathanaigh réad`, níor sheiceáil na modhanna "
"``previous_page_number () ``agus`` next_page_number () ``den :class: "
"`~django.core.pagin</topics/pagination> ator.page` an raibh an uimhir ar ais "
"laistigh den raon leathanaigh atá ann cheana. Seiceálann sé é anois agus "
"ardaíonn sé eisceacht: exc: `~django.core.paginator.invalidPage` nuair a "
"bhíonn an uimhir ró-íseal nó ró-ard."

msgid "Behavior of autocommit database option on PostgreSQL changed"
msgstr "Athraigh iompar rogha bunachar sonraí autocommit ar PostgreSQL"

msgid ""
"PostgreSQL's autocommit option didn't work as advertised previously. It did "
"work for single transaction block, but after the first block was left the "
"autocommit behavior was never restored. This bug is now fixed in 1.5. While "
"this is only a bug fix, it is worth checking your applications behavior if "
"you are using PostgreSQL together with the autocommit option."
msgstr ""
"Níor oibrigh rogha autocommit PostgreSQL mar a fógraíodh roimhe seo. "
"D'oibrigh sé le haghaidh bloc idirbheart aonair, ach tar éis don chéad bhloc "
"a fhágáil níor athchóirigh an t-iompar uathchomhartha riamh. Tá an fabht seo "
"socraithe anois i 1.5. Cé nach é seo ach socrú fabht, is fiú iompar "
"d'iarratais a sheiceáil má tá PostgreSQL á úsáid agat mar aon leis an rogha "
"autocommit."

msgid "Session not saved on 500 responses"
msgstr "Níor shábháiltear an seisiún ar 500 freagra"

msgid ""
"Django's session middleware will skip saving the session data if the "
"response's status code is 500."
msgstr ""
"Sceapfaidh meán-earraí seisiúin Django sonraí na seisiúin a shábháil más é "
"cód stádais an fhreagra 500."

msgid "Email checks on failed admin login"
msgstr "Seiceálacha ríomhphoist ar theip isteach riaracháin"

msgid ""
"Prior to Django 1.5, if you attempted to log into the admin interface and "
"mistakenly used your email address instead of your username, the admin "
"interface would provide a warning advising that your email address was not "
"your username. In Django 1.5, the introduction of :ref:`custom user models "
"<auth-custom-user>` has required the removal of this warning. This doesn't "
"change the login behavior of the admin site; it only affects the warning "
"message that is displayed under one particular mode of login failure."
msgstr ""
"Roimh Django 1.5, má rinne tú iarracht logáil isteach sa chomhéadan "
"riaracháin agus má d'úsáid tú do sheoladh ríomhphoist ar dhearmad in ionad "
"d'ainm úsáideora, chuirfeadh an comhéadan riaracháin rabhadh ar fáil ag "
"tabhairt comhairle nach é d'ainm úsáideora do sheoladh ríomhphoist. I Django "
"1.5, bhí an rabhadh seo a bhaint ag tabhairt isteach: ref: `samhlacha <auth-"
"custom-user>úsáideora saincheaptha `. Ní athraíonn sé seo iompar logála "
"isteach an láithreáin riaracháin; ní théann sé i bhfeidhm ach ar an "
"teachtaireacht rabhaidh a thaispeántar faoi mhodh áirithe amháin de theip "
"logála isteach."

msgid "Changes in tests execution"
msgstr "Athruithe ar fhorghníomhaithe"

msgid ""
"Some changes have been introduced in the execution of tests that might be "
"backward-incompatible for some testing setups:"
msgstr ""
"Tugadh roinnt athruithe isteach maidir le tástálacha a fhorghníomhú a "
"d'fhéadfadh a bheith comhoiriúnach ar ais le haghaidh roinnt socruithe "
"tástála:"

msgid "Database flushing in ``django.test.TransactionTestCase``"
msgstr "Sruthú bunachar sonraí i ``Django.Test.TransactionTestCase``"

msgid ""
"Previously, the test database was truncated *before* each test run in "
"a :class:`~django.test.TransactionTestCase`."
msgstr ""
"Roimhe seo, gearradh an bunachar sonraí tástála* roimh* gach tástáil a "
"reáchtáil in a:class: `~ django.test.transactionTestCase`."

msgid ""
"In order to be able to run unit tests in any order and to make sure they are "
"always isolated from each other, :class:`~django.test.TransactionTestCase` "
"will now reset the database *after* each test run instead."
msgstr ""
"D'fhonn a bheith in ann tástálacha aonaid a reáchtáil in aon ord agus chun a "
"chinntiú go bhfuil siad scoite óna chéile i gcónaí, athshocróidh :class: "
"`~django.test.transactionTestCase` an bunachar sonraí anois* tar éis * gach "
"tástála a rith ina ionad."

msgid "No more implicit DB sequences reset"
msgstr "Gan níos mó seicheamh DB intuigthe a athshocrú"

msgid ""
":class:`~django.test.TransactionTestCase` tests used to reset primary key "
"sequences automatically together with the database flushing actions "
"described above."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.test.TransactionTestCase` tástálacha a úsáidtear chun "
"seicheamh príomhúil a athshocrú go huathoibríoch in éineacht leis na "
"gníomhartha sruthaithe bunachar sonraí a thuairiscítear thuas."

msgid ""
"This has been changed so no sequences are implicitly reset. This can "
"cause :class:`~django.test.TransactionTestCase` tests that depend on hard-"
"coded primary key values to break."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé seo athraithe ionas nach ndéantar aon seicheamh a athshocrú go "
"hinchinneach. Is féidir leis seo tástálacha: class: "
"`~django.test.transactionTestCase` a bhraitheann ar phríomhluachanna crua-"
"chódaithe le briseadh."

msgid ""
"The new :attr:`~django.test.TransactionTestCase.reset_sequences` attribute "
"can be used to force the old behavior "
"for :class:`~django.test.TransactionTestCase` that might need it."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an tréith nua:attr: "
"`~django.test.transactionTestCase.reset_sequences` a úsáid chun an sean-"
"iompar a chur i bhfeidhm le haghaidh: :class: "
"`~django.test.transactionTestCase` a d'fhéadfadh a bheith ag teastáil uathu."

msgid "Ordering of tests"
msgstr "Tástálacha a ordú"

msgid ""
"In order to make sure all ``TestCase`` code starts with a clean database, "
"tests are now executed in the following order:"
msgstr ""
"D'fhonn a chinntiú go dtosaíonn gach cód ``Testcase ``le bunachar sonraí "
"glan, déantar tástálacha a fhorghníomhú anois san ord seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"First, all unit tests "
"(including :class:`unittest.TestCase`, :class:`~django.test.SimpleTestCase`, :class:`~django.test.TestCase` "
"and :class:`~django.test.TransactionTestCase`) are run with no particular "
"ordering guaranteed nor enforced among them."
msgstr ""
"Ar dtús, reáchtáiltear gach tástáil aonaid (lena n-áir:class: "
"`UnitTest.TestCase`, :class: `~django.test.testcase`, :class: "
"`~django.test.testcase` agus:class: `~django.test.transactionTestCase`) gan "
"aon ordú ar leith ráthaithe ná a chur i bhfeidhm ina measc."

msgid ""
"Then any other tests (e.g. doctests) that may alter the database without "
"restoring it to its original state are run."
msgstr ""
"Ansin reáchtáiltear aon tástálacha eile (m.sh. doctests) a d'fhéadfadh an "
"bunachar sonraí a athrú gan é a chur ar ais go dtí a staid bhunaidh."

msgid ""
"This should not cause any problems unless you have existing doctests which "
"assume a :class:`~django.test.TransactionTestCase` executed earlier left "
"some database state behind or unit tests that rely on some form of state "
"being preserved after the execution of other tests. Such tests are already "
"very fragile, and must now be changed to be able to run independently."
msgstr ""
"Níor chóir go mbeadh aon fhadhbanna mar thoradh air seo mura bhfuil doctests "
"ann cheana agat a ghlacann le a:class: `~django.test.TransactionTestCase` "
"forghníomhaithe níos luaithe d'fhág roinnt stát bunachar sonraí taobh thiar "
"de nó tástálacha aonaid a bhíonn ag brath ar chineál éigin stáit á chaomhnú "
"tar éis tástálacha eile a chur i bhfeidhm. Tá tástálacha den sórt sin an-"
"leochaileach cheana féin, agus caithfear iad a athrú anois le bheith in ann "
"rith go neamhspleách."

msgid "``cleaned_data`` dictionary kept for invalid forms"
msgstr ""
"Foclóir ``cleaned_data`` a choimeádtar le haghaidh foirmeacha neamhbhailí"

msgid ""
"The :attr:`~django.forms.Form.cleaned_data` dictionary is now always present "
"after form validation. When the form doesn't validate, it contains only the "
"fields that passed validation. You should test the success of the validation "
"with the :meth:`~django.forms.Form.is_valid()` method and not with the "
"presence or absence of the :attr:`~django.forms.Form.cleaned_data` attribute "
"on the form."
msgstr ""
"Tá an foclóir:attr: `~django.forms.form.cleaned_data` i láthair anois i "
"gcónaí tar éis bailíochtú foirme. Nuair nach ndéanann an fhoirm bailíochtú, "
"níl ann ach na réimsí a rith bailíochtú. Ba chóir duit rath na "
"bailíochtaithe a thástáil leis an modh:meth: `~django.forms.form.is_valid () "
"`agus ní le láithreacht nó easpa an tréith: :attr: "
"`~Django.forms.form.Cleaned_Data` ar an bhfoirm."

msgid "Behavior of ``syncdb`` with multiple databases"
msgstr "Iompar ``syncdb`` le bunachair sonraí iolracha"

msgid ""
"``syncdb`` now queries the database routers to determine if content types "
"(when :mod:`~django.contrib.contenttypes` is enabled) and permissions "
"(when :mod:`~django.contrib.auth` is enabled) should be created in the "
"target database. Previously, it created them in the default database, even "
"when another database was specified with the ``--database`` option."
msgstr ""
"Fiosraíonn ``syncdb`` anois ar na ródairí bunachar sonraí chun a fháil amach "
"an bhfuil cineálacha ábhair (nuair: mod: `~django.contrib.contenttypes` "
"cumasaithe) agus ceadanna (nuai:mod: `~django.contrib.auth` cumasaithe) a "
"chruthú sa spriocbhunachar sonraí. Roimhe seo, chruthaigh sé iad sa "
"bhunachar sonraí réamhshocraithe, fiú nuair a sonraíodh bunachar sonraí eile "
"leis an rogha ``--database`."

msgid ""
"If you use ``syncdb`` on multiple databases, you should ensure that your "
"routers allow synchronizing content types and permissions to only one of "
"them. See the docs on the :ref:`behavior of contrib apps with multiple "
"databases <contrib_app_multiple_databases>` for more information."
msgstr ""
"Má úsáideann tú ``syncdb`` ar iliomad bunachair sonraí, ba cheart duit a "
"chinntiú go gceadaíonn do ródairí cineálacha agus ceadanna ábhair a "
"shioncronú do cheann amháin acu. <contrib_app_multiple_databases>Féach na "
"doiciméid ar an: ref: `iompar aipeanna contrib le bunachair sonraí iolracha "
"`le tuilleadh faisnéise le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise."

msgid "XML deserializer will not parse documents with a DTD"
msgstr "Ní dhéanfaidh deserializer XML doiciméid a pháirseáil le DTD"

msgid ""
"In order to prevent exposure to denial-of-service attacks related to "
"external entity references and entity expansion, the XML model deserializer "
"now refuses to parse XML documents containing a DTD (DOCTYPE definition). "
"Since the XML serializer does not output a DTD, this will not impact typical "
"usage, only cases where custom-created XML documents are passed to Django's "
"model deserializer."
msgstr ""
"D'fhonn nochtadh d'ionsaithe diúltaithe seirbhíse a bhaineann le tagairtí "
"eintiteas seachtracha agus leathnú eintiteas a chosc, diúltaíonn an dí-"
"erializer samhail XML anois doiciméid XML ina bhfuil DTD (sainmhíniú "
"DOCTYPE) a pháirseáil. Ós rud é nach n-aschuireann an serializer XML DTD, ní "
"bheidh tionchar aige seo ar úsáid tipiciúil, ach cásanna ina gcuirtear "
"cáipéisí XML cruthaithe saincheaptha ar aghaidh chuig dísherializer samhail "
"Django."

msgid "Formsets default ``max_num``"
msgstr "Foirmsets réamhshocraithe ``max_num``"

msgid ""
"A (default) value of ``None`` for the ``max_num`` argument to a formset "
"factory no longer defaults to allowing any number of forms in the formset. "
"Instead, in order to prevent memory-exhaustion attacks, it now defaults to a "
"limit of 1000 forms. This limit can be raised by explicitly setting a higher "
"value for ``max_num``."
msgstr ""
"Ní réamhshocraíonn luach (réamhshocraithe) ``None`` don argóint ``max_num`` "
"chuig monarcha tacar foirmeacha a thuilleadh chun aon líon foirmeacha a "
"cheadú sa tacar foirme. Ina áit sin, d'fhonn ionsaithe ídithe cuimhne a "
"chosc, réamhshocraíonn sé anois teorainn 1000 foirm. Is féidir an teorainn "
"seo a ardú trí luach níos airde a shocrú go sainráite do `max_num``."

msgid ""
":class:`django.forms.ModelMultipleChoiceField` now returns an empty "
"``QuerySet`` as the empty value instead of an empty list."
msgstr ""
":class: `Django.Forms.ModelMultipleChoiceField` filleann ``QuerySet`` folamh "
"anois mar an luach folamh in ionad liosta folamh."

msgid ""
":func:`~django.utils.http.int_to_base36` properly raises a :exc:`TypeError` "
"instead of :exc:`ValueError` for non-integer inputs."
msgstr ""
":func: Ardaíonn `~django.utils.http.int_to_base36` i gceart a:exc: "
"`TypeError` in ionad:exc: `ValueError` le haghaidh ionchuir neamh-sláireach."

msgid ""
"The ``slugify`` template filter is now available as a standard Python "
"function at :func:`django.utils.text.slugify`. Similarly, ``remove_tags`` is "
"available at ``django.utils.html.remove_tags()``."
msgstr ""
"Tá an scagaire teimpléad ``slugify` ar fáil anois mar fheidhm chaighdeánach "
"Python ag:func: `django.utils.text.slugify`. Ar an gcaoi chéanna, tá "
"`remove_tags`` ar fáil ag ``django.utils.html.remove_tags () ``."

msgid ""
"Uploaded files are no longer created as executable by default. If you need "
"them to be executable change :setting:`FILE_UPLOAD_PERMISSIONS` to your "
"needs. The new default value is ``0o666`` (octal) and the current umask "
"value is first masked out."
msgstr ""
"Ní chruthaítear comhaid uaslódáilte a thuilleadh mar fhorghníomhachtaithe "
"Más gá duit iad a bheith infheidhmithe athraigh: setting: "
"`FILE_UPLOAD_PERMISSIONS` do chuid riachtanas. Is é `0o666`` (octal) an "
"luach réamhshocraithe nua agus cuirtear an luach umask reatha a chumasc "
"amach ar dtús."

msgid ""
"The :class:`F expressions <django.db.models.F>` supported bitwise operators "
"by ``&`` and ``|``. These operators are now available using ``.bitand()`` "
"and ``.bitor()`` instead. The removal of ``&`` and ``|`` was done to be "
"consistent with :ref:`Q() expressions <complex-lookups-with-q>` and "
"``QuerySet`` combining where the operators are used as boolean AND and OR "
"operators."
msgstr ""
"Thacaigh an: aicme: abairtí `F `le hoibreoirí gi <django.db.models.F>otáin "
"le `&`` agus ``|``. Tá na hoibreoirí seo ar fáil anois ag baint úsáide as "
"``.bitand () ``agus ``.bitor ()`` ina ionad. Rinneadh `&`` agus ``|`` a "
"bhaint le bheith comhsheasmhach le:ref: `Q () abairtí `agus ``<complex-"
"lookups-with-q>QuerySet`` ag comhcheangal nuair a úsáidtear na hoibreoirí "
"mar oibreoirí boolean AND agus OR."

msgid ""
"In a ``filter()`` call, when :class:`F expressions <django.db.models.F>` "
"contained lookups spanning multi-valued relations, they didn't always reuse "
"the same relations as other lookups along the same chain. This was changed, "
"and now F() expressions will always use the same relations as other lookups "
"within the same ``filter()`` call."
msgstr ""
"I nglao ``filter () ``, nuair a bhí cuardaigh ag abairtí `class: `F "
"<django.db.models.F>`a chuimsíonn caidreamh illuachmhar, níor athúsáid siad "
"na caidreamh céanna i gcónaí le cuardaigh eile ar feadh an slabhra céanna. "
"Athraíodh é seo, agus anois úsáidfidh nathanna F () na caidreamh céanna i "
"gcónaí le cuardaigh eile laistigh den ghlao ``filter () `céanna."

msgid ""
"The :ttag:`csrf_token` template tag is no longer enclosed in a div. If you "
"need HTML validation against pre-HTML5 Strict DTDs, you should add a div "
"around it in your pages."
msgstr ""
"Níl an clib teimpléad: ttag: `csrf_token` iata i div a thuilleadh. Má "
"theastaíonn bailíochtú HTML uait i gcoinne DTDanna docht réamh-HTML5, ba "
"cheart duit div a chur timpeall air i do leathanaigh."

msgid ""
"The template tags library ``adminmedia``, which only contained the "
"deprecated template tag ``{% admin_media_prefix %}``, was removed. "
"Attempting to load it with ``{% load adminmedia %}`` will fail. If your "
"templates still contain that line you must remove it."
msgstr ""
"Baineadh na leabharlann clibeanna teimpléad ``adminmedia``, nach raibh ach "
"an chlib teimpléad díscoite ``{% admin_media_prefix%}``. Teipfidh iarracht é "
"a luchtú le ``{% load adminmedia%}``. Má tá an líne sin fós i do theimpléid "
"ní mór duit í a bhaint."

msgid ""
"Because of an implementation oversight, it was possible to "
"use :doc:`django.contrib.redirects </ref/contrib/redirects>` without "
"enabling :doc:`django.contrib.sites </ref/contrib/sites>`. This isn't "
"allowed any longer. If you're using ``django.contrib.redirects``, make "
"sure :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` contains ``django.contrib.sites``."
msgstr ""
"Mar gheall ar mhaoirseacht cur chun feidhme, bhí sé in ann: doc: "
"`django.contrib.redirects` a úsáid gan cumasú:doc: `django</ref/contrib/"
"redirects> </ref/contrib/sites> .contrib.sites`. Ní cheadaítear é seo a "
"thuilleadh. Má tá `django.contrib.redirects`` á úsáid agat, déan cinnte go "
"bhfuil ``django.contrib.sites`` sa `SETTING: `INSTALLED_APPS`."

msgid ""
":meth:`BoundField.label_tag <django.forms.BoundField.label_tag>` now escapes "
"its ``contents`` argument. To avoid the HTML escaping, "
"use :func:`django.utils.safestring.mark_safe` on the argument before passing "
"it."
msgstr ""
"<django.forms.BoundField.label_tag>:meth: Éalaíonn `BoundField.label_tag "
"`anois dá argóint ``contents``. Chun an HTML a sheachaint, bain úsáid as: "
"func: `django.utils.safestring.mark_safe` ar an argóint sula ndéantar é a "
"rith."

msgid ""
"Accessing reverse one-to-one relations fetched "
"via :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.select_related` now "
"raises :exc:`~django.db.models.Model.DoesNotExist` instead of returning "
"``None``."
msgstr ""
"Fuarthas rochtain a fháil ar chaidrimh aon-le-duine ar ais trí:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.select_related` anois:exc: "
"`~django.db.models.model.doesNotExist` in ionad ``None`` a thabhairt ar ais."

msgid "Features deprecated in 1.5"
msgstr "Gnéithe atá díscríofa i 1.5"

msgid "``django.contrib.localflavor``"
msgstr "``django.contrib.localflavor``"

msgid ""
"The localflavor contrib app has been split into separate packages. "
"``django.contrib.localflavor`` itself will be removed in Django 1.6, after "
"an accelerated deprecation."
msgstr ""
"Tá an aip contrib localflavour roinnte i bpacáistí ar leithligh. Bainfear "
"``django.contrib.localflavor`` féin i Django 1.6, tar éis díscríobh "
"luathaithe."

msgid ""
"The new packages are available on GitHub. The core team cannot efficiently "
"maintain these packages in the long term — it spans just a dozen countries "
"at this time; similar to translations, maintenance will be handed over to "
"interested members of the community."
msgstr ""
"Tá na pacáistí nua ar fáil ar GitHub. Ní féidir leis an bcroífhoireann na "
"pacáistí seo a chothabháil go héifeachtúil san fhadtéarma - ní chuimsíonn sé "
"ach dosaen tíortha ag an am seo; cosúil le haistriúcháin, tabharfar "
"cothabháil ar fáil do bhaill den phobal a bhfuil suim acu."

msgid "``django.contrib.markup``"
msgstr "``django.contrib.markup``"

msgid ""
"The markup contrib module has been deprecated and will follow an accelerated "
"deprecation schedule. Direct use of Python markup libraries or 3rd party tag "
"libraries is preferred to Django maintaining this functionality in the "
"framework."
msgstr ""
"Tá an modúl contrib marcála díscoite agus leanfaidh sé sceideal luathaithe "
"díluasaithe. Is fearr úsáid dhíreach leabharlanna marcála Python nó "
"leabharlanna clibeanna tríú páirtí ná Django a choinneáil an fheidhmiúlacht "
"seo sa chreat."

msgid "``AUTH_PROFILE_MODULE``"
msgstr "``AUTH_PROFILE_MODULE ``"

msgid ""
"With the introduction of :ref:`custom user models <auth-custom-user>`, there "
"is no longer any need for a built-in mechanism to store user profile data."
msgstr ""
"Agus: ref: `samhlacha úsáideora saincheaptha <auth-custom-user>`a thabhairt "
"isteach, níl aon ghá le meicníocht ionsuite a thuilleadh chun sonraí próifíl "
"úsáideora a stóráil."

msgid ""
"You can still define user profiles models that have a one-to-one relation "
"with the User model - in fact, for many applications needing to associate "
"data with a User account, this will be an appropriate design pattern to "
"follow. However, the ``AUTH_PROFILE_MODULE`` setting, and the "
"``django.contrib.auth.models.User.get_profile()`` method for accessing the "
"user profile model, should not be used any longer."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat samhlacha próifílí úsáideora a shainiú fós a bhfuil gaol "
"duine le duine acu leis an tsamhail Úsáideora - i ndáiríre, i gcás go leor "
"feidhmchlár a theastaíonn sonraí a cheangal le cuntas Úsáideora, is patrún "
"dearaidh iomchuí é seo le leanúint. Mar sin féin, níor cheart an socrú "
"``AUTH_PROFILE_MODULE``, agus an modh "
"``Django.contrib.auth.models.user.get_profile () ``chun rochtain a fháil ar "
"an tsamhail phróifíl úsáideora, a úsáid a thuilleadh."

msgid "Streaming behavior of :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse`"
msgstr "Iompar sruthú de:aicme: `~django.http.httpResponse`"

msgid ""
"Django 1.5 deprecates the ability to stream a response by passing an "
"iterator to :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse`. If you rely on this "
"behavior, switch to :class:`~django.http.StreamingHttpResponse`. "
"See :ref:`explicit-streaming-responses` above."
msgstr ""
"Déanann Django 1.5 an cumas freagra a shruthú trí athraitheoir a chur chuig: "
"class: `~django.http.httpResponse`. Má tá tú ag brath ar an iompar seo, "
"aistrigh chu:class: `~django.http.StreamInghttPresponse`. Féach:ref: "
"`explicit-streaming-freagrais` thuas."

msgid ""
"In Django 1.7 and above, the iterator will be consumed immediately "
"by :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse`."
msgstr ""
"I Django 1.7 agus os a chionn, ídífear an t-athraitheoir láithreach:class: "
"`~django.http.httpResponse`."

msgid "``django.utils.simplejson``"
msgstr "``django.utils.simplejson``"

msgid ""
"Since Django 1.5 drops support for Python 2.5, we can now rely on "
"the :mod:`json` module being available in Python's standard library, so "
"we've removed our own copy of ``simplejson``. You should now "
"import :mod:`json` instead of ``django.utils.simplejson``."
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é go dtiteann Django 1.5 tacaíocht do Python 2.5, is féidir linn "
"brath anois ar an modúl: mod: `json` atá ar fáil i leabharlann chaighdeánach "
"Python, mar sin tá ár gcóip féin de `simplejson`` bainte againn. Ba chóir "
"duit anois: mod: `json` a iompórtáil in ionad ``django.utils.simplejson``."

msgid ""
"Unfortunately, this change might have unwanted side-effects, because of "
"incompatibilities between versions of ``simplejson`` -- see "
"the :ref:`backwards-incompatible changes <simplejson-incompatibilities>` "
"section. If you rely on features added to ``simplejson`` after it became "
"Python's :mod:`json`, you should import ``simplejson`` explicitly."
msgstr ""
"<simplejson-incompatibilities>Ar an drochuair, d'fhéadfadh fo-iarsmaí nach "
"dteastaíonn a bheith ag an athrú seo, mar gheall ar neamhoiriúnachtaí idir "
"leaganacha de ``simplejson`` - féach an roinn:ref: `athruithe neamh-"
"inchomhoiriúnacha '. Má tá tú ag brath ar ghnéithe a chuirtear le "
"`simplejson`` tar éis dó a bheith ina Python 's:mod: `json`, ba cheart duit "
"``simplejson`` a iompórtáil go sainráite."

msgid "``django.utils.encoding.StrAndUnicode``"
msgstr "``Django.Utils.Encoding.StrandUnicode``"

msgid ""
"The ``django.utils.encoding.StrAndUnicode`` mix-in has been deprecated. "
"Define a ``__str__`` method and apply the "
"``django.utils.encoding.python_2_unicode_compatible`` decorator instead."
msgstr ""
"Tá an meascán ``Django.Utils.Encoding.StrandUnicode`` díluaite. Sainmhínigh "
"modh ``__str__`` agus cuir an maisitheoir "
"``django.utils.encoding.python_2_unicode_compatible`` i bhfeidhm ina ionad."

msgid "``django.utils.itercompat.product``"
msgstr "``django.utils.itercompat.product``"

msgid ""
"The ``django.utils.itercompat.product`` function has been deprecated. Use "
"the built-in :func:`itertools.product` instead."
msgstr ""
"Tá an fheidhm ``django.utils.itercompat.product`` díluaite. Úsáid an "
"bunaithe:func: `itertools.product` ina ionad."

msgid "``cleanup`` management command"
msgstr "Ordú bainistíochta ``glantacha``"

msgid ""
"The ``cleanup`` management command has been deprecated and replaced "
"by :djadmin:`clearsessions`."
msgstr ""
"Tá an t-ordú bainistíochta ``glantach`` a dhíchur agus cuireadh: djadmin: "
"`clearsessions` ina ionad."

msgid "``daily_cleanup.py`` script"
msgstr "Script ``daily_cleanup.py``"

msgid ""
"The undocumented ``daily_cleanup.py`` script has been deprecated. Use "
"the :djadmin:`clearsessions` management command instead."
msgstr ""
"Tá an script ``daily_cleanup.py`` neamhdhoiciméadaithe a dhíchur. Úsáid an t-"
"ordú bainistíochta: djadmin: `clearsessions` ina ionad."

msgid "``depth`` keyword argument in ``select_related``"
msgstr "``doimhneacht ``argóint eochairfhocal i ``roghnaithe_related``"

msgid ""
"The ``depth`` keyword argument "
"in :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.select_related` has been "
"deprecated. You should use field names instead."
msgstr ""
"Tá an argóint eochairfhocal ``depth`` in:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.select_related` díluaite. Ba chóir duit "
"ainmneacha réimse a úsáid ina ionad."

msgid "Django 1.5.1 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.5.1"

msgid "*March 28, 2013*"
msgstr "*28 Márta, 2013*"

msgid ""
"This is Django 1.5.1, a bugfix release for Django 1.5. It's completely "
"backwards compatible with Django 1.5, but includes a handful of fixes."
msgstr ""
"Seo Django 1.5.1, scaoileadh bugfix do Django 1.5. Tá sé comhoiriúnach go "
"hiomlán ar ais le Django 1.5, ach tá dornán socruithe ann."

msgid ""
"The biggest fix is for a memory leak introduced in Django 1.5. Under certain "
"circumstances, repeated iteration over querysets could leak memory - "
"sometimes quite a bit of it. If you'd like more information, the details are "
"in :ticket:`our ticket tracker <19895>` (and in :bpo:`a related issue "
"<17468>` in Python itself)."
msgstr ""
"Is é an socrú is mó ná sceitheadh cuimhne a tugadh isteach i Django 1.5. "
"Faoi imthosca áirithe, d'fhéadfadh athrú arís agus arís eile thar "
"cheisteanna cuimhne a sceitheadh - uaireanta beagán de. <17468>Más mian leat "
"tuilleadh faisnéise, tá na sonraí in:ticket: `ár rianaitheoir ticéad "
"<19895>`(agus in:bpo: `saincheist ghaolmhar` i Python féin)."

msgid ""
"If you've noticed memory problems under Django 1.5, upgrading to 1.5.1 "
"should fix those issues."
msgstr ""
"Má thug tú faoi deara fadhbanna cuimhne faoi Django 1.5, ba cheart go "
"réiteodh uasghrádú go 1.5.1 na fadhbanna sin."

msgid "Django 1.5.1 also includes a couple smaller fixes:"
msgstr "Cuimsíonn Django 1.5.1 cúpla socruithe níos lú freisin:"

msgid ""
"Module-level warnings emitted during tests are no longer silently hidden "
"(:ticket:`18985`)."
msgstr ""
"Ní chuirtear rabhaidh ar leibhéal an mhodúil a astaítear le linn tástálacha "
"i bhfolach go ciúin a thuilleadh (:ticket: `18985`)."

msgid ""
"Prevented filtering on password hashes in the user admin (:ticket:`20078`)."
msgstr ""
"Cosc ar scagadh ar hashes pasfhocal i riarachán an úsáideora (:ticket: "
"`20078`)."

msgid "Django 1.5.10 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.5.10"

msgid "Django 1.5.10 fixes a regression in the 1.5.9 security release."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.5.10 aischéimniú sa scaoileadh slándála 1.5.9."

msgid "Django 1.5.11 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.5.11"

msgid "Django 1.5.11 fixes a couple regressions in the 1.5.9 security release."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.5.11 cúpla aischéimniú sa scaoileadh slándála 1.5.9."

msgid "Django 1.5.12 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.5.12"

msgid "Django 1.5.12 fixes a regression in the 1.5.9 security release."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.5.12 aischéimniú sa scaoileadh slándála 1.5.9."

msgid "Django 1.5.2 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.5.2"

msgid "This is Django 1.5.2, a bugfix and security release for Django 1.5."
msgstr "Seo Django 1.5.2, scaoileadh bugfix agus slándála do Django 1.5."

msgid "XSS vulnerability in :mod:`django.contrib.admin`"
msgstr "Leochaileacht XSS in:mod: `django.contrib.admin `"

msgid ""
"If a :class:`~django.db.models.URLField` is used in Django 1.5, it displays "
"the current value of the field and a link to the target on the admin change "
"page. The display routine of this widget was flawed and allowed for XSS."
msgstr ""
"Má úsáidtear a:class: `~Django.db.Models.URLField` i Django 1.5, taispeánann "
"sé luach reatha an réimse agus nasc leis an sprioc ar an leathanach "
"athraithe riaracháin. Bhí gnáthamh taispeána an ghuirléid seo lochtach agus "
"ceadaíodh do XSS."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash with :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.prefetch_related` "
"(#19607) as well as some ``pickle`` regressions with ``prefetch_related`` "
"(#20157 and #20257)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste le:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.prefetch_related` (#19607) chomh maith le "
"roinnt aischéimnithe ``pickle`` le `prefetch_related`` (#20157 agus #20257)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression in :mod:`django.contrib.gis` in the Google Map output on "
"Python 3 (#20773)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú in:mod: `django.contrib.gis` san aschur Google Map ar "
"Python 3 (#20773)."

msgid ""
"Made ``DjangoTestSuiteRunner.setup_databases`` properly handle aliases for "
"the default database (#19940) and prevented ``teardown_databases`` from "
"attempting to tear down aliases (#20681)."
msgstr ""
"Rinne sé ``DjangoTestSuiterunner.setup_databases`` ainmneacha a láimhseáil i "
"gceart don bhunachar sonraí réamhshocraithe (#19940) agus chuir sé cosc ar "
"``teardown_databases`` iarracht a chur síos ainmneacha (#20681)."

msgid ""
"Fixed the ``django.core.cache.backends.memcached.MemcachedCache`` backend's "
"``get_many()`` method on Python 3 (#20722)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh an modh ``get_many () ``cúltaca "
"``django.core.cache.backends.memcachedCache`` ar Python 3 (#20722)."

msgid ""
"Fixed :mod:`django.contrib.humanize` translation syntax errors. Affected "
"languages: Mexican Spanish, Mongolian, Romanian, Turkish (#20695)."
msgstr ""
"Socraithe:mod: earráidí comhréireachta aistriúcháin "
"`django.contrib.humanize`. Teangacha tionchair: Spáinnis Mheicsiceo, "
"Mongóilis, Rómáinis, Tuircis (#20695)."

msgid "Added support for wheel packages (#19252)."
msgstr "Tacaíocht bhreise do phacáistí roth (#19252)."

msgid "The CSRF token now rotates when a user logs in."
msgstr "Rothlaíonn an comhartha CSRF anois nuair a logálann úsáideoir isteach."

msgid "Some Python 3 compatibility fixes including #20212 and #20025."
msgstr ""
"Roinnt socruithe comhoiriúnachta Python 3 lena n-áirítear #20212 agus #20025."

msgid ""
"Fixed some rare cases where :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.get` "
"exceptions recursed infinitely (#20278)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh roinnt cásanna neamhchoitianta ina ndéantar eisceachtaí: meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.get` athfhillteach gan teorainn (#20278)."

msgid ""
":djadmin:`makemessages` no longer crashes with ``UnicodeDecodeError`` "
"(#20354)."
msgstr ""
":djadmin: ní théiteann `makemessages` le `UnicodeDecodeError`` (#20354) a "
"thuilleadh."

msgid "Fixed ``geojson`` detection with SpatiaLite."
msgstr "Braite seasta ``geojson`` le SpatiaLite."

msgid ""
":meth:`~django.test.SimpleTestCase.assertContains` once again works with "
"binary content (#20237)."
msgstr ""
":meth: `~django.test.simpletestCase.assertContains` oibríonn arís le hábhar "
"dénártha (#20237)."

msgid ""
"Fixed :class:`~django.db.models.ManyToManyField` if it has a Unicode "
"``name`` parameter (#20207)."
msgstr ""
"Socraithe:Class: `~django.db.models.manyToManyField` má tá paraiméadar "
"Unicode ``ainm ``aige (#20207)."

msgid ""
"Ensured that the WSGI request's path is correctly based on the "
"``SCRIPT_NAME`` environment variable or the :setting:`FORCE_SCRIPT_NAME` "
"setting, regardless of whether or not either has a trailing slash (#20169)."
msgstr ""
"Cinntigh sé go bhfuil cosán an iarratais WSGI bunaithe i gceart ar an athróg "
"comhshaoil ``SCRIPT_NAME`` nó ar an socrú: `FORCE_SCRIPT_NAME`, is cuma cibé "
"an bhfuil slash rianaithe (#20169) nó nach bhfuil."

msgid "Django 1.5.3 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.5.3"

msgid ""
"This is Django 1.5.3, the third release in the Django 1.5 series. It "
"addresses one security issue and also contains an opt-in feature to enhance "
"the security of :mod:`django.contrib.sessions`."
msgstr ""
"Is é seo Django 1.5.3, an tríú eisiúint sa tsraith Django 1.5. Tugann sé "
"aghaidh ar shaincheist slándála amháin agus tá gné roghnaithe ann freisin "
"chun slándáil: mod: `django.contrib.sessions` a fheabhsú."

msgid ""
"Mitigating a remote-code execution vulnerability "
"in :mod:`django.contrib.sessions`"
msgstr ""
"Leochaileacht forghníomhaithe iargúlta cód a mhaolú in:mod: "
"`django.contrib.sessions`"

msgid ""
":mod:`django.contrib.sessions` currently uses :mod:`pickle` to serialize "
"session data before storing it in the backend. If you're using "
"the :ref:`signed cookie session backend<cookie-session-backend>` "
"and :setting:`SECRET_KEY` is known by an attacker (there isn't an inherent "
"vulnerability in Django that would cause it to leak), the attacker could "
"insert a string into their session which, when unpickled, executes arbitrary "
"code on the server. The technique for doing so is simple and easily "
"available on the internet. Although the cookie session storage signs the "
"cookie-stored data to prevent tampering, a :setting:`SECRET_KEY` leak "
"immediately escalates to a remote code execution vulnerability."
msgstr ""
":mod: `django.contrib.sessions` úsáideann: mod: `pickle` faoi láthair chun "
"sonraí seisiúin a shraitheadh sula ndéantar iad a stóráil sa chúltaca. Má tá "
"cúltaca seisi <cookie-session-backend>úin fianán sínithe á úsáid agat: "
"agus:setting: `SECRET_KEY` is aithne ag ionsaitheoir (níl leochaileacht "
"bhunúsach i Django a chuirfeadh sé sceitheadh), d'fhéadfadh an t-"
"ionsaitheoir teaghrán a chur isteach ina seisiún a fhorghníomhaíonn cód "
"treallach ar an bhfreastalaí. Tá an teicníc chun é sin a dhéanamh simplí "
"agus ar fáil go héasca ar an idirlíon. Cé go síníonn stóráil seisiún fianán "
"na sonraí atá stóráilte ag fianán chun cur isteach a chosc, méadaíonn "
"sceitheadh a: setting: `SECRET_KEY` láithreach go leochaileacht iargúlta "
"forghníomhaithe cód."

msgid ""
"This attack can be mitigated by serializing session data using JSON rather "
"than :mod:`pickle`. To facilitate this, Django 1.5.3 introduces a new "
"setting, :setting:`SESSION_SERIALIZER`, to customize the session "
"serialization format. For backwards compatibility, this setting defaults to "
"using :mod:`pickle`. While JSON serialization does not support all Python "
"objects like :mod:`pickle` does, we highly recommend switching to JSON-"
"serialized values. Also, as JSON requires string keys, you will likely run "
"into problems if you are using non-string keys in ``request.session``. See "
"the :ref:`session_serialization` documentation for more details."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an t-ionsaí seo a mhaolú trí shraitheadh sonraí seisiúin ag baint "
"úsáide as JSON seachas: mod: `pickle`. Chun é seo a éascú, tugann Django "
"1.5.3 suíomh nua isteach, :setting: `SESSION_SERIALIZER`, chun an fhormáid "
"sraitheach seisiúin a shaincheapadh. Maidir le comhoiriúnacht ar ais, "
"réamhshocraíonn an socrú seo le húsáid: mod: `pickle`. Cé nach dtacaíonn "
"sraith JSON le gach réad Python cosúil:mod: `pickle` a dhéanann, molaimid go "
"mór aistriú chuig luachanna sraith JSON. Chomh maith leis sin, toisc go "
"dteastaíonn eochracha teaghrán ag JSON, is dócha go mbeidh fadhbanna ort má "
"tá eochracha neamh-sreang á úsáid agat i `request.session ``. Féach an "
"doiciméadach:ref: `session_serialization` le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid "Django 1.5.4 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.5.4"

msgid ""
"This is Django 1.5.4, the fourth release in the Django 1.5 series. It "
"addresses two security issues and one bug."
msgstr ""
"Is é seo Django 1.5.4, an ceathrú eisiúint sa tsraith Django 1.5. Tugann sé "
"aghaidh ar dhá shaincheist slándála agus fabht amháin."

msgid ""
"As of 1.5.4, Django's authentication framework imposes a 4096-byte limit on "
"passwords, and will fail authentication with any submitted password of "
"greater length."
msgstr ""
"Amhail 1.5.4, cuireann creat fíordheimhnithe Django teorainn 4096 beart ar "
"phasfhocail, agus teipeann sé ar fhíordheimhniú le haon phasfhocal curtha "
"isteach de fhad níos mó."

msgid ""
"Fixed a bug that prevented a ``QuerySet`` that "
"uses :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.prefetch_related` from being "
"pickled and unpickled more than once (the second pickling attempt raised an "
"exception) (#21102)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh fabht a chuir cosc ar ``QuerySet`` a úsáideas:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.prefetch_related` ó bheith picilte agus "
"gan piceáil níos mó ná uair amháin (d'ardaigh an dara iarracht piceála "
"eisceacht) (#21102)."

msgid "Django 1.5.5 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.5.5"

msgid ""
"Django 1.5.5 fixes a couple security-related bugs and several other bugs in "
"the 1.5 series."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.5.5 cúpla fabhtanna a bhaineann le slándáil agus roinnt "
"fabhtanna eile sa tsraith 1.5."

msgid ""
"Django 1.5.4 imposes a 4096-byte limit on passwords in order to mitigate a "
"denial-of-service attack through submission of bogus but extremely large "
"passwords. In Django 1.5.5, we've reverted this change and instead improved "
"the speed of our PBKDF2 algorithm by not rehashing the key on every "
"iteration."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann Django 1.5.4 teorainn 4096 beart ar phasfhocail d'fhonn ionsaí "
"diúltaithe seirbhíse a mhaolú trí phasfhocail bhréagacha ach thar a bheith "
"mór a chur isteach. I Django 1.5.5, rinneamar an t-athrú seo ar ais agus ina "
"ionad sin feabhsaigh muid luas ár algartam PBKDF2 trí gan an eochair ar gach "
"athrá a athdhéanamh."

msgid "Properly rotate CSRF token on login"
msgstr "Rothlaigh comhartha CSRF i gceart ar logáil isteach"

msgid ""
"This behavior introduced as a security hardening measure in Django 1.5.2 did "
"not work properly and is now fixed."
msgstr ""
"Níor oibrigh an t-iompar seo a tugadh isteach mar bheart cruasaithe slándála "
"i Django 1.5.2 i gceart agus tá sé socraithe anois."

msgid ""
"Fixed a Python 3 incompatibility in "
"``django.utils.text.unescape_entities()`` (#21185)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh neamhchomhoiriúnacht Python 3 i ``django.utils.text.unescape_entity "
"() ``(#21185)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a couple data corruption issues with ``QuerySet`` edge cases under "
"Oracle and MySQL (#21203, #21126)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh cúpla saincheist éillithe sonraí le cásanna imeall ``QuerySet "
"``faoi Oracle agus MySQL (#21203, #21126)."

msgid ""
"Fixed crashes when using combinations of ``annotate()``, "
"``select_related()``, and ``only()`` (#16436)."
msgstr ""
"Timpeanna seasta nuair a úsáidtear teaglaim de ``annotate () ``, "
"`select_related ()``, agus ``only () ``(#16436)."

msgid ""
"The undocumented ``django.core.servers.basehttp.WSGIServerException`` has "
"been removed. Use ``socket.error`` provided by the standard library instead."
msgstr ""
"Baineadh an ``django.core.servers.basehttp.wsgiserverexception`` gan "
"doiciméadú. Úsáid ``socket.error`` a sholáthraíonn an leabharlann "
"caighdeánach ina ionad."

msgid "Django 1.5.6 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.5.6"

msgid ""
"Django 1.5.6 fixes several bugs in 1.5.5, including three security issues."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.5.6 roinnt fabhtanna i 1.5.5, lena n-áirítear trí "
"shaincheist slándála."

msgid ""
"Fixed :class:`~django.contrib.auth.backends.ModelBackend` raising "
"``UnboundLocalError`` if :func:`~django.contrib.auth.get_user_model` raised "
"an error (#21439)."
msgstr ""
"Soced:Class: `~django.contrib.auth.backends.modelBackend` ag ardú "
"``UnBoundLocalError`` if: func: `~django.contrib.auth.get_user_model` "
"earráid (#21439)."

msgid ""
"Additionally, Django's vendored version of six, ``django.utils.six``, has "
"been upgraded to the latest release (1.6.1)."
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, tá leagan díolta Django de sé, ``django.utils.six ``, "
"uasghrádaithe go dtí an eisiúint is déanaí (1.6.1)."

msgid "Django 1.5.7 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.5.7"

msgid "Django 1.5.7 fixes a regression in the 1.5.6 security release."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.5.7 aischéimniú sa scaoileadh slándála 1.5.6."

msgid "Django 1.5.8 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.5.8"

msgid "Django 1.5.8 fixes two security issues in 1.5.8."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.5.8 dhá shaincheist slándála i 1.5.8."

msgid "Django 1.5.9 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.5.9"

msgid "Django 1.5.9 fixes several security issues in 1.5.8."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.5.9 roinnt saincheisteanna slándála i 1.5.8."

msgid "Django 1.6 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.6"

msgid "Dedicated to Malcolm Tredinnick"
msgstr "Tiomnaithe do Malcolm Tredinnick"

msgid ""
"On March 17, 2013, the Django project and the free software community lost a "
"very dear friend and developer."
msgstr ""
"Ar 17 Márta, 2013, chaill tionscadal Django agus an pobal bogearraí saor in "
"aisce cara agus forbróir an-daor."

msgid ""
"Malcolm was a long-time contributor to Django, a model community member, a "
"brilliant mind, and a friend. His contributions to Django — and to many "
"other open source projects — are nearly impossible to enumerate. Many on the "
"core Django team had their first patches reviewed by him; his mentorship "
"enriched us. His consideration, patience, and dedication will always be an "
"inspiration to us."
msgstr ""
"Bhí Malcolm ina rannchuiditheoir fadtréimhse le Django, ball samhail "
"phobail, intinn iontach, agus cara. Tá sé beagnach dodhéanta a chuid "
"ranníocaíochtaí le Django - agus le go leor tionscadal foinse oscailte eile "
"- a chur in iúl. Rinne sé athbhreithniú ar a gcéad phaistí ag go leor ar an "
"gcroífhoireann Django; saibhrigh a mheantóireacht sinn. Beidh a mheas, a "
"fhoighne agus a thiomantas ina inspioráid dúinn i gcónaí."

msgid "This release of Django is for Malcolm."
msgstr "Tá an scaoileadh seo de Django do Malcolm."

msgid "-- The Django Developers"
msgstr "- Forbróirí Django"

msgid "Welcome to Django 1.6!"
msgstr "Fáilte go dtí Django 1.6!"

msgid ""
"These release notes cover the :ref:`new features <whats-new-1.6>`, as well "
"as some :ref:`backwards incompatible changes <backwards-incompatible-1.6>` "
"you'll want to be aware of when upgrading from Django 1.5 or older versions. "
"We've also dropped some features, which are detailed in :ref:`our "
"deprecation plan <deprecation-removed-in-1.6>`, and we've :ref:`begun the "
"deprecation process for some features <deprecated-features-1.6>`."
msgstr ""
"Clúdaíonn na nótaí scaoilte seo na:ref: `gnéithe nua <whats-new-1.6>`, chomh "
"maith le roinnt: ref: `athruithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha ar chúl<backwards-"
"incompatible-1.6>` a mbeidh tú ag iarraidh a bheith ar an eolas fúthu agus "
"tú ag uasghrádú ó Django 1.5 nó leaganacha níos sine. <deprecated-"
"features-1.6>Tá roinnt gnéithe titim againn freisin, atá mionsonraithe "
"in:ref: `ár bplean díghabhála <deprecation-removed-in-1.6>`, agus "
"chuireamaire:ref: `tús leis an bpróiseas díghabhála do roinnt gnéithe`."

msgid ""
"Django 1.6, like Django 1.5, requires Python 2.6.5 or above. Python 3 is "
"also officially supported. We **highly recommend** the latest minor release "
"for each supported Python series (2.6.X, 2.7.X, 3.2.X, and 3.3.X)."
msgstr ""
"Éilíonn Django 1.6, cosúil le Django 1.5, Python 2.6.5 nó os a chionn. "
"Tacaítear le Python 3 go hoifigiúil freisin. Molaimid** go hard** an "
"mionscaoileadh is déanaí do gach sraith Python tacaithe (2.6.X, 2.7.X, "
"3.2.X, agus 3.3.X)."

msgid ""
"Django 1.6 will be the final release series to support Python 2.6; beginning "
"with Django 1.7, the minimum supported Python version will be 2.7."
msgstr ""
"Beidh Django 1.6 an tsraith scaoilte deiridh chun tacú le Python 2.6; ag "
"tosú le Django 1.7, is é 2.7 an leagan Python íosta a thacaítear."

msgid "Python 3.4 is not supported, but support will be added in Django 1.7."
msgstr "Ní thacaítear le Python 3.4, ach cuirfear tacaíocht leis i Django 1.7."

msgid "What's new in Django 1.6"
msgstr "Cad atá nua i Django 1.6"

msgid "Simplified default project and app templates"
msgstr "Teimpléid tionscadail réamhshocraithe agus aip"

msgid ""
"The default templates used by :djadmin:`startproject` "
"and :djadmin:`startapp` have been simplified and modernized. The :doc:`admin "
"</ref/contrib/admin/index>` is now enabled by default in new projects; "
"the :doc:`sites </ref/contrib/sites>` framework no longer "
"is. :ref:`clickjacking prevention <clickjacking-prevention>` is now on and "
"the database defaults to SQLite."
msgstr ""
"Tá na teimpléid réamhshocraithe a úsáideann: djadmin: `startproject` "
"agus:djadmin: `startapp` simplithe agus nuachóirithe. Tá an: doc: `admin` </"
"ref/contrib/admin/index> cumasaithe anois de réir réamhshocraithe i "
"dtionscadail nua; níl an creat:doc: `sites</ref/contrib/sites> `a "
"thuilleadh. :ref: Tá `cosc clickjacking <clickjacking-prevention>`ar siúl "
"anois agus tá an bunachar sonraí réamhshocraithe go SQLite."

msgid ""
"If the default templates don't suit your tastes, you can use :ref:`custom "
"project and app templates <custom-app-and-project-templates>`."
msgstr ""
"<custom-app-and-project-templates>Mura n-oireann na teimpléid "
"réamhshocraithe do do chlas, is féidir leat: ref: `teimpléid tionscadail "
"agus aipeanna saincheaptha `a úsáid."

msgid "Improved transaction management"
msgstr "Bainistíocht idirbheart níos fearr"

msgid ""
"Django's transaction management was overhauled. Database-level autocommit is "
"now turned on by default. This makes transaction handling more explicit and "
"should improve performance. The existing APIs were deprecated, and new APIs "
"were introduced, as described in the :doc:`transaction management docs </"
"topics/db/transactions>`."
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh athchóiriú ar bhainistíocht idirbheart Django. Tá autocommit ar "
"leibhéal bunachar sonraí casaithe air anois de réir réamhshocraithe. Fágann "
"sé seo láimhseáil idirbheart níos folláine agus ba cheart go bhfeabhsó "
"Rinneadh na APIs atá ann cheana a dhíchur, agus tugadh APIs nua isteach, mar "
"a thuairiscítear in:doc: `doiciméid bainistíochta idirbhearta` </topics/db/"
"transactions>."

msgid "Persistent database connections"
msgstr "Nasc bunachar sonraí leanúnacha"

msgid ""
"Django now supports reusing the same database connection for several "
"requests. This avoids the overhead of reestablishing a connection at the "
"beginning of each request. For backwards compatibility, this feature is "
"disabled by default. See :ref:`persistent-database-connections` for details."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn Django anois leis an nasc bunachar sonraí céanna a athúsáid le "
"haghaidh roinnt iarratais. Seachnaíonn sé seo an lasbhreas a bhaineann le "
"nasc a athbhunú ag tús gach iarratais. Le haghaidh comhoiriúnacht ar ais, tá "
"an ghné seo díchumasaithe de réir réamhshocraithe Féach: ref: `persistent-"
"database-nastions` le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid "Discovery of tests in any test module"
msgstr "Tástálacha a fháil in aon mhodúl tástála"

msgid ""
"Django 1.6 ships with a new test runner that allows more flexibility in the "
"location of tests. The previous runner "
"(``django.test.simple.DjangoTestSuiteRunner``) found tests only in the "
"``models.py`` and ``tests.py`` modules of a Python package "
"in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`."
msgstr ""
"Seolann Django 1.6 le rádálaí tástála nua a cheadaíonn níos mó solúbthachta "
"i suíomh na dtástálacha. Ní bhfuair an rádálaí roimhe seo "
"(`Django.test.simple.DjangoTestSuiterunner``) tástálacha ach sna modúil "
"``models.py`` agus ``tests.py`` de phacáiste Python in:setting: "
"`INSTALLED_APPS`."

msgid ""
"The new runner (``django.test.runner.DiscoverRunner``) uses the test "
"discovery features built into ``unittest2`` (the version of ``unittest`` in "
"the Python 2.7+ standard library, and bundled with Django). With test "
"discovery, tests can be located in any module whose name matches the pattern "
"``test*.py``."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann an rádálaí nua (``Django.Test.Runner.DiscoverRunner``) na gnéithe "
"fionnachtana tástála atá tógtha i `unittest2`` (an leagan de ``unittest`` sa "
"leabharlann caighdeánach Python 2.7+, agus curtha le Django). Le "
"fionnachtain tástála, is féidir tástálacha a shuíomh in aon mhodúl a "
"mheaitseálann a n-ainm leis an bpatrún ``test*.py``."

msgid ""
"In addition, the test labels provided to ``./manage.py test`` to nominate "
"specific tests to run must now be full Python dotted paths (or directory "
"paths), rather than ``applabel.TestCase.test_method_name`` pseudo-paths. "
"This allows running tests located anywhere in your codebase, rather than "
"only in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`. For more details, see :doc:`/topics/"
"testing/index`."
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, cuireadh na lipéid tástála ar fáil do ``. Caithfidh "
"tástáil /manage.py chun tástálacha sonracha a ainmniú le reáchtáil caithfidh "
"cosáin iomlána poncaí Python (nó cosáin eolaire) a bheith anois, seachas "
"``Applabel.TestCase.test_METHOD_name`` bréag-bhealaí. Ligeann sé seo "
"tástálacha a reáchtáil atá suite in áit ar bith i do bhunachar cóid, seachas "
"in: setting: `INSTALLED_APPS` amháin. Le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí, "
"féach:doc: `/topics/tástáil/innéacs `."

msgid ""
"This change is backwards-incompatible; see the :ref:`backwards-"
"incompatibility notes<new-test-runner>`."
msgstr ""
"<new-test-runner>Tá an t-athrú seo chomhoiriúnach ar chúl; féach na:ref: "
"`nótaí neamh-inchomhoiriúnachta ar ais `."

msgid "Time zone aware aggregation"
msgstr "Comhiomlánú feasach ar chrios ama"

msgid ""
"The support for :doc:`time zones </topics/i18n/timezones>` introduced in "
"Django 1.4 didn't work well with :meth:`QuerySet.dates() "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.dates>`: aggregation was always performed "
"in UTC. This limitation was lifted in Django 1.6. "
"Use :meth:`QuerySet.datetimes() <django.db.models.query.QuerySet.datetimes>` "
"to perform time zone aware aggregation on "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.DateTimeField`."
msgstr ""
"</topics/i18n/timezones> <django.db.models.query.QuerySet.dates>Níor oibrigh "
"an tacaíocht do: doc: `criosanna ama' a tugadh isteach i Django 1.4 go maith "
"le: meth: `QuerySet.dates () `: rinneadh comhiomlánú i gcónaí i UTC. "
"Ardaíodh an teorannú seo i Django 1.6. Úsáid: Meth: `QuerySet.DateTimes () "
"`chun comhiomlánú feasach ar chrios ama a a: class: "
"`~django.db.models.DateTime "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.datetimes>Field`."

msgid "Support for savepoints in SQLite"
msgstr "Tacaíocht do phointí sábhála i SQLite"

msgid ""
"Django 1.6 adds support for savepoints in SQLite, with "
"some :ref:`limitations <savepoints-in-sqlite>`."
msgstr ""
"<savepoints-in-sqlite>Cuireann Django 1.6 tacaíocht le haghaidh pointí "
"sábhála i SQLite, le roinnt: ref: `teorainneacha `."

msgid "``BinaryField`` model field"
msgstr "Réimse samhail ``Binaryfield``"

msgid ""
"A new :class:`django.db.models.BinaryField` model field allows storage of "
"raw binary data in the database."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn réimse samhail nua:class: `Django.db.Models.BinaryField` sonraí "
"dénártha amh a stóráil sa bhunachar sonraí."

msgid "GeoDjango form widgets"
msgstr "Giuirléidí foirm GeodJango"

msgid ""
"GeoDjango now provides :doc:`form fields and widgets </ref/contrib/gis/forms-"
"api>` for its geo-specialized fields. They are OpenLayers-based by default, "
"but they can be customized to use any other JS framework."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn GeodJango anois:doc: `réimsí foirm agus giuirléid' dá réimsí "
"geo-speisialaithe. </ref/contrib/gis/forms-api> Tá siad bunaithe ar "
"OpenLayers de réir réamhshocraithe, ach is féidir iad a shaincheapadh chun "
"aon creat JS eile a úsáid."

msgid "``check`` management command added for verifying compatibility"
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh ordú bainistíochta “seiceáil” leis chun comhoiriúnacht a fhíor"

msgid ""
"A :djadmin:`check` management command was added, enabling you to verify if "
"your current configuration (currently oriented at settings) is compatible "
"with the current version of Django."
msgstr ""
"A: DjaDmin: Cuireadh ordú bainistíochta 'check' leis, rud a chuireann ar "
"chumas duit a fhíorú an bhfuil do chumraíocht reatha (dírithe ar shocruithe "
"faoi láthair) comhoiriúnach leis an leagan reatha de Django."

msgid ":meth:`Model.save() <django.db.models.Model.save()>` algorithm changed"
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.Model.save () >:meth: Athraigh algartam `Model.save ()"

msgid ""
"The :meth:`Model.save() <django.db.models.Model.save()>` method now tries to "
"directly ``UPDATE`` the database if the instance has a primary key value. "
"Previously ``SELECT`` was performed to determine if ``UPDATE`` or ``INSERT`` "
"were needed. The new algorithm needs only one query for updating an existing "
"row while the old algorithm needed two. See :meth:`Model.save() "
"<django.db.models.Model.save()>` for more details."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an modh: Meth: `Model.save () iarracht anois "
"``<django.db.models.Model.save () > UPDATE`` an bunachar sonraí a dhéanamh "
"go díreach má tá príomhluach ag an gcás. Roimhe seo rinneadh ``SELECT`` chun "
"a chinneadh an raibh gá le ``UPDATE`` nó ``INSERT``. Níl ach ceist amháin ag "
"teastáil ón algartam nua chun sraith atá ann cheana a nuashonrú agus bhí dhá "
"cheann ag teastáil ar an sean- <django.db.models.Model.save () >Féach: Meth: "
"`Model.save () `le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid ""
"In some rare cases the database doesn't report that a matching row was found "
"when doing an ``UPDATE``. An example is the PostgreSQL ``ON UPDATE`` trigger "
"which returns ``NULL``. In such cases it is possible to "
"set :attr:`django.db.models.Options.select_on_save` flag to force saving to "
"use the old algorithm."
msgstr ""
"I roinnt cásanna neamhchoitianta ní thuairiscíonn an bunachar sonraí gur "
"aimsíodh sraith mheaitseála nuair a dhéantar ``UPDATE``. Sampla is ea an "
"truicear PostgreSQL ``ON UPDATE`` a fhilleann ``NULL``. I gcásanna den sórt "
"sin is féidir bratach: attr: `django.db.models.options.select_on_save` a "
"shocrú chun sábháil a chur i bhfeidhm chun an sean-algartam a úsáid."

msgid ""
"Authentication backends can raise ``PermissionDenied`` to immediately fail "
"the authentication chain."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le cúltaca fíordheimhnithe ``Ceaduithead`` a ardú chun teip ar an "
"slabhra fíordheimhnithe láithreach."

msgid ""
"The ``HttpOnly`` flag can be set on the CSRF cookie "
"with :setting:`CSRF_COOKIE_HTTPONLY`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an bhratach `HTTPONLY` a shocrú ar an bhfianán CSRF le:setting: "
"`CSRF_COOKIE_HTTPONLY`."

msgid ""
"The ``assertQuerysetEqual()`` now checks for undefined order and "
"raises :exc:`ValueError` if undefined order is spotted. The order is seen as "
"undefined if the given ``QuerySet`` isn't ordered and there is more than one "
"ordered value to compare against."
msgstr ""
"Seiceálann an ``assertQuerySetEqual () ``anois ar ordú neamhshainithe agus "
"ardaíonn sé: exc: `ValueError` má fheictear ordú neamhshainithe. Feictear go "
"bhfuil an t-ordú neamhshainithe mura n-ordaítear an ``QuerySet` a thugtar "
"agus tá níos mó ná luach ordaithe amháin le comparáid a dhéanamh ina gcoinne."

msgid ""
"Added :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.earliest` for symmetry "
"with :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.latest`."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh leis: Meth: `~django.db.models.query.queryset.earliest` le haghaidh "
"siméadracht le:meth: `~django.db.models.query.queryset.latest`."

msgid ""
"In addition to :lookup:`year`, :lookup:`month` and :lookup:`day`, the ORM "
"now supports :lookup:`hour`, :lookup:`minute` and :lookup:`second` lookups."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith le:lookup: `year`, :lookup: `month` agus:lookup: `day`, tacaíonn "
"an ORM anois:lookup: `hour`, :lookup: `nóiméad` agus:lookup: `soicin` "
"cuardaigh."

msgid "Django now wraps all :pep:`249` exceptions."
msgstr "Fillteann Django anois gach eisceacht: pep: `249`."

msgid ""
"The default widgets "
"for :class:`~django.forms.EmailField`, :class:`~django.forms.URLField`, :class:`~django.forms.IntegerField`, :class:`~django.forms.FloatField` "
"and :class:`~django.forms.DecimalField` use the new type attributes "
"available in HTML5 (``type='email'``, ``type='url'``, ``type='number'``). "
"Note that due to erratic support of the ``number`` input type with localized "
"numbers in current browsers, Django only uses it when numeric fields are not "
"localized."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann na giuirléidí réamhshocraithe daga:class: "
"`~django.forms.emailField`, :class: `~django.forms.URLField`, :class: "
"`~django.forms.IntegerField`, :class: `~django.forms.floatfield` agus:class: "
"`~django.forms.decimalfield` na tréithe nua cineál atá ar fáil i HTML5 "
"(``type = 'email'`, `type = 'url ``, `type = 'url``, `type = 'uimhre'``). "
"Tabhair faoi deara, mar gheall ar thacaíocht neamhréitiúil don chineál "
"ionchuir ``uimhir ``le huimhreacha logánaithe i mbrabhsálaithe reatha, ní "
"úsáideann Django é ach nuair nach bhfuil réimsí uimhriúla logánaithe."

msgid ""
"The ``number`` argument for :ref:`lazy plural translations <lazy-plural-"
"translations>` can be provided at translation time rather than at definition "
"time."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an argóint ``uimhre`` d':ref: `aistriúcháin iolrach leisciúil "
"<lazy-plural-translations>`a sholáthar ag am aistriúcháin seachas ag am "
"sainmhínithe."

msgid ""
"For custom management commands: Verification of the presence of valid "
"settings in commands that ask for it by using the "
"``BaseCommand.can_import_settings`` internal option is now performed "
"independently from handling of the locale that should be active during the "
"execution of the command. The latter can now be influenced by the new "
"``BaseCommand.leave_locale_alone`` internal option. See :ref:`management-"
"commands-and-locales` for more details."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le horduithe bainistíochta saincheaptha: Déantar fíorú ar láithreacht "
"socruithe bailí in orduithe a iarrann é tríd an rogha inmheánach "
"``BaseCommand.CAN_IMPORT_SETTINGS` a úsáid go neamhspleách ó láimhseáil an "
"áitiúil ba chóir a bheith gníomhach le linn forghníomhú an ordaithe. Is "
"féidir leis an rogha inmheánach nua ``BaseCommand.leave_locale_alone`` "
"tionchar a imirt ar an dara ceann anois. Féach:ref: `management-commands-and-"
"locales` le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid ""
"The :attr:`~django.views.generic.edit.DeletionMixin.success_url` "
"of :class:`~django.views.generic.edit.DeletionMixin` is now interpolated "
"with its ``object``’s ``__dict__``."
msgstr ""
"Tá an: Attr: `~django.views.generic.edit.deletionMixin.success_URL` o:class: "
"`~django.views.generic.edit.deletionMixin` idirphóilte anois le ``__dict__`` "
"a `object``."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.http.HttpResponseRedirect` "
"and :class:`~django.http.HttpResponsePermanentRedirect` now provide an "
"``url`` attribute (equivalent to the URL the response will redirect to)."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.http.httpResponsereDirect` agus:class: "
"`~django.http.httpResponsePermanentDirect` tréith ``url ``anois (comhionann "
"leis an URL a atreoróidh an freagra chuig)."

msgid ""
"The ``MemcachedCache`` cache backend now uses the latest :mod:`pickle` "
"protocol available."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann cúltaca taisce ``MemcachedCache`` an prótacal is déanaí:mod: "
"`pickle` atá ar fáil anois."

msgid ""
"Added :class:`~django.contrib.messages.views.SuccessMessageMixin` which "
"provides a ``success_message`` attribute "
"for :class:`~django.views.generic.edit.FormView` based classes."
msgstr ""
"Added:Class: `~django.contrib.messages.views.successMessageMixin` a "
"sholáthraíonn tréith ``success_message`` d'aicmí bunaithe le haghaidh: "
"class: `~django.views.generic.edit.formView` ranganna bunaithe."

msgid ""
"Added the :attr:`django.db.models.ForeignKey.db_constraint` "
"and :attr:`django.db.models.ManyToManyField.db_constraint` options."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh na roghanna: attr: `Django.db.Models.ForeignKey.DB_Constraint` "
"agus:attr: `Django.db.Models.manyTomanyField.DB_Constraint` leis."

msgid ""
"The jQuery library embedded in the admin has been upgraded to version 1.9.1."
msgstr ""
"Tá an leabharlann jQuery leabaithe sa riarachán uasghrádaithe go leagan "
"1.9.1."

msgid ""
"Syndication feeds (:mod:`django.contrib.syndication`) can now pass extra "
"context through to feed templates using a new :meth:`Feed.get_context_data() "
"<django.contrib.syndication.Feed.get_context_data>` callback."
msgstr ""
"<django.contrib.syndication.Feed.get_context_data>Is féidir le fothaí "
"sindiciúcháin (:mod: `django.contrib.syndication`) comhthéacs breise a chur "
"tríd anois chun teimpléid a bheathú ag baint úsáide as glao nua: meth: "
"`feed.get_context_data () `."

msgid ""
"The admin list columns have a ``column-<field_name>`` class in the HTML so "
"the columns header can be styled with CSS, e.g. to set a column width."
msgstr ""
"Tá <field_name>rang ```column- ``ag na colúin liosta riaracháin sa HTML "
"ionas gur féidir ceanntásc na gcolún a stíleáil le CSS, m.sh. chun leithead "
"colún a shocrú."

msgid ""
"The :ref:`isolation level<database-isolation-level>` can be customized under "
"PostgreSQL."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an: Ref: `leibhéal aonrú <database-isolation-level>`a "
"shaincheapadh faoi PostgreSQL."

msgid ""
"The :ttag:`blocktrans` template tag now respects "
"``TEMPLATE_STRING_IF_INVALID`` for variables not present in the context, "
"just like other template constructs."
msgstr ""
"Tá meas anois ag an gclib teimpléad:ttag: `blocktrans` "
"``TEMPLATE_STRING_IF_INVALID`` d'athróga nach bhfuil i láthair sa "
"chomhthéacs, díreach cosúil le tógáil teimpléad eile."

msgid ""
"``SimpleLazyObject``\\s will now present more helpful representations in "
"shell debugging situations."
msgstr ""
"Cuirfidh ``SimpleLazyObject``\\ s léirithe níos cabhrach i láthair anois i "
"gcásanna dífhabhtaithe bhlaosc."

msgid ""
"Generic :class:`~django.contrib.gis.db.models.GeometryField` is now editable "
"with the OpenLayers widget in the admin."
msgstr ""
"Gineálach:Class: `~django.contrib.gis.db.models.geometryfield` is féidir a "
"chur in eagar anois leis an ngiuirléid OpenLayers sa riarachán."

msgid ""
"The documentation contains a :doc:`deployment checklist </howto/deployment/"
"checklist>`."
msgstr ""
"Tá a: doc: `seicliosta imscartáil` sa doiciméad</howto/deployment/checklist> "
"ú."

msgid "The :djadmin:`diffsettings` command gained a ``--all`` option."
msgstr "Fuair an t-ordú: Djadmin: `diffsettings` rogha ``--all``."

msgid ""
"``django.forms.fields.Field.__init__`` now calls ``super()``, allowing field "
"mixins to implement ``__init__()`` methods that will reliably be called."
msgstr ""
"``Django.Forms.Fields.Field. Glaonn __init__`` anois ``super () ``, ag "
"ligean do mheascáin allamuigh modhanna ``__init__ ()`` a chur i bhfeidhm a "
"ghlaofar go hiontaofa."

msgid ""
"The ``validate_max`` parameter was added to ``BaseFormSet`` "
"and :func:`~django.forms.formsets.formset_factory`, and ``ModelForm`` and "
"inline versions of the same.  The behavior of validation for formsets with "
"``max_num`` was clarified.  The previously undocumented behavior that "
"hardened formsets against memory exhaustion attacks was documented, and the "
"undocumented limit of the higher of 1000 or ``max_num`` forms was changed so "
"it is always 1000 more than ``max_num``."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an paraiméadar ``validate_max`` le `BaseFormSet`` agus:func: "
"`~django.forms.formsets.formset_factory`, agus ``ModelForm`` agus leaganacha "
"inlíne den chéanna. Soiléiríodh iompar bailíochtaithe do fhoirmeacha le "
"``max_num``. Rinneadh doiciméadú ar an iompar neamhdhoiciméadaithe roimhe "
"seo a chruaigh foirmeacha i gcoinne ionsaithe ídithe cuimhne, agus athraíodh "
"teorainn neamhdhoiciméadaithe na bhfoirmeacha níos airde 1000 nó ``max_num`` "
"mar sin tá sé 1000 níos mó ná `max_num`` i gcónaí."

msgid ""
"Added ``BCryptSHA256PasswordHasher`` to resolve the password truncation "
"issue with bcrypt."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh `bcryptsha256PasswordHasher`` leis chun an saincheist a bhriseadh "
"pasfhocal le bcrypt a réiteach."

msgid ""
":pypi:`Pillow` is now the preferred image manipulation library to use with "
"Django. :pypi:`PIL` is pending deprecation (support to be removed in Django "
"1.8). To upgrade, you should **first** uninstall PIL, **then** install "
"Pillow."
msgstr ""
":pypi:Is é `Pillow` an leabharlann ionramhála íomhá is fearr le húsáid le "
"Django anois. :pypi: Tá `PIL` ar feitheamh dímheasa (tacaíocht le baint as "
"Django 1.8). Chun uasghrádú a dhéanamh, ba cheart duit **PIL a dhíshuiteáil "
"ar dtús, ** ansin ** Pillow a shuiteáil."

msgid ":class:`~django.forms.ModelForm` accepts several new ``Meta`` options."
msgstr ""
":class: `~Django.Forms.ModelForm` glacann le roinnt roghanna ``Meta`` nua."

msgid ""
"Fields included in the ``localized_fields`` list will be localized (by "
"setting ``localize`` on the form field)."
msgstr ""
"Déanfar réimsí atá san áireamh sa liosta ``localized_fields`` logánaithe "
"(trí ``localize`` a shocrú ar an réimse foirme)."

msgid ""
"The  ``labels``, ``help_texts`` and ``error_messages`` options may be used "
"to customize the default fields, see :ref:`modelforms-overriding-default-"
"fields` for details."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir na roghanna ``labels``, `help_texts`` agus ``error_messages`` a "
"úsáid chun na réimsí réamhshocraithe a shaincheapadh, féach:ref: `modelforms-"
"overriding-default-fields` le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid ""
"The ``choices`` argument to model fields now accepts an iterable of "
"iterables instead of requiring an iterable of lists or tuples."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an argóint ``roghnaí`` le réimsí samhlacha anois le athrinnithe "
"athraitheacha in ionad athraitheanta liostaí nó tupáil a bheith ag teastáil."

msgid ""
"The reason phrase can be customized in HTTP responses "
"using :attr:`~django.http.HttpResponse.reason_phrase`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an abairt chúis a shaincheapadh i bhfreagraí HTTP ag baint "
"úsáidea:attr: `~django.http.httpResponse.Reason_Phrase`."

msgid ""
"When giving the URL of the next page for "
"``django.contrib.auth.views.logout()``, "
"``django.contrib.auth.views.password_reset()``, "
"``django.contrib.auth.views.password_reset_confirm()``, and "
"``django.contrib.auth.views.password_change()``, you can now pass URL names "
"and they will be resolved."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a thugtar URL an chéad leathanaigh eile le haghaidh "
"``django.contrib.auth.views.logout () ``, "
"`django.contrib.auth.views.password_reset ()``, "
"`django.contrib.auth.views.password_reset_confirm () ``, agus "
"``django.contrib.auth.views.wordpass_change ()``, is féidir leat ainmneacha "
"URL a rith anois agus réiteofar iad."

msgid ""
"The new :option:`dumpdata --pks` option specifies the primary keys of "
"objects to dump. This option can only be used with one model."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn an rogha nua:option: `dumpdata --pks` eochracha príomhúil na rudaí "
"le dumpáil. Ní féidir an rogha seo a úsáid ach le samhail amháin."

msgid ""
"Added ``QuerySet`` methods :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.first` "
"and :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.last` which are convenience "
"methods returning the first or last object matching the filters. Returns "
"``None`` if there are no objects matching."
msgstr ""
"Cuir modhanna ``QuerySet`` leis: meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.first` agus:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.last` ar modhanna áisiúlachta iad a "
"thugann an chéad réad nó an rud deireanach a mheaitseálann na scagairí. "
"Tugann sé ar ais ``None`` mura bhfuil aon rudaí ann a mheaitseáil."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.views.generic.base.View` "
"and :class:`~django.views.generic.base.RedirectView` now support HTTP "
"``PATCH`` method."
msgstr ""
":class: `~Django.Views.Generic.Base.View` agus:class: "
"`~Django.Views.Generic.Base.RedirectView` tacaíonn anois le modh HTTP "
"```PATCH``."

msgid ""
"``GenericForeignKey`` now takes an optional ``for_concrete_model`` argument, "
"which when set to ``False`` allows the field to reference proxy models. The "
"default is ``True`` to retain the old behavior."
msgstr ""
"Glacann ``GenericForeignKey`` argóint roghnach ``for_concrete_model`` anois, "
"a ligeann don réimse tagairt do mhúnlaí seachfhreastalaí nuair a shocraítear "
"é go `False`. Is é an réamhshocrú ``True`` chun an sean-iompar a choinneáil."

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.middleware.locale.LocaleMiddleware` now stores the "
"active language in session if it is not present there. This prevents loss of "
"language settings after session flush, e.g. logout."
msgstr ""
"Stórálann an :class:`~django.middleware.locale.LocaleMiddleware` an teanga "
"ghníomhach sa seisiún anois mura bhfuil sí i láthair ann. Cuireann sé seo "
"cosc ​​​​ar chaillteanas socruithe teanga tar éis sruthlú seisiúin, e.g. logáil "
"amach."

msgid ""
":exc:`~django.core.exceptions.SuspiciousOperation` has been differentiated "
"into a number of subclasses, and each will log to a matching named logger "
"under the ``django.security`` logging hierarchy. Along with this change, a "
"``handler400`` mechanism and default view are used whenever a "
"``SuspiciousOperation`` reaches the WSGI handler to return an "
"``HttpResponseBadRequest``."
msgstr ""
":exc: Tá `~django.core.exceptions.SuspiciousOperation` idirdhealaithe i "
"roinnt fo-aicmí, agus logálfaidh gach ceann acu ar logaire meaitseála "
"ainmnithe faoin ordlathas logála ``django.security``. In éineacht leis an "
"athrú seo, úsáidtear meicníocht ``handler400` agus amharc réamhshocraithe "
"aon uair a shroicheann ``SuspiciousOperation`` an láimhseálaí WSGI chun "
"``HttpResponseBadRequest`` a thabhairt ar ais."

msgid ""
"The :exc:`~django.db.models.Model.DoesNotExist` exception now includes a "
"message indicating the name of the attribute used for the lookup."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn an eisceacht: EXC: `~django.db.models.model.doesNotExist` "
"teachtaireacht anois a léiríonn ainm na tréithe a úsáidtear don chuardach."

msgid ""
"The :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.get_or_create` method no longer "
"requires at least one keyword argument."
msgstr ""
"Ní theastaíonn argóint eochairfhocal amháin ar a laghad ag an modh: Meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.get_or_create` a thuilleadh."

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.test.SimpleTestCase` class includes a new assertion "
"helper for testing formset errors: "
"``django.test.SimpleTestCase.assertFormsetError()``."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn an ranga:Class: `~Django.Test.SimpleTestCase` cúntóir dearbhaithe "
"nua chun earráidí foirmset a thástáil: "
"``Django.Test.SimpleTestCase.AssertFormSetError () ``."

msgid ""
"The list of related fields added to "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet` "
"by :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.select_related` can be cleared "
"using ``select_related(None)``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir liosta na réimsí gaolmhara a cuireadh le a:class: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset` trí:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.queryset.select_related` a ghlanadh trí ``select_related "
"(None) ``."

msgid ""
"The :meth:`~django.contrib.admin.InlineModelAdmin.get_extra` "
"and :meth:`~django.contrib.admin.InlineModelAdmin.get_max_num` methods "
"on :class:`~django.contrib.admin.InlineModelAdmin` may be overridden to "
"customize the extra and maximum number of inline forms."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir na modhanna: Meth: "
"`~django.contrib.admin.inlineModelAdmin.get_extra` agus:meth: "
"`~django.contrib.admin.inlineModelAdmin.get_max_num` ar: class: "
"`~django.contrib.admin.inlineModelAdmin` a shaincheapadh chun líon breise "
"agus uasta na bhfoirmeacha inlíne a shaincheapadh."

msgid ""
"Formsets now have "
"a :meth:`~django.forms.formsets.BaseFormSet.total_error_count` method."
msgstr ""
"Tá modh a: meth: `~django.forms.formsets.baseFormSet.TOTAL_ERROR_COUNT` ag "
"Formsets anois."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.forms.ModelForm` fields can now override error messages "
"defined in model fields by using "
"the :attr:`~django.forms.Field.error_messages` argument of a ``Field``’s "
"constructor. To take advantage of this new feature with your custom "
"fields, :ref:`see the updated recommendation <raising-validation-error>` for "
"raising a ``ValidationError``."
msgstr ""
":class: Is féidir le réimsí `~Django.Forms.ModelForm` teachtaireachtaí "
"earráide a shainmhínítear i réimsí samhail a shárú anois trí:attr: "
"`~django.forms.field.error_messages` argóint de thógálaí ``Field`` a úsáid. "
"Chun leas a bhaint as an ngné nua seo le do réimsí saincheaptha, :ref: "
"`féach an moladh nuashonraithe `chun ``Error <raising-validation-"
"error>Validation` a ardú."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin` now preserves filters on the list "
"view after creating, editing or deleting an object. It's possible to restore "
"the previous behavior of clearing filters by setting "
"the :attr:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.preserve_filters` attribute to "
"``False``."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.contrib.admin.modelAdmin` caomhnú scagairí ar an amharc "
"liosta anois tar éis réad a chruthú, a chur in eagar nó a scriosadh. Is "
"féidir iompar roimhe seo na scagairí glantacháin a chur ar ais tríd an "
"tréith: attr: `~django.contrib.admin.modeladmin.preserve_filters` a shocrú "
"le ``False``."

msgid ""
"Added :meth:`FormMixin.get_prefix<django.views.generic.edit.FormMixin.get_prefix>` "
"(which "
"returns :attr:`FormMixin.prefix<django.views.generic.edit.FormMixin.prefix>` "
"by default) to allow customizing the :attr:`~django.forms.Form.prefix` of "
"the form."
msgstr ""
"<django.views.generic.edit.FormMixin.prefix>Cuireadh leis: Meth: "
"`FormMixin.Get_Prefix `(a fhilleann: attr: "
"`FormMixin.Prefix<django.views.generic.edit.FormMixin.get_prefix>` de réir "
"réamhshocraithe) chun ceadú: attr: `~django.forms.form.prefix` na foirme a "
"shaincheapadh."

msgid ""
"Raw queries (``Manager.raw()`` or ``cursor.execute()``) can now use the "
"\"pyformat\" parameter style, where placeholders in the query are given as "
"``'%(name)s'`` and the parameters are passed as a dictionary rather than a "
"list (except on SQLite). This has long been possible (but not officially "
"supported) on MySQL and PostgreSQL, and is now also available on Oracle."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le ceisteanna amha (`Manager.raw () ``nó `cursor.execute ()``) an "
"stíl pharaiméadar “pyformat” a úsáid anois, áit a dtugtar ``% (name) s'` "
"``sealbhóirí ionaid sa cheist agus cuirtear na paraiméadair mar fhoclóir "
"seachas liosta (ach amháin ar SQLite). Tá sé seo indéanta le fada (ach níor "
"thacaíodh sé go hoifigiúil) ar MySQL agus PostgreSQL, agus tá sé ar fáil "
"anois ar Oracle freisin."

msgid ""
"The default iteration count for the PBKDF2 password hasher has been "
"increased by 20%. This backwards compatible change will not affect existing "
"passwords or users who have subclassed "
"``django.contrib.auth.hashers.PBKDF2PasswordHasher`` to change the default "
"value. Passwords :ref:`will be upgraded <password-upgrades>` to use the new "
"iteration count as necessary."
msgstr ""
"Méadaíodh 20% an líon athraithe réamhshocraithe don hasher pasfhocal PBKDF2. "
"Ní dhéanfaidh an t-athrú comhoiriúnach ar chúl difear do phasfhocail nó ar "
"úsáideoirí atá ann cheana a rinne fo-aicmiú "
"``Django.contrib.auth.hashers.pbkdf2PasswordHasher`` chun an luach "
"réamhshocraithe a athrú. Pasfhocal: ref: 'uasghrádófar <password-"
"upgrades>`chun an comhaireamh athraithe nua a úsáid de réir mar is gá."

msgid "Backwards incompatible changes in 1.6"
msgstr "Athruithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha ar ais i 1.6"

msgid ""
"In addition to the changes outlined in this section, be sure to review "
"the :ref:`deprecation plan <deprecation-removed-in-1.6>` for any features "
"that have been removed. If you haven't updated your code within the "
"deprecation timeline for a given feature, its removal may appear as a "
"backwards incompatible change."
msgstr ""
"<deprecation-removed-in-1.6>Chomh maith leis na hathruithe a leagtar amach "
"sa chuid seo, déan cinnte athbhreithniú a dhéanamh ar an:ref: `plean "
"díréachtaithe `le haghaidh aon ghnéithe a baineadh. Mura ndearna tú do chód "
"a nuashonrú laistigh den amlíne díscoilte do ghné ar leith, d'fhéadfadh go "
"mbeadh sé a bhaint mar athrú neamh-chomhoiriúnach ar chúl."

msgid "New transaction management model"
msgstr "Samhail nua bainistíochta idirbheart"

msgid "Behavior changes"
msgstr "Athruithe iompraíochta"

msgid ""
"Database-level autocommit is enabled by default in Django 1.6. While this "
"doesn't change the general spirit of Django's transaction management, there "
"are a few backwards-incompatibilities."
msgstr ""
"Tá autocommit ar leibhéal bunachar sonraí cumasaithe de réir réamhshocraithe "
"i Django 1.6. Cé nach n-athraíonn sé seo spiorad ginearálta bainistíochta "
"idirbheart Django, tá cúpla neamhoiriúnacht cúil ann."

msgid "Savepoints and ``assertNumQueries``"
msgstr "Savepoints agus ``AssertNumqueries``"

msgid ""
"The changes in transaction management may result in additional statements to "
"create, release or rollback savepoints. This is more likely to happen with "
"SQLite, since it didn't support savepoints until this release."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh ráitis bhreise a bheith mar thoradh ar na hathruithe i "
"mbainistíocht idirbheart chun pointí sábhála a chruthú, a scaoileadh Is "
"dóichí go dtarlóidh sé seo le SQLite, ós rud é nár thacaigh sé le pointí "
"sábhála go dtí an scaoileadh seo."

msgid ""
"If tests using :meth:`~django.test.TransactionTestCase.assertNumQueries` "
"fail because of a higher number of queries than expected, check that the "
"extra queries are related to savepoints, and adjust the expected number of "
"queries accordingly."
msgstr ""
"Má theipeann ar thástálacha ag baint úsáidea:meth: "
"`~django.test.transactionTestCase.assertNumqueries` mar gheall ar líon níos "
"airde ceisteanna ná mar a bhíothas ag súil leis, seiceáil go bhfuil baint ag "
"na ceisteanna breise le pointí sábhála, agus coigeartaigh líon na "
"gceisteanna a bhfuil súil leis dá réir."

msgid "Autocommit option for PostgreSQL"
msgstr "Rogha Autocommit do PostgreSQL"

msgid ""
"In previous versions, database-level autocommit was only an option for "
"PostgreSQL, and it was disabled by default. This option is now ignored and "
"can be removed."
msgstr ""
"I leaganacha roimhe seo, ní raibh autocommit ar leibhéal bunachar sonraí ach "
"rogha do PostgreSQL, agus cuireadh faoi dhíchumasú é de réir "
"réamhshocraithe. Déantar neamhaird ar an rogha seo anois agus is féidir é a "
"bhaint."

msgid "New test runner"
msgstr "Rathóir tástála nua"

msgid ""
"In order to maintain greater consistency with Python's ``unittest`` module, "
"the new test runner (``django.test.runner.DiscoverRunner``) does not "
"automatically support some types of tests that were supported by the "
"previous runner:"
msgstr ""
"D'fhonn comhsheasmhacht níos mó a choinneáil le modúl `unittest`` Python, ní "
"thacaíonn an reathóir tástála nua (``Django.Test.Runner.DiscoverRunner``) go "
"huathoibríoch le roinnt cineálacha tástálacha a thacaigh an rádálaí roimhe "
"seo:"

msgid ""
"Tests in ``models.py`` and ``tests/__init__.py`` files will no longer be "
"found and run. Move them to a file whose name begins with ``test``."
msgstr ""
"Ní aimsífear agus ní reáchtálfar tástálacha i gcomhaid ``models.py`` agus "
"``tests/__init__.py`` a thuilleadh. Bog iad chuig comhad a dtosaíonn a n-"
"ainm le ``tást``."

msgid ""
"Doctests will no longer be automatically discovered. To integrate doctests "
"in your test suite, follow the :ref:`recommendations in the Python "
"documentation <doctest-unittest-api>`."
msgstr ""
"Ní aimsífear doctests go huathoibríoch a thuilleadh. <doctest-unittest-"
"api>Chun doctests a chomhtháthú i do shraith tástála, lean na:ref: `moltaí i "
"ndoiciméadú Python `."

msgid ""
"Django bundles a modified version of the :mod:`doctest` module from the "
"Python standard library (in ``django.test._doctest``) and includes some "
"additional doctest utilities. These utilities are deprecated and will be "
"removed in Django 1.8; doctest suites should be updated to work with the "
"standard library's doctest module (or converted to ``unittest``-compatible "
"tests)."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann Django leagan modhnaithe den mhodúl: mod: `doctest` ó leabharlann "
"caighdeánach Python (i `django.test. _doctest``) agus tá roinnt fóntais "
"doctest breise ann. Tá na fóntais seo díscríofa agus bainfear iad i Django "
"1.8; ba chóir sraith doctest a nuashonrú chun oibriú le modúl doctest an "
"leabharlainne caighdeánach (nó a thiontú go tástálacha comhoiriúnacha "
"``unittest`)."

msgid ""
"If you wish to delay updates to your test suite, you can set "
"your :setting:`TEST_RUNNER` setting to "
"``django.test.simple.DjangoTestSuiteRunner`` to fully restore the old test "
"behavior. ``DjangoTestSuiteRunner`` is deprecated but will not be removed "
"from Django until version 1.8."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat moill a chur ar nuashonruithe ar do tsraith tástála, is féidir "
"leat do shocrú: setting: `TEST_RUNNER` a shocrú go "
"``DJANGO.TEST.SIMPLE.DJANGOTESTSUITERUNNER`` chun an sean-iompar tástála a "
"chur ar ais go hiomlán. Tá ``DjangoTestSuiterunner`` díluaite ach ní "
"bhainfear é as Django go dtí leagan 1.8."

msgid ""
"Removal of ``django.contrib.gis.tests.GeoDjangoTestSuiteRunner`` GeoDjango "
"custom test runner"
msgstr ""
"Baint de ``Django.contrib.gis.tests.geodjangoTestSuiterunner`` ``rádaí "
"tástála saincheaptha GeodJango"

msgid ""
"This is for developers working on the GeoDjango application itself and "
"related to the item above about changes in the test runners:"
msgstr ""
"Tá sé seo d'fhorbróirí atá ag obair ar an bhfeidhmchlár GeodJango féin agus "
"a bhaineann leis an mír thuas faoi athruithe sna reathaithe tástála:"

msgid ""
"The ``django.contrib.gis.tests.GeoDjangoTestSuiteRunner`` test runner has "
"been removed and the standalone GeoDjango tests execution setup it "
"implemented isn't supported anymore. To run the GeoDjango tests simply use "
"the new ``DiscoverRunner`` and specify the ``django.contrib.gis`` app."
msgstr ""
"Baineadh an reathnóir tástála "
"`Django.contrib.gis.tests.geodjangoTestsuitRunner ``agus ní thacaítear leis "
"an socrú forghníomhaithe tástálacha neamhspleách GeodJango a chuir sé i "
"bhfeidhm níos mó. Chun na tástálacha GeodJango a reáchtáil ní gá ach an "
"`DiscoverRunner`` nua a úsáid agus an aip `django.contrib.gis`` a shonrú."

msgid "Custom user models in tests"
msgstr "Múnlaí úsáideora saincheaptha i dtá"

msgid ""
"The introduction of the new test runner has also slightly changed the way "
"that test models are imported. As a result, any test that overrides "
"``AUTH_USER_MODEL`` to test behavior with one of Django's test user models "
"( ``django.contrib.auth.tests.custom_user.CustomUser`` and "
"``django.contrib.auth.tests.custom_user.ExtensionUser``) must now explicitly "
"import the User model in your test module::"
msgstr ""
"D'athraigh tabhairt isteach an rádálaí tástála nua beagán ar an mbealach a "
"allmhairítear samhlacha tástála. Mar thoradh air sin, ní mór d'aon tástáil a "
"sháraíonn ``AUTH_USER_MODEL`` chun iompar a thástáil le ceann de mhúnlaí "
"úsáideora tástála Django "
"(`Django.contrib.auth.tests.contrib.extensionUser``) an tsamhail Úsáideora a "
"allmhairiú go sainráite i do mhodúl tástála anois:"

msgid ""
"This import forces the custom user model to be registered. Without this "
"import, the test will be unable to swap in the custom user model, and you "
"will get an error reporting:"
msgstr ""
"Cuireann an t-allmhairiú seo iallach ar an tsamhail úsáideora saincheaptha a "
"Gan an t-allmhairiú seo, ní bheidh an tástáil in ann malartú sa tsamhail "
"úsáideora saincheaptha, agus gheobhaidh tú tuairisciú earráide:"

msgid "Time zone-aware ``day``, ``month``, and ``week_day`` lookups"
msgstr ""
"Cuardaigh ``lá ``, `mhí``, agus ``laeth_seachtaine`` atá ar an eolas ar "
"chrios ama"

msgid ""
"Django 1.6 introduces time zone support for :lookup:`day`, :lookup:`month`, "
"and :lookup:`week_day` lookups when :setting:`USE_TZ` is ``True``. These "
"lookups were previously performed in UTC regardless of the current time zone."
msgstr ""
"Tugann Django 1.6 tacaíocht crios ama isteach le haghaidh: lookup: "
"`day`, :lookup: `month`, agus:lookup: `week_day` cuardaigh nuai:setting: "
"`USE_TZ` ``True``. Rinneadh na cuardaigh seo roimhe seo i UTC beag beann ar "
"an crios ama reatha."

msgid ""
"This requires :ref:`time zone definitions in the database <database-time-"
"zone-definitions>`. If you're using SQLite, you must install pytz_. If "
"you're using MySQL, you must install pytz_ and load the time zone tables "
"with `mysql_tzinfo_to_sql`_."
msgstr ""
"<database-time-zone-definitions>Éilíonn sé seo: ref: `sainmhínithe crios ama "
"sa bhunachar sonraí `. Má tá SQLite á úsáid agat, ní mór duit pytz_ a "
"shuiteáil. Má tá MySQL á úsáid agat, ní mór duit pytz_ a shuiteáil agus na "
"táblaí crios ama a luchtú le `mysql_tzinfo_to_sql`_."

msgid "Addition of ``QuerySet.datetimes()``"
msgstr "Cuir leis ``QuerySet.DateTimes () ``"

msgid ""
"When the :doc:`time zone support </topics/i18n/timezones>` added in Django "
"1.4 was active, :meth:`QuerySet.dates() "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.dates>` lookups returned unexpected "
"results, because the aggregation was performed in UTC. To fix this, Django "
"1.6 introduces a new API, :meth:`QuerySet.datetimes() "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.datetimes>`. This requires a few changes in "
"your code."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhí an: doc: `tacaíocht crios ama' a cuireadh i Django 1.4 "
"gníomhach, :meth: `QuerySet.dates () `</topics/i18n/timezones> d'fhill "
"cuardaigh torthaí gan choinne, toisc gur rinneadh an comhiomlánú i "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.dates>UTC. "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.datetimes>Chun é seo a shocrú, tugann "
"Django 1.6 API nua isteach,: meth: `QuerySet.DateTimes () `. Éilíonn sé seo "
"cúpla athrú i do chód."

msgid "``QuerySet.dates()`` returns ``date`` objects"
msgstr "Tugann ``QuerySet.dates () ``rudaí ``dáta``"

msgid ""
":meth:`QuerySet.dates() <django.db.models.query.QuerySet.dates>` now returns "
"a list of :class:`~datetime.date`. It used to return a list "
"of :class:`~datetime.datetime`."
msgstr ""
":meth: `QuerySet.dates () `filleann liosta "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.dates>anois de:class: `~datetime.date`. "
"Bhain sé úsáid as liosta de:class: `~datetime.datetime` a thabhairt ar ais."

msgid ""
":meth:`QuerySet.datetimes() <django.db.models.query.QuerySet.datetimes>` "
"returns a list of :class:`~datetime.datetime`."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.datetimes>:meth: `QuerySet.dateTimes () "
"`filleann liosta de:class: `~datetime.datetime`."

msgid "``QuerySet.dates()`` no longer usable on ``DateTimeField``"
msgstr ""
"``QuerySet.dates () ``nach bhfuil inúsáidte a thuilleadh ar ``DateTimeField``"

msgid ""
":meth:`QuerySet.dates() <django.db.models.query.QuerySet.dates>` raises an "
"error if it's used on :class:`~django.db.models.DateTimeField` when time "
"zone support is active. Use :meth:`QuerySet.datetimes() "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.datetimes>` instead."
msgstr ""
":meth: Ardaíonn `QuerySet.dates () "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.dates>`earráid má úsáidtear é ar:class: "
"`~Django.db.Models.DateTimeField` nuair a bhíonn tacaíocht crios ama "
"gníomhach. <django.db.models.query.QuerySet.datetimes>Úsáid: Meth: "
"`QuerySet.dateTimes () `ina ionad."

msgid "``date_hierarchy`` requires time zone definitions"
msgstr "Éilíonn ``date_hierarchy`` sainmhínithe crios ama"

msgid ""
"The :attr:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.date_hierarchy` feature of the "
"admin now relies on :meth:`QuerySet.datetimes() "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.datetimes>` when it's used on "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.DateTimeField`."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.datetimes>Braitheann gné: Attr: "
"`~django.contrib.admin.modeladmin.date_hierarchy` den riarachán anois "
"ar:meth: `QuerySet.DateTimes () `nuair a úsáidtear é ar a:class: "
"`~Django.db.Models.DateTimeField`."

msgid ""
"This requires time zone definitions in the database when :setting:`USE_TZ` "
"is ``True``. :ref:`Learn more <database-time-zone-definitions>`."
msgstr ""
"Éilíonn sé seo sainmhínithe crios ama sa bhunachar sonraí nuai:setting: "
"`USE_TZ` ``True``. <database-time-zone-definitions>:ref: `Foghlaim níos mó `."

msgid "``date_list`` in generic views requires time zone definitions"
msgstr "``date_list`` i dtuairimí cineálacha teastaíonn sainmhínithe crios ama"

msgid ""
"For the same reason, accessing ``date_list`` in the context of a date-based "
"generic view requires time zone definitions in the database when the view is "
"based on a :class:`~django.db.models.DateTimeField` and :setting:`USE_TZ` is "
"``True``. :ref:`Learn more <database-time-zone-definitions>`."
msgstr ""
"Ar an gcúis chéanna, teastaíonn sainmhínithe crios ama sa bhunachar sonraí "
"chun rochtain a fháil ar `date_list`` i gcomhthéacs radharc cineálach dáta-"
"bhunaithe nuair a bhíonn an radharc bunaithe ar a:class: "
"`~Django.db.Models.DateTimeField` agus:setting: `USE_TZ` `True``. <database-"
"time-zone-definitions>:ref: `Foghlaim níos mó `."

msgid "New lookups may clash with model fields"
msgstr "D'fhéadfadh cuardaigh nua teacht ar réimsí samhail"

msgid ""
"Django 1.6 introduces ``hour``, ``minute``, and ``second`` lookups "
"on :class:`~django.db.models.DateTimeField`. If you had model fields called "
"``hour``, ``minute``, or ``second``, the new lookups will clash with you "
"field names. Append an explicit :lookup:`exact` lookup if this is an issue."
msgstr ""
"Tugann Django 1.6 isteach cuardach ```huair ``, `nóiméad``, agus ``soicind "
"``ar:class: `~django.db.Models.DateTimeField`. Má bhí réimsí samhail agat ar "
"a dtugtar ``huair ``, `nóiméad``, nó ``soicind``, beidh na cuardaigh nua ag "
"teacht le hainmneacha réimse leat. Cuir cuardach explit:lookup: `exact` i "
"gceist más saincheist é seo."

msgid "``BooleanField`` no longer defaults to ``False``"
msgstr "Ní réamhshocraíonn ``Booleanfield`` go ``False`` a thuilleadh"

msgid ""
"When a :class:`~django.db.models.BooleanField` doesn't have an "
"explicit :attr:`~django.db.models.Field.default`, the implicit default value "
"is ``None``. In previous version of Django, it was ``False``, but that "
"didn't represent accurately the lack of a value."
msgstr ""
"Nuair nach bhfuil explicit:attr: `~django.db.models.booleanfield` ag "
"a:class: `~django.db.models.field.default`, is é ``None ``an luach "
"réamhshocraithe intuigthe. Sa leagan roimhe seo de Django, “False” a bhí "
"ann, ach níor léirigh sé sin go cruinn an easpa luach."

msgid ""
"Code that relies on the default value being ``False`` may raise an exception "
"when saving new model instances to the database, because ``None`` isn't an "
"acceptable value for a :class:`~django.db.models.BooleanField`. You should "
"either specify ``default=False`` in the field definition, or ensure the "
"field is set to ``True`` or ``False`` before saving the object."
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh cód atá ag brath ar an luach réamhshocraithe ná ``False`` "
"eisceacht a ardú agus cásanna samhail nua á shábháil ar an mbunachar sonraí, "
"toisc nach luach inghlactha é ``None`` do a:class: "
"`~Django.db.Models.BooleanField`. Ba chóir duit ``Default=False`` a shonrú "
"sa sainmhíniú réimse, nó a chinntiú go bhfuil an réimse socraithe go "
"``True`` nó ``False`` sula sábhálfar an réad."

msgid "Translations and comments in templates"
msgstr "Aistriúcháin agus tuairimí i d"

msgid "Extraction of translations after comments"
msgstr "Aistriúcháin a eastóscadh tar éis"

msgid ""
"Extraction of translatable literals from templates with "
"the :djadmin:`makemessages` command now correctly detects i18n constructs "
"when they are located after a ``{#`` / ``#}``-type comment on the same line. "
"E.g.:"
msgstr ""
"Aithníonn eastóscadh litríochtaí inaistrithe ó theimpléid leis an "
"ordú:djadmin: `makemessages` tógáil i18n i gceart anois nuair a bhíonn siad "
"suite i ndiaidh trácht cineál ``{#``/`#}`` ar an líne chéanna. M.sh.:"

msgid "Location of translator comments"
msgstr "Suíomh tuairimí aistritheora"

msgid ""
":ref:`translator-comments-in-templates` specified using ``{#`` / ``#}`` need "
"to be at the end of a line. If they are not, the comments are ignored "
"and :djadmin:`makemessages` will generate a warning. For example:"
msgstr ""
":ref: caithfidh `translator-comments-in-temples` a shonraítear ag baint "
"úsáide as ``{#``/``#}`` a bheith ag deireadh líne. Mura bhfuil siad, déantar "
"neamhaird ar na tuairimí agus ginfidh: djadmin: `makemessages` rabhadh. Mar "
"shampla:"

msgid "Quoting in ``reverse()``"
msgstr "Ag lua i ``reverse () ``"

msgid ""
"When reversing URLs, Django didn't apply ``django.utils.http.urlquote`` to "
"arguments before interpolating them in URL patterns. This bug is fixed in "
"Django 1.6. If you worked around this bug by applying URL quoting before "
"passing arguments to ``reverse()``, this may result in double-quoting. If "
"this happens, simply remove the URL quoting from your code. You will also "
"have to replace special characters in URLs used "
"in :func:`~django.test.SimpleTestCase.assertRedirects` with their encoded "
"versions."
msgstr ""
"Agus URLanna á aisiompú, níor chuir Django ``django.utils.http.urlquote`` i "
"bhfeidhm ar argóintí sula ndéantar iad a ionghabháil i bpatrúin URL. Tá an "
"fabht seo socraithe i Django 1.6. Má d'oibrigh tú timpeall ar an fabht seo "
"trí luachan URL a chur i bhfeidhm sula ndéantar argóintí a chur chuig "
"``reverse () ``, d'fhéadfadh luachan dúbailte a bheith mar thoradh air seo. "
"Má tharlaíonn sé seo, ní gá ach an URL atá ag luachan as do chód a bhaint. "
"Beidh ort freisin carachtair speisialta in URLanna a úsáidtear in:func: "
"`~django.test.simpletestCase.assertDirects` a gcuid leaganacha ionchódaithe "
"a chur in ionad."

msgid "Storage of IP addresses in the comments app"
msgstr "Seoltaí IP a stóráil san aip tráchtanna"

msgid ""
"The comments app now uses a ``GenericIPAddressField`` for storing "
"commenters' IP addresses, to support comments submitted from IPv6 addresses. "
"Until now, it stored them in an ``IPAddressField``, which is only meant to "
"support IPv4. When saving a comment made from an IPv6 address, the address "
"would be silently truncated on MySQL databases, and raise an exception on "
"Oracle. You will need to change the column type in your database to benefit "
"from this change."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann an aip tráchtanna anois ``GenericipAddressfield` chun seoltaí IP "
"tráchtaireoirí a stóráil, chun tacú le tráchtanna a chuirtear isteach ó "
"sheoltaí IPv6. Go dtí seo, stóráil sé iad i ``iPaddressfield`, nach bhfuil i "
"gceist ach tacú le IPv4. Agus trácht a dhéantar ó sheoladh IPv6 á shábháil, "
"déanfaí an seoladh a ghearradh go ciúin ar bhunachair sonraí MySQL, agus "
"ardófaí eisceacht ar Oracle. Beidh ort an cineál colúin a athrú i do "
"bhunachar sonraí chun leas a bhaint as an athrú seo."

msgid "For MySQL, execute this query on your project's database:"
msgstr ""
"Maidir le MySQL, déan an cheist seo ar bhunachar sonraí do thionscadail:"

msgid "For Oracle, execute this query:"
msgstr "Maidir le Oracle, déan an cheist seo:"

msgid ""
"If you do not apply this change, the behavior is unchanged: on MySQL, IPv6 "
"addresses are silently truncated; on Oracle, an exception is generated. No "
"database change is needed for SQLite or PostgreSQL databases."
msgstr ""
"Mura gcuireann tú an t-athrú seo i bhfeidhm, níl an t-iompar gan athrú: ar "
"MySQL, gearrtar seoltaí IPv6 go ciúin; ar Oracle, gintear eisceacht. Níl aon "
"athrú bunachar sonraí ag teastáil le haghaidh bunachair sonraí SQLite nó "
"PostgreSQL."

msgid "Percent literals in ``cursor.execute`` queries"
msgstr "Céatadán litríochta i gceisteanna ``cursor.execute``"

msgid ""
"When you are running raw SQL queries through the :ref:`cursor.execute "
"<executing-custom-sql>` method, the rule about doubling percent literals "
"(``%``) inside the query has been unified. Past behavior depended on the "
"database backend. Now, across all backends, you only need to double literal "
"percent characters if you are also providing replacement parameters. For "
"example::"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhíonn ceisteanna SQL amha á <executing-custom-sql>reáchtáil agat "
"tríd an modh:ref: `cursor.execut`, tá an riail maidir le litríochtaí faoin "
"gcéad (`%``) a dhúbailt taobh istigh den cheist aontaithe. Bhí iompar roimhe "
"seo ag brath ar chúlcheann an bhunachar sonraí. Anois, thar gach cúltaca, ní "
"gá duit ach carachtair faoin gcéad liteartha a dhúbailt má tá paraiméadair "
"athsholáthair á sholáthar agat freisin. Mar shampla::"

msgid "``SQLite`` users need to check and update such queries."
msgstr ""
"Ní mór d'úsáideoirí `SQLite`` ceisteanna den sórt sin a sheiceáil agus a "
"nuashonrú."

msgid "Help text of model form fields for ManyToManyField fields"
msgstr "Téacs cabhrach de réimsí foirme samhail do réimsí ManyTomanyField"

msgid ""
"HTML rendering of model form fields corresponding "
"to :class:`~django.db.models.ManyToManyField` model fields used to get the "
"hard-coded sentence:"
msgstr ""
"Rindreáil HTML de réimsí foirme samhail a fhreagraíonn do:class: "
"`~django.db.models.manyToManyField` réimsí samhail a úsáidtear chun an "
"abairt crua-chódaithe a fháil:"

msgid ""
"*Hold down \"Control\", or \"Command\" on a Mac, to select more than one.*"
msgstr ""
"* Coinnigh síos “Rialú”, nó “Ordú” ar Mac, chun níos mó ná ceann amháin a "
"roghnú. *"

msgid ""
"(or its translation to the active locale) imposed as the help legend shown "
"along them if neither :attr:`model <django.db.models.Field.help_text>` "
"nor :attr:`form <django.forms.Field.help_text>` ``help_text`` attributes "
"were specified by the user (or this string was appended to any ``help_text`` "
"that was provided)."
msgstr ""
"(nó a aistriúchán go dtí an áit ghníomhach) a fhorchuir mar an finscéal "
"cabhrach a thaispeántar leo mura shon "
"<django.db.models.Field.help_text><django.forms.Field.help_text>raigh an t-"
"úsáideoir tréithe: attr: `model `nor:attr: `form` `help_text`` (nó cuireadh "
"an sreang seo i gceangal le haon `help_text`` a sholáthraíodh)."

msgid ""
"Since this happened at the model layer, there was no way to prevent the text "
"from appearing in cases where it wasn't applicable such as form fields that "
"implement user interactions that don't involve a keyboard and/or a mouse."
msgstr ""
"Ó tharla sé seo ag an gciseal samhail, ní raibh aon bhealach ann chun an "
"téacs a chosc ó bheith le feiceáil i gcásanna nach raibh sé infheidhme mar "
"réimsí foirme a chuireann idirghníomhaíochtaí úsáideora i bhfeidhm nach "
"mbaineann méarchlár agus/nó luch."

msgid ""
"Starting with Django 1.6, as an ad-hoc temporary backward-compatibility "
"provision, the logic to add the \"Hold down...\" sentence has been moved to "
"the model form field layer and modified to add the text only when the "
"associated widget is :class:`~django.forms.SelectMultiple` or selected "
"subclasses."
msgstr ""
"Ag tosú le Django 1.6, mar fhoráil sealadach comhoiriúnachta siar ad-hoc, "
"aistríodh an loighic chun an abairt “Coinnigh síos...” a chur chuig ciseal "
"réimse foirme samhail agus modhnaíodh chun an téacs a chur leis ach amháin "
"nuair is é an giuirléid gaolmhar: class: `~django.forms.selectMultiple` nó "
"fo-aicmí roghnaithe."

msgid ""
"The change can affect you in a backward incompatible way if you employ "
"custom model form fields and/or widgets for ``ManyToManyField`` model fields "
"whose UIs do rely on the automatic provision of the mentioned hard-coded "
"sentence. These form field implementations need to adapt to the new scenario "
"by providing their own handling of the ``help_text`` attribute."
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh an t-athrú dul i bhfeidhm ort ar bhealach neamh-chomhoiriúnach ar "
"chúl má úsáideann tú réimsí foirme samhail saincheaptha agus/nó giuirléidí "
"do réimsí samhail ``ManyTomanyField` a bhfuil a UIanna ag brath ar sholáthar "
"uathoibríoch na habairte crua-chódaithe luaite. Caithfidh na forfheidhmithe "
"réimse foirmeacha seo oiriúnú don chás nua trína láimhseáil féin ar an "
"tréith ``help_text`` a sholáthar."

msgid ""
"Applications that use Django :doc:`model form </topics/forms/modelforms>` "
"facilities together with Django built-in form :doc:`fields </ref/forms/"
"fields>` and :doc:`widgets </ref/forms/widgets>` aren't affected but need to "
"be aware of what's described in :ref:`m2m-help_text-deprecation` below."
msgstr ""
"Ní bhíonn tionchar ag iarratais a úsáideann áiseanna Django:doc: `foirm "
"samhail` </topics/forms/modelforms> mar aon le foirm ionsuite Django: doc: "
"`fields` agus:doc: `widgets` ach ní mór a bheith ar an eolas faoin méid atá "
"cur síos in:ref: `m2m-help_text-deprecation` </ref/forms/fields> </ref/forms/"
"widgets> thíos."

msgid "QuerySet iteration"
msgstr "Athrú QuerySet"

msgid ""
"The ``QuerySet`` iteration was changed to immediately convert all fetched "
"rows to ``Model`` objects. In Django 1.5 and earlier the fetched rows were "
"converted to ``Model`` objects in chunks of 100."
msgstr ""
"Athraíodh an t-athrú ``QuerySet` chun gach sraitheanna a fuarthas a thiontú "
"go rudaí ``Samhail ``. I Django 1.5 agus níos luaithe tiontaíodh na "
"sraitheanna a fuarthas go rudaí ``Samhail ``i gcodanna de 100."

msgid ""
"Existing code will work, but the amount of rows converted to objects might "
"change in certain use cases. Such usages include partially looping over a "
"queryset or any usage which ends up doing ``__bool__`` or ``__contains__``."
msgstr ""
"Oibreoidh an cód atá ann cheana, ach d'fhéadfadh méid na sraitheanna a "
"thiontú go rudaí athrú i gcásanna úsáide áirithe I measc na n-úsáidí den "
"sórt sin tá lúbadh go páirteach thar shraith fiosrúcháin nó aon úsáid a "
"chríochnaíonn ag déanamh ``__bool__`` nó ``__contains__``."

msgid ""
"Notably most database backends did fetch all the rows in one go already in "
"1.5."
msgstr ""
"Go háirithe thóg an chuid is mó de chúltaca bunachar sonraí na sraitheanna "
"go léir in aon ghuair cheana féin i 1.5."

msgid ""
"It is still possible to convert the fetched rows to ``Model`` objects lazily "
"by using the :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.iterator()` method."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir fós na sraitheanna a fuarthas a thiontú go rudaí ``Model ``go "
"leisciúil tríd an modh: meth: `~django.db.models.query.queryset.iterator () "
"`a úsáid."

msgid ""
":meth:`BoundField.label_tag<django.forms.BoundField.label_tag>` now includes "
"the form's :attr:`~django.forms.Form.label_suffix`"
msgstr ""
"<django.forms.BoundField.label_tag>:meth: `BoundField.label_tag `tá an "
"fhoirm anois: attr: `~django.forms.form.label_suffix`"

msgid ""
"This is consistent with how methods "
"like :meth:`Form.as_p<django.forms.Form.as_p>` "
"and :meth:`Form.as_ul<django.forms.Form.as_ul>` render labels."
msgstr ""
"<django.forms.Form.as_ul>Tá sé seo comhsheasmhach leis an gcaoi a ndéanann "
"modhanna cosúil:meth: `Form.as_P <django.forms.Form.as_p>`agus:meth: "
"`Form.as_ul` lipéid a dhéanann."

msgid "If you manually render ``label_tag`` in your templates:"
msgstr "Má rindeann tú ``label_tag`` de láimh i do theimpléid:"

msgid ""
"you'll want to remove the colon (or whatever other separator you may be "
"using) to avoid duplicating it when upgrading to Django 1.6. The following "
"template in Django 1.6 will render identically to the above template in "
"Django 1.5, except that the colon will appear inside the ``<label>`` element."
msgstr ""
"beidh tú ag iarraidh an colon a bhaint (nó cibé deighilteoir eile a "
"d'fhéadfá a bheith á úsáid) chun é a dhúbailt a sheachaint agus tú ag "
"uasghrádú go Django 1.6. <label>Déanfaidh an teimpléad seo a leanas i Django "
"1.6 go comhionann leis an teimpléad thuas i Django 1.5, ach amháin go mbeidh "
"an colon le feiceáil taobh istigh den eilimint ```."

msgid "will render something like:"
msgstr "déanfaidh sé rud éigin cosúil le:"

msgid ""
"If you want to keep the current behavior of rendering ``label_tag`` without "
"the ``label_suffix``, instantiate the form ``label_suffix=''``. You can also "
"customize the ``label_suffix`` on a per-field basis using the new "
"``label_suffix`` parameter on :meth:`~django.forms.BoundField.label_tag`."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat an t-iompar reatha a bhaineann le rindreáil ``label_tag`` a "
"choinneáil gan an ``label_suffix``, cuir an fhoirm ``label_suffix=\"``. Is "
"féidir leat an `label_suffix`` a shaincheapadh freisin ar bhonn in aghaidh "
"an réimse ag baint úsáide as an paraiméadar nua ``label_suffix`` ar:meth: "
"`~django.forms.boundfield.label_tag`."

msgid "Admin views ``_changelist_filters`` GET parameter"
msgstr "Tuairimí riaracháin ``_changelist_filters`` paraiméadar GET"

msgid ""
"To achieve preserving and restoring list view filters, admin views now pass "
"around the ``_changelist_filters`` GET parameter. It's important that you "
"account for that change if you have custom admin templates or if your tests "
"rely on the previous URLs. If you want to revert to the original behavior "
"you can set the :attr:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.preserve_filters` "
"attribute to ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Chun scagairí amharc liosta a chaomhnú agus a athchóiriú a bhaint amach, "
"téann tuairimí riaracháin timpeall an pharaiméadair GET "
"``_changelist_filters`` anois. Tá sé tábhachtach go gcuirfidh tú cuntas ar "
"an athrú sin má tá teimpléid riaracháin saincheaptha agat nó má tá do "
"thástálacha ag brath ar na URLanna roimhe seo. Más mian leat filleadh ar an "
"iompar bunaidh is féidir leat an tréith: attr: "
"`~django.contrib.admin.modeladmin.preserve_filters` a shocrú go ``False``."

msgid ""
"``django.contrib.auth`` password reset uses base 64 encoding of ``User`` PK"
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann athshocrú pasfhocal ``django.contrib.auth`` ionchódú bonn 64 de "
"``Úsáideoir ``PK"

msgid ""
"Past versions of Django used base 36 encoding of the ``User`` primary key in "
"the password reset views and URLs "
"(``django.contrib.auth.views.password_reset_confirm()``). Base 36 encoding "
"is sufficient if the user primary key is an integer, however, with the "
"introduction of custom user models in Django 1.5, that assumption may no "
"longer be true."
msgstr ""
"D'úsáid leaganacha roimhe seo de Django ionchódú bonn 36 den phríomh-eochair "
"``Úsáideoir ``sna tuairimí athshocraithe pasfhocal agus URLanna "
"(``django.contrib.auth.views.password_reset_confirm ()``). Is leor ionchódú "
"Bonn 36 más sláimhir é príomh-eochair an úsáideora, áfach, le samhlacha "
"úsáideora saincheaptha a thabhairt isteach i Django 1.5, b'fhéidir nach "
"mbeidh an toimhde sin fíor a thuilleadh."

msgid ""
"``django.contrib.auth.views.password_reset_confirm()`` has been modified to "
"take a ``uidb64`` parameter instead of ``uidb36``. If you are reversing this "
"view, for example in a custom ``password_reset_email.html`` template, be "
"sure to update your code."
msgstr ""
"Athraíodh ``django.contrib.auth.views.password_reset_confirm () ``chun "
"paraiméadar ``uidb64`` a ghlacadh in ionad ``uidb36``. Má tá an dearcadh seo "
"á aisiompú agat, mar shampla i dteimpléad saincheaptha "
"``password_reset_email.html`, bí cinnte do chód a nuashonrú."

msgid ""
"A temporary shim for ``django.contrib.auth.views.password_reset_confirm()`` "
"that will allow password reset links generated prior to Django 1.6 to "
"continue to work has been added to provide backwards compatibility; this "
"will be removed in Django 1.7. Thus, as long as your site has been running "
"Django 1.6 for more than ``PASSWORD_RESET_TIMEOUT_DAYS``, this change will "
"have no effect. If not (for example, if you upgrade directly from Django 1.5 "
"to Django 1.7), then any password reset links generated before you upgrade "
"to Django 1.7 or later won't work after the upgrade."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh shim sealadach do `django.contrib.auth.views.password_reset_verify "
"() ``a ligfidh naisc athshocraithe pasfhocal a ghintear roimh Django 1.6 "
"leanúint ag obair chun comhoiriúnacht ar ais a sholáthar; bainfear é seo i "
"Django 1.7. Dá bhrí sin, chomh fada agus a bheidh do shuíomh ag rith Django "
"1.6 ar feadh níos mó ná ``PASSWORD_RESET_TIMEOUT_DAYS ``, ní bheidh aon "
"éifeacht ag an athrú seo. Mura bhfuil (mar shampla, má dhéanann tú uasghrádú "
"díreach ó Django 1.5 go Django 1.7), ansin ní oibreoidh aon naisc "
"athshocraithe pasfhocal a ghintear sula ndéanann tú uasghrádú go Django 1.7 "
"nó níos déanaí tar éis an uasghrádaithe."

msgid ""
"In addition, if you have any custom password reset URLs, you will need to "
"update them by replacing ``uidb36`` with ``uidb64`` and the dash that "
"follows that pattern with a slash. Also add ``_\\-`` to the list of "
"characters that may match the ``uidb64`` pattern."
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, má tá aon URLanna athshocraithe pasfhocal saincheaptha "
"agat, beidh ort iad a nuashonrú trí ``uidb36` a chur in ionad ``uidb64`` "
"agus an doic a leanann an patrún sin le slash. Cuir ``_\\ -`` freisin leis "
"an liosta carachtair a d'fhéadfadh a mheaitseáil leis an bpatrún ``uidb64``."

msgid "For example::"
msgstr "Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"You may also want to add the shim to support the old style reset links. "
"Using the example above, you would modify the existing url by replacing "
"``django.contrib.auth.views.password_reset_confirm`` with "
"``django.contrib.auth.views.password_reset_confirm_uidb36`` and also remove "
"the ``name`` argument so it doesn't conflict with the new url::"
msgstr ""
"B'fhéidir gur mhaith leat an shim a chur leis freisin chun tacú leis na "
"naisc athshocraithe sean-stíl. Ag baint úsáide as an sampla thuas, mhodhnófá "
"an url atá ann cheana trí "
"`django.contrib.auth.auth.views.password_reset_confirm`` a chur in ionad "
"`django.contrib.auth.views.password_reset_confirm_uidb36`` agus bain an "
"argóint ``ainm `ionas nach mbeidh sé ag teacht ar an url nua::"

msgid ""
"You can remove this URL pattern after your app has been deployed with Django "
"1.6 for ``PASSWORD_RESET_TIMEOUT_DAYS``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an patrún URL seo a bhaint tar éis d'aip a imscaradh le "
"Django 1.6 le haghaidh ``PASSWORD_RESET_TIMEOUT_DAYS ``."

msgid "Default session serialization switched to JSON"
msgstr "Athraigh sraith seisiúin réamhshocraithe go JSON"

msgid ""
"Historically, :mod:`django.contrib.sessions` used :mod:`pickle` to serialize "
"session data before storing it in the backend. If you're using "
"the :ref:`signed cookie session backend<cookie-session-backend>` "
"and :setting:`SECRET_KEY` is known by an attacker (there isn't an inherent "
"vulnerability in Django that would cause it to leak), the attacker could "
"insert a string into their session which, when unpickled, executes arbitrary "
"code on the server. The technique for doing so is simple and easily "
"available on the internet. Although the cookie session storage signs the "
"cookie-stored data to prevent tampering, a :setting:`SECRET_KEY` leak "
"immediately escalates to a remote code execution vulnerability."
msgstr ""
"Go stairiúil, d'úsáid :mod: `django.contrib.sessions`: mod: `pickle` chun "
"sonraí seisiúin a shraitheadh sula ndéantar iad a stóráil sa chúltaca. Má tá "
"cúltaca seisi <cookie-session-backend>úin fianán sínithe á úsáid agat: "
"agus:setting: `SECRET_KEY` is aithne ag ionsaitheoir (níl leochaileacht "
"bhunúsach i Django a chuirfeadh sé sceitheadh), d'fhéadfadh an t-"
"ionsaitheoir teaghrán a chur isteach ina seisiún a fhorghníomhaíonn cód "
"treallach ar an bhfreastalaí. Tá an teicníc chun é sin a dhéanamh simplí "
"agus ar fáil go héasca ar an idirlíon. Cé go síníonn stóráil seisiún fianán "
"na sonraí atá stóráilte ag fianán chun cur isteach a chosc, méadaíonn "
"sceitheadh a: setting: `SECRET_KEY` láithreach go leochaileacht iargúlta "
"forghníomhaithe cód."

msgid ""
"This attack can be mitigated by serializing session data using JSON rather "
"than :mod:`pickle`. To facilitate this, Django 1.5.3 introduced a new "
"setting, :setting:`SESSION_SERIALIZER`, to customize the session "
"serialization format. For backwards compatibility, this setting defaulted to "
"using :mod:`pickle` in Django 1.5.3, but we've changed the default to JSON "
"in 1.6. If you upgrade and switch from pickle to JSON, sessions created "
"before the upgrade will be lost. While JSON serialization does not support "
"all Python objects like :mod:`pickle` does, we highly recommend using JSON-"
"serialized sessions. Be aware of the following when checking your code to "
"determine if JSON serialization will work for your application:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an t-ionsaí seo a mhaolú trí shraitheadh sonraí seisiúin ag baint "
"úsáide as JSON seachas: mod: `pickle`. Chun é seo a éascú, thug Django 1.5.3 "
"suíomh nua isteach, :setting: `SESSION_SERIALIZER`, chun an fhormáid "
"sraitheach seisiúin a shaincheapadh. Maidir le comhoiriúnacht ar ais, "
"réamhshocraigh an socrú seo le húsáid: mod: `pickle` i Django 1.5.3, ach tá "
"an réamhshocraithe athraithe againn go JSON i 1.6. Má dhéanann tú uasghrádú "
"agus ag aistriú ó phiocán go JSON, caillfear seisiúin a cruthaíodh roimh an "
"uasghrádú Cé nach dtacaíonn sraith JSON le gach réad Python cosúil:mod: "
"`pickle` a dhéanann, molaimid go mór seisiúin JSON sraitheach a úsáid. Bí ar "
"an eolas faoi na rudaí seo a leanas agus tú ag seiceáil do chód chun a fháil "
"amach an n-oibreoidh sraith JSON do d'iarratas:"

msgid ""
"JSON requires string keys, so you will likely run into problems if you are "
"using non-string keys in ``request.session``."
msgstr ""
"Teastaíonn eochracha teaghrán ó JSON, mar sin is dócha go mbeidh fadhbanna "
"ort má tá eochracha neamh-sreang á úsáid agat i `request.session ``."

msgid ""
"Setting session expiration by passing ``datetime`` values "
"to :meth:`~django.contrib.sessions.backends.base.SessionBase.set_expiry` "
"will not work as ``datetime`` values are not serializable in JSON. You can "
"use integer values instead."
msgstr ""
"Ní oibreoidh éag seisiúin trí luachanna ``datetime`` a rith chuig: "
"`~django.contrib.sessions.backends.base.sessionbase.set_expiry` toisc nach "
"bhfuil luachanna ``datetime`` sraitheach i JSON. Is féidir leat luachanna "
"sláimhir a úsáid ina ionad sin."

msgid "See the :ref:`session_serialization` documentation for more details."
msgstr ""
"Féach an doiciméadach:ref: `session_serialization` le haghaidh tuilleadh "
"sonraí."

msgid "Object Relational Mapper changes"
msgstr "Athraíonn Mapper Coibhneasta Cuspóir"

msgid ""
"Django 1.6 contains many changes to the ORM. These changes fall mostly in "
"three categories:"
msgstr ""
"Tá go leor athruithe ar an ORM i Django 1.6. Tagann na hathruithe seo den "
"chuid is mó i dtrí chatagóir:"

msgid ""
"Bug fixes (e.g. proper join clauses for generic relations, query combining, "
"join promotion, and join trimming fixes)"
msgstr ""
"Socruithe fabhtanna (m.sh. clásail ceangail cearta le haghaidh caidreamh "
"cineálach, ceisteanna a chomhcheangal, páirt a chur chun cinn, agus ceartú"

msgid ""
"Preparation for new features. For example the ORM is now internally ready "
"for multicolumn foreign keys."
msgstr ""
"Ullmhú le haghaidh gnéithe nua. Mar shampla tá an ORM réidh go hinmheánach "
"anois le haghaidh eochracha eachtracha ilcholumn."

msgid "General cleanup."
msgstr "Glanadh ginearálta."

msgid ""
"These changes can result in some compatibility problems. For example, some "
"queries will now generate different table aliases. This can "
"affect :meth:`QuerySet.extra() <django.db.models.query.QuerySet.extra>`. In "
"addition some queries will now produce different results. An example "
"is :meth:`exclude(condition) <django.db.models.query.QuerySet.exclude>` "
"where the condition is a complex one (referencing multijoins "
"inside :class:`Q objects <django.db.models.Q>`). In many cases the affected "
"queries didn't produce correct results in Django 1.5 but do now. "
"Unfortunately there are also cases that produce different results, but "
"neither Django 1.5 nor 1.6 produce correct results."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh roinnt fadhbanna comhoiriúnachta a bheith mar thoradh ar Mar "
"shampla, ginfidh roinnt ceisteanna ainmneacha tábla éagsúla anois. "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.extra>Is féidir leis seo dul i bhfeidhm ar: "
"meth: `QuerySet.extra () `. Ina theannta sin, tabharfaidh roinnt ceisteanna "
"torthaí difriúla anois. <django.db.models.Q>Is sampla: meth: `eisiamh "
"(coinníoll) <django.db.models.query.QuerySet.exclude>`nuair is ceann casta é "
"an coinníoll (tagairt ilchomhtháirteacha taobh istigh: aicme: `rudaí Q`). I "
"go leor cásanna níor thug na ceisteanna a raibh tionchar orthu torthaí "
"cearta i Django 1.5 ach déanann siad anois. Ar an drochuair tá cásanna ann "
"freisin a tháirgeann torthaí éagsúla, ach ní tháirgeann Django 1.5 ná 1.6 "
"torthaí cearta."

msgid "Finally, there have been many changes to the ORM internal APIs."
msgstr "Faoi dheireadh, rinneadh go leor athruithe ar na APIs inmheánacha ORM."

msgid ""
"The ``django.db.models.query.EmptyQuerySet`` can't be instantiated any more "
"- it is only usable as a marker class for checking "
"if :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.none` has been called: "
"``isinstance(qs.none(), EmptyQuerySet)``"
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir an `Django.db.Models.Query.EmptyQuerySet`` a thabhairt níos mó - "
"níl sé inúsáidte ach mar aicme marcóra chun seiceáil má:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.none` tugtar: ``isinstance (qs.none (), "
"emptyQuerySet) ``"

msgid ""
"If your CSS/JavaScript code used to access HTML input widgets by type, you "
"should review it as ``type='text'`` widgets might be now output as "
"``type='email'``, ``type='url'`` or ``type='number'`` depending on their "
"corresponding field type."
msgstr ""
"Má úsáidtear do chód CSS/JavaScript chun giuirléidí ionchuir HTML a rochtain "
"de réir cineál, ba cheart duit é a athbhreithniú mar d'fhéadfadh giuirléidí "
"``type='text'`` a aschur anois mar ``type='email'``, `type='url'`` nó "
"``type='number'` ag brath ar a gcineál réimse comhfhreagrach."

msgid ""
"Form field's :attr:`~django.forms.Field.error_messages` that contain a "
"placeholder should now always use a named placeholder (``\"Value '%(value)s' "
"is too big\"`` instead of ``\"Value '%s' is too big\"``). See the "
"corresponding field documentation for details about the names of the "
"placeholders. The changes in 1.6 particularly "
"affect :class:`~django.forms.DecimalField` "
"and :class:`~django.forms.ModelMultipleChoiceField`."
msgstr ""
"Foirm field's:attr: `~django.forms.field.error_messages` ina bhfuil "
"sealbhóir áite ba cheart anois sealbhóir áit ainmnithe a úsáid i gcónaí "
"(`\"Luach '% (value) s' ró-mhór\"`` in ionad ``\"Luach '%s' ró-mór\"`). "
"Féach an doiciméadú réimse comhfhreagrach le haghaidh sonraí faoi ainmneacha "
"na sealbhóirí áite. Bíonn tionchar go háirithe ag na hathruithe i 1.6 ar: "
"aicme: `~django.forms.decimalfield` agus:class: "
"`~django.forms.ModelMultipleChoiceField`."

msgid ""
"Some :attr:`~django.forms.Field.error_messages` "
"for :class:`~django.forms.IntegerField`, :class:`~django.forms.EmailField`, "
"``IPAddressField``, :class:`~django.forms.GenericIPAddressField`, "
"and :class:`~django.forms.SlugField` have been suppressed because they "
"duplicated error messages already provided by validators tied to the fields."
msgstr ""
"Some:attr: `~django.forms.field.error_messages` le haghaidh: aicme: "
"`~django.forms.integerfield`, :class: `~django.forms.emailfield`, "
"``iPadressfield``, :class: `~django.forms.genericipAddressField`, "
"agus:class: `Django.Forms.~GineRicipAddressField` Cuireadh "
"Jango.Forms.SlugField` faoi chois toisc gur dhúbailte siad teachtaireachtaí "
"earráide a sholáthraíodh cheana féin ag bailíochtóirí ceangailte leis na "
"réimsí."

msgid ""
"Due to a change in the form validation "
"workflow, :class:`~django.forms.TypedChoiceField` ``coerce`` method should "
"always return a value present in the ``choices`` field attribute. That "
"limitation should be lift again in Django 1.7."
msgstr ""
"Mar gheall ar athrú ar an sreabhadh oibre bailíochtaithe foirme, ba "
"cheart: :class: `~django.forms.TypedChoiceField` modh ```coerce`` luach atá "
"i láthair sa tréith réimse ``roghanna ``a thabhairt ar ais i gcónaí. Ba "
"chóir an teorannú sin a ardú arís i Django 1.7."

msgid ""
"There have been changes in the way timeouts are handled in cache backends. "
"Explicitly passing in ``timeout=None`` no longer results in using the "
"default timeout. It will now set a non-expiring timeout. Passing 0 into the "
"memcache backend no longer uses the default timeout, and now will set-and-"
"expire-immediately the value."
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh athruithe ar an mbealach a láimhseáiltear amach ama i gcúltaca "
"taisce. Ní féidir an t-am réamhshocraithe a úsáid a thuilleadh mar thoradh "
"ar ``timeout=None`` ag dul isteach go sainráite. Socróidh sé anois ama neamh-"
"éag. Ní úsáideann tú 0 isteach sa chúltaca memcache an t-am réamhshocraithe "
"a thuilleadh, agus anois socraíonn sé agus rachaidh sé in éag an luach "
"láithreach."

msgid ""
"The ``django.contrib.flatpages`` app used to set custom HTTP headers for "
"debugging purposes. This functionality was not documented and made caching "
"ineffective so it has been removed, along with its generic implementation, "
"previously available in ``django.core.xheaders``."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear an aip ``django.contrib.flatpages`` chun ceanntásca saincheaptha "
"HTTP a shocrú chun críocha dífhabhtaithe. Níor doiciméadaíodh an "
"fheidhmiúlacht seo agus rinneadh an caistriú neamhéifeachtach mar sin "
"baineadh í, mar aon lena chur i bhfeidhm cineálach, ar fáil roimhe seo in "
"`django.core.xheaders`."

msgid ""
"The ``XViewMiddleware`` has been moved from ``django.middleware.doc`` to "
"``django.contrib.admindocs.middleware`` because it is an implementation "
"detail of admindocs, proven not to be reusable in general."
msgstr ""
"Tá an `xViewMiddleware`` aistrithe ó ``django.middleware.doc`` go "
"``django.contrib.admindocs.middleware`` toisc gur mionsonraí cur chun "
"feidhme de admindocs é, cruthaithe nach bhfuil sé in-athúsáidte i gcoitinne."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.db.models.GenericIPAddressField` will now only allow "
"``blank`` values if ``null`` values are also allowed. Creating a "
"``GenericIPAddressField`` where ``blank`` is allowed but ``null`` is not "
"will trigger a model validation error because ``blank`` values are always "
"stored as ``null``. Previously, storing a ``blank`` value in a field which "
"did not allow ``null`` would cause a database exception at runtime."
msgstr ""
":class: `~Django.db.Models.GenericipAddressField` anois ní cheadóidh "
"luachanna ``blank`` má cheadaítear luachanna ``null`` freisin. Cruthú "
"``GenericipAddressField`` ina gceadaítear ``blank`` ach nach bhfuil `null`` "
"spreagfaidh earráid bailíochtaithe samhail toisc go stóráiltear luachanna "
"``blank`` i gcónaí mar `null``. Roimhe seo, bheadh eisceacht bunachar sonraí "
"ina chúis le luach ``blank`` a stóráil i réimse nár cheadaigh ``null``."

msgid ""
"If a ``NoReverseMatch`` exception is raised from a method when rendering a "
"template, it is not silenced. For example, ``{{ obj.view_href }}`` will "
"cause template rendering to fail if ``view_href()`` raises "
"``NoReverseMatch``. There is no change to the :ttag:`{% url %}<url>` tag, it "
"causes template rendering to fail like always when ``NoReverseMatch`` is "
"raised."
msgstr ""
"Má ardaítear eisceacht ``NoReverseMatch`` ó mhodh agus teimpléad á "
"rindreáil, ní dhéantar é a thostú. Mar shampla, beidh ``{{obj.view_href}}`` "
"mar thoradh ar rindreáil teimpléid má ardaíonn ``view_href () "
"```noReverseMatch``. Níl aon athrú ar an gclibe:ttag: `{% url%}<url>`, is "
"cúis leis go dteipeann ar rindreáil teimpléid mar i gcónaí nuair a ardaítear "
"``noReverseMatch``."

msgid ""
":meth:`django.test.Client.logout` now "
"calls :meth:`django.contrib.auth.logout` which will send "
"the :func:`~django.contrib.auth.signals.user_logged_out` signal."
msgstr ""
":meth: `django.test.client.logout` glaonna anois:meth: "
"`django.contrib.auth.logout` a sheolfaidh an comhartha:func: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.signals.user_logged_out`."

msgid ""
":ref:`Authentication views <built-in-auth-views>` are now reversed by name, "
"not their locations in ``django.contrib.auth.views``. If you are using the "
"views without a ``name``, you should update your ``urlpatterns`` to use "
"``django.conf.urls.url()`` with the ``name`` parameter. For example::"
msgstr ""
":ref: Déantar tuairim <built-in-auth-views>í fíordheimhniúcháin a aisiompú "
"anois de réir ainm, ní a suíomhanna i ``django.contrib.auth.views``. Má tá "
"na tuairimí á úsáid agat gan ``ainm ``, ba cheart duit do `urlpatterns`` a "
"nuashonrú chun ``django.conf.urls.url ()`` a úsáid leis an bparaiméadar "
"``ainm ``. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
":class:`~django.views.generic.base.RedirectView` now has a ``pattern_name`` "
"attribute which allows it to choose the target by reversing the URL."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.views.generic.base.redirectView` tá tréith ``pattern_name`` "
"anois a ligeann dó an sprioc a roghnú tríd an URL a aisiompú."

msgid ""
"In Django 1.4 and 1.5, a blank string was unintentionally not considered to "
"be a valid password. This "
"meant :meth:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User.set_password()` would save a "
"blank password as an unusable password "
"like :meth:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User.set_unusable_password()` does, "
"and thus :meth:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User.check_password()` always "
"returned ``False`` for blank passwords. This has been corrected in this "
"release: blank passwords are now valid."
msgstr ""
"I Django 1.4 agus 1.5, níor measadh go neamhghnó gur pasfhocal bailí é "
"teaghrán bán. Sábhálfadh an meant:meth: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.user.set_password () `pasfhocal bán mar "
"phasfhocal neamhúsáidte cosúil:meth: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.user.set_unusable_password ()`, agus déanann sé "
"sin: meth: `~django.contrib.auth.models.user.check_Chuir pasfhocal () `ar "
"ais i gcónaí ``False`` le haghaidh pasfhocail bhána. Ceartaíodh é seo san "
"eisiúint seo: tá pasfhocail bán bailí anois."

msgid ""
"The admin :attr:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.changelist_view` "
"previously accepted a ``pop`` GET parameter to signify it was to be "
"displayed in a popup. This parameter has been renamed to ``_popup`` to be "
"consistent with the rest of the admin views. You should update your custom "
"templates if they use the previous parameter name."
msgstr ""
"Ghlac an admin :attr:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.changelist_view` le "
"paraiméadar GET ``pop`` chun a chur in iúl go raibh sé le taispeáint i "
"bpíosa aníos. Athainmníodh an paraiméadar seo go `` _ aníos aníos`` chun a "
"bheith comhsheasmhach leis an gcuid eile de na hamharcanna riaracháin. Ba "
"cheart duit do theimpléid saincheaptha a nuashonrú má úsáideann siad an t-"
"ainm paraiméadar roimhe seo."

msgid ""
":meth:`~django.core.validators.validate_email` now accepts email addresses "
"with ``localhost`` as the domain."
msgstr ""
":meth: `~django.core.validators.validate_email` glacann anois le seoltaí "
"ríomhphoist le ``localhost`` mar an fearainn."

msgid ""
"The new :option:`makemessages --keep-pot` option prevents deleting the "
"temporary ``.pot`` file generated before creating the ``.po`` file."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann an rogha nua:option: `makemessages --keep-pot` cosc ar an gcomhad "
"sealadach ``.pot`` a ghintear a scriosadh sula gcruthaítear an comhad "
"``.po``."

msgid ""
"The undocumented ``django.core.servers.basehttp.WSGIServerException`` has "
"been removed. Use ``socket.error`` provided by the standard library instead. "
"This change was also released in Django 1.5.5."
msgstr ""
"Baineadh an ``django.core.servers.basehttp.wsgiserverexception`` gan "
"doiciméadú. Úsáid ``socket.error`` a sholáthraíonn an leabharlann "
"caighdeánach ina ionad. Scaoileadh an t-athrú seo freisin i Django 1.5.5."

msgid ""
"The signature "
"of :meth:`django.views.generic.base.RedirectView.get_redirect_url` has "
"changed and now accepts positional arguments as well (``*args, **kwargs``). "
"Any unnamed captured group will now be passed to ``get_redirect_url()`` "
"which may result in a ``TypeError`` if you don't update the signature of "
"your custom method."
msgstr ""
"Tá síniú de:meth: `Django.Views.Generic.Base.RedirectView.get_Redirect_URL` "
"athraithe agus glacann sé anois le hargóintí seasmhacha freisin (``*args, "
"**kwargs ``). Cuirfear aon ghrúpa gabháilte gan ainm ar aghaidh chuig "
"``get_redirect_url () ``agus d'fhéadfadh ``typeError`` a bheith mar thoradh "
"air mura ndéanann tú síniú do mhodha saincheaptha a nuashonrú."

msgid "Features deprecated in 1.6"
msgstr "Gnéithe atá díscríofa i 1.6"

msgid "Transaction management APIs"
msgstr "APIs bainistíochta idirbheart"

msgid ""
"Transaction management was completely overhauled in Django 1.6, and the "
"current APIs are deprecated:"
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh athchóiriú go hiomlán ar bhainistíocht idirbheart i Django 1.6, "
"agus tá na APIs reatha dlús:"

msgid "``django.middleware.transaction.TransactionMiddleware``"
msgstr "``Django.middleware.Transaction.TransactionMiddleWare``"

msgid "``django.db.transaction.autocommit``"
msgstr "``django.db.transaction.autochommit``"

msgid "``django.db.transaction.commit_on_success``"
msgstr "``django.db.transaction.comit_on_rath``"

msgid "``django.db.transaction.commit_manually``"
msgstr "``django.db.transaction.comm_lámh``"

msgid "the ``TRANSACTIONS_MANAGED`` setting"
msgstr "an socrú ``TRANSACTIONS_MANAGED``"

msgid "``django.contrib.comments``"
msgstr "``django.contrib.tuairim``"

msgid ""
"Django's comment framework has been deprecated and is no longer supported. "
"It will be available in Django 1.6 and 1.7, and removed in Django 1.8. Most "
"users will be better served with a custom solution, or a hosted product like "
"Disqus__."
msgstr ""
"Tá creat tráchta Django díluaite agus ní thacaítear leis a thuilleadh. Beidh "
"sé ar fáil i Django 1.6 agus 1.7, agus bainfear é i Django 1.8. Freastalfar "
"níos fearr ar fhormhór na n-úsáideoirí le réiteach saincheaptha, nó táirge "
"óstáilte mar Disqus__."

msgid ""
"The code formerly known as ``django.contrib.comments`` is `still available "
"in an external repository`__."
msgstr ""
"Tá an cód ar a dtugtar ``django.contrib.comments`` roimhe seo `fós ar fáil i "
"stóras seachtrach`__."

msgid "Support for PostgreSQL versions older than 8.4"
msgstr "Tacaíocht do leaganacha PostgreSQL níos sine ná 8.4"

msgid ""
"The end of upstream support periods was reached in December 2011 for "
"PostgreSQL 8.2 and in February 2013 for 8.3. As a consequence, Django 1.6 "
"sets 8.4 as the minimum PostgreSQL version it officially supports."
msgstr ""
"Sroichtear deireadh na dtréimhsí tacaíochta suas srutha i mí na Nollag 2011 "
"do PostgreSQL 8.2 agus i mí Feabhra 2013 do 8.3. Mar thoradh air sin, "
"socraíonn Django 1.6 8.4 mar an leagan íosta PostgreSQL a thacaíonn sé go "
"hoifigiúil."

msgid ""
"You're strongly encouraged to use the most recent version of PostgreSQL "
"available, because of performance improvements and to take advantage of the "
"native streaming replication available in PostgreSQL 9.x."
msgstr ""
"Spreagtar go láidir duit an leagan is déanaí de PostgreSQL atá ar fáil a "
"úsáid, mar gheall ar fheabhsuithe feidhmíochta agus chun leas a bhaint as an "
"macasamhail sruthú dúchasach atá ar fáil i PostgreSQL 9.x."

msgid "Changes to :ttag:`cycle` and :ttag:`firstof`"
msgstr "Athruithe ar:ttag: `timthriall` agus:ttag: `firstof`"

msgid ""
"The template system generally escapes all variables to avoid XSS attacks. "
"However, due to an accident of history, the :ttag:`cycle` "
"and :ttag:`firstof` tags render their arguments as-is."
msgstr ""
"De ghnáth éalaíonn an córas teimpléid gach athróg chun ionsaithe XSS a "
"sheachaint. Mar gheall ar thimpiste staire, áfach, tugann na clibeanna:ttag: "
"`cicle` agus:ttag: `firstof` a gcuid argóintí mar atá."

msgid ""
"Django 1.6 starts a process to correct this inconsistency. The ``future`` "
"template library provides alternate implementations of :ttag:`cycle` "
"and :ttag:`firstof` that autoescape their inputs. If you're using these "
"tags, you're encouraged to include the following line at the top of your "
"templates to enable the new behavior:"
msgstr ""
"Tosaíonn Django 1.6 próiseas chun an neamhréireacht seo a cheartú. "
"Soláthraíonn leabharlann teimpléad ``todhcha`` cur i bhfeidhm malartacha "
"de:ttag: `cicle` agus:ttag: `firstof` a n-ionchuir a n-ionchuir a n-"
"uathoibríoch. Má tá na clibeanna seo á úsáid agat, moltar duit an líne seo a "
"leanas a áireamh ag barr do theimpléid chun an t-iompar nua a chumasú:"

msgid "or:"
msgstr "nó:"

msgid ""
"The tags implementing the old behavior have been deprecated, and in Django "
"1.8, the old behavior will be replaced with the new behavior. To ensure "
"compatibility with future versions of Django, existing templates should be "
"modified to use the ``future`` versions."
msgstr ""
"Tá na clibeanna a chuireann an sean-iompar i bhfeidhm imithe i léig, agus i "
"Django 1.8, cuirfear an t-iompar nua in ionad an tseaniompar. Chun "
"comhoiriúnacht le leaganacha amach anseo de Django a chinntiú, ba cheart "
"teimpléid atá ann cheana a mhodhnú chun na leaganacha ``future`` a úsáid."

msgid ""
"If necessary, you can temporarily disable auto-escaping "
"with :func:`~django.utils.safestring.mark_safe` or :ttag:`{% autoescape off "
"%} <autoescape>`."
msgstr ""
"<autoescape>Más gá, is féidir leat éalú uathoibríoch a dhíchumasú go "
"sealadach le:func: `~django.utils.safestring.mark_safe` nó:ttag: `{% "
"autoescape off%}`."

msgid "``CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_ANONYMOUS_ONLY`` setting"
msgstr "``CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_ANONYMOUS_ONLY`` socrú"

msgid ""
"``CacheMiddleware`` and ``UpdateCacheMiddleware`` used to provide a way to "
"cache requests only if they weren't made by a logged-in user. This mechanism "
"was largely ineffective because the middleware correctly takes into account "
"the ``Vary: Cookie`` HTTP header, and this header is being set on a variety "
"of occasions, such as:"
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear ``Cachemiddleware`` agus ``UpdateCacheMiddleware`` chun bealach a "
"sholáthar chun iarratais a thaisceadh ach amháin mura ndearna úsáideoir "
"logáilte isteach iad. Bhí an meicníocht seo neamhéifeachtach den chuid is mó "
"toisc go gcuireann an meán-earraí ceannteideal HTTP ``Vary: Cookie` san "
"áireamh i gceart, agus tá an ceannteideal seo á leagan síos ar ócáidí "
"éagsúla, mar shampla:"

msgid "accessing the session, or"
msgstr "rochtain a fháil ar an seisiún, nó"

msgid "using CSRF protection, which is turned on by default, or"
msgstr ""
"ag baint úsáide as cosaint CSRF, atá casaithe air de réir réamhshocraithe, nó"

msgid ""
"using a client-side library which sets cookies, like `Google Analytics`__."
msgstr ""
"ag baint úsáide as leabharlann taobh an chliaint a shocraíonn fianáin, "
"cosúil le `Google Analytics`__."

msgid ""
"This makes the cache effectively work on a per-session basis regardless of "
"the ``CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_ANONYMOUS_ONLY`` setting."
msgstr ""
"Fágann sé seo go n-oibríonn an taisce go héifeachtach ar bhonn in aghaidh na "
"seisiúin beag beann ar an socrú ``CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_ANONYMOUS_ONLY`."

msgid "``SEND_BROKEN_LINK_EMAILS`` setting"
msgstr "Socrú ```SEND_BROKEN_LINK_EMAILS``"

msgid ""
":class:`~django.middleware.common.CommonMiddleware` used to provide basic "
"reporting of broken links by email when ``SEND_BROKEN_LINK_EMAILS`` is set "
"to ``True``."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.middleware.common.commonMiddleware` a úsáidtear chun "
"tuairisciú bunúsach a sholáthar ar naisc briste trí ríomhphost nuair a "
"shocraítear ``SEND_BROKEN_LINK_EMAILS`` go `True``."

msgid ""
"Because of intractable ordering problems "
"between :class:`~django.middleware.common.CommonMiddleware` "
"and :class:`~django.middleware.locale.LocaleMiddleware`, this feature was "
"split out into a new "
"middleware: :class:`~django.middleware.common.BrokenLinkEmailsMiddleware`."
msgstr ""
"Mar gheall ar fhadhbanna ordaithe dochreidte idir:class: "
"`~django.middleware.common.commonMiddleware` agus:class: "
"`~django.middleware.locale.localeMiddleware`, roinntear an ghné seo amach i "
"middleware nua: :class: "
"`~django.middleware.common.BrokenLinkemMiddailsLeware`."

msgid ""
"If you're relying on this feature, you should add "
"``'django.middleware.common.BrokenLinkEmailsMiddleware'`` to your "
"``MIDDLEWARE_CLASSES`` setting and remove ``SEND_BROKEN_LINK_EMAILS`` from "
"your settings."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag brath ar an ngné seo, ba chóir duit "
"``Django.middleware.common.BrokenLinkemailsMiddleware'` a chur le do shuíomh "
"``MIDDLEWARE_CLASSES`` agus `SEND_BROKEN_LINK_EMAILS`` a bhaint as do "
"shocruithe."

msgid "``_has_changed`` method on widgets"
msgstr "Modh ``_has_changed`` ar ghuirléidí"

msgid ""
"If you defined your own form widgets and defined the ``_has_changed`` method "
"on a widget, you should now define this method on the form field itself."
msgstr ""
"Má shainigh tú do ghuirléidí foirme féin agus má shainigh tú an modh "
"``_has_changed`` ar ghuirléid, ba cheart duit an modh seo a shainiú anois ar "
"an réimse foirme féin."

msgid "``module_name`` model _meta attribute"
msgstr "``module_name`` tréith samhail _meta"

msgid ""
"``Model._meta.module_name`` was renamed to ``model_name``. Despite being a "
"private API, it will go through a regular deprecation path."
msgstr ""
"``Samhail. Ainmníodh _meta.module_name`` go ``model_name``. In ainneoin gur "
"API príobháideach é, rachaidh sé trí chosán diúltaithe rialta."

msgid "``get_(add|change|delete)_permission`` model _meta methods"
msgstr "Modhanna múnla _meta ``get_ (cuir |athraithe|scriosadh) _ceadúna``"

msgid ""
"``Model._meta.get_(add|change|delete)_permission`` methods were deprecated. "
"Even if they were not part of the public API they'll also go through a "
"regular deprecation path. You can replace them with "
"``django.contrib.auth.get_permission_codename('action', Model._meta)`` where "
"``'action'`` is ``'add'``, ``'change'``, or ``'delete'``."
msgstr ""
"``Samhail. Cuireadh modhanna _meta.get_ (add |athraithe|scriosadh) ar "
"mhodhanna _ceadúnaí. Fiú mura raibh siad mar chuid den API poiblí rachaidh "
"siad trí chosán diúltaithe rialta freisin. Is féidir leat "
"``django.contrib.auth.get_permission_codename ('action', Samhail) a chur in "
"ionad iad. _meta) ``áit a bhfuil ``'gníomh'` ```'add'``, ```athraithe``, nó "
"```'scriose'`."

msgid "``get_query_set`` and similar methods renamed to ``get_queryset``"
msgstr ""
"Athainmníodh ``get_query_set`` agus modhanna comhchosúla go ``get_queryset``"

msgid ""
"Methods that return a ``QuerySet`` such as ``Manager.get_query_set`` or "
"``ModelAdmin.queryset`` have been renamed to ``get_queryset``."
msgstr ""
"Athainmníodh modhanna a thugann `QuerySet`` ar nós `Manager.get_query_set`` "
"nó ``ModelAdmin.querySet`` go `get_queryset``."

msgid ""
"If you are writing a library that implements, for example, a "
"``Manager.get_query_set`` method, and you need to support old Django "
"versions, you should rename the method and conditionally add an alias with "
"the old name::"
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag scríobh leabharlann a chuireann modh `Manager.get_query_set`` i "
"bhfeidhm, mar shampla, agus ní mór duit tacú le seanleaganacha Django, ba "
"cheart duit an modh a athainmniú agus alias a chur leis an sean-ainm go "
"coinníollach::"

msgid ""
"If you are writing a library that needs to call the ``get_queryset`` method "
"and must support old Django versions, you should write::"
msgstr ""
"Má tá leabharlann á scríobh agat a chaithfidh glaoch ar an modh "
"``get_queryset`` agus nach gcaithfidh tú tacú le seanleaganacha Django, ba "
"chóir duit scríobh:"

msgid ""
"In the general case of a custom manager that both implements its own "
"``get_queryset`` method and calls that method, and needs to work with older "
"Django versions, and libraries that have not been updated yet, it is useful "
"to define a ``get_queryset_compat`` method as below and use it internally to "
"your manager::"
msgstr ""
"I gcás ginearálta bainisteoir saincheaptha a chur i bhfeidhm a mhodh "
"`get_queryset` féin agus a ghlaonn an modh sin, agus a chaithfidh oibriú le "
"leaganacha níos sine Django, agus leabharlanna nár nuashonraíodh fós, tá sé "
"úsáideach modh `get_queryset_compat` a shainiú mar thíos agus é a úsáid go "
"hinmheánach do do bhainisteoir:"

msgid ""
"This helps to minimize the changes that are needed, but also works correctly "
"in the case of subclasses (such as ``RelatedManagers`` from Django 1.5) "
"which might override either ``get_query_set`` or ``get_queryset``."
msgstr ""
"Cuidíonn sé seo leis na hathruithe atá ag teastáil a íoslaghdú, ach oibríonn "
"sé i gceart freisin i gcás fo-aicmí (mar shampla ``RelatedManagers`` ó "
"Django 1.5) a d'fhéadfadh ``get_query_set`` nó ``get_queryset`` a shárú."

msgid "``shortcut`` view and URLconf"
msgstr "Amharc ``gearrchearr`` agus URLConf"

msgid ""
"The ``shortcut`` view was moved from ``django.views.defaults`` to "
"``django.contrib.contenttypes.views`` shortly after the 1.0 release, but the "
"old location was never deprecated. This oversight was corrected in Django "
"1.6 and you should now use the new location."
msgstr ""
"Bogadh an radharc ``shortcut`` ó `django.views.defaults`` go "
"``django.contrib.contenttypes.views`` go gairid tar éis an scaoileadh 1.0, "
"ach níor dhíothas an sean-áit riamh. Ceartaíodh an maoirseacht seo i Django "
"1.6 agus ba cheart duit an suíomh nua a úsáid anois."

msgid ""
"The URLconf ``django.conf.urls.shortcut`` was also deprecated. If you're "
"including it in an URLconf, simply replace::"
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh an URLConf ``django.conf.urls.shortcut`` a dhíchur freisin. Má tá "
"tú ag áireamh é i URLConf, ní gá ach: a chur in ionad:"

msgid "with::"
msgstr "le::"

msgid "``ModelForm`` without ``fields`` or ``exclude``"
msgstr "``Samhlfhoirme`` gan `réimsí ``nó ``eisiam``"

msgid ""
"Previously, if you wanted a :class:`~django.forms.ModelForm` to use all "
"fields on the model, you could simply omit the ``Meta.fields`` attribute, "
"and all fields would be used."
msgstr ""
"Roimhe seo, dá dteastaíonn uait a:class: `~Django.Forms.ModelForm` chun gach "
"réimse ar an tsamhail a úsáid, d'fhéadfá an tréith ``Meta.Fields`` a "
"fhágáil, agus úsáidfí gach réimse."

msgid ""
"This can lead to security problems where fields are added to the model and, "
"unintentionally, automatically become editable by end users. In some cases, "
"particular with boolean fields, it is possible for this problem to be "
"completely invisible. This is a form of `Mass assignment vulnerability "
"<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mass_assignment_vulnerability>`_."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh fadhbanna slándála a bheith mar thoradh air seo ina gcuirtear "
"réimsí leis an tsamhail agus, gan aon ghnó, a éiríonn siad in-"
"eagarthóireachta go huathoibríoch I roinnt cásanna, go háirithe le réimsí "
"boolean, is féidir go mbeadh an fhadhb seo dofheicthe go hiomlán. < https://"
"en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mass_assignment_vulnerability>Is foirm é seo de "
"`Leochaileacht sannadh ollmhóraí`_."

msgid ""
"For this reason, this behavior is deprecated, and using the ``Meta.exclude`` "
"option is strongly discouraged. Instead, all fields that are intended for "
"inclusion in the form should be listed explicitly in the ``fields`` "
"attribute."
msgstr ""
"Ar an gcúis seo, déantar an t-iompar seo a dhíchur, agus déantar an rogha "
"`Meta.exclude` a úsáid go láidir. Ina áit sin, ba chóir gach réimse atá "
"beartaithe lena áireamh san fhoirm a liostáil go sainráite sa tréith "
"``réimsí `fields``."

msgid ""
"If this security concern really does not apply in your case, there is a "
"shortcut to explicitly indicate that all fields should be used - use the "
"special value ``\"__all__\"`` for the fields attribute::"
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil feidhm ag an imní slándála seo i ndáiríre i do chás, tá aicearra "
"ann chun a léiriú go sainráite gur chóir gach réimse a úsáid - bain úsáid as "
"an luach speisialta ``\"__all__\"`` don tréith réimsí:"

msgid ""
"If you have custom ``ModelForms`` that only need to be used in the admin, "
"there is another option. The admin has its own methods for defining fields "
"(``fieldsets`` etc.), and so adding a list of fields to the ``ModelForm`` is "
"redundant. Instead, simply omit the ``Meta`` inner class of the "
"``ModelForm``, or omit the ``Meta.model`` attribute. Since the "
"``ModelAdmin`` subclass knows which model it is for, it can add the "
"necessary attributes to derive a functioning ``ModelForm``. This behavior "
"also works for earlier Django versions."
msgstr ""
"Má tá ``ModelForms ``saincheaptha agat nach gá ach a úsáid sa riarachán, tá "
"rogha eile ann. Tá a mhodhanna féin ag an riarachán chun réimsí a shainiú "
"(`fieldsets`` srl.), agus mar sin tá sé iomarcach liosta réimsí a chur leis "
"an `Modelform``. Ina áit sin, fág ach an aicme istigh ``Meta`` den "
"`ModelForm ``a fhágáil, nó an tréith ``Meta.Model`` a fhágáil. Ós rud é go "
"bhfuil a fhios ag an bhfo-aicme `ModelAdmin` cén tsamhail dó a bhfuil sé, "
"féadfaidh sé na tréithe riachtanacha a chur leis chun `ModelForm "
"``feidhmiúil a bhaint amach. Oibríonn an t-iompar seo freisin le haghaidh "
"leaganacha Django níos luaithe."

msgid "``UpdateView`` and ``CreateView`` without explicit fields"
msgstr "``UpdateView`` agus ``CreateView`` gan réimsí follasacha"

msgid ""
"The generic views :class:`~django.views.generic.edit.CreateView` "
"and :class:`~django.views.generic.edit.UpdateView`, and anything else "
"derived from :class:`~django.views.generic.edit.ModelFormMixin`, are "
"vulnerable to the security problem described in the section above, because "
"they can automatically create a ``ModelForm`` that uses all fields for a "
"model."
msgstr ""
"Tá na tuairimí cineálacha:class: `~django.views.generic.edit.createView` "
"agus:class: `~django.views.generic.edit.updateView`, agus aon rud eile a "
"dhíorthaítear ó:class: `~Django.Views.Generic.Edit.ModelFormMixin`, "
"leochaileach don fhadhb slándála a thuairiscítear sa chuid thuas, toisc gur "
"féidir leo ``ModelFormixin` a chruthú go huathoibríoch Foirm ``a úsáideann "
"gach réimse le haghaidh samhail."

msgid ""
"For this reason, if you use these views for editing models, you must also "
"supply the ``fields`` attribute (new in Django 1.6), which is a list of "
"model fields and works in the same way as "
"the :class:`~django.forms.ModelForm` ``Meta.fields`` attribute. "
"Alternatively, you can set the ``form_class`` attribute to a ``ModelForm`` "
"that explicitly defines the fields to be used. Defining an ``UpdateView`` or "
"``CreateView`` subclass to be used with a model but without an explicit list "
"of fields is deprecated."
msgstr ""
"Ar an gcúis seo, má úsáideann tú na tuairimí seo chun samhlacha a chur in "
"eagar, ní mór duit an tréith ``fields` (nua i Django 1.6) a sholáthar "
"freisin, ar liosta de réimsí samhlacha é agus a oibríonn ar an mbealach "
"céanna leis an tréith: `~django.forms.modelform` `Meta.fields``. De rogha "
"air sin, is féidir leat an tréith ``form_class`` a shocrú le ``Modelform`` a "
"shainmhíníonn go sainráite na réimsí atá le húsáid. Tá fo-aicme "
"``UpdateView`` nó `CreateView`` a shainmhíniú le húsáid le samhail ach gan "
"liosta follasach réimsí a shainmhíniú."

msgid ""
"Munging of help text of model form fields for ``ManyToManyField`` fields"
msgstr ""
"Téacs cabhrach de réimsí foirm mhúnla a ghearradh do réimsí "
"``ManyTomanyField`"

msgid ""
"All special handling of the ``help_text`` attribute of ``ManyToManyField`` "
"model fields performed by standard model or model form fields as described "
"in :ref:`m2m-help_text` above is deprecated and will be removed in Django "
"1.8."
msgstr ""
"Tá gach láimhseáil speisialta ar an tréith ``help_text`` de réimsí samhail "
"``ManyTomanyField`` a dhéantar ag réimsí caighdeánacha samhail nó foirm "
"mhúnla mar a thuairiscítear in:ref: `m2m-help_text` thuas a dhíothú agus "
"bainfear é i Django 1.8."

msgid ""
"Help text of these fields will need to be handled either by applications, "
"custom form fields or widgets, just like happens with the rest of the model "
"field types."
msgstr ""
"Ní mór téacs cabhrach na réimsí seo a láimhseáil le feidhmchláir, réimsí "
"foirme saincheaptha nó giuirléidí, díreach mar a tharlaíonn leis an gcuid "
"eile de na cineálacha réimse samhail."

msgid "Django 1.6.1 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.6.1"

msgid "*December 12, 2013*"
msgstr "*12 Nollaig, 2013*"

msgid ""
"This is Django 1.6.1, a bugfix release for Django 1.6. In addition to the "
"bug fixes listed below, translations submitted since the 1.6 release are "
"also included."
msgstr ""
"Is é seo Django 1.6.1, scaoileadh bugfix do Django 1.6. Chomh maith leis na "
"réitigh fabhtanna atá liostaithe thíos, tá aistriúcháin a cuireadh isteach ó "
"scaoileadh 1.6 san áireamh freisin."

msgid "Bug fixes"
msgstr "Socruithe fabhtanna"

msgid ""
"Fixed ``BCryptSHA256PasswordHasher`` with ``py-bcrypt`` and Python 3 "
"(#21398)."
msgstr ""
"Seasta ``bCryptsha256PasswordHasher`` le `py-bcrypt`` agus Python 3 (#21398)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression that prevented a ``ForeignKey`` with a hidden reverse "
"manager (``related_name`` ending with '+') from being used as a lookup for "
"``prefetch_related`` (#21410)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú a chuir cosc ar ``ForeignKey`` le bainisteoir droim i "
"bhfolach (``related_name`` ag críochnú le '+') a úsáid mar chuardach do "
"``prefetch_related`` (#21410)."

msgid ""
"Fixed :meth:`Queryset.datetimes<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.datetimes>` "
"raising ``AttributeError`` in some situations (#21432)."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.datetimes>Socraithe: Meth: "
"`QuerySet.DateTimes `ag ardú ``AttributeError`` i roinnt cásanna (#21432)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression that prevented editable ``GenericRelation`` subclasses "
"from working in ``ModelForms`` (#21428)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú a chuir cosc ar fho-aicmí ``GenericRelation`, "
"eagarthóireachta ó bheith ag obair i `ModelForms' (#21428)."

msgid ""
"Added missing ``to_python`` method for ``ModelMultipleChoiceField`` which is "
"required in Django 1.6 to properly detect changes from initial values "
"(#21568)."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh modh `to_python`` in easnamh le haghaidh "
"``ModelMultipleChoiceField`` atá riachtanach i Django 1.6 chun athruithe a "
"bhrath i gceart ó luachanna tosaigh (#21568)."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``django.contrib.humanize`` translations where the Unicode sequence "
"for the non-breaking space was returned verbatim (#21415)."
msgstr ""
"Aistriúcháin ``django.contrib.humanize`` seasta inar cuireadh seicheamh "
"Unicode don spás neamh-bhriseadh ar ais focal faire (#21415)."

msgid ""
"Fixed :djadmin:`loaddata` error when fixture file name contained any dots "
"not related to file extensions (#21457) or when fixture path was relative "
"but located in a subdirectory (#21551)."
msgstr ""
"Socraithe: DJADmin: earráid `loaddata` nuair a bhí aon poncanna in ainm an "
"chomhaid daingneáin nach raibh baint acu le síntí comhaid (#21457) nó nuair "
"a bhí cosán daingneáin coibhneasta ach suite i bhfo-eolaire (#21551)."

msgid ""
"Fixed display of inline instances in formsets when parent has 0 for primary "
"key (#21472)."
msgstr ""
"Taispeántas seasta cásanna inlíne i bhfoirmeacha nuair a bhíonn 0 ag an "
"tuismitheoir don eochair bhunscoile (#21472)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression where custom querysets for foreign keys were overwritten "
"if ``ModelAdmin`` had ordering set (#21405)."
msgstr ""
"Socraíodh aischéimniú inar scríobhadh ceisteanna saincheaptha le haghaidh "
"eochracha eachtracha eachtracha má bhí tacar ordaithe ag ``ModelAdmin` "
"(#21405)."

msgid ""
"Removed mention of a feature in the ``--locale``/``-l`` option of the "
"``makemessages`` and ``compilemessages`` commands that never worked as "
"promised: Support of multiple locale names separated by commas. It's still "
"possible to specify multiple locales in one run by using the option multiple "
"times (#21488, #17181)."
msgstr ""
"Luadh bainte ar ghné sna horduithe ``--locale``/``-l`` de na horduithe "
"``makemessages`` agus ``compilemessages`` nár oibrigh riamh mar a gealladh: "
"Tacaíocht d'ainmneacha áitiúla iolracha atá scartha le camóga. Is féidir fós "
"go leor áiteanna a shonrú in aon rith amháin tríd an rogha a úsáid arís agus "
"arís eile (#21488, #17181)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression that unnecessarily triggered settings configuration when "
"importing ``get_wsgi_application`` (#21486)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú a spreag cumraíocht socruithe gan ghá agus iad ag "
"iompórtáil ``get_wsgi_application`` (#21486)."

msgid ""
"Fixed test client ``logout()`` method when using the cookie-based session "
"backend (#21448)."
msgstr ""
"Modh “logout ()” cliant tástála seasta agus an cúltaca seisiúin bunaithe ar "
"fianáin á úsáid (#21448)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when a ``GeometryField`` uses a non-geometric widget (#21496)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste nuair a úsáideann ``GeometryField` giuirléid neamh-"
"geoiméadrach (#21496)."

msgid "Fixed password hash upgrade when changing the iteration count (#21535)."
msgstr ""
"Uasghrádú hash pasfhocal seasta agus an comhaireamh athraithe á athrú "
"(#21535)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a bug in the debug view when the URLconf only contains one element "
"(#21530)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh fabht sa radharc dífhabhtaithe nuair nach bhfuil ach eilimint "
"amháin sa URLConf (#21530)."

msgid ""
"Re-added missing search result count and reset link in changelist admin view "
"(#21510)."
msgstr ""
"Athchuir comhaireamh torthaí cuardaigh in easnamh agus nasc athshocraithe i "
"radharc riaracháin an liosta athraithe (#21510)."

msgid ""
"The current language is no longer saved to the session by "
"``LocaleMiddleware`` on every response, but rather only after a logout "
"(#21473)."
msgstr ""
"Ní shábháiltear an teanga reatha chuig an seisiún ag ``Localemiddleware`` ar "
"gach freagra, ach amháin tar éis logáil amach (#21473)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when executing ``runserver`` on non-English systems and when "
"the formatted date in its output contained non-ASCII characters (#21358)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste nuair a bhí ``runserver ``á fhorghníomhú ar chórais neamh-"
"Bhéarla agus nuair a bhí carachtair neamh-ASCII sa dáta formáidithe ina "
"aschur (#21358)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash in the debug view after an exception occurred on Python ≥ 3.3 "
"(#21443)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste sa radharc dífhabhtaithe tar éis eisceacht tarlú ar Python "
"≥ 3.3 (#21443)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash in :class:`~django.db.models.ImageField` on some platforms "
"(Homebrew and RHEL6 reported) (#21355)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste in:class: `~django.db.models.imagefield` ar roinnt ardáin "
"(tuairiscigh Homebrew agus RHEL6) (#21355)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression when using generic relations in "
"``ModelAdmin.list_filter`` (#21431)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú nuair a bhíonn caidreamh cineálach á úsáid agat i "
"``ModelAdmin.list_filter`` (#21431)."

msgid "Django 1.6.10 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.6.10"

msgid "Django 1.6.10 fixes several security issues in 1.6.9."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.6.10 roinnt saincheisteanna slándála i 1.6.9."

msgid "Database denial-of-service with ``ModelMultipleChoiceField``"
msgstr "Diúltú seirbhíse bunachar sonraí le ``ModelMultipleChoicefield`"

msgid ""
"Given a form that uses ``ModelMultipleChoiceField`` and "
"``show_hidden_initial=True`` (not a documented API), it was possible for a "
"user to cause an unreasonable number of SQL queries by submitting duplicate "
"values for the field's data. The validation logic in "
"``ModelMultipleChoiceField`` now deduplicates submitted values to address "
"this issue."
msgstr ""
"Mar gheall ar fhoirm a úsáideann ``ModelMultipleChoiceField`` agus "
"``show_hidden_initial=true`` (ní API doiciméadaithe), bhí sé indéanta "
"d'úsáideoir líon míréasúnta fiosrúcháin SQL a chur faoi deara trí luachanna "
"dúblacha a chur isteach do shonraí an réimse. Déanann an loighic "
"bailíochtaithe in `ModelMultipleChoiceField` luachanna curtha isteach a "
"dhídhúbailt anois chun aghaidh a thabhairt ar an gceist seo."

msgid "Django 1.6.11 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.6.11"

msgid "Django 1.6.11 fixes two security issues in 1.6.10."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.6.11 dhá shaincheist slándála i 1.6.10."

msgid "Denial-of-service possibility with ``strip_tags()``"
msgstr "Féidearthacht seirbhíse a dhiúltú le ``strip_tags () ``"

msgid ""
"Last year :func:`~django.utils.html.strip_tags`  was changed to work "
"iteratively. The problem is that the size of the input it's processing can "
"increase on each iteration which results in an infinite loop in "
"``strip_tags()``. This issue only affects versions of Python that haven't "
"received :bpo:`a bugfix in HTMLParser <20288>`; namely Python < 2.7.7 and "
"3.3.5. Some operating system vendors have also backported the fix for the "
"Python bug into their packages of earlier versions."
msgstr ""
"An bhliain seo caite: athraíodh func: `~django.utils.html.strip_tags` chun "
"oibriú go hiarrthúil. Is í an fhadhb atá ann ná gur féidir le méid an "
"ionchuir a phróiseálann sé méadú ar gach athrá a mbíonn lúb gan teorainn mar "
"thoradh air i `strip_tags () `. Ní théann an tsaincheist seo ach ar "
"leaganacha de Python nach bhfuair: bpo: `bugfix in HTMLParser <20288>`; "
"eadhon Python <2.7.7 agus 3.3.5. Tá roinnt díoltóirí córais oibriúcháin tar "
"éis an socrú don fhabhtán Python a chur ar ais ina bpacáistí de leaganacha "
"níos luaithe."

msgid ""
"To remedy this issue, ``strip_tags()`` will now return the original input if "
"it detects the length of the string it's processing increases. Remember that "
"absolutely NO guarantee is provided about the results of ``strip_tags()`` "
"being HTML safe. So NEVER mark safe the result of a ``strip_tags()`` call "
"without escaping it first, for example "
"with :func:`~django.utils.html.escape`."
msgstr ""
"Chun an cheist seo a leigheas, cuirfidh `strip_tags () ``an t-ionchur "
"bunaidh ar ais anois má aimsíonn sé fad an teaghrán a mhéadaíonn sé. "
"Cuimhnigh nach gcuirtear aon ráthaíocht ar fáil go hiomlán faoi thorthaí "
"`strip_tags () ``a bheith sábháilte HTML. Mar sin NÁ marcáil go sábháilte "
"toradh glao ``strip_tags () ``gan éalú air ar dtús, mar shampla le:func: "
"`~django.utils.html.escape`."

msgid "Django 1.6.2 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.6.2"

msgid "*February 6, 2014*"
msgstr "*6 Feabhra, 2014*"

msgid ""
"This is Django 1.6.2, a bugfix release for Django 1.6. Django 1.6.2 fixes "
"several bugs in 1.6.1:"
msgstr ""
"Seo Django 1.6.2, scaoileadh bugfix do Django 1.6. Socraíonn Django 1.6.2 "
"roinnt fabhtanna i 1.6.1:"

msgid ""
"Prevented the base geometry object of a prepared geometry to be garbage "
"collected, which could lead to crash Django (:ticket:`21662`)."
msgstr ""
"Chuir sé cosc ar réad geoiméadrach bonn geoiméadra ullmhaithe a bhailiú "
"truflais, rud a d'fhéadfadh a bheith mar thoradh ar thimpiste Django "
"(:ticket: `21662`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when executing the :djadmin:`changepassword` command when the "
"user object representation contained non-ASCII characters (:ticket:`21627`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste agus an t-ordú:djadmin: `changepassword` á fhorghníomhú "
"nuair a bhí carachtair neamh-ASCII san ionadaíocht réad úsáideora (:ticket: "
"`21627`)."

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`collectstatic` command will raise an error rather than default "
"to using the current working directory if :setting:`STATIC_ROOT` is not set. "
"Combined with the ``--clear`` option, the previous behavior could wipe "
"anything below the current working directory (:ticket:`21581`)."
msgstr ""
"Ardóidh an t-ordú: DjaDmin: `collectstatic` earráid seachas réamhshocraithe "
"chun an eolaire oibre reatha a úsáid mura bhfuil: setting: `STATIC_ROOT` "
"socraithe. In éineacht leis an rogha ``--clear``, d'fhéadfadh an t-iompar "
"roimhe seo aon rud a scriosadh faoi bhun an eolaire oibre reatha (: ticket: "
"`21581`)."

msgid "Fixed mail encoding on Python 3.3.3+ (:ticket:`21093`)."
msgstr "Ionchódú ríomhphoist seasta ar Python 3.3.3+ (: ticéad: `21093`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed an issue where when ``settings.DATABASES['default']['AUTOCOMMIT'] = "
"False``, the connection wasn't in autocommit mode but Django pretended it "
"was."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh saincheist nuair a bhí `Settings.databases ['default'] "
"['AUTOCOMMIT'] = False ``, an nasc i mód autocommit ach ligean Django go "
"raibh sé."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression in multiple-table inheritance ``exclude()`` queries "
"(:ticket:`21787`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú i gceisteanna oidhreachta ioltábla ``eisiamh () "
"``(:ticket: `21787`)."

msgid ""
"Added missing items to ``django.utils.timezone.__all__`` (:ticket:`21880`)."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh míreanna in easnamh le ``django.utils.timezone. __all__`` (:ticéad: "
"`21880`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a field misalignment issue with ``select_related()`` and model "
"inheritance (:ticket:`21413`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh saincheist mí-ailínithe réimse le ``select_related () ``agus "
"oidhreacht mhúnla (:ticket: `21413`)."

msgid "Fixed join promotion for negated ``AND`` conditions (:ticket:`21748`)."
msgstr ""
"Cur chun cinn ceangail seasta do choinníollacha ``AND`` diúltaithe (:ticket: "
"`21748`)."

msgid ""
"Oracle database introspection now works with boolean and float fields "
"(:ticket:`19884`)."
msgstr ""
"Oibríonn ionbhreithniú bunachar sonraí Oracle anois le réimsí boolean agus "
"snámhphointe (:ticket: `19884`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed an issue where lazy objects weren't actually marked as safe when "
"passed through :func:`~django.utils.safestring.mark_safe` and could end up "
"being double-escaped (:ticket:`21882`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh saincheist nár mharcáladh rudaí leisciúla mar shábháilte i ndáiríre "
"nuair a chuirtear trí:func: `~django.utils.safestring.mark_safe` agus "
"d'fhéadfadh éalú faoi dhó (:ticket: `21882`)."

msgid ""
"Additionally, Django's vendored version of six, ``django.utils.six`` has "
"been upgraded to the latest release (1.5.2)."
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, tá leagan díolta Django de sé, ``django.utils.six "
"``uasghrádaithe go dtí an eisiúint is déanaí (1.5.2)."

msgid "Django 1.6.3 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.6.3"

msgid ""
"Django 1.6.3 fixes several bugs in 1.6.2, including three security issues, "
"and makes one backwards-incompatible change:"
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.6.3 roinnt fabhtanna i 1.6.2, lena n-áirítear trí "
"shaincheist slándála, agus déanann sé athrú amháin atá neamh-chomhoiriúnach "
"ar chúl:"

msgid "``select_for_update()`` requires a transaction"
msgstr "Éilíonn ``select_for_update () ``idirbheart"

msgid ""
"Historically, queries that "
"use :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.select_for_update()` could be "
"executed in autocommit mode, outside of a transaction. Before Django 1.6, "
"Django's automatic transactions mode allowed this to be used to lock records "
"until the next write operation. Django 1.6 introduced database-level "
"autocommit; since then, execution in such a context voids the effect of "
"``select_for_update()``. It is, therefore, assumed now to be an error and "
"raises an exception."
msgstr ""
"Go stairiúil, d'fhéadfaí ceisteanna a úsáideann: meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.select_for_update () `a fhorghníomhú i mód "
"autocommit, lasmuigh d'idirbheart. Roimh Django 1.6, cheadaigh modh "
"idirbhearta uathoibríoch Django é seo a úsáid chun taifid a ghlasáil go dtí "
"an chéad oibríocht scríbhneoireachta eile. Thug Django 1.6 isteach "
"autocommit ar leibhéal bunachar sonraí; ó shin i leith, cuireann forghníomhú "
"i gcomhthéacs den sórt sin éifeacht ``select_for_update () `i bhfolamh. "
"Glactar leis, dá bhrí sin, gur earráid é anois agus ardaíonn sé eisceacht."

msgid ""
"This change was made because such errors can be caused by including an app "
"which expects global transactions (e.g. :setting:`ATOMIC_REQUESTS <DATABASE-"
"ATOMIC_REQUESTS>` set to ``True``), or Django's old autocommit behavior, in "
"a project which runs without them; and further, such errors may manifest as "
"data-corruption bugs."
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh an t-athrú seo <DATABASE-ATOMIC_REQUESTS>toisc gur féidir earráidí "
"den sórt sin a bheith mar thoradh ar aip a bhfuil súil le hidirbhearta "
"domhanda a áireamh (m.sh.: setting: `ATOMIC_REQUESTS `socraithe go `True``), "
"nó sean-iompar uathoibrithe Django, i dtionscadal a ritheann gan iad; agus "
"ina bhreis, féadfaidh earráidí den sórt sin a léiriú mar fhabhtanna éillithe "
"sonraí."

msgid ""
"This change may cause test failures if you use ``select_for_update()`` in a "
"test class which is a subclass of :class:`~django.test.TransactionTestCase` "
"rather than :class:`~django.test.TestCase`."
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh an t-athrú seo a bheith ina chúis le teipeanna tástála má "
"úsáideann tú ``select_for_update () ``i rang tástála atá ina fho-aicme "
"de:class: `~django.test.transactionTestCase` seachas: "
"`~django.test.testcase` seachas: `~django.test.testcase`."

msgid ""
"Content retrieved from the GeoIP library is now properly decoded from its "
"default ``iso-8859-1`` encoding (:ticket:`21996`)."
msgstr ""
"Déantar ábhar a aisghabhadh ón leabharlann GeoIP a dhíchódú i gceart anois "
"óna ionchódú réamhshocraithe ``iso-8859-1` (:ticket: `21996`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``AttributeError`` when "
"using :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.bulk_create` with "
"``ForeignObject`` (:ticket:`21566`)."
msgstr ""
"Seasta ``AttributeError`` nuair a úsáidtear: meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.bulk_create` le ``ForeignObject`` "
"(:ticket: `21566`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed crash of ``QuerySet``\\s that use ``F() + timedelta()`` when their "
"query was compiled more once (:ticket:`21643`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste seasta de ``QuerySet``\\ s a úsáideann ``F () + timedelta () "
"``nuair a cuireadh a gcuid ceist le tiomsú níos mó uair amháin (:ticket: "
"`21643`)."

msgid ""
"Prevented custom ``widget`` class attribute "
"of :class:`~django.forms.IntegerField` subclasses from being overwritten by "
"the code in their ``__init__`` method (:ticket:`22245`)."
msgstr ""
"Cosc ar thréith aicme saincheaptha ``widget`` de:class: "
"`~django.forms.IntegerField` ó fho-aicmí a fhorscríobh leis an gcód ina modh "
"``__init__`` (:ticket: `22245`)."

msgid ""
"Improved :func:`~django.utils.html.strip_tags` accuracy (but it still cannot "
"guarantee an HTML-safe result, as stated in the documentation)."
msgstr ""
"Feabhsaithe:func: `~django.utils.html.strip_tags` cruinneas (ach ní féidir "
"leis toradh sábháilte HTML a ráthú fós, mar a luaitear sa doiciméadú)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression in the :mod:`django.contrib.gis` SQL compiler for non-"
"concrete fields (:ticket:`22250`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú sa tiomsaitheoir SQL: mod: `django.contrib.gis` le "
"haghaidh réimsí neamhchoincréite (:ticket: `22250`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed :attr:`ModelAdmin.preserve_filters "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.preserve_filters>` when running a site with "
"a URL prefix (:ticket:`21795`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraithe:attr: `ModelAdmin.preserve_filters "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.preserve_filters>`agus suíomh á reáchtáil "
"le réimír URL (:ticket: `21795`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash in the ``find_command`` management utility when the ``PATH`` "
"environment variable wasn't set (:ticket:`22256`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste sa bhfóntais bhainistíochta ``find_command ``nuair nár "
"socraíodh an t-athróg comhshaoil ``PATH` (:ticket: `22256`)."

msgid "Fixed :djadmin:`changepassword` on Windows (:ticket:`22364`)."
msgstr "Socraithe: DJADmin: `changepassword` ar Windows (:ticket: `22364`)."

msgid "Avoided shadowing deadlock exceptions on MySQL (:ticket:`22291`)."
msgstr ""
"Seachnaíodh eisceachtaí deacrachta a scáthú ar MySQL (:ticket: `22291`)."

msgid "Wrapped database exceptions in ``_set_autocommit`` (:ticket:`22321`)."
msgstr ""
"Eisceachtaí bunachar sonraí fillte i ``_set_autocommit ``(:ticket: `22321`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed atomicity when closing a database connection or when the database "
"server disconnects (:ticket:`21239` and :ticket:`21202`)"
msgstr ""
"Atomachas seasta nuair a dhúnadh nasc bunachar sonraí nó nuair a "
"dhícheanglaíonn an freastalaí bunachar sonraí (:ticket: `21239` agus:ticéad: "
"`21202`)"

msgid ""
"Fixed regression in ``prefetch_related`` that caused the related objects "
"query to include an unnecessary join (:ticket:`21760`)."
msgstr ""
"Aischéimniú seasta i `prefetch_related`` a d'fhág go n-áireodh ceist na "
"rudaí gaolmhara ceangal neamhriachtanach (:ticket: `21760`)."

msgid ""
"Additionally, Django's vendored version of six, ``django.utils.six`` has "
"been upgraded to the latest release (1.6.1)."
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, tá leagan díolta Django de sé, ``django.utils.six "
"``uasghrádaithe go dtí an eisiúint is déanaí (1.6.1)."

msgid "Django 1.6.4 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.6.4"

msgid "Django 1.6.4 fixes several bugs in 1.6.3."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.6.4 roinnt fabhtanna i 1.6.3."

msgid ""
"Added backwards compatibility support for the :mod:`django.contrib.messages` "
"cookie format of Django 1.4 and earlier to facilitate upgrading to 1.6 from "
"1.4 (:ticket:`22426`)."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh tacaíocht comhoiriúnachta ar ais leis an bhformáid fianáin: mod: "
"`django.contrib.messages` de Django 1.4 agus níos luaithe chun uasghrádú go "
"1.6 a éascú ó 1.4 (:ticket: `22426`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed the ``object_id`` of the ``LogEntry`` that's created after a user "
"password change in the admin (:ticket:`22515`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh an `object_id`` den `Logentry`` a cruthaíodh tar éis athrú "
"pasfhocal úsáideora sa riarachán (:ticket: `22515`)."

msgid "Django 1.6.5 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.6.5"

msgid "Django 1.6.5 fixes two security issues and several bugs in 1.6.4."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.6.5 dhá shaincheist slándála agus roinnt fabhtanna i "
"1.6.4."

msgid ""
"Issue: Caches may incorrectly be allowed to store and serve private data"
msgstr ""
"Saincheist: D'fhéadfaí cead a thabhairt do chaches sonraí príobháideacha a "
"stóráil agus a sheirbh"

msgid "Issue: Malformed redirect URLs from user input not correctly validated"
msgstr ""
"Saincheist: URLanna atreoraithe mífheidhmithe ó ionchur úsáideora nach "
"bhfuil bailíochtú i gceart"

msgid ""
"Made the ``year_lookup_bounds_for_datetime_field`` Oracle backend method "
"Python 3 compatible (:ticket:`22551`)."
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh an modh cúltaca Oracle ``year_lookup_bouns_for_datetime_field`` "
"comhoiriúnach Python 3 (:ticket: `22551`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``pgettext_lazy`` crash when receiving bytestring content on Python 2 "
"(:ticket:`22565`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste seasta ``pgettext_lazy`` nuair a fhaightear ábhar bytestring ar "
"Python 2 (:ticket: `22565`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed the SQL generated when filtering by a negated ``Q`` object that "
"contains a ``F`` object. (:ticket:`22429`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh an SQL a ghintear nuair a dhéantar é a scagadh ag réad ``Q`` "
"diúltaithe ina bhfuil réad ``F ``. (:ticéad: `22429`)."

msgid ""
"Avoided overwriting data fetched by ``select_related()`` in certain cases "
"which could cause minor performance regressions (:ticket:`22508`)."
msgstr ""
"Seachnaíodh sonraí a fhaightear ag ``select_related () ``a fhorscríobh i "
"gcásanna áirithe a d'fhéadfadh mionaiséireachtaí feidhmíochta a bheith ina "
"chúis le haischéimniú feidhmíochta (:ticket: `22508`)."

msgid "Django 1.6.6 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.6.6"

msgid "Django 1.6.6 fixes several security issues and bugs in 1.6.5."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.6.6 roinnt saincheisteanna slándála agus fabhtanna i "
"1.6.5."

msgid ""
"In older versions of Django it was possible to reveal any field's data by "
"modifying the \"popup\" and \"to_field\" parameters of the query string on "
"an admin change form page. For example, requesting a URL like ``/admin/auth/"
"user/?_popup=1&t=password`` and viewing the page's HTML allowed viewing the "
"password hash of each user. While the admin requires users to have "
"permissions to view the change form pages in the first place, this could "
"leak data if you rely on users having access to view only certain fields on "
"a model."
msgstr ""
"I leaganacha níos sine de Django bhíothas in ann sonraí aon réimse a "
"nochtadh trí na paraiméadair \"aníos\" agus \"to_field\" den teaghrán "
"fiosrúcháin a mhodhnú ar leathanach foirm athraithe riaracháin. Mar shampla, "
"ceadaíodh URL mar ``/ admin/auth/user/?_popup=1&t=password`` agus féachaint "
"ar HTML an leathanaigh féachaint ar hash pasfhocail gach úsáideoir. Cé go n-"
"éilíonn an riarthóir cead a bheith ag úsáideoirí féachaint ar leathanaigh na "
"bhfoirm athraithe ar an gcéad dul síos, d'fhéadfadh sé seo sonraí a "
"sceitheadh ​​​​má tá tú ag brath ar rochtain a bheith ag úsáideoirí chun "
"féachaint ar réimsí áirithe ar shamhail amháin."

msgid ""
"Corrected email and URL validation to reject a trailing dash "
"(:ticket:`22579`)."
msgstr ""
"Bailíochtú ríomhphoist agus URL ceartaithe chun diúltú a chur ar shiúl "
"(:ticket: `22579`)."

msgid "Prevented indexes on PostgreSQL virtual fields (:ticket:`22514`)."
msgstr "Innéacsanna coiscthe ar réimsí fíorúla PostgreSQL (:ticket: `22514`)."

msgid ""
"Prevented edge case where values of FK fields could be initialized with a "
"wrong value when an inline model formset is created for a relationship "
"defined to point to a field other than the PK (:ticket:`13794`)."
msgstr ""
"Cás imeall coiscthe ina bhféadfaí luachanna réimsí FK a thionscnamh le luach "
"mícheart nuair a chruthaítear foirmshraith samhail inlíne le haghaidh "
"caidreamh a shainiú chun díriú ar réimse seachas an PK (:ticket: `13794`)."

msgid ""
"Restored ``pre_delete``  signals for ``GenericRelation`` cascade deletion "
"(:ticket:`22998`)."
msgstr ""
"Comharthaí ``pre_delete`` athchóirithe le haghaidh scriosadh cascaire "
"```GenericRelation` (:ticket: `22998`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed transaction handling when specifying non-default database in "
"``createcachetable`` and ``flush`` (:ticket:`23089`)."
msgstr ""
"Láimhseáil idirbheart seasta nuair a shonraítear bunachar sonraí neamh-"
"réamhshocraithe i ``createcachetable`` agus ``flush ``(:ticket: `23089`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed the \"ORA-01843: not a valid month\" errors when using Unicode with "
"older versions of Oracle server (:ticket:`20292`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh na hearráidí “ORA-01843: ní mí bailí” agus Unicode á n-úsáid agat "
"le leaganacha níos sine de fhreastalaí Oracle (:ticket: `20292`)."

msgid ""
"Restored bug fix for sending Unicode email with Python 2.6.5 and below "
"(:ticket:`19107`)."
msgstr ""
"Socrú fabht athchóirithe chun ríomhphost Unicode a sheoladh le Python 2.6.5 "
"agus thíos (:ticket: `19107`)."

msgid ""
"Prevented ``UnicodeDecodeError`` in ``runserver`` with non-UTF-8 and non-"
"English locale (:ticket:`23265`)."
msgstr ""
"Cosc ar ``UnicodeDecodeError`` i ``runserver`` le logale neamh-UTF-8 agus "
"neamh-Bhéarla (:ticket: `23265`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed JavaScript errors while editing multi-geometry objects in the "
"OpenLayers widget (:ticket:`23137`, :ticket:`23293`)."
msgstr ""
"Earráidí JavaScript seasta agus rudaí il-geoiméadrach á n-eagarthóireacht sa "
"ghuirléid OpenLayers (:ticket: `23137`, :ticket: `23293`)."

msgid ""
"Prevented a crash on Python 3 with query strings containing unencoded non-"
"ASCII characters (:ticket:`22996`)."
msgstr ""
"Chuir sé cosc ar thimpiste ar Python 3 le teaghráin fiosrúcháin ina raibh "
"carachtair neamh-ASCII neamh-ionchódaithe (:ticket: `22996`)."

msgid "Django 1.6.7 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.6.7"

msgid ""
"Django 1.6.7 fixes several bugs in 1.6.6, including a regression related to "
"a security fix in that release."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.6.7 roinnt fabhtanna i 1.6.6, lena n-áirítear aischéimniú "
"a bhaineann le socrú slándála sa scaoileadh sin."

msgid ""
"Allowed inherited and m2m fields to be referenced in the admin "
"(:ticket:`23329`)."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaítear do réimsí oidhreachta agus m2m a thagairt sa riarachán (:ticket: "
"`23329`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when using ``QuerySet.defer()`` with ``select_related()`` "
"(:ticket:`23370`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste agus tú ag úsáid ``QuerySet.defer () ``le ``select_related "
"()`` (:ticket: `23370`)."

msgid "Django 1.6.8 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.6.8"

msgid "Django 1.6.8 fixes a couple regressions in the 1.6.6 security release."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.6.8 cúpla aischéimniú sa scaoileadh slándála 1.6.6."

msgid "Django 1.6.9 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.6.9"

msgid "Django 1.6.9 fixes a regression in the 1.6.6 security release."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.6.9 aischéimniú sa scaoileadh slándála 1.6.6."

msgid "Django 1.7 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.7"

msgid "Welcome to Django 1.7!"
msgstr "Fáilte go dtí Django 1.7!"

msgid ""
"These release notes cover the :ref:`new features <whats-new-1.7>`, as well "
"as some :ref:`backwards incompatible changes <backwards-incompatible-1.7>` "
"you'll want to be aware of when upgrading from Django 1.6 or older versions. "
"We've :ref:`begun the deprecation process for some features <deprecated-"
"features-1.7>`, and some features have reached the end of their deprecation "
"process and :ref:`have been removed <removed-features-1.7>`."
msgstr ""
"Clúdaíonn na nótaí scaoilte seo na:ref: `gnéithe nua <whats-new-1.7>`, chomh "
"maith le roinnt athruithe: ref: `athruithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha ar "
"chúl<backwards-incompatible-1.7>` a mbeidh tú ag iarraidh a bheith ar an "
"eolas fúthu agus tú ag uasghrádú ó Django 1.6 nó leaganacha níos sine. "
"<removed-features-1.7>Thosaigh muid: Ref: `an próiseas díghabhála do roinnt "
"<deprecated-features-1.7>gnéithe `, agus tá roinnt gnéithe tar éis deireadh "
"a bpróiseas díscrúdaithe agus:ref: `baineadh`."

msgid ""
"Django 1.7 requires Python 2.7, 3.2, 3.3, or 3.4. We **highly recommend** "
"and only officially support the latest release of each series."
msgstr ""
"Éilíonn Django 1.7 Python 2.7, 3.2, 3.3, nó 3.4. Molaimid** go hard** agus "
"ní thacaímid go hoifigiúil ach leis an scaoileadh is déanaí de gach sraith."

msgid ""
"The Django 1.6 series is the last to support Python 2.6. Django 1.7 is the "
"first release to support Python 3.4."
msgstr ""
"Is é an tsraith Django 1.6 an ceann deireanach a thacaíonn le Python 2.6. Is "
"é Django 1.7 an chéad eisiúint chun tacú le Python 3.4."

msgid ""
"This change should affect only a small number of Django users, as most "
"operating-system vendors today are shipping Python 2.7 or newer as their "
"default version. If you're still using Python 2.6, however, you'll need to "
"stick to Django 1.6 until you can upgrade your Python version. Per :doc:`our "
"support policy </internals/release-process>`, Django 1.6 will continue to "
"receive security support until the release of Django 1.8."
msgstr ""
"Níor cheart go mbíonn tionchar ag an athrú seo ach ar líon beag úsáideoirí "
"Django, mar tá formhór na ndíoltóirí córais oibriúcháin inniu ag seoladh "
"Python 2.7 nó níos nuaí mar a leagan réamhshoc Má tá Python 2.6 á úsáid agat "
"fós, áfach, beidh ort cloí le Django 1.6 go dtí gur féidir leat do leagan "
"Python a uasghrádú. Per:doc: `ár mbeartas tacaíochta ', leanfaidh </"
"internals/release-process> Django 1.6 ag fáil tacaíochta slándála go dtí go "
"scaoilfear Django 1.8."

msgid "What's new in Django 1.7"
msgstr "Cad atá nua i Django 1.7"

msgid "Schema migrations"
msgstr "Imirce scéime"

msgid ""
"Django now has built-in support for schema migrations. It allows models to "
"be updated, changed, and deleted by creating migration files that represent "
"the model changes and which can be run on any development, staging or "
"production database."
msgstr ""
"Tá tacaíocht ionsuite ag Django anois d'imirce scéime. Ligeann sé samhlacha "
"a nuashonrú, a athrú agus a scriosadh trí chomhaid imirce a chruthú a "
"léiríonn na hathruithe samhail agus ar féidir iad a reáchtáil ar aon "
"bhunachar sonraí forbartha, stáitsithe nó táirgeachta."

msgid ""
"Migrations are covered in :doc:`their own documentation</topics/"
"migrations>`, but a few of the key features are:"
msgstr ""
"Tá imirce clúdaithe in:doc: `a gcuid doiciméadaithe féin`, ach is iad seo a "
"leanas cu@@</topics/migrations> id de na príomhghnéithe:"

msgid ""
"``syncdb`` has been deprecated and replaced by ``migrate``. Don't worry - "
"calls to ``syncdb`` will still work as before."
msgstr ""
"Tá `syncdb`` díluaite agus tá ``imirce`` ina ionad. Ná bíodh imní ort - "
"oibreoidh glaonna chuig `syncdb`` fós mar a bhí roimhe seo."

msgid ""
"A new ``makemigrations`` command provides an easy way to autodetect changes "
"to your models and make migrations for them."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn ordú nua ``makemigrations` bealach éasca chun athruithe ar do "
"mhúnlaí a bhrath uathoibríoch agus imirce a dhéanamh dóibh."

msgid ""
"``django.db.models.signals.pre_syncdb`` and "
"``django.db.models.signals.post_syncdb`` have been deprecated, to be "
"replaced by :data:`~django.db.models.signals.pre_migrate` "
"and :data:`~django.db.models.signals.post_migrate` respectively. These new "
"signals have slightly different arguments. Check the documentation for "
"details."
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh ``django.db.models.signals.pre_syncdb`` agus "
"``django.db.models.signals.post_syncdb`` a chur in ionad:: "
"`~django.db.models.signals.pre_migrate` agus:data: "
"`~django.db.models.signals.post_migrate` faoi seach. Tá argóintí beag "
"difriúil ag na comharthaí nua seo. Seiceáil an doiciméadú le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid ""
"The ``allow_syncdb`` method on database routers is now called "
"``allow_migrate``, but still performs the same function. Routers with "
"``allow_syncdb`` methods will still work, but that method name is deprecated "
"and you should change it as soon as possible (nothing more than renaming is "
"required)."
msgstr ""
"Tugtar `allow_migrate`` anois ar an modh `allow_syncdb`` ar ródairí bunachar "
"sonraí, ach comhlíonann sé an fheidhm chéanna fós. Oibreoidh ródairí le "
"modhanna `allow_syncdb`` fós, ach tá an t-ainm modh sin díscoite agus ba "
"chóir duit é a athrú a luaithe is féidir (ní gá aon rud níos mó ná "
"athainmniú)."

msgid ""
"``initial_data`` fixtures are no longer loaded for apps with migrations; if "
"you want to load initial data for an app, we suggest you create a migration "
"for your application and define "
"a :class:`~django.db.migrations.operations.RunPython` "
"or :class:`~django.db.migrations.operations.RunSQL` operation in the "
"``operations`` section of the migration."
msgstr ""
"Ní chuirtear daingneáin `initial_data ``luchtaithe a thuilleadh le haghaidh "
"aipeanna le himirce; más mian leat sonraí tosaigh a luchtú d'aip, molaimid "
"duit imirce a chruthú do d'iarratas agus a: class: "
"`~django.db.migrations.operations.runpython` nó:class: "
"`~django.db.migrations.operations.runsql` a shainiú sa "
"`operations`operations`operations`` “roinn den imirce."

msgid ""
"Test rollback behavior is different for apps with migrations; in particular, "
"Django will no longer emulate rollbacks on non-transactional databases or "
"inside ``TransactionTestCase`` :ref:`unless specifically requested <test-"
"case-serialized-rollback>`."
msgstr ""
"<test-case-serialized-rollback>Tá iompar aistrithe tástála difriúil "
"d'aipeanna le himirce; go háirithe, ní dhéanfaidh Django aithris ar ais a "
"thuilleadh ar bhunachair sonraí neamh-idirbheartaíochta nó taobh istigh de "
"`TransactionTestCase``: ref: `mura n-iarrtar go sonrach `."

msgid ""
"It is not advised to have apps without migrations depend on (have "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey` "
"or :class:`~django.db.models.ManyToManyField` to) apps with migrations."
msgstr ""
"Ní mholtar aipeanna gan imirce a bheith ag brath ar (a: class: "
"`~django.db.models.foreignKey` nó: class: "
"`~django.db.models.manyToManyField` go) aipeanna le himirce."

msgid "App-loading refactor"
msgstr "Athbhreithneoir luchtaithe aip"

msgid ""
"Historically, Django applications were tightly linked to models. A singleton "
"known as the \"app cache\" dealt with both installed applications and "
"models. The models module was used as an identifier for applications in many "
"APIs."
msgstr ""
"Go stairiúil, bhí feidhmchláir Django nasctha go docht le samhlacha. "
"Dhéileáil aonair ar a dtugtar “taisce an aip” le feidhmchláir agus samhlacha "
"suiteáilte araon. Úsáideadh an modúl samhlacha mar aitheantóir d'iarratais i "
"go leor APIs."

msgid ""
"As the concept of :doc:`Django applications </ref/applications>` matured, "
"this code showed some shortcomings. It has been refactored into an \"app "
"registry\" where models modules no longer have a central role and where it's "
"possible to attach configuration data to applications."
msgstr ""
"De réir mar a tháinig coincheap de:doc: `Feidhmchláir Django` aibí, léirigh "
"an cód seo roinnt easna</ref/applications> imh. Athraíodh é i “chlárlann "
"aipeanna” áit nach bhfuil ról lárnach ag modúil samhlacha a thuilleadh agus "
"áit ar féidir sonraí cumraíochta a cheangal le feidhmchláir."

msgid "Improvements thus far include:"
msgstr "I measc feabhsuithe go dtí seo tá:"

msgid ""
"Applications can run code at startup, before Django does anything else, with "
"the :meth:`~django.apps.AppConfig.ready` method of their configuration."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le feidhmchláir cód a reáchtáil ag tosú, sula ndéanann Django aon "
"rud eile, leis an modh: meth: `~django.apps.appconfig.ready` dá gcumraíocht."

msgid ""
"Application labels are assigned correctly to models even when they're "
"defined outside of ``models.py``. You don't have to "
"set :attr:`~django.db.models.Options.app_label` explicitly any more."
msgstr ""
"Sanntar lipéid iarratais i gceart do mhúnlaí fiú nuair a shainmhínítear iad "
"lasmuigh de `models.py`. Ní gá duit: attr: "
"`~django.db.models.options.app_label` a shocrú go sainráite níos mó."

msgid ""
"It is possible to omit ``models.py`` entirely if an application doesn't have "
"any models."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir ``models.py`` a fhágáil go hiomlán mura bhfuil aon mhúnlaí ag "
"feidhmchlár."

msgid ""
"Applications can be relabeled with the :attr:`~django.apps.AppConfig.label` "
"attribute of application configurations, to work around label conflicts."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir iarratais a athlipéadú leis an tréith: attr: "
"`~django.apps.appconfig.label` de chumraíochtaí feidhmchláir, chun oibriú "
"timpeall coimhlintí lipéad."

msgid ""
"The name of applications can be customized in the admin with "
"the :attr:`~django.apps.AppConfig.verbose_name` of application "
"configurations."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir ainm na bhfeidhmchlár a shaincheapadh sa riarachán len:attr: "
"`~django.apps.appconfig.verbose_name` cumraíochtaí feidhmchláir."

msgid ""
"The admin automatically calls :func:`~django.contrib.admin.autodiscover()` "
"when Django starts. You can consequently remove this line from your URLconf."
msgstr ""
"Glaonn an riarachán go huathoibríoch: func: "
"`~django.contrib.admin.autoDiscovery () `nuair a thosaíonn Django. Dá bhrí "
"sin is féidir leat an líne seo a bhaint as do URLConf."

msgid ""
"Django imports all application configurations and models as soon as it "
"starts, through a deterministic and straightforward process. This should "
"make it easier to diagnose import issues such as import loops."
msgstr ""
"Allmhairíonn Django gach cumraíocht agus múnla feidhmchláir a luaithe a "
"thosaíonn sé, trí phróiseas cinntitheach agus simplí. Ba cheart go n-éascódh "
"sé sin saincheisteanna allmhairithe a dhiagnóiseadh mar lúba allmhairithe."

msgid "New method on Field subclasses"
msgstr "Modh nua ar fho-aicmí Allamuigh"

msgid ""
"To help power both schema migrations and to enable easier addition of "
"composite keys in future releases of Django, "
"the :class:`~django.db.models.Field` API now has a new required method: "
"``deconstruct()``."
msgstr ""
"Chun cabhrú le himirce scéime a chumhachtú agus chun eochracha ilchodacha a "
"chur leis níos éasca in eisiúintí Django amach anseo, tá modh nua "
"riachtanach anois ag an API: class: `~Django.db.Models.Field`: ``deconstruct "
"() `."

msgid "This method takes no arguments, and returns a tuple of four items:"
msgstr ""
"Ní ghlacann an modh seo aon argóintí, agus tugann sé tuple de cheithre mhír "
"ar ais:"

msgid ""
"``name``: The field's attribute name on its parent model, or ``None`` if it "
"is not part of a model"
msgstr ""
"``ainm``: Ainm tréith an réimse ar a mhúmhúnla, nó ``None ``mura bhfuil sé "
"mar chuid de mhúnla"

msgid ""
"``path``: A dotted, Python path to the class of this field, including the "
"class name."
msgstr ""
"``path``: Conair poncanach, Python chuig rang an réimse seo, lena n-áirítear "
"ainm an ranga."

msgid "``args``: Positional arguments, as a list"
msgstr "``args``: Argóintí seasaimh, mar liosta"

msgid "``kwargs``: Keyword arguments, as a dict"
msgstr "``kwargs``: Argóintí eochairfhocal, mar ordacht"

msgid ""
"These four values allow any field to be serialized into a file, as well as "
"allowing the field to be copied safely, both essential parts of these new "
"features."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann na ceithre luach seo aon réimse a shraitheadh i gcomhad, chomh maith "
"le ligean an réimse a chóipeáil go sábháilte, an dá chuid riachtanach de na "
"gnéithe nua seo."

msgid ""
"This change should not affect you unless you write custom Field subclasses; "
"if you do, you may need to reimplement the ``deconstruct()`` method if your "
"subclass changes the method signature of ``__init__`` in any way. If your "
"field just inherits from a built-in Django field and doesn't override "
"``__init__``, no changes are necessary."
msgstr ""
"Níor chóir go gcuirfeadh an t-athrú seo difear ort mura scríobhann tú fo-"
"aicmí Réimse saincheaptha; má dhéanann tú, b'fhéidir go mbeidh ort an modh "
"``deconstruct () `a athchur i bhfeidhm má athraíonn do fho-aicme síniú modh "
"``__init__`` ar bhealach ar bith. Mura n-oidhreann do réimse ach ó réimse "
"ionsuite Django agus mura n-athraíonn sé ``__init__``, níl aon athruithe "
"riachtanach."

msgid ""
"If you do need to override ``deconstruct()``, a good place to start is the "
"built-in Django fields (``django/db/models/fields/__init__.py``) as several "
"fields, including ``DecimalField`` and ``DateField``, override it and show "
"how to call the method on the superclass and simply add or remove extra "
"arguments."
msgstr ""
"Más gá duit ``deconstruct () ``a shárú, áit mhaith le tosú ná na réimsí "
"Django ionsuite (``django/db/models/fields/__init__.py``) mar roinnt réimsí, "
"lena n-áirítear ``Decimalfield`` agus `Datefield``, é a shárú agus taispeáin "
"conas an modh a ghlaoch ar an sárrang agus ach breise a chur nó a bhaint "
"argóintí."

msgid ""
"This also means that all arguments to fields must themselves be "
"serializable; to see what we consider serializable, and to find out how to "
"make your own classes serializable, read the :ref:`migration serialization "
"documentation <migration-serializing>`."
msgstr ""
"<migration-serializing>Ciallaíonn sé seo freisin go gcaithfidh gach argóint "
"a bhaineann le réimsí a bheith inshraitheach; chun a fheiceáil cad a "
"mheasaimid inseriálaithe, agus chun a fháil amach conas do ranganna féin a "
"dhéanamh inshraitheach, léigh an:ref: `doiciméadú sraitheoireachta imirce `."

msgid "Calling custom ``QuerySet`` methods from the ``Manager``"
msgstr "Ag glaoch ar mhodhanna saincheaptha ``QuerySet ``ón `Bainiste``"

msgid ""
"Historically, the recommended way to make reusable model queries was to "
"create methods on a custom ``Manager`` class. The problem with this approach "
"was that after the first method call, you'd get back a ``QuerySet`` instance "
"and couldn't call additional custom manager methods."
msgstr ""
"Go stairiúil, ba é an bealach a mholtar chun ceisteanna samhail in-"
"athúsáidte a dhéanamh ná modhanna a chruthú ar rang saincheaptha "
"``Bainiste``. Ba í an fhadhb leis an gcur chuige seo ná go bhfaighfeá sampla "
"`QuerySet` ar ais tar éis an chéad ghlao modh agus nach bhféadfá modhanna "
"bainisteora saincheaptha breise a ghlaoch."

msgid ""
"Though not documented, it was common to work around this issue by creating a "
"custom ``QuerySet`` so that custom methods could be chained; but the "
"solution had a number of drawbacks:"
msgstr ""
"Cé nach raibh sé doiciméadaithe, bhí sé coitianta oibriú timpeall ar an "
"gceist seo trí “QuerySet” saincheaptha a chruthú ionas go bhféadfaí modhanna "
"saincheaptha a shlánú; ach bhí roinnt míbhuntáistí ag an réiteach:"

msgid ""
"The custom ``QuerySet`` and its custom methods were lost after the first "
"call to ``values()`` or ``values_list()``."
msgstr ""
"Cailleadh an saincheaptha ``QuerySet` agus a mhodhanna saincheaptha tar éis "
"an chéad ghlao chuig ``values () ``nó `values_list ()``."

msgid ""
"Writing a custom ``Manager`` was still necessary to return the custom "
"``QuerySet`` class and all methods that were desired on the ``Manager`` had "
"to be proxied to the ``QuerySet``. The whole process went against the DRY "
"principle."
msgstr ""
"Bhí gá fós ag scríobh saincheaptha ``Bainiste`` chun an rang saincheaptha "
"``QuerySet`` a thabhairt ar ais agus b'éigean gach modh a bhí ag teastáil ar "
"an ``Bainiste`` a sheoladh chuig an `QuerySet``. Chuaigh an próiseas iomlán "
"i gcoinne prionsabal DRY."

msgid ""
"The :meth:`QuerySet.as_manager() "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.as_manager>` class method can now "
"directly :ref:`create Manager with QuerySet methods <create-manager-with-"
"queryset-methods>`::"
msgstr ""
"<create-manager-with-queryset-methods>Is féidir leis an modh ranga:Meth: "
"`QuerySet.as_Manager () <django.db.models.query.QuerySet.as_manager>`anois "
"go díreach anois:ref: `Bainisteoir a chruthú le modhanna QuerySet`:"

msgid "Using a custom manager when traversing reverse relations"
msgstr "Bainisteoir saincheaptha a úsáid agus caidreamh droim ar ais"

msgid ""
"It is now possible to :ref:`specify a custom manager <using-custom-reverse-"
"manager>` when traversing a reverse relationship::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir anois:ref: `bainisteoir saincheaptha a shonrú <using-custom-"
"reverse-manager>`agus caidreamh droim ar ais::"

msgid "New system check framework"
msgstr "Creat seiceála córais nua"

msgid ""
"We've added a new :doc:`System check framework </ref/checks>` for detecting "
"common problems (like invalid models) and providing hints for resolving "
"those problems. The framework is extensible so you can add your own checks "
"for your own apps and libraries."
msgstr ""
"Chuireamar nua:doc: `Creat seiceála córas` chun fadhbanna coitianta a bhrath "
"(cosú</ref/checks> il le samhlacha neamhbhailí) agus leideanna a sholáthar "
"chun na fadhbanna sin a réiteach. Tá an creat inleathnaithe ionas gur féidir "
"leat do sheiceálacha féin a chur le haghaidh d'aipeanna agus leabharlanna "
"féin."

msgid ""
"To perform system checks, you use the :djadmin:`check` management command. "
"This command replaces the older ``validate`` management command."
msgstr ""
"Chun seiceálacha córais a dhéanamh, úsáideann tú an t-ordú bainistíochta: "
"djadmin: `check`. Cuireann an t-ordú seo in ionad an t-ordú bainistíochta "
"`bailíochta` níos sine."

msgid "New ``Prefetch`` object for advanced ``prefetch_related`` operations."
msgstr "Réad nua ``Prefetch`` le haghaidh ardoibríochtaí ``prefetch_related``."

msgid ""
"The new :class:`~django.db.models.Prefetch` object allows customizing "
"prefetch operations."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn an réad nua:class: `~django.db.models.prefetch` oibríochtaí "
"réamhfhillte a shaincheapadh."

msgid ""
"You can specify the ``QuerySet`` used to traverse a given relation or "
"customize the storage location of prefetch results."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an “QuerySet” a shonrú a úsáidtear chun caidreamh ar leith a "
"thrasú nó suíomh stórála na dtorthaí réamhfhaighte a shaincheapadh."

msgid ""
"This enables things like filtering prefetched relations, "
"calling :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.select_related()` from a "
"prefetched relation, or prefetching the same relation multiple times with "
"different querysets. "
"See :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.prefetch_related()` for more "
"details."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann sé seo ar chumas rudaí cosúil le caidrimh réamhfhaighte a scagadh, "
"glaoch ar: meth: `~django.db.models.query.queryset.select_related () `ó "
"ghaol réamhfhaighte, nó an gaol céanna a réamhghabháil arís agus arís eile "
"le ceisteanna éagsúla. Féach: Meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.prefetch_related () `le haghaidh tuilleadh "
"sonraí."

msgid "Admin shortcuts support time zones"
msgstr "Tacaíonn aicearraí riaracháin le criosanna ama"

msgid ""
"The \"today\" and \"now\" shortcuts next to date and time input widgets in "
"the admin are now operating in the :ref:`current time zone <default-current-"
"time-zone>`. Previously, they used the browser time zone, which could result "
"in saving the wrong value when it didn't match the current time zone on the "
"server."
msgstr ""
"<default-current-time-zone>Tá na aicearraí “inniu” agus “anois” in aice le "
"giuirléidí ionchuir dáta agus ama sa riarachán ag feidhmiú anois in:ref: "
"`crios ama reatha `. Roimhe seo, d'úsáid siad crios ama an bhrabhsálaí, rud "
"a d'fhéadfadh an luach mícheart a shábháil nuair nach raibh sé ag teacht "
"leis an gcrios ama reatha ar an bhfreastalaí."

msgid ""
"In addition, the widgets now display a help message when the browser and "
"server time zone are different, to clarify how the value inserted in the "
"field will be interpreted."
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, taispeánann na giuirléidí teachtaireacht cabhrach anois "
"nuair a bhíonn crios ama an bhrabhsálaí agus an fhreastalaí difriúil, chun a "
"shoiléiriú conas a léirmhíneofar an luach a cuireadh isteach sa réimse."

msgid "Using database cursors as context managers"
msgstr "Ag baint úsáide as cursóirí bunachar sonraí mar bhainiste"

msgid ""
"Prior to Python 2.7, database cursors could be used as a context manager. "
"The specific backend's cursor defined the behavior of the context manager. "
"The behavior of magic method lookups was changed with Python 2.7 and cursors "
"were no longer usable as context managers."
msgstr ""
"Roimh Python 2.7, d'fhéadfaí cúrsóirí bunachar sonraí a úsáid mar "
"bhainisteoir comhthéacs. Sainmhínigh cúrsóir an chúltaca sonrach iompar an "
"bhainisteora comhthéacs. Athraíodh iompar cuardaigh modh draíochta le Python "
"2.7 agus ní raibh cúrsóirí inúsáidte a thuilleadh mar bhainisteoirí "
"comhthéacs."

msgid ""
"Django 1.7 allows a cursor to be used as a context manager. That is, the "
"following can be used::"
msgstr ""
"Ligeann Django 1.7 cúrsóir a úsáid mar bhainisteoir comhthéacs. Is é sin, is "
"féidir an méid seo a leanas a úsáid:"

msgid "instead of::"
msgstr "in ionad:"

msgid "Custom lookups"
msgstr "Cuardaigh saincheaptha"

msgid ""
"It is now possible to write custom lookups and transforms for the ORM. "
"Custom lookups work just like Django's built-in lookups (e.g. ``lte``, "
"``icontains``) while transforms are a new concept."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir anois cuardaigh agus claochruithe saincheaptha a scríobh don ORM. "
"Oibríonn cuardaigh saincheaptha díreach cosúil le cuardaigh ionsuite Django "
"(m.sh. ``lte``, `icontains`) agus is coincheap nua iad claochluithe."

msgid ""
"The :class:`django.db.models.Lookup` class provides a way to add lookup "
"operators for model fields. As an example it is possible to add ``day_lte`` "
"operator for ``DateFields``."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn an rang:class: `Django.db.Models.lookup` bealach chun oibreoirí "
"cuardaigh a chur le haghaidh réimsí samhail. Mar shampla is féidir oibreoir "
"``day_lte`` a chur le haghaidh ``Datefields``."

msgid ""
"The :class:`django.db.models.Transform` class allows transformations of "
"database values prior to the final lookup. For example it is possible to "
"write a ``year`` transform that extracts year from the field's value. "
"Transforms allow for chaining. After the ``year`` transform has been added "
"to ``DateField`` it is possible to filter on the transformed value, for "
"example ``qs.filter(author__birthdate__year__lte=1981)``."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn an rang:class: `Django.DB.Models.Transform` claochlú luachanna "
"bunachar sonraí roimh an gcuardach deiridh. Mar shampla, is féidir claochlú "
"``bliain ``a scríobh a bhaineann bliain ó luach an réimse. Ceadaíonn "
"claochruithe slabhraithe. Tar éis an claochlú ``bliain ``a chur le "
"``Datefield`` is féidir scagadh a dhéanamh ar an luach claochlaithe, mar "
"shampla ``qs.filter (author__birthdate__year__lte=1981)``."

msgid ""
"For more information about both custom lookups and transforms refer to "
"the :doc:`custom lookups </howto/custom-lookups>` documentation."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise faoi chuardach saincheaptha agus "
"claochruithe araon féach ar an doiciméad:doc: `custom lookups` </howto/"
"custom-lookups>."

msgid "Improvements to ``Form`` error handling"
msgstr "Feabhsuithe ar láimhseáil earráide ``Foirme``"

msgid "``Form.add_error()``"
msgstr "``Form.add_Error () ``"

msgid "Previously there were two main patterns for handling errors in forms:"
msgstr ""
"Roimhe seo bhí dhá phríomhphatrún ann chun earráidí i bhfoirmeacha a "
"láimhseáil:"

msgid ""
"Raising a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` from within certain "
"functions (e.g. ``Field.clean()``, ``Form.clean_<fieldname>()``, or "
"``Form.clean()`` for non-field errors.)"
msgstr ""
"<fieldname>Ag ardú a:exc: `~django.core.exceptions.validationError` ó "
"laistigh de fheidhmeanna áirithe (m.sh. `Field.clean () ``, `Form.clean_ "
"()``, nó ``Form.clean () ``le haghaidh earráidí neamh-réimse.)"

msgid ""
"Fiddling with ``Form._errors`` when targeting a specific field in "
"``Form.clean()`` or adding errors from outside of a \"clean\" method (e.g. "
"directly from a view)."
msgstr ""
"Ag glacadh le ``Foirm. _earráidí ``agus tú ag díriú ar réimse ar leith i "
"`Form.clean ()`` nó earráidí a chur leis ó lasmuigh de mhodh “glan” (m.sh. "
"go díreach ó radharc)."

msgid ""
"Using the former pattern was straightforward since the form can guess from "
"the context (i.e. which method raised the exception) where the errors belong "
"and automatically process them. This remains the canonical way of adding "
"errors when possible. However the latter was fiddly and error-prone, since "
"the burden of handling edge cases fell on the user."
msgstr ""
"Bhí sé simplí an chéad phatrún a úsáid ós rud é gur féidir leis an bhfoirm a "
"thuairim ón gcomhthéacs (ie cén modh a d'ardaigh an eisceacht) cá mbaineann "
"na hearráidí agus iad a phróiseáil Is é seo an bealach canónach chun "
"earráidí a chur leis nuair is féidir. Mar sin féin, bhí an dara ceann "
"díreach agus seans ó earráidí, ós rud é gur thit an t-ualach a bhaineann le "
"cásanna imeall a láimhseáil ar an úsáideoir."

msgid ""
"The new :meth:`~django.forms.Form.add_error()` method allows adding errors "
"to specific form fields from anywhere without having to worry about the "
"details such as creating instances of ``django.forms.utils.ErrorList`` or "
"dealing with ``Form.cleaned_data``. This new API replaces manipulating "
"``Form._errors`` which now becomes a private API."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an modh nua:meth: `~django.forms.form.add_error () `earráidí a chur "
"le réimsí foirme ar leith ó áit ar bith gan a bheith buartha faoi na sonraí "
"mar shampla cásanna de `Django.Forms.utils.errorList`` a chruthú nó déileáil "
"le ``Form.Cleaned_Data``. Cuireann an API nua seo in ionad ionramháil "
"``Foirm. _earráidí ``atá anois ina API príobháideach."

msgid ""
"See :ref:`validating-fields-with-clean` for an example using "
"``Form.add_error()``."
msgstr ""
"Féach:ref: `validating-fields-with-clean` mar shampla ag baint úsáide as "
"``form.add_error () ``."

msgid "Error metadata"
msgstr "Meiteashonraí earrá"

msgid ""
"The :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` constructor accepts "
"metadata such as error ``code`` or ``params`` which are then available for "
"interpolating into the error message (see :ref:`raising-validation-error` "
"for more details); however, before Django 1.7 those metadata were discarded "
"as soon as the errors were added to :attr:`Form.errors "
"<django.forms.Form.errors>`."
msgstr ""
"<django.forms.Form.errors>Glacann an tógálaí:EXC: "
"`~Django.Core.Exceptions.ValidationError` le meiteashonraí mar earráid "
"``code`` nó `params`` atá ar fáil ansin le hidirphóireacht isteach sa "
"teachtaireacht earráide (féach: `raising-validation-error` le haghaidh "
"tuilleadh sonraí); áfach, roimh Django 1.7 cuireadh na meiteashonraí sin a "
"luaithe a cuireadh na hearráidí la:attr: `Form.Earráidí `."

msgid ""
":attr:`Form.errors <django.forms.Form.errors>` and "
"``django.forms.utils.ErrorList`` now store the ``ValidationError`` instances "
"so these metadata can be retrieved at any time through the "
"new :meth:`Form.errors.as_data <django.forms.Form.errors.as_data()>` method."
msgstr ""
"<django.forms.Form.errors.as_data () >:attr: `Form.error` agus "
"``<django.forms.Form.errors>Django.Forms.Utils.ErrorList`` a stóráil anois "
"na cásanna ``ValidationError`` ionas gur féidir na meiteashonraí seo a "
"aisghabháil ag am ar bith tríd an modh nua:meth: `Form.errors.as_data`."

msgid ""
"The retrieved ``ValidationError`` instances can then be identified thanks to "
"their error ``code`` which enables things like rewriting the error's message "
"or writing custom logic in a view when a given error is present. It can also "
"be used to serialize the errors in a custom format such as XML."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir na cásanna ``ValidationError`` a aisghabháil ansin a aithint a "
"bhuíochas dá n-earráid ```cód ``a chuireann ar chumas rudaí cosúil le "
"teachtaireacht an earráide a athscríobh nó loighic saincheaptha a scríobh i "
"radharc nuair a bhíonn earráid ar leith i láthair. Is féidir é a úsáid "
"freisin chun na hearráidí a shraitheadh i bhformáid saincheaptha mar XML."

msgid ""
"The new :meth:`Form.errors.as_json() <django.forms.Form.errors.as_json()>` "
"method is a convenience method which returns error messages along with error "
"codes serialized as JSON. ``as_json()`` uses ``as_data()`` and gives an idea "
"of how the new system could be extended."
msgstr ""
"Is modh áisiúlachta é an modh nua:meth: `Form.errors.as_json () a thugann "
"teachtaireachtaí earráide ar ais mar aon le "
"<django.forms.Form.errors.as_json () > cóid earráide a shraitheann mar JSON. "
"Úsáideann ``as_json () ```as_data ()`` agus tugann sé tuairim faoin gcaoi a "
"bhféadfaí an córas nua a leathnú."

msgid "Error containers and backward compatibility"
msgstr "Coimeádáin earráide agus comhoiriú"

msgid ""
"Heavy changes to the various error containers were necessary in order to "
"support the features above, specifically :attr:`Form.errors "
"<django.forms.Form.errors>`, ``django.forms.utils.ErrorList``, and the "
"internal storages of :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError`. These "
"containers which used to store error strings now store ``ValidationError`` "
"instances and public APIs have been adapted to make this as transparent as "
"possible, but if you've been using private APIs, some of the changes are "
"backwards incompatible; see :ref:`validation-error-constructor-and-internal-"
"storage` for more details."
msgstr ""
"Bhí gá le hathruithe troma ar na coimeádáin earráide éagsúla chun tacú leis "
"na gnéithe thuas, go sonraí:attr: `Form.Errors `, "
"`Django.Forms.Utils.ErrorList``, agus na stórálaí inmheánacha de:exc: "
"`~Django.Core.Exceptions.Vali <django.forms.Form.errors>dationError`. "
"Stórálann na coimeádáin seo a d'úsáid teaghráin earráide cásanna "
"`ValidationError` anois agus tá APIs poiblí oiriúnaithe chun é seo a "
"dhéanamh chomh trédhearcach agus is féidir, ach má bhí APIs príobháideacha á "
"úsáid agat, tá cuid de na hathruithe ag teacht ar ais; féach:ref: "
"`validation-error-constructor-and-internal-storage` le haghaidh tuilleadh "
"sonraí."

msgid ""
"You can now "
"implement :attr:`~django.contrib.admin.AdminSite.site_header`, :attr:`~django.contrib.admin.AdminSite.site_title`, "
"and :attr:`~django.contrib.admin.AdminSite.index_title` attributes on a "
"custom :class:`~django.contrib.admin.AdminSite` in order to easily change "
"the admin site's page title and header text. No more needing to override "
"templates!"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat a chur i bhfeidhm anois:attr: "
"`~django.contrib.admin.admin.adminsite.header`, :attr: "
"`~django.contrib.admin.admin.admin.title`, agus: attr: "
"`~django.contrib.admin.admin.adminsite.index_title` tréithe "
"saincheapa:class: `~django.contrib.admin.site` in ord chun teideal "
"leathanaigh agus téacs ceanntásc an láithreáin riaracháin a athrú go héasca. "
"Níl gá níos mó teimpléid a shárú!"

msgid ""
"Buttons in :mod:`django.contrib.admin` now use the ``border-radius`` CSS "
"property for rounded corners rather than GIF background images."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann cnaipí in:mod: `django.contrib.admin` an maoin CSS `border-"
"radius`` anois le haghaidh coirnéil cruinn seachas íomhánna cúlra GIF."

msgid ""
"Some admin templates now have ``app-<app_name>`` and ``model-<model_name>`` "
"classes in their ``<body>`` tag to allow customizing the CSS per app or per "
"model."
msgstr ""
"Tá ranganna ``app- ``agus`` <app_name>model- ``ag roinnt teimpléid "
"riaracháin ina gclib`` `<model_name>` ``chun an CSS a shaincheapadh in "
"aghaidh an aip nó in aghaidh an t <body>samhail a cheadú."

msgid ""
"The admin changelist cells now have a ``field-<field_name>`` class in the "
"HTML to enable style customizations."
msgstr ""
"Tá rang ``field-<field_name>`` sa HTML anois ag na cealla athraithe "
"riaracháin chun saincheaptha stíl a chumasú."

msgid ""
"The admin's search fields can now be customized per-request thanks to the "
"new :meth:`django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.get_search_fields` method."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir réimsí cuardaigh an riaracháin a shaincheapadh anois in aghaidh "
"iarratais a bhuíochas leis an modh nua: meth: "
"`django.contrib.admin.modeladmin.get_search_fields`."

msgid ""
"The :meth:`ModelAdmin.get_fields() "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.get_fields>` method may be overridden to "
"customize the value of :attr:`ModelAdmin.fields "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.fields>`."
msgstr ""
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.fields>Féadfar an modh: Meth: "
"`ModelAdmin.get_fields () <django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.get_fields>`a "
"athshealbhú chun luach: attr: `ModelAdmin.fields` a shaincheapadh."

msgid ""
"In addition to the existing ``admin.site.register`` syntax, you can use the "
"new :func:`~django.contrib.admin.register` decorator to register "
"a :class:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin`."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith leis an gcomhréir `admin.site.register`` atá ann cheana, is "
"féidir leat an maisitheoir nua:func: `~django.contrib.admin.register` a "
"úsáid chun a:class: `~django.contrib.admin.modelAdmin` a chlárú."

msgid ""
"You may specify :meth:`ModelAdmin.list_display_links "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.list_display_links>` ``= None`` to disable "
"links on the change list page grid."
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh tú a shonró:meth: `ModelAdmin.list_display_links ``= None` "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.list_display_links>`chun naisc ar an "
"eangach leathanaigh liosta athraithe a dhíchumasú."

msgid ""
"You may now specify :attr:`ModelAdmin.view_on_site "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.view_on_site>` to control whether or not to "
"display the \"View on site\" link."
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh tú anois: attr: `ModelAdmin.view_on_site "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.view_on_site>`a shonrú chun rialú a "
"dhéanamh ar an nasc “Amharc ar an láithreán” a thaispeáint nó nach bhfuil."

msgid ""
"You can specify a descending ordering for a :attr:`ModelAdmin.list_display "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.list_display>` value by prefixing the "
"``admin_order_field`` value with a hyphen."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat ordú íslitheach a shonrú do luach a: attr: "
"`ModelAdmin.list_display <django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.list_display>`tríd "
"an luach `admin_order_field` a réamhshocrú le hiphen."

msgid ""
"The :meth:`ModelAdmin.get_changeform_initial_data() "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.get_changeform_initial_data>` method may be "
"overridden to define custom behavior for setting initial change form data."
msgstr ""
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.get_changeform_initial_data>Féadfar an "
"modh: Meth: `ModelAdmin.get_ChangeForm_Initial_Data () `a athshealbhú chun "
"iompar saincheaptha a shainiú chun sonraí foirme athraithe tosaigh a shocrú."

msgid ""
"Any ``**kwargs`` passed "
"to :meth:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User.email_user()` are passed to the "
"underlying :func:`~django.core.mail.send_mail` call."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The :func:`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.permission_required` decorator "
"can take a list of permissions as well as a single permission."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leis an maisitheoir: Func: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.permission_required` liosta ceadanna a "
"ghlacadh chomh maith le cead amháin."

msgid ""
"You can override the new :meth:`AuthenticationForm.confirm_login_allowed() "
"<django.contrib.auth.forms.AuthenticationForm.confirm_login_allowed>` method "
"to more easily customize the login policy."
msgstr ""
"<django.contrib.auth.forms.AuthenticationForm.confirm_login_allowed>Is "
"féidir leat an modh nua:meth: `AuthenticationForm.confirm_login_allow () `a "
"shárú chun an beartas logála isteach a shaincheapadh níos éasca."

msgid ""
"``django.contrib.auth.views.password_reset()`` takes an optional "
"``html_email_template_name`` parameter used to send a multipart HTML email "
"for password resets."
msgstr ""
"Glacann ``django.contrib.auth.views.password_reset () ``paraiméadar roghnach "
"``html_email_template_name`` a úsáidtear chun ríomhphost HTML ilpháirteach a "
"sheoladh le haghaidh athshocraithe pasfhocal."

msgid ""
"The :meth:`AbstractBaseUser.get_session_auth_hash() "
"<django.contrib.auth.models.AbstractBaseUser.get_session_auth_hash>` method "
"was added and if your :setting:`AUTH_USER_MODEL` inherits "
"from :class:`~django.contrib.auth.models.AbstractBaseUser`, changing a "
"user's password now invalidates old sessions if the "
"``django.contrib.auth.middleware.SessionAuthenticationMiddleware`` is "
"enabled. See :ref:`session-invalidation-on-password-change` for more details."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an modh: Meth: `AbstractBaseUser.get_session_auth_hash () "
"<django.contrib.auth.models.AbstractBaseUser.get_session_auth_hash>`leis "
"agus má tá do: setting: `AUTH_USER_MODEL` oidhreacht ó:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.abstractBaseUser`, athraíonn pasfhocal "
"úsáideora anois sean-seisiúin má tá an "
"`Django.Contrib.Authentic.leware.session.session.Tá “MiddleWare” cumasaithe. "
"Féach: Ref: `seision-invalidation-on-pasfho-athraithe' le haghaidh tuilleadh "
"sonraí."

msgid "``django.contrib.formtools``"
msgstr "``django.contrib.formtools``"

msgid ""
"Calls to ``WizardView.done()`` now include a ``form_dict`` to allow easier "
"access to forms by their step name."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn glaonna chuig `WizardView.done () ``anois ``form_dict`` chun "
"rochtain níos éasca a cheadú ar fhoirmeacha de réir a n-ainm céim."

msgid ""
"The default OpenLayers library version included in widgets has been updated "
"from 2.11 to 2.13."
msgstr ""
"Nuashonraíodh an leagan réamhshocraithe leabharlainne OpenLayers atá san "
"áireamh i giuirléidí ó 2.11 go 2.13."

msgid ""
"Prepared geometries now also support the ``crosses``, ``disjoint``, "
"``overlaps``, ``touches`` and ``within`` predicates, if GEOS 3.3 or later is "
"installed."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn geoiméadraí ullmhaithe anois leis na réamhtheacháin ``crosses`, "
"`disjunt``, `overlaps``, `touches`` agus ``laistigh de ``, má tá GEOS 3.3 nó "
"níos déanaí suiteáilte."

msgid ":mod:`django.contrib.messages`"
msgstr ":mod: `django.contrib.teachtaireachtaí `"

msgid ""
"The backends for :mod:`django.contrib.messages` that use cookies, will now "
"follow the :setting:`SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE` "
"and :setting:`SESSION_COOKIE_HTTPONLY` settings."
msgstr ""
"Leanfaidh na cúltaca le haghaidh: mod: `django.contrib.messages` a úsáideann "
"fianáin, anois socruithe: :setting: `SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE` agus:setting: "
"`SESSION_COOKIE_HTTPONLY`."

msgid ""
"The :ref:`messages context processor <message-displaying>` now adds a "
"dictionary of default levels under the name ``DEFAULT_MESSAGE_LEVELS``."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann an:ref: próiseálaí comhthéacs `teachtaireachtaí <message-"
"displaying>`foclóir leibhéil réamhshocraithe anois faoin ainm "
"``DEFAULT_MESSAGE_LEVELS``."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.contrib.messages.Message` objects now have a ``level_tag`` "
"attribute that contains the string representation of the message level."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.contrib.messages.message` tréith ``level_tag`` anois ag "
"rudaí ina bhfuil léiriú teaghrán leibhéal na teachtaireachta."

msgid ":mod:`django.contrib.redirects`"
msgstr ":mod: `django.contrib.redirects`"

msgid ""
":class:`~django.contrib.redirects.middleware.RedirectFallbackMiddleware` has "
"two new attributes "
"(:attr:`~django.contrib.redirects.middleware.RedirectFallbackMiddleware.response_gone_class` "
"and :attr:`~django.contrib.redirects.middleware.RedirectFallbackMiddleware.response_redirect_class`) "
"that specify the types of :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse` instances the "
"middleware returns."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.contrib.redirects.middleware.redirectFallbackMiddleware` tá "
"dhá thréith nua ag `(:attr: "
"`~django.contrib.redirects.middleware.redirectFallbackmiddleware.response_gone_class` "
"agus:attr: "
"`~django.contrib.redirectmiddleware.redirectmiddleware.redirectfallbackmiddleware.Ware.Response_Redirect_Class`) "
"a shonraíonn na cineálacha de:class: `~django.http.httpResponse` cásanna a "
"fhilleann an middleware."

msgid ""
"The ``\"django.contrib.sessions.backends.cached_db\"`` session backend now "
"respects :setting:`SESSION_CACHE_ALIAS`. In previous versions, it always "
"used the ``default`` cache."
msgstr ""
"Tá cúltaca seisiúin ``\"django.contrib.sessions.backends.cached_db\"`` meas "
"anois:setting: `SESSION_CACHE_ALIAS`. I leaganacha roimhe seo, d'úsáid sé an "
"taisce ``default` i gcónaí."

msgid ":mod:`django.contrib.sitemaps`"
msgstr ":mod: `django.contrib.sitemaps`"

msgid ""
"The :mod:`sitemap framework<django.contrib.sitemaps>` now makes use "
"of :attr:`~django.contrib.sitemaps.Sitemap.lastmod` to set a ``Last-"
"Modified`` header in the response. This makes it possible for "
"the :class:`~django.middleware.http.ConditionalGetMiddleware` to handle "
"conditional ``GET`` requests for sitemaps which set ``lastmod``."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann an creat:MOD: `mapa láithreáin <django.contrib.sitemaps>`anois "
"ó:attr: `~django.contrib.siteMaps.SiteMap.LastMod` chun ceannteideal ```Last-"
"Modified` a shocrú sa fhreagra. De bharr seo is féidir leis na:class: "
"`~django.middleware.http.ConditionalGetMiddleware` iarratais choinníollacha "
"``GET`` a láimhseáil ar léarscáileanna láithreáin a shocraíonn ``lastmod``."

msgid ""
"The new :class:`django.contrib.sites.middleware.CurrentSiteMiddleware` "
"allows setting the current site on each request."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn an nua:class: "
"`django.contrib.sites.middleware.currentsiteMiddleware` an suíomh reatha a "
"shocrú ar gach iarratas."

msgid ""
"The :ref:`static files storage classes <staticfiles-storages>` may be "
"subclassed to override the permissions that collected static files and "
"directories receive by setting "
"the :attr:`~django.core.files.storage.FileSystemStorage.file_permissions_mode` "
"and :attr:`~django.core.files.storage.FileSystemStorage.directory_permissions_mode` "
"parameters. See :djadmin:`collectstatic` for example usage."
msgstr ""
"Féad <staticfiles-storages>far ranganna stórála comhaid statacha: Ref: a fho-"
"aicmiú chun na ceadanna a bhailíodh comhaid statacha agus eolairí a "
"fhaigheann a shárú trí:attr: "
"`~django.core.files.storage.filesystemstorage.fileSystemStorage.file_permissions_mode` "
"agus:attr: `~django.core.files.storage.directory_permissions_mode` "
"paraiméadair. Féach: DjaDmin: `collectstatic` mar shampla úsáid."

msgid ""
"The ``CachedStaticFilesStorage`` backend gets a sibling class "
"called :class:`~django.contrib.staticfiles.storage.ManifestStaticFilesStorage` "
"that doesn't use the cache system at all but instead a JSON file called "
"``staticfiles.json`` for storing the mapping between the original file name "
"(e.g. ``css/styles.css``) and the hashed file name (e.g. ``css/"
"styles.55e7cbb9ba48.css``). The ``staticfiles.json`` file is created when "
"running the :djadmin:`collectstatic` management command and should be a less "
"expensive alternative for remote storages such as Amazon S3."
msgstr ""
"Faigheann an cúltaca ``CachedStaticFilesStorage`` rang deartháireacha ar a "
"dtugtar: `~django.contrib.staticfiles.storage.manifestStaticFilesStorage` "
"nach n-úsáideann an córas taisce ar chor ar bith ach ina ionad sin comhad "
"JSON ar a dtugtar ``staticfiles.json`` chun an mapáil a stóráil idir ainm an "
"chomhaid bunaidh (m.sh. `css/styles.c` ss``) agus ainm an chomhaid hashed "
"(m.sh. ``css/styles.55e7cbb9ba48.css``). Cruthaítear an comhad "
"``staticfiles.json`` agus an t-ordú bainistíochta: djadmin: `collectstatic` "
"á reáchtáil agus ba chóir go mbeadh sé ina rogha eile níos saoire do "
"stórálaí iargúlta mar Amazon S3."

msgid ""
"See "
"the :class:`~django.contrib.staticfiles.storage.ManifestStaticFilesStorage` "
"docs for more information."
msgstr ""
"Féach na docs:class: "
"`~django.contrib.staticFiles.Storage.ManifestStaticFilesStorage` docs le "
"haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise."

msgid ""
":djadmin:`findstatic` now accepts verbosity flag level 2, meaning it will "
"show the relative paths of the directories it searched. "
"See :djadmin:`findstatic` for example output."
msgstr ""
": djadmin: Glacann `findstatic` anois le leibhéal bratach verbosity 2, rud a "
"chiallaíonn go dtaispeánfaidh sé cosáin choibhneasta na n-eolairí a "
"chuardaigh sé. Féach: djaDmin: `findstatic` mar aschur mar shampla."

msgid ":mod:`django.contrib.syndication`"
msgstr ":mod: `django.contrib.syndication`"

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.utils.feedgenerator.Atom1Feed` syndication feed's "
"``updated`` element now utilizes ``updateddate`` instead of ``pubdate``, "
"allowing the ``published`` element to be included in the feed (which relies "
"on ``pubdate``)."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann eilimint ``updated`` fotha sindiciúcháin an:class: "
"`~django.utils.feedgenerator.atom1feed` anois ``updateddate`` in ionad "
"``pubdate``, ag ligean an eilimint ``foilsithe ``a chur san áireamh sa "
"bheatha (atá ag brath ar ``pubdate``)."

msgid ""
"Access to caches configured in :setting:`CACHES` is now available "
"via :data:`django.core.cache.caches`. This dict-like object provides a "
"different instance per thread. It supersedes "
"``django.core.cache.get_cache()`` which is now deprecated."
msgstr ""
"Tá rochtain ar chaches cumraithe in:setting: `CACHES` ar fáil anois "
"trí:data: `django.core.cache.caches`. Soláthraíonn an réad cosúil le dict "
"seo sampla difriúil in aghaidh an snáithe. Cuireann sé in ionad "
"``django.core.cache.get_cache () ``atá díluachtaithe anois."

msgid ""
"If you instantiate cache backends directly, be aware that they aren't thread-"
"safe any more, as :data:`django.core.cache.caches` now yields different "
"instances per thread."
msgstr ""
"Má chuireann tú cúltaca taisce isteach go díreach, bí ar an eolas nach "
"bhfuil siad sábháilte ó shnáithe níos mó, mar: data: "
"`django.core.cache.caches` tagann cásanna difriúla in aghaidh an snáithe "
"anois."

msgid ""
"Defining the :setting:`TIMEOUT <CACHES-TIMEOUT>` argument of "
"the :setting:`CACHES` setting as ``None`` will set the cache keys as \"non-"
"expiring\" by default. Previously, it was only possible to pass "
"``timeout=None`` to the cache backend's ``set()`` method."
msgstr ""
"Ag sainmhí <CACHES-TIMEOUT>niú argóint:setting: `TIMEOUT `den socrú: "
"`CACHES` mar ``None`` socraítear na heochracha taisce mar “neamh-éag” de "
"réir réamhshocraithe. Roimhe seo, ní raibh sé indéanta ach ``timeout = "
"none`` a chur chuig modh ``set () ``cúltaca taisce."

msgid "Cross Site Request Forgery"
msgstr "Falsaíocht Iarratas Tras-Láithreáin"

msgid ""
"The :setting:`CSRF_COOKIE_AGE` setting facilitates the use of session-based "
"CSRF cookies."
msgstr ""
"Éascaíonn an socrú: SETTING: `CSRF_COOKIE_AGE` úsáid fianáin CSRF bunaithe "
"ar sheisiún."

msgid ""
":func:`~django.core.mail.send_mail` now accepts an ``html_message`` "
"parameter for sending a multipart :mimetype:`text/plain` and :mimetype:`text/"
"html` email."
msgstr ""
":func: `~django.core.mail.send_mail` glacann anois le paraiméadar "
"``html_message`` chun ríomhphost multipart:mimetype: `text/plain` "
"agus:mimetype: `text/html` a sheoladh."

msgid ""
"The SMTP :class:`~django.core.mail.backends.smtp.EmailBackend` now accepts a "
"``timeout`` parameter."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an SMTP: Class: `~django.core.mail.backends.smtp.emailBackend` le "
"paraiméadar ``timeout`` anois."

msgid ""
"File locking on Windows previously depended on the PyWin32 package; if it "
"wasn't installed, file locking failed silently. That dependency has been "
"removed, and file locking is now implemented natively on both Windows and "
"Unix."
msgstr ""
"Bhí glasáil comhad ar Windows ag brath roimhe seo ar an bpacáiste PyWin32; "
"mura raibh sé suiteáilte, theip ar ghlasáil comhaid go ciúin. Tá an "
"spleáchas sin bainte, agus cuirtear glasáil comhad i bhfeidhm go dúchasach "
"anois ar Windows agus Unix araon."

msgid "File Uploads"
msgstr "Uaslódálacha Comhad"

msgid ""
"The new :attr:`UploadedFile.content_type_extra "
"<django.core.files.uploadedfile.UploadedFile.content_type_extra>` attribute "
"contains extra parameters passed to the ``content-type`` header on a file "
"upload."
msgstr ""
"Tá paraiméadair bhreise sa tréith nua:attr: `uploadedfile.content_type_extra "
"<django.core.files.uploadedfile.UploadedFile.content_type_extra>`a chuirtear "
"chuig an gceannteideal ``content-type`` ar uaslódáil comhad."

msgid ""
"The new :setting:`FILE_UPLOAD_DIRECTORY_PERMISSIONS` setting controls the "
"file system permissions of directories created during file upload, "
"like :setting:`FILE_UPLOAD_PERMISSIONS` does for the files themselves."
msgstr ""
"Rialaíonn an socrú nua:setting: `FILE_UPLOAD_DIRECTORY_PERMISSIONS` ceadanna "
"córais chomhaid eolairí a cruthaíodh le linn uaslódála comhaid, "
"cosúil:setting: `FILE_UPLOAD_PERMISSIONS` a dhéanann do na comhaid féin."

msgid ""
"The :attr:`FileField.upload_to <django.db.models.FileField.upload_to>` "
"attribute is now optional. If it is omitted or given ``None`` or an empty "
"string, a subdirectory won't be used for storing the uploaded files."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.FileField.upload_to>Tá an tréith: Attr: "
"`FileField.upload_to `roghnach anois. Má fhágann nó má thugtar ``None ``nó "
"teaghrán folamh é, ní úsáidfear fo-eolaire chun na comhaid uaslódáilte a "
"stóráil."

msgid ""
"Uploaded files are now explicitly closed before the response is delivered to "
"the client. Partially uploaded files are also closed as long as they are "
"named ``file`` in the upload handler."
msgstr ""
"Dúntar comhaid uaslódáilte go sainráite anois sula seachadtar an freagra don "
"chliant. Dúntar comhaid uaslódáilte go páirteach chomh fada agus a "
"ainmnítear “comhad” orthu sa láimhseálaí uaslódála."

msgid ""
":meth:`Storage.get_available_name() "
"<django.core.files.storage.Storage.get_available_name>` now appends an "
"underscore plus a random 7 character alphanumeric string (e.g. "
"``\"_x3a1gho\"``), rather than iterating through an underscore followed by a "
"number (e.g. ``\"_1\"``, ``\"_2\"``, etc.) to prevent a denial-of-service "
"attack. This change was also made in the 1.6.6, 1.5.9, and 1.4.14 security "
"releases."
msgstr ""
":meth: Cuireann `Storage.get_available_name () "
"<django.core.files.storage.Storage.get_available_name>`béim anois móide "
"sreang alfauméireach randamach 7 charachtar (m.sh. ``\"_x3a1gho\"``), "
"seachas athrá trí bhuscór ina dhiaidh sin uimhir (m.sh. ``\"_1\"``, `_2\"``, "
"etc.) chun ionsaí diúltaithe seirbhíse a chosc. Rinneadh an t-athrú seo "
"freisin sna eisiúintí slándála 1.6.6, 1.5.9, agus 1.4.14."

msgid ""
"The ``<label>`` and ``<input>`` tags rendered "
"by :class:`~django.forms.RadioSelect` "
"and :class:`~django.forms.CheckboxSelectMultiple` when looping over the "
"radio buttons or checkboxes now include ``for`` and ``id`` attributes, "
"respectively. Each radio button or checkbox includes an ``id_for_label`` "
"attribute to output the element's ID."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn na clibeanna ``<label>`` agus ```` a rinneadh ag: class: "
"`<input>~django.forms.RadioSelect` agus:class: "
"`~django.forms.checkboxSelectMultiple` agus iad ag lúbsáil thar na cnaipí "
"raidió nó na boscaí seiceála anois tréithe ``for`` agus `id``, faoi seach. "
"Cuimsíonn gach cnaipe raidió nó bosca seiceála tréith ``id_for_label`` chun "
"aitheantas an eilimint a aschur."

msgid ""
"The ``<textarea>`` tags rendered by :class:`~django.forms.Textarea` now "
"include a ``maxlength`` attribute if "
"the :class:`~django.db.models.TextField` model field has a ``max_length``."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn na clibeanna <textarea>```a rinneadh ag:class: "
"`~django.forms.textarea` tréith ``maxlength`` anois má tá réimse samhail "
"``max_`long` ag an réimse samhail: :class: `~django.db.Models.textField`."

msgid ""
":attr:`Field.choices<django.db.models.Field.choices>` now allows you to "
"customize the \"empty choice\" label by including a tuple with an empty "
"string or ``None`` for the key and the custom label as the value. The "
"default blank option ``\"----------\"`` will be omitted in this case."
msgstr ""
":attr: Ligeann `Field. <django.db.models.Field.choices>Choices `duit anois "
"an lipéad “rogha folamh” a shaincheapadh trí tuple a áireamh le sreang "
"folamh nó ``None`` don eochair agus an lipéad saincheaptha mar an luach. "
"Fágfar an rogha bán réamhshocraithe ``” ------------ “`` sa chás seo."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.forms.MultiValueField` allows optional subfields by setting "
"the ``require_all_fields`` argument to ``False``. The ``required`` attribute "
"for each individual field will be respected, and a new ``incomplete`` "
"validation error will be raised when any required fields are empty."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.forms.MultivalueField` ceadaíonn fo-réimsí roghnacha tríd "
"an argóint `requi_all_fields`` a shocrú go ``False``. Déanfar urramú ar an "
"tréith ``riachtan`` do gach réimse aonair, agus ardófar earráid "
"bailíochtaithe nua ``neamhiomlán`` nuair a bheidh aon réimsí riachtanacha "
"folamh."

msgid ""
"The :meth:`~django.forms.Form.clean` method on a form no longer needs to "
"return ``self.cleaned_data``. If it does return a changed dictionary then "
"that will still be used."
msgstr ""
"Ní gá don modh: Meth: `~django.forms.form.clean` ar fhoirm "
"``self.cleaned_data`` a thabhairt ar ais a thuilleadh. Má thugann sé foclóir "
"athraithe ar ais ansin úsáidfear é fós."

msgid ""
"After a temporary regression in Django 1.6, it's now possible again to "
"make :class:`~django.forms.TypedChoiceField` ``coerce`` method return an "
"arbitrary value."
msgstr ""
"Tar éis aischéimniú sealadach i Django 1.6, is féidir anois: class: "
"`~django.forms.TypedChoiceField` ``coerce`` modh luach treallach a thabhairt "
"ar ais."

msgid ""
":attr:`SelectDateWidget.months <django.forms.SelectDateWidget.months>` can "
"be used to customize the wording of the months displayed in the select "
"widget."
msgstr ""
":attr: Is féidir `SelectDateWidget.months "
"<django.forms.SelectDateWidget.months>`a úsáid chun foclaíocht na míonna a "
"thaispeántar sa ghuirléid roghnaithe a shaincheapadh."

msgid ""
"The ``min_num`` and ``validate_min`` parameters were added "
"to :func:`~django.forms.formsets.formset_factory` to allow validating a "
"minimum number of submitted forms."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh na paraiméadair ``min_num`` agus ``validate_min`` la:func: "
"`~django.forms.formsets.formset_factory` chun líon íosta foirmeacha curtha "
"isteach a bhailíochtú."

msgid ""
"The metaclasses used by ``Form`` and ``ModelForm`` have been reworked to "
"support more inheritance scenarios. The previous limitation that prevented "
"inheriting from both ``Form`` and ``ModelForm`` simultaneously have been "
"removed as long as ``ModelForm`` appears first in the MRO."
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh na meiteachlasanna a úsáideann ``Form`` agus `ModelForm ``athoibriú "
"chun tacú le níos mó cásanna oidhreachta. Baineadh an teorannú roimhe seo a "
"chuir cosc ar oidhreacht ó ``Form`` agus `ModelForm`` araon ag an am céanna "
"chomh fada agus a fheictear ``ModelForm`` ar dtús sa MRO."

msgid ""
"It's now possible to remove a field from a ``Form`` when subclassing by "
"setting the name to ``None``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir anois réimse a bhaint as ``Foirm ``agus tú ag fo-aicmiú tríd an "
"ainm a shocrú go ``None``."

msgid ""
"It's now possible to customize the error messages for ``ModelForm``’s "
"``unique``, ``unique_for_date``, and ``unique_together`` constraints. In "
"order to support ``unique_together`` or any other ``NON_FIELD_ERROR``, "
"``ModelForm`` now looks for the ``NON_FIELD_ERROR`` key in the "
"``error_messages`` dictionary of the ``ModelForm``’s inner ``Meta`` class. "
"See :ref:`considerations regarding model's error_messages <considerations-"
"regarding-model-errormessages>` for more details."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir anois na teachtaireachtaí earráide a shaincheapadh le haghaidh "
"srianta ```unique``, `unique_for_date``, agus ```unique_together "
"``ModelForm``. D'fhonn tacú le ``unique_together`` nó aon "
"``NON_FIELD_ERROR`` eile, féachann ``Modelform`` anois an eochair "
"``NON_FIELD_ERROR`` sa fhoclóir ``error_messages`` de rang `Meta`` istigh "
"``ModelForm``. <considerations-regarding-model-errormessages>Féach:ref: "
"`breithnithe maidir le earr_messages an tsamhail `le haghaidh tuilleadh "
"sonraí."

msgid ""
"The :attr:`django.middleware.locale.LocaleMiddleware.response_redirect_class` "
"attribute allows you to customize the redirects issued by the middleware."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn an tréith: Attr: "
"`Django.middleware.locale.localeMiddleware.RESPONSE_REDIRECT_CLASS` duit na "
"hathreoruithe arna eisiúint ag an middleware a shaincheapadh."

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.middleware.locale.LocaleMiddleware` now stores the "
"user's selected language with the session key ``_language``. This should "
"only be accessed using the ``LANGUAGE_SESSION_KEY`` constant. Previously it "
"was stored with the key ``django_language`` and the ``LANGUAGE_SESSION_KEY`` "
"constant did not exist, but keys reserved for Django should start with an "
"underscore. For backwards compatibility ``django_language`` is still read "
"from in 1.7. Sessions will be migrated to the new key as they are written."
msgstr ""
"Stórálann an:class: `~django.middleware.locale.localeMiddleware` teanga "
"roghnaithe an úsáideora anois leis an eochair seisiúin ``_language``. Níor "
"cheart rochtain a fháil air seo ach ag baint úsáide as an tairiseach "
"``LANGUAGE_SESSION_KEY``. Roimhe seo stóráilíodh é leis an eochair "
"`django_language`` agus ní raibh an tairiseach ``LANGUAGE_SESSION_KEY`` ann, "
"ach ba chóir go dtosódh eochracha atá curtha in áirithe do Django le béim. "
"Maidir le comhoiriúnacht ar chúl léitear ``django_language`` fós ó in 1.7. "
"Aimirfear na seisiúin chuig an eochair nua de réir mar a bheidh siad scríofa."

msgid ""
"The :ttag:`blocktrans` tag now supports a ``trimmed`` option. This option "
"will remove newline characters from the beginning and the end of the content "
"of the ``{% blocktrans %}`` tag, replace any whitespace at the beginning and "
"end of a line and merge all lines into one using a space character to "
"separate them. This is quite useful for indenting the content of a ``{% "
"blocktrans %}`` tag without having the indentation characters end up in the "
"corresponding entry in the ``.po`` file, which makes the translation process "
"easier."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn an clibe:ttag: `blocktrans` anois le rogha ``trimmed`. Bainfidh an "
"rogha seo carachtair líne nua ó thús agus deireadh ábhair an chlib ``{% "
"blocktrans%} `, cuirfidh sé in ionad aon spás bán ag tús agus deireadh líne "
"agus cumasc na líne go léir i gceann amháin ag baint úsáide as carachtar "
"spáis chun iad a scaradh. Tá sé seo úsáideach go leor chun ábhar chlib ``{% "
"blocktrans%}`` a iontráil gan na carachtair iontrála a bheith ag críochnú "
"san iontráil chomhfhreagrach sa chomhad `.po``, rud a fhágann go bhfuil an "
"próiseas aistriúcháin níos éasca."

msgid ""
"When you run :djadmin:`makemessages` from the root directory of your "
"project, any extracted strings will now be automatically distributed to the "
"proper app or project message file. See :ref:`how-to-create-language-files` "
"for details."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a rith tú: djadmin: `makemessages` ó eolaire fréimhe do thionscadail, "
"dáilfear aon teaghráin bainte go huathoibríoch anois chuig an aip ceart nó "
"ar chomhad teachtaireachta tionscadail. Féach: Ref: `conas-chomhaid teanga a "
"chruthaithe' le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`makemessages` command now always adds the ``--previous`` "
"command line flag to the ``msgmerge`` command, keeping previously translated "
"strings in ``.po`` files for fuzzy strings."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann an t-ordú: DjaDmin: `makemessages` anois an bhratach líne ordaithe "
"``--roimhe ``i gcónaí leis an ordú ``msgmerge``, ag coinneáil teaghráin "
"aistrithe roimhe seo i gcomhaid ``.po`` le haghaidh teaghráin doiléir."

msgid ""
"The following settings to adjust the language cookie options were "
"introduced: :setting:`LANGUAGE_COOKIE_AGE`, :setting:`LANGUAGE_COOKIE_DOMAIN` "
"and :setting:`LANGUAGE_COOKIE_PATH`."
msgstr ""
"Tugadh isteach na socruithe seo a leanas chun na roghanna fianán teanga a "
"choigeartú: :setting: `LANGUAGE_COOKIE_AGE`, :setting: "
"`LANGUAGE_COOKIE_DOMAIN` agus:setting: `LANGUAGE_COOKIE_PATH`."

msgid "Added :doc:`/topics/i18n/formatting` for Esperanto."
msgstr "Cuireadh leis: doc: `/topics/i18n/foirmiúcháin` don Esperanto."

msgid ""
"The new :option:`--no-color` option for ``django-admin`` disables the "
"colorization of management command output."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an rogha nua:rogha: `--no-color` le haghaidh ``django-admin ``dathú "
"aschur ordaithe bainistíochta a dhíchumasú."

msgid ""
"The new :option:`dumpdata --natural-foreign` and :option:`dumpdata --natural-"
"primary` options, and the new ``use_natural_foreign_keys`` and "
"``use_natural_primary_keys`` arguments for ``serializers.serialize()``, "
"allow the use of natural primary keys when serializing."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn na roghanna nua:option: `dumpdata --natural-foreign` agus:option: "
"`dumpdata --natural-primary`, agus na hargóintí nua "
"``use_natural_foreign_keys`` agus `use_natural_primary_keys`` le haghaidh "
"`serializers.serialize () ``, eochracha príomhúil nádúrtha a úsáid agus iad "
"ag sraith."

msgid ""
"It is no longer necessary to provide the cache table name or the ``--"
"database`` option for the :djadmin:`createcachetable` command. Django takes "
"this information from your settings file. If you have configured multiple "
"caches or multiple databases, all cache tables are created."
msgstr ""
"Ní gá a thuilleadh ainm an tábla taisce nó an rogha ``--database` a "
"sholáthar don ordú:djadmin: `createcachetable`. Tógann Django an fhaisnéis "
"seo ó do chomhad socruithe. Má tá iliomad caches nó bunachair sonraí "
"iolracha cumraithe agat, cruthaítear gach tábla taisce."

msgid "The :djadmin:`runserver` command received several improvements:"
msgstr "Fuair an t-ordú: Djadmin: `runserver` roinnt feabhsúcháin:"

msgid ""
"On Linux systems, if :pypi:`pyinotify` is installed, the development server "
"will reload immediately when a file is changed. Previously, it polled the "
"filesystem for changes every second. That caused a small delay before "
"reloads and reduced battery life on laptops."
msgstr ""
"Ar chórais Linux, má tá :pypi:`pyinotify` suiteáilte, athlódálfar an "
"freastalaí forbartha láithreach nuair a athraítear comhad. Roimhe seo, rinne "
"sé vótaíocht ar an gcóras comhad le haghaidh athruithe gach soicind. Ba "
"chúis leis sin moill bheag roimh athlódáil agus saol ceallraí laghdaithe ar "
"ríomhairí glúine."

msgid ""
"In addition, the development server automatically reloads when a translation "
"file is updated, i.e. after running :djadmin:`compilemessages`."
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, athlódálann an freastalaí forbartha go huathoibríoch nuair "
"a dhéantar comhad aistriúcháin a nuashonrú, i.e. tar éis rith: djadmin: "
"`compilemessages`."

msgid ""
"All HTTP requests are logged to the console, including requests for static "
"files or ``favicon.ico`` that used to be filtered out."
msgstr ""
"Tá gach iarratas HTTP logáilte chuig an gconsól, lena n-áirítear iarratais "
"ar chomhaid statacha nó “favicon.ico” a bhíodh scagadh amach."

msgid ""
"Management commands can now produce syntax colored output under Windows if "
"the ANSICON third-party tool is installed and active."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le horduithe bainistíochta aschur daite comhréire a tháirgeadh "
"anois faoi Windows má tá uirlis tríú páirtí ANSICON suiteáilte agus "
"gníomhach."

msgid ""
":djadmin:`collectstatic` command with symlink option is now supported on "
"Windows NT 6 (Windows Vista and newer)."
msgstr ""
":djadmin: Tacaítear anois le ordú `collectstatic` le rogha symlink ar "
"Windows NT 6 (Windows Vista agus níos nuaí)."

msgid ""
"Initial SQL data now works better if the :pypi:`sqlparse` Python library is "
"installed."
msgstr ""
"Oibríonn sonraí tosaigh SQL anois má tá leabharlann Python: pypi: `sqlparse` "
"suiteáilte."

msgid ""
"Note that it's deprecated in favor of "
"the :class:`~django.db.migrations.operations.RunSQL` operation of "
"migrations, which benefits from the improved behavior."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go bhfuil sé dlús i bhfabhar oibriú imirce:class: "
"`~django.db.migrations.operations.runsql`, a bhaineann leas as an iompar "
"feabhsaithe."

msgid ""
"The :meth:`QuerySet.update_or_create() "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.update_or_create>` method was added."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.update_or_create>Cuireadh an modh: Meth: "
"`QuerySet.UPDATE_OR_CREATE () `leis."

msgid ""
"The new :attr:`~django.db.models.Options.default_permissions` model ``Meta`` "
"option allows you to customize (or disable) creation of the default add, "
"change, and delete permissions."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an rogha múnla nua:attr: "
"`~django.db.models.options.default_permissions` `Meta`` duit cruthú na "
"ceadanna réamhshocraithe a chur leis, a athrú agus a scriosadh a "
"shaincheapadh (nó a dhíchumasú)."

msgid ""
"Explicit :class:`~django.db.models.OneToOneField` for :ref:`multi-table-"
"inheritance` are now discovered in abstract classes."
msgstr ""
"Faightear Explicit:class: `~django.db.models.onetoonefield` for:ref: `multi-"
"table-heritance` anois i ranganna teibí."

msgid ""
"It is now possible to avoid creating a backward relation "
"for :class:`~django.db.models.OneToOneField` by setting "
"its :attr:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey.related_name` to ``'+'`` or ending "
"it with ``'+'``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir anois caidreamh cúil a chruthú do:class: "
"`~django.db.models.onetoonefield` a sheachaint trí:attr: "
"`~django.db.models.foreignkey.related_name` a shocrú go ``'+'`` nó é a "
"chríochnú le ``'+'``."

msgid ""
":class:`F expressions <django.db.models.F>` support the power operator "
"(``**``)."
msgstr ""
":class: Tacaíonn abairtí `F <django.db.models.F>`leis an oibreoir cumhachta "
"(``**``)."

msgid ""
"The ``remove()`` and ``clear()`` methods of the related managers created by "
"``ForeignKey`` and ``GenericForeignKey`` now accept the ``bulk`` keyword "
"argument to control whether or not to perform operations in bulk (i.e. using "
"``QuerySet.update()``). Defaults to ``True``."
msgstr ""
"Glacann modhanna ``remove () ``agus `clear ()`` na mbainisteoirí gaolmhara a "
"chruthaigh ``ForeignKey`` agus ``GenericForeignKey`` anois leis an argóint "
"eochairfhocal ``bulk`` chun rialú a dhéanamh cibé acu oibríochtaí a dhéanamh "
"ar an mórchóir (ie ag baint úsáide as ``QuerySet.Update () `). "
"Réamhshocraithe go ``True``."

msgid ""
"It is now possible to use ``None`` as a query value for the :lookup:`iexact` "
"lookup."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir anois ``None`` a úsáid mar luach fiosrúcháin don chuardach:lookup: "
"`iexact`."

msgid ""
"It is now possible to pass a callable as value for the "
"attribute :attr:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey.limit_choices_to` when "
"defining a ``ForeignKey`` or ``ManyToManyField``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir anois glaoch a chur ar aghaidh mar luach don tréith: attr: "
"`~Django.db.Models.ForeignKey.LIMIT_CHOICES_TO` agus ``ForeignKey`` nó "
"``ManyTomanyField`` á shainiú."

msgid ""
"Calling :meth:`only() <django.db.models.query.QuerySet.only>` "
"and :meth:`defer() <django.db.models.query.QuerySet.defer>` on the result "
"of :meth:`QuerySet.values() <django.db.models.query.QuerySet.values>` now "
"raises an error (before that, it would either result in a database error or "
"incorrect data)."
msgstr ""
"Ardaíonn glaoch: Meth: `only () "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.only>`agus:meth: `defer ()` "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.defer>ar thoradh: meth: `QuerySet.Values () "
"`earráid anois (roimh sin, bheadh earráid bunachar sonraí "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.values>nó sonraí míchearta mar thoradh air)."

msgid ""
"You can use a single list for ``index_together`` (rather than a list of "
"lists) when specifying a single set of fields."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat liosta amháin a úsáid le haghaidh `index_together ``(seachas "
"liosta liostaí) agus sraith amháin réimsí á shonrú agat."

msgid ""
"Custom intermediate models having more than one foreign key to any of the "
"models participating in a many-to-many relationship are now permitted, "
"provided you explicitly specify which foreign keys should be used by setting "
"the new :attr:`ManyToManyField.through_fields "
"<django.db.models.ManyToManyField.through_fields>` argument."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.ManyToManyField.through_fields>Ceadaítear samhlacha "
"idirmheánacha saincheaptha a bhfuil níos mó ná eochair eachtrach amháin acu "
"d'aon cheann de na samhlacha atá rannpháirteach i gcaidreamh go leor anois, "
"ar choinníoll go sonraíonn tú go sainráite cé na heochracha eachtracha ba "
"chóir a úsáid tríd an argóint nua:attr: `ManyTomanyField.through_fields `a "
"shocrú."

msgid ""
"Assigning a model instance to a non-relation field will now throw an error. "
"Previously this used to work if the field accepted integers as input as it "
"took the primary key."
msgstr ""
"Déanfar earráid anois a shannadh samhail samhail a shannadh do réimse "
"neamhghaolmhar. Roimhe seo bhí sé seo ag obair má ghlac an réimse le "
"sláimhreacha mar ionchur mar a ghlac sé an príomh-eochair."

msgid ""
"Integer fields are now validated against database backend specific min and "
"max values based on their :meth:`internal_type "
"<django.db.models.Field.get_internal_type>`. Previously model field "
"validation didn't prevent values out of their associated column data type "
"range from being saved resulting in an integrity error."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.Field.get_internal_type>Tá réimsí sláireach bailíochtaithe "
"anois i gcoinne luachanna min agus uasta sonracha cúltaca bunachar sonraí "
"bunaithe ar a gcuid: meth: `internal_type `. Níor chuir bailíochtú réimse "
"samhail roimhe seo cosc ar luachanna as a raon cineálacha sonraí colún "
"gaolmhar a shábháil mar thoradh ar earráid sláine."

msgid ""
"It is now possible to "
"explicitly :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.order_by` a relation "
"``_id`` field by using its attribute name."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir anois réimse gaolmhar ``_id`` a chur in iúl go soiléirí:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.order_by` trí a ainm tréithe a úsáid."

msgid ""
"The ``enter`` argument was added to "
"the :data:`~django.test.signals.setting_changed` signal."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an argóint `enter ``leis an gcomhartha: data: "
"`~django.test.signals.setting_changed`."

msgid ""
"The model signals can be now be connected to using a ``str`` of the "
"``'app_label.ModelName'`` form – just like related fields – to lazily "
"reference their senders."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir na comharthaí samhail a nascadh anois le ``str`` den fhoirm "
"``App_Label.ModelName'` a úsáid - díreach cosúil le réimsí gaolmhara - chun "
"tagairt a thabhairt dá gcuid seoltóirí go leisciúil."

msgid ""
"The :meth:`Context.push() <django.template.Context.push>` method now returns "
"a context manager which automatically calls :meth:`pop() "
"<django.template.Context.pop>` upon exiting the ``with`` statement. "
"Additionally, :meth:`push() <django.template.Context.push>` now accepts "
"parameters that are passed to the ``dict`` constructor used to build the new "
"context level."
msgstr ""
"<django.template.Context.pop>Tugann an modh: Meth: `Context.push () "
"<django.template.Context.push>`bainisteoir comhthéacs ar ais anois a "
"ghlaonn: meth: `pop ()` go huathoibríoch nuair a fhágann sé an ráiteas "
"``with`. Ina theann <django.template.Context.push>ta sin, glacann: meth: "
"`push () `anois le paraiméadair a chuirtear chuig an tógálaí ``dict`` a "
"úsáidtear chun an leibhéal comhthéacs nua a thógáil."

msgid ""
"The new :meth:`Context.flatten() <django.template.Context.flatten>` method "
"returns a ``Context``'s stack as one flat dictionary."
msgstr ""
"Tugann an modh nua:meth: `Context.flatten () "
"<django.template.Context.flatten>`cruach ``Context`` ar ais mar fhoclóir "
"comhréidh amháin."

msgid ""
"``Context`` objects can now be compared for equality (internally, this "
"uses :meth:`Context.flatten() <django.template.Context.flatten>` so the "
"internal structure of each ``Context``'s stack doesn't matter as long as "
"their flattened version is identical)."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir rudaí `Context`` a chur i gcomparáid anois le haghaidh "
"comhionannais (go hinmheánach, úsáideann sé seo: meth: `Context.flatten () "
"<django.template.Context.flatten>`mar sin ní cuma struchtúr inmheánach gach "
"cruach ``Context`` chomh fada agus a leagan comhréadaithe comhionann)."

msgid ""
"The :ttag:`widthratio` template tag now accepts an ``\"as\"`` parameter to "
"capture the result in a variable."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an chlib teimpléad: ttag: `widthratio` anois le paraiméadar "
"```as\"`` chun an toradh a ghabháil in athróg."

msgid ""
"The :ttag:`include` template tag will now also accept anything with a "
"``render()`` method (such as a ``Template``) as an argument. String "
"arguments will be looked up "
"using :func:`~django.template.loader.get_template` as always."
msgstr ""
"Glacfaidh an clib teimpléad:ttag: `include` anois le haon rud a bhfuil modh "
"`render () ``(mar shampla ``Teimpléad``) mar argóint. Breathnófar argóintí "
"teaghráin ag baint úsáide as: func: `~django.template.loader.get_template` "
"mar i gcónaí."

msgid "It is now possible to :ttag:`include` templates recursively."
msgstr "Is féidir anois teimpléid: ttag: `include` athshlánach."

msgid ""
"Template objects now have an origin attribute set when ``TEMPLATE_DEBUG`` is "
"``True``. This allows template origins to be inspected and logged outside of "
"the ``django.template`` infrastructure."
msgstr ""
"Tá tréith tionscnaimh socraithe ag rudaí teimpléad anois nuair is é "
"``TEMPLATE_DEBUG` ``True``. Ligeann sé seo bunús teimpléid a iniúchadh agus "
"a logáil lasmuigh den bhonneagar `django.template``."

msgid ""
"``TypeError`` exceptions are no longer silenced when raised during the "
"rendering of a template."
msgstr ""
"Ní dhéantar eisceachtaí `TypeError` a thostú a thuilleadh nuair a ardaítear "
"iad le linn rindreáil teimpléad."

msgid ""
"The following functions now accept a ``dirs`` parameter which is a list or "
"tuple to override ``TEMPLATE_DIRS``:"
msgstr ""
"Glacann na feidhmeanna seo a leanas anois le paraiméadar ``dirs`` atá ina "
"liosta nó tuple chun ``TEMPLATE_DIRS`` a shárú:"

msgid ":func:`django.template.loader.get_template()`"
msgstr ":func: `django.template.loader.get_template () `"

msgid ":func:`django.template.loader.select_template()`"
msgstr ":func: `django.template.loader.select_template () `"

msgid ":func:`django.shortcuts.render()`"
msgstr ":func: `django.shortcuts.render () `"

msgid ""
"The :tfilter:`time` filter now accepts timezone-related :ref:`format "
"specifiers <date-and-time-formatting-specifiers>` ``'e'``, ``'O'`` , ``'T'`` "
"and ``'Z'`` and is able to digest :ref:`time-zone-aware "
"<naive_vs_aware_datetimes>` ``datetime`` instances performing the expected "
"rendering."
msgstr ""
"<naive_vs_aware_datetimes>Glacann an scagair:TFilter: `time` anois le "
"sonraitheoirí ama a bhaineann le crios ama:ref: `formáid ````````,```````, "
"```````agus ``Z <date-and-time-formatting-specifiers>'``agus tá sé in ann "
"cásanna a dhíleá:ref: `time-chrione-aware` `datetime`` cásanna a bhfuil súil "
"leis."

msgid ""
"The :ttag:`cache` tag will now try to use the cache called "
"\"template_fragments\" if it exists and fall back to using the default cache "
"otherwise. It also now accepts an optional ``using`` keyword argument to "
"control which cache it uses."
msgstr ""
"Déanfaidh an clibe:ttag: `cache` iarracht anois an taisce ar a dtugtar "
"“template_fragments” a úsáid má tá sé ann agus tiocfaidh sé ar ais chun an "
"taisce réamhshocraithe a úsáid ar mhalairt eile. Glacann sé anois le argóint "
"eochairfhocal roghnach ``úsáid ``chun rialú a dhéanamh ar an taisce a "
"úsáideann sé."

msgid ""
"The new :tfilter:`truncatechars_html` filter truncates a string to be no "
"longer than the specified number of characters, taking HTML into account."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann an scagaire nua:tfilter: `truncatechars_html` teaghrán a bhaint "
"amach nach bhfuil níos faide ná an líon sonraithe carachtair, ag cur HTML "
"san áireamh."

msgid ""
"The new :attr:`HttpRequest.scheme <django.http.HttpRequest.scheme>` "
"attribute specifies the scheme of the request (``http`` or ``https`` "
"normally)."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn an tréith nua:attr: `HttpRequest.scheme "
"<django.http.HttpRequest.scheme>`scéim an iarratais (``http`` nó ``https`` "
"de ghnáth)."

msgid ""
"The shortcut :func:`redirect() <django.shortcuts.redirect>` now supports "
"relative URLs."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn an gearrgearrth:func: `redirect () "
"<django.shortcuts.redirect>`anois le URLanna coibhneasta."

msgid ""
"The new :class:`~django.http.JsonResponse` subclass "
"of :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse` helps easily create JSON-encoded "
"responses."
msgstr ""
"Cuidíonn an fo-aicme nua:class: `~django.http.JSONResponse` de:class: "
"`~Django.http.HttpResponse` le freagraí ionchódaithe JSON a chruthú go "
"héasca."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.test.runner.DiscoverRunner` has two new "
"attributes, :attr:`~django.test.runner.DiscoverRunner.test_suite` "
"and :attr:`~django.test.runner.DiscoverRunner.test_runner`, which facilitate "
"overriding the way tests are collected and run."
msgstr ""
":class: `~Django.Test.Runner.DiscoverRunner` dhá thréith nua ag: attr: "
"`~django.test.runner.discoverrunner.test_suite` agus:attr: "
"`~django.test.runner.discoverRunner.test_runner`, a éascaíonn an tslí a "
"bhailítear agus a reáchtáil."

msgid ""
"The ``fetch_redirect_response`` argument was added "
"to :meth:`~django.test.SimpleTestCase.assertRedirects`. Since the test "
"client can't fetch externals URLs, this allows you to use "
"``assertRedirects`` with redirects that aren't part of your Django app."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an argóint ``fetch_redirect_response`` la:meth: "
"`~django.test.simpletestcase.assertDirects`. Ós rud é nach féidir leis an "
"gcliant tástála URLanna seachtracha a fháil, tugann sé seo deis duit "
"``AssertreDirects` a úsáid le hathreoruithe nach bhfuil mar chuid de d'aip "
"Django."

msgid ""
"Correct handling of scheme when making comparisons "
"in :meth:`~django.test.SimpleTestCase.assertRedirects`."
msgstr ""
"Láimhseáil cheart na scéime agus comparáidí á dhéanamh in:meth: "
"`~django.test.simpletestCase.assertDirects`."

msgid ""
"The ``secure`` argument was added to all the request methods "
"of :class:`~django.test.Client`. If ``True``, the request will be made "
"through HTTPS."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an argóint `secure`` leis na modhanna iarratais uile de:class: "
"`~django.test.client`. Má tá “Fíor”, déanfar an t-iarratas trí HTTPS."

msgid ""
":meth:`~django.test.TransactionTestCase.assertNumQueries` now prints out the "
"list of executed queries if the assertion fails."
msgstr ""
":meth: `~django.test.transactionTestCase.assertNumqueries` anois priontáil "
"liosta na gceisteanna forghníomhaithe má theipeann ar an dearbhú."

msgid ""
"The ``WSGIRequest`` instance generated by the test handler is now attached "
"to the :attr:`django.test.Response.wsgi_request` attribute."
msgstr ""
"Tá an cás ``WSGIrequest`` a ghineann an láimhseálaí tástála ceangailte anois "
"leis an tréith: attr: `Django.Test.Response.wsgi_request`."

msgid ""
"The database settings for testing have been collected into a dictionary "
"named :setting:`TEST <DATABASE-TEST>`."
msgstr ""
"<DATABASE-TEST>Bailíodh na socruithe bunachar sonraí le haghaidh tástála "
"isteach i bhfoclóir darb ainmne:setting: `TEST `."

msgid "Utilities"
msgstr "Fóntais"

msgid ""
":class:`~django.core.validators.RegexValidator` now accepts the "
"optional :attr:`~django.core.validators.RegexValidator.flags` and "
"Boolean :attr:`~django.core.validators.RegexValidator.inverse_match` "
"arguments. The :attr:`~django.core.validators.RegexValidator.inverse_match` "
"attribute determines if the :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` "
"should be raised when the regular expression pattern matches (``True``) or "
"does not match (``False``, by default) the provided ``value``. "
"The :attr:`~django.core.validators.RegexValidator.flags` attribute sets the "
"flags used when compiling a regular expression string."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.core.validators.regexvalidator` glacann anois leis na "
"hargóintí roghnaí:attr: `~django.core.validators.regexvalidator.flags` agus "
"boolean:attr: `~django.core.validators.regexvalidator.inverse_match`. "
"Cinneann an tréith: `~django.core.validators.regexvalidator.inverse_match` "
"an cheart an:exc: `~django.core.exceptions.validationError` a ardú nuair a "
"mheaitseálann an patrún abairt rialta (`True``) nó nach bhfuil (`False``, de "
"réir réamhshocraithe) an `value`` curtha ar fáil. Socraíonn an tréith: Attr: "
"`~django.core.validators.regexvalidator.flags` na bratacha a úsáidtear agus "
"teaghrán abairt rialta á thiomsú."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.core.validators.URLValidator` now accepts an optional "
"``schemes`` argument which allows customization of the accepted URI schemes "
"(instead of the defaults ``http(s)`` and ``ftp(s)``)."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.core.validators.URLValidator` anois glacann argóint "
"roghnach ``schemes`` a cheadaíonn saincheapadh na scéimeanna URI a nglactar "
"leo (in ionad na réamhshocraithe ``http (s) ``agus ``ftp (s)``)."

msgid ""
":func:`~django.core.validators.validate_email` now accepts addresses with "
"IPv6 literals, like ``example@[2001:db8::1]``, as specified in RFC 5321."
msgstr ""
":func: `~django.core.validators.validate_email` glacann anois le seoltaí le "
"litríochtaí IPv6, mar ``example@ [2001: db8: :1] ``, mar a shonraítear i RFC "
"5321."

msgid "Backwards incompatible changes in 1.7"
msgstr "Athruithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha ar ais i 1.7"

msgid ""
"In addition to the changes outlined in this section, be sure to review "
"the :ref:`deprecation plan <deprecation-removed-in-1.7>` for any features "
"that have been removed. If you haven't updated your code within the "
"deprecation timeline for a given feature, its removal may appear as a "
"backwards incompatible change."
msgstr ""
"<deprecation-removed-in-1.7>Chomh maith leis na hathruithe a leagtar amach "
"sa chuid seo, déan cinnte athbhreithniú a dhéanamh ar an:ref: `plean "
"díréachtaithe `le haghaidh aon ghnéithe a baineadh. Mura ndearna tú do chód "
"a nuashonrú laistigh den amlíne díscoilte do ghné ar leith, d'fhéadfadh go "
"mbeadh sé a bhaint mar athrú neamh-chomhoiriúnach ar chúl."

msgid "``allow_syncdb`` / ``allow_migrate``"
msgstr "``allow_syncdb``/``allow_migrate``"

msgid ""
"While Django will still look at ``allow_syncdb`` methods even though they "
"should be renamed to ``allow_migrate``, there is a subtle difference in "
"which models get passed to these methods."
msgstr ""
"Cé go bhféachfaidh Django fós ar mhodhanna `allow_syncdb`` cé gur chóir iad "
"a athainmniú go `allow_migrate``, tá difríocht caolchúiseach ann inar "
"chuirtear samhlacha chuig na modhanna seo."

msgid ""
"For apps with migrations, ``allow_migrate`` will now get "
"passed :ref:`historical models <historical-models>`, which are special "
"versioned models without custom attributes, methods or managers. Make sure "
"your ``allow_migrate`` methods are only referring to fields or other items "
"in ``model._meta``."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le feidhmchláir le himirce, gheobhaidh `allow_migrate`` pas "
"anois:ref: `samhlacha stairiúla `, ar samhlacha leaganacha speisialta iad "
"gan tréithe<historical-models>, modhanna nó bainisteoirí saincheaptha. Déan "
"cinnte nach bhfuil do mhodhanna `allow_migrate`` ag tagairt ach do réimsí nó "
"do mhíreanna eile sa `samhail. _meta``."

msgid "initial_data"
msgstr "sonraí tosaigh"

msgid ""
"Apps with migrations will not load ``initial_data`` fixtures when they have "
"finished migrating. Apps without migrations will continue to load these "
"fixtures during the phase of ``migrate`` which emulates the old ``syncdb`` "
"behavior, but any new apps will not have this support."
msgstr ""
"Ní luchtálfaidh aipeanna le himirce daingneáin ``initial_data` nuair a "
"bheidh imirce críochnaithe acu. Leanfaidh aipeanna gan imirce ag luchtú na "
"daingneáin seo le linn na céime ``imirce`` a dhéanann aithris ar an sean-"
"iompar ``syncdb`, ach ní bheidh an tacaíocht seo ag aon aipeanna nua."

msgid ""
"Instead, you are encouraged to load initial data in migrations if you need "
"it (using the ``RunPython`` operation and your model classes); this has the "
"added advantage that your initial data will not need updating every time you "
"change the schema."
msgstr ""
"Ina áit sin, moltar duit sonraí tosaigh a luchtú in imirce má theastaíonn "
"uait (ag baint úsáide as an oibríocht ``RunPython`` agus do ranganna "
"samhail); tá an buntáiste breise aige seo nach mbeidh gá le do shonraí "
"tosaigh a nuashonrú gach uair a athraíonn tú an scéim."

msgid ""
"Additionally, like the rest of Django's old ``syncdb`` code, "
"``initial_data`` has been started down the deprecation path and will be "
"removed in Django 1.9."
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, cosúil leis an gcuid eile de sheanchód ``syncdb`` Django, "
"cuireadh tús le ``initial_data`` síos an chosáin díghabhála agus bainfear é "
"i Django 1.9."

msgid "``deconstruct()`` and serializability"
msgstr "``dífhoirmiú () ``agus inshraitheacht"

msgid ""
"Django now requires all Field classes and all of their constructor arguments "
"to be serializable. If you modify the constructor signature in your custom "
"Field in any way, you'll need to implement a ``deconstruct()`` method; we've "
"expanded the custom field documentation with :ref:`instructions on "
"implementing this method <custom-field-deconstruct-method>`."
msgstr ""
"Éilíonn Django anois go mbeidh gach rang Allamuigh agus gach ceann dá n-"
"argóintí tógálaí inshraitheach. <custom-field-deconstruct-method>Má "
"mhodhnóidh tú síniú an tógálaí i do Réimse saincheaptha ar bhealach ar bith, "
"beidh ort modh `déconstrúchtacht () `a chur i bhfeidhm; tá an doiciméadú "
"réimse saincheaptha leathnaithe againn le: ref: `treoracha maidir leis an "
"modh seo a chur i bhfeidhm`."

msgid ""
"The requirement for all field arguments to be :ref:`serializable <migration-"
"serializing>` means that any custom class instances being passed into Field "
"constructors - things like custom Storage subclasses, for instance - need to "
"have a :ref:`deconstruct method defined on them as well <custom-deconstruct-"
"method>`, though Django provides a handy class decorator that will work for "
"most applications."
msgstr ""
"Ci <migration-serializing>allaíonn an riachtanas go mbeadh gach argóint "
"allamui:ref: `serializable `go gcaithfidh aon chásanna aicme saincheaptha a "
"chuirtear chuig tógálaí Páirce - rudaí cosúil le fo-aicmí Stórála "
"saincheaptha, mar shampla - a shainiú: `modh dífhoirmithe orthu chomh "
"maith<custom-deconstruct-method>`, cé go soláthraíonn Django maisitheoir "
"aicme áisiúil a oibreoidh don chuid is mó de na feidhmchláir."

msgid "App-loading changes"
msgstr "Athruithe luchtaithe aip"

msgid "Start-up sequence"
msgstr "Seicheamh tosaithe"

msgid ""
"Django 1.7 loads application configurations and models as soon as it starts. "
"While this behavior is more straightforward and is believed to be more "
"robust, regressions cannot be ruled out. See :ref:`applications-"
"troubleshooting` for solutions to some problems you may encounter."
msgstr ""
"Luchtaíonn Django 1.7 cumraíochtaí agus samhlacha feidhmchláir a luaithe a "
"thosaíonn sé. Cé go bhfuil an t-iompar seo níos simplí agus creidtear go "
"bhfuil sé níos láidre, ní féidir aischéimnithe a chur in iúl. Féach: "
"tagairt: `iarratais-fabhtcheartú 'le haghaidh réitigh ar roinnt fadhbanna a "
"d'fhéadfadh a bheith agat."

msgid "Standalone scripts"
msgstr "Scripteanna neamhspleácha"

msgid ""
"If you're using Django in a plain Python script — rather than a management "
"command — and you rely on the :envvar:`DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE` environment "
"variable, you must now explicitly initialize Django at the beginning of your "
"script with:"
msgstr ""
"Má tá Django á úsáid agat i script Python simplí - seachas ordú "
"bainistíochta - agus má tá tú ag brath ar an athróg comhshaoil: envvar: "
"`DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE`, ní mór duit Django a thionscnamh go sainráite "
"anois ag tús do script le:"

msgid "Otherwise, you will hit an ``AppRegistryNotReady`` exception."
msgstr "Seachas sin, buailfidh tú eisceacht ``AppregistryNotready`."

msgid "WSGI scripts"
msgstr "Scripteanna WSGI"

msgid ""
"Until Django 1.3, the recommended way to create a WSGI application was::"
msgstr ""
"Go dtí Django 1.3, ba é an bealach a mholtar chun feidhmchlár WSGI a chruthú "
"ná:"

msgid "In Django 1.4, support for WSGI was improved and the API changed to::"
msgstr "I Django 1.4, feabhsaíodh tacaíocht do WSGI agus athraíodh an API go:"

msgid ""
"If you're still using the former style in your WSGI script, you need to "
"upgrade to the latter, or you will hit an ``AppRegistryNotReady`` exception."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú fós ag úsáid an chéad stíl i do script WSGI, ní mór duit uasghrádú "
"a dhéanamh go dtí an dara ceann, nó buailfidh tú eisceacht "
"``AppregistryNotready`."

msgid "App registry consistency"
msgstr "Comhsheasmhacht clárlainne aip"

msgid ""
"It is no longer possible to have multiple installed applications with the "
"same label. In previous versions of Django, this didn't always work "
"correctly, but didn't crash outright either."
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir feidhmchláir iolracha suiteáilte a bheith agat leis an lipéad "
"céanna a thuilleadh. I leaganacha roimhe seo de Django, níor oibrigh sé seo "
"i gceart i gcónaí, ach níor thimpiste go díreach ach an oiread."

msgid ""
"If you have two apps with the same label, you should create "
"an :class:`~django.apps.AppConfig` for one of them and override "
"its :class:`~django.apps.AppConfig.label` there. You should then adjust your "
"code wherever it references this application or its models with the old "
"label."
msgstr ""
"Má tá dhá aip agat a bhfuil an lipéad céanna orthu, ba cheart "
"duit :class:`~django.apps.AppConfig` a chruthú le haghaidh ceann amháin acu "
"agus a :rang:`~ django.apps.AppConfig.label` a shárú ann. Ba cheart duit do "
"chód a choigeartú ansin cibé áit a ndéanann sé tagairt don fheidhmchlár seo "
"nó dá mhúnlaí leis an seanlipéad."

msgid ""
"It isn't possible to import the same model twice through different paths any "
"more. As of Django 1.6, this may happen only if you're manually putting a "
"directory and a subdirectory on :envvar:`PYTHONPATH`. Refer to the section "
"on the new project layout in the :doc:`1.4 release notes </releases/1.4>` "
"for migration instructions."
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir an tsamhail chéanna a allmhairiú faoi dhó trí chosáin éagsúla a "
"thuilleadh. Amhail Django 1.6, d'fhéadfadh sé seo tarlú ach amháin má tá tú "
"ag cur eolaire agus fochomhadlann de láimh ar :envvar:`PYTHONPATH`. Déan "
"tagairt don rannán ar leagan amach nua an tionscadail sa :doc:`1.4 nótaí "
"scaoilte </releases/1.4>` le haghaidh treoracha imirce."

msgid "You should make sure that:"
msgstr "Ba chóir duit a chinntiú go bhfuil:"

msgid ""
"All models are defined in applications that are listed "
"in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` or have an "
"explicit :attr:`~django.db.models.Options.app_label`."
msgstr ""
"Sainmhínítear gach samhail in iarratais atá liostaithe in:setting: "
"`INSTALLED_APPS` nó a bhfuil sainmhíniú acu: attr: "
"`~django.db.models.options.app_label`."

msgid ""
"Models aren't imported as a side-effect of loading their application. "
"Specifically, you shouldn't import models in the root module of an "
"application nor in the module that define its configuration class."
msgstr ""
"Ní dhéantar samhlacha a allmhairiú mar fho-iarmhairt dá bhfeidhmchlár a "
"luchtú. Go sonrach, níor cheart duit samhlacha a iompórtáil i modúl fréimhe "
"feidhmchláir ná sa mhodúl a shainmhíníonn a rang cumraíochta."

msgid ""
"Django will enforce these requirements as of version 1.9, after a "
"deprecation period."
msgstr ""
"Déanfaidh Django na ceanglais seo a fhorfheidhmiú amhail leagan 1.9, tar éis "
"tréimhse díscrúdaithe."

msgid "Subclassing AppCommand"
msgstr "Fo-aicmiú AppCommand"

msgid ""
"Subclasses of :class:`~django.core.management.AppCommand` must now implement "
"a :meth:`~django.core.management.AppCommand.handle_app_config` method "
"instead of ``handle_app()``. This method receives "
"an :class:`~django.apps.AppConfig` instance instead of a models module."
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh fo-aicmí de:class: `~django.core.management.appCommand` modh "
"a:meth: `~django.core.management.appCommand.handle_app_config` a chur i "
"bhfeidhm anois in ionad ``handle_app () ``. Faigheann an modh seo sampla: "
"class: `~django.apps.appconfig` in ionad modúl samhlacha."

msgid "Introspecting applications"
msgstr "Feidhmchláir ionbhreathnú"

msgid ""
"Since :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` now supports application configuration "
"classes in addition to application modules, you should review code that "
"accesses this setting directly and use the app registry "
"(:attr:`django.apps.apps`) instead."
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é go dtacaíonn: SETTING: `INSTALLED_APPS` le ranganna cumraíochta "
"feidhmchláir anois i dteannta le modúil feidhmchláir, ba cheart duit "
"athbhreithniú a dhéanamh ar an gcód a fhaigheann rochtain ar an socrú seo go "
"díreach agus clárlann an aipeanna a úsáid (:attr: `django.apps`) ina ionad."

msgid ""
"The app registry has preserved some features of the old app cache. Even "
"though the app cache was a private API, obsolete methods and arguments will "
"be removed through a standard deprecation path, with the exception of the "
"following changes that take effect immediately:"
msgstr ""
"Chaomhnaigh clárlann an aip roinnt gnéithe den tsean-taisce aip. Cé gur API "
"príobháideach a bhí i taisce an aip, bainfear modhanna agus argóintí atá as "
"feidhm trí chosán caighdeánach díghníomhaíochta, seachas na hathruithe seo a "
"leanas a théann i bhfeidhm láithreach:"

msgid ""
"``get_model`` raises :exc:`LookupError` instead of returning ``None`` when "
"no model is found."
msgstr ""
"Ardaíonn ``get_model``: exc: `LookuPerror` in ionad ``None`` a thabhairt ar "
"ais nuair nach bhfaightear aon mhúnla."

msgid ""
"The ``only_installed`` argument of ``get_model`` and ``get_models`` no "
"longer exists, nor does the ``seed_cache`` argument of ``get_model``."
msgstr ""
"Níl an argóint ``only_installled`` de `get_model`` agus ``get_models`` ann a "
"thuilleadh, ná níl an argóint `seed_cache`` de `get_model ``get_model``."

msgid "Management commands and order of :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`"
msgstr "Orduithe bainistíochta agus ordú de:shocrú: `INSTALLED_APPS`"

msgid ""
"When several applications provide management commands with the same name, "
"Django loads the command from the application that comes first "
"in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`. Previous versions loaded the command from the "
"application that came last."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a sholáthraíonn roinnt feidhmchlár orduithe bainistíochta leis an ainm "
"céanna, lódálann Django an t-ordú ón bhfeidhmchlár a thagann den chéad uair "
"i : socrú: `INSTALLED_APPS`. Lódáil leaganacha roimhe seo an t-ordú ón "
"bhfeidhmchlár a tháinig go deireanach."

msgid ""
"This brings discovery of management commands in line with other parts of "
"Django that rely on the order of :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`, such as static "
"files, templates, and translations."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé seo fionnachtain ar orduithe bainistíochta i gcomhréir le codanna "
"eile de Django atá ag brath ar an ord de:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS`, mar "
"shampla comhaid statacha, teimpléid agus aistriúcháin."

msgid "``ValidationError`` constructor and internal storage"
msgstr "Tógálaí agus stóráil inmheánach ``ValidationError``"

msgid ""
"The behavior of the ``ValidationError`` constructor has changed when it "
"receives a container of errors as an argument (e.g. a ``list`` or an "
"``ErrorList``):"
msgstr ""
"Tá athrú tagtha ar iompar an tógálaí `ValidationError`` nuair a fhaigheann "
"sé coimeádán earráidí mar argóint (m.sh. `liosta`` nó ``Liosta`` Error``):"

msgid ""
"It converts any strings it finds to instances of ``ValidationError`` before "
"adding them to its internal storage."
msgstr ""
"Athraíonn sé aon teaghráin a aimsíonn sé go cásanna de ``ValidationError`` "
"sula gcuireann sé iad lena stóráil inmheánach."

msgid ""
"It doesn't store the given container but rather copies its content to its "
"own internal storage; previously the container itself was added to the "
"``ValidationError`` instance and used as internal storage."
msgstr ""
"Ní stóráilíonn sé an coimeádán ar leith ach cóipeálann sé a ábhar chuig a "
"stóráil inmheánach féin; roimhe seo cuireadh an coimeádán féin leis an gcás "
"“ValidationError” agus úsáideadh é mar stóráil inmheánach."

msgid ""
"This means that if you access the ``ValidationError`` internal storages, "
"such as ``error_list``; ``error_dict``; or the return value of "
"``update_error_dict()`` you may find instances of ``ValidationError`` where "
"you would have previously found strings."
msgstr ""
"Ciallaíonn sé seo má rochtain agat ar na stórálaí inmheánacha "
"``ValidationError``, mar shampla ``error_list``; `error_dict``; nó luach "
"tuairisceáin ``update_error_dict () ``, d'fhéadfá cásanna "
"``validationError`` a fháil ina bhfaighidh tú teaghráin roimhe seo."

msgid ""
"Also if you directly assigned the return value of ``update_error_dict()`` to "
"``Form._errors`` you may inadvertently add ``list`` instances where "
"``ErrorList`` instances are expected. This is a problem because unlike a "
"simple ``list``, an ``ErrorList`` knows how to handle instances of "
"``ValidationError``."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith leis sin má shannaigh tú luach tuairisceáin ``update_error_dict "
"() ``go díreach chuig ``Foirm. Féadfaidh tú cásanna ``liosta`` a chur leis "
"go neamhthuiscint ina bhfuiltear ag súil le cásanna ```ErrorList``. Is fadhb "
"í seo mar murab ionann agus ``liosta`` simplí, tá a fhios ag ``ErrorLiost`` "
"conas cásanna de ``ValidationError`` a láimhseáil."

msgid ""
"Most use-cases that warranted using these private APIs are now covered by "
"the newly introduced :meth:`Form.add_error() "
"<django.forms.Form.add_error()>` method::"
msgstr ""
"<django.forms.Form.add_error () >Tá an chuid is mó de na cásanna úsáide a "
"thug ráthas úsáid na APIs príobháideacha seo clúdaithe anois leis an modh "
"nua:meth: `Form.add_error ()::"

msgid ""
"If you need both Django <= 1.6 and 1.7 compatibility you can't "
"use :meth:`Form.add_error() <django.forms.Form.add_error()>` since it wasn't "
"available before Django 1.7, but you can use the following workaround to "
"convert any ``list`` into ``ErrorList``::"
msgstr ""
"Má theastaíonn comhoiriúnacht Django <= 1.6 agus 1.7 uait "
"<django.forms.Form.add_error () > ní féidir leat a úsáid:meth: "
"`Form.add_error (:D) ós rud é nach raibh sé ar fáil roimh Django 1.7, ach is "
"féidir leat an réiteach seo a leanas a úsáid chun aon ``liosta ``a thiontú "
"go ``Liosta Error``:"

msgid "Behavior of ``LocMemCache`` regarding pickle errors"
msgstr "Iompar ``Locmemcache`` maidir le hearráidí picéil"

msgid ""
"An inconsistency existed in previous versions of Django regarding how pickle "
"errors are handled by different cache backends. "
"``django.core.cache.backends.locmem.LocMemCache`` used to fail silently when "
"such an error occurs, which is inconsistent with other backends and leads to "
"cache-specific errors. This has been fixed in Django 1.7, "
"see :ticket:`21200` for more details."
msgstr ""
"Bhí neamhréireacht ann i leaganacha roimhe seo de Django maidir leis an "
"gcaoi a láimhseálann cúltaca taisce éagsúla earráidí picéar. D'úsáid "
"``django.core.cache.backends.locmem.locmemcache`` a theipeann go ciúin nuair "
"a tharlaíonn earráid den sórt sin, rud atá míchomhsheasmhach le cúltaca eile "
"agus mar thoradh air earráidí cache-shonracha. Socraíodh é seo i Django 1.7, "
"féach: ticéad: `21200` le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid "Cache keys are now generated from the request's absolute URL"
msgstr "Gintear eochracha taisce anois ó URL iomlán an iarratais"

msgid ""
"Previous versions of Django generated cache keys using a request's path and "
"query string but not the scheme or host. If a Django application was serving "
"multiple subdomains or domains, cache keys could collide. In Django 1.7, "
"cache keys vary by the absolute URL of the request including scheme, host, "
"path, and query string. For example, the URL portion of a cache key is now "
"generated from ``https://www.example.com/path/to/?key=val`` rather than ``/"
"path/to/?key=val``. The cache keys generated by Django 1.7 will be different "
"from the keys generated by older versions of Django. After upgrading to "
"Django 1.7, the first request to any previously cached URL will be a cache "
"miss."
msgstr ""
"Gin leaganacha roimhe seo d'eochracha taisce Django ag baint úsáide as cosán "
"iarratais agus sreang ceisteanna ach ní an scéim nó an óstach. Dá mbeadh "
"feidhmchlár Django ag freastal ar iolrchuid fofhearann nó fearainn, "
"d'fhéadfadh eochracha taisce imbhualadh I Django 1.7, athraíonn eochracha "
"taisce de réir URL iomlán na hiarratais lena n-áirítear scéim, óstach, cosán "
"agus sreang fiosrúcháin. Mar shampla, gintear an chuid URL d'eochair taisce "
"anois ó ``https://www.example.com/path/to/?key=val`` seachas ```/path/to/? "
"eochair = val ``. Beidh na heochracha taisce a ghineann Django 1.7 difriúil "
"ó na heochracha a ghineann leaganacha níos sine de Django. Tar éis uasghrádú "
"a dhéanamh go Django 1.7, is é an chéad iarratas ar aon URL a chóstáiltear "
"roimhe seo ná cailleadh taisce."

msgid "Passing ``None`` to ``Manager.db_manager()``"
msgstr "Ag dul ``None`` chuig ``Manager.db_Manager () ``"

msgid ""
"In previous versions of Django, it was possible to use "
"``db_manager(using=None)`` on a model manager instance to obtain a manager "
"instance using default routing behavior, overriding any manually specified "
"database routing. In Django 1.7, a value of ``None`` passed to db_manager "
"will produce a router that *retains* any manually assigned database routing "
"-- the manager will *not* be reset. This was necessary to resolve an "
"inconsistency in the way routing information cascaded over joins. "
"See :ticket:`13724` for more details."
msgstr ""
"I leaganacha roimhe seo de Django, bhí sé indéanta ``db_manager (Using = "
"None) ``a úsáid ar shampla bainisteora samhail chun sampla bainisteora a "
"fháil ag baint úsáide as iompar ródaithe réamhshocraithe, ag dul i bhfeidhm "
"ar aon ródú bunachar sonraí sonraithe de láimh. I Django 1.7, táirgfidh "
"luach ``None ``a chuirtear chuig db_manager ródaire a choinníon* aon ródú "
"bunachar sonraí sannta de láimh - ní athshocrófar an bainisteoir*. Bhí sé "
"seo riachtanach chun neamhréireacht a réiteach ar an mbealach a chuaigh "
"faisnéis ródaithe thar chomhpháirtithe. Féach: ticéad: `13724` le haghaidh "
"tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid "``pytz`` may be required"
msgstr "D'fhéadfadh go mbeadh gá le ``pytz``"

msgid ""
"If your project handles datetimes before 1970 or after 2037 and Django "
"raises a :exc:`ValueError` when encountering them, you will have to "
"install :pypi:`pytz`. You may be affected by this problem if you use "
"Django's time zone-related date formats or :mod:`django.contrib.syndication`."
msgstr ""
"Má láimhseálann do thionscadal amanna dáta roimh 1970 nó tar éis 2037 agus "
"má ardaíonn Django a:exc: `ValueError` agus tú ag teacht ar aghaidh orthu, "
"beidh ort: pypi: `pytz` a shuiteáil. D'fhéadfadh go mbeadh tionchar ag an "
"bhfadhb seo ort má úsáideann tú formáidí dáta a bhaineann le crios ama "
"Django nó: mod: `django.contrib.syndication`."

msgid "``remove()`` and ``clear()`` methods of related managers"
msgstr ""
"Modhanna ``bhaint () ``agus ``soiléir ()`` modhanna bainisteoirí gaolmhara"

msgid ""
"The ``remove()`` and ``clear()`` methods of the related managers created by "
"``ForeignKey``, ``GenericForeignKey``, and ``ManyToManyField`` suffered from "
"a number of issues. Some operations ran multiple data modifying queries "
"without wrapping them in a transaction, and some operations didn't respect "
"default filtering when it was present (i.e. when the default manager on the "
"related model implemented a custom ``get_queryset()``)."
msgstr ""
"D'fhulaing roinnt saincheisteanna ar na modhanna ``remove () `agus ``clear "
"() ``na mbainisteoirí gaolmhara a chruthaigh ``ForeignKey``, "
"`GenericForeignKey``, agus ``ManyTomanyField``. Rith roinnt oibríochtaí "
"iolracha ceisteanna modhnaithe sonraí gan iad a fhilleadh in idirbheart, "
"agus níor mheas roinnt oibríochtaí scagadh réamhshocraithe nuair a bhí sé i "
"láthair (ie nuair a chuir an bainisteoir réamhshocraithe ar an tsamhail "
"ghaolmhar saincheaptha ``get_queryset () `i bhfeidhm)."

msgid "Fixing the issues introduced some backward incompatible changes:"
msgstr ""
"Le réiteach na gceisteanna tugadh isteach roinnt athruithe ar gcúl nach "
"raibh comhoiriúnach:"

msgid ""
"The default implementation of ``remove()`` for ``ForeignKey`` related "
"managers changed from a series of ``Model.save()`` calls to a single "
"``QuerySet.update()`` call. The change means that ``pre_save`` and "
"``post_save`` signals aren't sent anymore. You can use the ``bulk=False`` "
"keyword argument to revert to the previous behavior."
msgstr ""
"D'athraigh cur i bhfeidhm réamhshocraithe ``remove () ``do bhainisteoirí "
"gaolmhara ``ForeignKey`` ó shraith glaonna ``Model.save ()`` chuig glao "
"``QuerySet.Update () ``amháin. Ciallaíonn an t-athrú nach seoltar comharthaí "
"``pre_save`` agus ``post_save`` níos mó. Is féidir leat an argóint "
"eochairfhocal ``Bulk=False`` a úsáid chun filleadh ar an iompar roimhe seo."

msgid ""
"The ``remove()`` and ``clear()`` methods for ``GenericForeignKey`` related "
"managers now perform bulk delete. The ``Model.delete()`` method isn't called "
"on each instance anymore. You can use the ``bulk=False`` keyword argument to "
"revert to the previous behavior."
msgstr ""
"Déanann na modhanna ``remove () ``agus ``clear ()`` do bhainisteoirí "
"gaolmhara ``GenericForeignKey`` mór-scriosadh anois. Ní ghlaofar an modh "
"``Model.delete () ``ar gach cás níos mó. Is féidir leat an argóint "
"eochairfhocal ``Bulk=False`` a úsáid chun filleadh ar an iompar roimhe seo."

msgid ""
"The ``remove()`` and ``clear()`` methods for ``ManyToManyField`` related "
"managers perform nested queries when filtering is involved, which may or may "
"not be an issue depending on your database and your data itself. "
"See :ref:`this note <nested-queries-performance>` for more details."
msgstr ""
"Déanann na modhanna ``remove () ``agus ``clear ()`` do bhainisteoirí "
"gaolmhara ``ManyTomanyField`` ceisteanna neadaithe nuair a bhíonn scagadh i "
"gceist, rud a d'fhéadfadh a bheith ina cheist nó nach bhféadfadh a bheith "
"ina cheist ag brath ar do bhunachar sonraí agus do chuid sonraí féin. Féach: "
"Ref: `an nóta seo <nested-queries-performance>`le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid "Admin login redirection strategy"
msgstr "Straitéis atreoraithe logála isteach riaracháin"

msgid ""
"Historically, the Django admin site passed the request from an unauthorized "
"or unauthenticated user directly to the login view, without HTTP "
"redirection. In Django 1.7, this behavior changed to conform to a more "
"traditional workflow where any unauthorized request to an admin page will be "
"redirected (by HTTP status code 302) to the login page, with the ``next`` "
"parameter set to the referring path. The user will be redirected there after "
"a successful login."
msgstr ""
"Go stairiúil, chuir suíomh riaracháin Django an t-iarratas ó úsáideoir "
"neamhúdaraithe nó neamhfhíordheimhnithe go díreach chuig an radharc logála "
"isteach, gan atreorú HTTP. I Django 1.7, d'athraigh an t-iompar seo chun "
"cloí le sreabhadh oibre níos traidisiúnta ina n-atreorófar aon iarratas "
"neamhúdaraithe chuig leathanach riaracháin (trí chód stádais HTTP 302) chuig "
"an leathanach logála isteach, leis an paraiméadar ```next ``socraithe chuig "
"an gcosán tagartha. Déanfar an t-úsáideoir a atreorú ansin tar éis logáil "
"isteach rathúil."

msgid ""
"Note also that the admin login form has been updated to not contain the "
"``this_is_the_login_form`` field (now unused) and the ``ValidationError`` "
"code has been set to the more regular ``invalid_login`` key."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara freisin go bhfuil an fhoirm logála isteach riaracháin "
"nuashonraithe ionas nach bhfuil an réimse ``this_is_the_login_form`` (nach "
"úsáidtear anois) agus go bhfuil an cód ``validationError`` socraithe go dtí "
"an eochair ``invalid_login`` níos rialta."

msgid ""
"This change was made because such errors can be caused by including an app "
"which expects global transactions (e.g. :setting:`ATOMIC_REQUESTS <DATABASE-"
"ATOMIC_REQUESTS>` set to ``True``), or Django's old autocommit behavior, in "
"a project which runs without them; and further, such errors may manifest as "
"data-corruption bugs. It was also made in Django 1.6.3."
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh an t-athrú seo <DATABASE-ATOMIC_REQUESTS>toisc gur féidir earráidí "
"den sórt sin a bheith mar thoradh ar aip a bhfuil súil le hidirbhearta "
"domhanda a áireamh (m.sh.: setting: `ATOMIC_REQUESTS `socraithe go `True``), "
"nó sean-iompar uathoibrithe Django, i dtionscadal a ritheann gan iad; agus "
"ina bhreis, féadfaidh earráidí den sórt sin a léiriú mar fhabhtanna éillithe "
"sonraí. Rinneadh é freisin i Django 1.6.3."

msgid "Contrib middleware removed from default ``MIDDLEWARE_CLASSES``"
msgstr "Contrib middleware bainte ó réamhshocraithe ``MIDDLEWARE_CLASSES``"

msgid ""
"The :ref:`app-loading refactor <app-loading-refactor-17-release-note>` "
"deprecated using models from apps which are not part of "
"the :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` setting. This exposed an incompatibility "
"between the default :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` and ``MIDDLEWARE_CLASSES`` in "
"the global defaults (``django.conf.global_settings``). To bring these "
"settings in sync and prevent deprecation warnings when doing things like "
"testing reusable apps with minimal "
"settings, :class:`~django.contrib.sessions.middleware.SessionMiddleware`, :class:`~django.contrib.auth.middleware.AuthenticationMiddleware`, "
"and :class:`~django.contrib.messages.middleware.MessageMiddleware` were "
"removed from the defaults. These classes will still be included in the "
"default settings generated by :djadmin:`startproject`. Most projects will "
"not be affected by this change but if you were not previously declaring the "
"``MIDDLEWARE_CLASSES`` in your project settings and relying on the global "
"default you should ensure that the new defaults are in line with your "
"project's needs. You should also check for any code that accesses "
"``django.conf.global_settings.MIDDLEWARE_CLASSES`` directly."
msgstr ""
"Díscaoileadh an: Ref: `app loading refactor <app-loading-refactor-17-release-"
"note>`as samhlacha ó aipeanna nach cuid den socrú: setting: "
"`INSTALLED_APPS`. Nocht sé seo neamhoiriúnacht idir an "
"réamhshocraithe:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS` agus ``MIDDLEWARE_CLASSES`` sna "
"réamhshocraithe domhanda (``django.conf.global_settings``). Chun na "
"socruithe seo a shioncronú agus rabhaidh dífhabhtaithe a chosc agus tú ag "
"déanamh rudaí cosúil le feidhmchláir in-athúsáidte a thástáil le socruithe "
"íosta, :class: `~django.contrib.auth.middleware.AuthenticationMiddleware`, "
"agus:class: `~django.contrib.messages.middleware` Baineadh "
"MessageMiddleware` ó na réamhshocruithe. Cuirfear na ranganna seo san "
"áireamh fós sna socruithe réamhshocraithe a ghineann: djadmin: "
"`startproject`. Ní bheidh tionchar ag an athrú seo ar chuid is mó de na "
"tionscadail ach mura raibh tú ag dearbhú roimhe seo an `MIDDLEWARE_CLASSES` "
"i do shuíomhanna tionscadail agus ag brath ar an réamhshocrú domhanda ba "
"cheart duit a chinntiú go bhfuil na réamhshocruithe nua ag teacht le "
"riachtanais do thionscadail. Ba chóir duit seiceáil freisin le haghaidh aon "
"chód a fhaigheann rochtain ar "
"``Django.conf.GLOBAL_settings.middleware_classes`` go díreach."

msgid ""
"The :meth:`django.core.files.uploadhandler.FileUploadHandler.new_file()` "
"method is now passed an additional ``content_type_extra`` parameter. If you "
"have a custom :class:`~django.core.files.uploadhandler.FileUploadHandler` "
"that implements ``new_file()``, be sure it accepts this new parameter."
msgstr ""
"Tá paraiméadar breise ``content_type_extra`` ag an modh:Meth: "
"`django.core.files.uploadhandler.fileUploadHandler.new_file () `. Má tá "
"saincheap:class: `~django.core.files.uploadhandler.fileUploadHandler` agat a "
"chuireann ``new_file () `i bhfeidhm, bí cinnte go nglacann sé leis an "
"bparaiméadar nua seo."

msgid ""
":class:`ModelFormSet<django.forms.models.BaseModelFormSet>`\\s no longer "
"delete instances when ``save(commit=False)`` is called. "
"See :attr:`~django.forms.formsets.BaseFormSet.can_delete` for instructions "
"on how to manually delete objects from deleted forms."
msgstr ""
":class: Ní scriosann `ModelFormSet <django.forms.models.BaseModelFormSet>`\\ "
"s cásanna a thuilleadh nuair a ghlaítear ``save (Commit=false) ``. Féach: "
"attr: `~django.forms.formsets.baseformset.can_delete` le haghaidh treoracha "
"maidir le conas rudaí a scriosadh de láimh ó fhoirmeacha scriosta."

msgid ""
"Loading empty fixtures emits a ``RuntimeWarning`` rather than "
"raising :exc:`~django.core.management.CommandError`."
msgstr ""
"Astaíonn daingneáin folamh ag luchtú ``RuntimeWarning`` seachas ardú: exc: "
"`~Django.Core.Management.CommandError`."

msgid ""
":func:`django.contrib.staticfiles.views.serve` will now raise "
"an :exc:`~django.http.Http404` exception instead "
"of :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ImproperlyConfigured` when :setting:`DEBUG` "
"is ``False``. This change removes the need to conditionally add the view to "
"your root URLconf, which in turn makes it safe to reverse by name. It also "
"removes the ability for visitors to generate spurious HTTP 500 errors by "
"requesting static files that don't exist or haven't been collected yet."
msgstr ""
":func: Ardóidh `django.contrib.staticfiles.views.serve` eisceacht anois:exc: "
"`~django.http.http404` in ionad:exc: "
"`~django.core.exceptions.imProperlyConfigured` nuai:setting: `DEBUG` "
"`False``. Cuireann an t-athrú seo deireadh leis an ngá chun an dearcadh a "
"chur go coinníollach le do fhréamh URLConf, rud a fhágann go bhfuil sé "
"sábháilte aisiompú de réir ainm. Cuireann sé deireadh leis an gcumas do "
"chuairteoirí earráidí HTTP 500 bréige a ghiniúint trí chomhaid statacha nach "
"bhfuil ann nó nár bailíodh fós a iarraidh."

msgid ""
"The :meth:`django.db.models.Model.__eq__` method is now defined in a way "
"where instances of a proxy model and its base model are considered equal "
"when primary keys match. Previously only instances of exact same class were "
"considered equal on primary key match."
msgstr ""
"Sainmhínítear an modh :meth:`django.db.models.Model.__eq__` anois ar "
"bhealach ina mbreathnaítear ar chásanna de shamhail seachfhreastalaí agus a "
"bhunsamhail nuair a mheaitseálann eochracha príomhúla. Roimhe seo níor "
"measadh go raibh ach cásanna den aicme chéanna cruinn cothrom ar "
"eochairmheaitseáil na bunscoile."

msgid ""
"The :meth:`django.db.models.Model.__eq__` method has changed such that two "
"``Model`` instances without primary key values won't be considered equal "
"(unless they are the same instance)."
msgstr ""
"An: Meth: `Django.DB.Models.Model. Tá modh __eq__` athraithe ionas nach "
"measfar dhá chás ``Samhail ``gan príomhluachanna comhionann (mura bhfuil "
"siad an cás céanna)."

msgid ""
"The :meth:`django.db.models.Model.__hash__` method will now raise "
"``TypeError`` when called on an instance without a primary key value. This "
"is done to avoid mutable ``__hash__`` values in containers."
msgstr ""
"An: Meth: `Django.DB.Models.Model. Ardóidh modh __hash__` `TypeError`` anois "
"nuair a ghlaonn sé ar chás gan príomhluach eochair. Déantar é seo chun "
"luachanna ``__hash__`` inathraithe i gcoimeádáin a sheachaint."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.db.models.AutoField` columns in SQLite databases will now be "
"created using the ``AUTOINCREMENT`` option, which guarantees monotonic "
"increments. This will cause primary key numbering behavior to change on "
"SQLite, becoming consistent with most other SQL databases. This will only "
"apply to newly created tables. If you have a database created with an older "
"version of Django, you will need to migrate it to take advantage of this "
"feature. For example, you could do the following:"
msgstr ""
":class: `~Django.db.Models.AutoField` colúin i mbunachair sonraí SQLite a "
"chruthófar anois ag baint úsáide as an rogha ``AUTOINCREMENT``, a ráthaíonn "
"incréimeanna monotónacha. Cuirfidh sé seo faoi deara go n-athróidh iompar "
"uimhriúcháin príomhúil ar SQLite, ag éirí comhsheasmhach leis an gcuid is mó "
"de bhunachar Ní bhainfidh sé seo ach le táblaí nua-chruthaithe. Má tá "
"bunachar sonraí cruthaithe agat le leagan níos sine de Django, beidh ort é a "
"aistriú chun leas a bhaint as an ngné seo. Mar shampla, d'fhéadfá an méid "
"seo a leanas a dhéanamh:"

msgid "Use :djadmin:`dumpdata` to save your data."
msgstr "Úsáid:djaDmin: `dumpdata` chun do chuid sonraí a shábháil."

msgid "Rename the existing database file (keep it as a backup)."
msgstr ""
"Athainmnigh an comhad bunachar sonraí atá ann cheana (coinnigh mar chúltaca "
"é)."

msgid "Run :djadmin:`migrate` to create the updated schema."
msgstr "Run:djaDmin: `imirce` chun an scéim nuashonraithe a chruthú."

msgid "Use :djadmin:`loaddata` to import the fixtures you exported in (1)."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid: DjaDmin: `loaddata` chun na daingneáin a onnmhairigh tú iontu iontu a "
"iompórtáil (1)."

msgid ""
"``django.contrib.auth.models.AbstractUser`` no longer defines "
"a :meth:`~django.db.models.Model.get_absolute_url()` method. The old "
"definition returned  ``\"/users/%s/\" % urlquote(self.username)`` which was "
"arbitrary since applications may or may not define such a url in "
"``urlpatterns``. Define a ``get_absolute_url()`` method on your own custom "
"user object or use :setting:`ABSOLUTE_URL_OVERRIDES` if you want a URL for "
"your user."
msgstr ""
"``Django.Contrib.Auth.Models.AbstractUser`` ní shainmhíníonn a:meth a "
"thuilleadh: `~django.db.models.model.get_absolute_url () `modh. D'fhill an "
"sean-sainmhíniú ``” /users/%s/”% urlquote (self.username)`` a bhí treallach "
"ós rud é go bhféadfadh feidhmchláir url den sórt sin a shainiú in "
"`urlpatterns`` nó nach bhféadfadh iarratais. Sainmhínigh modh "
"``get_absolute_url () ``ar do réad úsáideora saincheaptha féin nó "
"úsáide:setting: `ABSOLUTE_URL_OVERRIDES` más mian leat URL d'úsáideoir."

msgid ""
"The static asset-serving functionality of "
"the :class:`django.test.LiveServerTestCase` class has been simplified: Now "
"it's only able to serve content already present in :setting:`STATIC_ROOT` "
"when tests are run. The ability to transparently serve all the static assets "
"(similarly to what one gets with :setting:`DEBUG = True <DEBUG>` at "
"development-time) has been moved to a new class that lives in the "
"``staticfiles`` application (the one actually in charge of such "
"feature): :class:`django.contrib.staticfiles.testing.StaticLiveServerTestCase`. "
"In other words, ``LiveServerTestCase`` itself is less powerful but at the "
"same time has less magic."
msgstr ""
"Tá feidhmiúlacht statach ag freastal sócmhainní an ranga:class: "
"`django.test.liveservertestcase` simplithe: Anois níl sé in ann ach ábhar "
"atá i láthair cheana féin a sheirbheáil in:setting: `STATIC_ROOT` nuair a "
"reáchtáiltear tástálacha. Tá an cumas chun na sócmhainní statacha go léir a "
"sheirbheáil go trédhearcach (cosú <DEBUG>il leis an méid a fhaigheann duine "
"leis: socrú: `DEBUG = True `ag am forbartha) chuig rang nua a chónaíonn san "
"fheidhmchlár `staticfiles` (an ceann atá i ndáiríre i gceannas ar an ngné "
"den sórt sin): :class: "
"`django.contrib.staticfiles.testing.clistativeServertestcase`. Is é sin le "
"rá, tá ``Liveservertestcase ``féin chomh cumhachtach ach ag an am céanna tá "
"níos lú draíochta aige."

msgid ""
"Rationale behind this is removal of dependency of non-contrib code on "
"contrib applications."
msgstr ""
"Is é an réasúnaíocht atá taobh thiar de seo ná spleáchas ar chód neamh-"
"contrib a bhaint ar iarratais contrib."

msgid ""
"The old cache URI syntax (e.g. ``\"locmem://\"``) is no longer supported. It "
"still worked, even though it was not documented or officially supported. If "
"you're still using it, please update to the current :setting:`CACHES` syntax."
msgstr ""
"Ní thacaítear leis an sean-chomhréir URI taisce (m.sh. ``\"locmem: //\"``) a "
"thuilleadh. D'oibrigh sé fós, cé nár doiciméadaíodh nó nár thacaíodh leis go "
"hoifigiúil. Má tá tú fós á úsáid agat, nuashonraigh an chomhréir reatha: "
"setting: `CACHES` le do thoil."

msgid ""
"The default ordering of ``Form`` fields in case of inheritance has changed "
"to follow normal Python MRO. Fields are now discovered by iterating through "
"the MRO in reverse with the topmost class coming last. This only affects you "
"if you relied on the default field ordering while having fields defined on "
"both the current class *and* on a parent ``Form``."
msgstr ""
"Tá athrú tagtha ar ordú réamhshocraithe réimsí ``Foirm`` i gcás oidhreachta "
"chun gnáth-MRO Python a leanúint. Aimsítear réimsí anois trí athrá tríd an "
"MRO ar ais agus an rang is barr ag teacht go deireanach. Níl tionchar aige "
"seo ort ach amháin má bhraith tú ar ordú réamhshocraithe an réimse agus "
"réimsí sainmhínithe agat ar an aicme reatha* agus* araon ar thuismitheoir "
"`Foirm ``."

msgid ""
"The ``required`` argument of :class:`~django.forms.SelectDateWidget` has "
"been removed. This widget now respects the form field's ``is_required`` "
"attribute like other widgets."
msgstr ""
"Baineadh an argóint ``riachtan`` de:class: `~django.forms.selectDateWidget`. "
"Déanann an giuirléid seo meas anois ar thréith ``is_required`` réimse an "
"fhoirme cosúil le giuirléidí eile."

msgid ""
"``Widget.is_hidden`` is now a read-only property, getting its value by "
"introspecting the presence of ``input_type == 'hidden'``."
msgstr ""
"Is maoin léite amháin é ``Widget.is_Hidden`` anois, ag fáil a luach trí "
"input_type == 'hidden'` a fheiceáil ar láithreacht ``input_type == 'hidden'`."

msgid ""
":meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.select_related` now chains in the "
"same way as other similar calls like ``prefetch_related``. That is, "
"``select_related('foo', 'bar')`` is equivalent to "
"``select_related('foo').select_related('bar')``. Previously the latter would "
"have been equivalent to ``select_related('bar')``."
msgstr ""
":meth: `~django.db.models.query.queryset.select_related` slabhraíonn anois "
"ar an mbealach céanna le glaonna cosúla eile cosúil le `prefetch_related``. "
"Is é sin, tá ``select_related ('foo', 'bar') ``comhionann le "
"``select_related ('foo') .select_related ('bar')``. Roimhe seo bheadh an "
"dara ceann comhionann le ``select_related ('bar') ``."

msgid "GeoDjango dropped support for GEOS < 3.1."
msgstr "Thit GeodJango tacaíocht do GEOS <3.1."

msgid ""
"The ``init_connection_state`` method of database backends now executes in "
"autocommit mode (unless you set :setting:`AUTOCOMMIT <DATABASE-AUTOCOMMIT>` "
"to ``False``). If you maintain a custom database backend, you should check "
"that method."
msgstr ""
"<DATABASE-AUTOCOMMIT>Cuirtear an modh `init_connection_state`` de "
"chúlchúlachtaí bunachar sonraí i mód autocommit anois (mura socraíonn tú: "
"`AUTOCOMMIT `go `False``). Má choinníonn tú cúltaca bunachar sonraí "
"saincheaptha, ba cheart duit an modh sin a sheiceáil."

msgid ""
"The ``django.db.backends.BaseDatabaseFeatures.allows_primary_key_0`` "
"attribute has been renamed to ``allows_auto_pk_0`` to better describe it. "
"It's ``True`` for all database backends included with Django except MySQL "
"which does allow primary keys with value 0. It only forbids *autoincrement* "
"primary keys with value 0."
msgstr ""
"Athainmníodh an tréith "
"``Django.db.backends.basedatabaseFeatures.allows_primary_key_0`` go "
"``allows_auto_pk_0`` chun cur síos níos fearr air. Is “True” é do gach "
"cúltaca bunachar sonraí atá san áireamh le Django seachas MySQL a cheadaíonn "
"eochracha bunscoile le luach 0. Ní chuireann sé cosc ach eochracha "
"príomhúla* autoincrement* le luach 0."

msgid ""
"Shadowing model fields defined in a parent model has been forbidden as this "
"creates ambiguity in the expected model behavior. In addition, clashing "
"fields in the model inheritance hierarchy result in a system check error. "
"For example, if you use multi-inheritance, you need to define custom primary "
"key fields on parent models, otherwise the default ``id`` fields will clash. "
"See :ref:`model-multiple-inheritance-topic` for details."
msgstr ""
"Tá cosc curtha ar réimsí samhail a shainmhínítear i samhail tuismitheora "
"toisc go gcruthaíonn sé seo débhríocht in iompar an tsamhail a Ina theannta "
"sin, bíonn earráid seiceála córais mar thoradh ar réimsí comhraic san "
"ordlathas oidhreachta samhail. Mar shampla, má úsáideann tú iloidhreacht, ní "
"mór duit príomhréimsí saincheaptha bunscoile a shainiú ar mhúnlaí "
"tuismitheoirí, ar shlí eile beidh na réimsí réamhshocraithe ``id ``ag teacht "
"isteach. Féach:ref: `model-multiple-oidhreance-topic` le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid ""
"``django.utils.translation.parse_accept_lang_header()`` now returns "
"lowercase locales, instead of the case as it was provided. As locales should "
"be treated case-insensitive this allows us to speed up locale detection."
msgstr ""
"Filleann ``django.utils.translation.parse_accept_lang_header () ``áiteanna "
"litreacha beaga anois, in ionad an cás mar a cuireadh ar fáil é. Toisc gur "
"chóir cóireáil le háiteanna neamh-íogair, tugann sé seo deis dúinn brath "
"áitiúil a bhrostú."

msgid ""
"``django.utils.translation.get_language_from_path()`` and "
"``django.utils.translation.trans_real.get_supported_language_variant()`` now "
"no longer have a ``supported`` argument."
msgstr ""
"``django.utils.translation.get_language_from_path () ``agus "
"``django.utils.translation.trans_real.get_supported_language_variant ()`` "
"anois níl argóint ``tacaithe ``a thuilleadh."

msgid ""
"The ``shortcut`` view in ``django.contrib.contenttypes.views`` now supports "
"protocol-relative URLs (e.g. ``//example.com``)."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn an radharc ``shortcut`` i `django.contrib.contenttypes.views`` "
"anois le URLanna coibhneasta le prótacail (m.sh. ``//example.com``)."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.contrib.contenttypes.fields.GenericRelation` now supports an "
"optional ``related_query_name`` argument. Setting ``related_query_name`` "
"adds a relation from the related object back to the content type for "
"filtering, ordering and other query operations."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.contrib.contentTypes.Fields.GenericRelation` tacaíonn anois "
"le argóint roghnach ``related_query_name``. Cuireann socrú "
"``related_query_name`` gaol ón réad gaolmhar ar ais leis an gcineál ábhair "
"le haghaidh scagadh, ordú agus oibríochtaí fiosrúcháin eile."

msgid ""
"When running tests on PostgreSQL, the :setting:`USER` will need read access "
"to the built-in ``postgres`` database. This is in lieu of the previous "
"behavior of connecting to the actual non-test database."
msgstr ""
"Agus tástálacha á reáchtáil ar PostgreSQL, beidh rochtain léite ag teastáil "
"uir:setting: `USER` ar an mbunachar sonraí `postgres` ionsuite. Tá sé seo in "
"ionad an iompar roimhe seo maidir le nascadh leis an mbunachar sonraí neamh-"
"thástála iarbhír."

msgid ""
"As part of the :doc:`System check framework </ref/checks>`, :ref:`fields, "
"models, and model managers <field-checking>` all implement a ``check()`` "
"method that is registered with the check framework. If you have an existing "
"method called ``check()`` on one of these objects, you will need to rename "
"it."
msgstr ""
"Mar chuid den chreat seiceála córas:doc: ``, :ref: `réim</ref/checks> sí, "
"samhlacha agus bainisteoirí samhlacha `cuireann gach duine modh ``check "
"<field-checking>()`` cláraithe leis an gcreat seiceála i bhfeidhm. Má tá "
"modh ann cheana agat ar a dtugtar ``check () ``ar cheann de na rudaí seo, "
"beidh ort é a athainmniú."

msgid ""
"As noted above in the \"Cache\" section of \"Minor Features\", defining "
"the :setting:`TIMEOUT <CACHES-TIMEOUT>` argument of the :setting:`CACHES` "
"setting as ``None`` will set the cache keys as \"non-expiring\". Previously, "
"with the memcache backend, a :setting:`TIMEOUT <CACHES-TIMEOUT>` of ``0`` "
"would set non-expiring keys, but this was inconsistent with the set-and-"
"expire (i.e. no caching) behavior of ``set(\"key\", \"value\", timeout=0)``. "
"If you want non-expiring keys, please update your settings to use ``None`` "
"instead of ``0`` as the latter now designates set-and-expire in the settings "
"as well."
msgstr ""
"Mar a luadh thuas sa chuid “Cache” de “Mionghnéithe”, ag sainmhíniú argóint: "
"socrú: `TIMEOUT `den socrú:` <CACHES-TIMEOUT>CACHES` mar ``None`` socraítear "
"na heochracha taisce mar “neamh-éag”. Roimhe seo, leis an gcúltaca memcache, "
"socraíodh a: socrú: `TIMEOUT <CACHES-TIMEOUT>`de `0`` eochracha neamh-éag, "
"ach bhí sé seo neamhréidh le hiompar socraithe agus éag (ie gan aon "
"chaching) ``set (“key”, “value”, timeout = 0) ``. Más mian leat eochracha "
"nach bhfuil in éag, nuashonraigh do shocruithe le do thoil chun ``None ``a "
"úsáid in ionad ``0`` mar a ainmníonn an dara ceann anois socraithe agus éag "
"sna socruithe freisin."

msgid ""
"The ``sql*`` management commands now respect the ``allow_migrate()`` method "
"of :setting:`DATABASE_ROUTERS`. If you have models synced to non-default "
"databases, use the ``--database`` flag to get SQL for those models "
"(previously they would always be included in the output)."
msgstr ""
"Tá meas anois ag na horduithe bainistíochta `sql*`` an modh `allow_migration "
"() ``de:setting: `DATABASE_ROUTERS`. Má tá samhlacha agat sioncronaithe le "
"bunachair sonraí neamh-réamhshocraithe, bain úsáid as an bhratach ``--"
"bunachar sonraí ``chun SQL a fháil do na samhlacha sin (roimhe seo bheadh "
"siad san áireamh san aschur i gcónaí)."

msgid ""
"Decoding the query string from URLs now falls back to the ISO-8859-1 "
"encoding when the input is not valid UTF-8."
msgstr ""
"Titeann díchódú an teaghrán fiosrúcháin ó URLanna anois ar ais chuig an "
"ionchódú ISO-8859-1 nuair nach bhfuil an t-ionchur bailí UTF-8."

msgid ""
"With the addition of the "
"``django.contrib.auth.middleware.SessionAuthenticationMiddleware`` to the "
"default project template (pre-1.7.2 only), a database must be created before "
"accessing a page using :djadmin:`runserver`."
msgstr ""
"Leis an `django.contrib.auth.middleware.sessionAuthenticationMiddleware`` a "
"chur leis an teimpléad réamhshocraithe tionscadail (réamh-1.7.2 amháin), ní "
"mór bunachar sonraí a chruthú sula bhfaightear rochtain ar leathanach ag "
"baint úsáidea:djadmin: `runserver`."

msgid ""
"The addition of the ``schemes`` argument to ``URLValidator`` will appear as "
"a backwards-incompatible change if you were previously using a custom "
"regular expression to validate schemes. Any scheme not listed in ``schemes`` "
"will fail validation, even if the regular expression matches the given URL."
msgstr ""
"Beidh an argóint ``scéimeanna ``a chur le `URLValidator`` le feiceáil mar "
"athrú neamh-chomhoiriúnach le cúl má bhí tú ag úsáid abairt rialta "
"saincheaptha roimhe seo chun scéimeanna a bhailíochtú. Teipfidh ar aon scéim "
"nach bhfuil liostaithe i “scéimeanna” bailíochtú, fiú má mheaitseálann an "
"abairt rialta leis an URL a thugtar."

msgid "Features deprecated in 1.7"
msgstr "Gnéithe atá díscríofa i 1.7"

msgid "``django.core.cache.get_cache``"
msgstr "``django.core.cache.get_cache``"

msgid ""
"``django.core.cache.get_cache`` has been supplanted "
"by :data:`django.core.cache.caches`."
msgstr ""
"Tá ``django.core.cache.get_cache`` curtha in ionad ag: data: "
"`django.core.cache.caches`."

msgid "``django.utils.dictconfig``/``django.utils.importlib``"
msgstr "``django.utils.dictconfig``/``django.utils.importlib``"

msgid ""
"``django.utils.dictconfig`` and ``django.utils.importlib`` were copies of "
"respectively :mod:`logging.config` and :mod:`importlib` provided for Python "
"versions prior to 2.7. They have been deprecated."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóipeanna iad ``django.utils.dictconfig`` agus "
"``django.utils.importlib`` cóipeanna de réir seach:mod: `logging.config` "
"agus:mod: `importlib` a chuirtear ar fáil do leaganacha Python roimh 2.7. Tá "
"siad díscríofa."

msgid "``django.utils.module_loading.import_by_path``"
msgstr "``django.utils.module_loading.import_by_path``"

msgid ""
"The current ``django.utils.module_loading.import_by_path`` function catches "
"``AttributeError``, ``ImportError``, and ``ValueError`` exceptions, and re-"
"raises :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ImproperlyConfigured`. Such exception "
"masking makes it needlessly hard to diagnose circular import problems, "
"because it makes it look like the problem comes from inside Django. It has "
"been deprecated in favor "
"of :meth:`~django.utils.module_loading.import_string`."
msgstr ""
"Gabhann an fheidhm reatha ``django.utils.module_loading.import_by_path`` "
"eisceachtaí ``AttributeError``, `ImportError``, agus ``ValueError``, agus "
"athardaíonn sé: exc: `~Django.Core.Exceptions.imProperlyConfigured`. De "
"bharr mascáil eisceachta den sórt sin tá sé deacair gan ghá fadhbanna "
"iompórtála ciorclach a dhiagnóisiú, toisc go dtugann sé cuma go dtagann an "
"fhadhb ón taobh Tá sé curtha i bhfabhar: meth: "
"`~django.utils.module_loading.import_string`."

msgid "``django.utils.tzinfo``"
msgstr "``django.utils.tzinfo``"

msgid ""
"``django.utils.tzinfo`` provided two :class:`~datetime.tzinfo` subclasses, "
"``LocalTimezone`` and ``FixedOffset``. They've been deprecated in favor of "
"more correct alternatives provided "
"by :mod:`django.utils.timezone`, :func:`django.utils.timezone.get_default_timezone` "
"and :func:`django.utils.timezone.get_fixed_timezone`."
msgstr ""
"Chuir ``django.utils.tzinfo`` dhá fho-aicme: `~datetime.tzinfo` ar fáil, "
"``LocalTimeZone`` agus ``FixedOffset``. Tá siad curtha i bhfabhar roghanna "
"níos cearta a sholáthraí:mod: `django.utils.timezone`, :func: "
"`django.utils.timezone.get_default_timezone` agus:func: "
"`django.utils.timezone.get_fixed_timezone`."

msgid "``django.utils.unittest``"
msgstr "``django.utils.unittest``"

msgid ""
"``django.utils.unittest`` provided uniform access to the ``unittest2`` "
"library on all Python versions. Since ``unittest2`` became the standard "
"library's :mod:`unittest` module in Python 2.7, and Django 1.7 drops support "
"for older Python versions, this module isn't useful anymore. It has been "
"deprecated. Use :mod:`unittest` instead."
msgstr ""
"Chuir ``django.utils.unittest`` rochtain aonfhoirmeach ar an leabharlann "
"``unittest2`` ar gach leagan Python. Ós rud é gur tháinig `unittest2`` mar "
"modúl caighdeánach leabharlainne: mod: `unittest` i Python 2.7, agus go "
"dtiteann Django 1.7 tacaíocht do leaganacha Python níos sine, níl an modúl "
"seo úsáideach níos mó. Tá sé díscríofa. Úsáid: MOD: `unittest` ina ionad."

msgid "``django.utils.datastructures.SortedDict``"
msgstr "``Django.utils.DataStructures.Sorteddict``"

msgid ""
"As :class:`~collections.OrderedDict` was added to the standard library in "
"Python 2.7, ``SortedDict`` is no longer needed and has been deprecated."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh `~Collections.OrderedDict` as:Class: `~Collections.OrderedDict` "
"leis an leabharlann caighdeánach i Python 2.7, níl ``SortedDict`` ag "
"teastáil a thuilleadh agus tá sé díscoite."

msgid ""
"The two additional, deprecated methods provided by ``SortedDict`` "
"(``insert()`` and ``value_for_index()``) have been removed. If you relied on "
"these methods to alter structures like form fields, you should now treat "
"these ``OrderedDict``\\s as immutable objects and override them to change "
"their content."
msgstr ""
"Baineadh an dá mhodh breise, dlús a sholáthraíonn ``Sorteddict`` (``insert "
"() ``agus ``value_for_index ()``). Má bhí tú ag brath ar na modhanna seo "
"chun struchtúir cosúil le réimsí foirme a athrú, ba cheart duit anois na "
"`OrderedDict' seo a chóireáil mar rudaí do-athraithe agus iad a athrú chun a "
"n-ábhar a athrú."

msgid ""
"For example, you might want to override ``MyFormClass.base_fields`` "
"(although this attribute isn't considered a public API) to change the "
"ordering of fields for all ``MyFormClass`` instances; or similarly, you "
"could override ``self.fields`` from inside ``MyFormClass.__init__()``, to "
"change the fields for a particular form instance. For example (from Django "
"itself)::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat `MyFormClass.base_Fields`` a athrú "
"(cé nach meastar gur API poiblí an tréith seo) chun ordú réimsí do gach cás "
"``MyFormClass`` a athrú; nó ar an gcaoi chéanna, d'fhéadfá ``self.fields`` a "
"shárú ón taobh istigh de `MyFormClass. __init__ () ``, chun na réimsí a "
"athrú le haghaidh foirm áirithe. Mar shampla (ó Django féin):"

msgid "Custom SQL location for models package"
msgstr "Suíomh saincheaptha SQL do phacáiste samhlacha"

msgid ""
"Previously, if models were organized in a package (``myapp/models/``) rather "
"than simply ``myapp/models.py``, Django would look for initial SQL data in "
"``myapp/models/sql/``. This bug has been fixed so that Django will search "
"``myapp/sql/`` as documented. After this issue was fixed, migrations were "
"added which deprecates initial SQL data. Thus, while this change still "
"exists, the deprecation is irrelevant as the entire feature will be removed "
"in Django 1.9."
msgstr ""
"Roimhe seo, dá mbeadh samhlacha eagraithe i bpacáiste (``myapp/models/``) "
"seachas ``myapp/models.py``, chuardódh Django sonraí tosaigh SQL i ``myapp/"
"models/sql/``. Socraíodh an fabht seo ionas go ndéanfaidh Django cuardach ar "
"``myapp/sql/`` mar a dhoiciméadaithe. Tar éis an tsaincheist seo a shocrú, "
"cuireadh imirce leis a dhíspreagann sonraí tosaigh SQL. Dá bhrí sin, cé go "
"bhfuil an t-athrú seo ann fós, níl an diúltú neamhábhachtach mar bainfear an "
"ghné iomlán i Django 1.9."

msgid "Reorganization of ``django.contrib.sites``"
msgstr "Athfhoirmiú ``django.contrib.sites``"

msgid ""
"``django.contrib.sites`` provides reduced functionality when it isn't "
"in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`. The app-loading refactor adds some constraints "
"in that situation. As a consequence, two objects were moved, and the old "
"locations are deprecated:"
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn ``django.contrib.sites`` feidhmiúlacht laghdaithe nuair nach "
"bhfuil sé in:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS`. Cuireann an t-athfhachtóir "
"luchtaithe aip roinnt srianta sa chás sin. Mar thoradh air sin, bogadh dhá "
"réad, agus tá na sean-áiteanna measartha:"

msgid ""
":class:`~django.contrib.sites.requests.RequestSite` now lives in "
"``django.contrib.sites.requests``."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.contrib.sites.requests.requestsite` anois ina chónaí i "
"``django.contrib.sites.requests``."

msgid ""
":func:`~django.contrib.sites.shortcuts.get_current_site` now lives in "
"``django.contrib.sites.shortcuts``."
msgstr ""
":func: `~django.contrib.sites.shortcuts.get_current_site` ina chónaí anois i "
"``django.contrib.sites.shortcuts``."

msgid "``declared_fieldsets`` attribute on ``ModelAdmin``"
msgstr "Tréith ``declared_fieldsets`` ar `ModelAdmin``"

msgid ""
"``ModelAdmin.declared_fieldsets`` has been deprecated. Despite being a "
"private API, it will go through a regular deprecation path. This attribute "
"was mostly used by methods that bypassed ``ModelAdmin.get_fieldsets()`` but "
"this was considered a bug and has been addressed."
msgstr ""
"Tá ``ModelAdmin.Declared_FieldSets`` imithe. In ainneoin gur API "
"príobháideach é, rachaidh sé trí chosán diúltaithe rialta. Baineadh úsáid as "
"an tréith seo den chuid is mó trí mhodhanna a sheachain "
"``ModelAdmin.get_FieldSets () ``ach meastar gur fabht é seo agus tugadh "
"aghaidh air."

msgid "Reorganization of ``django.contrib.contenttypes``"
msgstr "Athfhoirmiú ``django.contrib.contenttypes``"

msgid ""
"Since ``django.contrib.contenttypes.generic`` defined both admin and model "
"related objects, an import of this module could trigger unexpected side "
"effects. As a consequence, its contents were split "
"into :mod:`~django.contrib.contenttypes` submodules and the "
"``django.contrib.contenttypes.generic`` module is deprecated:"
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é go sainmhíníodh ``django.contrib.contenttypes.generic`` rudaí a "
"bhaineann le riarachán agus samhail araon, d'fhéadfadh allmhairiú an mhodúil "
"seo fo-iarsmaí gan choinne a spreagadh. Mar thoradh air sin, roinníodh a "
"ábhar go fo-mhodúil: mod: `~django.contrib.contenttypes` agus tá an modúl "
"``django.contrib.contenttypes.generic`` díluaite:"

msgid ""
":class:`~django.contrib.contenttypes.fields.GenericForeignKey` "
"and :class:`~django.contrib.contenttypes.fields.GenericRelation` now live "
"in :mod:`~django.contrib.contenttypes.fields`."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.contrib.contentTypes.Fields.GenericForeignKey` agus:class: "
"`~django.contrib.contentTypes.Fields.GenericRelation` anois ina gcónaí "
"in:mod: `~django.contrib.contenttypes.fields`."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.contrib.contenttypes.forms.BaseGenericInlineFormSet` "
"and :func:`~django.contrib.contenttypes.forms.generic_inlineformset_factory` "
"now live in :mod:`~django.contrib.contenttypes.forms`."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.contrib.contenttypes.forms.baseGenericInlineFormSet` "
"agus:func: "
"`~django.contrib.contenttypes.forms.generic_inlineformset_factory` anois beo "
"in:mod: `~django.contrib.contenttypes.forms`."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.contrib.contenttypes.admin.GenericInlineModelAdmin`, :class:`~django.contrib.contenttypes.admin.GenericStackedInline` "
"and :class:`~django.contrib.contenttypes.admin.GenericTabularInline` now "
"live in :mod:`~django.contrib.contenttypes.admin`."
msgstr ""
":class: "
"`~django.contrib.contentTypes.admin.GenericInlineModelAdmin`, :class: "
"`~django.contrib.contentTypes.admin.GenericStackedInline` agus:class: "
"`~django.contrib.contentTypes.admin.GenericTabularIn` anois beo in:mod: "
"`~django.contrib.contentcineálach.admin”."

msgid "``syncdb``"
msgstr "``Syncdb``"

msgid ""
"The ``syncdb`` command has been deprecated in favor of the "
"new :djadmin:`migrate` command. ``migrate`` takes the same arguments as "
"``syncdb`` used to plus a few more, so it's safe to just change the name "
"you're calling and nothing else."
msgstr ""
"Tá an t-ordú ``syncdb`` díluaite i bhfabhar an ordaithe nua:djadmin: "
"`migrate`. Glacann ``migrate`` na hargóintí céanna le ``syncdb`` a úsáidtear "
"chun cúpla ceann eile, mar sin tá sé sábháilte an t-ainm atá á ghlaoch agat "
"a athrú agus rud ar bith eile."

msgid "``util`` modules renamed to ``utils``"
msgstr "Athainmníodh modúil ``util`` go ``utils``"

msgid ""
"The following instances of ``util.py`` in the Django codebase have been "
"renamed to ``utils.py`` in an effort to unify all util and utils references:"
msgstr ""
"Athainmníodh na cásanna seo a leanas de `util.py`` sa chód-bhunachar Django "
"go ``utils.py`` in iarracht gach tagairt util agus utils a aontú:"

msgid "``django.contrib.admin.util``"
msgstr "``django.contrib.admin.util``"

msgid "``django.contrib.gis.db.backends.util``"
msgstr "``django.contrib.gis.db.backends.util``"

msgid "``django.db.backends.util``"
msgstr "``django.db.backends.util``"

msgid "``django.forms.util``"
msgstr "``django.forms.util``"

msgid "``get_formsets`` method on ``ModelAdmin``"
msgstr "Modh ``get_formsets`` ar `ModelAdmin``"

msgid ""
"``ModelAdmin.get_formsets`` has been deprecated in favor of the "
"new :meth:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.get_formsets_with_inlines`, in "
"order to better handle the case of selectively showing inlines on a "
"``ModelAdmin``."
msgstr ""
"Tá `ModelAdmin.get_FormSets`` curtha i bhfabhar an nua:meth: "
"`~django.contrib.admin.modeladmin.get_formsets_with_inlines`, d'fhonn "
"láimhseáil níos fearr an cás a bhaineann le línte a thaispeáint go roghnach "
"ar `ModelAdmin``."

msgid ""
"The ``django.db.models.IPAddressField`` and ``django.forms.IPAddressField`` "
"fields have been deprecated in favor "
"of :class:`django.db.models.GenericIPAddressField` "
"and :class:`django.forms.GenericIPAddressField`."
msgstr ""
"Tá na réimsí ``Django.db.Models.iPaddressField`` agus "
"``Django.Forms.iPaddressField`` curtha i bhfabhr:class: "
"`Django.db.Models.GenericipAddressField` agus:class: "
"`Django.Forms.GenericipAddressField`."

msgid "``BaseMemcachedCache._get_memcache_timeout`` method"
msgstr "``BaseMemcachedCache. Modh _get_memcache_timeout``"

msgid ""
"The ``BaseMemcachedCache._get_memcache_timeout()`` method has been renamed "
"to ``get_backend_timeout()``. Despite being a private API, it will go "
"through the normal deprecation."
msgstr ""
"An ``BaseMemcachedCache. Athainmníodh modh _get_memcache_timeout () ``go "
"`get_backend_timeout ()``. In ainneoin gur API príobháideach é, rachaidh sé "
"tríd an ngnáthdháileadh."

msgid "Natural key serialization options"
msgstr "Príomhroghanna sraith nádúrtha"

msgid ""
"The ``--natural`` and ``-n`` options for :djadmin:`dumpdata` have been "
"deprecated. Use :option:`dumpdata --natural-foreign` instead."
msgstr ""
"Tá na roghanna ``--natural`` agus ``-n`` le haghaidh: djadmin: `dumpdata` "
"curtha as. Úsáid: rogha: `dumpdata --natural-foreign` ina ionad."

msgid ""
"Similarly, the ``use_natural_keys`` argument for ``serializers.serialize()`` "
"has been deprecated. Use ``use_natural_foreign_keys`` instead."
msgstr ""
"Ar an gcaoi chéanna, tá an argóint ``use_natural_keys`` do "
"`serializers.serialize () ``díluaite. Úsáid ``use_natural_foreign_keys`` ina "
"ionad."

msgid "Merging of ``POST`` and ``GET`` arguments into ``WSGIRequest.REQUEST``"
msgstr "Argóintí ``POST ``agus `GET`` a chumasc i ``WSGIrequest.request``"

msgid ""
"It was already strongly suggested that you use ``GET`` and ``POST`` instead "
"of ``REQUEST``, because the former are more explicit. The property "
"``REQUEST`` is deprecated and will be removed in Django 1.9."
msgstr ""
"Moladh go láidir cheana féin go n-úsáideann tú ``GET`` agus `POST ````POST`` "
"in ionad ``REQUEST``, toisc go bhfuil an chéad cheann níos soiléire. Tá an "
"maoin ``IARRAIDH ``díluachtaithe agus bainfear í i Django 1.9."

msgid "``django.utils.datastructures.MergeDict`` class"
msgstr "Aicme ``Django.Utils.DataStructures.Mergedict``"

msgid ""
"``MergeDict`` exists primarily to support merging ``POST`` and ``GET`` "
"arguments into a ``REQUEST`` property on ``WSGIRequest``. To merge "
"dictionaries, use ``dict.update()`` instead. The class ``MergeDict`` is "
"deprecated and will be removed in Django 1.9."
msgstr ""
"Tá ``Mergedict`` ann go príomha chun tacú le hargóintí `POST ``agus `GET`` a "
"chumasc i maoin ``REQUEST`` ar `WSGIREQUEST``. Chun foclóirí a chumasc, bain "
"úsáid as ``dict.update () ``ina ionad. Tá an rang ``Mergedict`` díluaite "
"agus bainfear é i Django 1.9."

msgid "Language codes ``zh-cn``, ``zh-tw`` and ``fy-nl``"
msgstr "Cóid teanga ``zh-cn``, `zh-tw`` agus ``fy-nl``"

msgid ""
"The currently used language codes for Simplified Chinese ``zh-cn``, "
"Traditional Chinese ``zh-tw`` and (Western) Frysian ``fy-nl`` are deprecated "
"and should be replaced by the language codes ``zh-hans``, ``zh-hant`` and "
"``fy`` respectively. If you use these language codes, you should rename the "
"locale directories and update your settings to reflect these changes. The "
"deprecated language codes will be removed in Django 1.9."
msgstr ""
"Tá na cóid teanga a úsáidtear faoi láthair do Sínis Simplithe ``zh-cn``, "
"Sínis Traidisiúnta ``zh-tw`` agus (Iarthar) Fríseach ``fy-nl`` a chur in "
"ionad agus ba chóir na cóid teanga `zh-hans``, `zh-hant`` agus ``fy`` faoi "
"seach iad. Má úsáideann tú na cóid teanga seo, ba cheart duit na heolairí "
"áitiúla a athainmniú agus do shocruithe a nuashonrú chun na hathruithe seo a "
"léiriú Bainfear na cóid teanga díscoite i Django 1.9."

msgid "``django.utils.functional.memoize`` function"
msgstr "Feidhm ``django.utils.functional.memoize ``"

msgid ""
"The function ``memoize`` is deprecated and should be replaced by the "
"``functools.lru_cache`` decorator (available from Python 3.2 onward)."
msgstr ""
"Tá an fheidhm ``memoize ``díluaite agus ba cheart an maisitheoir "
"``functools.lru_cache`` (ar fáil ó Python 3.2 ar aghaidh) a chur ina ionad."

msgid ""
"Django ships a backport of this decorator for older Python versions and it's "
"available at ``django.utils.lru_cache.lru_cache``. The deprecated function "
"will be removed in Django 1.9."
msgstr ""
"Seolann Django backport den mhaisitheoir seo do leaganacha Python níos sine "
"agus tá sé ar fáil ag ``django.utils.lru_cache.lru_cache``. Bainfear an "
"fheidhm atá díscríofa i Django 1.9."

msgid "Geo Sitemaps"
msgstr "Léarscáileanna Suímh Geo"

msgid ""
"Google has retired support for the Geo Sitemaps format. Hence Django support "
"for Geo Sitemaps is deprecated and will be removed in Django 1.8."
msgstr ""
"Tá tacaíocht ar scor ag Google don fhormáid Geo Sitemaps. Dá bhrí sin tá "
"tacaíocht Django do Geo Sitemaps as lasc agus bainfear é i Django 1.8."

msgid "Passing callable arguments to queryset methods"
msgstr "Argóintí inghlaonta a chur chuig modhanna ceisteanna"

msgid ""
"Callable arguments for querysets were an undocumented feature that was "
"unreliable. It's been deprecated and will be removed in Django 1.9."
msgstr ""
"Gné neamhdhoiciméadaithe a bhí ag argóintí inghlaonta do cheisteanna a bhí "
"ann nach raibh iontaofa. Tá sé díscríofa agus bainfear é i Django 1.9."

msgid ""
"Callable arguments were evaluated when a queryset was constructed rather "
"than when it was evaluated, thus this feature didn't offer any benefit "
"compared to evaluating arguments before passing them to queryset and created "
"confusion that the arguments may have been evaluated at query time."
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh measúnú ar argóintí inghlaoite nuair a tógadh sraith fiosrúcháin "
"seachas nuair a rinneadh é a mheas, mar sin níor bhain an ghné seo tairbhe "
"ar bith as i gcomparáid le measúnú a dhéanamh ar argóintí sular cuireadh ar "
"aghaidh chuig queryset iad agus chruthaigh sé mearbhall go mb’fhéidir gur "
"measadh na hargóintí ag am fiosrúcháin."

msgid "``ADMIN_FOR`` setting"
msgstr "Socrú ``ADMIN_FOR``"

msgid ""
"The ``ADMIN_FOR`` feature, part of the admindocs, has been removed. You can "
"remove the setting from your configuration at your convenience."
msgstr ""
"Tá an ghné ``ADMIN_FOR``, cuid den admindocs, bainte amach. Is féidir leat "
"an socrú a bhaint as do chumraíocht ag áisiúlacht duit."

msgid "``SplitDateTimeWidget`` with ``DateTimeField``"
msgstr "``SplitDateTimeWidget`` le ``DateTimeField``"

msgid ""
"``SplitDateTimeWidget`` support in :class:`~django.forms.DateTimeField` is "
"deprecated, use ``SplitDateTimeWidget`` "
"with :class:`~django.forms.SplitDateTimeField` instead."
msgstr ""
"Tá tacaíocht ``SplitDateTimeWidget`` in:class: `~django.forms.DateTimeField` "
"díluaite, bain úsáid as ``SplitDateTimeWidget`` le:class: "
"`~django.forms.splitDateTimeField` ina ionad."

msgid "``validate``"
msgstr "``bailíocht``"

msgid ""
"The ``validate`` management command is deprecated in favor of "
"the :djadmin:`check` command."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear an t-ordú bainistíochta `bailite`` a dhíchur i bhfabhar an "
"orduithe: djadmin: `check`."

msgid "``django.core.management.BaseCommand``"
msgstr "``Django.Core.Management.BaseCommand``"

msgid ""
"``requires_model_validation`` is deprecated in favor of a new "
"``requires_system_checks`` flag. If the latter flag is missing, then the "
"value of the former flag is used. Defining both ``requires_system_checks`` "
"and ``requires_model_validation`` results in an error."
msgstr ""
"Tá ``requres_model_validation`` a dhíchur i bhfabhar bratach nua "
"``requires_system_checks``. Má tá an bhratach deiridh in easnamh, úsáidtear "
"luach an iar-bhratach. Tá earráid mar thoradh ar ``requires_system_checks`` "
"agus `requres_model_validation`` araon a shainmhíniú."

msgid "The ``check()`` method has replaced the old ``validate()`` method."
msgstr ""
"Tá an modh ``check () ``tar éis an sean-mhodh ``validate ()`` in ionad."

msgid "``ModelAdmin`` validators"
msgstr "Bailíochtóirí ``Modeladmin ``"

msgid ""
"The ``ModelAdmin.validator_class`` and ``default_validator_class`` "
"attributes are deprecated in favor of the new ``checks_class`` attribute."
msgstr ""
"Tá na tréithe ``ModelAdmin.validator_class`` agus `default_validator_class`` "
"a dhíchur i bhfabhar na tréithe nua ``checks_class``."

msgid ""
"The ``ModelAdmin.validate()`` method is deprecated in favor of "
"``ModelAdmin.check()``."
msgstr ""
"Tá an modh ``ModelAdmin.validate () `díluaite i bhfabhar ``ModelAdmin.check "
"() ``."

msgid "The ``django.contrib.admin.validation`` module is deprecated."
msgstr "Tá an modúl ``django.contrib.admin.validation`` a dhíchur."

msgid "``django.db.backends.DatabaseValidation.validate_field``"
msgstr "``Django.db.backends.databaseValidation.validate_field``"

msgid ""
"This method is deprecated in favor of a new ``check_field`` method. The "
"functionality required by ``check_field()`` is the same as that provided by "
"``validate_field()``, but the output format is different. Third-party "
"database backends needing this functionality should provide an "
"implementation of ``check_field()``."
msgstr ""
"Tá an modh seo gan moladh i bhfabhar modh nua ``seiceáil_réimse``. Tá an "
"fheidhmiúlacht a éilíonn `` check_field()`` mar an gcéanna leis an "
"bhfeidhmiúlacht a sholáthraíonn ``validate_field()``, ach tá an fhormáid "
"aschuir difriúil. Ba cheart go soláthródh inneall bunachar sonraí tríú "
"páirtí a bhfuil gá acu leis an bhfeidhmiúlacht seo cur i bhfeidhm "
"``check_field()``."

msgid "Loading ``ssi`` and ``url`` template tags from ``future`` library"
msgstr ""
"Clibeanna teimpléad ``ssi`` agus ``url ``á luchtú ó leabharlann ``todhcha``"

msgid ""
"Django 1.3 introduced ``{% load ssi from future %}`` and ``{% load url from "
"future %}`` syntax for forward compatibility of the ``ssi`` and :ttag:`url` "
"template tags. This syntax is now deprecated and will be removed in Django "
"1.9. You can simply remove the ``{% load ... from future %}`` tags."
msgstr ""
"Thug Django 1.3 isteach comhréir ``{% load ssi ón todhchaí%}`` agus ``{% "
"load url ón todhchaí%}`` le haghaidh comhoiriúnacht ar aghaidh na gclibeanna "
"teimpléad ``ssi`` agus:ttag: `url `. Tá an comhréireacht seo díscríofa anois "
"agus bainfear é i Django 1.9. Ní féidir leat ach na clibeanna ``{% load... a "
"bhaint as clibeanna%}`` sa todhchaí."

msgid "``django.utils.text.javascript_quote``"
msgstr "``django.utils.text.javascript_quote``"

msgid ""
"``javascript_quote()`` was an undocumented function present in "
"``django.utils.text``. It was used internally in the "
"``javascript_catalog()`` view whose implementation was changed to make use "
"of ``json.dumps()`` instead. If you were relying on this function to provide "
"safe output from untrusted strings, you should use "
"``django.utils.html.escapejs`` or the :tfilter:`escapejs` template filter. "
"If all you need is to generate valid JavaScript strings, you can simply use "
"``json.dumps()``."
msgstr ""
"Feidhm neamhdhoiciméadaithe a bhí ann i ``javascript_quote () ``i láthair in "
"``django.utils.text``. Úsáideadh é go hinmheánach sa radharc "
"`javascript_catalog () ``a athraíodh a chur i bhfeidhm chun ``json.dumps "
"()`` a úsáid ina ionad. Má bhí tú ag brath ar an bhfeidhm seo chun aschur "
"sábháilte a sholáthar ó teaghráin neamhiontaofa, ba cheart duit an scagaire "
"teimpléad ``django.utils.html.escapejs`` nó an scagaire teimpléad: "
"`escapejs` a úsáid. Más rud a theastaíonn uait ná teaghráin JavaScript bailí "
"a ghiniúint, is féidir leat ``json.dumps () ``a úsáid."

msgid "``fix_ampersands`` utils method and template filter"
msgstr "Modh úsáideach agus scagaire teimpléad ``fix_ampersands``"

msgid ""
"The ``django.utils.html.fix_ampersands`` method and the ``fix_ampersands`` "
"template filter are deprecated, as the escaping of ampersands is already "
"taken care of by Django's standard HTML escaping features. Combining this "
"with ``fix_ampersands`` would either result in double escaping, or, if the "
"output is assumed to be safe, a risk of introducing XSS vulnerabilities. "
"Along with ``fix_ampersands``, ``django.utils.html.clean_html`` is "
"deprecated, an undocumented function that calls ``fix_ampersands``. As this "
"is an accelerated deprecation, ``fix_ampersands`` and ``clean_html`` will be "
"removed in Django 1.8."
msgstr ""
"Tá an modh ``django.utils.html.fix_ampersands`` agus an scagaire teimpléad "
"``fix_ampersands`` a dhíchur, toisc go dtugann gnéithe caighdeánacha "
"éalaithe HTML Django aire d'éalú ampersandaí cheana féin. Bheadh éalú "
"dúbailte mar thoradh air seo le `fix_ampersands`, nó, má ghlactar leis go "
"bhfuil an t-aschur sábháilte, baol go dtabharfar leochaileachtaí XSS a "
"thabhairt isteach. In éineacht le ``fix_ampersands``, tá "
"`django.utils.html.clean_html`` díscoite, feidhm neamhdhoiciméadaithe a "
"ghlaonn ``fix_ampersands``. Toisc gur díphríocht luathaithe é seo, bainfear "
"``fix_ampersands`` agus ``clean_html`` i Django 1.8."

msgid "Reorganization of database test settings"
msgstr "Athrú socruithe tástála bunachar sonraí"

msgid ""
"All database settings with a ``TEST_`` prefix have been deprecated in favor "
"of entries in a :setting:`TEST <DATABASE-TEST>` dictionary in the database "
"settings. The old settings will be supported until Django 1.9. For backwards "
"compatibility with older versions of Django, you can define both versions of "
"the settings as long as they match."
msgstr ""
"<DATABASE-TEST>Tá gach socrú bunachar sonraí le réimír ``TEST_`` díluaite i "
"bhfabhar iontrálacha i bhfoclóir a:setting: `TEST `i socruithe bunachar "
"sonraí. Tacófar leis na sean-socruithe go dtí Django 1.9. Maidir le "
"comhoiriúnacht ar ais le leaganacha níos sine de Django, is féidir leat an "
"dá leagan de na socruithe a shainiú chomh fada agus a mheaitseálann siad."

msgid "FastCGI support"
msgstr "Tacaíocht FastCGI"

msgid ""
"FastCGI support via the ``runfcgi`` management command will be removed in "
"Django 1.9. Please deploy your project using WSGI."
msgstr ""
"Bainfear tacaíocht FastCGI tríd an ordú bainistíochta ``runfcgi` i Django "
"1.9. Imscaradh do thionscadal le do thoil ag úsáid WSGI."

msgid "Moved objects in ``contrib.sites``"
msgstr "Rudaí bogadh i `contrib.sites``"

msgid ""
"Following the app-loading refactor, two objects in "
"``django.contrib.sites.models`` needed to be moved because they must be "
"available without importing ``django.contrib.sites.models`` when "
"``django.contrib.sites`` isn't installed. Import ``RequestSite`` from "
"``django.contrib.sites.requests`` and ``get_current_site()`` from "
"``django.contrib.sites.shortcuts``. The old import locations will work until "
"Django 1.9."
msgstr ""
"Tar éis an athfhachtóir luchtaithe aip, b'éigean dhá réad i "
"`django.contrib.sites.models`` a bhogadh toisc go gcaithfidh siad a bheith "
"ar fáil gan `django.contrib.sites.models`` a allmhairiú nuair nach bhfuil "
"``django.contrib.sites`` suiteáilte. Iompórtáil ``requestsite`` ó "
"``django.contrib.sites.requests`` agus ``get_current_site () ``ó "
"`django.contrib.sites.shortcuts``. Oibreoidh na sean-áiteanna allmhairithe "
"go dtí Django 1.9."

msgid "``django.forms.forms.get_declared_fields()``"
msgstr "``django.forms.forms.get_declarred_fields () ``"

msgid ""
"Django no longer uses this functional internally. Even though it's a private "
"API, it'll go through the normal deprecation cycle."
msgstr ""
"Ní úsáideann Django an fheidhmiú seo go hinmheánach. Cé gur API "
"príobháideach é, rachaidh sé tríd an ngnáththimthriall díscrúdaithe."

msgid "Private Query Lookup APIs"
msgstr "APIs Cuardaigh Ceisteanna Príobháideacha"

msgid ""
"Private APIs ``django.db.models.sql.where.WhereNode.make_atom()`` and "
"``django.db.models.sql.where.Constraint`` are deprecated in favor of the "
"new :doc:`custom lookups API </ref/models/lookups>`."
msgstr ""
"Tá APIs príobháideacha ``Django.db.Models.Sql.where.whereNode.Make_Atom () "
"``agus ``Django.db.Models.sql.where.</ref/models/lookups> Constraint`` a "
"dhíchur i bhfabhar an nua:doc: `lookups saincheaptha API`."

msgid "Features removed in 1.7"
msgstr "Gnéithe bainte i 1.7"

msgid ""
"These features have reached the end of their deprecation cycle and are "
"removed in Django 1.7. See :ref:`deprecated-features-1.5` for details, "
"including how to remove usage of these features."
msgstr ""
"Tá na gnéithe seo tar éis deireadh a dtimthriall díscrúdaithe bainte amach "
"agus baintear iad i Django 1.7. Féach: Ref: `deprecated-features-1.5` le "
"haghaidh sonraí, lena n-áirítear conas úsáid na ngnéithe seo a bhaint."

msgid "``django.utils.simplejson`` is removed."
msgstr "Baintear ``django.utils.simplejson``."

msgid "``django.utils.itercompat.product`` is removed."
msgstr "Baintear ``django.utils.itercompat.product``."

msgid ""
"INSTALLED_APPS and TEMPLATE_DIRS are no longer corrected from a plain string "
"into a tuple."
msgstr ""
"Ní cheartaítear INSTALLED_APPS agus TEMPLATE_DIRS a thuilleadh ó shreang "
"simplí isteach i dtuple."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.http.HttpResponse`, :class:`~django.template.response.SimpleTemplateResponse`, :class:`~django.template.response.TemplateResponse`, "
"``render_to_response()``, :func:`~django.contrib.sitemaps.views.index`, "
"and :func:`~django.contrib.sitemaps.views.sitemap` no longer take a "
"``mimetype`` argument"
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.http.httpResponse`, :class: "
"`~django.template.response.simpletemplateResponse`, :class: "
"`~django.template.response.templateResponse`, ``render_to_response () "
"``, :func: `~django.contrib.viewsitemaps.s.index`, agus:func: "
"`~django.contrib.sitemaps.views.sitemap` ní ghlacann argóint ``mimetype`` a "
"thuilleadh"

msgid ""
":class:`~django.http.HttpResponse` immediately consumes its content if it's "
"an iterator."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.http.httpResponse` ídíonn a ábhar láithreach más "
"athraitheoir é."

msgid ""
"The ``AUTH_PROFILE_MODULE`` setting, and the ``get_profile()`` method on the "
"User model are removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear an socrú ``AUTH_PROFILE_MODULE``, agus an modh ``get_profile () "
"``ar an tsamhail Úsáideora."

msgid "The ``cleanup`` management command is removed."
msgstr "Baintear an t-ordú bainistíochta ``glantach``."

msgid "The ``daily_cleanup.py`` script is removed."
msgstr "Baintear an script `daily_cleanup.py``."

msgid ""
":meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.select_related` no longer has a "
"``depth`` keyword argument."
msgstr ""
":meth: Níl argóint eochairfhocal ``depth`` ag "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.select_related` a thuilleadh."

msgid ""
"The ``get_warnings_state()``/``restore_warnings_state()`` functions "
"from :mod:`django.test.utils` and the ``save_warnings_state()``/ "
"``restore_warnings_state()`` :ref:`django.test.*TestCase <django-testcase-"
"subclasses>` are removed."
msgstr ""
"Feidhmíonn ``get_warnings_state () ``/``restore_warnings_state () ``ó:mod: "
"`django.test.utils` agus an ``save_warnings_state () ``/ "
"``restore_warnings_state () ``:ref: `django.test. * Baintear tástá <django-"
"testcase-subclasses>il `."

msgid ""
"The ``check_for_test_cookie`` method "
"in :class:`~django.contrib.auth.forms.AuthenticationForm` is removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear an modh ``check_for_test_cookie`` in:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.forms.AuthenticationForm`."

msgid ""
"The version of ``django.contrib.auth.views.password_reset_confirm()`` that "
"supports base36 encoded user IDs "
"(``django.contrib.auth.views.password_reset_confirm_uidb36``) is removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear an leagan de ``django.contrib.auth.views.password_reset_confirm () "
"``a thacaíonn le ID úsáideora ionchódaithe base36 "
"(``django.contrib.auth.views.password_reset_confirm_uidb36``)."

msgid "The ``django.utils.encoding.StrAndUnicode`` mix-in is removed."
msgstr "Baintear an meascán ``django.utils.encoding.StrandUnicode``."

msgid "Django 1.7.1 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.7.1"

msgid "Django 1.7.1 fixes several bugs in 1.7."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.7.1 roinnt fabhtanna i 1.7."

msgid ""
"Added a more helpful error message if you try to migrate an app without "
"first creating the ``contenttypes`` table (:ticket:`22411`)."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh teachtaireacht earráide níos cabhrach leis má dhéanann tú iarracht "
"aip a aistriú gan an tábla ``contenttypes`` a chruthú ar dtús (:ticket: "
"`22411`)."

msgid ""
"Modified migrations dependency algorithm to avoid possible infinite "
"recursion."
msgstr ""
"Algartam spleáchais imirce modhnaithe chun athshlánú gan teorainn a "
"sheachaint."

msgid ""
"Fixed a ``UnicodeDecodeError`` when the ``flush`` error message contained "
"Unicode characters (:ticket:`22882`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh ``UnicodeDecodeError`` nuair a bhí carachtair Unicode sa "
"teachtaireacht earráide ``flush ``(:ticket: `22882`)."

msgid ""
"Reinstated missing ``CHECK`` SQL clauses which were omitted on some backends "
"when not using migrations (:ticket:`23416`)."
msgstr ""
"Athshocraigh clásail SQL ``CHECK`` in easnamh a cuireadh ar fágáil ar roinnt "
"cúltaca nuair nach n-úsáideann imirce (:ticket: `23416`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed serialization of ``type`` objects in migrations (:ticket:`22951`)."
msgstr "Sraitheadh seasta rudaí ``cineál` `i imirce (:ticket: `22951`)."

msgid ""
"The ``@deconstructible`` decorator now fails with a ``ValueError`` if the "
"decorated object cannot automatically be imported (:ticket:`23418`)."
msgstr ""
"Teipeann ar an maisitheoir ``@deconstructible`` anois le ``Error lua`` mura "
"féidir an réad maisithe a allmhairiú go huathoibríoch (:ticket: `23418`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a typo in an ``inlineformset_factory()`` error message that caused a "
"crash (:ticket:`23451`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh clóscríobh i dteachtaireacht earráide ``inlineformset_factory () "
"``a bhí ina chúis le timpiste (:ticket: `23451`)."

msgid ""
"Restored the ability to use :setting:`ABSOLUTE_URL_OVERRIDES` with the "
"``'auth.User'`` model (:ticket:`11775`). As a side effect, the setting now "
"adds a ``get_absolute_url()`` method to any model that appears in "
"``ABSOLUTE_URL_OVERRIDES`` but doesn't define ``get_absolute_url()``."
msgstr ""
"Athchóirigh an cumas chun úsáid: setting: `ABSOLUTE_URL_OVERRIDES` leis an "
"tsamhail ```Auth.user'` (:ticket: `11775`). Mar fho-éifeacht, cuireann an "
"socrú modh ``get_absolute_url () ``anois le haon mhúnla atá le feiceáil in "
"``ABSOLUTE_URL_OVERRIDES`` ach nach sainmhíníonn ``get_absolute_url ()``."

msgid ""
"Avoided masking some ``ImportError`` exceptions during application loading "
"(:ticket:`22920`)."
msgstr ""
"Seachnaíodh roinnt eisceachtaí ``ImportTerror` a mhúscailt le linn "
"luchtaithe iarratais (:ticket: `22920`)."

msgid ""
"Empty ``index_together`` or ``unique_together`` model options no longer "
"results in infinite migrations (:ticket:`23452`)."
msgstr ""
"Ní bhíonn imirce gan teorainn mar thoradh ar roghanna samhail folamh "
"``index_together ``nó ``unique_together`` a thuilleadh (:ticket: `23452`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed crash in ``contrib.sitemaps`` if ``lastmod`` returned a ``date`` "
"rather than a ``datetime`` (:ticket:`23403`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste seasta i `contrib.sitemaps`` má chuir ``lastmod`` `dáta ```` ar ais "
"seachas ``datetime`` (:ticket: `23403`)."

msgid ""
"Allowed migrations to work with ``app_label``\\s that have the same last "
"part (e.g. ``django.contrib.auth`` and ``vendor.auth``) (:ticket:`23483`)."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaítear imirce oibriú le ``app_label``\\ s a bhfuil an chuid deireanach "
"céanna acu (m.sh. ``django.contrib.auth`` agus ``vendor.auth``) (:ticket: "
"`23483`)."

msgid "Restored the ability to deepcopy ``F`` objects (:ticket:`23492`)."
msgstr ""
"Athchóirigh sé an cumas rudaí ``F ``a chóipeáil go doimhne (:ticket: "
"`23492`)."

msgid ""
"Formats for Welsh (``cy``) and several Chinese locales (``zh_CN``, "
"``zh_Hans``, ``zh_Hant`` and ``zh_TW``) have been added. Formats for "
"Macedonian have been fixed (trailing dot removed, :ticket:`23532`)."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh formáidí do na Breataine (`cy``) agus roinnt áiteanna Síneacha "
"(`zh_cn``, `zh_hans``, `zh_hant`` agus ``zh_tw``) curtha leis. Socraíodh "
"formáidí don Macadóinis (bainte pointe leanaí, :ticket: `23532`)."

msgid ""
"Added quoting of constraint names in the SQL generated by migrations to "
"prevent crash with uppercase characters in the name (:ticket:`23065`)."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh luachan ainmneacha srianta sa SQL a ghintear ag imirce chun "
"timpiste a chosc le carachtair uachtaracha san ainm (:ticket: `23065`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed renaming of models with a self-referential many-to-many field "
"(``ManyToManyField('self')``) (:ticket:`23503`)."
msgstr ""
"Athainmniú seasta samhlacha le réimse féin-tagartha go leor "
"(``ManyTomanyField ('self') `) (:ticket: `23503`)."

msgid ""
"Added "
"the :meth:`~django.contrib.admin.InlineModelAdmin.get_extra()`, :meth:`~django.contrib.admin.InlineModelAdmin.get_max_num()`, "
"and :meth:`~django.contrib.admin.InlineModelAdmin.get_min_num()` hooks "
"to :class:`~django.contrib.contenttypes.admin.GenericInlineModelAdmin` "
"(:ticket:`23539`)."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh: meth: `~django.contrib.admin.inlineModelAdmin.get_extra () "
"`, :meth: `~django.contrib.admin.inlineModelAdmin.get_max_num ()`, "
"agus:meth: `~django.contrib.admin.inlineModeladmin.get_min_num () `crúcaí "
"chuig:: `~django.contrib.contentTypes.admin.GenericInlineModelAdmin` "
"(:ticéad: `23539`)."

msgid ""
"Made ``migrations.RunSQL`` no longer require percent sign escaping. This is "
"now consistent with ``cursor.execute()`` (:ticket:`23426`)."
msgstr ""
"Ní theastaíonn comhartha faoin gcéad a éalú a thuilleadh ar "
"``Migrations.Runsql``. Tá sé seo ag teacht anois le ``cursor.execute () "
"``(:ticket: `23426`)."

msgid ""
"Made the ``SERIALIZE`` entry in the :setting:`TEST <DATABASE-TEST>` "
"dictionary usable (:ticket:`23421`)."
msgstr ""
"<DATABASE-TEST>Rinneadh an iontráil ``SERIALIZE`` sa bhfoclóir:socrú: "
"`TÁSTÁ` inúsáidte (:ticket: `23421`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed bug in migrations that prevented foreign key constraints to unmanaged "
"models with a custom primary key (:ticket:`23415`)."
msgstr ""
"Fabht seasta in imirce a chuir cosc ar theorainneacha eachtracha ar mhúnlaí "
"neamh-bhainistithe le príomh-eochair saincheaptha (:ticket: `23415`)."

msgid ""
"Added ``SchemaEditor`` for MySQL GIS backend so that spatial indexes will be "
"created for apps with migrations (:ticket:`23538`)."
msgstr ""
"“SchemaEditor” leis le haghaidh cúltaca MySQL GIS ionas go gcruthófar "
"innéacsanna spásúla d'aipeanna le himirce (:ticket: `23538`)."

msgid ""
"Added ``SchemaEditor`` for Oracle GIS backend so that spatial metadata and "
"indexes will be created for apps with migrations (:ticket:`23537`)."
msgstr ""
"“SchemaEditor” leis le haghaidh cúltaca Oracle GIS ionas go gcruthófar "
"meiteashonraí spásúla agus innéacsanna d'aipeanna le himirce (:ticket: "
"`23537`)."

msgid ""
"Coerced the ``related_name`` model field option to Unicode during migration "
"generation to generate migrations that work with both Python 2 and 3 "
"(:ticket:`23455`)."
msgstr ""
"Chuir iallach ar an rogha réimse samhail ``related_name`` le Unicode le linn "
"giniúint imirce chun imirceacha a ghiniúint a oibríonn le Python 2 agus 3 "
"araon (:ticket: `23455`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``MigrationWriter`` to handle builtin types without imports "
"(:ticket:`23560`)."
msgstr ""
"Seasta ``MigrationWriter`` chun cineálacha tógála a láimhseáil gan allmhairí "
"(:ticket: `23560`)."

msgid "Fixed ``deepcopy`` on ``ErrorList`` (:ticket:`23594`)."
msgstr "Socraigh ``deepcopy`` ar ``Liosta Error`` (:ticket: `23594`)."

msgid ""
"Made the :mod:`~django.contrib.admindocs` view to browse view details check "
"if the view specified in the URL exists in the URLconf. Previously it was "
"possible to import arbitrary packages from the Python path. This was not "
"considered a security issue because ``admindocs`` is only accessible to "
"staff users (:ticket:`23601`)."
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh an amharc: mod: `~django.contrib.admindocs` chun sonraí amharc a "
"bhrabhsáil seiceáil an bhfuil an radharc a shonraítear sa URL ann sa "
"URLConf. Roimhe seo bhí sé in ann pacáistí treallach a allmhairiú ón gcosán "
"Python. Níor mheastar gur saincheist slándála é seo toisc nach bhfuil "
"`admindocs` inrochtana ach d'úsáideoirí foirne (:ticket: `23601`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``UnicodeDecodeError`` crash in ``AdminEmailHandler`` with non-ASCII "
"characters in the request (:ticket:`23593`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste seasta ``UnicodeDecodeError`` i `AdminEmailHandler`` le carachtair "
"neamh-ASCII san iarratas (:ticket: `23593`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed missing ``get_or_create`` and ``update_or_create`` on related managers "
"causing ``IntegrityError`` (:ticket:`23611`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh ``get_or_create`` agus ``update_or_create`` ar iarraidh ar "
"bhainisteoirí gaolmhara ina chúis le ``IntegrityError`` (:ticket: `23611`)."

msgid ""
"Made :func:`~django.utils.http.urlsafe_base64_decode` return the proper type "
"(bytestring) on Python 3 (:ticket:`23333`)."
msgstr ""
"Déana:func: `~django.utils.http.urlsafe_base64_decode` filleadh an cineál "
"ceart (bytestring) ar Python 3 (:ticket: `23333`)."

msgid ""
":djadmin:`makemigrations` can now serialize timezone-aware values "
"(:ticket:`23365`)."
msgstr ""
": djadmin: is féidir le `makemigrations` luachanna atá ar an eolas ag crios "
"ama a shraitheadh anois (:ticket: `23365`)."

msgid ""
"Added a prompt to the migrations questioner when removing the null "
"constraint from a field to prevent an IntegrityError on existing NULL rows "
"(:ticket:`23609`)."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh pras leis an gceisteoir imirce agus an srian null á bhaint as "
"réimse chun IntegrityError a chosc ar shraitheanna NULL atá ann cheana "
"(:ticket: `23609`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed generic relations in ``ModelAdmin.list_filter`` (:ticket:`23616`)."
msgstr ""
"Caidreamh cineálach seasta i ``ModelAdmin.List_Filter`` (:ticket: `23616`)."

msgid ""
"Restored RFC compliance for the SMTP backend on Python 3 (:ticket:`23063`)."
msgstr ""
"Comhlíonadh RFC athchóirithe don chúltaca SMTP ar Python 3 (: ticket: "
"`23063`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash while parsing cookies containing invalid content "
"(:ticket:`23638`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste agus fianáin ina bhfuil ábhar neamhbhailí á pháirseáil "
"(:ticket: `23638`)."

msgid ""
"The system check framework now raises error **models.E020** when the class "
"method ``Model.check()`` is unreachable (:ticket:`23615`)."
msgstr ""
"Ardaíonn creat seiceála an chórais earráid anois **Models.E020** nuair a "
"bhíonn an modh ranga ``Model.check () ``inrochtana (:ticket: `23615`)."

msgid ""
"Made the Oracle test database creation drop the test user in the event of an "
"unclean exit of a previous test run (:ticket:`23649`)."
msgstr ""
"Rinne cruthú bunachar sonraí tástála Oracle an t-úsáideoir tástála a "
"scaoileadh i gcás imeacht neamhghlan de rith tástála roimhe seo (:ticket: "
"`23649`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed :djadmin:`makemigrations` to detect changes to :attr:`Meta.db_table "
"<django.db.models.Options.db_table>` (:ticket:`23629`)."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.Options.db_table>Socraithe: Djadmin: `makemigrations` chun "
"athruithe a bhrath go: attr: `Meta.db_table `(:ticket: `23629`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression when feeding the Django test client with an empty data "
"string (:ticket:`21740`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú agus tú ag beathú an cliant tástála Django le sreang "
"sonraí folamh (: ticéad: `21740`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression in :djadmin:`makemessages` where static files were "
"unexpectedly ignored (:ticket:`23583`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú in:djadmin: `makemessages` áit ar neamhaird ar chomhaid "
"statacha gan choinne (:ticket: `23583`)."

msgid "Django 1.7.10 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.7.10"

msgid "Django 1.7.10 fixes a security issue in 1.7.9."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.7.10 saincheist slándála i 1.7.9."

msgid "Django 1.7.11 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.7.11"

msgid "*November 24, 2015*"
msgstr "*24 Samhain, 2015*"

msgid "Django 1.7.11 fixes a security issue and a data loss bug in 1.7.10."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.7.11 saincheist slándála agus fabht caillteanais sonraí i "
"1.7.10."

msgid "Fixed settings leak possibility in ``date`` template filter"
msgstr ""
"Féidearthacht sceitheadh socruithe seasta i scagaire teimpléad ``dáta ``"

msgid ""
"If an application allows users to specify an unvalidated format for dates "
"and passes this format to the :tfilter:`date` filter, e.g. ``{{ last_updated|"
"date:user_date_format }}``, then a malicious user could obtain any secret in "
"the application's settings by specifying a settings key instead of a date "
"format. e.g. ``\"SECRET_KEY\"`` instead of ``\"j/m/Y\"``."
msgstr ""
"Má cheadaíonn feidhmchlár d'úsáideoirí formáid neamhbhailíochtaithe do "
"dhátaí a shonrú agus má chuireann an fhormáid seo chuig scagair:tfilter: "
"`date`, m.sh. ``{{last_updated|date:user_date_format}}``, ansin d'fhéadfadh "
"úsáideoir mailíseach aon rún a fháil i socruithe an fheidhmchláir trí "
"eochair socruithe in ionad formáid dáta. m.sh. `\"SECRET_KEY\"`` in ionad "
"`\"j/ym/ym/m ``."

msgid ""
"To remedy this, the underlying function used by the ``date`` template "
"filter, ``django.utils.formats.get_format()``, now only allows accessing the "
"date/time formatting settings."
msgstr ""
"Chun é seo a leigheas, ní cheadaíonn an bhfeidhm bhunúsach a úsáideann an "
"scagaire teimpléad ``dáta ``, `django.utils.formats.get_format () `, ach "
"rochtain a fháil ar na socruithe formáidithe dáta/ama."

msgid ""
"Fixed a data loss possibility with :class:`~django.db.models.Prefetch` if "
"``to_attr`` is set to a ``ManyToManyField`` (:ticket:`25693`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh féidearthacht caillteanais sonraí le:class: "
"`~django.db.models.prefetch` má tá ``to_attr`` socraithe go "
"``ManyTomanyField`` (:ticket: `25693`)."

msgid "Django 1.7.2 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.7.2"

msgid "Django 1.7.2 fixes several bugs in 1.7.1."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.7.2 roinnt fabhtanna i 1.7.1."

msgid ""
"Fixed migration's renaming of auto-created many-to-many tables when "
"changing :attr:`Meta.db_table <django.db.models.Options.db_table>` "
"(:ticket:`23630`)."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.Options.db_table>Athainmniú imirce seasta ar tháblaí go "
"leor a chruthaítear go huathoibríoch agus iad ag athrú: attr: `Meta.db_table "
"`(:ticket: `23630`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a migration crash when adding an explicit ``id`` field to a model on "
"SQLite (:ticket:`23702`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste imirce nuair a chuirtear réimse sainráite ``id ``le "
"samhail ar SQLite (:ticket: `23702`)."

msgid ""
"Added a warning for duplicate models when a module is reloaded. Previously a "
"``RuntimeError`` was raised every time two models clashed in the app "
"registry. (:ticket:`23621`)."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh rabhadh le haghaidh samhlacha dúblacha nuair a dhéantar modúl a "
"athluchtú. Roimhe seo ardaíodh ``RuntimeError`` gach uair a bhuail dhá "
"mhúnla i gclárlann an aip. (:ticéad: `23621`)."

msgid ""
"Prevented :djadmin:`flush` from loading initial data for migrated apps "
"(:ticket:`23699`)."
msgstr ""
"Cosc: Djadmin: `flush `ó luchtú sonraí tosaigh d'aipeanna imirceacha "
"(:ticket: `23699`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a :djadmin:`makemessages` regression in 1.7.1 "
"when :setting:`STATIC_ROOT` has the default ``None`` value (:ticket:`23717`)."
msgstr ""
"Seasta a: djadmin: aischéimniú `makemessages` i 1.7.1 nuai:setting: "
"`STATIC_ROOT` an luach réamhshocraithe ```None`` (:ticket: `23717`)."

msgid "Added GeoDjango compatibility with mysqlclient database driver."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh comhoiriúnacht GeodJango leis an tiománaí bunachar sonraí "
"mysqlclient."

msgid ""
"Fixed MySQL 5.6+ crash with ``GeometryField``\\s in migrations "
"(:ticket:`23719`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste seasta MySQL 5.6+ le ``GeometryField``\\ s in imirce (:ticket: "
"`23719`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a migration crash when removing a field that is referenced in "
"``AlterIndexTogether`` or ``AlterUniqueTogether`` (:ticket:`23614`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste imirce nuair a bhaint réimse dá dtagraítear in "
"``AlterIndexTogether`` nó ``AlterUniqueToGether`` (:ticket: `23614`)."

msgid "Updated the first day of the week in the Ukrainian locale to Monday."
msgstr ""
"Nuashonraigh an chéad lá den tseachtain i gceantar na hÚcráine go dtí Dé "
"Luain."

msgid ""
"Added support for transactional spatial metadata initialization on "
"SpatiaLite 4.1+ (:ticket:`23152`)."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíocht bhreise le haghaidh tionscnamh meiteashonraí spásúla "
"idirbheartaíochta ar SpatialITE 4.1+ (:ticket: `23152`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a migration crash that prevented changing a nullable field with a "
"default to non-nullable with the same default (:ticket:`23738`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste imirce a chuir cosc ar réimse in-neamhnaithe a athrú le "
"réamhshocraithe go neamh-neamh-neamhnaithe leis an réamhshocrú céanna "
"(:ticket: `23738`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a migration crash when adding ``GeometryField``\\s with ``blank=True`` "
"on PostGIS (:ticket:`23731`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste imirce nuair a chuirtear ``GeometryField``\\ s le ``Blank "
"= True`` ar PostGIS (:ticket: `23731`)."

msgid ""
"Allowed usage of ``DateTimeField()`` as ``Transform.output_field`` "
"(:ticket:`23420`)."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid cheadaithe de ``DateTimeField () ``mar `Transform.output_field`` "
"(:ticket: `23420`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a migration serializing bug involving ``float(\"nan\")`` and "
"``float(\"inf\")`` (:ticket:`23770`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh fabht sraitheach imirce lena mbaineann ``float (“nan”) ``agus "
"``float (“inf”)`` (:ticket: `23770`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression where custom form fields having a ``queryset`` attribute "
"but no ``limit_choices_to`` could not be used in "
"a :class:`~django.forms.ModelForm` (:ticket:`23795`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú nuair nach bhféadfaí réimsí foirme saincheaptha a "
"bhfuil tréith ``queryset`` ach gan aon ``limit_choices_to`` a úsáid in "
"a:class: `~django.forms.modelform` (:ticket: `23795`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a custom field type validation error with MySQL backend when "
"``db_type`` returned ``None`` (:ticket:`23761`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh earráid bailíochtaithe cineál réimse saincheaptha le cúltaca MySQL "
"nuair a d'fhill ``db_type`` ``None`` (:ticket: `23761`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a migration crash when a field is renamed that is part of an "
"``index_together`` (:ticket:`23859`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste imirce nuair a athainmnítear réimse atá mar chuid de "
"`index_together ``(:ticket: `23859`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed :djadmin:`squashmigrations` to respect the ``--no-optimize`` parameter "
"(:ticket:`23799`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraithe: Djadmin: `squashmigrations` chun an paraiméadar ``--no-optime`` a "
"urramú (:ticket: `23799`)."

msgid ""
"Made :class:`~django.db.migrations.operations.RenameModel` reversible "
"(:ticket:`22248`)"
msgstr ""
"Déanta: aicme: `~django.db.migrations.operations.RenameModel` "
"inchúlghabháilte (:ticket: `22248`)"

msgid ""
"Avoided unnecessary rollbacks of migrations from other apps when migrating "
"backwards (:ticket:`23410`)."
msgstr ""
"Seachnaíodh aistrithe gan ghá ar imirce ó aipeanna eile agus iad ag imirce "
"ar ais (:ticket: `23410`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a rare query error when using deeply nested subqueries "
"(:ticket:`23605`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh earráid fiosrúcháin neamhchoitianta agus fo-cheisteanna neadaithe "
"go domhain á úsáid agat (:ticket: `23605`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash in migrations when deleting a field that is part of a ``index/"
"unique_together`` constraint (:ticket:`23794`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste in imirce nuair a scriosadh réimse atá mar chuid de "
"shrianadh ``index/unique_together ``(:ticket: `23794`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``django.core.files.File.__repr__()`` when the file's ``name`` "
"contains Unicode characters (:ticket:`23888`)."
msgstr ""
"Seasta ``django.core.files.file. __repr__ () ``nuair a bhíonn carachtair "
"Unicode sa ``ainm`` comhad (:ticket: `23888`)."

msgid ""
"Added missing context to the admin's ``delete_selected`` view that prevented "
"custom site header, etc. from appearing (:ticket:`23898`)."
msgstr ""
"Chuir comhthéacs in easnamh leis an dearcadh ``delete_selected`` an "
"riaracháin a chuir cosc ar cheannteideal an láithreáin saincheaptha, srl. Ó "
"bheith le feiceáil (:ticket: `23898`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed an infinite loop bug for certain cyclic migration dependencies, and "
"made the error message for cyclic dependencies much more helpful."
msgstr ""
"D'eisigh sé fabht lúb gan teorainn le haghaidh spleáchais imirce "
"timthriallacha áirithe, agus rinne sé an teachtaireacht earráide do "
"spleáchais timthriallacha i bhfad níos cabhrach."

msgid "Added missing ``index_together`` handling for SQLite (:ticket:`23880`)."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh láimhseáil ``index_together ``in easnamh le haghaidh SQLite "
"(:ticket: `23880`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when ``RunSQL`` SQL content was collected by the schema "
"editor, typically when using ``sqlmigrate`` (:ticket:`23909`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste nuair a bhailigh an t-eagarthóir scéime ábhar SQL "
"``Runsql``, de ghnáth nuair a úsáideann `sqlmigrate`` (:ticket: `23909`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression in ``contrib.admin`` add/change views which caused some "
"``ModelAdmin`` methods to receive the incorrect ``obj`` value "
"(:ticket:`23934`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú i “contrib.admin” tuairimí a chuirt/athraigh ar chúis "
"le roinnt modhanna ``ModelAdmin`` an luach mícheart ``obj`` a fháil "
"(:ticket: `23934`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``runserver`` crash when socket error message contained Unicode "
"characters (:ticket:`23946`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste seasta ``runserver ``nuair a bhí carachtair Unicode i "
"dteachtaireacht earráide soicéad (:ticket: `23946`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed serialization of ``type`` when adding a ``deconstruct()`` method "
"(:ticket:`23950`)."
msgstr ""
"Sraitheadh seasta ar ``cineál` nuair a chuirtear modh ``deconstruct () "
"``leis (:ticket: `23950`)."

msgid ""
"Prevented the "
"``django.contrib.auth.middleware.SessionAuthenticationMiddleware`` from "
"setting a ``\"Vary: Cookie\"`` header on all responses (:ticket:`23939`)."
msgstr ""
"Chuir sé cosc ar an "
"`Django.contrib.auth.middleware.sessionAuthenticationMiddleware`` "
"ceannteideal ``\"Vary: Fianach\"` a shocrú ar gach freagra (:ticket: "
"`23939`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when adding ``blank=True`` to ``TextField()`` on MySQL "
"(:ticket:`23920`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste nuair a chuirtear ``Blank=True`` le ``TextField ()`` ar "
"MySQL (:ticket: `23920`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed index creation by the migration infrastructure, particularly when "
"dealing with PostgreSQL specific ``{text|varchar}_pattern_ops`` indexes "
"(:ticket:`23954`)."
msgstr ""
"Cruthú innéacs seasta ag an mbonneagar imirce, go háirithe nuair a "
"dhéileálfar le hinnéacsanna sonracha ``{text|varchar} _pattern_ops`` "
"PostgreSQL (:ticket: `23954`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed bug in ``makemigrations`` that created broken migration files when "
"dealing with multiple table inheritance and inheriting from more than one "
"model (:ticket:`23956`)."
msgstr ""
"Fabht seasta i `makemigrations`` a chruthaigh comhaid imirce briste agus iad "
"ag déileáil le oidhreacht iolrach tábla agus ag oidhreacht ó níos mó ná "
"samhail amháin (:ticket: `23956`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when a ``MultiValueField`` has invalid data (:ticket:`23674`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste nuair a bhíonn sonraí neamhbhailí ag ``MultivalueField` "
"(:ticket: `23674`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash in the admin when using \"Save as new\" and also deleting a "
"related inline (:ticket:`23857`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste sa riarachán agus tú ag úsáid “Sábháil mar nua” agus "
"inlíne gaolmhar á scriosadh freisin (:ticket: `23857`)."

msgid ""
"Always converted ``related_name`` to text (Unicode), since that is required "
"on Python 3 for interpolation. Removed conversion of ``related_name`` to "
"text in migration deconstruction (:ticket:`23455` and :ticket:`23982`)."
msgstr ""
"Tiontaigh ``related_name`` i gcónaí go téacs (Unicode), ós rud é go bhfuil "
"sé sin ag teastáil ar Python 3 le haghaidh idirpholú. Bainte tiontú "
"``related_name`` go téacs sa dífhoirgneamh imirce (:ticket: `23455` "
"agus:ticket: `23982`)."

msgid ""
"Enlarged the sizes of tablespaces which are created by default for testing "
"on Oracle (the main tablespace was increased from 200M to 300M and the "
"temporary tablespace from 100M to 150M). This was required to accommodate "
"growth in Django's own test suite (:ticket:`23969`)."
msgstr ""
"Méadaíodh méideanna na spás tábla a chruthaítear de réir réamhshocraithe le "
"haghaidh tástála ar Oracle (méadaíodh an príomh-spás tábla ó 200M go 300M "
"agus an spás tábla sealadach ó 100M go 150M). Bhí sé seo ag teastáil chun "
"freastal ar fhás i sraith tástála Django féin (:ticket: `23969`)."

msgid "Fixed ``timesince`` filter translations in Korean (:ticket:`23989`)."
msgstr ""
"Aistriúcháin scagaire seasta ``timesince`` i gCóiréis (:ticket: `23989`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed the SQLite ``SchemaEditor`` to properly add defaults in the absence of "
"a user specified ``default``. For example, a ``CharField`` with "
"``blank=True`` didn't set existing rows to an empty string which resulted in "
"a crash when adding the ``NOT NULL`` constraint (:ticket:`23987`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh an SQLite ``SchemaEditor`` chun réamhshocruithe a chur i gceart in "
"éagmais úsáideora sonraithe ``réamhshocraithe``. Mar shampla, níor shocraigh "
"``Charfield`` le ``Blank=True`` sraitheanna atá ann cheana chuig teaghrán "
"folamh a raibh timpiste mar thoradh air nuair a chuir an srian ``NOT NULL`` "
"leis (:ticket: `23987`)."

msgid ""
"``makemigrations`` no longer prompts for a default value when adding "
"``TextField()`` or ``CharField()`` without a ``default`` (:ticket:`23405`)."
msgstr ""
"Ní thuilleann ``makemigrations`` luach réamhshocraithe a thuilleadh nuair a "
"chuirtear ``textField () ``nó `charField ()`` ``leis gan `réamhshocraithe`` "
"(:ticket: `23405`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a migration crash when adding ``order_with_respect_to`` to a table "
"with existing rows (:ticket:`23983`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste imirce nuair a chuirtear ``order_with_respect_to`` le "
"tábla le sraitheanna atá ann cheana (:ticket: `23983`)."

msgid ""
"Restored the ``pre_migrate`` signal if all apps have migrations "
"(:ticket:`23975`)."
msgstr ""
"Athchóirigh an comhartha ``pre_migrate`` má tá imirce ag gach aip (:ticket: "
"`23975`)."

msgid ""
"Made admin system checks run for custom ``AdminSite``\\s (:ticket:`23497`)."
msgstr ""
"Déantar seiceálacha córais riaracháin a reáchtáil le haghaidh saincheaptha "
"``Adminsite``\\ s (:ticket: `23497`)."

msgid ""
"Ensured the app registry is fully populated when unpickling models. When an "
"external script (like a queueing infrastructure) reloads pickled models, it "
"could crash with an ``AppRegistryNotReady`` exception (:ticket:`24007`)."
msgstr ""
"Cinntigh go bhfuil clárlann an aipeanna daonra go hiomlán nuair a "
"dhíphictear Nuair a athlódálann script sheachtrach (cosúil le bonneagar "
"scuaine) samhlacha picilte, d'fhéadfadh sé titim le eisceacht "
"``AppregistryNotready` (:ticket: `24007`)."

msgid ""
"Added quoting to field indexes in the SQL generated by migrations to prevent "
"a crash when the index name requires it (:ticket:`24015`)."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh luachan le hinnéacsanna réimse sa SQL a ghintear ag imirce chun "
"timpiste a chosc nuair a éilíonn ainm an innéacs é (:ticket: `24015`)."

msgid ""
"Added ``datetime.time`` support to migrations questioner (:ticket:`23998`)."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh tacaíocht ``datetime.time`` leis an gceisteoir imirce (:ticket: "
"`23998`)."

msgid "Fixed admindocs crash on apps installed as eggs (:ticket:`23525`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste admindocs seasta ar aipeanna atá suiteáilte mar uibheacha (:ticket: "
"`23525`)."

msgid ""
"Changed migrations autodetector to generate an ``AlterModelOptions`` "
"operation instead of ``DeleteModel`` and ``CreateModel`` operations when "
"changing ``Meta.managed``. This prevents data loss when changing ``managed`` "
"from ``False`` to ``True`` and vice versa (:ticket:`24037`)."
msgstr ""
"Athraigh uathraitheoir imirce chun oibríocht ``AlterModelOptions` a "
"ghiniúint in ionad oibríochtaí ``DeleteModel`` agus `CreateModel`` nuair a "
"athraítear ``Meta.Managed ``. Cuireann sé seo cosc ar chaillteanas sonraí "
"nuair a athraítear ``bainistí`` ó `False`` go `True`` agus a mhalairt "
"(:ticket: `24037`)."

msgid ""
"Enabled the ``sqlsequencereset`` command on apps with migrations "
"(:ticket:`24054`)."
msgstr ""
"Cumasaigh an t-ordú `sqlsequencereset ``ar aipeanna le himirce (:ticket: "
"`24054`)."

msgid "Added tablespace SQL to apps with migrations (:ticket:`24051`)."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh spás tábla SQL leis na feidhmchláir le himirce (:ticket: `24051`)."

msgid ""
"Corrected ``contrib.sites`` default site creation in a multiple database "
"setup (:ticket:`24000`)."
msgstr ""
"Cruthú suíomh réamhshocraithe ``contrib.sites`` ceartaithe i socrú iolrach "
"bunachar sonraí (:ticket: `24000`)."

msgid ""
"Restored support for objects that aren't :class:`str` or :class:`bytes` in "
"``django.utils.safestring.mark_for_escaping()`` on Python 3."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíocht athchóirithe do rudaí nach bhfuil: class: `str` nó:class: `bytes` "
"i ``django.utils.safestring.mark_for_escaping () ``ar Python 3."

msgid ""
"Supported strings escaped by third-party libraries with the ``__html__`` "
"convention in the template engine (:ticket:`23831`)."
msgstr ""
"Téigh teaghráin tacaithe ag leabharlanna tríú páirtí leis an gcoinbhinsiún "
"``__html__`` san inneall teimpléad (:ticket: `23831`)."

msgid ""
"Prevented extraneous ``DROP DEFAULT`` SQL in migrations (:ticket:`23581`)."
msgstr "Cosc ar SQL seachtrach ``DROP DEFAULT`` in imirce (:ticket: `23581`)."

msgid ""
"Restored the ability to use more than five levels of subqueries "
"(:ticket:`23758`)."
msgstr ""
"Athchóirigh sé an cumas níos mó ná cúig leibhéal fo-cheisteanna a úsáid "
"(:ticket: `23758`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed crash when ``ValidationError`` is initialized with a "
"``ValidationError`` that is initialized with a dictionary (:ticket:`24008`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste seasta nuair a thosaítear ``ValidationError`` le "
"``ValidationError`` a thionscnaítear le foclóir (:ticket: `24008`)."

msgid ""
"Prevented a crash on apps without migrations when running ``migrate --list`` "
"(:ticket:`23366`)."
msgstr ""
"Chuir sé cosc ar thimpiste ar aipeanna gan imirce agus iad ag rith ``migrant "
"--list`` (:ticket: `23366`)."

msgid "Django 1.7.3 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.7.3"

msgid "Django 1.7.3 fixes several security issues and bugs in 1.7.2."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.7.3 roinnt saincheisteanna slándála agus fabhtanna i "
"1.7.2."

msgid ""
"The default iteration count for the PBKDF2 password hasher has been "
"increased by 25%. This part of the normal major release process was "
"inadvertently omitted in 1.7. This backwards compatible change will not "
"affect users who have subclassed "
"``django.contrib.auth.hashers.PBKDF2PasswordHasher`` to change the default "
"value."
msgstr ""
"Méadaíodh 25% an líon athraithe réamhshocraithe don hasher pasfhocal PBKDF2. "
"Cuireadh an chuid seo den ghnáthphróiseas scaoilte mór ar fágáil go "
"neamhthuiscint i 1.7. Ní dhéanfaidh an t-athrú comhoiriúnach ar chúl difear "
"d'úsáideoirí a bhfuil fo-aicmithe ag "
"``Django.contrib.auth.hashers.pbkdf2PasswordHasher`` chun an luach "
"réamhshocraithe a athrú."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash in the CSRF middleware when handling non-ASCII referer header "
"(:ticket:`23815`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste sa mheán-earraí CSRF agus ceannteideal tagairtí neamh-"
"ASCII á láimhseáil (:ticket: `23815`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash in the ``django.contrib.auth.redirect_to_login`` view when "
"passing a ``reverse_lazy()`` result on Python 3 (:ticket:`24097`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste sa radharc ``django.contrib.auth.redirect_to_login`` nuair "
"a chuirtear toradh ``reverse_lazy () ``ar Python 3 (:ticket: `24097`)."

msgid "Added correct formats for Greek (``el``) (:ticket:`23967`)."
msgstr "Cuireadh formáidí cearta leis an nGréigis (``el``) (:ticket: `23967`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a migration crash when unapplying a migration where multiple "
"operations interact with the same model (:ticket:`24110`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste imirce nuair a dhíchuirtear imirce i bhfeidhm ina n-"
"idirghníomhaíonn oibríochtaí iolracha leis an tsamhail chéanna (:ticket: "
"`24110`)."

msgid "Django 1.7.4 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.7.4"

msgid "Django 1.7.4 fixes several bugs in 1.7.3."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.7.4 roinnt fabhtanna i 1.7.3."

msgid ""
"Fixed a migration crash when unapplying ``contrib.contenttypes``’s or "
"``contrib.auth``’s first migration (:ticket:`24075`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste imirce nuair a dhíchuirtear an chéad imirce "
"``contrib.contenttypes`` nó `contrib.auth`` a chur i bhfeidhm (:ticket: "
"`24075`)."

msgid ""
"Made the migration's ``RenameModel`` operation rename ``ManyToManyField`` "
"tables (:ticket:`24135`)."
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh táblaí ``ManyTomanyField`` oibríocht ``Renamemodel`` an imirce a "
"athainmniú (:ticket: `24135`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a migration crash on MySQL when migrating from a ``OneToOneField`` to "
"a ``ForeignKey`` (:ticket:`24163`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste imirce ar MySQL agus tú ag imirce ó ``OneTooneField`` go "
"``ForeignKey`` (:ticket: `24163`)."

msgid ""
"Prevented the ``static.serve`` view from producing ``ResourceWarning``\\s in "
"certain circumstances (security fix regression, :ticket:`24193`)."
msgstr ""
"Chuir sé cosc ar an dearcadh `static.serve` ``ResourceWarning`` a tháirgeadh "
"i gcúinsí áirithe (aischéimniú socraithe slándála, :ticket: `24193`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed schema check for ManyToManyField to look for internal type instead of "
"checking class instance, so you can write custom m2m-like fields with the "
"same behavior. (:ticket:`24104`)."
msgstr ""
"Seiceáil scéime seasta do ManyTomanyField chun cineál inmheánach a lorg in "
"ionad sampla ranga a sheiceáil, ionas gur féidir leat réimsí saincheaptha "
"cosúil le m2m a scríobh leis an iompar céanna. (:ticéad: `24104`)."

msgid "Django 1.7.5 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.7.5"

msgid "*February 25, 2015*"
msgstr "*25 Feabhra, 2015*"

msgid "Django 1.7.5 fixes several bugs in 1.7.4."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.7.5 roinnt fabhtanna i 1.7.4."

msgid ""
"Reverted a fix that prevented a migration crash when unapplying "
"``contrib.contenttypes``’s or ``contrib.auth``’s first migration "
"(:ticket:`24075`) due to severe impact on the test performance "
"(:ticket:`24251`) and problems in multi-database setups (:ticket:`24298`)."
msgstr ""
"Aisghairm socrú a chuir cosc ar thimpiste imirce nuair a dhíchuir an chéad "
"imirce `contrib.contenttypes`` nó `contrib.auth`` (:ticket: `24075`) mar "
"gheall ar thionchar mór ar fheidhmíocht na tástála (:ticket: `24251`) agus "
"fadhbanna i socruithe ilbhunachar sonraí (:ticket: `24298`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression that prevented custom fields inheriting from "
"``ManyToManyField`` from being recognized in migrations (:ticket:`24236`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú a chuir cosc ar réimsí saincheaptha a d'oidhreacht ó "
"``ManyTomanyField`` a aithint in imirce (:ticket: `24236`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed crash in ``contrib.sites`` migrations when a default database isn't "
"used (:ticket:`24332`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste seasta i imirce `contrib.sites`` nuair nach n-úsáidtear bunachar "
"sonraí réamhshocraithe (:ticket: `24332`)."

msgid ""
"Added the ability to set the isolation level on PostgreSQL with psycopg2 ≥ "
"2.4.2 (:ticket:`24318`). It was advertised as a new feature in Django 1.6 "
"but it didn't work in practice."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an cumas leis an leibhéal aonair a shocrú ar PostgreSQL le psycopg2 "
"≥ 2.4.2 (: ticket: `24318`). Fógraíodh é mar ghné nua i Django 1.6 ach níor "
"oibrigh sé go praiticiúil."

msgid "Formats for the Azerbaijani locale (``az``) have been added."
msgstr "Cuireadh formáidí don áitiúil na hAsarbaiseáise (`az``) leis."

msgid "Django 1.7.6 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.7.6"

msgid "*March 9, 2015*"
msgstr "*9 Márta, 2015*"

msgid "Django 1.7.6 fixes a security issue and several bugs in 1.7.5."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.7.6 saincheist slándála agus roinnt fabhtanna i 1.7.5."

msgid ""
"Mitigated an XSS attack via properties in ``ModelAdmin.readonly_fields``"
msgstr "Laghdaigh sé ionsaí XSS trí airíonna in ``ModelAdmin.Readonly_Fields``"

msgid ""
"The :attr:`ModelAdmin.readonly_fields "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.readonly_fields>` attribute in the Django "
"admin allows displaying model fields and model attributes. While the former "
"were correctly escaped, the latter were not. Thus untrusted content could be "
"injected into the admin, presenting an exploitation vector for XSS attacks."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn an tréith: Attr: `ModelAdmin.ReadOnly_Fields "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.readonly_fields>`sa riarachán Django réimsí "
"samhail agus tréithe samhail a thaispeáint. Cé gur éalaigh an chéad cheann i "
"gceart, ní raibh an dara ceann acu. Mar sin d'fhéadfaí ábhar neamhiontaofa a "
"instealladh isteach sa riarachán, ag cur veicteoir saothrú i láthair "
"d'ionsaithe XSS."

msgid ""
"In this vulnerability, every model attribute used in ``readonly_fields`` "
"that is not an actual model field (e.g. a :class:`property`) will **fail to "
"be escaped** even if that attribute is not marked as safe. In this release, "
"autoescaping is now correctly applied."
msgstr ""
"Sa leochaileacht seo, ní theipfidh gach tréith samhail a úsáidtear in "
"`readonly_fields`` nach réimse samhail iarbhír é (m.sh. a:class: `property`) "
"a éaló** fiú mura bhfuil an tréith sin marcáilte mar shábháilte. Sa eisiúint "
"seo, cuirtear autoescaping i bhfeidhm i gceart anois."

msgid ""
"Fixed crash when coercing ``ManyRelatedManager`` to a string "
"(:ticket:`24352`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste seasta agus tú ag cur ``ManyRelatedManager`` a iallach chuig "
"teaghrán (:ticket: `24352 `)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a bug that prevented migrations from adding a foreign key constraint "
"when converting an existing field to a foreign key (:ticket:`24447`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh fabht a chuir cosc ar imirce srian eochair eachtrach a chur leis "
"agus réimse atá ann cheana a thiontú go eochair eachtrach (:ticket: `24447`)."

msgid "Django 1.7.7 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.7.7"

msgid "Django 1.7.7 fixes several bugs and security issues in 1.7.6."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.7.7 roinnt fabhtanna agus saincheisteanna slándála i "
"1.7.6."

msgid ""
"Fixed renaming of classes in migrations where renaming a subclass would "
"cause incorrect state to be recorded for objects that referenced the "
"superclass (:ticket:`24354`)."
msgstr ""
"Athainmniú seasta ranganna in imirce ina ndéanfadh athainmniú fo-aicme a "
"thaifeadadh stát mícheart do rudaí a thug tagairt don sáraicme (:ticket: "
"`24354`)."

msgid ""
"Stopped writing migration files in dry run mode when merging migration "
"conflicts. When ``makemigrations --merge`` is called with ``verbosity=3`` "
"the migration file is written to ``stdout`` (:ticket:`24427`)."
msgstr ""
"Stop comhaid imirce a scríobh i mód rith tirim agus coinbhleachtaí imirce á "
"chumasc. Nuair a thugtar ``makemigrations --merge`` le ``verbosity=3`` "
"scríobhtar an comhad imirce chuig ``stdout`` (:ticket: `24427`)."

msgid "Django 1.7.8 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.7.8"

msgid "*May 1, 2015*"
msgstr "*1 Bealtaine, 2015*"

msgid "Django 1.7.8 fixes:"
msgstr "Django 1.7.8 socruithe:"

msgid ""
"Database introspection with SQLite 3.8.9 (released April 8, 2015) "
"(:ticket:`24637`)."
msgstr ""
"Introspéireacht bunachar sonraí le SQLite 3.8.9 (eisithe 8 Aibreán, 2015) "
"(:ticket: `24637`)."

msgid "A database table name quoting regression in 1.7.2 (:ticket:`24605`)."
msgstr ""
"Ainm tábla bunachar sonraí a luann aischéimniú i 1.7.2 (:ticket: `24605`)."

msgid ""
"The loss of ``null``/``not null`` column properties during field alteration "
"of MySQL databases (:ticket:`24595`)."
msgstr ""
"Cailliúint airíonna colún ``null``/`not null`` le linn athrú réimse "
"bunachair sonraí MySQL (:ticket: `24595`)."

msgid "Django 1.7.9 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.7.9"

msgid "Django 1.7.9 fixes several security issues and bugs in 1.7.8."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.7.9 roinnt saincheisteanna slándála agus fabhtanna i "
"1.7.8."

msgid ""
":func:`~django.core.validators.validate_ipv4_address`, :func:`~django.core.validators.validate_slug`, "
"and :class:`~django.core.validators.URLValidator` are also affected, "
"however, as of Django 1.6 the ``GenericIPAddresseField``, "
"``IPAddressField``, ``SlugField``, and ``URLField`` form fields which use "
"these validators all strip the input, so the possibility of newlines "
"entering your data only exists if you are using these validators outside of "
"the form fields."
msgstr ""
":func: `~django.core.validators.validate_ipv4_address`, :func: "
"`~django.core.validators.validate_slug`, agus:class: "
"`~django.core.validators.urlvalidator` tionchar freisin, áfach, mar Django "
"1.6 an `GenericipseField``, ``Scaoileann réimsí foirme Ipaddressfield``, "
"`SlugField``, agus `URLField`` a úsáideann na bailíochtóirí seo an t-"
"ionchur, mar sin níl an fhéidearthacht línte nua isteach do chuid sonraí ann "
"ach má tá na bailíochtóirí seo á úsáid agat lasmuigh de na réimsí foirme."

msgid ""
"Prevented the loss of ``null``/``not null`` column properties during field "
"renaming of MySQL databases (:ticket:`24817`)."
msgstr ""
"Cosc ar chailliúint airíonna colún ``null``/`not null`` le linn athainmniú "
"réimse bunachair sonraí MySQL (:ticket: `24817`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``SimpleTestCase.assertRaisesMessage()`` on Python 2.7.10 "
"(:ticket:`24903`)."
msgstr ""
"Seasta ``SimpleTestCase.assertRaisesMessage () ``ar Python 2.7.10 (:ticket: "
"`24903`)."

msgid "Django 1.8 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.8"

msgid "*April 1, 2015*"
msgstr "*1 Aibreán, 2015*"

msgid "Welcome to Django 1.8!"
msgstr "Fáilte go dtí Django 1.8!"

msgid ""
"These release notes cover the :ref:`new features <whats-new-1.8>`, as well "
"as some :ref:`backwards incompatible changes <backwards-incompatible-1.8>` "
"you'll want to be aware of when upgrading from Django 1.7 or older versions. "
"We've also :ref:`begun the deprecation process for some features <deprecated-"
"features-1.8>`, and some features have reached the end of their deprecation "
"process and :ref:`have been removed <removed-features-1.8>`."
msgstr ""
"Clúdaíonn na nótaí scaoilte seo na:ref: `gnéithe nua <whats-new-1.8>`, chomh "
"maith le roinnt athruithe: ref: `athruithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha ar "
"chúl<backwards-incompatible-1.8>` a mbeidh tú ag iarraidh a bheith ar an "
"eolas fúthu agus tú ag uasghrádú ó Django 1.7 nó leaganacha níos sine. "
"<removed-features-1.8>Táimid freisin: ref: `tús a chur leis an bpróiseas "
"diúltaithe do roinnt <deprecated-features-1.8>gnéithe `, agus tá roinnt "
"gnéithe tar éis deireadh a bpróiseas díscrúdaithe agus:ref: `baineadh`."

msgid ""
"Django 1.8 has been designated as Django's second :term:`long-term support "
"release <Long-term support release>`. It will receive security updates for "
"at least three years after its release. Support for the previous LTS, Django "
"1.4, will end 6 months from the release date of Django 1.8."
msgstr ""
"<Long-term support release>Ainmníodh Django 1.8 mar an dara téarma Django: "
"`scaoileadh tacaíochta fadtéarmach `. Gheobhaidh sé nuashonruithe slándála "
"ar feadh trí bliana ar a laghad tar éis a scaoilte Beidh deireadh le "
"tacaíocht don LTS roimhe seo, Django 1.4, 6 mhí ó dháta scaoilte Django 1.8."

msgid ""
"Django 1.8 requires Python 2.7, 3.2, 3.3, 3.4, or 3.5. We **highly "
"recommend** and only officially support the latest release of each series."
msgstr ""
"Éilíonn Django 1.8 Python 2.7, 3.2, 3.3, 3.4, nó 3.5. Molaimid** go hard** "
"agus ní thacaímid go hoifigiúil ach leis an scaoileadh is déanaí de gach "
"sraith."

msgid "Django 1.8 is the first release to support Python 3.5."
msgstr "Is é Django 1.8 an chéad eisiúint chun tacú le Python 3.5."

msgid ""
"Due to the end of upstream support for Python 3.2 in February 2016, we won't "
"test Django 1.8.x on Python 3.2 after the end of 2016."
msgstr ""
"Mar gheall ar dheireadh na tacaíochta suas srutha do Python 3.2 i mí Feabhra "
"2016, ní dhéanfaimid tástáil Django 1.8.x ar Python 3.2 tar éis dheireadh "
"2016."

msgid "What's new in Django 1.8"
msgstr "Cad atá nua i Django 1.8"

msgid "``Model._meta`` API"
msgstr "``Samhail. API _meta``"

msgid ""
"Django now has a formalized API for :doc:`Model._meta </ref/models/meta>`, "
"providing an officially supported way to :ref:`retrieve fields <model-meta-"
"field-api>` and filter fields based on their :ref:`attributes <model-field-"
"attributes>`."
msgstr ""
"Tá API foirmiúil ag Django anois le haghaidh: doc: `Samhail. </ref/models/"
"meta> <model-field-attributes>_meta`, ag soláthar bealach tacaithe go "
"hoifigiúil chuir:ref: `réimsí a aisghabháil `agus réimsí a scagadh bunaithe "
"ar <model-meta-field-api>a n:ref: `tréithe`."

msgid ""
"The ``Model._meta`` object has been part of Django since the days of "
"pre-0.96 \"Magic Removal\" -- it just wasn't an official, stable API. In "
"recognition of this, we've endeavored to maintain backwards-compatibility "
"with the old API endpoint where possible. However, API endpoints that aren't "
"part of the new official API have been deprecated and will eventually be "
"removed."
msgstr ""
"An ``Samhail. Tá réad _meta`` mar chuid de Django ó laethanta roimh 0.96 "
"“Magic Removal” - ní raibh sé ach API oifigiúil cobhsaí. Mar aitheantas air "
"seo, rinneamar iarracht comhoiriúnacht cúil a choinneáil leis an sean-"
"chríochphointe API nuair is féidir. Mar sin féin, tá críochphointí API nach "
"cuid den API oifigiúil nua dímheasta agus bainfear iad sa deireadh."

msgid "Multiple template engines"
msgstr "Innill teimpléad iliom"

msgid ""
"Django 1.8 defines a stable API for integrating template backends. It "
"includes built-in support for the Django template language and "
"for :class:`~django.template.backends.jinja2.Jinja2`. It supports rendering "
"templates with multiple engines within the same project. Learn more about "
"the new features in the :doc:`topic guide </topics/templates>` and check the "
"upgrade instructions in older versions of the documentation."
msgstr ""
"Sainmhíníonn Django 1.8 API cobhsaí chun cúltaca teimpléad a chomhtháthú. "
"Cuimsíonn sé tacaíocht ionsuite don teanga teimpléad Django agus le "
"haghaidh: class: `~django.template.backends.jinja2.jinja2`. Tacaíonn sé le "
"teimpléid rindreála le ilinnill laistigh den tionscadal céanna. Faigh "
"tuilleadh eolais faoi na gnéithe nua in:doc: `treoir topaic` agus seiceáil "
"na treoracha u</topics/templates> asghrádaithe i leaganacha níos sine den "
"doiciméadú."

msgid "Security enhancements"
msgstr "Feabhsuithe slándála"

msgid ""
"Several features of the :pypi:`django-secure` third-party library have been "
"integrated into "
"Django. :class:`django.middleware.security.SecurityMiddleware` provides "
"several security enhancements to the request/response cycle. The "
"new :option:`check --deploy` option allows you to check your production "
"settings file for ways to increase the security of your site."
msgstr ""
"Tá roinnt gnéithe den leabharlann tríú páirtí: pypi: `django-secure` "
"comhtháite i Django. :class: Soláthraíonn "
"`django.middleware.security.securityMiddleware` roinnt feabhsuithe slándála "
"don timthriall iarrata/freagartha. Ligeann an rogha nua:option: `check --"
"deploy` duit do chomhad socruithe táirgeachta a sheiceáil le haghaidh bealaí "
"chun slándáil do shuíomh a mhéadú."

msgid "New PostgreSQL specific functionality"
msgstr "Feidhmiúlacht shonrach nua PostgreSQL"

msgid ""
"Django now has a module with extensions for PostgreSQL specific features, "
"such "
"as :class:`~django.contrib.postgres.fields.ArrayField`, :class:`~django.contrib.postgres.fields.HStoreField`, :ref:`range-"
"fields`, and :lookup:`unaccent` lookup. A full breakdown of the features is "
"available :doc:`in the documentation </ref/contrib/postgres/index>`."
msgstr ""
"Tá modúl ag Django anois le síntí do ghnéithe sonracha PostgreSQL, mar "
"shampla:class: `~django.contrib.postgres.fields.arrayfield`, :class: "
"`~django.contrib.postgres.fields.hstorefield`, :ref: `range-fields`, "
"agus:lookup: `unaccent` lookup. Tá miondealú iomlán ar na gnéithe ar fáil: "
"doc: `sa doiciméadúis' </ref/contrib/postgres/index>."

msgid "New data types"
msgstr "Cineálacha sonraí nua"

msgid ""
"Django now has a :class:`~django.db.models.UUIDField` for storing "
"universally unique identifiers. It is stored as the native ``uuid`` data "
"type on PostgreSQL and as a fixed length character field on other backends. "
"There is a corresponding :class:`form field <django.forms.UUIDField>`."
msgstr ""
"Tá a: class: `~django.db.models.uuidfield` ag Django anois chun aitheantóirí "
"uathúla go huilíoch a stóráil. Stóráiltear é mar an chineál sonraí dúchasach "
"``uuid ``ar PostgreSQL agus mar réimse carachtar fad seasta ar chúlchúrsaí "
"eile. <django.forms.UUIDField>Tá comhfhreagrach ann: aicme: `réimse foirm `."

msgid ""
"Django now has a :class:`~django.db.models.DurationField` for storing "
"periods of time - modeled in Python by :class:`~python:datetime.timedelta`. "
"It is stored in the native ``interval`` data type on PostgreSQL, as a "
"``INTERVAL DAY(9) TO SECOND(6)`` on Oracle, and as a ``bigint`` of "
"microseconds on other backends. Date and time related arithmetic has also "
"been improved on all backends. There is a corresponding :class:`form field "
"<django.forms.DurationField>`."
msgstr ""
"Tá a: class: `~Django.db.Models.DurationField` ag Django anois chun tréimhsí "
"ama a stóráil - múnlaithe i Python ag:class: `~python:datetime.timedelta`. "
"Stóráiltear é sa chineál sonraí dúchasach ``interval ``ar PostgreSQL, mar "
"`INTERVAL DAY (9) GO SECOND (6)`` ar Oracle, agus mar `bigint ``de "
"mhicreasoicind ar chúltaca eile. Feabhsaíodh uimhríocht a bhaineann le dáta "
"agus am ar gach cúltaca freisin. <django.forms.DurationField>Tá "
"comhfhreagrach ann: aicme: `réimse foirm `."

msgid "Query Expressions, Conditional Expressions, and Database Functions"
msgstr "Nathanna Fiosrúcháin, Nathanna Coinníollach agus Feidhmean"

msgid ""
":doc:`Query Expressions </ref/models/expressions>` allow you to create, "
"customize, and compose complex SQL expressions. This has enabled annotate to "
"accept expressions other than aggregates. Aggregates are now able to "
"reference multiple fields, as well as perform arithmetic, similar to ``F()`` "
"objects. :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.order_by` has also gained "
"the ability to accept expressions."
msgstr ""
":doc: Ligeann `Expressions Questions` duit nathan</ref/models/expressions> "
"na casta SQL a chruthú, a shaincheapadh agus a chumadh. Chuir sé seo ar "
"chumas annotate glacadh le nathanna seachas comhiomlánacha. Tá "
"comhiomlánaithe in ann tagairt a dhéanamh anois le réimsí iolracha, chomh "
"maith le uimhríocht a dhéanamh, cosúil le rudaí `F () `. :meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.order_by` tá an cumas faighte ag glacadh "
"le nathanna freisin."

msgid ""
":doc:`Conditional Expressions </ref/models/conditional-expressions>` allow "
"you to use :keyword:`if` ... :keyword:`elif` ... :keyword:`else` logic "
"within queries."
msgstr ""
":doc: Ligeann `Expressions Coinníollach` duit:keyword: `if `</ref/models/"
"conditional-expressions>... :keyword: `elif`... :keyword: loighic `else` "
"laistigh de cheisteanna."

msgid ""
"A collection of :doc:`database functions </ref/models/database-functions>` "
"is also included with functionality such "
"as :class:`~django.db.models.functions.Coalesce`, :class:`~django.db.models.functions.Concat`, "
"and :class:`~django.db.models.functions.Substr`."
msgstr ""
"Tá bailiúchán de:doc: `feidhmeanna bunachar sonraí` san áireamh freisin le "
"feidhmiúlacht amsúil:class: `~Django.db.Models.Functions.Coalesce` </ref/"
"models/database-functions>, :class: `~Django.db.Models.Functions.concat`, "
"agus:class: `~Django.db.Models.Functions.substr`."

msgid "``TestCase`` data setup"
msgstr "Socrú sonraí ``Testcase ``"

msgid ""
":class:`~django.test.TestCase` has been refactored to allow for data "
"initialization at the class level using transactions and savepoints. "
"Database backends which do not support transactions, like MySQL with the "
"MyISAM storage engine, will still be able to run these tests but won't "
"benefit from the improvements. Tests are now run within two "
"nested :func:`~django.db.transaction.atomic()` blocks: one for the whole "
"class and one for each test."
msgstr ""
":class: “~django.test.testcase` athchóirithe chun sonraí a thionscnamh ag "
"leibhéal an ranga ag baint úsáide as idirbhearta agus pointí sábhála. Beidh "
"cúltaca bunachar sonraí nach dtacaíonn le hidirbhearta, cosúil le MySQL leis "
"an inneall stórála MyISAM, in ann na tástálacha seo a reáchtáil fós ach ní "
"bhainfidh siad leas as na feabhsuithe. Reáchtáiltear tástálacha anois "
"laistigh de dhá bhloc neasta: func: `~django.db.transaction.atomic () `: "
"ceann don rang iomlán agus ceann do gach tástáil."

msgid ""
"The class method :meth:`TestCase.setUpTestData() "
"<django.test.TestCase.setUpTestData>` adds the ability to set up test data "
"at the class level. Using this technique can speed up the tests as compared "
"to using ``setUp()``."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann an modh ranga: meth: `TestCase.setupTestData () "
"<django.test.TestCase.setUpTestData>`an cumas sonraí tástála a chur ar bun "
"ag leibhéal an ranga. Trí úsáid a bhaint as an teicníc seo is féidir leis na "
"tástálacha a bhrostú i gcomparáid le ``Setup () ``a úsáid."

msgid ""
"Fixture loading within ``TestCase`` is now performed once for the whole "
"``TestCase``."
msgstr ""
"Déantar luchtú daingneáin laistigh de ``Tástchás ``uair amháin anois don "
"``tástchás`` iomlán."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin` now has "
"a :meth:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.has_module_permission` method to "
"allow limiting access to the module on the admin index page."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.contrib.admin.modelAdmin` anois tá a: meth: "
"`~django.contrib.admin.modeladmin.has_module_permission` modh chun rochtain "
"a theorannú ar an modúl ar an leathanach innéacs riaracháin a cheadú."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.contrib.admin.InlineModelAdmin` now has an "
"attribute :attr:`~django.contrib.admin.InlineModelAdmin.show_change_link` "
"that supports showing a link to an inline object's change form."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.contrib.admin.inlineModelAdmin` tá tréith anois:attr: "
"`~django.contrib.admin.inlineModelAdmin.show_change_link` a thacaíonn le "
"nasc a thaispeáint le foirm athraithe réad inlíne."

msgid ""
"Use the new ``django.contrib.admin.RelatedOnlyFieldListFilter`` "
"in :attr:`ModelAdmin.list_filter "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.list_filter>` to limit the ``list_filter`` "
"choices to foreign objects which are attached to those from the "
"``ModelAdmin``."
msgstr ""
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.list_filter>Úsáid an "
"`Django.contrib.admin.RelatedOnlyFieldListFilter`` nua in:attr: "
"`ModelAdmin.list_Filter `chun na roghanna ``list_filter`` a theorannú le "
"rudaí eachtracha atá ceangailte leo siúd ón ``ModelAdmin``."

msgid ""
"The :meth:`ModelAdmin.delete_view() "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.delete_view>` displays a summary of objects "
"to be deleted on the deletion confirmation page."
msgstr ""
"Taispeánann an:Meth: `ModelAdmin.delete_view () "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.delete_view>`achoimre ar rudaí atá le "
"scriosadh ar an leathanach deimhnithe scriosadh."

msgid ""
"The jQuery library embedded in the admin has been upgraded to version 1.11.2."
msgstr ""
"Tá an leabharlann jQuery leabaithe sa riarachán uasghrádaithe go leagan "
"1.11.2."

msgid ""
"You can now specify :attr:`AdminSite.site_url "
"<django.contrib.admin.AdminSite.site_url>` in order to display a link to the "
"front-end site."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat anois a shonrú: attr: `adminsite.site_url "
"<django.contrib.admin.AdminSite.site_url>`d'fhonn nasc a thaispeáint chuig "
"an suíomh tosaigh."

msgid ""
"You can now specify :attr:`ModelAdmin.show_full_result_count "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.show_full_result_count>` to control whether "
"or not the full count of objects should be displayed on a filtered admin "
"page."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat anois a shonrú: attr: `ModelAdmin.show_full_result_count "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.show_full_result_count>`chun rialú a "
"dhéanamh ar chóir líon iomlán rudaí a thaispeáint ar leathanach riaracháin "
"scagtha nó nach bhfuil."

msgid ""
"The ``AdminSite.password_change()`` method now has an ``extra_context`` "
"parameter."
msgstr ""
"Tá paraiméadar ``extra_context`` anois ag an modh "
"``adminsite.password_change () ``."

msgid ""
"You can now control who may login to the admin site by overriding "
"only :meth:`AdminSite.has_permission() "
"<django.contrib.admin.AdminSite.has_permission>` "
"and :attr:`AdminSite.login_form "
"<django.contrib.admin.AdminSite.login_form>`. The ``base.html`` template has "
"a new block ``usertools`` which contains the user-specific header. A new "
"context variable ``has_permission``, which gets its value "
"from :meth:`~django.contrib.admin.AdminSite.has_permission`, indicates "
"whether the user may access the site."
msgstr ""
"<django.contrib.admin.AdminSite.has_permission><django.contrib.admin.AdminSite.login_form>Is "
"féidir leat a rialú anois cé a d'fhéadfadh logáil isteach ar an suíomh "
"riaracháin trí shárú amháin: meth: `adminsite.has_permit () `agus:attr: "
"`adminsite.login_form`. Tá bloc nua ``usertools`` sa teimpléad ``base.html`` "
"ina bhfuil an ceannteideal úsáideora sonrach. Léiríonn athróg comhthéacs nua "
"``has_permission``, a fhaigheann a luach ó:meth: "
"`~django.contrib.admin.admin.adminsite.has_permission`, an bhféadfaidh an t-"
"úsáideoir rochtain a fháil ar an suíomh."

msgid ""
"Foreign key dropdowns now have buttons for changing or deleting related "
"objects using a popup."
msgstr ""
"Tá cnaipí anois ag eochair eachtracha chun rudaí gaolmhara a athrú nó a "
"scriosadh ag baint úsáide as pop-up."

msgid ":mod:`django.contrib.admindocs`"
msgstr ":mod: `django.contrib.admindocs`"

msgid "reStructuredText is now parsed in model docstrings."
msgstr ""
"déantar reStructuredText a pharsáil anois i sraitheoga doctúir samhail."

msgid ""
"Authorization backends can now "
"raise :class:`~django.core.exceptions.PermissionDenied` "
"in :meth:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User.has_perm` "
"and :meth:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User.has_module_perms` to short-"
"circuit permission checking."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le cúltaca údaraithe a ardú anois:class: "
"`~django.core.exceptions.permissionDenied` in:meth: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.user.has_perm` agus:meth: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.user.has_module_permS` chun seiceáil cead "
"gearrchiorcad."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.contrib.auth.forms.PasswordResetForm` now has a "
"method :meth:`~django.contrib.auth.forms.PasswordResetForm.send_mail` that "
"can be overridden to customize the mail to be sent."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.contrib.auth.forms.PasswordResetForm` anois tá modh: meth: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.forms.passwordResetForm.send_mail` is féidir a "
"athshlánú chun an post atá le seoladh a shaincheapadh."

msgid ""
"The ``max_length`` of :attr:`Permission.name "
"<django.contrib.auth.models.Permission.name>` has been increased from 50 to "
"255 characters. Please run the database migration."
msgstr ""
"<django.contrib.auth.models.Permission.name>Tá an ``max_length ``o:attr: "
"`Permission.name `méadaithe ó 50 go 255 carachtar. Rith an imirce bunachar "
"sonraí le do thoil."

msgid ""
":attr:`~django.contrib.auth.models.CustomUser.USERNAME_FIELD` "
"and :attr:`~django.contrib.auth.models.CustomUser.REQUIRED_FIELDS` now "
"supports :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey`\\s."
msgstr ""
":attr: `~django.contrib.auth.models.customUser.UserName_Field` agus:attr: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.customUser.required_fields` tacaíonn "
"anois:class: `~Django.db.Models.ForeignKey`\\ s."

msgid ""
"The default iteration count for the PBKDF2 password hasher has been "
"increased by 33%. This backwards compatible change will not affect users who "
"have subclassed ``django.contrib.auth.hashers.PBKDF2PasswordHasher`` to "
"change the default value."
msgstr ""
"Méadaíodh 33% ar an líon athraithe réamhshocraithe don hasher pasfhocal "
"PBKDF2. Ní dhéanfaidh an t-athrú comhoiriúnach ar chúl difear d'úsáideoirí a "
"bhfuil fo-aicmithe ag ``Django.contrib.auth.hashers.pbkdf2PasswordHasher`` "
"chun an luach réamhshocraithe a athrú."

msgid ""
"A new :doc:`GeoJSON serializer </ref/contrib/gis/serializers>` is now "
"available."
msgstr ""
"Tá nua:doc: `GeoJSON serializer` ar fáil anois </ref/contrib/gis/"
"serializers>."

msgid ""
"It is now allowed to include a subquery as a geographic lookup argument, for "
"example "
"``City.objects.filter(point__within=Country.objects.filter(continent='Africa').values('mpoly'))``."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé ceadaithe anois fo-cheist a áireamh mar argóint cuardaigh geografach, "
"mar shampla ``City.Objects.filter (point__within=Country.Objects.filter "
"(continent='Africa') .values ('mpoly')) ``."

msgid ""
"The SpatiaLite backend now supports ``Collect`` and ``Extent`` aggregates "
"when the database version is 3.0 or later."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn an cúltaca SpatiaLite anois le comhiomlánacha ``Collect`` agus "
"``Extent`` nuair a bhíonn leagan an bhunachar sonraí 3.0 nó níos déanaí."

msgid ""
"The PostGIS 2 ``CREATE EXTENSION postgis`` and the SpatiaLite ``SELECT "
"InitSpatialMetaData`` initialization commands are now automatically run "
"by :djadmin:`migrate`."
msgstr ""
"Déantar an PostGIS 2 `CREATE EXTENSION postgis ``agus na horduithe "
"tionscnaíochta SpatialLite ``SELECT initSpatialMetadata`` a reáchtáil go "
"huathoibríoch anois ag: djadmin: `migrate`."

msgid ""
"The GDAL interface now supports retrieving properties of :ref:`raster "
"(image) data file <raster-data-source-objects>`."
msgstr ""
"<raster-data-source-objects>Tacaíonn comhéadan GDAL anois le hairíonna "
"comhad sonraí: ref: `raster (íomhá) `a aisghabháil."

msgid ""
"Compatibility shims for ``SpatialRefSys`` and ``GeometryColumns`` changed in "
"Django 1.2 have been removed."
msgstr ""
"Baineadh shimsí comhoiriúnachta do ``SpatialRefsys`` agus "
"``GeometryColumns`` a athraíodh i Django 1.2."

msgid ""
"All GDAL-related exceptions are now raised with ``GDALException``. The "
"former ``OGRException`` has been kept for backwards compatibility but should "
"not be used any longer."
msgstr ""
"Ardaítear gach eisceacht a bhaineann le GDAL anois le ``GdalException``. "
"Coinníodh an sean-`Ogrexception` le haghaidh comhoiriúnacht ar ais ach níor "
"chóir é a úsáid níos mó."

msgid ""
"Session cookie is now deleted "
"after :meth:`~django.contrib.sessions.backends.base.SessionBase.flush()` is "
"called."
msgstr ""
"Scriostar fianán seisiúin anois tar éis: meth: "
"`~django.contrib.sessions.backends.base.sessionbase.flush () `tugtar."

msgid ""
"The new :attr:`Sitemap.i18n <django.contrib.sitemaps.Sitemap.i18n>` "
"attribute allows you to generate a sitemap based on the :setting:`LANGUAGES` "
"setting."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an tréith nua:attr: `SiteMap.i18n "
"<django.contrib.sitemaps.Sitemap.i18n>`duit léarscáil an láithreáin "
"ghiniúint bunaithe ar an socrú: socrú: `LANGUAGES`."

msgid ""
":func:`~django.contrib.sites.shortcuts.get_current_site` will now lookup the "
"current site based on :meth:`request.get_host() "
"<django.http.HttpRequest.get_host>` if the :setting:`SITE_ID` setting is not "
"defined."
msgstr ""
"<django.http.HttpRequest.get_host>:func: "
"`~django.contrib.sites.shortcuts.get_current_site` cuardóidh anois ar an "
"suíomh reatha bunaithe ar:meth: `request.get_host () `mura sainmhínítear an "
"socrú:setting: `SITE_ID`."

msgid ""
"The default :class:`~django.contrib.sites.models.Site` created when running "
"``migrate`` now respects the :setting:`SITE_ID` setting (instead of always "
"using ``pk=1``)."
msgstr ""
"Tá meas ag an réamhshocraithe:class: `~django.contrib.sites.models.site` a "
"cruthaíodh agus ``migrate`` á reáchtáil anois leis an socrú:setting: "
"`SITE_ID` (in ionad `pk=1`` a úsáid i gcónaí)."

msgid ""
"The ``incr()`` method of the "
"``django.core.cache.backends.locmem.LocMemCache`` backend is now thread-safe."
msgstr ""
"Tá an modh `incr () ``den chúltaca "
"``django.core.cache.backends.locmem.locmemcache`` sábháilte le snáithe anois."

msgid "Cryptography"
msgstr "Cripteagrafaíocht"

msgid ""
"The ``max_age`` parameter of "
"the :meth:`django.core.signing.TimestampSigner.unsign` method now also "
"accepts a :py:class:`datetime.timedelta` object."
msgstr ""
"Glacann paraiméadar ``max_age`` den modh: meth: "
"`django.core.signing.timeStampSigner.unsign` anois le réad a:py:class: "
"`datetime.timedelta`."

msgid ""
"The MySQL backend no longer strips microseconds from ``datetime`` values as "
"MySQL 5.6.4 and up supports fractional seconds depending on the declaration "
"of the datetime field (when ``DATETIME`` includes fractional precision "
"greater than 0). New datetime database columns created with Django 1.8 and "
"MySQL 5.6.4 and up will support microseconds. See the :ref:`MySQL database "
"notes <mysql-fractional-seconds>` for more details."
msgstr ""
"Ní bhaineann an cúltaca MySQL microsoicind a thuilleadh ó luachanna "
"``datetime` toisc go dtacaíonn MySQL 5.6.4 agus suas le soicindí codánacha "
"ag brath ar dhearbhú an réimse dáta-ama (nuair a chuimsíonn ``DATETIME`` "
"cruinneas codánach níos mó ná 0). Tacóidh colúin nua bunachar sonraí dáta-"
"ama a cruthaíodh le Django 1.8 agus MySQL 5.6.4 agus suas le micreasoicind. "
"Féach na:ref: `Nótaí bunachar sonraí MySQL <mysql-fractional-seconds>`le "
"haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid ""
"The MySQL backend no longer creates explicit indexes for foreign keys when "
"using the InnoDB storage engine, as MySQL already creates them automatically."
msgstr ""
"Ní chruthaíonn inneall MySQL innéacsanna follasacha d’eochracha eachtracha a "
"thuilleadh agus inneall stórála InnoDB á úsáid, mar go gcruthaíonn MySQL iad "
"go huathoibríoch cheana féin."

msgid ""
"The Oracle backend no longer defines the ``connection_persists_old_columns`` "
"feature as ``True``. Instead, Oracle will now include a cache busting clause "
"when getting the description of a table."
msgstr ""
"Ní shainmhíníonn cúltaca Oracle an ghné ``connection_persists_old_columns` a "
"thuilleadh mar ``True``. Ina áit sin, cuirfidh Oracle clásal bustaíochta "
"taisce anois agus tú ag fáil tuairisc ar thábla."

msgid ""
":ref:`Email backends <topic-email-backends>` now support the context manager "
"protocol for opening and closing connections."
msgstr ""
":ref: Tacaíonn `cúltaca ríomhphoist <topic-email-backends>`anois le prótacal "
"bainisteora comhthéacs chun naisc a oscailt agus a dhúnadh."

msgid ""
"The SMTP email backend now supports ``keyfile`` and ``certfile`` "
"authentication with the :setting:`EMAIL_SSL_CERTFILE` "
"and :setting:`EMAIL_SSL_KEYFILE` settings."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn an cúltaca ríomhphoist SMTP anois le fíordheimhniú ``keyfile`` agus "
"``certfile`` leis na socruithe:: `EMAIL_SSL_CERTFILE` agus:setting: "
"`EMAIL_SSL_KEYFILE`."

msgid ""
"The SMTP :class:`~django.core.mail.backends.smtp.EmailBackend` now supports "
"setting the ``timeout`` parameter with the :setting:`EMAIL_TIMEOUT` setting."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn an SMTP: Class: `~django.core.mail.backends.smtp.emailBackend` "
"anois leis an bparaiméadar ``timeout`` a shocrú leis an socrú: setting: "
"`EMAIL_TIMEOUT`."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.core.mail.EmailMessage` and ``EmailMultiAlternatives`` now "
"support the ``reply_to`` parameter."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.core.mail.emailMessage` agus ``EmailMultiAlternatives`` "
"tacaíonn anois leis an paraiméadar ``reply_to`."

msgid ""
":meth:`Storage.get_available_name() "
"<django.core.files.storage.Storage.get_available_name>` "
"and :meth:`Storage.save() <django.core.files.storage.Storage.save>` now take "
"a ``max_length`` argument to implement storage-level maximum filename length "
"constraints. Filenames exceeding this argument will get truncated. This "
"prevents a database error when appending a unique suffix to a long filename "
"that already exists on the storage. See the :ref:`deprecation note <storage-"
"max-length-update>` about adding this argument to your custom storage "
"classes."
msgstr ""
"<django.core.files.storage.Storage.save>:meth: `Storage.get_available_name "
"() <django.core.files.storage.Storage.get_available_name>`agus:meth: "
"`Storage.save ()` glac argóint ``max_length ``anois chun srianta uasmhéid "
"ainm comhaid ar leibhéal stórála a chur i bhfeidhm. Déanfar ainmneacha "
"comhaid a sháraíonn an argóint seo a ghearradh. Cuireann sé seo cosc ar "
"earráid bunachar sonraí agus iarmhír uathúil á chur leis ainm fada comhaid "
"atá ann cheana féin ar an stóráil. Féach an:ref: `nóta díghabhála <storage-"
"max-length-update>`maidir leis an argóint seo a chur le do ranganna stórála "
"saincheaptha."

msgid ""
"Form widgets now render attributes with a value of ``True`` or ``False`` as "
"HTML5 boolean attributes."
msgstr ""
"Déanann giuirléidí foirme tréithe anois le luach ``True`` nó `False`` mar "
"thréithe boolean HTML5."

msgid ""
"The new :meth:`~django.forms.Form.has_error()` method allows checking if a "
"specific error has happened."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an modh nua:meth: `~django.forms.form.has_error () `a sheiceáil an "
"bhfuil earráid ar leith tarla."

msgid ""
"If :attr:`~django.forms.Form.required_css_class` is defined on a form, then "
"the ``<label>`` tags for required fields will have this class present in its "
"attributes."
msgstr ""
"<label>Má shainmhínítear `~django.forms.form.required_css_class` ar fhoirm, "
"ansin beidh an rang seo i láthair ina tréithe ar na clibeanna ```do réimsí "
"riachtanacha."

msgid ""
"The rendering of non-field errors in unordered lists (``<ul>``) now includes "
"``nonfield`` in its list of classes to distinguish them from field-specific "
"errors."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn rindreáil earráidí neamh-réimse i liostaí neamh-ordaithe (```<ul>) "
"anois ``neamh-réimse`` ina liosta ranganna chun iad a idirdhealú ó earráidí "
"réimsiú-shonracha."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.forms.Field` now accepts "
"a :attr:`~django.forms.Field.label_suffix` argument, which will override the "
"form's :attr:`~django.forms.Form.label_suffix`. This enables customizing the "
"suffix on a per-field basis — previously it wasn't possible to override a "
"form's :attr:`~django.forms.Form.label_suffix` while using  shortcuts such "
"as ``{{ form.as_p }}`` in templates."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.forms.field` glacann anois le ha:attr: "
"`~django.forms.field.label_suffix` argóint, a sháróidh an fhoirm 's:attr: "
"`~django.forms.form.label_suffix`. Cuireann sé seo ar chumas an iarmhír a "
"shaincheapadh ar bhonn in aghaidh an réimse - roimhe seo ní raibh sé "
"indéanta foirm 's:attr: `~django.forms.form.label_suffix` a shárú agus "
"aicearraí mar ``{{form.as_p}} `a úsáid i dteimpléid."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.forms.SelectDateWidget` now accepts "
"an :attr:`~django.forms.SelectDateWidget.empty_label` argument, which will "
"override the top list choice label when :class:`~django.forms.DateField` is "
"not required."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.forms.selectDateWidget` glacann anois:attr: "
"`~django.forms.selectDateWidget.empty_label` argóint, a sháróidh an lipéad "
"rogha liosta barr nuain:class: `~Django.Forms.DateField` nach bhfuil gá."

msgid ""
"After an :class:`~django.forms.ImageField` has been cleaned and validated, "
"the ``UploadedFile`` object will have an additional ``image`` attribute "
"containing the Pillow ``Image`` instance used to check if the file was a "
"valid image. It will also update ``UploadedFile.content_type`` with the "
"image's content type as determined by Pillow."
msgstr ""
"Tar éis an:class: `~django.forms.imagefield` a ghlanadh agus a bhailíochtú, "
"beidh tréith breise ```image`` ag an réad ``UploadedFile`` ina bhfuil an cás "
"Pillow ``Image`` a úsáidtear chun seiceáil an raibh an comhad ina íomhá "
"bailí. Déanfaidh sé nuashonrú freisin ``uploadedfile.content_type`` le "
"cineál ábhair na híomhá mar a chinneann Pillow."

msgid ""
"You can now pass a callable that returns an iterable of choices when "
"instantiating a :class:`~django.forms.ChoiceField`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat glaoch a rith anois a thugann athrá roghanna ar ais agus a: "
"class: `~django.forms.choicefield` á gcur isteach."

msgid ""
"Generic views that "
"use :class:`~django.views.generic.list.MultipleObjectMixin` may now specify "
"the ordering applied to "
"the :attr:`~django.views.generic.list.MultipleObjectMixin.queryset` by "
"setting :attr:`~django.views.generic.list.MultipleObjectMixin.ordering` or "
"overriding :meth:`~django.views.generic.list.MultipleObjectMixin.get_ordering()`."
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh tuairimí cineálacha a úsáide:class: "
"`~Django.Views.Generic.List.MultipleObjectMixin` an t-ordú a chuirtear i "
"bhfeidhm ar:attr: `~django.views.generic.list.multipleObjectMixin.QuerySet` "
"a shonrú trí shocrú: attr: "
"`~django.views.generic.list.multipleObjectMixin.Ordering` nó "
"overriding` :meth: "
"`~django.views.generic.list.multipleObjectMixin.get_Ordering () `."

msgid ""
"The new :attr:`SingleObjectMixin.query_pk_and_slug "
"<django.views.generic.detail.SingleObjectMixin.query_pk_and_slug>` attribute "
"allows changing the behavior "
"of :meth:`~django.views.generic.detail.SingleObjectMixin.get_object()` so "
"that it'll perform its lookup using both the primary key and the slug."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn an tréith nua:attr: `SingleObjectMixin.query_pk_and_slug "
"`<django.views.generic.detail.SingleObjectMixin.query_pk_and_slug>iompar: "
"meth: `~django.views.generic.detail.singleObjectMixin.get_object ()` a athrú "
"ionas go ndéanfaidh sé a chuardach ag baint úsáide as an eochair phríomhúil "
"agus an slug araon."

msgid ""
"The :meth:`~django.views.generic.edit.FormMixin.get_form()` method doesn't "
"require a ``form_class`` to be provided anymore. If not provided "
"``form_class`` defaults "
"to :meth:`~django.views.generic.edit.FormMixin.get_form_class()`."
msgstr ""
"Ní éilíonn an modh:Meth: `~django.views.generic.edit.formmixin.get_form () "
"``form_class`` a sholáthar níos mó. Mura soláthraítear réamhshocraithe "
"``form_class`` to:meth: `~django.views.generic.edit.formmixin.get_form_class "
"() `."

msgid ""
"Placeholders in :attr:`ModelFormMixin.success_url "
"<django.views.generic.edit.ModelFormMixin.success_url>` now support the "
"Python :py:meth:`str.format()` syntax. The legacy ``%(<foo>)s`` syntax is "
"still supported but will be removed in Django 1.10."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn sealbhóirí ion:attr: `ModelFormMixin.success_url "
"<django.views.generic.edit.ModelFormMixin.success_url>`anois leis an "
"gcomhréir Python: py:Meth: `str.format ()`. Tacaítear fós leis an gcomhréir "
"oid <foo>hreachta ``% () s`` ach bainfear í i Django 1.10."

msgid ""
":setting:`FORMAT_MODULE_PATH` can now be a list of strings representing "
"module paths. This allows importing several format modules from different "
"reusable apps. It also allows overriding those custom formats in your main "
"Django project."
msgstr ""
":setting: Is féidir `FORMAT_MODULE_PATH` a bheith ina liosta de na teaghráin "
"a léiríonn cosáin modúl anois. Ligeann sé seo roinnt modúil formáide a "
"allmhairiú ó aipeanna athúsáidte Ligeann sé freisin na formáidí saincheaptha "
"sin a shárú i do phríomhthionscadal Django."

msgid ""
"The :class:`django.utils.log.AdminEmailHandler` class now has "
"a :meth:`~django.utils.log.AdminEmailHandler.send_mail` method to make it "
"more subclass friendly."
msgstr ""
"Tá a: meth: `~django.utils.log.adminemailHandler` modh anois ag an "
"rang:class: `~django.utils.log.adminemailHandler.send_mail` chun é a "
"dhéanamh níos cairdiúla do fho-aicme."

msgid ""
"Database connections are now always closed after a management command called "
"from the command line has finished doing its job."
msgstr ""
"Tá naisc bhunachar sonraí dúnta anois i gcónaí tar éis d'ordú bainistíochta "
"ar a dtugtar ón líne ordaithe a chuid oibre a dhéanamh críochnaithe."

msgid ""
"Commands from alternate package formats like eggs are now also discovered."
msgstr ""
"Aimsítear orduithe ó fhormáidí malartacha pacáiste mar uibheacha anois "
"freisin."

msgid ""
"The new :option:`dumpdata --output` option allows specifying a file to which "
"the serialized data is written."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an rogha nua:option: `dumpdata --output` comhad a shonrú ina bhfuil "
"na sonraí sraitheach scríofa air."

msgid ""
"The new :option:`makemessages --exclude` and :option:`compilemessages --"
"exclude` options allow excluding specific locales from processing."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn na roghanna nua:option: `makemessages --exclude` agus:option: "
"`compilemessages --exclude` a eisiamh ó phróiseáil."

msgid ""
":djadmin:`compilemessages` now has a ``--use-fuzzy`` or ``-f`` option which "
"includes fuzzy translations into compiled files."
msgstr ""
":djadmin: Tá rogha ``--use-fuzzy`` nó ``-f`` anois ag `compilemessages` a "
"chuimsíonn aistriúcháin doiléir i gcomhaid thiomsaithe."

msgid ""
"The :option:`loaddata --ignorenonexistent` option now ignores data for "
"models that no longer exist."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an roghna:option: `loaddata --ignorenonexistent` neamhaird anois ar "
"shonraí do mhúnlaí nach bhfuil ann a thuilleadh."

msgid ":djadmin:`runserver` now uses daemon threads for faster reloading."
msgstr ""
": djadmin: Úsáideann `runserver` snáitheanna daemon anois le haghaidh "
"athluchtú níos tapa."

msgid ""
":djadmin:`inspectdb` now outputs ``Meta.unique_together``. It is also able "
"to introspect :class:`~django.db.models.AutoField` for MySQL and PostgreSQL "
"databases."
msgstr ""
":djadmin: `inspectdb` anois aschuireann ``Meta.Unique_Together``. Tá sé in "
"ann ionfheiceáil freisin: class: `~django.db.models.autofield` do bhunachair "
"sonraí MySQL agus PostgreSQL."

msgid ""
"When calling management commands with options "
"using :func:`~django.core.management.call_command`, the option name can "
"match the command line option name (without the initial dashes) or the final "
"option destination variable name, but in either case, the resulting option "
"received by the command is now always the ``dest`` name specified in the "
"command option definition (as long as the command uses the :mod:`argparse` "
"module)."
msgstr ""
"Agus orduithe bainistíochta á ghlaoch agat le roghanna ag baint úsáid:func: "
"`~django.core.management.call_command`, is féidir leis an ainm rogha líne "
"ordaithe a mheaitseáil (gan na sraitheanna tosaigh) nó ainm athróg ceann "
"scríbe an rogha deiridh, is é an rogha a fhaigheann an t-ordú anois an t-"
"ainm `dest`` a shonraítear sa sainmhíniú rogha ordaithe (chomh fada agus a "
"úsáideann an t-ordú an:mod: modúl parse)."

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`dbshell` command now supports MySQL's optional SSL certificate "
"authority setting (``--ssl-ca``)."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn an t-ordú: DJadmin: `dbshell` anois le socrú údaráis roghnach "
"deimhnithe SSL MySQL (``- ssl-ca``)."

msgid ""
"The new :option:`makemigrations --name` allows giving the migration(s) a "
"custom name instead of a generated one."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn an nua:option: `makemigrations --name` ainm saincheaptha a "
"thabhairt don imirce/na himirce in ionad ceann a ghintear."

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`loaddata` command now prevents repeated fixture loading. "
"If :setting:`FIXTURE_DIRS` contains duplicates or a default fixture "
"directory path (``app_name/fixtures``), an exception is raised."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann an t-ordú: Djadmin: `loaddata` cosc anois ar luchtú daingneáin arís "
"agus arís eile. Má tá dúbailtí nó cosán eolaire daingneáin réamhshocraithe "
"(``app_name/fixtures``) i `FIXTURE_DIRS`, ardaítear eisceacht."

msgid ""
"The new ``makemigrations --exit`` option allows exiting with an error code "
"if no migrations are created."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn an rogha nua ``makemigrations --exit`` imeacht le cód earráide "
"mura gcruthaítear aon imirce."

msgid ""
"The new :djadmin:`showmigrations` command allows listing all migrations and "
"their dependencies in a project."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an t-ordú nua:djadmin: `showmigrations` gach imirce agus a gcuid "
"spleáchais a liostáil i dtionscadal."

msgid "Middleware"
msgstr "Meán-earraí"

msgid ""
"The :attr:`CommonMiddleware.response_redirect_class "
"<django.middleware.common.CommonMiddleware.response_redirect_class>` "
"attribute allows you to customize the redirects issued by the middleware."
msgstr ""
"<django.middleware.common.CommonMiddleware.response_redirect_class>Ceadaíonn "
"an tréith: Attr: `CommonMiddleware.Response_Redirect_class `duit na "
"hathreoruithe arna eisiúint ag an middleware a shaincheapadh."

msgid ""
"A debug message will be logged to the ``django.request`` logger when a "
"middleware raises a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.MiddlewareNotUsed` "
"exception in :setting:`DEBUG` mode."
msgstr ""
"Logálfar teachtaireacht dífhabhtaithe chuig an logger ``django.request`` "
"nuair a ardaíonn middleware a:exc: "
"`~django.core.exceptions.middlewareNotUsed` eisceacht in:setting: `DEBUG`."

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.db.migrations.operations.RunSQL` operation can now "
"handle parameters passed to the SQL statements."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leis an oibríocht: Class: "
"`~django.db.migrations.operations.runsql` paraiméadair a chuirtear chuig na "
"ráitis SQL a láimhseáil anois."

msgid ""
"It is now possible to have migrations (most probably :ref:`data migrations "
"<data-migrations>`) for applications without models."
msgstr ""
"<data-migrations>Is féidir anois imirce a bheith agat (is dóichí: ref: "
"`imirce sonraí `) d'iarratais gan samhlacha."

msgid ""
"Migrations can now :ref:`serialize model managers <using-managers-in-"
"migrations>` as part of the model state."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le himirce anois:ref: `bainisteoirí samhlacha a shraithu <using-"
"managers-in-migrations>'mar chuid den stát samhail."

msgid ""
"A :ref:`generic mechanism to handle the deprecation of model fields "
"<migrations-removing-model-fields>` was added."
msgstr ""
"<migrations-removing-model-fields>A: Ref: Cuireadh `meicníocht chineálach "
"chun díghníomhú réimsí samhlacha a láimhseáil leis."

msgid ""
"The :meth:`RunPython.noop() "
"<django.db.migrations.operations.RunPython.noop>` and :attr:`RunSQL.noop "
"<django.db.migrations.operations.RunSQL.noop>` class method/attribute were "
"added to ease in making ``RunPython`` and ``RunSQL`` operations reversible."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.migrations.operations.RunSQL.noop>Cuireadh modh/tréith aicme: "
"Meth: `RunPython.noop () "
"<django.db.migrations.operations.RunPython.noop>`agus:attr: `Runsql.noop` "
"chun oibríochtaí `RunPython`` agus `Runsql`` a dhéanamh inchúlghabháilte."

msgid ""
"The migration operations :class:`~django.db.migrations.operations.RunPython` "
"and :class:`~django.db.migrations.operations.RunSQL` now call "
"the :meth:`allow_migrate` method of database routers. The router can use the "
"newly introduced ``app_label`` and ``hints`` arguments to make a routing "
"decision. To take advantage of this feature you need to update the router to "
"the new ``allow_migrate`` signature, see the :ref:`deprecation section "
"<deprecated-signature-of-allow-migrate>` for more details."
msgstr ""
"Glaonn na hoibríochtaí imirce:class: "
"`~django.db.migrations.operations.runpython` agus:class: "
"`~django.db.migrations.operations.runsql` anois ar an modh: `allow_migrate` "
"de ródairí bunachar sonraí. Is féidir leis an ródaire na hargóintí "
"``app_label`` agus `hints`` nua-tugadh a úsáid chun cinneadh ródaithe a "
"dhéanamh. <deprecated-signature-of-allow-migrate>Chun leas a bhaint as an "
"ngné seo ní mór duit an ródaire a nuashonrú go dtí an síniú nua "
"`allow_migrate``, féach an ranna:ref: `diprecation `le haghaidh tuilleadh "
"sonraí."

msgid ""
"Django now logs at most 9000 queries in ``connections.queries``, in order to "
"prevent excessive memory usage in long-running processes in debug mode."
msgstr ""
"Logálann Django anois 9000 fiosrúchán ar a mhéad i `connections.queries``, "
"d'fhonn úsáid iomarcach cuimhne a chosc i bpróisis fhada i mód dífhabhtaithe."

msgid ""
"There is now a model ``Meta`` option to define a :attr:`default related name "
"<django.db.models.Options.default_related_name>` for all relational fields "
"of a model."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.Options.default_related_name>Tá rogha samhail ``Meta`` ann "
"anois chun a: attr: `ainm gaolmhar réamhshocraithe `a shainiú do gach réimse "
"gaolmhar de mhúnla."

msgid ""
"Pickling models and querysets across different versions of Django isn't "
"officially supported (it may work, but there's no guarantee). An extra "
"variable that specifies the current Django version is now added to the "
"pickled state of models and querysets, and Django raises a "
"``RuntimeWarning`` when these objects are unpickled in a different version "
"than the one in which they were pickled."
msgstr ""
"Ní thacaítear go hoifigiúil le samhlacha piceála agus ceisteanna cearraí ar "
"fud leaganacha éagsúla de Django (b'fhéidir go n-oibreoidh sé, ach níl aon "
"ráthaíocht ann). Cuirtear athróg breise a shonraíonn an leagan reatha Django "
"anois le staid picilte na samhlacha agus na gcearaiseanna, agus ardaíonn "
"Django ``RuntimeWarning`` nuair a dhéantar na rudaí seo neamhphicilte i "
"leagan difriúil ná an ceann inar piceáladh iad."

msgid ""
"Added :meth:`Model.from_db() <django.db.models.Model.from_db()>` which "
"Django uses whenever objects are loaded using the ORM. The method allows "
"customizing model loading behavior."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.Model.from_db () >Cuireadh leis: Meth: `Model.from_DB (`a "
"úsáideann Django aon uair a luchtaítear rudaí ag baint úsáide as an ORM. "
"Ligeann an modh iompar luchtaithe samhail a shaincheapadh."

msgid ""
"``extra(select={...})`` now allows you to escape a literal ``%s`` sequence "
"using ``%%s``."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann ``extra (select= {...}) `duit anois seicheamh liteartha ``%s`` éalú "
"ag baint úsáide as ``%%s``."

msgid ""
":doc:`Custom Lookups</howto/custom-lookups>` can now be registered using a "
"decorator pattern."
msgstr ""
":doc: Is féidir `Cuardach Saincheapaithe' a chlárú anois ag baint úsá@@</"
"howto/custom-lookups> ide as patrún maisitheora."

msgid ""
"The new :attr:`Transform.bilateral <django.db.models.Transform.bilateral>` "
"attribute allows creating bilateral transformations. These transformations "
"are applied to both ``lhs`` and ``rhs`` when used in a lookup expression, "
"providing opportunities for more sophisticated lookups."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn an tréith nua:attr: `Transform.bilateral "
"<django.db.models.Transform.bilateral>`claochlú déthaobhacha a chruthú. "
"Cuirtear na claochlú seo i bhfeidhm ar ``lhs`` agus `rhs`` araon nuair a "
"úsáidtear iad i léiriú cuardaigh, ag soláthar deiseanna le haghaidh "
"cuardaigh níos sofaisticiúla."

msgid ""
"SQL special characters (\\, %, _) are now escaped properly when a pattern "
"lookup (e.g. ``contains``, ``startswith``, etc.) is used with an ``F()`` "
"expression as the right-hand side. In those cases, the escaping is performed "
"by the database, which can lead to somewhat complex queries involving nested "
"``REPLACE`` function calls."
msgstr ""
"Éalaítear carachtair speisialta SQL (\\,%, _) i gceart anois nuair a "
"úsáidtear cuardach patrún (m.sh. ``contains``, ``startswith`, srl.) le "
"abairt ``F () ``mar an taobh deise. Sna cásanna sin, déanann an bunachar "
"sonraí an éalú, rud a d'fhéadfadh ceisteanna beagán casta a bheith mar "
"thoradh ar ghlaonna feidhme ``REPLACE`` neadaithe."

msgid ""
"You can now refresh model instances by using :meth:`Model.refresh_from_db() "
"<django.db.models.Model.refresh_from_db>`."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.Model.refresh_from_db>Is féidir leat cásanna samhail a "
"athnuachan anois trí:meth: `Model.fresh_from_db () `a úsáid."

msgid ""
"You can now get the set of deferred fields for a model "
"using :meth:`Model.get_deferred_fields() "
"<django.db.models.Model.get_deferred_fields>`."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.Model.get_deferred_fields>Is féidir leat an tacar réimsí "
"iarchurtha a fháil anois do mhúnla ag baint úsáidea:meth: "
"`Model.get_deferred_fields () `."

msgid ""
"Model field ``default``’s are now used when primary key field's are set to "
"``None``."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear réimsí samhail ``réamhshocraithe`` anois nuair a shocraítear "
"príomhréimsí eochair go ``None``."

msgid ""
"Exceptions from the ``(receiver, exception)`` tuples returned "
"by :meth:`Signal.send_robust() <django.dispatch.Signal.send_robust>` now "
"have their traceback attached as a ``__traceback__`` attribute."
msgstr ""
"<django.dispatch.Signal.send_robust>Tá eisceachtaí ó na tupáin ``(glacadóir, "
"eisceacht)`` ar ais ag: meth: `signal.send_robust () `tá a rianairiú "
"ceangailte anois mar thréith ``__traceback__``."

msgid ""
"The ``environ`` argument, which contains the WSGI environment structure from "
"the request, was added to the :data:`~django.core.signals.request_started` "
"signal."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an argóint ``timpeallacht ``, ina bhfuil struchtúr timpeallachta "
"WSGI ón iarraidh, leis an gcomhartha: data: "
"`~django.core.signals.request_started`."

msgid ""
"You can now import the :func:`~django.test.signals.setting_changed` signal "
"from ``django.core.signals`` to avoid loading ``django.test`` in non-test "
"situations. Django no longer does so itself."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an comhartha: func: `~django.test.signals.setting_changed` a "
"iompórtáil anois ó ``django.core.signals`` chun luchtú ``django.test`` a "
"sheachaint i gcásanna neamh-tástála. Ní dhéanann Django é sin féin a "
"thuilleadh."

msgid "System Check Framework"
msgstr "Creat Seiceála Córais"

msgid ":attr:`~django.core.checks.register` can now be used as a function."
msgstr ""
":attr: Is féidir `~django.core.checks.register` a úsáid anois mar fheidhm."

msgid ""
":tfilter:`urlize` now supports domain-only links that include characters "
"after the top-level domain (e.g. ``djangoproject.com/`` and "
"``djangoproject.com/download/``)."
msgstr ""
":tfilter: Tacaíonn `urlize` anois le naisc fearainn amháin a chuimsíonn "
"carachtair tar éis an fhearann barrleibhéil (m.sh. ``djangoproject.com/`` "
"agus ``djangoproject.com/download/``)."

msgid ""
":tfilter:`urlize` doesn't treat exclamation marks at the end of a domain or "
"its query string as part of the URL (the URL in e.g. ``'djangoproject.com!`` "
"is ``djangoproject.com``)"
msgstr ""
":tfilter: Ní dhéileálann `urlize` le marcanna buaitíochta ag deireadh "
"fearainn nó a shreang fiosrúcháin mar chuid den URL (an URL i m.sh. "
"``djangoproject.com! ``is é ``djangoproject.com``)"

msgid ""
"Added a :class:`locmem.Loader <django.template.loaders.locmem.Loader>` class "
"that loads Django templates from a Python dictionary."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh a:class leis: aicme `LocMem.Loader "
"<django.template.loaders.locmem.Loader>`a luchtaíonn teimpléid Django ó "
"fhoclóir Python."

msgid ""
"The :ttag:`now` tag can now store its output in a context variable with the "
"usual syntax: ``{% now 'j n Y' as varname %}``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leis an gclibe:ttag: `now` a aschur a stóráil anois in athróg "
"comhthéacs leis an ggnáthchomhréir: ``{% now 'j n Y' mar varname%}``."

msgid "``WSGIRequest`` now respects paths starting with ``//``."
msgstr "Tá meas ag ``WSGIrequest`` anois cosáin ag tosú le ``//``."

msgid ""
"The :meth:`HttpRequest.build_absolute_uri() "
"<django.http.HttpRequest.build_absolute_uri>` method now handles paths "
"starting with ``//`` correctly."
msgstr ""
"<django.http.HttpRequest.build_absolute_uri>Láimhseálann an modh:Meth: "
"`HttpRequest.build_absolute_uri () `cosáin anois ag tosú le ``//`` i gceart."

msgid ""
"If :setting:`DEBUG` is ``True`` and a request raises "
"a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.SuspiciousOperation`, the response will be "
"rendered with a detailed error page."
msgstr ""
"Más rud é: Setting: `DEBUG` ``True`` agus ardaíonn iarratas a:exc: "
"`~Django.Core.Exceptions.SuspiciousOperation`, tabharfar an freagra le "
"leathanach earráide mionsonraithe."

msgid ""
"The ``query_string`` argument of :class:`~django.http.QueryDict` is now "
"optional, defaulting to ``None``, so a blank ``QueryDict`` can now be "
"instantiated with ``QueryDict()`` instead of ``QueryDict(None)`` or "
"``QueryDict('')``."
msgstr ""
"Tá an argóint ``query_string`` de:class: `~django.http.QueryDict` roghnach "
"anois, ag réamhshocrú go ``None``, mar sin is féidir `QueryDict`` bán a chur "
"isteach anois le ``QueryDict () ``in ionad ``QueryDict (None)`` nó "
"`QueryDict (“) ``."

msgid ""
"The ``GET`` and ``POST`` attributes of an :class:`~django.http.HttpRequest` "
"object are now :class:`~django.http.QueryDict`\\s rather than dictionaries, "
"and the ``FILES`` attribute is now a ``MultiValueDict``. This brings this "
"class into line with the documentation and with ``WSGIRequest``."
msgstr ""
"Is iad tréithe ``GET`` agus `POST ```` réad an:class: "
"`~django.http.httpRequest` anois:class: `~django.http.querydict`\\ s seachas "
"foclóirí, agus is ``ValuMultiedict`` an tréith `FILES`` anois. Tugann sé seo "
"an rang seo ar aon dul leis an doiciméadú agus le ``WSGIrequest``."

msgid ""
"The :attr:`HttpResponse.charset <django.http.HttpResponse.charset>` "
"attribute was added."
msgstr ""
"<django.http.HttpResponse.charset>Cuireadh an tréith: Attr: "
"`HttpResponse.charSet `leis."

msgid ""
"``WSGIRequestHandler`` now follows RFC in converting URI to IRI, using "
"``uri_to_iri()``."
msgstr ""
"Leanann ``wsgirequestHandler`` RFC anois ag tiontú URI go IRI, ag baint "
"úsáide as ``uri_to_iri () ``."

msgid ""
"The :meth:`HttpRequest.get_full_path() "
"<django.http.HttpRequest.get_full_path>` method now escapes unsafe "
"characters from the path portion of a Uniform Resource Identifier (URI) "
"properly."
msgstr ""
"Éalaíonn an modh:Meth: `HttpRequest.get_full_path () "
"<django.http.HttpRequest.get_full_path>`carachtair neamhshábháilte anois ón "
"gcuid cosáin d'Aitheantóir Acmhainní Aonfhoirmeach (URI) i gceart."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.http.HttpResponse` now implements a few additional methods "
"like :meth:`~django.http.HttpResponse.getvalue` so that instances can be "
"used as stream objects."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.http.httpResponse` cuireann cúpla modh breise i bhfeidhm "
"anois cosúil:meth: `~django.http.httpResponse.getValue` ionas gur féidir "
"cásanna a úsáid mar rudaí srutha."

msgid ""
"The new :meth:`HttpResponse.setdefault() "
"<django.http.HttpResponse.setdefault>` method allows setting a header unless "
"it has already been set."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn an modh nua:meth: `HttpResponse.setDefault () "
"<django.http.HttpResponse.setdefault>`ceanntásc a shocrú mura bhfuil sé "
"socraithe cheana féin."

msgid "You can use the new :class:`~django.http.FileResponse` to stream files."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an new:class: `~django.http.fileResponse` a úsáid chun "
"comhaid a shruthlú."

msgid ""
"The :func:`~django.views.decorators.http.condition` decorator for "
"conditional view processing now supports the ``If-unmodified-since`` header."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn an maisitheoir: Func: `~django.views.decorators.http.condition` le "
"haghaidh próiseála amharc coinníollach anois leis an gceannteideal ``if-"
"unmodified-since``."

msgid ""
"The :class:`RequestFactory.trace() <django.test.RequestFactory>` "
"and :class:`Client.trace() <django.test.Client.trace>` methods were "
"implemented, allowing you to create ``TRACE`` requests in your tests."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh na modhanna: Class: `RequestFactory.trace () `agus "
"<django.test.RequestFactory>:class: `Client.trace ()` i bhfeidhm, rud a "
"ligeann duit iarratais ``TRACE` <django.test.Client.trace>`a chruthú i do "
"thástálacha."

msgid ""
"The ``count`` argument was added "
"to :meth:`~django.test.SimpleTestCase.assertTemplateUsed`. This allows you "
"to assert that a template was rendered a specific number of times."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an argóint ``count`` leis la:meth: "
"`~django.test.simpletestCase.assertTemplateUsed`. Ligeann sé seo duit a "
"dhearbhú gur rinneadh teimpléad ar fáil líon ar leith uaireanta."

msgid ""
"The new :meth:`~django.test.SimpleTestCase.assertJSONNotEqual` assertion "
"allows you to test that two JSON fragments are not equal."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an dearbhú nua:meth: "
"`~django.test.simpletestcase.assertjsonNoteQual` duit tástáil nach bhfuil "
"dhá bhrúin JSON cothrom."

msgid ""
"Added options to the :djadmin:`test` command to preserve the test database "
"(:option:`--keepdb <test --keepdb>`), to run the test cases in reverse order "
"(:option:`--reverse <test --reverse>`), and to enable SQL logging for "
"failing tests (:option:`--debug-sql <test --debug-sql>`)."
msgstr ""
"<test --debug-sql>Cuireadh roghanna leis an <test --keepdb>ordú:djadmin: "
"`tást` chun an bunachar sonraí tástála a chaomhnú (:option: `--keepdb `), "
"chun na cásanna tástála a reáchtáil in ord droim (:option: `--reverse`), "
"agus logáil SQL a chumasú le haghaidh tástálacha <test --reverse>a theip "
"(:option: `--debug-sql `)."

msgid ""
"Added the :attr:`~django.test.Response.resolver_match` attribute to test "
"client responses."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an tréith: attr: `~django.test.response.resolver_match` le freagraí "
"cliant a thástáil."

msgid ""
"Added several settings that allow customization of test tablespace "
"parameters for "
"Oracle: :setting:`DATAFILE`, :setting:`DATAFILE_TMP`, :setting:`DATAFILE_MAXSIZE` "
"and :setting:`DATAFILE_TMP_MAXSIZE`."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh roinnt socruithe leis a cheadaíonn saincheapadh paraiméadair spáis "
"tástála do Oracle: :setting: `DATAFILE`, :setting: `DATAFILE_TMP`, :setting: "
"`DATAFILE_MAXSIZE` agus:setting: `DATAFILE_TMP_MAXSIZE`."

msgid ""
"The :func:`~django.test.override_settings` decorator can now affect the "
"master router in :setting:`DATABASE_ROUTERS`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leis an maisitheoir: Func: `~django.test.override_settings` dul i "
"bhfeidhm anois ar an mháistir-ródaire in:setting: `DATABASE_ROUTERS`."

msgid "Added test client support for file uploads with file-like objects."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh tacaíocht cliant tástála le haghaidh uaslódála comhad le rudaí "
"cosúil le comhad."

msgid ""
"A shared cache is now used when testing with an SQLite in-memory database "
"when using Python 3.4+ and SQLite 3.7.13+. This allows sharing the database "
"between threads."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear taisce roinnte anois agus tú ag tástáil le bunachar sonraí in-"
"chuimhne SQLite agus Python 3.4+ agus SQLite 3.7.13+ á úsáid agat. Ligeann "
"sé seo an bunachar sonraí a roinnt idir snáithe."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.core.validators.URLValidator` now supports IPv6 addresses, "
"Unicode domains, and URLs containing authentication data."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.core.validators.urlValidator` tacaíonn anois le seoltaí "
"IPv6, fearainn Unicode, agus URLanna ina bhfuil sonraí fíordheimhnithe."

msgid "Backwards incompatible changes in 1.8"
msgstr "Athruithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha ar ais i 1.8"

msgid ""
"In addition to the changes outlined in this section, be sure to review "
"the :ref:`deprecation plan <deprecation-removed-in-1.8>` for any features "
"that have been removed. If you haven't updated your code within the "
"deprecation timeline for a given feature, its removal may appear as a "
"backwards incompatible change."
msgstr ""
"<deprecation-removed-in-1.8>Chomh maith leis na hathruithe a leagtar amach "
"sa chuid seo, déan cinnte athbhreithniú a dhéanamh ar an:ref: `plean "
"díréachtaithe `le haghaidh aon ghnéithe a baineadh. Mura ndearna tú do chód "
"a nuashonrú laistigh den amlíne díscoilte do ghné ar leith, d'fhéadfadh go "
"mbeadh sé a bhaint mar athrú neamh-chomhoiriúnach ar chúl."

msgid "Related object operations are run in a transaction"
msgstr "Reáchtáiltear oibríochtaí réad gaolmhara in idirbheart"

msgid ""
"Some operations on related objects such "
"as :meth:`~django.db.models.fields.related.RelatedManager.add()` or direct "
"assignment ran multiple data modifying queries without wrapping them in "
"transactions. To reduce the risk of data corruption, all data modifying "
"methods that affect multiple related objects (i.e. ``add()``, ``remove()``, "
"``clear()``, and direct assignment) now perform their data modifying queries "
"from within a transaction, provided your database supports transactions."
msgstr ""
"Rith roinnt oibríochtaí ar rudaí gaolmhara mar: meth: "
"`~Django.db.Models.Fields.Related.RelatedManager.add () `nó sannadh díreach "
"ceisteanna iolracha modhnaithe sonraí gan iad a fhilleadh in idirbhearta. "
"Chun an riosca éillithe sonraí a laghdú, déanann gach modh modhnú sonraí a "
"théann i bhfeidhm ar rudaí gaolmhara iolracha (ie `add () ``, `remove ()``, "
"`clear () `, agus sannadh díreach) anois a gcuid ceisteanna modhnaithe "
"sonraí ó idirbheart, ar choinníoll go dtacaíonn do bhunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"This has one backwards incompatible side effect, signal handlers triggered "
"from these methods are now executed within the method's transaction and any "
"exception in a signal handler will prevent the whole operation."
msgstr ""
"Tá fo-iarmhairt neamh-chomhoiriúnach amháin ag baint leis seo, déantar "
"láimhseálaithe comharthaí a spreagtar ó na modhanna seo a fhorghníomhú anois "
"laistigh d'idirbheart an mhodha agus cuirfidh aon eisceacht i láimhseálaí "
"comhartha cosc ​​ar an oibríocht iomlán."

msgid "Assigning unsaved objects to relations raises an error"
msgstr "Ardaíonn earráid neamhshábháilte a shannadh do chaidrimh"

msgid ""
"To more easily allow in-memory usage of models, this change was reverted in "
"Django 1.8.4 and replaced with a check during ``model.save()``. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Chun úsáid samhlacha i gcuimhne a cheadú níos éasca, cuireadh an t-athrú seo "
"ar ais i Django 1.8.4 agus cuireadh seiceáil ina ionad le linn `model.save "
"() `. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"A similar check on assignment to reverse one-to-one relations was removed in "
"Django 1.8.5."
msgstr ""
"Baineadh seiceáil den chineál céanna ar shannadh chun caidreamh duine le "
"duine a aisiompú i Django 1.8.5."

msgid ""
"Assigning unsaved objects to "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey`, :class:`~django.contrib.contenttypes.fields.GenericForeignKey`, "
"and :class:`~django.db.models.OneToOneField` now raises a :exc:`ValueError`."
msgstr ""
"Ardaíonn rudaí neamhshábháilte do a:class: "
"`~django.db.models.foreignKey`, :class: "
"`~django.contrib.contentTypes.Fields.GenericForeignKey`, agus:class: "
"`~django.db.models.onetoonefield` anois: exc: `ValueError`."

msgid ""
"Previously, the assignment of an unsaved object would be silently ignored. "
"For example:"
msgstr ""
"Roimhe seo, déanfaí neamhaird go ciúin ar shannadh réad neamhshábháilte. Mar "
"shampla:"

msgid "Now, an error will be raised to prevent data loss:"
msgstr "Anois, ardófar earráid chun caillteanas sonraí a chosc:"

msgid ""
"If you require allowing the assignment of unsaved instances (the old "
"behavior) and aren't concerned about the data loss possibility (e.g. you "
"never save the objects to the database), you can disable this check by using "
"the ``ForeignKey.allow_unsaved_instance_assignment`` attribute. (This "
"attribute was removed in 1.8.4 as it's no longer relevant.)"
msgstr ""
"Más gá duit cásanna neamhshábháilte a cheadú (an sean-iompar) agus mura "
"bhfuil imní ort faoin bhféidearthacht caillteanais sonraí (m.sh. ní "
"shábhálann tú na rudaí sa bhunachar sonraí riamh), is féidir leat an "
"seiceáil seo a dhíchumasú tríd an tréith "
"``ForeignKey.ALLOW_UNSAVED_INSTANCE_ASSIGNMENT`` a úsáid. (Baineadh an "
"tréith seo i 1.8.4 toisc nach bhfuil sé ábhartha a thuilleadh.)"

msgid "Management commands that only accept positional arguments"
msgstr "Orduithe bainistíochta nach nglacann ach argóintí seasaimh"

msgid ""
"If you have written a custom management command that only accepts positional "
"arguments and you didn't specify the ``args`` command variable, you might "
"get an error like ``Error: unrecognized arguments: ...``, as variable "
"parsing is now based on :py:mod:`argparse` which doesn't implicitly accept "
"positional arguments. You can make your command backwards compatible by "
"simply setting the ``args`` class variable. However, if you don't have to "
"keep compatibility with older Django versions, it's better to implement the "
"new :meth:`~django.core.management.BaseCommand.add_arguments` method as "
"described in :doc:`/howto/custom-management-commands`."
msgstr ""
"Má tá ordú bainistíochta saincheaptha scríofa agat nach nglacann ach le "
"hargóintí seasaimh agus nár shonraigh tú an t-athróg ordaithe `args`, "
"b'fhéidir go bhfaighidh tú earráid mar ``Earráid: argóintí "
"neamhaitheanta:... ``, mar tá parsáil athraitheach bunaithe anois ar:py:mod: "
"`argparse` nach nglacann le hargóintí seasaimh. Is féidir leat d'ordú a "
"dhéanamh comhoiriúnach ar ais trí athróg aicme ``args` a shocrú. Mar sin "
"féin, mura gá duit comhoiriúnacht a choinneáil le leaganacha níos sine "
"Django, is fearr an modh nua: meth: "
"`~django.core.management.basecommand.add_arguments` a chur i bhfeidhm mar a "
"thuairiscítear in:doc: `/howto/custom-management-commands`."

msgid "Custom test management command arguments through test runner"
msgstr "Argóintí ordaithe bainistíochta tástála saincheaptha trí reathóir"

msgid ""
"The method to add custom arguments to the ``test`` management command "
"through the test runner has changed. Previously, you could provide an "
"``option_list`` class variable on the test runner to add more arguments (à "
"la :py:mod:`optparse`). Now to implement the same behavior, you have to "
"create an ``add_arguments(cls, parser)`` class method on the test runner and "
"call ``parser.add_argument`` to add any custom arguments, as parser is now "
"an :py:class:`argparse.ArgumentParser` instance."
msgstr ""
"Tá athrú tagtha ar an modh chun argóintí saincheaptha a chur leis an ordú "
"bainistíochta `tástála` tríd an riteoir tástála. Roimhe seo, d'fhéadfá "
"athróg aicme ``option_list`` a sholáthar ar an reathróir tástála chun "
"tuilleadh argóintí a chur leis (à la: py:mod: `optparse`). Anois chun an t-"
"iompar céanna a chur i bhfeidhm, caithfidh tú modh aicme ``add_arguments "
"(cls, parser) ``a chruthú ar an reathnóir tástála agus glaoch ar "
"`parser.add_argument`` chun aon argóintí saincheaptha a chur leis, mar tá "
"parser anois:py:class: `ArgParse.ArgumentParser` sampla."

msgid ""
"Model check ensures auto-generated column names are within limits specified "
"by database"
msgstr ""
"Cinntíonn seiceáil mhúnla go bhfuil ainmneacha colún a ghintear uathoibríoch"

msgid ""
"A field name that's longer than the column name length supported by a "
"database can create problems. For example, with MySQL you'll get an "
"exception trying to create the column, and with PostgreSQL the column name "
"is truncated by the database (you may see a warning in the PostgreSQL logs)."
msgstr ""
"Féadann ainm réimse atá níos faide ná fad ainm an cholúin a thacaíonn "
"bunachar sonraí fadhbanna a chruthú. Mar shampla, le MySQL gheobhaidh tú "
"eisceacht ag iarraidh an colún a chruthú, agus le PostgreSQL déanann an "
"bunachar sonraí ainm an cholúin a ghearradh (b'fhéidir go bhfeicfidh tú "
"rabhadh sna logaí PostgreSQL)."

msgid ""
"A model check has been introduced to better alert users to this scenario "
"before the actual creation of database tables."
msgstr ""
"Tugadh seiceáil samhail isteach chun úsáideoirí a chur ar an eolas níos "
"fearr faoin gcás seo sula gcruthaítear táblaí bunachar sonraí iarbhír."

msgid ""
"If you have an existing model where this check seems to be a false positive, "
"for example on PostgreSQL where the name was already being truncated, simply "
"use :attr:`~django.db.models.Field.db_column` to specify the name that's "
"being used."
msgstr ""
"Má tá samhail ann cheana agat inar cosúil gur dearfach bréagach é an "
"seiceáil seo, mar shampla ar PostgreSQL áit a raibh an t-ainm á ghearradh "
"cheana féin, ní gá ach húsáid:attr: `~django.db.models.field.db_column` chun "
"an t-ainm atá á úsáid a shonrú."

msgid ""
"The check also applies to the columns generated in an implicit "
"``ManyToManyField.through`` model. If you run into an issue there, "
"use :attr:`~django.db.models.ManyToManyField.through` to create an explicit "
"model and then specify :attr:`~django.db.models.Field.db_column` on its "
"column(s) as needed."
msgstr ""
"Baineann an seiceáil freisin leis na colúin a ghintear i samhail intuigthe "
"``ManyTomanyField.through ``. Má ritheann tú i gceist ann, bain úsáid as: "
"attr: `~django.db.models.manyToManyField.through` chun samhail follasach a "
"chruthú agus ansin sonraithe:attr: `~django.db.models.field.db_column` ar a "
"cholún (anna) de réir mar is gá."

msgid "Query relation lookups now check object types"
msgstr "Seiceálann cuardaigh caidrimh ceisteanna anois cineálacha"

msgid ""
"Querying for model lookups now checks if the object passed is of correct "
"type and raises a :exc:`ValueError` if not. Previously, Django didn't care "
"if the object was of correct type; it just used the object's related field "
"attribute (e.g. ``id``) for the lookup. Now, an error is raised to prevent "
"incorrect lookups:"
msgstr ""
"Seiceálann fiosrú ar chuardach samhlacha anois an bhfuil an réad a rith den "
"chineál ceart agus ardaíonn sé a:exc: `ValueError` mura bhfuil. Roimhe seo, "
"ní raibh cúram ag Django an raibh an réad den chineál ceart; d'úsáid sé ach "
"tréith réimse gaolmhar an réada (m.sh. `id ``) don chuardach. Anois, "
"ardaítear earráid chun cuardach mícheart a chosc:"

msgid "``select_related()`` now checks given fields"
msgstr "Seiceálann ``select_related () ``réimsí ar leith anois"

msgid ""
"``select_related()`` now validates that the given fields actually exist. "
"Previously, nonexistent fields were silently ignored. Now, an error is "
"raised:"
msgstr ""
"Bailíonn ``select_related () ``anois go bhfuil na réimsí a thugtar ann i "
"ndáiríre. Roimhe seo, rinneadh neamhaird go ciúin ar réimsí gan ann. Anois, "
"ardaítear earráid:"

msgid "The validation also makes sure that the given field is relational:"
msgstr "Cinntíonn an bailíochtú freisin go bhfuil an réimse ar leith gaolmhar:"

msgid "Default ``EmailField.max_length`` increased to 254"
msgstr "Mhéadaigh réamhshocraithe ``emailfield.MAX_LENGTH`` go 254"

msgid ""
"The old default 75 character ``max_length`` was not capable of storing all "
"possible RFC3696/5321-compliant email addresses. In order to store all "
"possible valid email addresses, the ``max_length`` has been increased to 254 "
"characters. You will need to generate and apply database migrations for your "
"affected models (or add ``max_length=75`` if you wish to keep the length on "
"your current fields). A migration "
"for :attr:`django.contrib.auth.models.User.email` is included."
msgstr ""
"Ní raibh an sean-charachtar réamhshocraithe 75 ``max_length ``in ann gach "
"seoladh ríomhphoist féideartha a chomhlíonadh RFC3696/5321-a a stóráil. "
"D'fhonn gach seoladh ríomhphoist bailí féideartha a stóráil, tá an "
"``max_length ``méadaithe go 254 carachtar. Beidh ort imirce bunachar sonraí "
"a ghiniúint agus a chur i bhfeidhm do na samhlacha atá buailte (nó "
"``max_length = 75`` a chur leis más mian leat an fad a choinneáil ar do "
"réimsí reatha). Tá imirce le haghaidh: attr: "
"`django.contrib.auth.models.user.email` san áireamh."

msgid "Support for PostgreSQL versions older than 9.0"
msgstr "Tacaíocht do leaganacha PostgreSQL níos sine ná 9.0"

msgid ""
"The end of upstream support periods was reached in July 2014 for PostgreSQL "
"8.4. As a consequence, Django 1.8 sets 9.0 as the minimum PostgreSQL version "
"it officially supports."
msgstr ""
"Sroichtear deireadh na dtréimhsí tacaíochta suas srutha i mí Iúil 2014 do "
"PostgreSQL 8.4. Mar thoradh air sin, socraíonn Django 1.8 9.0 mar an leagan "
"íosta PostgreSQL a thacaíonn sé go hoifigiúil."

msgid ""
"This also includes dropping support for PostGIS 1.3 and 1.4 as these "
"versions are not supported on versions of PostgreSQL later than 8.4."
msgstr ""
"Áirítear leis seo freisin tacaíocht titim do PostGIS 1.3 agus 1.4 toisc nach "
"dtacaítear leis na leaganacha seo ar leaganacha de PostgreSQL níos déanaí ná "
"8.4."

msgid ""
"Django also now requires the use of Psycopg2 version 2.4.5 or higher (or "
"2.5+ if you want to use :mod:`django.contrib.postgres`)."
msgstr ""
"Éilíonn Django anois úsáid Psycopg2 leagan 2.4.5 nó níos airde (nó 2.5+ más "
"mian leat úsáid: mod: `django.contrib.postgres`)."

msgid "Support for MySQL versions older than 5.5"
msgstr "Tacaíocht do leaganacha MySQL níos sine ná 5.5"

msgid ""
"The end of upstream support periods was reached in January 2012 for MySQL "
"5.0 and December 2013 for MySQL 5.1. As a consequence, Django 1.8 sets 5.5 "
"as the minimum MySQL version it officially supports."
msgstr ""
"Sroichtear deireadh na dtréimhsí tacaíochta suas srutha i mí Eanáir 2012 do "
"MySQL 5.0 agus na Nollag 2013 do MySQL 5.1. Mar thoradh air sin, socraíonn "
"Django 1.8 5.5 mar an leagan íosta MySQL a thacaíonn sé go hoifigiúil."

msgid "Support for Oracle versions older than 11.1"
msgstr "Tacaíocht do leaganacha Oracle níos sine ná 11.1"

msgid ""
"The end of upstream support periods was reached in July 2010 for Oracle 9.2, "
"January 2012 for Oracle 10.1, and July 2013 for Oracle 10.2. As a "
"consequence, Django 1.8 sets 11.1 as the minimum Oracle version it "
"officially supports."
msgstr ""
"Sroichtear deireadh na dtréimhsí tacaíochta suas srutha i mí Iúil 2010 do "
"Oracle 9.2, Eanáir 2012 do Oracle 10.1, agus Iúil 2013 le haghaidh Oracle "
"10.2. Mar thoradh air sin, socraíonn Django 1.8 11.1 mar an leagan íosta "
"Oracle a thacaíonn sé go hoifigiúil."

msgid "Specific privileges used instead of roles for tests on Oracle"
msgstr "Pribhléidí sonracha a úsáidtear in ionad róil le haghaidh tástálacha"

msgid ""
"Earlier versions of Django granted the CONNECT and RESOURCE roles to the "
"test user on Oracle. These roles have been deprecated, so Django 1.8 uses "
"the specific underlying privileges instead. This changes the privileges "
"required of the main user for running tests (unless the project is "
"configured to avoid creating a test user). The exact privileges required now "
"are detailed in :ref:`Oracle notes <oracle-notes>`."
msgstr ""
"Thug leaganacha níos luaithe de Django na róil CONNECT agus RESOURCE don "
"úsáideoir tástála ar Oracle. Tá na róil seo imithe, mar sin úsáideann Django "
"1.8 na pribhléidí bunúsacha sonracha ina ionad sin. Athraíonn sé seo na "
"pribhléidí a theastaíonn ón bpríomh-úsáideoir le haghaidh tástálacha a "
"reáchtáil (mura bhfuil an tionscadal cumraithe chun úsáideoir tástála a "
"<oracle-notes>Tá na pribhléidí cruinne a theastaíonn anois mionsonraithe "
"in:ref: `Nótaí Oracle `."

msgid "``AbstractUser.last_login`` allows null values"
msgstr "Ceadaíonn ``Abstractuser.Last_Login`` luachanna null"

msgid ""
"The :attr:`AbstractUser.last_login "
"<django.contrib.auth.models.User.last_login>` field now allows null values. "
"Previously, it defaulted to the time when the user was created which was "
"misleading if the user never logged in. If you are using the default user "
"(:class:`django.contrib.auth.models.User`), run the database migration "
"included in ``contrib.auth``."
msgstr ""
"<django.contrib.auth.models.User.last_login>Ceadaíonn an réimse: Attr: "
"`AbstractUSER.LAST_LOGIN` luachanna neall anois. Roimhe seo, rinne sé "
"réamhshocraithe go dtí an t-am nuair a cruthaíodh an t-úsáideoir a bhí "
"míthreorach mura logáil isteach an t-úsáideoir riamh. Má tá an t-úsáideoir "
"réamhshocraithe á úsáid agat (:class: `django.contrib.auth.models.user`), "
"reáchtáil an imirce bunachar sonraí atá san áireamh i ``contrib.auth``."

msgid ""
"If you are using a custom user model that inherits from ``AbstractUser``, "
"you'll need to run :djadmin:`makemigrations` and generate a migration for "
"your app that contains that model. Also, if wish to set ``last_login`` to "
"``NULL`` for users who haven't logged in, you can run this query::"
msgstr ""
"Má tá samhail úsáideora saincheaptha á úsáid agat a fhaigheann oidhreacht ó "
"`AbstractUser`, beidh ort rith: djadmin: `makemigrations` agus imirce a "
"ghiniúint do d'aip ina bhfuil an tsamhail sin. Chomh maith leis sin, más "
"mian leat ``last_login`` a shocrú go ``NULL`` d'úsáideoirí nach bhfuil "
"logáil isteach orthu, is féidir leat an cheist seo a reáchtáil:"

msgid "Support for GEOS 3.1 and GDAL 1.6 has been dropped."
msgstr "Tá tacaíocht do GEOS 3.1 agus GDAL 1.6 titim."

msgid "Support for SpatiaLite < 2.4 has been dropped."
msgstr "Tá tacaíocht do SpatiaLite <2.4 titim."

msgid ""
"GIS-specific lookups have been refactored to use "
"the :class:`django.db.models.Lookup` API."
msgstr ""
"Athraíodh cuardaigh atá sonrach le GIS chun an API: class: "
"`Django.db.Models.lookup` a úsáid."

msgid ""
"The default ``str`` representation "
"of :class:`~django.contrib.gis.geos.GEOSGeometry` objects has been changed "
"from WKT to EWKT format (including the SRID). As this representation is used "
"in the serialization framework, that means that ``dumpdata`` output will now "
"contain the SRID value of geometry objects."
msgstr ""
"Athraíodh an léiriú réamhshocraithe ``str`` o:class: "
"`~django.contrib.gis.geos.geosgeometry` rudaí ó WKT go formáid EWKT (lena n-"
"áirítear an SRID). Toisc go n-úsáidtear an léiriú seo sa chreat sraitheach, "
"ciallaíonn sé sin go mbeidh luach SRID na rudaí geoiméadrachta anois ag "
"aschur `dumpdata`."

msgid ""
"Priority of context processors for ``TemplateResponse`` brought in line with "
"``render``"
msgstr ""
"Tosaíocht na bpróiseálaithe comhthéacs do ``TemplateResponse`` a thugtar i "
"gcomhréir le ``render``"

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.template.response.TemplateResponse` constructor is "
"designed to be a drop-in replacement for "
"the :func:`~django.shortcuts.render` function. However, it had a slight "
"incompatibility, in that for ``TemplateResponse``, context data from the "
"passed in context dictionary could be shadowed by context data returned from "
"context processors, whereas for ``render`` it was the other way around. This "
"was a bug, and the behavior of ``render`` is more appropriate, since it "
"allows the globally defined context processors to be overridden locally in "
"the view. If you were relying on the fact context data in a "
"``TemplateResponse`` could be overridden using a context processor, you will "
"need to change your code."
msgstr ""
"Tá an tógálaí: Class: `~Django.Template.Response.TemplateResponse` deartha "
"le bheith ina athsholáthar titim isteach don fheidhme:func: "
"`~django.shortcuts.render`. Mar sin féin, bhí neamhchomhoiriúnacht beag "
"aige, sa mhéid go bhféadfadh sonraí comhthéacs ón bhfoclóir a rith i "
"gcomhthéacs a scáthú le sonraí comhthéacs a chuir ar ais ó phróiseálaithe "
"comhthéacs, ach maidir le ``render`` bhí sé ar an mbealach eile. Ba fabht a "
"bhí anseo, agus tá iompar ``render`` níos oiriúnaí, ós rud é go gceadaíonn "
"sé na próiseálaithe comhthéacs atá sainmhínithe go domhanda a shárú go "
"háitiúil sa radharc. Má bhí tú ag brath ar an bhfíric go bhféadfaí sonraí "
"comhthéacs i “TemplateResponse” a shárú ag baint úsáide as próiseálaí "
"comhthéacs, beidh ort do chód a athrú."

msgid "Overriding ``setUpClass`` / ``tearDownClass`` in test cases"
msgstr "Sárú ``SetupClass``/``TearDownClass`` i gcásanna tástála"

msgid ""
"The decorators :func:`~django.test.override_settings` "
"and :func:`~django.test.modify_settings` now act at the class level when "
"used as class decorators. As a consequence, when overriding ``setUpClass()`` "
"or ``tearDownClass()``, the ``super`` implementation should always be called."
msgstr ""
"Gníomhaíonn na maisióirí: func: `~django.test.override_settings` agus:func: "
"`~django.test.modify_settings` anois ag leibhéal an ranga nuair a úsáidtear "
"iad mar mhaisitheoirí ranga. Mar thoradh air sin, nuair a bhíonn `setupClass "
"() ``nó `teardownClass ()`` a shárú, ba chóir cur i bhfeidhm ``super`` a "
"ghlaoch i gcónaí."

msgid "Removal of ``django.contrib.formtools``"
msgstr "Baineadh ``django.contrib.formtools``"

msgid ""
"The formtools contrib app has been moved to a separate package and the "
"relevant documentation pages have been updated or removed."
msgstr ""
"Bogadh an aip contrib formtools chuig pacáiste ar leithligh agus rinneadh na "
"leathanaigh doiciméadaithe ábhartha a nuashonrú nó a bhaint."

msgid "The new package is available `on GitHub`_ and on PyPI."
msgstr "Tá an pacáiste nua ar fáil `ar GitHub `_ agus ar PyPI."

msgid "Database connection reloading between tests"
msgstr "Athluchtú nasc bunachar sonraí idir tástálacha"

msgid ""
"Django previously closed database connections between each test within a "
"``TestCase``. This is no longer the case as Django now wraps the whole "
"``TestCase`` within a transaction. If some of your tests relied on the old "
"behavior, you should have them inherit from ``TransactionTestCase`` instead."
msgstr ""
"Dúnaigh Django naisc bunachar sonraí roimhe seo idir gach tástáil laistigh "
"de ``cás tástála``. Ní hamhlaigh sé seo a thuilleadh mar a fhilleann Django "
"anois an ``cás tástála`` iomlán laistigh d'idirbheart. Má bhí cuid de do "
"thástálacha ag brath ar an sean-iompar, ba cheart go mbeadh oidhreacht agat "
"ó `TransactionTestCase`` ina ionad sin."

msgid "Cleanup of the ``django.template`` namespace"
msgstr "Glanadh an spás ainmneacha ``django.template``"

msgid ""
"If you've been relying on private APIs exposed in the ``django.template`` "
"module, you may have to import them from ``django.template.base`` instead."
msgstr ""
"Má bhí tú ag brath ar APIs príobháideacha atá nochtaithe sa mhodúl "
"``django.template``, b'fhéidir go mbeidh ort iad a iompórtáil ó "
"`django.template.base`` ina ionad."

msgid ""
"Also private APIs ``django.template.base.compile_string()``, "
"``django.template.loader.find_template()``, and "
"``django.template.loader.get_template_from_string()`` were removed."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith leis sin baineadh APIs príobháideacha "
"``django.template.base.compile_string () ``, "
"`django.template.loader.find_template ()``, agus "
"``django.template.loader.get_template_from_string () ``."

msgid "``model`` attribute on private model relations"
msgstr "Tréith ``samhail ``ar chaidreamh samhail phríobháideach"

msgid ""
"In earlier versions of Django, on a model with a reverse foreign key "
"relationship (for example), ``model._meta.get_all_related_objects()`` "
"returned the relationship as a ``django.db.models.related.RelatedObject`` "
"with the ``model`` attribute set to the source of the relationship. Now, "
"this method returns the relationship as "
"``django.db.models.fields.related.ManyToOneRel`` (private API "
"``RelatedObject`` has been removed), and the ``model`` attribute is set to "
"the target of the relationship instead of the source. The source model is "
"accessible on the ``related_model`` attribute instead."
msgstr ""
"I leaganacha níos luaithe de Django, ar mhúnla le príomhchaidreamh eachtrach "
"ar ais (mar shampla), `samhail. Chuir _meta.get_all_related_objects () ``an "
"caidreamh ar ais mar ``Django.db.Models.Related.RelatedObject`` leis an "
"tréith ``model`` atá leagtha amach le foinse an chaidrimh. Anois, filleann "
"an modh seo an caidreamh mar ``Django.db.Models.Fields.Related.manyTooneRel "
"``(baineadh API príobháideach ``RelateDObject``), agus socraítear an tréith "
"``model`` ```` `` `` `` `` `` `` `` Tá an tsamhail foinse inrochtana ar an "
"tréith ``related_model`` ina ionad."

msgid "Consider this example from the tutorial in Django 1.8:"
msgstr "Smaoinigh ar an sampla seo ón rang teagaisc i Django 1.8:"

msgid "and compare it to the behavior on older versions:"
msgstr "agus déan comparáid idir é leis an iompar ar leaganacha níos sine:"

msgid ""
"To access the source model, you can use a pattern like this to write code "
"that will work with both Django 1.8 and older versions::"
msgstr ""
"Chun rochtain a fháil ar an tsamhail fhoinse, is féidir leat patrún mar seo "
"a úsáid chun cód a scríobh a oibreoidh le leaganacha Django 1.8 agus níos "
"sine araon::"

msgid "Also note that ``get_all_related_objects()`` is deprecated in 1.8."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara freisin go bhfuil ``get_all_related_objects () "
"``scothaithe i 1.8."

msgid ""
"The following changes to the database backend API are documented to assist "
"those writing third-party backends in updating their code:"
msgstr ""
"Déantar na hathruithe seo a leanas ar API inneall an bhunachair shonraí a "
"dhoiciméadú chun cabhrú leo siúd atá ag scríobh inneall tríú páirtí a gcód a "
"nuashonrú:"

msgid ""
"``BaseDatabaseXXX`` classes have been moved to ``django.db.backends.base``. "
"Please import them from the new locations::"
msgstr ""
"Tá ranganna ``BasedatabaSexxx`` aistríodh chuig ``django.db.backends.base``. "
"Iompórtáil iad ó na háiteanna nua le do thoil::"

msgid ""
"The ``data_types``, ``data_types_suffix``, and "
"``data_type_check_constraints`` attributes have moved from the "
"``DatabaseCreation`` class to ``DatabaseWrapper``."
msgstr ""
"Tá na tréithe ``data_types``, `data_types_suffix``, agus "
"``data_type_check_restricints`` tar éis bogadh ón rang ``DatabaseCreation`` "
"go `DatabaseWrapper``."

msgid ""
"The ``SQLCompiler.as_sql()`` method now takes a ``subquery`` parameter "
"(:ticket:`24164`)."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an modh ``SqlCompiler.as_sql () ``paraiméadar ``subcheiste`` anois "
"(:ticket: `24164`)."

msgid ""
"The ``BaseDatabaseOperations.date_interval_sql()`` method now only takes a "
"``timedelta`` parameter."
msgstr ""
"Ní thógann an modh ``BaseDatabaseOperations.Date_Interval_SQL () `anois ach "
"paraiméadar ``timedel`."

msgid ""
"``AdminSite`` no longer takes an ``app_name`` argument and its ``app_name`` "
"attribute has been removed. The application name is always ``admin`` (as "
"opposed to the instance name which you can still customize using "
"``AdminSite(name=\"...\")``."
msgstr ""
"Ní ghlacann ``adminsite`` argóint ``app_name`` a thuilleadh agus baineadh a "
"tréith ``app_name``. Is é “admin” ainm an fheidhmchláir i gcónaí (seachas "
"ainm na sampla is féidir leat a shaincheapadh fós ag baint úsáide as "
"``adminSite (ainm =”...”) `."

msgid ""
"The ``ModelAdmin.get_object()`` method (private API) now takes a third "
"argument named ``from_field`` in order to specify which field should match "
"the provided ``object_id``."
msgstr ""
"Tógann an modh ``ModelAdmin.get_Object () `(API príobháideach) anois tríú "
"argóint darb ainm ``from_field`` d'fhonn a shonrú cén réimse ba chóir a "
"mheaitseáil leis an `object_id`` a sholáthraítear."

msgid ""
"The :meth:`ModelAdmin.response_delete() "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.response_delete>` method now takes a second "
"argument named ``obj_id`` which is the serialized identifier used to "
"retrieve the object before deletion."
msgstr ""
"Tógann an modh: Meth: `ModelAdmin.response_delete () "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.response_delete>`an dara argóint darb ainm "
"``obj_id`` arb é an t-aitheantóir sraitheach a úsáidtear chun an réad a "
"aisghabháil sula scriosadh é."

msgid "Default autoescaping of functions in ``django.template.defaultfilters``"
msgstr ""
"Réamhshocraithe uathoibríoch feidhmeanna i ``django.template.defaultfilters``"

msgid ""
"In order to make built-in template filters that output HTML \"safe by "
"default\" when calling them in Python code, the following functions in "
"``django.template.defaultfilters`` have been changed to automatically escape "
"their input value:"
msgstr ""
"D'fhonn scagairí teimpléad ionsuite a dhéanamh a aschuireann HTML “sábháilte "
"de réir réamhshocraithe” agus iad ag glaoch i gcód Python, athraíodh na "
"feidhmeanna seo a leanas i `django.template.defaultfilters`` chun a luach "
"ionchuir a éalú go huathoibríoch:"

msgid "``join``"
msgstr "```Bhreastala``"

msgid "``linebreaksbr``"
msgstr "``linebreaksbr``"

msgid "``linebreaks_filter``"
msgstr "``linebreaks_filter``"

msgid "``linenumbers``"
msgstr "``Uimhreacha líne``"

msgid "``unordered_list``"
msgstr "``liosta_neamh-ordúnaí``"

msgid "``urlize``"
msgstr "``Urlize``"

msgid "``urlizetrunc``"
msgstr "``urlizetrunc``"

msgid ""
"You can revert to the old behavior by specifying ``autoescape=False`` if you "
"are passing trusted content. This change doesn't have any effect when using "
"the corresponding filters in templates."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat filleadh ar an sean-iompar trí ``autoescape=false ``a shonrú "
"má tá ábhar iontaofa á rith agat. Níl aon éifeacht ag an athrú seo agus na "
"scagairí comhfhreagracha á n-úsáid i dteimpléid."

msgid "``connections.queries`` is now a read-only attribute."
msgstr "Is tréith léite amháin é ``connections.queries`` anois."

msgid ""
"Database connections are considered equal only if they're the same object. "
"They aren't hashable any more."
msgstr ""
"Ní mheastar go bhfuil naisc bunachar sonraí comhionann ach amháin má tá siad "
"an réad céanna. Níl siad inúsáidte níos mó."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.middleware.gzip.GZipMiddleware` used to disable compression "
"for some content types when the request is from Internet Explorer, in order "
"to work around a bug in IE6 and earlier. This behavior could affect "
"performance on IE7 and later. It was removed."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.middleware.gzip.gzipMiddleware` a úsáidtear chun comhbhrú a "
"dhíchumasú do roinnt cineálacha ábhair nuair a bhíonn an t-iarratas ó "
"Internet Explorer, d'fhonn oibriú timpeall fabht in IE6 agus níos luaithe. "
"D'fhéadfadh an t-iompar seo dul i bhfeidhm ar fheidhmíocht ar IE7 agus níos "
"dé Baineadh é."

msgid ""
"``URLField.to_python`` no longer adds a trailing slash to pathless URLs."
msgstr ""
"Ní chuireann ``URLField.to_python`` slasc rianaithe le URLanna gan bhealach "
"a thuilleadh."

msgid ""
"The :tfilter:`length` template filter now returns ``0`` for an undefined "
"variable, rather than an empty string."
msgstr ""
"Filleann an scagaire teimpléad:TFilter: `Length` ``0`` anois le haghaidh "
"athróg neamhshainithe, seachas teaghrán folamh."

msgid ""
"``ForeignKey.default_error_message['invalid']`` has been changed from ``'%"
"(model)s instance with pk %(pk)r does not exist.'`` to ``'%(model)s instance "
"with %(field)s %(value)r does not exist.'`` If you are using this message in "
"your own code, please update the list of interpolated parameters. "
"Internally, Django will continue to provide the ``pk`` parameter in "
"``params`` for backwards compatibility."
msgstr ""
"Athraíodh ``ForeignKey.default_error_message ['neamhbhailí'] ``ó ```% "
"(model) s sampla le pk% (pk) r níl ann. '``go```% (model) s sampla le% "
"(field) s% (value) r níl ann.'`` Má tá an teachtaireacht seo á úsáid agat i "
"do chód féin, nuashonraigh liosta interpolach le do thoil paraiméadair. Go "
"hinmheánach, leanfaidh Django ar aghaidh ag soláthar an paraiméadar ``pk`` i "
"`params`` le haghaidh comhoiriúnacht ar ais."

msgid ""
"``UserCreationForm.error_messages['duplicate_username']`` is no longer used. "
"If you wish to customize that error message, :ref:`override it on the form "
"<modelforms-overriding-default-fields>` using the ``'unique'`` key in "
"``Meta.error_messages['username']`` or, if you have a custom form field for "
"``'username'``, using the ``'unique'`` key in "
"its :attr:`~django.forms.Field.error_messages` argument."
msgstr ""
"``UserCreationForm.error_messages ['duplicate_username'] ``ní úsáidtear a "
"thuilleadh. Más mian leat an teachtaireacht earráide sin a "
"shaincheapadh, :ref: `athraigh é ar an bhfoirm `ag baint <modelforms-"
"overriding-default-fields>úsáide as an eochair ``''unique'` i "
"`Meta.error_Messages ['username'] ``nó, má tá réimse foirme saincheaptha "
"agat le haghaidh ````username'``, úsáid an eochair `'unique'` in:attr: "
"`~django.forms.field.Argóint error_messages."

msgid ""
"The block ``usertools`` in the ``base.html`` template "
"of :mod:`django.contrib.admin` now requires the ``has_permission`` context "
"variable to be set. If you have any custom admin views that use this "
"template, update them to pass :meth:`AdminSite.has_permission() "
"<django.contrib.admin.AdminSite.has_permission>` as this new variable's "
"value or simply include :meth:`AdminSite.each_context(request) "
"<django.contrib.admin.AdminSite.each_context>` in the context."
msgstr ""
"Éilíonn an bloc ``usertools`` sa teimpléad ``base.html`` de:mod: "
"`django.contrib.admin` anois an athróg comhthéacs ``has_permission`` a "
"shocrú. <django.contrib.admin.AdminSite.each_context>Má tá aon tuairimí "
"riaracháin saincheaptha agat a úsá "
"<django.contrib.admin.AdminSite.has_permission>ideann an teimpléad seo, "
"nuashonraigh iad chun pas: meth: `adminsite.has_permit () `mar luach an "
"athróg nua seo nó go simplí:meth: `adminsite.Each_context (iarratas)` sa "
"chomhthéacs."

msgid ""
"Internal changes were made to the :class:`~django.forms.ClearableFileInput` "
"widget to allow more customization. The undocumented ``url_markup_template`` "
"attribute was removed in favor of ``template_with_initial``."
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh athruithe inmheánacha ar an giuirléid:: class: "
"`~django.forms.clearaableFileInput` chun níos mó saincheaptha a cheadú. "
"Baineadh an tréith ``url_markup_template`` neamhdhoiciméadaithe i bhfabhar "
"``template_with_initial``."

msgid ""
"For consistency with other major vendors, the ``en_GB`` locale now has "
"Monday as the first day of the week."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh comhsheasmhachta le mór-dhíoltóirí eile, tá Luain anois mar an "
"chéad lá den tseachtain ag an áitiúil ``En_Gb``."

msgid ""
"Seconds have been removed from any locales that had them in ``TIME_FORMAT``, "
"``DATETIME_FORMAT``, or ``SHORT_DATETIME_FORMAT``."
msgstr ""
"Baineadh soicindí ó aon áiteanna a raibh siad i `TIME_FORMAT``, "
"`DATETIME_FORMAT``, nó ``SHORT_DATETIME_FORMAT``."

msgid ""
"The default max size of the Oracle test tablespace has increased from 300M "
"(or 200M, before 1.7.2) to 500M."
msgstr ""
"Tá méadú tagtha ar mhéid uasta réamhshocraithe spás tábla tástála Oracle ó "
"300M (nó 200M, roimh 1.7.2) go 500M."

msgid ""
"``reverse()`` and ``reverse_lazy()`` now return Unicode strings instead of "
"bytestrings."
msgstr ""
"Filleann ``reverse () ``agus ``reverse_lazy ()`` teaghráin Unicode anois in "
"ionad bytestrings."

msgid ""
"The ``CacheClass`` shim has been removed from all cache backends. These "
"aliases were provided for backwards compatibility with Django 1.3. If you "
"are still using them, please update your project to use the real class name "
"found in the :setting:`BACKEND <CACHES-BACKEND>` key of "
"the :setting:`CACHES` setting."
msgstr ""
"Baineadh an shim ``Cacheclass`` ó gach cúltaca taisce. Cuireadh na "
"hainmneacha seo ar fáil le haghaidh comhoiriúnacht ar ais le Django 1.3. Má "
"tá tú fós á úsáid agat, nuashonraigh do thionscadal le do thoil chun an fíor-"
"ainm ranga atá le fáil san eochair:setting: `BACKEND `den socrú:setting: "
"`CACH <CACHES-BACKEND>ES` a úsáid."

msgid ""
"By default, :func:`~django.core.management.call_command` now always skips "
"the check framework (unless you pass it ``skip_checks=False``)."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, :func: `~django.core.management.call_command` "
"scipeánann an creat seiceála anois i gcónaí (mura rachaidh tú air "
"`skip_checks=false``)."

msgid ""
"When iterating over lines, :class:`~django.core.files.File` now "
"uses :pep:`universal newlines <278>`. The following are recognized as ending "
"a line: the Unix end-of-line convention ``'\\n'``, the Windows convention "
"``'\\r\\n'``, and the old Macintosh convention ``'\\r'``."
msgstr ""
"<278>Agus tú ag athrá thar línte, úsáideann: class: "
"`~django.core.files.file` anois: pep: `línte nua uilíoch `. Aithnítear na "
"nithe seo a leanas mar chríochnú líne: coinbhinsiún deireadh líne Unix ```\\"
"\\ n '`, coinbhinsiún Windows ``'\\ r\\ n '``, agus an sean-choinbhinsiún "
"Macintosh``'\\ r'``."

msgid ""
"The Memcached cache backends ``MemcachedCache`` and ``PyLibMCCache`` will "
"delete a key if ``set()`` fails. This is necessary to ensure the "
"``cache_db`` session store always fetches the most current session data."
msgstr ""
"Scriosfaidh na cúltaca taisce Memcached ``MemcachedCache`` agus "
"``Pylibmccache`` eochair má theipeann ``set () ``. Tá sé seo riachtanach "
"chun a chinntiú go bhfaigheann an siopa seisiún ``cache_db` na sonraí "
"seisiúin is reatha i gcónaí."

msgid ""
"Private APIs ``override_template_loaders`` and ``override_with_test_loader`` "
"in ``django.test.utils`` were removed. Override ``TEMPLATES`` with "
"``override_settings`` instead."
msgstr ""
"Baineadh APIs príobháideacha ``override_template_loaders`` agus "
"``override_with_test_loader`` i `django.test.utils``. Athraigh ``TEMPLATES`` "
"le ``override_settings`` ina ionad sin."

msgid ""
"Warnings from the MySQL database backend are no longer converted to "
"exceptions when :setting:`DEBUG` is ``True``."
msgstr ""
"Ní dhéantar rabhaidh ó chúltaca bunachar sonraí MySQL a thiontú go "
"eisceachtaí a thuilleadh nuair:socrú: “DEBUG” ná ``True``."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.http.HttpRequest` now has a simplified ``repr`` (e.g. "
"``<WSGIRequest: GET '/somepath/'>``). This won't change the behavior of "
"the :class:`~django.views.debug.SafeExceptionReporterFilter` class."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.http.httpRequest` tá ``repr`` simplithe anois (m.sh. ````) ."
"<WSGIRequest: GET '/somepath/'> Ní athróidh sé seo iompar an ranga:class: "
"`~django.views.debug.safeExceptionReporterFilter`."

msgid ""
"Class-based views that "
"use :class:`~django.views.generic.edit.ModelFormMixin` will raise "
"an :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ImproperlyConfigured` exception when both "
"the ``fields`` and ``form_class`` attributes are specified. Previously, "
"``fields`` was silently ignored."
msgstr ""
"Ardóidh tuairimí ranga-bhunaithe a úsáideann eisceacht: Class: "
"`~Django.Views.Generic.Edit.ModelFormMixin` an:exc: "
"`~Django.Core.Exceptions.ImProperlyConfigured` nuair a shonraítear na "
"tréithe ``fields`` agus `form_class` araon. Roimhe seo, rinneadh neamhaird "
"go ciúin ar `fields``."

msgid ""
"When following redirects, the test client now "
"raises :exc:`~django.test.client.RedirectCycleError` if it detects a loop or "
"hits a maximum redirect limit (rather than passing silently)."
msgstr ""
"Agus atreoruithe á leanúint agat, ardaíonn an cliant tástála anois:exc: "
"`~django.test.client.redirectCycleError` má bhraitheann sé lúb nó má "
"bhuaileann sé teorainn athsheolta uasta (seachas dul go ciúin)."

msgid ""
"Translatable strings set as the ``default`` parameter of the field are cast "
"to concrete strings later, so the return type of ``Field.get_default()`` is "
"different in some cases. There is no change to default values which are the "
"result of a callable."
msgstr ""
"Déantar teaghráin inaistrithe atá socraithe mar pharaiméadar ``default`` sa "
"réimse a chaitheamh chuig teaghráin choincréite níos déanaí, mar sin tá an "
"cineál tuairisceáin ``Field.get_default () ``difriúil i gcásanna áirithe. "
"Níl aon athrú ar luachanna réamhshocraithe atá mar thoradh ar inghlaoch."

msgid ""
"``GenericIPAddressField.empty_strings_allowed`` is now ``False``. Database "
"backends that interpret empty strings as null (only Oracle among the "
"backends that Django includes) will no longer convert null values back to an "
"empty string. This is consistent with other backends."
msgstr ""
"Is é ``GenericipAddressField.empty_Strings_Allowed`` anois ``False``. Ní "
"thiontfaidh cúltaca bunachar sonraí a léirmhíníonn teaghráin folamh mar null "
"(ach Oracle i measc na gcúltaca a chuimsíonn Django) luachanna neall a "
"thiontú ar ais go sreang folamh a thuilleadh. Tá sé seo ag teacht le cúltaca "
"eile."

msgid ""
"When the ``BaseCommand.leave_locale_alone`` attribute is ``False``, "
"translations are now deactivated instead of forcing the \"en-us\" locale. In "
"the case your models contained non-English strings and you counted on "
"English translations to be activated in management commands, this will not "
"happen any longer. It might be that new database migrations are generated "
"(once) after migrating to 1.8."
msgstr ""
"Nuair is é ``False`` an tréith ``BaseCommand.leave_locale_alone``, déantar "
"aistriúcháin a dhíghníomhachtú anois in ionad an áitiúil “en-us” a chur i "
"bhfeidhm. Sa chás go raibh teaghráin neamh-Béarla i do mhúnlaí agus go raibh "
"tú ag brath ar aistriúcháin Béarla le gníomhachtú in orduithe bainistíochta, "
"ní tharlóidh sé seo níos mó. D'fhéadfadh sé a bheith go ngintear imirce nua "
"bunachar sonraí (uair amháin) tar éis dul ar imirce go 1.8."

msgid ""
":func:`django.utils.translation.get_language()` now returns ``None`` instead "
"of :setting:`LANGUAGE_CODE` when translations are temporarily deactivated."
msgstr ""
":func: filleann `django.utils.translation.get_language () `anois ``None`` in "
"ionad:setting: `LANGUAGE_CODE` nuair a dhíghníomhachtar aistriúcháin go "
"sealadach."

msgid ""
"When a translation doesn't exist for a specific literal, the fallback is now "
"taken from the :setting:`LANGUAGE_CODE` language (instead of from the "
"untranslated ``msgid`` message)."
msgstr ""
"Nuair nach bhfuil aistriúchán ann le haghaidh litriúil ar leith, tógtar an "
"tagairt anois ón teanga:setting: `LANGUAGE_CODE` (in ionad ón teachtaireacht "
"``msgid`` gan aistriú)."

msgid ""
"The ``name`` field "
"of :class:`django.contrib.contenttypes.models.ContentType` has been removed "
"by a migration and replaced by a property. That means it's not possible to "
"query or filter a ``ContentType`` by this field any longer."
msgstr ""
"Tá an réimse ``ainm ``de:class: "
"`Django.Contrib.ContentTypes.Models.ContentType` bainte le himirce agus tá "
"maoin ina ionad. Ciallaíonn sé sin nach féidir ``ContentType`` a cheistiú nó "
"a scagadh tríd an réimse seo a thuilleadh."

msgid ""
"Be careful if you upgrade to Django 1.8 and skip Django 1.7. If you run "
"``manage.py migrate --fake``, this migration will be skipped and you'll see "
"a ``RuntimeError: Error creating new content types.`` exception because the "
"``name`` column won't be dropped from the database. Use ``manage.py migrate "
"--fake-initial`` to fake only the initial migration instead."
msgstr ""
"Bí cúramach má dhéanann tú uasghrádú go Django 1.8 agus má scipeann tú "
"Django 1.7. Má reáchtáil tú ``manage.py migration --fake``, scipeánfar an "
"imirce seo agus feicfidh tú ``RuntimeError: Earráid ag cruthú cineálacha nua "
"ábhair. ``eisceacht toisc nach dtiocfar an colún ``ainm`` ón mbunachar "
"sonraí. Úsáid ``manage.py migration --fake-initial`` chun an imirce tosaigh "
"a bhréalú amháin ina ionad."

msgid ""
"The new :option:`migrate --fake-initial` option allows faking initial "
"migrations. In 1.7, initial migrations were always automatically faked if "
"all tables created in an initial migration already existed."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn an rogha nua :rogha: `migrate --fake-initial` ascnaimh tosaigh a "
"bhréagnú. In 1.7, bhí ascnaimh tosaigh i gcónaí bréagach go huathoibríoch má "
"bhí na táblaí go léir a cruthaíodh le linn imirce tosaigh ann cheana féin."

msgid ""
"An app *without* migrations with a ``ForeignKey`` to an app *with* "
"migrations may now result in a foreign key constraint error when migrating "
"the database or running tests. In Django 1.7, this could fail silently and "
"result in a missing constraint. To resolve the error, add migrations to the "
"app without them."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh earráid eochairsrianta eachtrach a bheith mar thoradh ar aipe* "
"gan imirce le ``ForeignKey`` chuig aipe*la* imirce anois agus tú ag imirce "
"an mbunachar sonraí nó ag reáchtáil tástálacha. I Django 1.7, d'fhéadfadh go "
"dteipfeadh air seo go ciúin agus srian ar iarraidh a bheith mar thoradh air. "
"Chun an earráid a réiteach, cuir imirce leis an aip gan iad."

msgid "Features deprecated in 1.8"
msgstr "Gnéithe atá díscríofa i 1.8"

msgid "Selected methods in ``django.db.models.options.Options``"
msgstr "Modhanna roghnaithe i ``Django.db.Models.Options.Options``"

msgid ""
"As part of the formalization of the ``Model._meta`` API (from "
"the :class:`django.db.models.options.Options` class), a number of methods "
"have been deprecated and will be removed in Django 1.10:"
msgstr ""
"Mar chuid de fhoirmiú an `Mhúnla. API _meta`` (ón aicme:class: "
"`Django.db.Models.Options.Options`), tá roinnt modhanna curtha in iúl agus "
"bainfear iad i Django 1.10:"

msgid "Loading ``cycle`` and ``firstof`` template tags from ``future`` library"
msgstr ""
"Clibeanna teimpléad ``timthriall`` agus ``firstof`` á luchtú ó leabharlann "
"``todhcha``"

msgid ""
"Django 1.6 introduced ``{% load cycle from future %}`` and ``{% load firstof "
"from future %}`` syntax for forward compatibility of the :ttag:`cycle` "
"and :ttag:`firstof` template tags. This syntax is now deprecated and will be "
"removed in Django 1.10. You can simply remove the ``{% load ... from future "
"%}`` tags."
msgstr ""
"Thug Django 1.6 isteach ``{% timthriall ualaigh ón todhchaí%}`` agus ``{% "
"load firstof ón todhchaí%}`` comhréir le haghaidh comhoiriúnacht ar aghaidh "
"na gclibeanna teimpléad:ttag: `timthriall` agus:ttag: `firstof`. Tá an "
"comhréireacht seo díscríofa anois agus bainfear é i Django 1.10. Ní féidir "
"leat ach na clibeanna ``{% load... a bhaint as clibeanna%}`` sa todhchaí."

msgid "``django.conf.urls.patterns()``"
msgstr "``django.conf.urls.patrons () ``"

msgid ""
"In the olden days of Django, it was encouraged to reference views as strings "
"in ``urlpatterns``::"
msgstr ""
"Sna seanlaethanta de Django, spreagadh é chun tuairimí a thagairt mar "
"teaghráin i `urlpatterns`:"

msgid ""
"and Django would magically import ``myapp.views.myview`` internally and turn "
"the string into a real function reference. In order to reduce repetition "
"when referencing many views from the same module, the ``patterns()`` "
"function takes a required initial ``prefix`` argument which is prepended to "
"all views-as-strings in that set of ``urlpatterns``::"
msgstr ""
"agus d'iompórfadh Django ``myapp.views.myview`` go draíochtúil go "
"hinmheánach agus iompórfadh an teaghrán ina dtagairt feidhme fíor. D'fhonn "
"athrá a laghdú agus iad ag tagairt go leor tuairimí ón modúl céanna, glacann "
"an fheidhm ``patrúin () ``argóint tosaigh riachtanach ``prefix`` atá "
"réamhdhéanta do gach dearcadh mar teaghráin sa tsraith sin de "
"``urlpatterns``:"

msgid ""
"In the modern era, we have updated the tutorial to instead recommend "
"importing your views module and referencing your view functions (or classes) "
"directly. This has a number of advantages, all deriving from the fact that "
"we are using normal Python in place of \"Django String Magic\": the errors "
"when you mistype a view name are less obscure, IDEs can help with "
"autocompletion of view names, etc."
msgstr ""
"Sa ré nua-aimseartha, rinneamar an rang teagaisc a nuashonrú chun do mhodúl "
"tuairimí a iompórtáil agus tagairt a dhéanamh go díreach do fheidhmeanna "
"radhairc (nó ranganna). Tá roinnt buntáistí aige seo, gach rud a eascraíonn "
"ón bhfíric go bhfuilimid ag úsáid gnáth-Python in ionad “Django String "
"Magic”: níl na hearráidí nuair a chríochnóidh tú ainm amharc níos doiléire, "
"is féidir le IDEanna cabhrú le huathchomhlánú ainmneacha amharc, srl."

msgid ""
"So these days, the above use of the ``prefix`` arg is much more likely to be "
"written (and is better written) as::"
msgstr ""
"Mar sin na laethanta seo, is dóichí go scríobfar an úsáid thuas den "
"``prefix`` arg (agus is fearr é scríofa) mar:"

msgid ""
"Thus ``patterns()`` serves little purpose and is a burden when teaching new "
"users (answering the newbie's question \"why do I need this empty string as "
"the first argument to ``patterns()``?\"). For these reasons, we are "
"deprecating it. Updating your code is as simple as ensuring that "
"``urlpatterns`` is a list of ``django.conf.urls.url()`` instances. For "
"example::"
msgstr ""
"Dá bhrí sin is beag cuspóir a fhreastalaíonn ``patrúin () ``agus is ualach é "
"agus úsáideoirí nua á múineadh (ag freagairt ceist an newbie “cén fáth a "
"dteastaíonn an sreang folamh seo uaim mar an chéad argóint le ``patrúin "
"()``?”). Ar na cúiseanna seo, táimid ag cur síos air. Tá do chód a nuashonrú "
"chomh simplí le a chinntiú gur liosta de chásanna ``django.conf.urls.url () "
"``é `urlpatterns`. Mar shampla::"

msgid "Passing a string as ``view`` to ``django.conf.urls.url()``"
msgstr "Ag cur sreang mar ``view`` chuig ``django.conf.urls.url () ``"

msgid ""
"Related to the previous item, referencing views as strings in the ``url()`` "
"function is deprecated. Pass the callable view as described in the previous "
"section instead."
msgstr ""
"Baineann leis an mír roimhe seo, tá tagairt a thabhairt do thuairimí mar "
"theagairtí sa fheidhm ``url () ``. Pas an radharc inghlaonta mar a "
"thuairiscítear sa chuid roimhe seo ina ionad sin."

msgid "Template-related settings"
msgstr "Socruithe a bhaineann le teimpléad"

msgid ""
"As a consequence of the multiple template engines refactor, several settings "
"are deprecated in favor of :setting:`TEMPLATES`:"
msgstr ""
"Mar thoradh ar athfhachtóir na n-inneall teimpléad iolracha, déantar roinnt "
"socruithe a dhíchur i bhfabhra:setting: `TEMPLATES`:"

msgid "``django.core.context_processors``"
msgstr "``django.core.context_processors``"

msgid ""
"Built-in template context processors have been moved to "
"``django.template.context_processors``."
msgstr ""
"Tá próiseálaithe comhthéacs teimpléad ionsuite aistrithe chuig "
"``django.template.context_processors``."

msgid "``django.test.SimpleTestCase.urls``"
msgstr "``Django.Test.SimpleTestCase.URLs``"

msgid ""
"The attribute ``SimpleTestCase.urls`` for specifying URLconf configuration "
"in tests has been deprecated and will be removed in Django 1.10. "
"Use :func:`@override_settings(ROOT_URLCONF=...) "
"<django.test.override_settings>` instead."
msgstr ""
"Tá an tréith ``SimpleTestCase.url ``chun cumraíocht URLConf a shonrú i "
"dtástálacha a dhíchur agus bainfear é i Django 1.10. Úsáid: FUNC: "
"`@override_settings (ROOT_URLCONF =...) <django.test.override_settings>`ina "
"ionad sin."

msgid "``prefix`` argument to :func:`~django.conf.urls.i18n.i18n_patterns`"
msgstr "Argóint ``prefix`` chuig: func: `~django.conf.urls.i18n.i18n_patterns`"

msgid ""
"Related to the previous item, the ``prefix`` argument "
"to :func:`django.conf.urls.i18n.i18n_patterns` has been deprecated. Simply "
"pass a list of ``django.conf.urls.url()`` instances instead."
msgstr ""
"Baineann leis an mír roimhe seo, tá an argóint ``prefix`` go:func: "
"`django.conf.urls.i18n.i18n_patterns` curtha in iúl. Níl ort ach liosta de "
"chásanna ``django.conf.urls.url () ``a rith ina ionad."

msgid ""
"Using an incorrect count of unpacked values in the :ttag:`for` template tag"
msgstr ""
"Ag baint úsáide as comhaireamh mícheart luachanna neamhphacáilte sa chlib "
"teimpléad:ttag: `for`"

msgid ""
"Using an incorrect count of unpacked values in :ttag:`for` tag will raise an "
"exception rather than fail silently in Django 1.10."
msgstr ""
"Ag baint úsáide as comhaireamh mícheart de luachanna neamhphacáilte i gclib: "
"ttag: `for`, ardóidh eisceacht seachas go teip go ciúin i Django 1.10."

msgid "Passing a dotted path to ``reverse()`` and :ttag:`url`"
msgstr "Ag dul i gcosán poncaigh chuig ``reverse () ``agus:ttag: `url`"

msgid ""
"Reversing URLs by Python path is an expensive operation as it causes the "
"path being reversed to be imported. This behavior has also resulted in a "
"`security issue`_. Use :ref:`named URL patterns <naming-url-patterns>` for "
"reversing instead."
msgstr ""
"Is oibríocht daor é URLanna a aisiompú le cosán Python mar is cúis leis an "
"gcosán a iompórtáil. Mar thoradh ar an iompar seo tá `saincheist slándála`_ "
"mar thoradh ar an iompar seo freisin. Úsáid:ref: `patrúin URL ainmnithe "
"<naming-url-patterns>`chun aisiompú ina ionad sin."

msgid ""
"If you are using :mod:`django.contrib.sitemaps`, add the ``name`` argument "
"to the ``url`` that "
"references :func:`django.contrib.sitemaps.views.sitemap`::"
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag baint úsáide:mod: `django.contrib.sitemaps`, cuir an argóint "
"``ainm`` leis an `url ``a thagann tagair:func: "
"`django.contrib.sitemaps.views.sitemap`:"

msgid ""
"to ensure compatibility when reversing by Python path is removed in Django "
"1.10."
msgstr ""
"chun comhoiriúnacht a chinntiú nuair a bhaintear cosán Python a aisiompú i "
"Django 1.10."

msgid ""
"Similarly for GIS sitemaps, add "
"``name='django.contrib.gis.sitemaps.views.kml'`` or "
"``name='django.contrib.gis.sitemaps.views.kmz'``."
msgstr ""
"Mar an gcéanna le haghaidh léarscáileanna láithreáin GIS, cuir "
"``name='django.contrib.gis.sitemaps.views.kml'`` nó "
"``name='django.contrib.gis.sitemaps.views.kmz'``."

msgid ""
"If you are using a Python path for the :setting:`LOGIN_URL` "
"or :setting:`LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL` setting, use the name of the ``url()`` "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"Má tá cosán Python á úsáid agat don socrú:: `LOGIN_URL` nó:setting: "
"`LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL`, bain úsáid as ainm an ``url () ``ina ionad."

msgid "Aggregate methods and modules"
msgstr "Modhanna agus modúil chomhiomlána"

msgid ""
"The ``django.db.models.sql.aggregates`` and "
"``django.contrib.gis.db.models.sql.aggregates`` modules (both private API), "
"have been deprecated as ``django.db.models.aggregates`` and "
"``django.contrib.gis.db.models.aggregates`` are now also responsible for SQL "
"generation. The old modules will be removed in Django 1.10."
msgstr ""
"Tá na modúil ``django.db.models.sql.aggregates`` agus "
"``django.contrib.gis.db.models.sql.aggregates`` (an dá API príobháideach), "
"curtha as ``django.db.models.aggregates`` agus "
"``django.contrib.gis.db.models.aggregates`` tá siad freagrach anois as "
"giniúint SQL freisin. Bainfear na sean-mhodúil i Django 1.10."

msgid ""
"If you were using the old modules, see :doc:`Query Expressions </ref/models/"
"expressions>` for instructions on rewriting custom aggregates using the new "
"stable API."
msgstr ""
"Má bhí na sean-mhodúil á úsáid agat, féach: doc: `Query Expressions` </ref/"
"models/expressions> le haghaidh treoracha maidir le comhiomlánacha "
"saincheaptha a athscríobh ag baint úsáide as an API cobhsaí nua."

msgid ""
"The following methods and properties of ``django.db.models.sql.query.Query`` "
"have also been deprecated and the backwards compatibility shims will be "
"removed in Django 1.10:"
msgstr ""
"Tá na modhanna agus na hairíonna seo a leanas de "
"`Django.db.Models.sql.query.query`` a dhíchur freisin agus bainfear na shims "
"comhoiriúnachta ar ais i Django 1.10:"

msgid "``Query.aggregates``, replaced by ``annotations``."
msgstr "``Query.aggregates``, ina ionad `annotations``."

msgid "``Query.aggregate_select``, replaced by ``annotation_select``."
msgstr "``Query.Aggregate_Select``, `annotation_select`` in ionad."

msgid "``Query.add_aggregate()``, replaced by ``add_annotation()``."
msgstr "``Query.add_aggregate () ``, ina ionad ``add_annotation ()``."

msgid "``Query.set_aggregate_mask()``, replaced by ``set_annotation_mask()``."
msgstr "``Query.set_aggregate_mask () ``, ina ionad `set_annotation_mask ()``."

msgid ""
"``Query.append_aggregate_mask()``, replaced by ``append_annotation_mask()``."
msgstr ""
"``Query.append_aggregate_mask () ``, ina ionad ``append_annotation_mask ()``."

msgid "Extending management command arguments through ``Command.option_list``"
msgstr "Argóintí ordaithe bainistíochta a leathnú trí ``Command.option_list``"

msgid ""
"Management commands now use :py:mod:`argparse` instead of :py:mod:`optparse` "
"to parse command-line arguments passed to commands. This also means that the "
"way to add custom arguments to commands has changed: instead of extending "
"the ``option_list`` class list, you should now override "
"the :meth:`~django.core.management.BaseCommand.add_arguments` method and add "
"arguments through ``argparse.add_argument()``. See :ref:`this example "
"<custom-commands-options>` for more details."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann orduithe bainistíochta anois: py:mod: `argparse` in ionad:py:mod: "
"`optparse` chun argóintí líne ordaithe a chuirtear chuig orduithe a "
"pháirseáil. Ciallaíonn sé seo freisin go bhfuil athrú tagtha ar an mbealach "
"chun argóintí saincheaptha a chur le horduithe: in ionad an liosta ranga "
"``option_list`` a leathnú, ba cheart duit anois an modh:meth: "
"`~django.core.management.baseCommand.add_arguments` a shárú agus argóintí a "
"chur trí `argparse.add_argument () `. Féach: ref: `an sampla seo <custom-"
"commands-options>`le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid "``django.core.management.NoArgsCommand``"
msgstr "``Django.Core.Management.NoArgsCommand``"

msgid ""
"The class ``NoArgsCommand`` is now deprecated and will be removed in Django "
"1.10. Use :class:`~django.core.management.BaseCommand` instead, which takes "
"no arguments by default."
msgstr ""
"Tá an rang ``NoArgsCommand`` díluaite anois agus bainfear é i Django 1.10. "
"Úsáid:class: `~django.core.management.baseCommand` ina ionad sin, nach "
"dtógann aon argóintí de réir réamhshocraithe."

msgid "Listing all migrations in a project"
msgstr "Liostáil gach imirce i dtionscadal"

msgid ""
"The ``--list`` option of the :djadmin:`migrate` management command is "
"deprecated and will be removed in Django 1.10. Use :djadmin:`showmigrations` "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"Tá an rogha ``--list`` den ordú bainistíochta: djadmin: `migrate` "
"díluachtaithe agus bainfear é i Django 1.10. Úsáid: djaDmin: "
"`showmigrations` ina ionad."

msgid ""
"``cache_choices`` option of ``ModelChoiceField`` and "
"``ModelMultipleChoiceField``"
msgstr ""
"Rogha ``cache_choices`` de `ModelChoiceField`` agus "
"``ModelMultipleChoiceField``"

msgid ""
":class:`~django.forms.ModelChoiceField` "
"and :class:`~django.forms.ModelMultipleChoiceField` took an undocumented, "
"untested option ``cache_choices``. This cached querysets between multiple "
"renderings of the same ``Form`` object. This option is subject to an "
"accelerated deprecation and will be removed in Django 1.9."
msgstr ""
":class: `~Django.Forms.ModelChoiceField` agus:class: "
"`~django.forms.ModelMultipleChoiceField` rogha neamhdhoiciméadaithe, "
"neamhthástáilte ``cache_choices``. Cuireann an ceisteanna taiscéadaithe seo "
"idir illéiriú den réad ``Foirm ``céanna. Tá an rogha seo faoi réir "
"díghníomhú luathaithe agus bainfear é i Django 1.9."

msgid "``django.template.resolve_variable()``"
msgstr "``django.template.resolve_variable () ``"

msgid ""
"The function has been informally marked as \"Deprecated\" for some time. "
"Replace ``resolve_variable(path, context)`` with "
"``django.template.Variable(path).resolve(context)``."
msgstr ""
"Tá an fheidhm marcáilte go neamhfhoirmiúil mar “Díluachtaithe” le tamall. "
"Cuir ``resolve_variable (cosán, comhthéacs) ``in ionad "
"``django.template.variable (path) .solve (comhthéacs)``."

msgid "``django.contrib.webdesign``"
msgstr "``django.contrib.webdesign``"

msgid ""
"It provided the :ttag:`lorem` template tag which is now included in the "
"built-in tags. Simply remove ``'django.contrib.webdesign'`` "
"from :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` and ``{% load webdesign %}`` from your "
"templates."
msgstr ""
"Chuir sé an clib teimpléad: ttag: `lorem` ar fáil atá san áireamh anois sna "
"clibeanna ionsuite. Níl ort ach ``'django.contrib.webdesign'`` a bhaint "
"ó:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS` agus ``{% load webdesign%}`` ó do theimpléid."

msgid "``error_message`` argument to ``django.forms.RegexField``"
msgstr "``error_message`` argóint chuig ``django.forms.regexfield``"

msgid ""
"It provided backwards compatibility for pre-1.0 code, but its functionality "
"is redundant. Use ``Field.error_messages['invalid']`` instead."
msgstr ""
"Chuir sé comhoiriúnacht ar ais do chód réamh-1.0, ach tá a fheidhmiúlacht "
"iomarcach. Úsáid ``field.error_messages ['neamhbhailí'] ``ina ionad."

msgid "Old :tfilter:`unordered_list` syntax"
msgstr "Sean:tFilter: comhréir `unordered_list`"

msgid ""
"An older (pre-1.0), more restrictive and verbose input format for "
"the :tfilter:`unordered_list` template filter has been deprecated::"
msgstr ""
"Tá formáid ionchuir níos sine (réamh-1.0), níos srianta agus níos teoranta "
"don scagaire teimpléad:tfilter: `unordered_list` a dhíchur::"

msgid "Using the new syntax, this becomes::"
msgstr "Ag baint úsáide as an gcomhréir nua, éiríonn sé seo:"

msgid "``django.forms.Field._has_changed()``"
msgstr "``Django.Forms.Field. _aigh_athraithe () ``"

msgid ""
"Rename this method to :meth:`~django.forms.Field.has_changed` by removing "
"the leading underscore. The old name will still work until Django 1.10."
msgstr ""
"Athainmnigh an modh seo go: meth: `~django.forms.field.has_changed` tríd an "
"bhunscór tosaigh a bhaint. Oibreoidh an sean-ainm fós go dtí Django 1.10."

msgid "``django.utils.html.remove_tags()`` and ``removetags`` template filter"
msgstr ""
"``django.utils.html.remove_tags () ``agus scagaire teimpléad ```removetags``"

msgid ""
"``django.utils.html.remove_tags()`` as well as the template filter "
"``removetags`` have been deprecated as they cannot guarantee safe output. "
"Their existence is likely to lead to their use in security-sensitive "
"contexts where they are not actually safe."
msgstr ""
"Tá ``django.utils.html.remove_tags () ``chomh maith leis an scagaire "
"teimpléad ``removetags`` a dhíchur mar ní féidir leo aschur sábháilte a "
"ráthú. Is dócha go n-úsáidfear iad i gcomhthéacsanna atá íogair ó shlándáil "
"nuair nach bhfuil siad sábháilte i ndáiríre."

msgid ""
"The unused and undocumented ``django.utils.html.strip_entities()`` function "
"has also been deprecated."
msgstr ""
"Tá an fheidhm ``django.utils.html.strip_entity () ``neamhúsáidte agus neamh-"
"dhoiciméadaithe a dhíchur freisin."

msgid ""
"``is_admin_site`` argument to ``django.contrib.auth.views.password_reset()``"
msgstr ""
"``is_admin_site`` argóint chuig ``django.contrib.auth.views.password_reset "
"() ``"

msgid "It's a legacy option that should no longer be necessary."
msgstr "Is rogha oidhreachta é nár chóir go mbeadh gá a thuilleadh."

msgid "``SubfieldBase``"
msgstr "``Subfieldbase``"

msgid ""
"``django.db.models.fields.subclassing.SubfieldBase`` has been deprecated and "
"will be removed in Django 1.10. Historically, it was used to handle fields "
"where type conversion was needed when loading from the database, but it was "
"not used in ``.values()`` calls or in aggregates. It has been replaced "
"with :meth:`~django.db.models.Field.from_db_value`."
msgstr ""
"Tá ``Django.db.Models.Fields.subclassing.subfieldbase`` díluaite agus "
"bainfear é i Django 1.10. Go stairiúil, baineadh úsáid as chun réimsí a "
"láimhseáil ina raibh gá le comhshó cineálacha agus iad á luchtú ón mbunachar "
"sonraí, ach níor úsáideadh é i nglaonna `.values () `nó i gcomhiomlánacha. "
"Cuireadh: meth: `~django.db.models.field.from_db_value` in ionad é."

msgid ""
"The new approach doesn't call the :meth:`~django.db.models.Field.to_python` "
"method on assignment as was the case with ``SubfieldBase``. If you need that "
"behavior, reimplement the ``Creator`` class `from Django's source code "
"<https://github.com/django/django/blob/stable/1.8.x/django/db/models/fields/"
"subclassing.py#L31-L44>`_ in your project."
msgstr ""
"Ní ghlaonn an cur chuige nua ar an modh:: meth: "
"`~django.db.models.field.to_python` ar shannadh mar a bhí le "
"``SubfieldBase``. < https://github.com/django/django/blob/stable/1.8.x/"
"django/db/models/fields/subclassing.py#L31-L44>Má theastaíonn an t-iompar "
"sin uait, athchur i bhfeidhm an aicme ``Cruthaitheoir ``ó chód foinse Django "
"`_ i do thionscadal."

msgid "``django.utils.checksums``"
msgstr "``django.utils.checksums``"

msgid ""
"The ``django.utils.checksums`` module has been deprecated and will be "
"removed in Django 1.10. The functionality it provided (validating checksum "
"using the Luhn algorithm) was undocumented and not used in Django. The "
"module has been moved to the :pypi:`django-localflavor` package (version "
"1.1+)."
msgstr ""
"Tá an modúl ``django.utils.checksums`` díluaite agus bainfear é i Django "
"1.10. Ní raibh an fheidhmiúlacht a sholáthair sé (seicsum a bhailíochtú ag "
"baint úsáide as algartam Luhn) gan doiciméadú agus níor úsáidtear é i "
"Django. Tá an modúl aistrithe chuig an bpacáiste: pypi: `django-localflavor` "
"(leagan 1.1+)."

msgid "``InlineAdminForm.original_content_type_id``"
msgstr "``InlineAdminForm.Original_Content_Type_ID ``"

msgid ""
"The ``original_content_type_id`` attribute on ``InlineAdminForm`` has been "
"deprecated and will be removed in Django 1.10. Historically, it was used to "
"construct the \"view on site\" URL. This URL is now accessible using the "
"``absolute_url`` attribute of the form."
msgstr ""
"Tá an tréith ``original_content_type_id`` ar ``inlineAdminform`` díluaite "
"agus bainfear é i Django 1.10. Go stairiúil, baineadh úsáid as chun an URL "
"“amharc ar an láithreán” a thógáil. Tá an URL seo inrochtana anois ag baint "
"úsáide as tréith ``absolute_url ``den fhoirm."

msgid ""
"``django.views.generic.edit.FormMixin.get_form()``’s ``form_class`` argument"
msgstr ""
"Argóint ``foirm_clas`` ``django.views.generic.edit.formmixin.get_form ()``"

msgid ""
"``FormMixin`` subclasses that override the ``get_form()`` method should make "
"sure to provide a default value for the ``form_class`` argument since it's "
"now optional."
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart do fho-aicmí `FormMixin`` a sháraíonn an modh ``get_form () ``a "
"chinntiú go gcuirfeadh luach réamhshocraithe a sholáthar don argóint "
"``form_class`` ós rud é go bhfuil sé roghnach anois."

msgid ""
"Rendering templates loaded by :func:`~django.template.loader.get_template()` "
"with a :class:`~django.template.Context`"
msgstr ""
"Teimpléid rindreála luchtaithe ag: func: "
"`~django.template.loader.get_template () `le a:class: "
"`~django.template.context`"

msgid ""
"The return type of :func:`~django.template.loader.get_template()` has "
"changed in Django 1.8: instead of a :class:`django.template.Template`, it "
"returns a ``Template`` instance whose exact type depends on which backend "
"loaded it."
msgstr ""
"Tá athrú tagtha ar an gcineál tuairisceáin de:func: "
"`~django.template.loader.get_template () `i Django 1.8: in ionad a:class: "
"`django.template.template`, filleann sé sampla ``Template`` ar ais a bhfuil "
"a chineál cruinn ag brath ar an gcúltaca a luchtaigh é."

msgid ""
"Both classes provide a ``render()`` method, however, the former takes "
"a :class:`django.template.Context` as an argument while the latter expects "
"a :class:`dict`. This change is enforced through a deprecation path for "
"Django templates."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn an dá rang modh `render () ``, áfach, glacann an chéad cheann "
"a:class: `django.template.context` mar argóint agus tá an dara ceann ag súil "
"le a:class: `dict`. Cuirtear an t-athrú seo i bhfeidhm trí chosán diúltaithe "
"do theimpléid Django."

msgid ""
"All this also applies to :func:`~django.template.loader.select_template()`."
msgstr ""
"Baineann sé seo go léir freisin la:func: "
"`~django.template.loader.select_template () `."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.template.Template` and :class:`~django.template.Context` "
"classes in template responses"
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.template.template` agus:class: `~django.template.context` "
"ranganna i bhfreagraí teimpléad"

msgid ""
"Some methods of :class:`~django.template.response.SimpleTemplateResponse` "
"and :class:`~django.template.response.TemplateResponse` "
"accepted :class:`django.template.Context` "
"and :class:`django.template.Template` objects as arguments. They should now "
"receive :class:`dict` and backend-dependent template objects respectively."
msgstr ""
"Roinnt modhanna de:class: `~django.template.response.simpletemplateResponse` "
"agus:class: `~django.template.response.templateResponse` ghlacth:class: "
"`django.template.context` agus:class: `django.template.template.template` "
"rudaí mar argóintí. Ba chóir dóibh anois: aicme: `dict` agus rudaí teimpléad "
"atá ag brath ar chúltaca faoi seach a fháil."

msgid ""
"This also applies to the return types if you have subclassed either template "
"response class."
msgstr ""
"Baineann sé seo freisin leis na cineálacha tuairisceáin má tá ceachtar aicme "
"freagartha teimpléad curtha agat."

msgid ""
"Check the :doc:`template response API documentation </ref/template-"
"response>` for details."
msgstr ""
"Seiceáil an doiciméadú :doc:`template response API </ref/template-response>` "
"le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid "``current_app`` argument of template-related APIs"
msgstr "Argóint ``current_app ``de APIs a bhaineann le teimpléad"

msgid ""
"The following functions and classes will no longer accept a ``current_app`` "
"parameter to set an URL namespace in Django 1.10:"
msgstr ""
"Ní ghlacfaidh na feidhmeanna agus na ranganna seo a leanas le paraiméadar "
"``current_app`` a thuilleadh chun spás ainmneacha URL a shocrú i Django 1.10:"

msgid ""
"Set ``request.current_app`` instead, where ``request`` is the first argument "
"to these functions or classes. If you're using a plain ``Context``, use a "
"``RequestContext`` instead."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh ``request.current_app ``ina ionad sin, áit a bhfuil ``request`` an "
"chéad argóint leis na feidhmeanna nó na ranganna seo. Má tá “Context” simplí "
"á úsáid agat, bain úsáid as ``requestContext`` ina ionad."

msgid ""
"``dictionary`` and ``context_instance`` arguments of rendering functions"
msgstr ""
"Argóintí ``foclóir`` agus ``context_instance`` na bhfeidhmeanna rindreála"

msgid ""
"The following functions will no longer accept the ``dictionary`` and "
"``context_instance`` parameters in Django 1.10:"
msgstr ""
"Ní ghlacfaidh na feidhmeanna seo a leanas leis na paraiméadair "
"``Dictionary`` agus `context_instance`` i Django 1.10 a thuilleadh:"

msgid ""
"Use the ``context`` parameter instead. When ``dictionary`` is passed as a "
"positional argument, which is the most common idiom, no changes are needed."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid an paraiméadar ``context`` ina ionad. Nuair a chuirtear `foclóir` ar "
"rith mar argóint seasaimh, arb é an t-athrú is coitianta, ní gá aon "
"athruithe."

msgid ""
"If you're passing a :class:`~django.template.Context` in "
"``context_instance``, pass a :class:`dict` in the ``context`` parameter "
"instead. If you're passing a :class:`~django.template.RequestContext`, pass "
"the request separately in the ``request`` parameter."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag rith a:class: `~django.template.context` i `context_instance``, "
"pas a:class: `dict` sa pharaiméadar ``context`` ina ionad. Má tá tú ag rith "
"a:class: `~django.template.requestContext`, cuir an t-iarratas ar leithligh "
"sa pharaiméadar ``request``."

msgid "``dirs`` argument of template-finding functions"
msgstr "Argóint ``dirs`` de fheidhmeanna aimsithe teimpléad"

msgid ""
"The following functions will no longer accept a ``dirs`` parameter to "
"override ``TEMPLATE_DIRS`` in Django 1.10:"
msgstr ""
"Ní ghlacfaidh na feidhmeanna seo a leanas le paraiméadar ``dirs`` a "
"thuilleadh chun `TEMPLATE_DIRS`` a shárú i Django 1.10:"

msgid ""
"The parameter didn't work consistently across different template loaders and "
"didn't work for included templates."
msgstr ""
"Níor oibrigh an paraiméadar go comhsheasmhach thar lódairí teimpléid éagsúla "
"agus níor oibrigh sé do theimpléid áirithe."

msgid "``django.template.loader.BaseLoader``"
msgstr "``Django.Template.Loader.BaseLoader``"

msgid ""
"``django.template.loader.BaseLoader`` was renamed to "
"``django.template.loaders.base.Loader``. If you've written a custom template "
"loader that inherits ``BaseLoader``, you must inherit ``Loader`` instead."
msgstr ""
"Athainmníodh ``Django.Template.Loader`` go "
"`Django.Template.Loaders.Base.Loader``. Má tá lódóir teimpléad saincheaptha "
"scríofa agat a fhaigheann ``Baseloader`` oidhreachta, ní mór duit ``Loader`` "
"a oidhreacht ina ionad sin."

msgid "``django.test.utils.TestTemplateLoader``"
msgstr "``Django.Test.Utils.TestTemplateLoader ``"

msgid ""
"Private API ``django.test.utils.TestTemplateLoader`` is deprecated in favor "
"of ``django.template.loaders.locmem.Loader`` and will be removed in Django "
"1.9."
msgstr ""
"Tá API príobháideach ``Django.Test.Utils.TestTemplateLoader`` a dhíchur i "
"bhfabhar ``Django.Template.Loaders.Locmem.Loader`` agus bainfear é i Django "
"1.9."

msgid "Support for the ``max_length`` argument on custom ``Storage`` classes"
msgstr ""
"Tacaíocht don argóint ``max_length ``ar ranganna saincheaptha ``Stóráil``"

msgid ""
"``Storage`` subclasses should add ``max_length=None`` as a parameter "
"to :meth:`~django.core.files.storage.Storage.get_available_name` and/"
"or :meth:`~django.core.files.storage.Storage.save` if they override either "
"method. Support for storages that do not accept this argument will be "
"removed in Django 1.10."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go gcuirfeadh fo-aicmí ``Max_Length=None`` mar pharaiméadar chuig: "
"`~django.core.files.storage.storage.get_available_name` agus/nó :meth: "
"`~django.core.files.storage.storage.save` má sháraíonn siad ceachtar modh. "
"Bainfear tacaíocht do stórais nach nglacann leis an argóint seo i Django "
"1.10."

msgid "``qn`` replaced by ``compiler``"
msgstr "cuir ``qn`` in ionad ``tiomsaitheoir ``"

msgid ""
"In previous Django versions, various internal ORM methods (mostly ``as_sql`` "
"methods) accepted a ``qn`` (for \"quote name\") argument, which was a "
"reference to a function that quoted identifiers for sending to the database. "
"In Django 1.8, that argument has been renamed to ``compiler`` and is now a "
"full ``SQLCompiler`` instance. For backwards-compatibility, calling a "
"``SQLCompiler`` instance performs the same name-quoting that the ``qn`` "
"function used to. However, this backwards-compatibility shim is immediately "
"deprecated: you should rename your ``qn`` arguments to ``compiler``, and "
"call ``compiler.quote_name_unless_alias(...)`` where you previously called "
"``qn(...)``."
msgstr ""
"I leaganacha Django roimhe seo, ghlac modhanna inmheánacha ORM éagsúla "
"(modhanna `as_sql`` den chuid is mó) le argóint ``qn`` (le haghaidh “ainm "
"luachana”), a bhí ina thagairt d'fheidhm a luaigh aitheantóirí le seoladh "
"chuig an mbunachar sonraí. I Django 1.8, athainmníodh an argóint sin go "
"``compiler`` agus is sampla iomlán ``SQLcompiler`` í anois. Maidir le "
"comhoiriúnacht ar ais, déanann glaoch ar shampla ``SQLCompiler`` an t-ainm "
"céanna a luaitear leis an bhfeidhm ``qn``. Mar sin féin, déantar an shim "
"comhoiriúnachta cúil seo a dhíchur láithreach: ba cheart duit d'argóintí "
"``qn`` a athainmniú go ``compiler``, agus glaoch ar "
"``compiler.quote_name_unless_alias (...) ``áit ar thug tú ``qn (...)`` "
"roimhe seo."

msgid "Default value of ``RedirectView.permanent``"
msgstr "Luach réamhshocraithe de ``RedirectView.permanent``"

msgid ""
"The default value of the :attr:`RedirectView.permanent "
"<django.views.generic.base.RedirectView.permanent>` attribute will change "
"from ``True`` to ``False`` in Django 1.9."
msgstr ""
"Athróidh luach réamhshocraithe an tréith: attr: `RedirectView.permanent "
"<django.views.generic.base.RedirectView.permanent>`ó ``True`` go ``False`` i "
"Django 1.9."

msgid ""
"Using ``AuthenticationMiddleware`` without "
"``SessionAuthenticationMiddleware``"
msgstr ""
"Ag baint úsáide as ``AuthenticationMiddleWare`` gan "
"`SessionAuthenticationMiddleware``"

msgid ""
"``django.contrib.auth.middleware.SessionAuthenticationMiddleware`` was added "
"in Django 1.7. In Django 1.7.2, its functionality was moved to "
"``auth.get_user()`` and, for backwards compatibility, enabled only if "
"``'django.contrib.auth.middleware.SessionAuthenticationMiddleware'`` appears "
"in ``MIDDLEWARE_CLASSES``."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh ``django.contrib.auth.middleware.sessionAuthenticationMiddleware`` "
"`i Django 1.7. I Django 1.7.2, aistríodh a fheidhmiúlacht chuig "
"`auth.get_user () ``agus, le haghaidh comhoiriúnacht ar ais, cumasaíodh é "
"ach amháin má tá "
"``django.contrib.auth.middleware.sessionAuthenticationMiddleware'` `le "
"feiceáil i `MIDDLEWARE_CLASSES`."

msgid ""
"In Django 1.10, session verification will be enabled regardless of whether "
"or not ``SessionAuthenticationMiddleware`` is enabled (at which point "
"``SessionAuthenticationMiddleware`` will have no significance). You can add "
"it to your ``MIDDLEWARE_CLASSES`` sometime before then to opt-in. Please "
"read the :ref:`upgrade considerations <session-invalidation-on-password-"
"change>` first."
msgstr ""
"I Django 1.10, cumasófar fíorú seisiúin beag beann an bhfuil "
"``SessionAuthenticationMiddleware` cumasaithe nó nach bhfuil (ag an bpointe "
"sin ní bheidh aon tábhacht ag ``SessionAuthenticationMiddleware``). Is "
"féidir leat é a chur le do `MIDDLEWARE_CLASSES`` am éigin roimh sin chun "
"roghnú isteach. <session-invalidation-on-password-change>Léigh le do thoil "
"an:ref: `breithnithe uasghrádaithe `ar dtús."

msgid "``django.contrib.sitemaps.FlatPageSitemap``"
msgstr "``Django.Contrib.Sitemaps.FlatPageSitemap``"

msgid ""
"``django.contrib.sitemaps.FlatPageSitemap`` has moved to "
"``django.contrib.flatpages.sitemaps.FlatPageSitemap``. The old import "
"location is deprecated and will be removed in Django 1.9."
msgstr ""
"Tá ``Django.Contrib.SiteMaps.FlatPageSitemap`` tar éis bogadh chuig "
"``Django.Contrib.FlatPages.Sitemaps.FlatPageSitemap``. Tá an sean-shuíomh "
"allmhairithe díscoite agus bainfear é i Django 1.9."

msgid "Model ``Field.related``"
msgstr "Múnla ``Field.Related``"

msgid ""
"Private attribute ``django.db.models.Field.related`` is deprecated in favor "
"of ``Field.rel``.  The latter is an instance of "
"``django.db.models.fields.related.ForeignObjectRel`` which replaces "
"``django.db.models.related.RelatedObject``. The ``django.db.models.related`` "
"module has been removed and the ``Field.related`` attribute will be removed "
"in Django 1.10."
msgstr ""
"Tá tréith phríobháideach ``Django.db.Models.Field.Related`` a dhíchur i "
"bhfabhar ``Field.rel``. Is sampla é an dara ceann de "
"``Django.db.Models.Fields.Related.ForeignoBjectrel`` a chuireann in ionad "
"``Django.db.Models.Related.RelatedObject``. Baineadh an modúl "
"``django.db.models.related`` agus bainfear an tréith ``Field.Related`` i "
"Django 1.10."

msgid "``ssi`` template tag"
msgstr "Clib teimpléad ``ssi``"

msgid ""
"The ``ssi`` template tag allows files to be included in a template by "
"absolute path. This is of limited use in most deployment situations, and "
"the :ttag:`include` tag often makes more sense. This tag is now deprecated "
"and will be removed in Django 1.10."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an chlib teimpléad ``ssi`` comhaid a áireamh i dteimpléad de réir "
"cosán iomlán. Úsáidtear teoranta é seo i bhformhór na gcásanna imscartha, "
"agus is minic a bhíonn níos ciall ag an gclibe:ttag: `include`. Tá an chlib "
"seo imithe anois agus bainfear é i Django 1.10."

msgid "``=`` as comparison operator in ``if`` template tag"
msgstr "``=`` mar oibreoir comparáide i gclib teimpléad ``if ``"

msgid ""
"Using a single equals sign with the ``{% if %}`` template tag for equality "
"testing was undocumented and untested. It's now deprecated in favor of "
"``==``."
msgstr ""
"Bhí comhartha comhionann amháin a úsáid leis an gclib teimpléad ``{% if%}`` "
"le haghaidh tástáil comhionannais gan doiciméadú agus gan tástáil. Tá sé "
"curtha anois i bhfabhar ``==``."

msgid "``%(<foo>)s`` syntax in ``ModelFormMixin.success_url``"
msgstr "Comhréir ``% (<foo>) s`` i `ModelFormMixin.Success_URL``"

msgid ""
"The legacy ``%(<foo>)s`` syntax in :attr:`ModelFormMixin.success_url "
"<django.views.generic.edit.ModelFormMixin.success_url>` is deprecated and "
"will be removed in Django 1.10."
msgstr ""
"<django.views.generic.edit.ModelFormMixin.success_url>Tá an comhréir "
"oidhreachta ``% (<foo>) s`` in:attr: `ModelFormMixin.Success_URL "
"`díluachtaithe agus bainfear é i Django 1.10."

msgid "``GeoQuerySet`` aggregate methods"
msgstr "Modhanna comhiomlána ``GeoquerySet ``"

msgid ""
"The ``collect()``, ``extent()``, ``extent3d()``, ``make_line()``, and "
"``unionagg()`` aggregate methods are deprecated and should be replaced by "
"their function-based aggregate equivalents (``Collect``, ``Extent``, "
"``Extent3D``, ``MakeLine``, and ``Union``)."
msgstr ""
"Tá na modhanna comhiomlána ``collection () ``, `mhéid ()``, `extent3d () ``, "
"`make_line ()``, agus ``unionagg () ``,`` luchtaithe agus ba cheart a "
"gcoibhéisí comhiomlán feidhmiúbhunaithe a chur in ionad iad (`Collect``, "
"`Extent``, `Extent3D``, `Makeline``, agus ``Aontas ``)."

msgid "Signature of the ``allow_migrate`` router method"
msgstr "Síniú an modh ródaire `allow_migrate``"

msgid ""
"The signature of the :meth:`allow_migrate` method of database routers has "
"changed from ``allow_migrate(db, model)`` to ``allow_migrate(db, app_label, "
"model_name=None, **hints)``."
msgstr ""
"Tá síniú an modh:meth: `allow_migrate` de ródairí bunachar sonraí athraithe "
"ó ``allow_migration (db, model) ``go `allow_migration (db, app_label, "
"model_name=None, **leideanna)``."

msgid ""
"When ``model_name`` is set, the value that was previously given through the "
"``model`` positional argument may now be found inside the ``hints`` "
"dictionary under the key ``'model'``."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a shocraítear ``model_name``, is féidir an luach a tugadh roimhe seo "
"tríd an argóint seasaimh ``samhail` `a fháil taobh istigh den fhoclóir "
"``leideanna ``faoin eochair ``samhail``."

msgid ""
"After switching to the new signature the router will also be called by "
"the :class:`~django.db.migrations.operations.RunPython` "
"and :class:`~django.db.migrations.operations.RunSQL` operations."
msgstr ""
"Tar éis aistriú go dtí an síniú nua glaofar an ródaire freisin ag na "
"hoibríochtaí:: class: `~django.db.migrations.operations.runpython` "
"agus:class: `~django.db.migrations.operations.runsql`."

msgid "Features removed in 1.8"
msgstr "Gnéithe bainte i 1.8"

msgid ""
"These features have reached the end of their deprecation cycle and are "
"removed in Django 1.8. See :ref:`deprecated-features-1.6` for details, "
"including how to remove usage of these features."
msgstr ""
"Tá na gnéithe seo tar éis deireadh a dtimthriall díscrúdaithe bainte amach "
"agus baintear iad i Django 1.8. Féach: Ref: `deprecated-features-1.6` le "
"haghaidh sonraí, lena n-áirítear conas úsáid na ngnéithe seo a bhaint."

msgid "``django.contrib.comments`` is removed."
msgstr "Baintear ``django.contrib.comments``."

msgid "The following transaction management APIs are removed:"
msgstr "Baintear na APIs bainistíochta idirbheart seo a leanas:"

msgid "``TransactionMiddleware``"
msgstr "``Idirbheartaíocht Meánmhéireach``"

msgid ""
"the decorators and context managers ``autocommit``, ``commit_on_success``, "
"and ``commit_manually``, defined in ``django.db.transaction``"
msgstr ""
"na maisitheoirí agus na bainisteoirí comhthéacs ``autochommit``, "
"`commit_on_rath``, agus ``commit_láimh``, a shainmhínítear in "
"``django.db.transaction``"

msgid ""
"the functions ``commit_unless_managed`` and ``rollback_unless_managed``, "
"also defined in ``django.db.transaction``"
msgstr ""
"na feidhmeanna ``commit_unless_managed`` agus ``rollback_unless_managed``, "
"atá sainmhínithe freisin in ``django.db.transaction``"

msgid ""
"The :ttag:`cycle` and :ttag:`firstof` template tags auto-escape their "
"arguments."
msgstr ""
"Ealaíonn clibeanna teimpléad:ttag: `timthriall` agus:ttag: `firstof` a n-"
"argóintí go huathoibríoch."

msgid "The ``SEND_BROKEN_LINK_EMAILS`` setting is removed."
msgstr "Baintear an socrú ``SEND_BROKEN_LINK_EMAILS``."

msgid "``django.middleware.doc.XViewMiddleware`` is removed."
msgstr "Baintear ``django.middleware.doc.xviewmiddleware``."

msgid "The ``Model._meta.module_name`` alias is removed."
msgstr "An ``Samhail. Baintear alias _meta.module_name``."

msgid ""
"The backward compatible shims introduced to rename ``get_query_set`` and "
"similar queryset methods are removed. This affects the following classes: "
"``BaseModelAdmin``, ``ChangeList``, ``BaseCommentNode``, "
"``GenericForeignKey``, ``Manager``, ``SingleRelatedObjectDescriptor`` and "
"``ReverseSingleRelatedObjectDescriptor``."
msgstr ""
"Baintear na shimanna comhoiriúnacha ar chúl a tugadh isteach chun "
"``get_query_set`` a athainmniú agus modhanna ceisteanna comhchosúla. Bíonn "
"tionchar aige seo ar na haicmí seo a leanas: `BaseModelAdmin``, "
"`Changelist``, `BaseCommentNode``, `GenericForeignKey``, ``Manager``, "
"`SingleRelateDObjectDescriptor`` agus "
"``ReversesingleRelateDobjectDescriptor``."

msgid ""
"The backward compatible shims introduced to rename the attributes "
"``ChangeList.root_query_set`` and ``ChangeList.query_set`` are removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear na shims comhoiriúnacha ar chúl a tugadh isteach chun na tréithe "
"``changelist.root_query_set`` agus `Changelist.query_set`` a athainmniú."

msgid ""
"``django.views.defaults.shortcut`` and ``django.conf.urls.shortcut`` are "
"removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear ``django.views.defaults.shortcut`` agus "
"``django.conf.urls.shortcut``."

msgid "Support for the Python Imaging Library (PIL) module is removed."
msgstr "Baintear tacaíocht do mhodúl Leabharlann Íomháithe Python (PIL)."

msgid "The following private APIs are removed:"
msgstr "Baintear na APIs príobháideacha seo a leanas:"

msgid "``django.db.backend``"
msgstr "``django.db.backend``"

msgid "``django.db.close_connection()``"
msgstr "``django.db.close_connection () ``"

msgid "``django.db.backends.creation.BaseDatabaseCreation.set_autocommit()``"
msgstr ""
"``Django.db.backends.creation.basedatabasecreation.set_autoCommit () ``"

msgid "``django.db.transaction.is_managed()``"
msgstr "``django.db.transaction.is_managed () ``"

msgid "``django.db.transaction.managed()``"
msgstr "``django.db.transaction.managed () ``"

msgid "``django.forms.widgets.RadioInput`` is removed."
msgstr "Baintear ``Django.Forms.Widgets.RadioInput``."

msgid ""
"The module ``django.test.simple`` and the class "
"``django.test.simple.DjangoTestSuiteRunner`` are removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear an modúl ``django.test.simple`` agus an rang "
"``Django.Test.Simple.DjangoTestSuiterunner``."

msgid "The module ``django.test._doctest`` is removed."
msgstr "An modúl ``django.test. Baintear _doctest ``."

msgid ""
"The ``CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_ANONYMOUS_ONLY`` setting is removed. This change "
"affects both ``django.middleware.cache.CacheMiddleware`` and "
"``django.middleware.cache.UpdateCacheMiddleware`` despite the lack of a "
"deprecation warning in the latter class."
msgstr ""
"Baintear an socrú ``CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_ANONYMOUS_ONLY``. Bíonn tionchar ag an "
"athrú seo ar ``django.middleware.cache.cacheMiddleware`` agus "
"``django.middleware.cache.updatecacheMiddleware`` araon in ainneoin easpa "
"rabhaidh díphríochta sa rang deireanach."

msgid ""
"Usage of the hard-coded *Hold down \"Control\", or \"Command\" on a Mac, to "
"select more than one.* string to override or append to user-provided "
"``help_text`` in forms for ``ManyToMany`` model fields is not performed by "
"Django anymore either at the model or forms layer."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid an “Rialú”, nó “Ordú” crua-chódaithe ar Mac, chun níos mó ná ceann "
"amháin a roghnó.* ní dhéanann Django níos mó ag an gciseal samhail ná ag an "
"gciseal foirmeacha samhail ``ManyTomany` a thuilleadh le ``help_text`` a "
"sholáthraíonn an úsáideoir."

msgid ""
"The ``Model._meta.get_(add|change|delete)_permission`` methods are removed."
msgstr ""
"An ``Samhail. Baintear modhanna _meta.get_ (add|change|scriosadh) _ceadúnaí."

msgid ""
"The session key ``django_language`` is no longer read for backwards "
"compatibility."
msgstr ""
"Ní léitear an eochair seisiúin ``django_language`` a thuilleadh le haghaidh "
"comhoiriúnacht ar ais."

msgid ""
"Geographic Sitemaps are removed (``django.contrib.gis.sitemaps.views.index`` "
"and ``django.contrib.gis.sitemaps.views.sitemap``)."
msgstr ""
"Baintear léarscáileanna Suímh Geografacha "
"(``django.contrib.gis.sitemaps.views.index`` agus "
"``django.contrib.gis.sitemaps.views.sitemap``)."

msgid ""
"``django.utils.html.fix_ampersands``, the ``fix_ampersands`` template "
"filter, and ``django.utils.html.clean_html`` are removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear ``django.utils.html.fix_ampersands``, an scagaire teimpléad "
"``fix_ampersands``, agus ``django.utils.html.clean_html``."

msgid "Django 1.8.1 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoileadh Django 1.8.1"

msgid ""
"Django 1.8.1 fixes several bugs in 1.8 and includes some optimizations in "
"the migrations framework."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.8.1 roinnt fabhtanna i 1.8 agus tá roinnt optamaithe san "
"áireamh sa chreat imirce."

msgid ""
"Added support for serializing :class:`~datetime.timedelta` objects in "
"migrations (:ticket:`24566`)."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíocht bhreise do shraitheoireacht: class: `~datetime.timedelta` rudaí in "
"imirce (:ticket: `24566`)."

msgid ""
"Restored proper parsing of the :djadmin:`testserver` command's positional "
"arguments (fixture names) (:ticket:`24571`)."
msgstr ""
"Athchóirigh parsáil cheart ar argóintí seasaimh an ordaithe: djadmin: "
"`testserver` (ainmneacha daingneáin) (:ticket: `24571`)."

msgid ""
"Prevented ``TypeError`` in translation functions ``check_for_language()`` "
"and ``get_language_bidi()`` when translations are deactivated "
"(:ticket:`24569`)."
msgstr ""
"Cosc ar ``typeerror`` i bhfeidhmeanna aistriúcháin ``check_for_language () "
"``agus ``get_language_bidi ()`` nuair a dhíghníomhachtar aistriúcháin "
"(:ticket: `24569`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed :djadmin:`squashmigrations` command when "
"using :class:`~django.db.migrations.operations.SeparateDatabaseAndState` "
"(:ticket:`24278`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraithe:DjaDmin: ordú `squashmigrations` nuair a úsáidtear: class: "
"`~django.db.migrations.Operations.SeparateDatabaseAndState` (:ticket: "
"`24278`)."

msgid ""
"Stripped microseconds from ``datetime`` values when using an older version "
"of the MySQLdb DB API driver as it does not support fractional seconds "
"(:ticket:`24584`)."
msgstr ""
"Micreasoicind a scriosadh ó luachanna ``datetime`` agus leagan níos sine den "
"tiománaí API MySQLDB DB á úsáid toisc nach dtacaíonn sé le soicindí "
"codánacha (:ticket: `24584`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a migration crash when "
"altering :class:`~django.db.models.ManyToManyField`\\s (:ticket:`24513`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste imirce nuair a athraí:class: "
"`~django.db.models.manyTomanyField`\\ s (:ticket: `24513`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash with ``QuerySet.update()`` on foreign keys to one-to-one "
"fields (:ticket:`24578`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste le ``QuerySet.Update () ``ar eochracha eachtracha chuig "
"réimsí duine le duine (:ticket: `24578`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression in the model detail view "
"of :mod:`~django.contrib.admindocs` when a model has a reverse foreign key "
"relation (:ticket:`24624`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú i radharc mionsonraí an tsamhail ar:mod: "
"`~django.contrib.admindocs` nuair a bhíonn caidreamh eochair eachtrach droim "
"ag samhail (:ticket: `24624`)."

msgid ""
"Prevented arbitrary file inclusions in :mod:`~django.contrib.admindocs` "
"(:ticket:`24625`)."
msgstr ""
"Cosc ar chuimsiú comhad treallach in:mod: `~django.contrib.admindocs` "
"(:ticket: `24625`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash with ``QuerySet.update()`` on foreign keys to instances with "
"``uuid`` primary keys (:ticket:`24611`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste le ``QuerySet.Update () ``ar eochracha eachtracha go "
"cásanna le eochracha príomhúil ``uuid`` (:ticket: `24611`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed database introspection with SQLite 3.8.9 (released April 8, 2015) "
"(:ticket:`24637`)."
msgstr ""
"Introspéireacht bunachar sonraí seasta le SQLite 3.8.9 (eisithe 8 Aibreán, "
"2015) (:ticket: `24637`)."

msgid ""
"Updated ``urlpatterns`` examples generated by :djadmin:`startproject` to "
"remove usage of referencing views by dotted path in "
"``django.conf.urls.url()`` which is deprecated in Django 1.8 "
"(:ticket:`24635`)."
msgstr ""
"Samplaí nuashonraithe ``urlpatterns`` a ghineann: djadmin: `startproject` "
"chun úsáid tuairimí tagartha a bhaint de réir cosán poncair i "
"``django.conf.urls.url () ``atá díscoite i Django 1.8 (:ticket: `24635`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed queries where an expression was referenced in ``order_by()``, but "
"wasn't part of the select clause. An example query is "
"``qs.annotate(foo=F('field')).values('pk').order_by('foo'))`` "
"(:ticket:`24615`)."
msgstr ""
"Fiosruithe seasta inar tagraíodh abairt i ``order_by () ``, ach nach raibh "
"sé mar chuid den chlásal roghnaithe. Is é ceist shamplach ná ``qs.annotate "
"(foo=f ('field')) .values ('pk') .order_by ('foo')) ``(:ticket: `24615`)."

msgid "Fixed a database table name quoting regression (:ticket:`24605`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh ainm tábla bunachar sonraí ag lua aischéimniú (:ticket: `24605`)."

msgid ""
"Prevented the loss of ``null``/``not null`` column properties during field "
"alteration of MySQL databases (:ticket:`24595`)."
msgstr ""
"Cosc ar chailliúint airíonna colún ``null``/`not null`` le linn athrú réimse "
"bunachair sonraí MySQL (:ticket: `24595`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed JavaScript path of ``contrib.admin``’s related field widget when using "
"alternate static file storages (:ticket:`24655`)."
msgstr ""
"Conair JavaScript seasta de ghuirléid réimse gaolmhar ``contrib.admin`` "
"nuair a úsáidtear stórálaí comhad statacha malartacha (:ticket: `24655`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a migration crash when adding new relations to models "
"(:ticket:`24573`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste imirce nuair a chuirtear caidreamh nua le samhlacha "
"(:ticket: `24573`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a migration crash when applying migrations with model managers on "
"Python 3 that were generated on Python 2 (:ticket:`24701`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste imirce agus imirce á chur i bhfeidhm le bainisteoirí "
"samhail ar Python 3 a ghintear ar Python 2 (:ticket: `24701`)."

msgid ""
"Restored the ability to use iterators as queryset filter arguments "
"(:ticket:`24719`)."
msgstr ""
"Athchóirigh sé an cumas athraitheoirí a úsáid mar argóintí scagaire "
"ceisteanna (:ticket: `24719`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a migration crash when renaming the target model of a many-to-many "
"relation (:ticket:`24725`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste imirce nuair a athainmnítear an spriocmhúnla de chaidreamh "
"go leor (:ticket: `24725`)."

msgid ""
"Removed flushing of the test database with :option:`test --keepdb`, which "
"prevented apps with data migrations from using the option (:ticket:`24729`)."
msgstr ""
"Bainte sruthú an bhunachar sonraí tástála le: rogha: `test --keepdb`, a "
"chuir cosc ar aipeanna le himirce sonraí an rogha a úsáid (:ticket: `24729`)."

msgid "Fixed ``makemessages`` crash in some locales (:ticket:`23271`)."
msgstr "Timpiste seasta ``makemessages`` i roinnt áiteanna (:ticket: `23271`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed help text positioning of ``contrib.admin`` fields that use the "
"``ModelAdmin.filter_horizontal`` and ``filter_vertical`` options "
"(:ticket:`24676`)."
msgstr ""
"Suíomh téacs cabhrach seasta ar réimsí ``contrib.admin ``a úsáideann na "
"roghanna ``ModelAdmin.filter_horizontal`` agus `filter_vertical`` (:ticket: "
"`24676`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``AttributeError: function 'GDALAllRegister' not found`` error when "
"initializing ``contrib.gis`` on Windows."
msgstr ""
"Seasta ``AttributeError: ní aimsíodh feidhm 'GdalAllRegister' earráid ``agus "
"`contrib.gis`` á thosú ar Windows."

msgid "Optimizations"
msgstr "Optamú"

msgid ""
"Changed ``ModelState`` to deepcopy fields instead of deconstructing and "
"reconstructing (:ticket:`24591`). This speeds up the rendering of model "
"states and reduces memory usage when running :djadmin:`manage.py migrate "
"<migrate>` (although other changes in this release may negate any "
"performance benefits)."
msgstr ""
"Athraíodh ``ModelState`` go réimsí doimhchóipeála in ionad dífhoirmiú agus "
"athchóiriú (:ticket: `24591`). Luasghraíonn sé seo rindreáil stáit samhail "
"agus laghdaíonn sé úsáid cuimhne agus é ag rith: djadmin: `manage.py "
"migration <migrate>`(cé go bhféadfadh athruithe eile sa scaoileadh seo aon "
"sochair feidhmíochta a dhiúltú)."

msgid "Django 1.8.10 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.8.10"

msgid "*March 1, 2016*"
msgstr "*1 Márta, 2016*"

msgid "Django 1.8.10 fixes two security issues and several bugs in 1.8.9."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.8.10 dhá shaincheist slándála agus roinnt fabhtanna i "
"1.8.9."

msgid ""
"CVE-2016-2512: Malicious redirect and possible XSS attack via user-supplied "
"redirect URLs containing basic auth"
msgstr ""
"CVE-2016-2512: Atreorú mailíseach agus ionsaí XSS féideartha trí URLanna "
"atreoraithe a sholáthraíonn an úsáideoir ina bhfuil auth bunúsach"

msgid ""
"Django relies on user input in some cases (e.g. "
"``django.contrib.auth.views.login()`` and :doc:`i18n </topics/i18n/index>`) "
"to redirect the user to an \"on success\" URL. The security check for these "
"redirects (namely ``django.utils.http.is_safe_url()``) considered some URLs "
"with basic authentication credentials \"safe\" when they shouldn't be."
msgstr ""
"Braitheann Django ar ionchur úsáideora i roinnt cásanna (m.sh. "
"``django.contrib.auth.views.login () ``agus:doc: `i18n`) chun an t-úsáideoir "
"a atreorú chuig URL “ar rath”. </topics/i18n/index> Mheas an seiceáil "
"slándála do na haatreoruithe seo (eadhon ``django.utils.http.is_safe_url () "
"``) roinnt URLanna le dintiúir fíordheimhnithe bunúsacha “sábháilte” nuair "
"nár chóir iad a bheith."

msgid ""
"For example, a URL like ``http://mysite.example.com\\@attacker.com`` would "
"be considered safe if the request's host is ``http://mysite.example.com``, "
"but redirecting to this URL sends the user to ``attacker.com``."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, measfaí URL cosúil le ``http://"
"mysite.example.com\\@attacker.com`` sábháilte más óstach an iarratais "
"``http://mysite.example.com``, ach seolann athreorú chuig an URL seo an t-"
"úsáideoir chuig ``attacker.com``."

msgid ""
"CVE-2016-2513: User enumeration through timing difference on password hasher "
"work factor upgrade"
msgstr ""
"CVE-2016-2513: Áireamh úsáideora trí dhifríocht uainiúcháin ar uasghrádú "
"fachtóra oibre pasfhocal"

msgid ""
"In each major version of Django since 1.6, the default number of iterations "
"for the ``PBKDF2PasswordHasher`` and its subclasses has increased. This "
"improves the security of the password as the speed of hardware increases, "
"however, it also creates a timing difference between a login request for a "
"user with a password encoded in an older number of iterations and login "
"request for a nonexistent user (which runs the default hasher's default "
"number of iterations since Django 1.6)."
msgstr ""
"I ngach mór-leagan de Django ó 1.6, tá méadú tagtha ar líon réamhshocraithe "
"na n-athraitheoirí don `PBKDF2PasswordHasher`` agus a fho-aicmí. Feabhsaíonn "
"sé seo slándáil an phasfhocal de réir mar a mhéadaíonn luas na crua-earraí, "
"áfach, cruthaíonn sé difríocht uainithe freisin idir iarratas logála isteach "
"d'úsáideoir le pasfhocal ionchódaithe i líon níos sine athrá agus iarratas "
"logála isteach d'úsáideoir nach bhfuil ann (a ritheann líon réamhshocraithe "
"athraithe an hasher ó Django 1.6)."

msgid ""
"This only affects users who haven't logged in since the iterations were "
"increased. The first time a user logs in after an iterations increase, their "
"password is updated with the new iterations and there is no longer a timing "
"difference."
msgstr ""
"Ní théann sé seo ach ar úsáideoirí nach bhfuil logáil isteach orthu ó "
"mhéadaíodh na hathrith. An chéad uair a logálann úsáideoir isteach tar éis "
"méadú ar athrá, déantar a bhfocal faire a nuashonrú leis na hathrith nua "
"agus níl difríocht uainithe ann a thuilleadh."

msgid ""
"The new ``BasePasswordHasher.harden_runtime()`` method allows hashers to "
"bridge the runtime gap between the work factor (e.g. iterations) supplied in "
"existing encoded passwords and the default work factor of the hasher. This "
"method is implemented for ``PBKDF2PasswordHasher``  and "
"``BCryptPasswordHasher``. The number of rounds for the latter hasher hasn't "
"changed since Django 1.4, but some projects may subclass it and increase the "
"work factor as needed."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an modh nua ``BasePasswordHasher.harden_Runtime () ``do hashers an "
"bhearna runama a dhroicheadh idir an fachtóir oibre (m.sh. athraithe) a "
"sholáthraítear sna pasfhocail ionchódaithe atá ann cheana agus fachtóir "
"oibre réamhshocraithe an hasher. Cuirtear an modh seo i bhfeidhm le haghaidh "
"``PBKDF2PasswordHasher`` agus ``BCryptPasswordHasher``. Níor athraigh líon "
"na mbabhtaí don hasher deireanach ó Django 1.4, ach féadfaidh roinnt "
"tionscadail é a fho-aicmiú agus an fachtóir oibre a mhéadú de réir mar is gá."

msgid ""
"A warning will be emitted for any :ref:`third-party password hashers that "
"don't implement <write-your-own-password-hasher>` a ``harden_runtime()`` "
"method."
msgstr ""
"Asteofar rabhadh do haon:ref: `hashers pasfhocal tríú páirtí nach gcuireann "
"modh ``harden_runtime () <write-your-own-password-hasher>`i bhfeidhm`."

msgid ""
"If you have different password hashes in your database (such as SHA1 hashes "
"from users who haven't logged in since the default hasher switched to PBKDF2 "
"in Django 1.4), the timing difference on a login request for these users may "
"be even greater and this fix doesn't remedy that difference (or any "
"difference when changing hashers). You may be able to :ref:`upgrade those "
"hashes <wrapping-password-hashers>` to prevent a timing attack for that case."
msgstr ""
"Má tá hashes pasfhocal difriúla agat i do bhunachar sonraí (mar shampla "
"hashes SHA1 ó úsáideoirí nár logáil isteach ó athraigh an hasher "
"réamhshocraithe go PBKDF2 i Django 1.4), d'fhéadfadh an difríocht uainithe "
"ar iarratas logála isteach do na húsáideoirí seo a bheith níos mó fós agus "
"ní leigheasann an socrú seo an difríocht sin (nó aon difríocht agus hashers "
"á athrú). B'fhéidir go mbeidh tú in ann: ref: `uasgh <wrapping-password-"
"hashers>rádú a dhéanamh ar na hashes sin `chun ionsaí uainiúcháin a chosc "
"don chás sin."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash on PostgreSQL that prevented using ``TIME_ZONE=None`` and "
"``USE_TZ=False`` (:ticket:`26177`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste ar PostgreSQL a chuir cosc ar ``time_zone=none`` agus "
"``use_tz=false`` (:ticket: `26177`) a úsáid."

msgid ""
"Added system checks for query name clashes of hidden relationships "
"(:ticket:`26162`)."
msgstr ""
"Seiceálacha córais breise le haghaidh comhraic ainmneacha fiosrúcháin ar "
"chaidrimh i bhfolach (:ticket: `26162`)."

msgid ""
"Made ``forms.FileField`` and ``utils.translation.lazy_number()`` picklable "
"(:ticket:`26212`)."
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh ``Forms.FileField`` agus ``utils.translation.lazy_number () "
"``picklable (:ticket: `26212`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed :class:`~django.contrib.postgres.fields.RangeField` "
"and :class:`~django.contrib.postgres.fields.ArrayField` serialization with "
"``None`` values (:ticket:`26215`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraithe:Class: `~django.contrib.postgres.fields.rangefield` agus:class: "
"`~django.contrib.postgres.fields.arrayfield` sraith le luachanna ``None "
"``(:ticket: `26215`)."

msgid ""
"Reallowed dashes in top-level domain names of URLs checked by "
"``URLValidator`` to fix a regression in Django 1.8 (:ticket:`26204`)."
msgstr ""
"Drátaí athluchtaithe in ainmneacha fearainn barrleibhéil URLanna a "
"sheiceálann ``URLValidator`` chun aischéimniú a shocrú i Django 1.8 "
"(:ticket: `26204`)."

msgid "Fixed ``BoundField`` to reallow slices of subwidgets (:ticket:`26267`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh ``Boundfield`` chun slisní fo-ghuirléidí a athíoslódáil (:ticket: "
"`26267`)."

msgid ""
"Prevented ``ContentTypeManager`` instances from sharing their cache "
"(:ticket:`26286`)."
msgstr ""
"Chuir sé cosc ar chásanna ``ContentTypeManager`` ó a taisce a roinnt "
"(:ticket: `26286`)."

msgid "Django 1.8.11 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.8.11"

msgid "*March 5, 2016*"
msgstr "*5 Márta, 2016*"

msgid ""
"Django 1.8.11 fixes a regression on Python 2 in the 1.8.10 security release "
"where ``utils.http.is_safe_url()`` crashes on bytestring URLs "
"(:ticket:`26308`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.8.11 aischéimniú ar Python 2 sa scaoileadh slándála "
"1.8.10 ina dtiocfaidh ``utils.http.is_safe_url () ``ar URLanna bytestring "
"(:ticket: `26308`)."

msgid "Django 1.8.12 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.8.12"

msgid "*April 1, 2016*"
msgstr "*1 Aibreán, 2016*"

msgid "Django 1.8.12 fixes several bugs in 1.8.11."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.8.12 roinnt fabhtanna i 1.8.11."

msgid ""
"Made ``MultiPartParser`` ignore filenames that normalize to an empty string "
"to fix crash in ``MemoryFileUploadHandler`` on specially crafted user input "
"(:ticket:`26325`)."
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh ``MultipartParser`` neamhaird ar ainmneacha comhaid a normalaíonn "
"go sreang folamh chun timpiste a shocrú i `MemoryFileUploadHandler`` ar "
"ionchur úsáideora atá déanta go speisialta (:ticket: `26325`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed data loss on SQLite where ``DurationField`` values with fractional "
"seconds could be saved as ``None`` (:ticket:`26324`)."
msgstr ""
"Caillteanas sonraí seasta ar SQLite áit ar féidir luachanna ``DurationField` "
"le soicindí codánach a shábháil mar ``None ``(:ticket: `26324`)."

msgid ""
"Restored the functionality of the admin's ``raw_id_fields`` in "
"``list_editable`` (:ticket:`26387`)."
msgstr ""
"Athchóirigh feidhmiúlacht ``raw_id_fields`` an riaracháin i "
"``list_editable`` (:ticket: `26387`)."

msgid "Django 1.8.13 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.8.13"

msgid "*May 2, 2016*"
msgstr "*2 Bealtaine, 2016*"

msgid "Django 1.8.13 fixes several bugs in 1.8.12."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.8.13 roinnt fabhtanna i 1.8.12."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``TimeField`` microseconds round-tripping on MySQL and SQLite "
"(:ticket:`26498`)."
msgstr ""
"Micreasoicind seasta ``Timfield ``triping babhta ar MySQL agus SQLite "
"(:ticket: `26498`)."

msgid ""
"Restored conversion of an empty string to null when saving values of "
"``GenericIPAddressField`` on SQLite and MySQL (:ticket:`26557`)."
msgstr ""
"Tiontaigh teaghrán folamh athchóirithe go null nuair a shábháil luachanna "
"``GenericipAddressField`` ar SQLite agus MySQL (:ticket: `26557`)."

msgid "Django 1.8.14 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.8.14"

msgid "*July 18, 2016*"
msgstr "*18 Iúil, 2016*"

msgid "Django 1.8.14 fixes a security issue and a bug in 1.8.13."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.8.14 saincheist slándála agus fabht i 1.8.13."

msgid "XSS in admin's add/change related popup"
msgstr "XSS i anaisín a bhaineann le cuirte/athrú riaracháin"

msgid ""
"Unsafe usage of JavaScript's ``Element.innerHTML`` could result in XSS in "
"the admin's add/change related popup. ``Element.textContent`` is now used to "
"prevent execution of the data."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh XSS a bheith mar thoradh ar úsáid neamhshábháilte de "
"`Element.innerHTML`` JavaScript i bpop a bhaineann le cuirte/athrú an "
"riaracháin. Úsáidtear ``Element.textContent`` anois chun cosc a chur ar "
"fhorghníomhú na sonraí."

msgid ""
"The debug view also used ``innerHTML``. Although a security issue wasn't "
"identified there, out of an abundance of caution it's also updated to use "
"``textContent``."
msgstr ""
"D'úsáid an radharc dífhabhtaithe ``innerHTML`` freisin. Cé nár sainaithníodh "
"saincheist slándála ansin, as go leor rabhadh déantar é a nuashonrú freisin "
"chun “TextContent” a úsáid."

msgid ""
"Fixed missing ``varchar/text_pattern_ops`` index on ``CharField`` and "
"``TextField`` respectively when using ``AddField`` on PostgreSQL "
"(:ticket:`26889`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh innéacs ``varchar/text_pattern_ops`` atá ar iarraidh ar "
"``Charfield`` agus ``Textfield`` faoi seach nuair a úsáidtear ``Addfield`` "
"ar PostgreSQL (:ticket: `26889`)."

msgid "Django 1.8.15 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.8.15"

msgid "*September 26, 2016*"
msgstr "*26 Meán Fómhair, 2016*"

msgid "Django 1.8.15 fixes a security issue in 1.8.14."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.8.15 saincheist slándála i 1.8.14."

msgid "CSRF protection bypass on a site with Google Analytics"
msgstr "Seachbhóthar cosanta CSRF ar shuíomh le Google Analytics"

msgid ""
"An interaction between Google Analytics and Django's cookie parsing could "
"allow an attacker to set arbitrary cookies leading to a bypass of CSRF "
"protection."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh idirghníomhaíocht idir Google Analytics agus parsáil fianán "
"Django ligean d'ionsaitheoir fianáin treallach a shocrú mar thoradh ar "
"sheachbhóthar cosanta CSRF."

msgid ""
"The parser for ``request.COOKIES`` is simplified to better match the "
"behavior of browsers and to mitigate this attack. ``request.COOKIES`` may "
"now contain cookies that are invalid according to :rfc:`6265` but are "
"possible to set via ``document.cookie``."
msgstr ""
"Déantar an parser do ``Request.cookies`` a shimpliú chun iompar brabhsálaí a "
"mheaitseáil níos fearr agus chun an t-ionsaí seo a mhaolú. D'fhéadfadh go "
"mbeadh fianáin anois ag `request.cookies`` atá neamhbhailí de réir: rfc: "
"`6265` ach is féidir iad a shocrú trí `document.cookie``."

msgid "Django 1.8.16 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.8.16"

msgid "Django 1.8.16 fixes two security issues in 1.8.15."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.8.16 dhá shaincheist slándála i 1.8.15."

msgid "Django 1.8.17 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.8.17"

msgid "Django 1.8.17 fixes a regression in 1.8.16."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.8.17 aischéimniú i 1.8.16."

msgid "Django 1.8.18 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.8.18"

msgid "Django 1.8.18 fixes two security issues in 1.8.17."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.8.18 dhá shaincheist slándála i 1.8.17."

msgid "Django 1.8.19 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.8.19"

msgid "Django 1.8.19 fixes two security issues in 1.18.18."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.8.19 dhá shaincheist slándála i 1.18.18."

msgid ""
"The ``django.utils.html.urlize()`` function was extremely slow to evaluate "
"certain inputs due to a catastrophic backtracking vulnerability in a regular "
"expression. The ``urlize()`` function is used to implement the ``urlize`` "
"and ``urlizetrunc`` template filters, which were thus vulnerable."
msgstr ""
"Bhí an fheidhm ``django.utils.html.urlize () `thar a bheith mall chun "
"ionchuir áirithe a mheas mar gheall ar leochaileacht siar-rianaithe "
"tubaisteach i léiriú rialta. Úsáidtear an fheidhm ``urlize () ``chun na "
"scagairí teimpléad ``urlize`` agus ``urlizetrunc`` a chur i bhfeidhm, a bhí "
"leochaileach dá bhrí sin."

msgid ""
"The problematic regular expression is replaced with parsing logic that "
"behaves similarly."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear loighic pharsála a iompraíonn mar an gcéanna in ionad an slonn "
"rialta fhadhbach."

msgid "Django 1.8.2 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.8.2"

msgid "*May 20, 2015*"
msgstr "*20 Bealtaine, 2015*"

msgid "Django 1.8.2 fixes a security issue and several bugs in 1.8.1."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.8.2 saincheist slándála agus roinnt fabhtanna i 1.8.1."

msgid "Fixed session flushing in the ``cached_db`` backend"
msgstr "Sruthlaigh seisiún seasta sa chúlcheann ``cached_db``"

msgid ""
"A change to ``session.flush()`` in the ``cached_db`` session backend in "
"Django 1.8 mistakenly sets the session key to an empty string rather than "
"``None``. An empty string is treated as a valid session key and the session "
"cookie is set accordingly. Any users with an empty string in their session "
"cookie will use the same session store. ``session.flush()`` is called by "
"``django.contrib.auth.logout()`` and, more seriously, by "
"``django.contrib.auth.login()`` when a user switches accounts. If a user is "
"logged in and logs in again to a different account (without logging out) the "
"session is flushed to avoid reuse. After the session is flushed (and its "
"session key becomes ``''``) the account details are set on the session and "
"the session is saved. Any users with an empty string in their session cookie "
"will now be logged into that account."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn athrú ar ``session.flush () ``sa chúlcheann seisiúin ``cached_db`` "
"i Django 1.8 eochair an seisiúin go teaghrán folamh seachas ``None``. "
"Déileáltar le sreang folamh mar eochair bhailí seisiúin agus socraítear an "
"fianán seisiúin dá réir. Úsáideoidh aon úsáideoirí a bhfuil sreang folamh "
"acu ina bhfianán seisiúin an siopa seisiúin céanna. Tugtar ``session.flush "
"() ``le `django.contrib.auth.logout ()`` agus, níos dáiríre, ag "
"``django.contrib.auth.login () ``nuair a athraíonn úsáideoir cuntais. Má tá "
"úsáideoir logáilte isteach agus má logálann isteach arís chuig cuntas "
"difriúil (gan logáil amach) déantar an seisiún a shruthlú chun athúsáid a "
"sheachaint. Tar éis an seisiún a shruthlú (agus éiríonn a eochair seisiúin "
"```) socraítear sonraí an chuntais ar an seisiún agus sábhálfar an seisiún. "
"Déanfar aon úsáideoirí a bhfuil teaghrán folamh ina bhfianán seisiúin "
"logáilte isteach sa chuntas sin anois."

msgid "Fixed check for template engine alias uniqueness (:ticket:`24685`)."
msgstr ""
"Seiceáil sheasta le haghaidh uathúlacht alias inneall teimpléad (:ticket: "
"`24685`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed crash when reusing the same ``Case`` instance in a query "
"(:ticket:`24752`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste seasta nuair a athúsáidtear an cás céanna ``Cás ``i bhfiosrúchán "
"(:ticket: `24752`)."

msgid ""
"Corrected join promotion for ``Case`` expressions. For example, annotating a "
"query with a  ``Case`` expression could unexpectedly filter out results "
"(:ticket:`24766`)."
msgstr ""
"Cur chun cinn ceartaithe le haghaidh abairtí ``Cás'. Mar shampla, "
"d'fhéadfadh torthaí a scagadh amach gan choinne (:ticket: `24766`) a chur in "
"anótáil ar cheist le léiriú ``Cás ``."

msgid ""
"Fixed negated ``Q`` objects in expressions. Cases like "
"``Case(When(~Q(friends__age__lte=30)))`` tried to generate a subquery which "
"resulted in a crash (:ticket:`24705`)."
msgstr ""
"Rud seasta diúltaithe ``Q`` i nathanna. Rinne cásanna mar ``Cás (Nuair (~Q "
"(cairde__age__lte=30))) `iarracht fo-cheist a ghiniúint a raibh timpiste mar "
"thoradh air (:ticket: `24705`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed incorrect GROUP BY clause generation on MySQL when the query's model "
"has a self-referential foreign key (:ticket:`24748`)."
msgstr ""
"Giniúint clásal GRÚPA MÍCHEART SOCRAITHE AR MySQL nuair a bhíonn eochair "
"eachtrach féin-tagartha ag tsamhail an cheistiúcháin (:ticket: `24748`)."

msgid ""
"Implemented ``ForeignKey.get_db_prep_value()`` so that ``ForeignKey``\\s "
"pointing to :class:`~django.db.models.UUIDField` and inheritance on models "
"with ``UUIDField`` primary keys work correctly "
"(:ticket:`24698`, :ticket:`24712`)."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh i bhfeidhm ``ForeignKey.get_DB_Prep_Value () ``ionas go n-oibríonn "
"``ForeignKey``\\ s ag díriú chuar:class: `~django.db.models.uuidfield` agus "
"oidhreacht ar mhúnlaí le heochracha bunscoile ``UUIDField`` i gceart "
"(:ticket: `24698`, :ticket: `24712`)."

msgid "Fixed ``isnull`` lookup for ``HStoreField`` (:ticket:`24751`)."
msgstr ""
"Cuardach seasta ``isnull`` le haghaidh ``hStorefield`` (:ticket: `24751`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a MySQL crash when a migration removes a combined index "
"( ``unique_together`` or ``index_together``) containing a foreign key "
"(:ticket:`24757`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste MySQL nuair a bhíonn imirce innéacs comhcheangailte "
"(``unique_together`` nó ``index_together ``) ina bhfuil eochair eachtrach "
"(:ticket: `24757`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed session cookie deletion when using :setting:`SESSION_COOKIE_DOMAIN` "
"(:ticket:`24799`)."
msgstr ""
"Scriosadh fianán seisiúin sheasta nuair a úsáidtear: socrú: "
"`SESSION_COOKIE_DOMAIN` (:ticket: `24799`)."

msgid ""
"On PostgreSQL, when no access is granted for the ``postgres`` database, "
"Django now falls back to the default database when it normally requires a "
"\"no database\" connection (:ticket:`24791`)."
msgstr ""
"Ar PostgreSQL, nuair nach ndeonaítear aon rochtain don bhunachar sonraí "
"`postgres`, tagann Django ar ais anois chuig an mbunachar sonraí "
"réamhshocraithe nuair a theastaíonn nasc “gan bunachar sonraí” uaidh de "
"ghnáth (:ticket: `24791`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed display of ``contrib.admin``’s ``ForeignKey`` widget when it's used in "
"a row with other fields (:ticket:`24784`)."
msgstr ""
"Taispeántas seasta de ghuirléid ``ForeignKey`` `contrib.admin`` nuair a "
"úsáidtear é i ndiaidh a chéile le réimsí eile (:ticket: `24784`)."

msgid "Django 1.8.3 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.8.3"

msgid "Django 1.8.3 fixes several security issues and bugs in 1.8.2."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.8.3 roinnt saincheisteanna slándála agus fabhtanna i "
"1.8.2."

msgid ""
"Also, ``django.utils.deprecation.RemovedInDjango20Warning`` was renamed to "
"``RemovedInDjango110Warning`` as the version roadmap was revised to 1.9, "
"1.10, 1.11 (LTS), 2.0 (drops Python 2 support). For backwards compatibility, "
"``RemovedInDjango20Warning`` remains as an importable alias."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith leis sin, athainmníodh "
"`Django.utils.deprecation.removedindJango20Warning`` go "
"``RemovedIndJango110Warning`` de réir mar a athbhreithníodh treochlár an "
"leagan go 1.9, 1.10, 1.11 (LTS), 2.0 (titeann tacaíocht Python 2). Maidir le "
"comhoiriúnacht ar ais, tá ``Removedindjango20Warning`` fós mar ainm "
"iniompórtáilte."

msgid "Denial-of-service possibility in URL validation"
msgstr "Féidearthacht seirbhíse a dhiúltú i mbailíochtú URL"

msgid ""
":class:`~django.core.validators.URLValidator` included a regular expression "
"that was extremely slow to evaluate against certain invalid inputs. This "
"regular expression has been simplified and optimized."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.core.validators.URLValidator` bhí abairt rialta ann a bhí "
"thar a bheith mall le meastóireacht i gcoinne ionchuir neamhbhailí áirithe. "
"Tá an abairt rialta seo simplithe agus optamaithe."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``BaseRangeField.prepare_value()`` to use each ``base_field``’s "
"``prepare_value()`` method (:ticket:`24841`)."
msgstr ""
"Seasta ``BaseRangeField.prepare_value () ``chun modh `prepare_value () `gach "
"``base_field`` a úsáid (:ticket: `24841`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed crash during :djadmin:`makemigrations` if a migrations module either "
"is missing ``__init__.py`` or is a file (:ticket:`24848`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste seasta le linn: djadmin: `makemigrations` má tá modúl imirce in "
"easnamh ``__init__.py`` nó gur comhad é (:ticket: `24848`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``QuerySet.exists()`` returning incorrect results after annotation "
"with ``Count()`` (:ticket:`24835`)."
msgstr ""
"Seasta ``QuerySet.exists () ``ag filleadh torthaí míchearta tar éis anótála "
"le ``Count ()`` (:ticket: `24835`)."

msgid "Corrected ``HStoreField.has_changed()`` (:ticket:`24844`)."
msgstr "Ceartaithe ``hStorefield.has_Changed () ``(:ticket: `24844`)."

msgid ""
"Reverted an optimization to the CSRF template context processor which caused "
"a regression (:ticket:`24836`)."
msgstr ""
"Chuir sé barrfheabhsú ar ais chuig próiseálaí comhthéacs teimpléad CSRF a "
"bhí ina chúis le aischéimniú (:ticket: `24836`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression which caused template context processors to overwrite "
"variables set on a ``RequestContext`` after it's created (:ticket:`24847`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú a d'fhág próiseálaithe comhthéacs teimpléid athróga atá "
"leagtha síos ar ``RequestContext`` a fhorscríobh tar éis é a chruthú "
"(:ticket: `24847`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when using a reverse one-to-one relation in "
"``ModelAdmin.list_display`` (:ticket:`24851`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste nuair a úsáidtear caidreamh droim duine le duine i "
"``ModelAdmin.list_display`` (:ticket: `24851`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed quoting of SQL when renaming a field to ``AutoField`` in PostgreSQL "
"(:ticket:`24892`)."
msgstr ""
"Luachan seasta SQL nuair a athainmnítear réimse go ``Autofield`` i "
"PostgreSQL (:ticket: `24892`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed lack of unique constraint when changing a field from "
"``primary_key=True`` to ``unique=True`` (:ticket:`24893`)."
msgstr ""
"Easpa srianta uathúil seasta agus réimse á athrú ó ``primary_key=true`` go "
"``unique=true`` (:ticket: `24893`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed queryset pickling when using ``prefetch_related()`` after deleting "
"objects (:ticket:`24831`)."
msgstr ""
"Picáil tacar ceisteanna seasta nuair a úsáidtear ``prefetch_related () ``tar "
"éis rudaí a scriosadh (:ticket: `24831`)."

msgid ""
"Allowed using ``choices`` longer than 1 day with ``DurationField`` "
"(:ticket:`24897`)."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaítear ag baint úsáide as ``roghnaí`` níos faide ná 1 lá le "
"``Durationfield`` (:ticket: `24897`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when loading squashed migrations from two apps with a "
"dependency between them, where the dependent app's replaced migrations are "
"partially applied (:ticket:`24895`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraíodh timpiste nuair a luchtaítear imirce scrúdaithe ó dhá aip le "
"spleáchas eatarthu, áit a gcuirtear imirce athsholáthair an aip "
"cleithiúnaithe i bhfeidhm go páirteach (:ticket: `24895`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed recording of applied status for squashed (replacement) migrations "
"(:ticket:`24628`)."
msgstr ""
"Taifeadadh seasta ar stádas iarrtha le haghaidh imirce scáite "
"(athsholáthair) (:ticket: `24628`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed queryset annotations when using ``Case`` expressions with "
"``exclude()`` (:ticket:`24833`)."
msgstr ""
"Anótaí socraithe ceisteanna nuair a úsáidtear abairtí ``Cás ``le ``eisiamh "
"()`` (:ticket: `24833`)."

msgid ""
"Corrected join promotion for multiple ``Case`` expressions. Annotating a "
"query with multiple  ``Case`` expressions could unexpectedly filter out "
"results (:ticket:`24924`)."
msgstr ""
"Cur chun cinn ceartaithe maidir le nathanna iolracha ``Cáis`. D'fhéadfadh sé "
"torthaí a scagadh amach gan choinne (:ticket: `24924`) a chur ar fiosrú le "
"nathanna iolracha ``Cás ``."

msgid "Fixed usage of transforms in subqueries (:ticket:`24744`)."
msgstr "Úsáid sheasta na n-athruithe i bhfo-cheisteanna (:ticket: `24744`)."

msgid ""
"Provided better backwards compatibility for the ``verbosity`` argument in "
"``optparse`` management commands by casting it to an integer "
"(:ticket:`24769`)."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíodh comhoiriúnacht níos fearr ar ais don argóint ``verbosity`` in "
"orduithe bainistíochta ``optparse` tríd í a chaitheamh go sláimhir (:ticket: "
"`24769`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``prefetch_related()`` on databases other than PostgreSQL for models "
"using UUID primary keys (:ticket:`24912`)."
msgstr ""
"Seasta ``prefetch_related () ``ar bhunachair sonraí seachas PostgreSQL do "
"mhúnlaí a úsáideann eochracha bunscoile UUID (:ticket: `24912`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed removing ``unique_together`` constraints on MySQL (:ticket:`24972`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraithe ag baint srianta ``unique_together`` ar MySQL (:ticket: `24972`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed crash when uploading images with MIME types that Pillow doesn't "
"detect, such as bitmap, in ``forms.ImageField`` (:ticket:`24948`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste seasta agus íomhánna á uaslódáil le cineálacha MIME nach "
"bhraitheann Pillow, mar shampla bitmap, i ``Forms.imagefield`` (:ticket: "
"`24948`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression when deleting a model through the admin that has a "
"``GenericRelation`` with a ``related_query_name`` (:ticket:`24940`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú agus múnla á scriosadh tríd an riarachán a bhfuil "
"``GenericRelation` aige le ``related_query_name`` (:ticket: `24940`)."

msgid ""
"Reallowed non-ASCII values for ``ForeignKey.related_name`` on Python 3 by "
"fixing the false positive system check (:ticket:`25016`)."
msgstr ""
"Luachanna neamh-ASCII a athshlánú do ``ForeignKey.RELATED_NAME`` ar Python 3 "
"trí sheiceáil an chórais dearfach bréagach a shocrú (:ticket: `25016`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed inline forms that use a parent object that has a ``UUIDField`` primary "
"key and a child object that has an ``AutoField`` primary key "
"(:ticket:`24958`)."
msgstr ""
"Foirmeacha inlíne seasta a úsáideann réad tuismitheora a bhfuil eochair "
"phríomhúil ``UUIDField`` aige agus réad leanaí a bhfuil eochair phríomhúil "
"``Autofield` aige (:ticket: `24958`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression in the ``unordered_list`` template filter on certain "
"inputs (:ticket:`25031`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú sa scagaire teimpléad ``unordered_list`` ar ionchuir "
"áirithe (:ticket: `25031`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression in ``URLValidator`` that invalidated Punycode TLDs "
"(:ticket:`25059`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú in `URLValidator`` a chuir TLDanna Punycode neamhbhailí "
"(:ticket: `25059`)."

msgid "Improved ``pyinotify`` ``runserver`` polling (:ticket:`23882`)."
msgstr "Vótaíocht feabhsaithe ``pyinotify`` ``runserver`` (:ticket: `23882`)."

msgid "Django 1.8.4 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.8.4"

msgid "Django 1.8.4 fixes a security issue and several bugs in 1.8.3."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.8.4 saincheist slándála agus roinnt fabhtanna i 1.8.3."

msgid ""
"Added the ability to serialize values from the newly "
"added :class:`~django.db.models.UUIDField` (:ticket:`25019`)."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an cumas luachanna a shraitheadh ón nua-chuirte:class: "
"`~django.db.models.uuidfield` (:ticket: `25019`)."

msgid ""
"Added a system check warning if the old ``TEMPLATE_*`` settings are defined "
"in addition to the new ``TEMPLATES`` setting."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh rabhadh seiceála córais leis má shainmhínítear na sean-socruithe "
"``TEMPLATE_*`` i dteannta leis an socrú ``TEMPLATES`` nua."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``QuerySet.raw()`` so ``InvalidQuery`` is not raised when using the "
"``db_column`` name of a ``ForeignKey`` field with ``primary_key=True`` "
"(:ticket:`12768`)."
msgstr ""
"Seasta ``QuerySet.raw () ``mar sin ní ardaítear ``InvalidQuery`` nuair a "
"úsáidtear ainm ``db_column`` de réimse ``ForeignKey`` le "
"``primary_key=true`` (:ticket: `12768`)."

msgid ""
"Prevented an exception in ``TestCase.setUpTestData()`` from leaking the "
"transaction (:ticket:`25176`)."
msgstr ""
"Chuir sé cosc ar eisceacht i ``TestCase.setupTestData () ``ón idirbheart a "
"sceitheadh (:ticket: `25176`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``has_changed()`` method in ``contrib.postgres.forms.HStoreField`` "
"(:ticket:`25215`, :ticket:`25233`)."
msgstr ""
"Modh seasta ``has_changed () ``i `Contrib.Postgres.Forms.hStoreField`` "
"(:ticket: `25215`, :ticket: `25233`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed the recording of squashed migrations when running the ``migrate`` "
"command (:ticket:`25231`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh taifeadadh imirce scáite agus an t-ordú ``imirce`` á reáchtáil "
"(:ticket: `25231`)."

msgid ""
"Moved the :ref:`unsaved model instance assignment data loss check <unsaved-"
"model-instance-check-18>` to ``Model.save()`` to allow easier usage of in-"
"memory models (:ticket:`25160`)."
msgstr ""
"Ag bogadh seiceáil caillteanais sonraí sannadh samhail samhail "
"neamhshábháilte chuig ``<unsaved-model-instance-check-18>Model.save ()`` "
"chun samhlacha in-chuimhne a úsáid níos éasca (:ticket: `25160`)."

msgid ""
"Prevented ``varchar_patterns_ops`` and ``text_patterns_ops`` indexes for "
"``ArrayField`` (:ticket:`25180`)."
msgstr ""
"Cosc ar innéacsanna ``varchar_patterns_ops`` agus ``text_patterns_ops`` do "
"`Arrayfield`` (:ticket: `25180`)."

msgid "Django 1.8.5 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.8.5"

msgid "*October 3, 2015*"
msgstr "*Deireadh Fómhair 3, 2015*"

msgid "Django 1.8.5 fixes several bugs in 1.8.4."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.8.5 roinnt fabhtanna i 1.8.4."

msgid "Made the development server's autoreload more robust (:ticket:`24704`)."
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh uath-athluchtú an fhreastalaí forbartha níos láidre (:ticket: "
"`24704`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``AssertionError`` in some delete queries with a model containing a "
"field that is both a foreign and primary key (:ticket:`24951`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh ``AssertionError`` i roinnt ceisteanna scriosta le samhail ina "
"bhfuil réimse atá ina eochair eachtrach agus príomh-eochair araon (:ticket: "
"`24951`)."

msgid "Fixed ``AssertionError`` in some complex queries (:ticket:`24525`)."
msgstr ""
"Seasta ``AssertionError`` i roinnt ceisteanna casta (:ticket: `24525`)."

msgid "Fixed a migrations crash with ``GenericForeignKey`` (:ticket:`25040`)."
msgstr "Socraigh timpiste imirce le ``GenericForeignKey`` (:ticket: `25040`)."

msgid ""
"Made ``translation.override()`` clear the overridden language when a "
"translation isn't initially active (:ticket:`25295`)."
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh ``translation.override () ``an teanga a ghlanadh nuair nach bhfuil "
"aistriúchán gníomhach ar dtús (:ticket: `25295`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed crash when using a value in ``ModelAdmin.list_display`` that clashed "
"with a reverse field on the model (:ticket:`25299`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste seasta nuair a bhíonn luach á úsáid in `ModelAdmin.list_display`` a "
"bhuail le réimse droim ar an tsamhail (:ticket: `25299`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed autocompletion for options of non-``argparse`` management commands "
"(:ticket:`25372`)."
msgstr ""
"Uathchomhlánú seasta le haghaidh roghanna orduithe bainistíochta neamh-"
"`argparse` (:ticket: `25372`)."

msgid ""
"Alphabetized ordering of imports in ``from django.db import migrations, "
"models`` statement in newly created migrations (:ticket:`25384`)."
msgstr ""
"Ordú aibítreach allmhairí in ``ó django.db imirceacha allmhairiúcháin, "
"samhlacha ``ráiteas in imirce nua-chruthaithe (:ticket: `25384`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed migrations crash on MySQL when adding a text or a blob field with an "
"unhashable default (:ticket:`25393`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpeann imirce seasta ar MySQL nuair a chuireann téacs nó réimse blob leis "
"le réamhshocrú neamh-inúsáidte (:ticket: `25393`)."

msgid ""
"Changed ``Count`` queries to execute ``COUNT(*)`` instead of ``COUNT('*')`` "
"as versions of Django before 1.8 did (:ticket:`25377`). This may fix a "
"performance regression on some databases."
msgstr ""
"D'athraigh ceisteanna ``Count`` chun ``COUNT(*)`` a rith in ionad "
"``COUNT('*')`` mar a rinne leaganacha de Django roimh 1.8 (:ticéad:`25377`). "
"D'fhéadfadh sé seo aischéimniú feidhmíochta a shocrú ar roinnt bunachair "
"shonraí."

msgid ""
"Fixed custom queryset chaining with ``values()`` and ``values_list()`` "
"(:ticket:`20625`)."
msgstr ""
"Sraith ceisteanna saincheaptha seasta ag slabhraíocht le ``luachanna () "
"``agus ``values_list ()`` (:ticket: `20625`)."

msgid ""
"Moved the :ref:`unsaved model instance assignment data loss check <unsaved-"
"model-instance-check-18>` on reverse relations to ``Model.save()`` "
"(:ticket:`25160`)."
msgstr ""
"Ag aistriú an:ref: `seiceáil caillteanas sonraí sannadh samhail "
"neamhshábháilte <unsaved-model-instance-check-18>`ar chaidreamh droim chuig "
"``Model.save () ``(:ticket: `25160`)."

msgid ""
"Readded inline foreign keys to form instances when validating model formsets "
"(:ticket:`25431`)."
msgstr ""
"Eochracha eachtracha inlíne léite chun cásanna a fhoirmiú agus foirmeacha "
"samhail á bhailíochtú (:ticket: `25431`)."

msgid ""
"Allowed using ORM write methods after disabling autocommit "
"with :func:`set_autocommit(False) <django.db.transaction.set_autocommit>` "
"(:ticket:`24921`)."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.transaction.set_autocommit>Ceadaítear modhanna scríbhneoireachta "
"ORM a úsáid tar éis autocommit a dhíchumasú le:func: `set_autocommit (False) "
"`(:ticket: `24921`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed the ``manage.py test --keepdb`` option on Oracle (:ticket:`25421`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh an rogha ``manage.py test --keepdb`` ar Oracle (:ticket: `25421`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed incorrect queries with multiple many-to-many fields on a model with "
"the same 'to' model and with ``related_name`` set to '+' "
"(:ticket:`24505`, :ticket:`25486`)."
msgstr ""
"Ceisteanna míchearta socraithe le réimsí iolracha go leor ar mhúnla leis an "
"tsamhail 'to' céanna agus le `related_name`` socraithe go '+' (:ticket: "
"`24505`, :ticket: `25486`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed pickling a ``SimpleLazyObject`` wrapping a model (:ticket:`25389`)."
msgstr ""
"Seasta piceáil ar ``simplelazyobject`` a fhilleadh samhail (:ticket: "
"`25389`)."

msgid "Django 1.8.6 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.8.6"

msgid "*November 4, 2015*"
msgstr "*4 Samhain, 2015*"

msgid ""
"Django 1.8.6 adds official support for Python 3.5 and fixes several bugs in "
"1.8.5."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann Django 1.8.6 tacaíocht oifigiúil le haghaidh Python 3.5 agus "
"socraíonn sé roinnt fabhtanna i 1.8.5."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression causing ``ModelChoiceField`` to ignore "
"``prefetch_related()`` on its queryset (:ticket:`25496`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú ina chúis le ``ModelChoicefield`` neamhaird a dhéanamh "
"ar ``prefetch_related () ``ar a tacar ceisteanna (:ticket: `25496`)."

msgid ""
"Allowed \"mode=memory\" in SQLite test database name if supported "
"(:ticket:`12118`)."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaítear “mód = cuimhne” in ainm bunachar sonraí tástála SQLite má "
"thacaítear é (: ticket: `12118`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed system check crash on ``ForeignKey`` to abstract model "
"(:ticket:`25503`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste seiceála an chórais sheasta ar `ForeignKey`` go samhail teibí "
"(:ticket: `25503`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed incorrect queries when you have multiple ``ManyToManyField``\\s on "
"different models that have the same field name, point to the same model, and "
"have their reverse relations disabled (:ticket:`25545`)."
msgstr ""
"Ceisteanna míchearta socraithe nuair a bhíonn iolracha ``ManyTomanyField`` "
"agat ar mhúnlaí éagsúla a bhfuil an t-ainm réimse céanna acu, díriú ar an "
"tsamhail chéanna, agus a gcaidreamh droim dhíchumasaithe (:ticket: `25545`)."

msgid "Allowed filtering over a ``RawSQL`` annotation (:ticket:`25506`)."
msgstr "Scagadh ceadaithe thar anótáil ``Rawsql`` (:ticket: `25506`)."

msgid ""
"Made the ``Concat`` database function idempotent on SQLite (:ticket:`25517`)."
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh an fheidhm bunachar sonraí `Concat`` idempotent ar SQLite (:ticket: "
"`25517`)."

msgid ""
"Avoided a confusing stack trace when starting :djadmin:`runserver` with an "
"invalid :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` setting (:ticket:`25510`). This regression "
"appeared in 1.8.5 as a side effect of fixing :ticket:`24704`."
msgstr ""
"Seachnaíodh rian cruach mearbhall agus tú ag tosú: djadmin: `runserver` le "
"socrú neamhbhailí:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS` (:ticket: `25510`). Bhí an "
"aischéimniú seo le feiceáil i 1.8.5 mar fho-éifeacht a bhaineann le socrú: "
"ticéad: `24704`."

msgid ""
"Made deferred models use their proxied model's ``_meta.apps`` for caching "
"and retrieval (:ticket:`25563`). This prevents any models generated in data "
"migrations using ``QuerySet.defer()`` from leaking to test and application "
"code."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann samhlacha iarchurtha déanta ``_meta.apps`` a msamhail seachadaithe "
"le haghaidh taiscála agus aisghabhála (:ticket: `25563`). Cuireann sé seo "
"cosc ar aon mhúnlaí a ghintear in imirce sonraí ag baint úsáide as "
"``QuerySet.defer () ``ó sceitheadh chuig cód tástála agus feidhmchláir."

msgid ""
"Fixed a typo in the name of the ``strictly_above`` PostGIS lookup "
"(:ticket:`25592`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh clóscríobh in ainm an chuardach PostGIS ``strictly_above "
"``(:ticket: `25592`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed crash with ``contrib.postgres.forms.SplitArrayField`` and "
"``IntegerField`` on invalid value (:ticket:`25597`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste seasta le `Contrib.Postgres.Forms.SplitarRayField`` agus "
"``IntegerField`` ar luach neamhbhailí (:ticket: `25597`)."

msgid ""
"Added a helpful error message when Django and South migrations exist in the "
"same directory (:ticket:`25618`)."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh teachtaireacht earráide cabhrach leis nuair a bhíonn imirce Django "
"agus Theas san eolaire céanna (:ticket: `25618`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression in ``URLValidator`` that allowed URLs with consecutive "
"dots in the domain section (like ``http://example..com/``) to pass "
"(:ticket:`25620`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú in ``URLValidator`` a ligean do URLanna le poncanna as "
"a chéile sa chuid fearainn (cosúil le ``http://example..com/``) pas "
"(:ticket: `25620`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash with ``GenericRelation`` and "
"``BaseModelAdmin.to_field_allowed`` (:ticket:`25622`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste le ``GenericRelation`` agus "
"``BaseModelAdmin.to_Field_Allowed`` (:ticket: `25622`)."

msgid "Django 1.8.7 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.8.7"

msgid "Django 1.8.7 fixes a security issue and several bugs in 1.8.6."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.8.7 saincheist slándála agus roinnt fabhtanna i 1.8.6."

msgid ""
"Additionally, Django's vendored version of six, ``django.utils.six``, has "
"been upgraded to the latest release (1.10.0)."
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, tá leagan díolta Django de sé, ``django.utils.six ``, "
"uasghrádaithe go dtí an eisiúint is déanaí (1.10.0)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash of the debug view during the autumn DST change "
"when :setting:`USE_TZ` is ``False`` and ``pytz`` is installed."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste ar an radharc dífhabhtaithe le linn athrú DST an fhómhair "
"nuair a bhíonn: socrú: ``False`` `USE_TZ` agus ``pytz`` suiteáiltear."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression in 1.8.6 that caused database routers without an "
"``allow_migrate()`` method to crash (:ticket:`25686`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú i 1.8.6 a d'fhág go dtiocfadh ródairí bunachar sonraí "
"gan modh `allow_migration () ``timpeall (: ticket: `25686`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression in 1.8.6 by restoring the ability to use ``Manager`` "
"objects for the ``queryset`` argument of ``ModelChoiceField`` "
"(:ticket:`25683`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú i 1.8.6 tríd an gcumas rudaí ``Bainiste`` a úsáid le "
"haghaidh argóint ``Queryset ``de `ModelChoiceField`` (:ticket: `25683`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression in 1.8.6 that caused an application with South migrations "
"in the ``migrations`` directory to fail (:ticket:`25618`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú in 1.8.6 a d'fhág gur theip ar iarratas le himirce "
"Theas san eolaire ``imirce`` (:ticket: `25618`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression in 1.8 by making ``gettext()`` once again return UTF-8 "
"bytestrings on Python 2 if the input is a bytestring (:ticket:`25720`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú i 1.8 trí ``gettext () ``a chur ar ais arís bytestrings "
"UTF-8 ar Python 2 más bytestring é an t-ionchur (:ticket: `25720`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed serialization "
"of :class:`~django.contrib.postgres.fields.DateRangeField` "
"and :class:`~django.contrib.postgres.fields.DateTimeRangeField` "
"(:ticket:`24937`)."
msgstr ""
"Sraitheadh seasta de:class: `~django.contrib.postgres.fields.daterangefield` "
"agus:class: `~django.contrib.postgres.fields.dateTimeRangeField` (:ticket: "
"`24937`)."

msgid "Fixed the exact lookup of ``ArrayField`` (:ticket:`25666`)."
msgstr "Socraigh an cuardach cruinn ar ``Arrayfield`` (:ticket: `25666`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``Model.refresh_from_db()`` updating of ``ForeignKey`` fields with "
"``on_delete=models.SET_NULL`` (:ticket:`25715`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraithe ``Model.Refresh_From_DB () ``a nuashonrú ar réimsí ``ForeignKey`` "
"le ``on_delete=Models.set_Null`` (:ticket: `25715`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a duplicate query regression in 1.8 on proxied model deletion "
"(:ticket:`25685`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú ceisteanna dúbailte i 1.8 ar scriosadh samhail "
"seachadaithe (:ticket: `25685`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``set_FOO_order()`` crash when the ``ForeignKey`` of a model with "
"``order_with_respect_to`` references a model with a ``OneToOneField`` "
"primary key (:ticket:`25786`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste seasta ``set_foo_order () ``nuair a thagraíonn ``ForeignKey`` "
"samhail le ``order_with_respect_to` do mhúnla le príomheochair "
"``OneTooneField`` (:ticket: `25786`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed incorrect validation for ``PositiveIntegerField`` and "
"``PositiveSmallIntegerField`` on MySQL resulting in values greater than "
"4294967295 or 65535, respectively, passing validation and being silently "
"truncated by the database (:ticket:`25767`)."
msgstr ""
"Bailíochtú mícheart socraithe do `PositiveIntegerField`` agus "
"``PositivesMallIntegerField`` ar MySQL mar thoradh air sin tá luachanna níos "
"mó ná 4294967295 nó 65535 faoi seach, ag dul bailíochtú agus a ghearradh go "
"ciúin ag an mbunachar sonraí (:ticket: `25767`)."

msgid "Django 1.8.8 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.8.8"

msgid "*January 2, 2016*"
msgstr "*2 Eanáir, 2016*"

msgid "Django 1.8.8 fixes several bugs in 1.8.7."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.8.8 roinnt fabhtanna i 1.8.7."

msgid ""
"Python 3.2 users, please be advised that we've decided to drop support for "
"Python 3.2 in Django 1.8.x at the end of 2016. We won't break things "
"intentionally after that, but we won't test subsequent releases against "
"Python 3.2 either. Upstream support for Python 3.2 ends February 2016 so we "
"don't find much value in providing security updates for a version of Python "
"that could be insecure. To read more about the decision and to let us know "
"if this will be problematic for you, please read the `django-developers "
"thread <https://groups.google.com/g/django-developers/c/eMu5UQpUdWs/"
"discussion>`_."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideoirí Python 3.2, tabhair in iúl le do thoil gur shocraigh muid "
"tacaíocht do Python 3.2 a scaoileadh i Django 1.8.x ag deireadh 2016. Ní "
"bhrisefaimid rudaí d'aon ghnó ina dhiaidh sin, ach ní dhéanfaimid tástáil "
"eisiúintí ina dhiaidh sin i gcoinne Python 3.2 Críochnaíonn tacaíocht suas "
"srutha do Python 3.2 Feabhra 2016 mar sin ní bhfaighimid mórán luacha maidir "
"le nuashonruithe slándála a sholáthar do leagan de Python a d'fhéadfadh a "
"bheith neamhchinnte. < https://groups.google.com/g/django-developers/c/"
"eMu5UQpUdWs/discussion>Chun tuilleadh a léamh faoin gcinneadh agus chun a "
"chur in iúl dúinn an mbeidh sé seo fadhbanna duit, léigh an snáithe `django-"
"forbróirí `_ le do thoil."

msgid ""
"Fixed incorrect ``unique_together`` field name generation by ``inspectdb`` "
"(:ticket:`25274`)."
msgstr ""
"Giniúint ainm réimse mícheart ``unique_together`` socraithe le ``inspectdb`` "
"(:ticket: `25274`)."

msgid ""
"Corrected ``__len`` query lookup on ``ArrayField`` for empty arrays "
"(:ticket:`25772`)."
msgstr ""
"Cuardach ceisteanna ``__len`` ceartaithe ar ``Arrayfield`` le haghaidh "
"eagair folamh (:ticket: `25772`)."

msgid ""
"Restored the ability to use custom formats from ``formats.py`` with "
"``django.utils.formats.get_format()`` and the ``date`` template filter "
"(:ticket:`25812`)."
msgstr ""
"Athchóirigh an cumas formáidí saincheaptha a úsáid ó ``formats.py`` le "
"``django.utils.formats.get_format () ``agus an scagaire teimpléad ``dáta`` "
"(:ticket: `25812`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a state bug when migrating a ``SeparateDatabaseAndState`` operation "
"backwards (:ticket:`25896`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh fabht stáit agus oibríocht `SeparatedAtabaseandState` á aistriú ar "
"ais (:ticket: `25896`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed missing ``varchar/text_pattern_ops`` index on ``CharField`` and "
"``TextField`` respectively when using ``AlterField`` on PostgreSQL "
"(:ticket:`25412`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh innéacs ``varchar/text_pattern_ops`` ar iarraidh ar ``Charfield`` "
"agus ``Textfield`` faoi seach nuair a úsáidtear ``Alterfield`` ar PostgreSQL "
"(:ticket: `25412`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a state bug when using an ``AlterModelManagers`` operation "
"(:ticket:`25852`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh fabht stáit agus oibríocht ``AlterModelManagers' á úsáid agat "
"(:ticket: `25852`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression which prevented using a language not in Django's default "
"language list (:setting:`LANGUAGES`) (:ticket:`25915`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú a chuir cosc ar úsáid teanga nach raibh i liosta teanga "
"réamhshocraithe Django (:setting: `LANGUAGES`) (:ticket: `25915`)."

msgid ""
"``django.views.decorators.cache.never_cache()`` now sends more persuasive "
"headers (added ``no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate`` to ``Cache-Control``) "
"to better prevent caching (:ticket:`13008`). This fixes a problem where a "
"page refresh in Firefox cleared the selected entries in the admin's "
"``filter_horizontal`` and ``filter_vertical`` widgets, which could result in "
"inadvertent data loss if a user didn't notice that and then submitted the "
"form (:ticket:`22955`)."
msgstr ""
"Seolann ``django.views.decorators.cache.never_cache () ``ceannteidil níos "
"áitiúla anois (cuir ``no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate`` le ``Cache-"
"Control``) chun cúisceáil a chosc níos fearr (:ticket: `13008`). Socraíonn "
"sé seo fadhb nuair a ghlanadh athnuachan leathanaigh i Firefox na "
"hiontrálacha roghnaithe i giuirléidí ``filter_horizontal`` agus "
"`filter_vertical`` an riaracháin, rud a d'fhéadfadh caillteanas sonraí "
"neamhthuigne a bheith mar thoradh air mura dtugann úsáideoir faoi deara sin "
"agus ansin chuir an fhoirm isteach (:ticket: `22955`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression in the admin which ignored line breaks in read-only "
"fields instead of converting them to ``<br>`` (:ticket:`25465`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú sa riarachán a rinne neamhaird ar shosanna líne i "
"réimsí léite amháin in ionad iad a thiontú go ```<br>(:ticket: `25465`)."

msgid ""
"Made ``loaddata`` skip disabling and enabling database constraints when it "
"doesn't load any fixtures (:ticket:`23372`)."
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh scipeáil ``loaddata` a dhíchumasú agus a chumasú srianta bunachar "
"sonraí nuair nach luchtaíonn sé aon daingneáin (:ticket: `23372`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash in ``QuerySet.values()/values_list()`` after an ``annotate()`` "
"and ``order_by()`` when ``values()/values_list()`` includes a field not in "
"the ``order_by()`` (:ticket:`25316`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste in ``QuerySet.values () /values_list () ``tar éis "
"``annotate ()`` agus ``order_by () ``nuair a chuimsíonn ``values () /"
"values_list () `réimse nach bhfuil sa `ord_by ()`` (:ticket: `25316`)."

msgid "Django 1.8.9 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.8.9"

msgid "*February 1, 2016*"
msgstr "*1 Feabhra, 2016*"

msgid "Django 1.8.9 fixes several bugs in 1.8.8."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.8.9 roinnt fabhtanna i 1.8.8."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression that caused the \"user-tools\" items to display on the "
"admin's logout page (:ticket:`26035`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú a chúis leis na míreanna “úsáideora” a thaispeáint ar "
"leathanach logála amach an riaracháin (:ticket: `26035`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash in the translations system when the current language has no "
"translations (:ticket:`26046`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste sa chóras aistriúcháin nuair nach bhfuil aon aistriúcháin "
"ag an teanga reatha (:ticket: `26046`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression that caused the incorrect day to be selected when opening "
"the admin calendar widget for timezones from GMT+0100 to GMT+1200 "
"(:ticket:`24980`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú a d'fhág gur roghnaíodh an lá mícheart nuair a "
"osclaíodh an giuirléid féilire riaracháin do chóin ama ó GMT+0100 go "
"GMT+1200 (:ticket: `24980`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression in 1.8.8 causing incorrect index handling in migrations "
"on PostgreSQL when adding ``db_index=True`` or ``unique=True`` to a "
"``CharField`` or ``TextField`` that already had the other specified, or when "
"removing one of them from a field that had both, or when adding "
"``unique=True`` to a field already listed in ``unique_together`` "
"(:ticket:`26034`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú i 1.8.8 ina chúis le láimhseáil innéacs mícheart in "
"imirce ar PostgreSQL nuair a chuirtear ``db_index=true`` nó ``Unique=true`` "
"le `charfield`` nó ``Textfield`` a raibh an ceann eile sonraithe cheana "
"féin, nó nuair a bhain ceann acu ó réimse a bhí ann, nó nuair a chuireann "
"``Unique=true`` le réimse cheana féin i ``unique_together ``(:ticket: "
"`26034`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when using an ``__in`` lookup inside a ``Case`` expression "
"(:ticket:`26071`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste nuair a úsáidtear cuardach ``__in`` taobh istigh de abairt "
"``Cás ``(:ticket: `26071`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when using a reverse ``OneToOneField`` in "
"``ModelAdmin.readonly_fields`` (:ticket:`26060`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste nuair a úsáidtear droim ``OneToOneField`` i "
"`ModelAdmin.ReadOnly_Fields`` (:ticket: `26060`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression in Django 1.8.5 that broke copying a ``SimpleLazyObject`` "
"with ``copy.copy()`` (:ticket:`26122`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú i Django 1.8.5 a bhris cóipeáil ``simplelazyobject`` le "
"`copy.copy () ``(:ticket: `26122`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed the ``contrib.gis`` map widgets when using "
"``USE_THOUSAND_SEPARATOR=True`` (:ticket:`20415`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh na giuirléidí léarscáileanna ``contrib.gis`` nuair a úsáideann tú "
"``USE_THOUSAND_SEPARATOR=True`` (:ticket: `20415`)."

msgid "Django 1.9 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.9"

msgid "*December 1, 2015*"
msgstr "*1 Nollaig, 2015*"

msgid "Welcome to Django 1.9!"
msgstr "Fáilte go dtí Django 1.9!"

msgid ""
"These release notes cover the :ref:`new features <whats-new-1.9>`, as well "
"as some :ref:`backwards incompatible changes <backwards-incompatible-1.9>` "
"you'll want to be aware of when upgrading from Django 1.8 or older versions. "
"We've :ref:`dropped some features<removed-features-1.9>` that have reached "
"the end of their deprecation cycle, and we've :ref:`begun the deprecation "
"process for some features <deprecated-features-1.9>`."
msgstr ""
"Clúdaíonn na nótaí scaoilte seo na:ref: `gnéithe nua <whats-new-1.9>`, chomh "
"maith le roinnt athruithe: ref: `athruithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha ar "
"ais<backwards-incompatible-1.9>` beidh tú ag iarraidh a bheith ar an eolas "
"fúthu agus tú ag uasghrádú ó Django 1.8 nó leaganacha níos sine. <deprecated-"
"features-1.9>Chuireamar: Ref: `thit roinnt <removed-features-1.9>gnéithe `a "
"bhfuil deireadh a dtimthriall díghníomhaíochta bainte amach acu, agus "
"chuireamaire:ref: `thosaigh muid ar an bpróiseas díghníomhaíochta do roinnt "
"gnéithe`."

msgid ""
"Django 1.9 requires Python 2.7, 3.4, or 3.5. We **highly recommend** and "
"only officially support the latest release of each series."
msgstr ""
"Éilíonn Django 1.9 Python 2.7, 3.4, nó 3.5. Molaimid** go hard** agus ní "
"thacaímid go hoifigiúil ach leis an scaoileadh is déanaí de gach sraith."

msgid "The Django 1.8 series is the last to support Python 3.2 and 3.3."
msgstr ""
"Is é an tsraith Django 1.8 an ceann deireanach a thacaíonn le Python 3.2 "
"agus 3.3."

msgid "What's new in Django 1.9"
msgstr "Cad atá nua i Django 1.9"

msgid "Performing actions after a transaction commit"
msgstr "Gníomhartha a dhéanamh tar éis idirbheart a dhéanamh"

msgid ""
"The new :func:`~django.db.transaction.on_commit` hook allows performing "
"actions after a database transaction is successfully committed. This is "
"useful for tasks such as sending notification emails, creating queued tasks, "
"or invalidating caches."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn an crúca nua:func: `~django.db.transaction.on_commit gníomhartha a "
"dhéanamh tar éis idirbheart bunachar sonraí a dhéanamh go rathúil. Tá sé seo "
"úsáideach le haghaidh tascanna mar ríomhphoist fógra a sheoladh, tascanna "
"scuaine a chruthú, nó táscáin a chur ar bhailí."

msgid ""
"This functionality from the :pypi:`django-transaction-hooks` package has "
"been integrated into Django."
msgstr ""
"Tá an fheidhmiúlacht seo ón bpacáiste: pypi: `django-transaction-hooks` "
"comhtháite i Django."

msgid "Password validation"
msgstr "Bailíochtú pasfhocal"

msgid ""
"Django now offers password validation to help prevent the usage of weak "
"passwords by users. The validation is integrated in the included password "
"change and reset forms and is simple to integrate in any other code. "
"Validation is performed by one or more validators, configured in the "
"new :setting:`AUTH_PASSWORD_VALIDATORS` setting."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann Django bailíochtú pasfhocal ar fáil anois chun cabhrú le húsáid "
"pasfhocail laga ag úsáideoirí a chosc. Tá an bailíochtú comhtháite sna "
"foirmeacha athraithe agus athshocraithe pasfhocal san áireamh agus tá sé "
"simplí a chomhtháthú in aon chód eile. Déanann bailíochtaithe amháin nó níos "
"mó bailíochtú, cumraithe sa shocrú nua:setting: `AUTH_PASSWORD_VALIDATORS`."

msgid ""
"Four validators are included in Django, which can enforce a minimum length, "
"compare the password to the user's attributes like their name, ensure "
"passwords aren't entirely numeric, or check against an included list of "
"common passwords. You can combine multiple validators, and some validators "
"have custom configuration options. For example, you can choose to provide a "
"custom list of common passwords. Each validator provides a help text to "
"explain its requirements to the user."
msgstr ""
"Tá ceithre bhailíochtóir san áireamh i Django, ar féidir leo fad íosta a "
"fhorfheidhmiú, an pasfhocal a chur i gcomparáid le tréithe an úsáideora "
"cosúil lena n-ainm, a chinntiú nach bhfuil pasfhocail uimhriúla go hiomlán, "
"nó seiceáil i gcoinne liosta pasfhocail choitianta. Is féidir leat "
"ilbhailíochtóirí a chur le chéile, agus tá roghanna cumraíochta saincheaptha "
"ag roinnt bailíochtóirí. Mar shampla, is féidir leat a roghnú liosta "
"saincheaptha de phasfhocail choitianta a sholáthar. Soláthraíonn gach "
"bailíochtóir téacs cabhrach chun a riachtanais a mhíniú don úsáideoir."

msgid ""
"By default, no validation is performed and all passwords are accepted, so if "
"you don't set :setting:`AUTH_PASSWORD_VALIDATORS`, you will not see any "
"change. In new projects created with the default :djadmin:`startproject` "
"template, a simple set of validators is enabled. To enable basic validation "
"in the included auth forms for your project, you could set, for example::"
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, ní dhéantar aon bhailíochtú agus glactar leis na "
"pasfhocail go léir, mar sin mura socraíonn tú: setting: "
"`AUTH_PASSWORD_VALIDATORS`, ní fheicfidh tú aon athrú. I dtionscadail nua a "
"cruthaíodh leis an teimpléad réamhshocraithe: djadmin: `startproject`, "
"cumasaítear tacar simplí bailíochtóirí. Chun bailíochtú bunúsach a chumasú "
"sna foirmeacha auth san áireamh do do thionscadal, d'fhéadfá a shocrú, mar "
"shampla:"

msgid "See :ref:`password-validation` for more details."
msgstr "Féach:ref: `bailíochtú pasfhocal` le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid "Permission mixins for class-based views"
msgstr "Meascáin ceadúnais le haghaidh tuairimí rang-bhunaithe"

msgid ""
"Django now ships with the "
"mixins :class:`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.AccessMixin`, :class:`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.LoginRequiredMixin`, :class:`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.PermissionRequiredMixin`, "
"and :class:`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.UserPassesTestMixin` to provide the "
"functionality of the ``django.contrib.auth.decorators`` for class-based "
"views. These mixins have been taken from, or are at least inspired by, the "
"`django-braces`_ project."
msgstr ""
"Seolann Django anois leis na meascáin: class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.accessMixin`, :class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.loginrequiredMixin`, :class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.permissionrequiredMixin`, agus:class: "
"`~django.contrib.contrib.Mixins.userPassestestMixin` chun feidhmiúlacht an "
"``django.contrib.auth.decorators ``a sholáthar le haghaidh tuairimí rang-"
"bhunaithe. Tógadh na meascáin seo ón tionscadal `django-braces`_, nó "
"spreagtar iad ar a laghad."

msgid ""
"There are a few differences between Django's and ``django-braces``\\' "
"implementation, though:"
msgstr ""
"Tá cúpla difríocht idir cur i bhfeidhm Django agus ``django-braces ``\\ ', "
"áfach:"

msgid ""
"The :attr:`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.AccessMixin.raise_exception` "
"attribute can only be ``True`` or ``False``. Custom exceptions or callables "
"are not supported."
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir an tréith: Attr: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.accessMixin.raise_exception` a bheith ach "
"``True`` nó ``False``. Ní thacaítear le heisceachtaí saincheaptha nó glaonna."

msgid ""
"The :meth:`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.AccessMixin.handle_no_permission` "
"method does not take a ``request`` argument. The current request is "
"available in ``self.request``."
msgstr ""
"Ní ghlacann an modh:Meth: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.accessMixin.handle_no_permission` argóint "
"``iarraidh`. Tá an t-iarratas reatha ar fáil in ``self.request``."

msgid ""
"The custom ``test_func()`` "
"of :class:`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.UserPassesTestMixin` does not take a "
"``user`` argument. The current user is available in ``self.request.user``."
msgstr ""
"Ní ghlacann an saincheaptha ``test_func () ``o:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.userPassestestMixin` argóint ``úsáideora``. Tá "
"an t-úsáideoir reatha ar fáil in ``self.request.user``."

msgid ""
"The :attr:`permission_required "
"<django.contrib.auth.mixins.PermissionRequiredMixin>` attribute supports a "
"string (defining one permission) or a list/tuple of strings (defining "
"multiple permissions) that need to be fulfilled to grant access."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn an tréith: attr: `permission_required "
"<django.contrib.auth.mixins.PermissionRequiredMixin>`le sreang (cead amháin "
"a shainmhíníonn) nó le liosta/tiúpla teaghráin (ceadanna iolracha a shainiú) "
"nach mór a chomhlíonadh chun rochtain a dheonú."

msgid ""
"The "
"new :attr:`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.AccessMixin.permission_denied_message` "
"attribute allows passing a message to the ``PermissionDenied`` exception."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn an tréith nua:attr: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.accessmixin.permission_denied_message` "
"teachtaireacht a chur chuig an eisceacht ``PermissionDenied``."

msgid "New styling for ``contrib.admin``"
msgstr "Stíl nua do ``contrib.admin``"

msgid ""
"The admin sports a modern, flat design with new SVG icons which look perfect "
"on HiDPI screens. It still provides a fully-functional experience to `YUI's "
"A-grade`_ browsers. Older browser may experience varying levels of graceful "
"degradation."
msgstr ""
"Spóirt an riarthóir dearadh nua-aimseartha, cothrom le deilbhíní SVG nua a "
"bhreathnaíonn foirfe ar scáileáin HiDPI. Soláthraíonn sé eispéireas "
"lánfheidhmeach fós do bhrabhsálaithe `YUI A-grád`_. D’fhéadfadh leibhéil "
"éagsúla díghrádaithe a bheith ag brabhsálaithe níos sine."

msgid "Running tests in parallel"
msgstr "Tástálacha reatha go comhthreomhar"

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`test` command now supports a :option:`--parallel <test --"
"parallel>` option to run a project's tests in multiple processes in parallel."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn an t-ordú: DjaDmin: `tástála` anois le rogha a: `--comhthreomhar "
"`chun tástálacha tionscadail a reáchtáil i bpró <test --parallel>isis "
"iolracha go comhthreomhar."

msgid ""
"Each process gets its own database. You must ensure that different test "
"cases don't access the same resources. For instance, test cases that touch "
"the filesystem should create a temporary directory for their own use."
msgstr ""
"Faigheann gach próiseas a bhunachar sonraí féin. Ní mór duit a chinntiú nach "
"bhfuil rochtain ag cásanna tástála éagsúla ar na hacmhainní céanna Mar "
"shampla, ba cheart do chásanna tástála a théann i dteagmháil leis an gcóras "
"comhaid eolaire sealadach a chruthú lena n-úsáid féin."

msgid "This option is enabled by default for Django's own test suite provided:"
msgstr ""
"Tá an rogha seo cumasaithe de réir réamhshocraithe do shraith tástála Django "
"féin ar fáil:"

msgid "the OS supports it (all but Windows)"
msgstr "tacaíonn an OS leis (gach ceann ach Windows)"

msgid "the database backend supports it (all the built-in backends but Oracle)"
msgstr ""
"tacaíonn cúltaca an bhunachar sonraí leis (na cúltaca ionsuite go léir ach "
"Oracle)"

msgid "Admin views now have ``model_admin`` or ``admin_site`` attributes."
msgstr ""
"Tá tréithe ``model_admin ``nó ``admin_site`` ag tuairimí riaracháin anois."

msgid ""
"The URL of the admin change view has been changed (was at ``/admin/<app>/"
"<model>/<pk>/`` by default and is now at ``/admin/<app>/<model>/<pk>/change/"
"``). This should not affect your application unless you have hardcoded admin "
"URLs. In that case, replace those links by :ref:`reversing admin URLs <admin-"
"reverse-urls>` instead. Note that the old URL still redirects to the new one "
"for backwards compatibility, but it may be removed in a future version."
msgstr ""
"<app><model><pk>Athraíodh URL an radharc athraithe riaracháin (bhí sé ag ``/"
"admin//<app>//`` de réir réamh <model><pk>shocraithe agus tá sé anois ag ``/"
"admin///change/ ``). Níor cheart go ndéanfadh sé seo difear d'iarratas mura "
"bhfuil URLanna riaracháin crua-chódaithe agat. <admin-reverse-urls>Sa chás "
"sin, cuir na naisc sin in ionad: ref: `URLanna riaracháin a aisiompú `ina "
"ionad sin. Tabhair faoi deara go n-atreoraíonn an sean-URL go dtí an ceann "
"nua fós le haghaidh comhoiriúnacht ar ais, ach féadfar é a bhaint i leagan "
"amach anseo."

msgid ""
":meth:`ModelAdmin.get_list_select_related() "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.get_list_select_related>` was added to "
"allow changing the ``select_related()`` values used in the admin's "
"changelist query based on the request."
msgstr ""
":meth: Cuireadh `ModelAdmin.get_list_select_related () "
"`<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.get_list_select_related>leis chun ligean "
"na luachanna ``select_related () ``a úsáidtear i bhfiosrúchán an liosta "
"athraithe riaracháin bunaithe ar an iarratas a athrú."

msgid ""
"The ``available_apps`` context variable, which lists the available "
"applications for the current user, has been added to "
"the :meth:`AdminSite.each_context() "
"<django.contrib.admin.AdminSite.each_context>` method."
msgstr ""
"<django.contrib.admin.AdminSite.each_context>Cuireadh an t-athróg comhthéacs "
"`available_apps``, a liostaíonn na feidhmchláir atá ar fáil don úsáideoir "
"reatha, leis an modh: meth: `adminsite.each_context () `."

msgid ""
":attr:`AdminSite.empty_value_display "
"<django.contrib.admin.AdminSite.empty_value_display>` "
"and :attr:`ModelAdmin.empty_value_display "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.empty_value_display>` were added to "
"override the display of empty values in admin change list. You can also "
"customize the value for each field."
msgstr ""
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.empty_value_display>:attr: "
"`Adminsite.empty_value_display `agus:attr: "
"<django.contrib.admin.AdminSite.empty_value_display>`ModelAdmin.empty_value_display` "
"cuireadh leis chun taispeáint luachanna folmha i liosta athruithe riaracháin "
"a shárú. Is féidir leat an luach do gach réimse a shaincheapadh freisin."

msgid ""
"Added jQuery events :ref:`when an inline form is added or removed <admin-"
"javascript-inline-form-events>` on the change form page."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh imeachtaí jQuery leis: ref: `nuair a chuirtear foirm inlíne leis nó "
"baintear <admin-javascript-inline-form-events>`ar an leathanach foirm "
"athraithe."

msgid ""
"The time picker widget includes a '6 p.m' option for consistency of having "
"predefined options every 6 hours."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn an giuirléid roghnaithe ama rogha '6 p.m' chun "
"comhsheasmhainneacht roghanna réamhshainithe a bheith agat gach 6 uair an "
"chloig."

msgid "JavaScript slug generation now supports Romanian characters."
msgstr "Tacaíonn giniúint slug JavaScript anois le carachtair na Rómáine."

msgid ""
"The model section of the ``admindocs`` now also describes methods that take "
"arguments, rather than ignoring them."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an chuid samhail den `admindocs` cur síos anois ar mhodhanna a "
"thógann argóintí, seachas neamhaird a dhéanamh orthu."

msgid ""
"The default iteration count for the PBKDF2 password hasher has been "
"increased by 20%. This backwards compatible change will not affect users who "
"have subclassed ``django.contrib.auth.hashers.PBKDF2PasswordHasher`` to "
"change the default value."
msgstr ""
"Méadaíodh 20% an líon athraithe réamhshocraithe don hasher pasfhocal PBKDF2. "
"Ní dhéanfaidh an t-athrú comhoiriúnach ar chúl difear d'úsáideoirí a bhfuil "
"fo-aicmithe ag ``Django.contrib.auth.hashers.pbkdf2PasswordHasher`` chun an "
"luach réamhshocraithe a athrú."

msgid ""
"The ``BCryptSHA256PasswordHasher`` will now update passwords if its "
"``rounds`` attribute is changed."
msgstr ""
"Déanfaidh an `BCryptsha256PasswordHasher`` pasfhocail a nuashonrú anois má "
"athraítear a thréith ``rounds`."

msgid ""
"``AbstractBaseUser`` and ``BaseUserManager`` were moved to a new "
"``django.contrib.auth.base_user`` module so that they can be imported "
"without including ``django.contrib.auth`` in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` "
"(doing so raised a deprecation warning in older versions and is no longer "
"supported in Django 1.9)."
msgstr ""
"Bogadh ``AbstractBaseUser`` agus ``BaseUserManager`` chuig modúl nua "
"``django.contrib.auth.base_user`` ionas gur féidir iad a allmhairiú gan "
"``django.contrib.auth`` a chur san áireamh in:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS` (ag "
"déanamh amhlaidh rabhadh i leaganacha níos sine agus ní thacaíonn sé i "
"Django 1.9)."

msgid ""
"The permission argument "
"of :func:`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.permission_required()` accepts all "
"kinds of iterables, not only list and tuples."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an argóint ceada:func: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.permission_required () `le gach cineál "
"athraitheacha, ní amháin liosta agus tuples."

msgid ""
"The "
"new :class:`~django.contrib.auth.middleware.PersistentRemoteUserMiddleware` "
"makes it possible to use ``REMOTE_USER`` for setups where the header is only "
"populated on login pages instead of every request in the session."
msgstr ""
"De bharr nua:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.middleware.persistentRemoteUserMiddleware` is féidir "
"``REMOTE_USER`` a úsáid le haghaidh socruithe nach bhfuil an ceannteideal "
"ach ar leathanaigh logála isteach in ionad gach iarratas sa seisiún."

msgid ""
"The ``django.contrib.auth.views.password_reset()`` view accepts an "
"``extra_email_context`` parameter."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an radharc ``django.contrib.auth.views.password_reset () ``le "
"paraiméadar ``extra_email_context``."

msgid ""
"It's now possible to "
"use :attr:`~django.db.models.Options.order_with_respect_to` with a "
"``GenericForeignKey``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir anois: attr: `~django.db.models.options.ORDER_with_RESPECT_TO` a "
"úsáid le ``GenericForeignKey``."

msgid ""
"All ``GeoQuerySet`` methods have been deprecated and replaced "
"by :doc:`equivalent database functions </ref/contrib/gis/functions>`. As "
"soon as the legacy methods have been replaced in your code, you should even "
"be able to remove the special ``GeoManager`` from your GIS-enabled classes."
msgstr ""
"Tá gach modh ``GeoquerySet`` a dhíscríobh agus cuireadh: doc: `feidhmeanna "
"bunachar sonraí coibhéiseach 'ina ionad. </ref/contrib/gis/functions> Chomh "
"luath agus a cuirtear na modhanna oidhreachta in ionad i do chód, ba cheart "
"go mbeadh tú in ann an “Geomanager” speisialta a bhaint as do ranganna "
"cumasaithe GIS fiú."

msgid ""
"The GDAL interface now supports instantiating file-based and in-"
"memory :ref:`GDALRaster objects <raster-data-source-objects>` from raw data. "
"Setters for raster properties such as projection or pixel values have been "
"added."
msgstr ""
"<raster-data-source-objects>Tacaíonn an comhéadan GDAL anois le "
"comhadbhunaithe agus in-chuimhne:ref: `rudaí GDAlraster `ó shonraí amh. "
"Cuireadh socraithe le haghaidh airíonna raster cosúil le luachanna teilgean "
"nó picteilín."

msgid ""
"For PostGIS users, the "
"new :class:`~django.contrib.gis.db.models.RasterField` allows :ref:`storing "
"GDALRaster objects <creating-and-saving-raster-models>`. It supports "
"automatic spatial index creation and reprojection when saving a model. It "
"does not yet support spatial querying."
msgstr ""
"<creating-and-saving-raster-models>Maidir le húsáideoirí PostGIS, ceadaíonn "
"an nua:class: `~django.contrib.gis.db.models.rasterfield`: ref: `rudaí "
"GDAlraster a stóráil `. Tacaíonn sé le cruthú innéacs spásúil uathoibríoch "
"agus athléiriú nuair a shábháil Ní thacaíonn sé le fiosrúchán spásúil fós."

msgid ""
"The new :meth:`GDALRaster.warp() <django.contrib.gis.gdal.GDALRaster.warp>` "
"method allows warping a raster by specifying target raster properties such "
"as origin, width, height, or pixel size (among others)."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an <django.contrib.gis.gdal.GDALRaster.warp>modh nua:meth: "
"`gdalraster.warp () `raster a chreamú trí airíonna raster sprioc-raster a "
"shonrú mar bhunús, leithead, airde nó méid picteilín (i measc eile)."

msgid ""
"The new :meth:`GDALRaster.transform() "
"<django.contrib.gis.gdal.GDALRaster.transform>` method allows transforming a "
"raster into a different spatial reference system by specifying a target "
"``srid``."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an modh nua:meth: `gdalraster.transformer () "
"<django.contrib.gis.gdal.GDALRaster.transform>`raster a athrú go córas "
"tagartha spásúil difriúil trí sprioc ``srid`` a shonrú."

msgid ""
"The new :class:`~django.contrib.gis.geoip2.GeoIP2` class allows using "
"MaxMind's GeoLite2 databases which includes support for IPv6 addresses."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn an rang nua:class: `~django.contrib.gis.geoip2.geoip2` bunachair "
"sonraí GeoLite2 MaxMind a úsáid a chuimsíonn tacaíocht do sheoltaí IPv6."

msgid ""
"The default OpenLayers library version included in widgets has been updated "
"from 2.13 to 2.13.1."
msgstr ""
"Nuashonraíodh an leagan réamhshocraithe leabharlainne OpenLayers atá san "
"áireamh i giuirléidí ó 2.13 go 2.13.1."

msgid ""
"Added support for the :lookup:`rangefield.contained_by` lookup for some "
"built in fields which correspond to the range fields."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíocht bhreise don chuardach: lookup: `rangefield.contained_by` do roinnt "
"réimsí tógtha i réimsí a fhreagraíonn do na réimsí raon."

msgid "Added ``django.contrib.postgres.fields.JSONField``."
msgstr "Cuireadh ``django.contrib.postgres.fields.jsonfield`` leis."

msgid "Added :doc:`/ref/contrib/postgres/aggregates`."
msgstr "Cuireadh leis: doc: `/ref/contrib/postgres/aggregates`."

msgid ""
"Added the :class:`~django.contrib.postgres.functions.TransactionNow` "
"database function."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh feidhm bunachar sonraí: class: "
"`~django.contrib.postgres.functions.TransactionNow` leis."

msgid ""
"The session model and ``SessionStore`` classes for the ``db`` and "
"``cached_db`` backends are refactored to allow a custom database session "
"backend to build upon them. See :ref:`extending-database-backed-session-"
"engines` for more details."
msgstr ""
"Athraítear an tsamhail seisiúin agus na ranganna ``SessionStore`` do na "
"cúltaca ``db`` agus `cached_db`` chun ligean cúltaca seisiúin bunachar "
"sonraí saincheaptha tógáil orthu. Féach: Ref: `extending-database-backed-"
"seision-inneallaire` le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid ""
":func:`~django.contrib.sites.shortcuts.get_current_site` now handles the "
"case where ``request.get_host()`` returns ``domain:port``, e.g. "
"``example.com:80``. If the lookup fails because the host does not match a "
"record in the database and the host has a port, the port is stripped and the "
"lookup is retried with the domain part only."
msgstr ""
":func: `~django.contrib.sites.shortcuts.get_current_site` láimhseálann anois "
"an cás ina bhfilleann ``request.get_host () ````domain:port``, m.sh. "
"`example.com:80``. Má theipeann ar an cuardach toisc nach n-oireann an t-"
"óstach taifead sa bhunachar sonraí agus go bhfuil calafort ag an óstach, "
"déantar an calafort a dhíriú agus déantar an cuardach a athbhreithniú leis "
"an gcuid fearainn amháin."

msgid ""
"Support for multiple enclosures per feed item has been added. If multiple "
"enclosures are defined on a RSS feed, an exception is raised as RSS feeds, "
"unlike Atom feeds, do not support multiple enclosures per feed item."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh tacaíocht le haghaidh iolracha iolracha in aghaidh an earra beatha. "
"Má shainmhínítear iolrghabhálacha ar fhotha RSS, ardaítear eisceacht mar ní "
"thacaíonn fothaí RSS, murab ionann agus fothaí Atom, le iolracha iolracha in "
"aghaidh an earra beatha."

msgid ""
"``django.core.cache.backends.base.BaseCache`` now has a ``get_or_set()`` "
"method."
msgstr ""
"Tá modh ``get_or_set () ``anois ag "
"`django.core.cache.backends.base.baseCache``."

msgid ""
":func:`django.views.decorators.cache.never_cache` now sends more persuasive "
"headers (added ``no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate`` to ``Cache-Control``) "
"to better prevent caching. This was also added in Django 1.8.8."
msgstr ""
":func: Seolann `django.views.decorators.cache.never_cache` ceannteidil níos "
"áitiúla anois (cuireadh ``no-cache, no-store, riachtanach athbhreithnithe "
"``le `Cache-Control``) chun cúisceáil a chosc níos fearr. Cuireadh é seo "
"leis freisin i Django 1.8.8."

msgid ""
"The request header's name used for CSRF authentication can be customized "
"with :setting:`CSRF_HEADER_NAME`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir ainm ceanntásc an iarratais a úsáidtear le haghaidh fíordheimhniú "
"CSRF a shaincheapadh la:setting: `CSRF_HEADER_NAME`."

msgid ""
"The CSRF referer header is now validated against "
"the :setting:`CSRF_COOKIE_DOMAIN` setting if set. See :ref:`how-csrf-works` "
"for details."
msgstr ""
"Tá ceanntásc tagairtí CSRF bailíochtaithe anois i gcoinne an socruithe:: "
"`CSRF_COOKIE_DOMAIN` má tá sé socraithe. Féach: ref: `how csrf-works` le "
"haghaidh sonraí."

msgid ""
"The new :setting:`CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS` setting provides a way to allow "
"cross-origin unsafe requests (e.g. ``POST``) over HTTPS."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn an socrú nua:setting: `CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS` bealach chun "
"iarratais neamhshábháilte tras-bhunús (m.sh. `POST ``) a cheadú thar HTTPS."

msgid ""
"The PostgreSQL backend (``django.db.backends.postgresql_psycopg2``) is also "
"available as ``django.db.backends.postgresql``. The old name will continue "
"to be available for backwards compatibility."
msgstr ""
"Tá an cúltaca PostgreSQL (``django.db.backends.postgresql_psycopg2``) ar "
"fáil freisin mar ``django.db.backends.postgresql``. Leanfaidh an sean-ainm "
"ar fáil le haghaidh comhoiriúnacht ar ais."

msgid ""
":meth:`Storage.get_valid_name() "
"<django.core.files.storage.Storage.get_valid_name>` is now called when "
"the :attr:`~django.db.models.FileField.upload_to` is a callable."
msgstr ""
":meth: Glaoftar ar `Storage.get_valid_name () `anois nuair a bhíonn "
"ain:attr: `~django.db.models.filefield.upload_ "
"<django.core.files.storage.Storage.get_valid_name>to` inghlaonta."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.core.files.File` now has the ``seekable()`` method when "
"using Python 3."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.core.files.file` anois tá an modh ``searchable () ``ag "
"baint úsáide as Python 3."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.forms.ModelForm` accepts the new ``Meta`` option "
"``field_classes`` to customize the type of the fields. See :ref:`modelforms-"
"overriding-default-fields` for details."
msgstr ""
":class: `~Django.Forms.ModelForm` glacann leis an rogha nua ``Meta`` "
"``field_classes`` chun cineál na réimsí a shaincheapadh. Féach:ref: "
"`modelforms-overriding-default-fields` le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid ""
"You can now specify the order in which form fields are rendered with "
"the :attr:`~django.forms.Form.field_order` attribute, the ``field_order`` "
"constructor argument , or the :meth:`~django.forms.Form.order_fields` method."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat anois an t-ord ina ndéantar réimsí foirme a shonrú leis an "
"tréith: attr: `~django.forms.form.field_order`, an t-argóint tógálaí "
"``field_order``, nó an modh:meth: `~django.forms.form.ORDER_fields`."

msgid ""
"A form prefix can be specified inside a form class, not only when "
"instantiating a form. See :ref:`form-prefix` for details."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir réimír foirme a shonrú taobh istigh de rang foirme, ní amháin "
"nuair a bhíonn foirm á chur i bhfeidhm. Féach: ref: `form-prefix` le "
"haghaidh sonraí."

msgid ""
"You can now :ref:`specify keyword arguments <custom-formset-form-kwargs>` "
"that you want to pass to the constructor of forms in a formset."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat anois:ref: `argóintí eochairfhocal a shonrú <custom-formset-"
"form-kwargs>`a theastaíonn uait a chur chuig tógálaí foirmeacha i "
"bhfoirmeach."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.forms.SlugField` now accepts "
"an :attr:`~django.forms.SlugField.allow_unicode` argument to allow Unicode "
"characters in slugs."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.forms.slugfield` glacann anois leis an:attr: "
"`~django.forms.slugfield.allow_unicode` argóint chun carachtair Unicode a "
"cheadú i slúgaí."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.forms.CharField` now accepts "
"a :attr:`~django.forms.CharField.strip` argument to strip input data of "
"leading and trailing whitespace.  As this defaults to ``True`` this is "
"different behavior from previous releases."
msgstr ""
": class: `~django.forms.charfield` glacann anois le:: attr: "
"`~django.forms.charfield.strip` argóint chun sonraí ionchuir de spás bán "
"tosaigh agus leantach a stialladh. Toisc go bhfuil sé seo réamhshocraithe go "
"``True`` is iompar difriúil é seo ó eisiúintí roimhe seo."

msgid ""
"Form fields now support the :attr:`~django.forms.Field.disabled` argument, "
"allowing the field widget to be displayed disabled by browsers."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn réimsí foirme anois leis an argóint: attr: "
"`~django.forms.field.disabled`, rud a ligeann an giuirléid réimse a "
"thaispeáint faoi dhíchumasú ag brabhsálaithe."

msgid ""
"It's now possible to customize bound fields by overriding a "
"field's :meth:`~django.forms.Field.get_bound_field()` method."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir réimsí ceangailte a shaincheapadh anois trí mhodh réimse: meth: "
"`~django.forms.field.get_bound_field () `a shárú."

msgid ""
"Class-based views generated using ``as_view()`` now have ``view_class`` and "
"``view_initkwargs`` attributes."
msgstr ""
"Tá tréithe ``view_class`` agus `view_initkwargs`` anois ag tuairimí rang-"
"bhunaithe a ghintear ag baint úsáide as ``as_view () ``."

msgid ""
":func:`~django.utils.decorators.method_decorator` can now be used with a "
"list or tuple of decorators. It can also be used to :ref:`decorate classes "
"instead of methods <decorating-class-based-views>`."
msgstr ""
":func: Is féidir `~django.utils.decorators.method_decorator` a úsáid anois "
"le liosta nó tiúpla maisitheoirí. <decorating-class-based-views>Is féidir é "
"a úsáid freisin chun: ref: `ranganna a mhaisiú in ionad modhanna `."

msgid ""
"The :func:`django.views.i18n.set_language` view now properly redirects "
"to :ref:`translated URLs <url-internationalization>`, when available."
msgstr ""
"<url-internationalization>Atreoraíonn an amharc:func: "
"`django.views.i18n.set_language` i gceart anois chuig:ref: `URLanna "
"aistrithe `, nuair atá ar fáil."

msgid ""
"The ``django.views.i18n.javascript_catalog()`` view now works correctly if "
"used multiple times with different configurations on the same page."
msgstr ""
"Oibríonn an radharc ``django.views.i18n.javascript_catalog () ``i gceart "
"anois má úsáidtear é arís agus arís eile le cumraíochtaí éagsúla ar an "
"leathanach céanna."

msgid ""
"The :func:`django.utils.timezone.make_aware` function gained an ``is_dst`` "
"argument to help resolve ambiguous times during DST transitions."
msgstr ""
"Fuair an fheidhm:func: `django.utils.timezone.make_aware` argóint ``is_dst`` "
"chun cabhrú le hamanna débhríochta a réiteach le linn aistrithe DST."

msgid ""
"You can now use locale variants supported by gettext. These are usually used "
"for languages which can be written in different scripts, for example Latin "
"and Cyrillic (e.g. ``be@latin``)."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat leaganacha áitiúla a úsáid anois le tacaíocht ó gettext. "
"Úsáidtear iad seo de ghnáth le haghaidh teangacha is féidir iad a scríobh i "
"scripteanna éagsúla, mar shampla Laidin agus Cirillic (m.sh. `be @latin ``)."

msgid ""
"Added the ``django.views.i18n.json_catalog()`` view to help build a custom "
"client-side i18n library upon Django translations. It returns a JSON object "
"containing a translations catalog, formatting settings, and a plural rule."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an dearcadh ``django.views.i18n.json_catalog () `leis chun cabhrú "
"le leabharlann saincheaptha i18n ar thaobh an chliaint a thógáil ar "
"aistriúcháin Django. Tugann sé réad JSON ar ais ina bhfuil catalóg "
"aistriúcháin, socruithe formáidithe, agus riail iolra."

msgid ""
"Added the ``name_translated`` attribute to the object returned by "
"the :ttag:`get_language_info` template tag. Also added a corresponding "
"template filter: :tfilter:`language_name_translated`."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an tréith ``name_translated`` leis an réad ar ais ag an gclib "
"teimpléad:ttag: `get_language_info`. Chuir scagaire teimpléad comhfhreagrach "
"leis freisin: :tfilter: `language_name_translated`."

msgid ""
"You can now run :djadmin:`compilemessages` from the root directory of your "
"project and it will find all the app message files that were created "
"by :djadmin:`makemessages`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat anois: djadmin: `compilemessages` a rith ó eolaire fréimhe do "
"thionscadail agus gheobhaidh sé na comhaid teachtaireachta aip go léir a "
"chruthaigh: djadmin: `makemessages`."

msgid ""
":djadmin:`makemessages` now calls ``xgettext`` once per locale directory "
"rather than once per translatable file. This speeds up localization builds."
msgstr ""
":djadmin: glaonn `makemessages` anois ``xgettext`` uair amháin in aghaidh an "
"eolaire áitiúil seachas uair amháin in aghaidh an chomhaid inaistrithe. "
"Luasaíonn sé seo tógáil logánaithe."

msgid ""
":ttag:`blocktrans` supports assigning its output to a variable using "
"``asvar``."
msgstr ""
":ttag: tacaíonn `blocktrans` lena aschur a shannadh d'athróg ag baint úsáide "
"as ``asvar``."

msgid "Two new languages are available: Colombian Spanish and Scottish Gaelic."
msgstr ""
"Tá dhá theanga nua ar fáil: Spáinnis na Colóime agus Gaeilge na hAlban."

msgid ""
"The new :djadmin:`sendtestemail` command lets you send a test email to "
"easily confirm that email sending through Django is working."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an t-ordú nua:djadmin: `sendtestemail` duit ríomhphost tástála a "
"sheoladh chun a dhearbhú go héasca go bhfuil seoladh ríomhphoist trí Django "
"ag obair."

msgid ""
"To increase the readability of the SQL code generated "
"by :djadmin:`sqlmigrate`, the SQL code generated for each migration "
"operation is preceded by the operation's description."
msgstr ""
"Chun inléiteacht an chóid SQL a ghineann: djadmin: `sqlmigrate` a mhéadú, "
"cuirtear tuairisc na hoibríochta roimh an gcód SQL a ghintear do gach "
"oibríocht imirce."

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`dumpdata` command output is now deterministically ordered. "
"Moreover, when the ``--output`` option is specified, it also shows a "
"progress bar in the terminal."
msgstr ""
"Tá an t-aschur ordaithe: DJAdmin: `dumpdata` ordaithe go cinntiúil anois. "
"Thairis sin, nuair a shonraítear an rogha ``--aschur ``, taispeánann sé "
"barra dul chun cinn sa chríochfort freisin."

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`createcachetable` command now has a ``--dry-run`` flag to "
"print out the SQL rather than execute it."
msgstr ""
"Tá bratach ``--dry-run`` anois ag an ordú: DjaDmin: `createcachetable` chun "
"an SQL a phriontáil amach seachas é a fhorghníomhú."

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`startapp` command creates an ``apps.py`` file. Since it "
"doesn't use ``default_app_config`` (:ref:`a discouraged API <configuring-"
"applications-ref>`), you must specify the app config's path, e.g. "
"``'polls.apps.PollsConfig'``, in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` for it to be used "
"(instead of just ``'polls'``)."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaíonn an t-ordú:djaDmin: `startapp` comhad ``apps.py``. Ós rud é nach n-"
"úsáideann sé ``default_app_config`` (:ref: `a dhíspreagtha API `<configuring-"
"applications-ref>), ní mór duit cosán cumraíocht an aip a shonrú, m.sh. "
"``Polls.apps.pollsconfig'`, in:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS` chun é a úsáid (in "
"ionad ``polls'`` amháin)."

msgid ""
"When using the PostgreSQL backend, the :djadmin:`dbshell` command can "
"connect to the database using the password from your settings file (instead "
"of requiring it to be manually entered)."
msgstr ""
"Agus cúltaca PostgreSQL á úsáid agat, is féidir leis an ordú:djadmin: "
"`dbshell` nascadh leis an mbunachar sonraí ag baint úsáide as an bhfocal "
"faire ó do chomhad socruithe (in ionad a cheangal go ndéanfar é a iontráil "
"de láimh)."

msgid ""
"The ``django`` package may be run as a script, i.e. ``python -m django``, "
"which will behave the same as ``django-admin``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an pacáiste ``django`` a reáchtáil mar script, ie ``python -m "
"django``, a iompraíonn mar an gcéanna le ``django-admin``."

msgid ""
"Management commands that have the ``--noinput`` option now also take ``--no-"
"input`` as an alias for that option."
msgstr ""
"Glacann orduithe bainistíochta a bhfuil an rogha ``--noinput`` acu anois ``--"
"no-input`` mar ainm don rogha sin."

msgid ""
"Initial migrations are now marked with an :attr:`initial = True "
"<django.db.migrations.Migration.initial>` class attribute which "
"allows :option:`migrate --fake-initial` to more easily detect initial "
"migrations."
msgstr ""
"Tá imirce tosaigh marcáilte anois le tréith "
"<django.db.migrations.Migration.initial>aicme: attr: `inicial = True `a "
"cheadaíonn: rogha: `migrar --fake-initial` chun imirce tosaigh a bhrath níos "
"éasca."

msgid ""
"Added support for serialization of ``functools.partial`` and ``LazyObject`` "
"instances."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíocht bhreise le haghaidh sraitheadh cásanna ``functools.partial`` agus "
"``LazyObject``."

msgid ""
"When supplying ``None`` as a value in :setting:`MIGRATION_MODULES`, Django "
"will consider the app an app without migrations."
msgstr ""
"Agus “None” á sholáthar agat mar luach in:setting: `MIGRATION_MODULES`, "
"measfaidh Django an aip mar aip gan imirce."

msgid ""
"When applying migrations, the \"Rendering model states\" step that's "
"displayed when running migrate with verbosity 2 or higher now computes only "
"the states for the migrations that have already been applied. The model "
"states for migrations being applied are generated on demand, drastically "
"reducing the amount of required memory."
msgstr ""
"Agus imirce á chur i bhfeidhm, ní ríomhaíonn an chéim “Stáit samhail "
"rindreála” a thaispeántar agus imirce á reáchtáil le verbosity 2 nó níos "
"airde anois ach na stáit do na himirce a cuireadh i bhfeidhm cheana féin. "
"Gintear na stáit samhail maidir le himirce atá á chur i bhfeidhm ar éileamh, "
"ag laghdú go suntasach an méid cuimhne riachtanach."

msgid ""
"However, this improvement is not available when unapplying migrations and "
"therefore still requires the precomputation and storage of the intermediate "
"migration states."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, níl an feabhas seo ar fáil nuair nach gcuirtear i bhfeidhm "
"imirce agus mar sin tá gá fós le réamh-ríomh agus stóráil na stáit imirce "
"idirmheánacha."

msgid ""
"This improvement also requires that Django no longer supports mixed "
"migration plans. Mixed plans consist of a list of migrations where some are "
"being applied and others are being unapplied. This was never officially "
"supported and never had a public API that supports this behavior."
msgstr ""
"Éilíonn an feabhsú seo freisin nach dtacaíonn Django le pleananna imirce "
"measctha a thuilleadh. Is éard atá i bpleananna measctha liosta aistrithe a "
"bhfuil cuid acu á gcur i bhfeidhm agus cinn eile nach bhfuil á gcur i "
"bhfeidhm. Níor tugadh tacaíocht oifigiúil riamh dó seo agus ní raibh API "
"poiblí ann riamh a thacaíonn leis an iompar seo."

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`squashmigrations` command now supports specifying the starting "
"migration from which migrations will be squashed."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn an t-ordú: Djadmin: `squashmigrations` anois leis an imirce tosaigh "
"a shonrú óna ndéanfar imirce a scriosadh."

msgid ""
":meth:`QuerySet.bulk_create() <django.db.models.query.QuerySet.bulk_create>` "
"now works on proxy models."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.bulk_create>: meth: `QuerySet.bulk_create "
"() `oibríonn anois ar mhúnlaí seachfhreastalaí."

msgid ""
"Database configuration gained a :setting:`TIME_ZONE <DATABASE-TIME_ZONE>` "
"option for interacting with databases that store datetimes in local time and "
"don't support time zones when :setting:`USE_TZ` is ``True``."
msgstr ""
"Fuair cumraíocht bunachar sonraí a: leagan: `TIME_ZONE <DATABASE-"
"TIME_ZONE>`rogha chun idirghníomhú le bunachair sonraí a stóráilíonn amanna "
"dáta in am áitiúil agus nach dtacaíonn le criosanna ama nuai:socrú: `USE_TZ` "
"``True``."

msgid ""
"Added the :meth:`RelatedManager.set() "
"<django.db.models.fields.related.RelatedManager.set()>` method to the "
"related managers created by ``ForeignKey``, ``GenericForeignKey``, and "
"``ManyToManyField``."
msgstr ""
"Chuir an modh: meth: `RelatedManager.set () leis na bainisteoirí gaolmhara a "
"chruthaigh ``ForeignKey``, `GenericForeignKey``, "
"<django.db.models.fields.related.RelatedManager.set () > agus "
"``ManyTomanyField``."

msgid ""
"The :meth:`~django.db.models.fields.related.RelatedManager.add` method on a "
"reverse foreign key now has a ``bulk`` parameter to allow executing one "
"query regardless of the number of objects being added rather than one query "
"per object."
msgstr ""
"Tá paraiméadar ``bulk`` ag an modh: Meth: "
"`~Django.DB.Models.Fields.Related.RelatedManager.Add` ar eochair eachtrach "
"droim ar ais anois chun ceist amháin a fhorghníomhú beag beann ar líon na "
"rudaí atá á chur leis seachas ceist amháin in aghaidh an rud."

msgid ""
"Added the ``keep_parents`` parameter to :meth:`Model.delete() "
"<django.db.models.Model.delete>` to allow deleting only a child's data in a "
"model that uses multi-table inheritance."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an paraiméadar ``keep_parents`` chuig: meth: `Model.delete () "
"<django.db.models.Model.delete>`chun sonraí linbh a scriosadh amháin i "
"samhail a úsáideann oidhreacht il-tábla."

msgid ""
":meth:`Model.delete() <django.db.models.Model.delete>` "
"and :meth:`QuerySet.delete() <django.db.models.query.QuerySet.delete>` "
"return the number of objects deleted."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.delete>:meth: `Model.delete () `agus:meth: "
"<django.db.models.Model.delete>`QuerySet.delete ()` cuir ar ais líon na "
"rudaí a scriosadh."

msgid ""
"Added a system check to prevent defining both ``Meta.ordering`` and "
"``order_with_respect_to`` on the same model."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh seiceáil córais leis chun cosc a chur ar ``Meta.Ordering`` agus "
"``order_with_respect_to`` araon a shainiú ar an tsamhail chéanna."

msgid ""
":lookup:`Date and time <year>` lookups can be chained with other lookups "
"(such as :lookup:`exact`, :lookup:`gt`, :lookup:`lt`, etc.). For example: "
"``Entry.objects.filter(pub_date__month__gt=6)``."
msgstr ""
":lookup: Is <year>féidir cuardaigh `Dáta agus am `a shlánú le cuardaigh eile "
"(mar shampla:lookup: `exact`, :lookup: `gt`, :lookup: `lt`, srl.). Mar "
"shampla: ``Entry.Objects.filter (pub_date__month__gt=6) ``."

msgid ""
"Time lookups (hour, minute, second) are now supported "
"by :class:`~django.db.models.TimeField` for all database backends. Support "
"for backends other than SQLite was added but undocumented in Django 1.7."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn le cuardaigh ama (uair an chloig, nóiméad, dara) anois ó:class: "
"`~django.db.models.timefield` do gach cúltaca bunachar sonraí. Cuireadh "
"tacaíocht do chúltaca seachas SQLite leis ach gan doiciméadú i Django 1.7."

msgid ""
"You can specify the ``output_field`` parameter of "
"the :class:`~django.db.models.Avg` aggregate in order to aggregate over non-"
"numeric columns, such as ``DurationField``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an paraiméadar ``output_field`` den chomhiomlán: class: "
"`~django.db.models.avg` a shonrú d'fhonn comhiomlán a chomhiomlánú thar "
"cholúin neamh-uimhriúla, mar shampla ``DurationField``."

msgid ""
"Added the :lookup:`date` lookup to :class:`~django.db.models.DateTimeField` "
"to allow querying the field by only the date portion."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an cuardach: lookup: `dáta` chuig:: class: "
"`~django.db.models.DateTimeField` chun cead a dhéanamh ar an réimse a "
"fhiosrú faoin gcuid dáta amháin."

msgid ""
"Added the :class:`~django.db.models.functions.Greatest` "
"and :class:`~django.db.models.functions.Least` database functions."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh feidhmeanna bunachar sonraí:: class: "
"`~django.db.models.functions.greatest` agus:class: "
"`~django.db.models.functions.least` leis."

msgid ""
"Added the :class:`~django.db.models.functions.Now` database function, which "
"returns the current date and time."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh feidhm bunachar sonraí: class: `~django.db.models.functions.now` "
"leis, a thugann an dáta agus an t-am reatha ar ais."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.db.models.Transform` is now a subclass of :ref:`Func() <func-"
"expressions>` which allows ``Transform``\\s to be used on the right hand "
"side of an expression, just like regular ``Func``\\s. This allows "
"registering some database functions "
"like :class:`~django.db.models.functions.Length`, :class:`~django.db.models.functions.Lower`, "
"and :class:`~django.db.models.functions.Upper` as transforms."
msgstr ""
":class: `~Django.db.Models.Transform` anois fo-aicme de:ref: `Func () `a "
"cheadaíonn ``Transform``\\ s a úsáid <func-expressions>ar thaobh na láimhe "
"deise de abairt, díreach cosúil le `Func``\\ s rialta. Ceadaíonn sé seo "
"roinnt feidhmeanna bunachar sonraí cosúil:class: "
"`~Django.db.Models.functions.Length`, :class: `~Django.db.Models.Length` "
"GO.DB.Models.Functions.Lower`, agus:class: "
"`~Django.db.Models.Functions.Upper` mar athruithe."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.db.models.SlugField` now accepts "
"an :attr:`~django.db.models.SlugField.allow_unicode` argument to allow "
"Unicode characters in slugs."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.db.models.slugfield` anois glacann argóint an:attr: "
"`~django.db.models.slugfield.allow_unicode` argóint chun carachtair Unicode "
"a cheadú i slugs."

msgid "Added support for referencing annotations in ``QuerySet.distinct()``."
msgstr "Tacaíocht bhreise chun anótaí a thagairt i ``QuerySet.Distinct () ``."

msgid ""
"``connection.queries`` shows queries with substituted parameters on SQLite."
msgstr ""
"Taispeánann ``connection.queries`` ceisteanna le paraiméadair ionadaithe ar "
"SQLite."

msgid ""
":doc:`Query expressions </ref/models/expressions>` can now be used when "
"creating new model instances using ``save()``, ``create()``, and "
"``bulk_create()``."
msgstr ""
":doc: Is féidir `abairtí fiosraitheach` a úsáid </ref/models/expressions> "
"anois agus cásanna samhail nua á gcruthú ag baint úsáide as ``save () ``, "
"`create ()``, agus ``bulk_create () ``."

msgid ""
"Unless :attr:`HttpResponse.reason_phrase "
"<django.http.HttpResponse.reason_phrase>` is explicitly set, it now is "
"determined by the current value of :attr:`HttpResponse.status_code "
"<django.http.HttpResponse.status_code>`. Modifying the value of "
"``status_code`` outside of the constructor will also modify the value of "
"``reason_phrase``."
msgstr ""
"<django.http.HttpResponse.status_code>Unless:attr: Tá "
"`HttpResponse.Reason_frase "
"<django.http.HttpResponse.reason_phrase>`socraithe go sainráite, socraítear "
"é anois ag an luach reatha de:attr: `HttpResponse.STATUS_CODE`. Athrófar "
"luach ``status_code`` lasmuigh den tógálaí luach ``réasúna_frase`` freisin."

msgid "The debug view now shows details of chained exceptions on Python 3."
msgstr ""
"Taispeánann an dearcadh dífhabhtaithe sonraí faoi eisceachtaí slabhraithe ar "
"Python 3 anois."

msgid ""
"The default 40x error views now accept a second positional parameter, the "
"exception that triggered the view."
msgstr ""
"Glacann na tuairimí earráide réamhshocraithe 40x leis an dara paraiméadar "
"suímh anois, an eisceacht a spreag an radharc."

msgid ""
"View error handlers now "
"support :class:`~django.template.response.TemplateResponse`, commonly used "
"with class-based views."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn láimhseálaithe earráide féach anois:class: "
"`~django.template.response.templateResponse`, a úsáidtear go coitianta le "
"tuairimí rang-bhunaithe."

msgid ""
"Exceptions raised by the ``render()`` method are now passed to the "
"``process_exception()`` method of each middleware."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear eisceachtaí a ardaítear leis an modh ``render () ``anois chuig modh "
"``process_exception ()`` de gach middleware."

msgid ""
"Request middleware can now set :attr:`HttpRequest.urlconf "
"<django.http.HttpRequest.urlconf>` to ``None`` to revert any changes made by "
"previous middleware and return to using the :setting:`ROOT_URLCONF`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir iarratas a dhéanamh anois:attr: `HttpRequest.urlconf "
"<django.http.HttpRequest.urlconf>`go ``None`` chun aon athruithe a rinne "
"middleware roimhe seo a chur ar ais agus filleadh ar an: setting: "
"`ROOT_URLCONF` a úsáid."

msgid ""
"The :setting:`DISALLOWED_USER_AGENTS` check "
"in :class:`~django.middleware.common.CommonMiddleware` now raises "
"a :class:`~django.core.exceptions.PermissionDenied` exception as opposed to "
"returning an :class:`~django.http.HttpResponseForbidden` so "
"that :data:`~django.conf.urls.handler403` is invoked."
msgstr ""
"Ardaíonn an seiceála:SETTING: `DISALLOWED_USER_AGENTS` eisceacht in:class: "
"`~django.middleware.commonMiddleware` anois: a:class: "
"`~django.core.exceptions.permissiondenied` seachas filleadh ara:class: "
"`~django.http.http.httpresponsedden` ionas ionas go ndéan:data: "
"`~django.conf.forbid.conf.Iarraítear ar .urls.handler403`."

msgid ""
"Added :meth:`HttpRequest.get_port() <django.http.HttpRequest.get_port>` to "
"fetch the originating port of the request."
msgstr ""
"<django.http.HttpRequest.get_port>Cuireadh leis: Meth: `HttpRequest.get_port "
"() `chun calafort tionscnaimh an iarratais a fháil."

msgid ""
"Added the ``json_dumps_params`` parameter "
"to :class:`~django.http.JsonResponse` to allow passing keyword arguments to "
"the ``json.dumps()`` call used to generate the response."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an paraiméadar ``json_dumps_params`` chuig: class: "
"`~django.http.jsonResponse` chun argóintí eochairfhocal a chur chuig an "
"nglao ``json.dumps () ``a úsáidtear chun an freagra a ghiniúint."

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.middleware.common.BrokenLinkEmailsMiddleware` now "
"ignores 404s when the referer is equal to the requested URL. To circumvent "
"the empty referer check already implemented, some web bots set the referer "
"to the requested URL."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an :class:`~django.middleware.common.BrokenLinkEmailsMiddleware` "
"neamhaird anois ar 404anna nuair a bhíonn an moltóir cothrom leis an URL "
"iarrtha. Chun dul timpeall ar an tseiceáil atreoraithe folamh a cuireadh i "
"bhfeidhm cheana féin, shocraigh roinnt róbónna gréasáin an tagróir chuig an "
"URL iarrtha."

msgid ""
"Template tags created with the :meth:`~django.template.Library.simple_tag` "
"helper can now store results in a template variable by using the ``as`` "
"argument."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le clibeanna teimpléad a cruthaíodh leis an gcúntóir: meth: "
"`~django.template.library.simple_tag` torthaí a stóráil anois in athróg "
"teimpléad tríd an argóint ``as ``a úsáid."

msgid ""
"Added a :meth:`Context.setdefault() <django.template.Context.setdefault>` "
"method."
msgstr ""
"<django.template.Context.setdefault>Cuireadh: meth leis: `Context.setDefault "
"() `modh."

msgid ""
"The :ref:`django.template <django-template-logger>` logger was added and "
"includes the following messages:"
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh <django-template-logger>logger:ref: `django.template `leis agus tá "
"na teachtaireachtaí seo a leanas ann:"

msgid "A ``DEBUG`` level message for missing context variables."
msgstr ""
"Teachtaireacht leibhéal ``DEBUG` le haghaidh athróga comhthéacs atá in "
"easnamh."

msgid ""
"A ``WARNING`` level message for uncaught exceptions raised during the "
"rendering of an ``{% include %}`` when debug mode is off (helpful since ``{% "
"include %}`` silences the exception and returns an empty string)."
msgstr ""
"Teachtaireacht leibhéal `RABHADH ``d'eisceachtaí gan ghabháil a ardaíodh le "
"linn rindreáil`` {% include%} ``nuair a bhíonn modh dífhabhtaithe as "
"(cabhrach ós rud é go gcuireann`` {% include%} ``an eisceacht a thostaíonn "
"agus cuireann sé sreang folamh ar ais)."

msgid ""
"The :ttag:`firstof` template tag supports storing the output in a variable "
"using 'as'."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn an chlib teimpléad: ttag: `firstof` leis an aschur a stóráil in "
"athróg ag baint úsáide as 'as'."

msgid ""
":meth:`Context.update() <django.template.Context.update>` can now be used as "
"a context manager."
msgstr ""
":meth: Is féidir `Context.update () <django.template.Context.update>`a úsáid "
"anois mar bhainisteoir comhthéacs."

msgid "Django template loaders can now extend templates recursively."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le lódóirí teimpléid Django teimpléid a shíneadh go hathchúrsach "
"anois."

msgid ""
"The debug page template postmortem now include output from each engine that "
"is installed."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn an teimpléad leathanaigh dífhabhtaithe post mortem anois aschur ó "
"gach inneall atá suiteáilte."

msgid ""
":ref:`Debug page integration <template-debug-integration>` for custom "
"template engines was added."
msgstr ""
":ref: Cuireadh 'comhtháthú leathanaigh dífhabht <template-debug-"
"integration>'le haghaidh innill teimpléad saincheaptha leis."

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.template.backends.django.DjangoTemplates` backend gained "
"the ability to register libraries and builtins explicitly through the "
"template :setting:`OPTIONS <TEMPLATES-OPTIONS>`."
msgstr ""
"<TEMPLATES-OPTIONS>Fuair an cúltaca: Class: "
"`~django.template.backends.django.djangoTemplates` an cumas leabharlanna "
"agus tógáin a chlárú go sainráite tríd an teimpléad:setting: `OPTIONS `."

msgid ""
"The ``timesince`` and ``timeuntil`` filters were improved to deal with leap "
"years when given large time spans."
msgstr ""
"Feabhsaíodh na scagairí ``timesince`` agus ``timeuntil`` chun déileáil le "
"blianta léim nuair a thugtar spaitheanna móra ama."

msgid ""
"The ``include`` tag now caches parsed templates objects during template "
"rendering, speeding up reuse in places such as for loops."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an chlib `san áireamh ``rudaí teimpléid pháirseáilte anois le linn "
"rindreála teimpléid, ag luasú athúsáide in áiteanna mar lúb."

msgid ""
"Added the :meth:`json() <django.test.Response.json>` method to test client "
"responses to give access to the response body as JSON."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an modh: meth: `json () <django.test.Response.json>`leis chun "
"freagraí cliant a thástáil chun rochtain a thabhairt ar an gcomhlacht "
"freagartha mar JSON."

msgid ""
"Added the :meth:`~django.test.Client.force_login()` method to the test "
"client. Use this method to simulate the effect of a user logging into the "
"site while skipping the authentication and verification steps "
"of :meth:`~django.test.Client.login()`."
msgstr ""
"Chuir an modh: meth: `~django.test.client.force_login () `leis an gcliant "
"tástála. Úsáid an modh seo chun an éifeacht a bhaineann le húsáideoir logáil "
"isteach ar an suíomh a insamhail agus na céimeanna fíordheimhnithe agus "
"fíoraithe ag scipeáil de:meth: `~django.test.client.login () `."

msgid ""
"Regular expression lookaround assertions are now allowed in URL patterns."
msgstr "Ceadaítear dearbhú rialta breatharound abairt anois i bpatrúin URL."

msgid ""
"The application namespace can now be set using an ``app_name`` attribute on "
"the included module or object. It can also be set by passing a 2-tuple of "
"(<list of patterns>, <application namespace>) as the first argument to "
"``include()``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir spás ainmneacha an fheidhmchláir a shocrú anois ag baint úsáide as "
"tréith ``app_name`` ar an modúl nó an réad san áireamh. Is féidir é a shocrú "
"freisin trí dhá thúpla de (<list of patterns>,<application namespace>) a "
"rith mar an chéad argóint chun ``include () ``."

msgid "System checks have been added for common URL pattern mistakes."
msgstr "Cuireadh seiceálacha córais le haghaidh botúin patrún URL coitianta."

msgid ""
"Added :func:`django.core.validators.int_list_validator` to generate "
"validators of strings containing integers separated with a custom character."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh leis: func: `django.core.validators.int_list_validator` chun "
"bailíochtóirí teaghráin a ghiniúint ina bhfuil sláimhreacha scartha le "
"carachtar saincheaptha."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.core.validators.EmailValidator` now limits the length of "
"domain name labels to 63 characters per :rfc:`1034`."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.core.validators.emailValidator` teorann anois fad na lipéid "
"ainm fearainn go 63 carachtar per:rfc: `1034`."

msgid ""
"Added :func:`~django.core.validators.validate_unicode_slug` to validate "
"slugs that may contain Unicode characters."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh leis: func: `~django.core.validators.validate_unicode_slug` chun "
"slugs a bhféadfadh carachtair Unicode a bheith ina mbailíochtú."

msgid "Backwards incompatible changes in 1.9"
msgstr "Athruithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha ar ais i 1.9"

msgid ""
"In addition to the changes outlined in this section, be sure to review "
"the :ref:`removed-features-1.9` for the features that have reached the end "
"of their deprecation cycle and therefore been removed. If you haven't "
"updated your code within the deprecation timeline for a given feature, its "
"removal may appear as a backwards incompatible change."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith leis na hathruithe a leagtar amach sa chuid seo, déan cinnte "
"athbhreithniú a dhéanamh ar:ref: `removed-features-1.9` do na gnéithe a "
"shroich deireadh a dtimthriall díghabhála agus dá bhrí sin baineadh. Mura "
"ndearna tú do chód a nuashonrú laistigh den amlíne díscoilte do ghné ar "
"leith, d'fhéadfadh go mbeadh a bhaint mar athrú neamh-chomhoiriúnach ar chúl."

msgid ""
"A couple of new tests rely on the ability of the backend to introspect "
"column defaults (returning the result as ``Field.default``). You can set the "
"``can_introspect_default`` database feature to ``False`` if your backend "
"doesn't implement this. You may want to review the implementation on the "
"backends that Django includes for reference (:ticket:`24245`)."
msgstr ""
"Braitheann cúpla tástáil nua ar chumas an chúltaca réamhshocruithe colún a "
"ionchur (an toradh a thabhairt ar ais mar `Field.default'). Is féidir leat "
"an ghné bunachar sonraí ``can_introspect_default`` a shocrú go ``False`` "
"mura gcuireann do chúltaca seo i bhfeidhm. B'fhéidir gur mhaith leat "
"athbhreithniú a dhéanamh ar an gcur chun feidhme ar na cúltaca a chuimsíonn "
"Django le haghaidh tagartha (:ticket: `24245 `)."

msgid ""
"Registering a global adapter or converter at the level of the DB-API module "
"to handle time zone information of :class:`~datetime.datetime` values passed "
"as query parameters or returned as query results on databases that don't "
"support time zones is discouraged. It can conflict with other libraries."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear cuibheoir nó tiontaire domhanda a chlárú ag leibhéal an mhodúil DB-"
"API chun faisnéis chrios ama a láimhseáil de:class: `~datetime.datetime` "
"luachanna a rith mar pharaiméadair cheisteanna nó a chuirtear ar ais mar "
"thorthaí fiosrúcháin ar bhunachar sonraí nach dtacaíonn le criosanna ama. "
"Féadann sé coinbhleacht le leabharlanna eile."

msgid ""
"The recommended way to add a time zone to :class:`~datetime.datetime` values "
"fetched from the database is to register a converter for ``DateTimeField`` "
"in ``DatabaseOperations.get_db_converters()``."
msgstr ""
"Is é an bealach a mholtar chun crios ama a chur chuig:class: "
"`~datetime.datetime` luachanna a fhaightear ón mbunachar sonraí ná tiontaire "
"a chlárú do `DateTimeField`` i `DatabaseOperations.get_DB_Converters () ``."

msgid ""
"The ``needs_datetime_string_cast`` database feature was removed. Database "
"backends that set it must register a converter instead, as explained above."
msgstr ""
"Baineadh an ghné bunachar sonraí `needs_datetime_string_cast``. Caithfidh "
"cúltaca bunachar sonraí a leagann sé tiontaire a chlárú ina ionad sin, mar a "
"mhínítear thuas."

msgid ""
"The ``DatabaseOperations.value_to_db_<type>()`` methods were renamed to "
"``adapt_<type>field_value()`` to mirror the ``convert_<type>field_value()`` "
"methods."
msgstr ""
"<type><type>Athainmníodh na modhanna ``databaseOperations.value_to_db_ "
"<type>() ``go ``adapt_ field_value ()`` chun na modhanna ``convert_ "
"field_value () ``a scáthú."

msgid ""
"To use the new ``date`` lookup, third-party database backends may need to "
"implement the ``DatabaseOperations.datetime_cast_date_sql()`` method."
msgstr ""
"Chun an cuardach nua ``dáta ``a úsáid, b'fhéidir go mbeidh ar chúltaca "
"bunachar sonraí tríú páirtí an modh`` "
"DatabaseOperations.DateTime_Cast_Date_SQL () ``a chur i bhfeidhm."

msgid ""
"The ``DatabaseOperations.time_extract_sql()`` method was added. It calls the "
"existing ``date_extract_sql()`` method. This method is overridden by the "
"SQLite backend to add time lookups (hour, minute, second) "
"to :class:`~django.db.models.TimeField`, and may be needed by third-party "
"database backends."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an modh ``DatabaseOperations.TIME_EXTRACT_SQL ()`` leis. Glaonn sé "
"an modh ``date_extract_sql () `atá ann cheana. Cuireann an cúltaca SQLite ar "
"an modh seo chun cuardaigh ama (uair an chloig, nóiméad, dara) a chur chuig: "
"class: `~Django.db.Models.TimeField`, agus d'fhéadfadh go mbeadh gá le "
"cúltaca bunachar sonraí tríú páirtí uaidh."

msgid ""
"The ``DatabaseOperations.datetime_cast_sql()`` method (not to be confused "
"with ``DatabaseOperations.datetime_cast_date_sql()`` mentioned above) has "
"been removed. This method served to format dates on Oracle long before 1.0, "
"but hasn't been overridden by any core backend in years and hasn't been "
"called anywhere in Django's code or tests."
msgstr ""
"Tá an modh ``DatabaseOperations.DateTime_Cast_SQL () `(gan a mheascadh le`` "
"DatabaseOperations.DateTime_Cast_Date_SQL ()` luaitear thuas) baineadh. "
"D'fhreastail an modh seo chun dátaí a fhormáidiú ar Oracle i bhfad roimh "
"1.0, ach níor sháraigh aon chúltaca croí é le blianta agus níor ghlaoigh sé "
"áit ar bith i gcód nó i dtástálacha Django."

msgid ""
"In order to support test parallelization, you must implement the "
"``DatabaseCreation._clone_test_db()`` method and set "
"``DatabaseFeatures.can_clone_databases = True``. You may have to adjust "
"``DatabaseCreation.get_test_db_clone_settings()``."
msgstr ""
"D'fhonn tacú le comhthreomhaíocht tástála, ní mór duit an ``DatabaseCreation "
"a chur i bhfeidhm. Modh _clone_test_db () ``agus socraigh "
"``databaseFeatures.can_Clone_Databases = True``. B'fhéidir go mbeidh ort "
"``Databasecreation.get_test_db_clone_settings ()`` a choigeartú."

msgid "Default settings that were tuples are now lists"
msgstr "Is liostaí anois iad socruithe réamhshocraithe a bhí ina tuples"

msgid ""
"The default settings in ``django.conf.global_settings`` were a combination "
"of lists and tuples. All settings that were formerly tuples are now lists."
msgstr ""
"Ba iad na socruithe réamhshocraithe i `django.conf.global_settings`` meascán "
"de liostaí agus tuples. Is liostaí anois iad na socruithe go léir a bhí "
"tuples roimhe seo."

msgid "``is_usable`` attribute on template loaders is removed"
msgstr "Baintear tréith ``is_usable`` ar luchtaitheoirí teimpléad"

msgid ""
"Django template loaders previously required an ``is_usable`` attribute to be "
"defined. If a loader was configured in the template settings and this "
"attribute was ``False``, the loader would be silently ignored. In practice, "
"this was only used by the egg loader to detect if ``setuptools`` was "
"installed. The ``is_usable`` attribute is now removed and the egg loader "
"instead fails at runtime if ``setuptools`` is not installed."
msgstr ""
"D'éilíodh luchtóirí teimpléad Django roimhe seo tréith ``is_usable`` a "
"shainiú. Dá mbeadh lódóir cumraithe i socruithe na teimpléid agus dá mbeadh "
"an tréith seo `False``, déanfaí neamhaird ar an lódóir go ciúin. Go "
"praiticiúil, níor úsáid an lódóir uibheacha é seo ach chun a bhrath an raibh "
"“setuptools” suiteáilte. Baintear an tréith ``is_usable`` anois agus ina "
"ionad sin teipeann ar an lódóir uibheacha ag am rith mura bhfuil "
"`setuptools` suiteáilte."

msgid "Related set direct assignment"
msgstr "Socrú díreach gaolmhar"

msgid ""
"Direct assignment of related objects in the ORM used to perform a "
"``clear()`` followed by a call to ``add()``. This caused needlessly large "
"data changes and prevented using "
"the :data:`~django.db.models.signals.m2m_changed` signal to track individual "
"changes in many-to-many relations."
msgstr ""
"Sannadh díreach rudaí gaolmhara san ORM a úsáidtear chun ``clear () ``a "
"dhéanamh ina dhiaidh sin glao ar ``add ()``. Ba chúis leis seo athruithe "
"móra sonraí gan ghá agus chuir sé cosc ar an gcomhartha: data: "
"`~django.db.models.signals.m2m_changed` a úsáid chun athruithe aonair i "
"gcaidreamh go leor a rianú."

msgid ""
"Direct assignment now relies on the "
"new :meth:`~django.db.models.fields.related.RelatedManager.set` method on "
"related managers which by default only processes changes between the "
"existing related set and the one that's newly assigned. The previous "
"behavior can be restored by replacing direct assignment by a call to "
"``set()`` with the keyword argument ``clear=True``."
msgstr ""
"Braitheann sannadh díreach anois ar an modh nua:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.fields.related.relatedManager.set` ar bhainisteoirí "
"gaolmhara nach ndéanann ach athruithe a phróiseáil de réir réamhshocraithe "
"idir an tacar gaolmhar atá ann cheana agus an ceann atá nua-shannta. Is "
"féidir an t-iompar roimhe seo a athbhunú trí shannadh díreach a athsholáthar "
"trí ghlao chuig `set () ``leis an argóint eochairfhocal ``Clear=True``."

msgid ""
"``ModelForm``, and therefore ``ModelAdmin``, internally rely on direct "
"assignment for many-to-many relations and as a consequence now use the new "
"behavior."
msgstr ""
"Tá ``ModelForm”, agus dá bhrí sin ``ModelAdmin`, ag brath go hinmheánach ar "
"shannadh díreach le haghaidh caidrimh go leor agus mar thoradh air sin bain "
"úsáid as an iompar nua anois."

msgid "Filesystem-based template loaders catch more specific exceptions"
msgstr ""
"Glacann lódálaithe teimpléad bunaithe ar chóras comhaid eisceachtaí níos "
"sonracha"

msgid ""
"When using the :class:`filesystem.Loader "
"<django.template.loaders.filesystem.Loader>` "
"or :class:`app_directories.Loader "
"<django.template.loaders.app_directories.Loader>` template loaders, earlier "
"versions of Django raised a :exc:`~django.template.TemplateDoesNotExist` "
"error if a template source existed but was unreadable. This could happen "
"under many circumstances, such as if Django didn't have permissions to open "
"the file, or if the template source was a directory. Now, Django only "
"silences the exception if the template source does not exist. All other "
"situations result in the original ``IOError`` being raised."
msgstr ""
"Agus luchtóirí teimpléad:class: `FileSystem.loader "
"<django.template.loaders.filesystem.Loader>`nó:class: "
"`App_Directories.Loader` á "
"úsáid<django.template.loaders.app_directories.Loader>, d'ardaigh leaganacha "
"níos luaithe de Django earráid a:exc: "
"`~django.template.templateDoesNotExist` má bhí foinse teimpléad ann ach nach "
"raibh sé inléite. D'fhéadfadh sé seo tarlú faoi go leor imthosca, mar "
"shampla mura raibh ceadanna ag Django chun an comhad a oscailt, nó más "
"eolaire é foinse an teimpléid. Anois, ní thostaíonn Django ach an eisceacht "
"mura bhfuil an fhoinse teimpléid ann. Mar thoradh ar gach cás eile go n-"
"ardaítear an ``Ioerror` bunaidh."

msgid "HTTP redirects no longer forced to absolute URIs"
msgstr "Ní chuirtear iallach ar atreoruithe HTTP a thuilleadh chuig URIanna"

msgid ""
"Relative redirects are no longer converted to absolute URIs. :rfc:`2616` "
"required the ``Location`` header in redirect responses to be an absolute "
"URI, but it has been superseded by :rfc:`7231` which allows relative URIs in "
"``Location``, recognizing the actual practice of user agents, almost all of "
"which support them."
msgstr ""
"Ní thiontaítear atreoruithe coibhneasta go URIs iomlána a thuilleadh. :rfc: "
"D'éilíonn `2616` go mbeadh an ceannteideal ``Suíomh ``i bhfreagraí "
"atreoraithe ina URI iomlán, ach cuireadh in ionad aith:rfc: `7231` a "
"cheadaíonn URIs coibhneasta i ``Suíomh``, ag aithint cleachtas iarbhír "
"gníomhairí úsáideora, a thacaíonn beagnach gach ceann acu leo."

msgid ""
"Consequently, the expected URLs passed to ``assertRedirects`` should "
"generally no longer include the scheme and domain part of the URLs. For "
"example, ``self.assertRedirects(response, 'http://testserver/some-url/')`` "
"should be replaced by ``self.assertRedirects(response, '/some-url/')`` "
"(unless the redirection specifically contained an absolute URL)."
msgstr ""
"Dá bhrí sin, níor cheart go ginearálta go n-áireofaí sna URLanna ionchais a "
"cuireadh ar aghaidh chuig ``asertRedirects`` an scéim agus an chuid fearainn "
"de na URLanna a thuilleadh. Mar shampla, ba cheart `` "
"self.assertRedirects(response, '/ some-url/')`` (mura rud é bhí URL iomlán "
"go sonrach san atreorú)."

msgid ""
"In the rare case that you need the old behavior (discovered with an ancient "
"version of Apache with ``mod_scgi`` that interprets a relative redirect as "
"an \"internal redirect\"), you can restore it by writing a custom "
"middleware::"
msgstr ""
"Sa chás annamh go dteastaíonn an sean-iompar uait (a aimsíodh le leagan ársa "
"de Apache le `mod_scgi`` a léirmhíníonn atreorú coibhneasta mar “atreorú "
"inmheánach”), is féidir leat é a chur ar ais trí mheán saincheaptha a "
"scríobh:"

msgid "Dropped support for PostgreSQL 9.0"
msgstr "Tacaíocht titim do PostgreSQL 9.0"

msgid ""
"Upstream support for PostgreSQL 9.0 ended in September 2015. As a "
"consequence, Django 1.9 sets 9.1 as the minimum PostgreSQL version it "
"officially supports."
msgstr ""
"Tháinig deireadh le tacaíocht suas srutha do PostgreSQL 9.0 i Meán Fómhair "
"2015. Mar thoradh air sin, socraíonn Django 1.9 9.1 mar an leagan íosta "
"PostgreSQL a thacaíonn sé go hoifigiúil."

msgid "Dropped support for Oracle 11.1"
msgstr "Tacaíocht titim do Oracle 11.1"

msgid ""
"Upstream support for Oracle 11.1 ended in August 2015. As a consequence, "
"Django 1.9 sets 11.2 as the minimum Oracle version it officially supports."
msgstr ""
"Tháinig deireadh le tacaíocht suas srutha do Oracle 11.1 i mí Lúnasa 2015. "
"Mar thoradh air sin, socraíonn Django 1.9 11.2 mar an leagan íosta Oracle a "
"thacaíonn sé go hoifigiúil."

msgid "Bulk behavior of ``add()`` method of related managers"
msgstr "Iompar mórchóir modh `add () ``bainisteoirí gaolmhara"

msgid ""
"To improve performance, the ``add()`` methods of the related managers "
"created by ``ForeignKey`` and ``GenericForeignKey`` changed from a series of "
"``Model.save()`` calls to a single ``QuerySet.update()`` call. The change "
"means that ``pre_save`` and ``post_save`` signals aren't sent anymore. You "
"can use the ``bulk=False`` keyword argument to revert to the previous "
"behavior."
msgstr ""
"Chun feidhmíocht a fheabhsú, d'athraigh modhanna `add () ``na mbainisteoirí "
"gaolmhara a chruthaigh ``ForeignKey`` agus `GenericForeignKey`` ó shraith "
"glaonna ``Model.save ()`` chuig glao ``QuerySet.Update () ``amháin. "
"Ciallaíonn an t-athrú nach seoltar comharthaí ``pre_save`` agus "
"``post_save`` níos mó. Is féidir leat an argóint eochairfhocal "
"``Bulk=False`` a úsáid chun filleadh ar an iompar roimhe seo."

msgid "Template ``LoaderOrigin`` and ``StringOrigin`` are removed"
msgstr "Baintear teimpléad ``LoaderOrigin`` agus ``StringOrigin``"

msgid ""
"In previous versions of Django, when a template engine was initialized with "
"debug as ``True``, an instance of ``django.template.loader.LoaderOrigin`` or "
"``django.template.base.StringOrigin`` was set as the origin attribute on the "
"template object. These classes have been combined "
"into :class:`~django.template.base.Origin` and is now always set regardless "
"of the engine debug setting. For a minimal level of backwards compatibility, "
"the old class names will be kept as aliases to the new ``Origin`` class "
"until Django 2.0."
msgstr ""
"I leaganacha roimhe seo de Django, nuair a cuireadh inneall teimpléad a "
"thionscnamh le dífhabhtú mar ``True``, socraíodh sampla de "
"``Django.Template.Loader.LoaderOrigin`` nó "
"``Django.Template.Base.StringOrigin`` mar an tréith bunús ar an réad "
"teimpléid. Cuireadh na ranganna seo le chéile la:class: "
"`~django.template.base.origin` agus tá sé socraithe anois i gcónaí beag "
"beann ar an socrú dífhabhtaithe innill. Le haghaidh leibhéal íosta "
"comhoiriúnachta ar ais, coimeádfar na sean-ainmneacha ranga mar ainmneacha "
"don rang nua ``Origin` go dtí Django 2.0."

msgid "Changes to the default logging configuration"
msgstr "Athruithe ar an chumraíocht logála réamhshocraithe"

msgid ""
"To make it easier to write custom logging configurations, Django's default "
"logging configuration no longer defines ``django.request`` and "
"``django.security`` loggers. Instead, it defines a single ``django`` logger, "
"filtered at the ``INFO`` level, with two handlers:"
msgstr ""
"Chun go mbeidh sé níos éasca cumraíochtaí logála saincheaptha a scríobh, ní "
"shainmhíníonn cumraíocht logála réamhshocraithe Django logálaithe "
"``django.request`` agus ``django.security`` a thuilleadh. Ina áit sin, "
"sainmhíníonn sé logálaí `django ``amháin, a scagtar ag an leibhéal ``INFO``, "
"le dhá láimhseálaí:"

msgid ""
"``console``: filtered at the ``INFO`` level and only active if "
"``DEBUG=True``."
msgstr ""
"``console``: scagtha ag an leibhéal ``INFO ``agus níomhach ach amháin má tá "
"`debug = True``."

msgid ""
"``mail_admins``: filtered at the ``ERROR`` level and only active if "
"``DEBUG=False``."
msgstr ""
"``mail_admins``: scagtha ag an leibhéal ``ERROR`` agus níomhach ach amháin "
"má tá `debug = false``."

msgid ""
"If you aren't overriding Django's default logging, you should see minimal "
"changes in behavior, but you might see some new logging to the ``runserver`` "
"console, for example."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil tú ag dul i bhfeidhm ar logáil réamhshocraithe Django, ba cheart "
"go bhfeicfeá íosta athruithe ar iompar, ach b'fhéidir go bhfeicfidh tú "
"roinnt logáil nua chuig an gconsól ``runserver`, mar shampla."

msgid ""
"If you are overriding Django's default logging, you should check to see how "
"your configuration merges with the new defaults."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag cur i bhfeidhm ar logáil réamhshocraithe Django, ba chóir duit "
"seiceáil chun a fheiceáil conas a chumraíonn do chumraíocht leis na "
"réamhshocruithe nua."

msgid "``HttpRequest`` details in error reporting"
msgstr "Sonraí `HttpRequest ``i dtuairisciú earráide"

msgid ""
"It was redundant to display the full details of "
"the :class:`~django.http.HttpRequest` each time it appeared as a stack frame "
"variable in the HTML version of the debug page and error email. Thus, the "
"HTTP request will now display the same standard representation as other "
"variables (``repr(request)``). As a result, the "
"``ExceptionReporterFilter.get_request_repr()`` method and the undocumented "
"``django.http.build_request_repr()`` function were removed."
msgstr ""
"Bhí sé iomarcach na sonraí iomlána fao:class: `~django.http.httpRequest` a "
"thaispeáint gach uair a bhí sé le feiceáil mar athróg fráma cruach sa leagan "
"HTML den leathanach dífhabhtaithe agus ríomhphost earráide. Dá bhrí sin, "
"taispeánfaidh an t-iarratas HTTP an léiriú caighdeánach céanna anois le "
"hathróga eile (``repr (iarratas) ``). Mar thoradh air sin, baineadh an modh "
"``ExceptionReporterFilter.get_request_repr () ``agus an fheidhm "
"``django.http.build_request_repr ()`` neamhdhoiciméadaithe."

msgid ""
"The contents of the text version of the email were modified to provide a "
"traceback of the same structure as in the case of AJAX requests. The "
"traceback details are rendered by the "
"``ExceptionReporter.get_traceback_text()`` method."
msgstr ""
"Athraíodh ábhar leagan téacs an ríomhphoist chun rianú den struchtúr céanna "
"a sholáthar agus i gcás iarratais AJAX. Déantar na sonraí rianaithe a léiriú "
"ag an modh ``ExceptionReporter.get_TraceBack_Text () ``."

msgid "Removal of time zone aware global adapters and converters for datetimes"
msgstr ""
"Cuibheoirí agus tiontairí domhanda atá ar an eolas ar chrios ama a bhaint "
"d'amanna dáta"

msgid ""
"Django no longer registers global adapters and converters for managing time "
"zone information on :class:`~datetime.datetime` values sent to the database "
"as query parameters or read from the database in query results. This change "
"affects projects that meet all the following conditions:"
msgstr ""
"Ní chláraíonn Django oiriúntóirí agus tiontairí domhanda a thuilleadh chun "
"faisnéis crios ama a bhainistiú ar:rang: `~ datetime.datetime` luachanna a "
"chuirtear chuig an mbunachar sonraí mar pharaiméadair fiosrúcháin nó a "
"léitear ón mbunachar sonraí i dtorthaí fiosrúcháin. Bíonn tionchar ag an "
"athrú seo ar thionscadail a chomhlíonann na coinníollacha seo a leanas go "
"léir:"

msgid "The :setting:`USE_TZ` setting is ``True``."
msgstr "Is é an socrú: `USE_TZ` ``True``."

msgid ""
"The database is SQLite, MySQL, Oracle, or a third-party database that "
"doesn't support time zones. In doubt, you can check the value of "
"``connection.features.supports_timezones``."
msgstr ""
"Is é an bunachar sonraí SQLite, MySQL, Oracle, nó bunachar sonraí tríú "
"páirtí nach dtacaíonn le criosanna ama. Ar amhras, is féidir leat luach "
"``connection.features.supports_timezones`` a sheiceáil."

msgid ""
"The code queries the database outside of the ORM, typically with "
"``cursor.execute(sql, params)``."
msgstr ""
"Fiosraíonn an cód an bunachar sonraí lasmuigh den ORM, de ghnáth le "
"``cursor.execute (sql, params) ``."

msgid ""
"If you're passing aware :class:`~datetime.datetime` parameters to such "
"queries, you should turn them into naive datetimes in UTC::"
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag dul paraiméadair aware:class: `~datetime.datetime` chuig "
"ceisteanna den sórt sin, ba cheart duit iad a iompú ina dáta naif i UTC::"

msgid ""
"If you fail to do so, the conversion will be performed as in earlier "
"versions (with a deprecation warning) up until Django 1.11. Django 2.0 won't "
"perform any conversion, which may result in data corruption."
msgstr ""
"Má theipeann ort é sin a dhéanamh, déanfar an tiontú mar a bhí i leaganacha "
"níos luaithe (le rabhadh díghníomhaíochta) suas go dtí Django 1.11. Ní "
"dhéanfaidh Django 2.0 aon chomhshó, rud a d'fhéadfadh éilliú sonraí a bheith "
"mar thoradh air."

msgid ""
"If you're reading :class:`~datetime.datetime` values from the results, they "
"will be naive instead of aware. You can compensate as follows::"
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag léamh luachanna: class: `~datetime.datetime` ó na torthaí, beidh "
"siad naif in ionad a bheith ar an eolas. Is féidir leat cúiteamh mar seo a "
"leanas:"

msgid ""
"You don't need any of this if you're querying the database through the ORM, "
"even if you're using :meth:`raw() <django.db.models.query.QuerySet.raw>` "
"queries. The ORM takes care of managing time zone information."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.raw>Ní theastaíonn aon cheann de seo uait "
"má tá tú ag fiosrú ar an mbunachar sonraí tríd an ORM, fiú má tá ceisteanna: "
"meth: `raw () `á úsáid agat. Tugann an ORM aire d'fhaisnéis crios ama a "
"bhainistiú."

msgid "Template tag modules are imported when templates are configured"
msgstr "Allmhairítear modúil clibeanna teimpléid nuair a dhéantar teimpl"

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.template.backends.django.DjangoTemplates` backend now "
"performs discovery on installed template tag modules when instantiated. This "
"update enables libraries to be provided explicitly via the ``'libraries'`` "
"key of :setting:`OPTIONS <TEMPLATES-OPTIONS>` when defining "
"a :class:`~django.template.backends.django.DjangoTemplates` backend. Import "
"or syntax errors in template tag modules now fail early at instantiation "
"time rather than when a template with a :ttag:`{% load %}<load>` tag is "
"first compiled."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an cúltaca: Class: "
"`~django.template.backends.django.djangoTemplates` fionnachtain anois ar "
"mhodúil clibeanna teimpléad suiteáilte nuair a dhéantar iad a thionscnamh. "
"<TEMPLATES-OPTIONS>Cuireann an nuashonrú seo ar chumas leabharlanna a "
"sholáthar go sainráite tríd an eochair ``'libraries'` de:setting: `OPTIONS` "
"nuair a shainmhínítear a:class: "
"`~django.template.backends.django.djangoTemplates` cúltaca. Teipeann ar "
"earráidí allmhairithe nó comhréireachta i modúil clibeanna teimpléid go "
"luath anois ag am tionscnaíochta seachas nuair a dhéantar teimpléad le clib "
"a:ttag: `{% load%}<load>` a thiomsú ar dtús."

msgid "``django.template.base.add_to_builtins()`` is removed"
msgstr "``django.template.base.add_to_builtins () ``baintear"

msgid ""
"Although it was a private API, projects commonly used ``add_to_builtins()`` "
"to make template tags and filters available without using the :ttag:`{% load "
"%}<load>` tag. This API has been formalized. Projects should now define "
"built-in libraries via the ``'builtins'`` key of :setting:`OPTIONS "
"<TEMPLATES-OPTIONS>` when defining "
"a :class:`~django.template.backends.django.DjangoTemplates` backend."
msgstr ""
"<load>Cé gur API príobháideach a bhí ann, d'úsáid tionscadail go coitianta "
"``add_to_builtins () ``chun clibeanna teimpléad agus scagairí a chur ar fáil "
"gan an clibe:ttag: `{% load%}` a úsáid. Tá an API seo foirmithe. <TEMPLATES-"
"OPTIONS>Ba chóir do thionscadail leabharlanna ionsuite a shainmhíniú anois "
"tríd an eochair ```builtins'` de:setting: `OPTIONS` agus iad ag sainmhíniú "
"a:class: `~django.template.backends.django.djangoTemplates` cúltaca."

msgid "``simple_tag`` now wraps tag output in ``conditional_escape``"
msgstr ""
"Fillteann ``simple_tag ``aschur clibeanna anois i `conditional_escape``"

msgid ""
"In general, template tags do not autoescape their contents, and this "
"behavior is :ref:`documented <tags-auto-escaping>`. For tags "
"like :class:`~django.template.Library.inclusion_tag`, this is not a problem "
"because the included template will perform autoescaping. For "
"``assignment_tag()``, the output will be escaped when it is used as a "
"variable in the template."
msgstr ""
"<tags-auto-escaping>Go ginearálta, ní dhéanann clibeanna teimpléad a n-ábhar "
"go huathoibríoch, agus is é an t-iompar seo: ref: `doiciméadaithe `. Maidir "
"le clibeanna cosúil:class: `~django.template.library.inclusion_tag`, ní "
"fadhb í seo toisc go ndéanfaidh an teimpléad san áireamh autoescaping. "
"Maidir le ``assignment_tag () ``, éalófar an t-aschur nuair a úsáidtear é "
"mar athróg sa teimpléad."

msgid ""
"For the intended use cases of :class:`~django.template.Library.simple_tag`, "
"however, it is very easy to end up with incorrect HTML and possibly an XSS "
"exploit. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Maidir leis na cásanna úsáide atá beartaithe de:class: "
"`~django.template.library.simple_tag`, áfach, tá sé an-éasca deireadh a chur "
"le HTML mícheart agus b'fhéidir saothrú XSS. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"In older versions of Django, this will be an XSS issue because "
"``user.first_name`` is not escaped."
msgstr ""
"I leaganacha níos sine de Django, is saincheist XSS é seo toisc nach n-"
"éaltar ``user.first_name``."

msgid ""
"In Django 1.9, this is fixed: if the template context has "
"``autoescape=True`` set (the default), then ``simple_tag`` will wrap the "
"output of the tag function "
"with :func:`~django.utils.html.conditional_escape`."
msgstr ""
"I Django 1.9, socraítear é seo: má tá `autoescape=True`` socraithe ag "
"comhthéacs an teimpléid (an réamhshocraithe), ansin fillfidh ``simple_tag "
"``aschur na feidhme clibeanna le:func: "
"`~django.utils.html.conditional_escape`."

msgid ""
"To fix your ``simple_tag``\\s, it is best to apply the following practices:"
msgstr ""
"Chun do `simple_tag``\\ s a shocrú, is fearr na cleachtais seo a leanas a "
"chur i bhfeidhm:"

msgid ""
"Any code that generates HTML should use either the template system "
"or :func:`~django.utils.html.format_html`."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir d'aon chód a ghineann HTML an córas teimpléad nó: func: "
"`~django.utils.html.format_html` a úsáid."

msgid ""
"If the output of a ``simple_tag`` needs escaping, "
"use :func:`~django.utils.html.escape` "
"or :func:`~django.utils.html.conditional_escape`."
msgstr ""
"Má theastaíonn aschur ``simple_tag`` éalú, bain úsáid as: func: "
"`~django.utils.html.escape` nó:func: `~django.utils.html.conditional_escape`."

msgid ""
"If you are absolutely certain that you are outputting HTML from a trusted "
"source (e.g. a CMS field that stores HTML entered by admins), you can mark "
"it as such using :func:`~django.utils.safestring.mark_safe`."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú cinnte go bhfuil tú ag cur HTML ó fhoinse iontaofa (m.sh. réimse "
"CMS a stóráilíonn HTML a chuireann riarthóirí isteach), is féidir leat é a "
"mharcáil mar sin ag baint úsáid:func: `~django.utils.safestring.mark_safe`."

msgid ""
"Tags that follow these rules will be correct and safe whether they are run "
"on Django 1.9+ or earlier."
msgstr ""
"Beidh clibeanna a leanann na rialacha seo ceart agus sábháilte cibé an "
"bhfuil siad á reáchtáil ar Django 1.9+ nó níos luaithe."

msgid "``Paginator.page_range``"
msgstr "``Paginator.Page_Range``"

msgid ""
":attr:`Paginator.page_range <django.core.paginator.Paginator.page_range>` is "
"now an iterator instead of a list."
msgstr ""
":attr: Is iterator anois é `Paginator.page_range "
"<django.core.paginator.Paginator.page_range>`in ionad liosta."

msgid ""
"In versions of Django previous to 1.8, ``Paginator.page_range`` returned a "
"``list`` in Python 2 and a ``range`` in Python 3. Django 1.8 consistently "
"returned a list, but an iterator is more efficient."
msgstr ""
"I leaganacha de Django roimhe seo go 1.8, chuir `Paginator.Page_Range`` "
"``liost`` ar ais i Python 2 agus ``raon ``i Python 3. Chuir Django 1.8 "
"liosta ar ais go comhsheasmhach, ach tá iterator níos éifeachtaí."

msgid ""
"Existing code that depends on ``list`` specific features, such as indexing, "
"can be ported by converting the iterator into a ``list`` using ``list()``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an cód atá ann cheana atá ag brath ar ghnéithe sonracha ``liosta`, "
"mar shampla innéacsú, a iompar tríd an iterator a thiontú go `liosta`` ag "
"baint úsáide as ``liosta () ``."

msgid "Implicit ``QuerySet`` ``__in`` lookup removed"
msgstr "Cuardach intuigthe ```QuerySet`` ```__in`` bainte"

msgid "In earlier versions, queries such as::"
msgstr "I leaganacha níos luaithe, ceisteanna mar:"

msgid "would implicitly convert to::"
msgstr "thiontódh sé go hinchinneach go:"

msgid "resulting in SQL like ``\"related_id IN (SELECT id FROM ...)\"``."
msgstr "mar thoradh air SQL mar ``\"related_id IN (SELECT id FROM...) \"``."

msgid ""
"This implicit ``__in`` no longer happens so the \"IN\" SQL is now \"=\", and "
"if the subquery returns multiple results, at least some databases will throw "
"an error."
msgstr ""
"Ní tharlaíonn an ``__in`` intuigthe seo a thuilleadh mar sin is é an “IN” "
"SQL anois “=”, agus má fhilleann an fo-cheist torthaí iolracha, caitheoidh "
"roinnt bunachair sonraí ar a laghad earráid."

msgid "``contrib.admin`` browser support"
msgstr "Tacaíocht brabhsálaí ``contrib.admin``"

msgid ""
"The admin no longer supports Internet Explorer 8 and below, as these "
"browsers have reached end-of-life."
msgstr ""
"Ní thacaíonn an riarachán le Internet Explorer 8 agus thíos a thuilleadh, "
"mar tá deireadh saoil bainte amach ag na brabhsálaithe seo."

msgid ""
"CSS and images to support Internet Explorer 6 and 7 have been removed. PNG "
"and GIF icons have been replaced with SVG icons, which are not supported by "
"Internet Explorer 8 and earlier."
msgstr ""
"Baineadh CSS agus íomhánna chun tacú le Internet Explorer 6 agus 7. Cuireadh "
"deilbhíní SVG in ionad deilbhíní PNG agus GIF, nach dtacaíonn Internet "
"Explorer 8 agus níos luaithe leo."

msgid ""
"The jQuery library embedded in the admin has been upgraded from version "
"1.11.2 to 2.1.4. jQuery 2.x has the same API as jQuery 1.x, but does not "
"support Internet Explorer 6, 7, or 8, allowing for better performance and a "
"smaller file size. If you need to support IE8 and must also use the latest "
"version of Django, you can override the admin's copy of jQuery with your own "
"by creating a Django application with this structure:"
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh uasghrádú ar an leabharlann jQuery atá leabaithe sa riarachán ó "
"leagan 1.11.2 go 2.1.4. Tá an API céanna ag jQuery 2.x le jQuery 1.x, ach ní "
"thacaíonn sé le Internet Explorer 6, 7, nó 8, rud a cheadaíonn feidhmíocht "
"níos fearr agus méid comhaid níos lú. Más gá duit tacú le IE8 agus más gá "
"duit an leagan is déanaí de Django a úsáid freisin, is féidir leat cóip an "
"riaracháin de jQuery a shárú le do chuid féin trí fheidhmchlár Django a "
"chruthú leis an struchtúr seo:"

msgid "``SyntaxError`` when installing Django ``setuptools`` 5.5.x"
msgstr "``SyntaxError`` agus Django á shuiteáil ``setuptools`` 5.5.x"

msgid ""
"When installing Django 1.9 or 1.9.1 with ``setuptools`` 5.5.x, you'll see:"
msgstr ""
"Agus Django 1.9 nó 1.9.1 á shuiteáil agat le ``setuptools` 5.5.x, feicfidh "
"tú:"

msgid ""
"It's safe to ignore these errors (Django will still install just fine), but "
"you can avoid them by upgrading ``setuptools`` to a more recent version. If "
"you're using pip, you can upgrade pip using ``python -m pip install -U pip`` "
"which will also upgrade ``setuptools``. This is resolved in later versions "
"of Django as described in the :doc:`/releases/1.9.2`."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé sábháilte neamhaird a dhéanamh ar na hearráidí seo (suiteálfaidh "
"Django go breá fós), ach is féidir leat iad a sheachaint trí “setuptools” a "
"uasghrádú go leagan níos déanaí. Má tá píopa á úsáid agat, is féidir leat "
"píopa a uasghrádú ag baint úsáide as ``python -m pip install -U pip`` a "
"dhéanfaidh uasghrádú freisin ``setuptools`. Réitear é seo i leaganacha níos "
"déanaí de Django mar a thuairiscítear in:doc: `/releases/1.9.2`."

msgid ""
"The jQuery static files in ``contrib.admin`` have been moved into a ``vendor/"
"jquery`` subdirectory."
msgstr ""
"Tá na comhaid statacha jQuery i `contrib.admin ``aistríodh isteach i bhfo-"
"eolaire ``díolachóir/jquery``."

msgid ""
"The text displayed for null columns in the admin changelist ``list_display`` "
"cells has changed from ``(None)`` (or its translated equivalent) to ``-`` (a "
"dash)."
msgstr ""
"Tá an téacs a thaispeántar le haghaidh colúin null sa chealla athraithe "
"riaracháin ``list_display`` tar éis athrú ó ``(Níl aon)`` (nó a choibhéis "
"aistrithe) go ``-`` (sraith)."

msgid ""
"``django.http.responses.REASON_PHRASES`` and "
"``django.core.handlers.wsgi.STATUS_CODE_TEXT`` have been removed. Use "
"Python's Standard Library instead: :data:`http.client.responses` for Python "
"3 and `httplib.responses`_ for Python 2."
msgstr ""
"Baineadh ``Django.http.Responses.Reason_Phrases`` agus "
"``Django.Core.Handlers.wsgi.status_code_text``. Úsáid Leabharlann "
"Caighdeánach Python ina ionad sin: :data: `http.client.responses` do Python "
"3 agus `httplib.responses`_ do Python 2."

msgid "``ValuesQuerySet`` and ``ValuesListQuerySet`` have been removed."
msgstr "Baineadh ``ValueSquerySet`` agus ``ValuesListQuerySet``."

msgid ""
"The ``admin/base.html`` template no longer sets "
"``window.__admin_media_prefix__`` or ``window.__admin_utc_offset__``. Image "
"references in JavaScript that used that value to construct absolute URLs "
"have been moved to CSS for easier customization. The UTC offset is stored on "
"a data attribute of the ``<body>`` tag."
msgstr ""
"Ní leagann an teimpléad `admin/base.html` `fuinneog a thuilleadh. "
"__admin_media_prefix__`` nó ``fuinneog. __admin_utc_offset__``. Bogadh "
"tagairtí íomhá i JavaScript a d'úsáid an luach sin chun URLanna iomlána a "
"thógáil chuig CSS le haghaidh saincheaptha níos éasca. Stóráiltear an "
"fhritháireamh UTC ar thréith sonraí den chlib <body>```."

msgid ""
"``CommaSeparatedIntegerField`` validation has been refined to forbid values "
"like ``','``, ``',1'``, and ``'1,,2'``."
msgstr ""
"Tá bailíochtú ``CommaseParatedIntegerField`` scagtha chun luachanna cosúil "
"le ``', '``, ```,1'``, agus ```1, ,2'`` a thoirmeasc."

msgid ""
"Form initialization was moved from the :meth:`ProcessFormView.get() "
"<django.views.generic.edit.ProcessFormView.get>` method to the "
"new :meth:`FormMixin.get_context_data() "
"<django.views.generic.edit.FormMixin.get_context_data>` method. This may be "
"backwards incompatible if you have overridden the ``get_context_data()`` "
"method without calling ``super()``."
msgstr ""
"<django.views.generic.edit.FormMixin.get_context_data>Bogadh tionscnamh "
"foirme ón modh: meth: `ProcessFormView.get () `go dtí an "
"<django.views.generic.edit.ProcessFormView.get>modh nua:meth: "
"`formMixin.get_context_data ()`. D'fhéadfadh sé seo a bheith "
"neamhchomhoiriúnach ar ais má tá an modh `get_context_data () ``tar éis an "
"modh ``get_context_data () `a shárú gan glaoch ar ``super ()``."

msgid "Support for PostGIS 1.5 has been dropped."
msgstr "Tá tacaíocht do PostGIS 1.5 titim."

msgid ""
"The ``django.contrib.sites.models.Site.domain`` field was changed to "
"be :attr:`~django.db.models.Field.unique`."
msgstr ""
"Athraíodh an réimse ``django.contrib.sites.models.site.domain`` go mbe:attr: "
"`~django.db.models.field.unique`."

msgid ""
"In order to enforce test isolation, database queries are not allowed by "
"default in :class:`~django.test.SimpleTestCase` tests anymore. You can "
"disable this behavior by setting the ``allow_database_queries`` class "
"attribute to ``True`` on your test class."
msgstr ""
"D'fhonn aonrú tástála a fhorfheidhmiú, ní cheadaítear ceisteanna bunachar "
"sonraí de réir réamhshocraithe i dtástálacha: class: "
"`~django.test.simpletestCase` níos mó. Is féidir leat an t-iompar seo a "
"dhíchumasú tríd an tréith aicme `allow_database_queries`` a shocrú go "
"``True`` ar do rang tástála."

msgid ""
"``ResolverMatch.app_name`` was changed to contain the full namespace path in "
"the case of nested namespaces. For consistency with "
"``ResolverMatch.namespace``, the empty value is now an empty string instead "
"of ``None``."
msgstr ""
"Athraíodh ``ResolverMatch.App_Name`` chun an cosán iomlán spás ainmneacha a "
"bheith ann i gcás spás ainmneacha neadaithe. Le haghaidh comhsheasmhachta le "
"`ResolverMatch.Namespace``, is teaghrán folamh é an luach folamh anois in "
"ionad ``None``."

msgid "For security hardening, session keys must be at least 8 characters."
msgstr ""
"Chun slándáil a chruasú, caithfidh 8 gcarachtar ar a laghad a bheith sna "
"heochracha seisiúin."

msgid ""
"Private function ``django.utils.functional.total_ordering()`` has been "
"removed. It contained a workaround for a ``functools.total_ordering()`` bug "
"in Python versions older than 2.7.3."
msgstr ""
"Baineadh feidhm phríobháideach ``django.utils.functional.total_orders () ``. "
"Bhí réiteach ann le haghaidh fabht ``functools.total_orders () ``i "
"leaganacha Python níos sine ná 2.7.3."

msgid ""
"XML serialization (either through :djadmin:`dumpdata` or the syndication "
"framework) used to output any characters it received. Now if the content to "
"be serialized contains any control characters not allowed in the XML 1.0 "
"standard, the serialization will fail with a :exc:`ValueError`."
msgstr ""
"Sraitheadh XML (cibé acu trí:djadmin: `dumpdata` nó an creat sindiciúcháin) "
"a úsáidtear chun aon charachtair a fuair sé a aschur. Anois má tá aon "
"charachtair rialaithe nach gceadaítear sa chaighdeán XML 1.0 san ábhar atá "
"le sraitheadh, teipeann ar an sraitheadh le a:exc: `ValueError`."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.forms.CharField` now strips input of leading and trailing "
"whitespace by default. This can be disabled by setting the "
"new :attr:`~django.forms.CharField.strip` argument to ``False``."
msgstr ""
": class: `~django.forms.charfield` anois stiallann ionchur de spás bán "
"tosaigh agus rianaithe de réir réamhshocraithe. Is féidir é seo a dhíchumasú "
"tríd an argóint nua:attr: `~django.forms.charfield.strip` a shocrú go "
"``False``."

msgid ""
"Template text that is translated and uses two or more consecutive percent "
"signs, e.g. ``\"%%\"``, may have a new ``msgid`` after ``makemessages`` is "
"run (most likely the translation will be marked fuzzy). The new ``msgid`` "
"will be marked ``\"#, python-format\"``."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh go mbeadh `msgid`` nua ag téacs teimpléad a aistrítear agus a "
"úsáideann dhá chomhartha faoin gcéad as a chéile nó níos mó, m.sh. ``%%\"`, "
"tar éis `makemessages`` a reáchtáil (is dóichí go mbeidh an t-aistriúchán "
"doiléir). Marcálfar an ``msgid`` nua ```#, formáid python-\"``."

msgid ""
"If neither :attr:`request.current_app <django.http.HttpRequest.current_app>` "
"nor :class:`Context.current_app <django.template.Context>` are set, "
"the :ttag:`url` template tag will now use the namespace of the current "
"request. Set ``request.current_app`` to ``None`` if you don't want to use a "
"namespace hint."
msgstr ""
"<django.template.Context>Mura leagtar sí:attr: `request.current_app "
"<django.http.HttpRequest.current_app>`nor:class: `context.current_app` "
"socraithe, úsáidfidh an clib teimpléad:ttag: `url `spás ainmneacha an "
"iarratais reatha anois. Socraigh ``request.current_app`` go ``None`` mura "
"dteastaíonn uait leid spás ainmneacha a úsáid."

msgid ""
"The :setting:`SILENCED_SYSTEM_CHECKS` setting now silences messages of all "
"levels. Previously, messages of ``ERROR`` level or higher were printed to "
"the console."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an socrú: SETTING: `SILENCED_SYSTEM_CHECKS` teachtaireachtaí de gach "
"leibhéal a thostú anois. Roimhe seo, clóiteadh teachtaireachtaí de leibhéal "
"``ERROR` nó níos airde chuig an gconsól."

msgid ""
"The ``FlatPage.enable_comments`` field is removed from the ``FlatPageAdmin`` "
"as it's unused by the application. If your project or a third-party app "
"makes use of it, :ref:`create a custom ModelAdmin <flatpages-admin>` to add "
"it back."
msgstr ""
"Baintear an réimse ``flatpage.enable_comments`` ón ``FlatPageAdmin`` toisc "
"nach bhfuil sé in úsáid ag an bhfeidhmchlár. Má úsáideann do thionscadal nó "
"aip tríú páirtí é, :ref: `cruthaigh ModelAdmin saincheapaithe <flatpages-"
"admin>`chun é a chur ar ais."

msgid ""
"The return value "
"of :meth:`~django.test.runner.DiscoverRunner.setup_databases` and the first "
"argument of :meth:`~django.test.runner.DiscoverRunner.teardown_databases` "
"changed. They used to be ``(old_names, mirrors)`` tuples. Now they're just "
"the first item, ``old_names``."
msgstr ""
"Athraíodh luach tuairisceáin de:meth: "
"`~Django.Test.Runner.DiscoverRunner.Setup_Databases` agus an chéad argóint "
"de:meth: `~Django.Test.Runner.DiscoverRunner.TEARDOWN_Databases`. Ba ghnách "
"iad a bhí siad ina “(sean_ainmneacha, scátháin) ``tiúplaí. Anois níl siad "
"ach an chéad mhír, ``old_names``."

msgid ""
"By default :class:`~django.test.LiveServerTestCase` attempts to find an "
"available port in the 8081-8179 range instead of just trying port 8081."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe: class: `~django.test.liveservertestcase` iarracht "
"calafort atá ar fáil sa raon 8081-8179 a aimsiú in ionad triail a bhaint as "
"calafort 8081."

msgid ""
"The system checks for :class:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin` now check "
"instances rather than classes."
msgstr ""
"Seiceálann an córas le haghaidh: class: `~django.contrib.admin.modelAdmin` "
"cásanna anois seachas ranganna."

msgid ""
"The private API to apply mixed migration plans has been dropped for "
"performance reasons. Mixed plans consist of a list of migrations where some "
"are being applied and others are being unapplied."
msgstr ""
"Tá an API príobháideach chun pleananna imirce measctha a chur i bhfeidhm ar "
"chúiseanna feidhmíochta Is éard atá i bpleananna measctha liosta imirce ina "
"bhfuil cuid acu á chur i bhfeidhm agus nach bhfuil cuid eile á chur i "
"bhfeidhm."

msgid ""
"The related model object descriptor classes in "
"``django.db.models.fields.related`` (private API) are moved from the "
"``related`` module to ``related_descriptors`` and renamed as follows:"
msgstr ""
"Bogtar na ranganna tuairiscithe réad samhail gaolmhara i "
"``django.db.models.fields.related`` (API príobháideach) ón modúl `related`` "
"go `related_descriptors`` agus athainmnítear mar seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"``ReverseSingleRelatedObjectDescriptor`` is ``ForwardManyToOneDescriptor``"
msgstr ""
"Is é ``ReversesingleRelateDObjectDescriptor`` ``ForwardmanyTooneDescriptor``"

msgid "``SingleRelatedObjectDescriptor`` is ``ReverseOneToOneDescriptor``"
msgstr "Is é ``SingleRelateDObjectDescriptor`` ``ReverseOneTooneDescriptor``"

msgid "``ForeignRelatedObjectsDescriptor`` is ``ReverseManyToOneDescriptor``"
msgstr ""
"Is é ``ForeignRelateDObjectsDescriptor`` ``ReverseManyToOneDescriptor``"

msgid "``ManyRelatedObjectsDescriptor`` is ``ManyToManyDescriptor``"
msgstr "Is é ``ManyRelateDObjectsDescriptor`` ``ManyTomanyDescriptor``"

msgid ""
"If you implement a custom :data:`~django.conf.urls.handler404` view, it must "
"return a response with an HTTP 404 status code. "
"Use :class:`~django.http.HttpResponseNotFound` or pass ``status=404`` to "
"the :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse`. Otherwise, :setting:`APPEND_SLASH` "
"won't work correctly with ``DEBUG=False``."
msgstr ""
"Má chuireann tú amharc saincheap:data: `~django.conf.urls.handler404` i "
"bhfeidhm, caithfidh sé freagra a thabhairt ar ais le cód stádais HTTP 404. "
"Úsáid: aicme: `~django.http.httpResponseNotFound` nó pas ``status = 404`` "
"chuig an: aicme: `~django.http.httpResponse`. Seachas sin, :setting: ní "
"oibreoidh `APPEND_SLASH` i gceart le ``debug=false``."

msgid "Features deprecated in 1.9"
msgstr "Gnéithe atá díscríofa i 1.9"

msgid "``assignment_tag()``"
msgstr "``tascanna_assignment_tag () ``"

msgid ""
"Django 1.4 added the ``assignment_tag`` helper to ease the creation of "
"template tags that store results in a template variable. "
"The :meth:`~django.template.Library.simple_tag` helper has gained this same "
"ability, making the ``assignment_tag`` obsolete. Tags that use "
"``assignment_tag`` should be updated to use ``simple_tag``."
msgstr ""
"Chuir Django 1.4 an cúntóir ``assignment_tag ``le cruthú clibeanna teimpléad "
"a stóráilíonn athróg teimpléad torthaí a mhaolú. Tá an cumas céanna seo "
"faighte ag an gcúntóir: Meth: `~django.template.library.simple_tag`, rud a "
"fhágann go bhfuil an ``assignment_tag ``as feidhm. Ba chóir clibeanna a "
"úsáideann ``assignment_tag`` a nuashonrú chun ``simple_tag`` a úsáid."

msgid "``{% cycle %}`` syntax with comma-separated arguments"
msgstr "``{% timthriall%}`` comhréiteach le hargóintí scartha le camóg"

msgid ""
"The :ttag:`cycle` tag supports an inferior old syntax from previous Django "
"versions:"
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn an clibe:ttag: `timthriall` le sean-chomhréir níos ísle ó "
"leaganacha Django roimhe seo:"

msgid ""
"Its parsing caused bugs with the current syntax, so support for the old "
"syntax will be removed in Django 1.10 following an accelerated deprecation."
msgstr ""
"Ba chúis lena pháirsíú fabhtanna leis an gcomhréireacht reatha, mar sin "
"bainfear tacaíocht don sean-chomhréireacht i Django 1.10 tar éis díscrúdú "
"luathaithe."

msgid "``ForeignKey`` and ``OneToOneField`` ``on_delete`` argument"
msgstr "Argóint ``ForeignKey`` agus ``OneToonefield`` ``on_delete``"

msgid ""
"In order to increase awareness about cascading model deletion, the "
"``on_delete`` argument of ``ForeignKey`` and ``OneToOneField`` will be "
"required in Django 2.0."
msgstr ""
"D'fhonn feasacht a mhéadú faoi scriosadh samhail cascading, beidh an argóint "
"`on_delete`` de `ForeignKey`` agus ``OneToonefield`` ag teastáil i Django "
"2.0."

msgid ""
"Update models and existing migrations to explicitly set the argument. Since "
"the default is ``models.CASCADE``, add ``on_delete=models.CASCADE`` to all "
"``ForeignKey`` and ``OneToOneField``\\s that don't use a different option. "
"You can also pass it as the second positional argument if you don't care "
"about compatibility with older versions of Django."
msgstr ""
"Nuashonraigh samhlacha agus imirce reatha chun an argóint a shocrú go "
"sainráite. Ós rud é gurb é `Models.cascade`` an réamhshocraithe, cuir "
"``on_delete=Models.cascade`` le gach ``ForeignKey`` agus ``OneToOneField`` "
"nach n-úsáideann rogha difriúil. Is féidir leat é a chur ar aghaidh mar an "
"dara argóint seasaimh mura bhfuil cúram ort faoi chomhoiriúnacht le "
"leaganacha níos sine de Django."

msgid "``Field.rel`` changes"
msgstr "Athruithe ``Field.rel``"

msgid ""
"``Field.rel`` and its methods and attributes have changed to match the "
"related fields API. The ``Field.rel`` attribute is renamed to "
"``remote_field`` and many of its methods and attributes are either changed "
"or renamed."
msgstr ""
"``Field.rel`` agus tá a modhanna agus tréithe athraithe chun API na réimsí "
"gaolmhara a mheaitseáil. Athainmnítear an tréith ``Field.rel`` go "
"`remote_field`` agus athraítear nó athainmnítear go leor dá modhanna agus "
"tréithe."

msgid ""
"The aim of these changes is to provide a documented API for relation fields."
msgstr ""
"Is é aidhm na hathruithe seo API doiciméadaithe a sholáthar do réimsí "
"caidrimh."

msgid "``GeoManager`` and ``GeoQuerySet`` custom methods"
msgstr "Modhanna saincheaptha ``Geomanager`` agus ``GeoQuerySet ``"

msgid ""
"All custom ``GeoQuerySet`` methods (``area()``, ``distance()``, "
"``gml()``, ...) have been replaced by equivalent geographic expressions in "
"annotations (see in new features). Hence the need to set a custom "
"``GeoManager`` to GIS-enabled models is now obsolete. As soon as your code "
"doesn't call any of the deprecated methods, you can simply remove the "
"``objects = GeoManager()`` lines from your models."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh nathanna geografacha coibhéiseach in anótaí in ionad gach modh "
"saincheaptha ``GeoquerySet ``(`` limistéar () ``,`` fad () ``,`` gml () "
"``,...). Dá bhrí sin tá an gá saincheaptha ``Geomanager`` a shocrú do "
"mhúnlaí cumasaithe GIS as feidhm anois. Chomh luath agus nach nglaonn do "
"chód ar aon cheann de na modhanna dlite, is féidir leat na línte ``objects = "
"GeoManager () `a bhaint as do mhúnlaí."

msgid "Template loader APIs have changed"
msgstr "Athraigh APIs lódóra teimpléid"

msgid ""
"Django template loaders have been updated to allow recursive template "
"extending. This change necessitated a new template loader API. The old "
"``load_template()`` and ``load_template_sources()`` methods are now "
"deprecated. Details about the new API can be found :ref:`in the template "
"loader documentation <custom-template-loaders>`."
msgstr ""
"Nuashonraíodh lódóirí teimpléad Django chun teimpléad athfhillteach a "
"leathnú. Bhí API lódóir teimpléad nua ag teastáil leis an athrú seo. Tá na "
"sean-mhodhanna ``load_template () ``agus ``load_template_sources ()`` "
"díluachtaithe anois. <custom-template-loaders>Is féidir sonraí faoin API nua "
"a aimsiú:ref: `sa dhoiciméadú lódóirí teimpléad `."

msgid "Passing a 3-tuple or an ``app_name`` to ``include()``"
msgstr "Ag dul trí thúpla nó ``app_name`` chuig ``include () ``"

msgid ""
"The instance namespace part of passing a tuple as an argument to "
"``include()`` has been replaced by passing the ``namespace`` argument to "
"``include()``. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an chuid spás ainmneacha a bhaineann le tuple a chur mar argóint "
"chun `include () ``a chur in ionad an argóint ``spás ainmneacha`` a chur ar "
"aghaidh chuig `include () ``. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"The ``app_name`` argument to ``include()`` has been replaced by passing a 2-"
"tuple (as above), or passing an object or module with an ``app_name`` "
"attribute (as below). If the ``app_name`` is set in this new way, the "
"``namespace`` argument is no longer required. It will default to the value "
"of ``app_name``. For example, the URL patterns in the tutorial are changed "
"from:"
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an argóint `app_name`` chun `include () ``a chur in ionad trí dhá "
"tuple (mar thuas) a rith, nó réad nó modúl a rith le tréith ``app_name`` "
"(mar atá thíos). Má tá an ``app_name`` socraithe ar an mbealach nua seo, ní "
"theastaíonn an argóint ``spás ainm`` a thuilleadh. Beidh sé réamhshocraithe "
"go luach ``app_name``. Mar shampla, athraítear na patrúin URL sa rang "
"teagaisc ó:"

msgid "``mysite/urls.py``"
msgstr "``mysite/urls.py``"

msgid "to:"
msgstr "chuig:"

msgid "``polls/urls.py``"
msgstr "``polls/urls.py``"

msgid ""
"This change also means that the old way of including an ``AdminSite`` "
"instance is deprecated. Instead, pass ``admin.site.urls`` directly to "
"``django.conf.urls.url()``:"
msgstr ""
"Ciallaíonn an t-athrú seo freisin go bhfuil an seanbhealach chun sampla "
"``Admin Site`` a áireamh as dul in iúl. Ina áit sin, pas `admin.site.urls`` "
"go díreach chuig ``django.conf.urls.url () ``:"

msgid "``urls.py``"
msgstr "``urls.py``"

msgid "URL application namespace required if setting an instance namespace"
msgstr ""
"Teastaíonn spás ainmneacha feidhmchláir URL má shocraíonn spás ainmneacha "
"sampla"

msgid ""
"In the past, an instance namespace without an application namespace would "
"serve the same purpose as the application namespace, but it was impossible "
"to reverse the patterns if there was an application namespace with the same "
"name. Includes that specify an instance namespace require that the included "
"URLconf sets an application namespace."
msgstr ""
"San am atá caite, bheadh spás ainmneacha sampla gan spás ainmneacha "
"feidhmchláir ar an gcuspóir céanna le spás ainmneacha an fheidhmchláir, ach "
"ní raibh sé dodhéanta na patrúin a aisiompú má bhí spás ainmneacha "
"feidhmchláir leis an ainm céanna. Áirítear a shonraíonn spás ainmneacha "
"sampla a éilíonn go socraíonn an URLConf san áireamh spás ainmneacha "
"feidhmchláir."

msgid "``current_app`` parameter to ``contrib.auth`` views"
msgstr "Paraiméadar ``current_app`` chuig tuairimí ``contrib.auth``"

msgid ""
"All views in ``django.contrib.auth.views`` have the following structure:"
msgstr ""
"Tá an struchtúr seo a leanas ag gach tuairim i ``django.contrib.auth.views``:"

msgid ""
"As of Django 1.8, ``current_app`` is set on the ``request`` object. For "
"consistency, these views will require the caller to set ``current_app`` on "
"the ``request`` instead of passing it in a separate argument."
msgstr ""
"De réir Django 1.8, socraítear ``current_app`` ar an réad ``iarraidh`. Ar "
"mhaithe le comhsheasmhacht, éilfidh na tuairimí seo ar an nglaoiteoir "
"``current_app`` a shocrú ar an ``iarraidh`` in ionad é a rith in argóint ar "
"leithligh."

msgid "``django.contrib.gis.geoip``"
msgstr "``django.contrib.gis.geoip ``"

msgid ""
"The :mod:`django.contrib.gis.geoip2` module supersedes "
"``django.contrib.gis.geoip``. The new module provides a similar API except "
"that it doesn't provide the legacy GeoIP-Python API compatibility methods."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann an modúl:mod: `django.contrib.gis.geoip2` in ionad "
"``django.contrib.gis.geoip``. Soláthraíonn an modúl nua API den chineál "
"céanna ach amháin nach soláthraíonn sé na modhanna comhoiriúnachta API GeoIP-"
"Python oidhreachta."

msgid ""
"The ``weak`` argument to ``django.dispatch.signals.Signal.disconnect()`` has "
"been deprecated as it has no effect."
msgstr ""
"Tá an argóint ``lag`` chuig ``django.Dispatch.Signals.Signal.Disconnect () "
"``a dhíchur mar níl aon éifeacht aige."

msgid ""
"The ``check_aggregate_support()`` method of "
"``django.db.backends.base.BaseDatabaseOperations`` has been deprecated and "
"will be removed in Django 2.0. The more general "
"``check_expression_support()`` should be used instead."
msgstr ""
"Tá an modh ``check_aggregate_support () ``de "
"`Django.db.backends.base.baseDatabaseOperations`` a dhíchur agus bainfear é "
"i Django 2.0. Ba chóir an ``check_expression_support () ``níos ginearálta a "
"úsáid ina ionad."

msgid ""
"``django.forms.extras`` is deprecated. You can "
"find :class:`~django.forms.SelectDateWidget` in ``django.forms.widgets`` (or "
"simply ``django.forms``) instead."
msgstr ""
"Tá ``django.forms.extras`` imithe. Is féidir leat aimsi:class: "
"`~django.forms.selectDateWidget` i ``django.forms.widgets`` (nó "
"``django.forms``) ina ionad sin."

msgid ""
"Private API ``django.db.models.fields.add_lazy_relation()`` is deprecated."
msgstr ""
"Tá API príobháideach ``django.db.models.fields.add_lazy_relations () "
"``díluachtaithe."

msgid ""
"The ``django.contrib.auth.tests.utils.skipIfCustomUser()`` decorator is "
"deprecated. With the test discovery changes in Django 1.6, the tests for "
"``django.contrib`` apps are no longer run as part of the user's project. "
"Therefore, the ``@skipIfCustomUser`` decorator is no longer needed to "
"decorate tests in ``django.contrib.auth``."
msgstr ""
"Tá an maisitheoir ``django.contrib.auth.tests.utils.skipifCustomUser () "
"``díluaite. Leis na hathruithe fionnachtana tástála i Django 1.6, ní "
"reáchtáiltear na tástálacha le haghaidh aipeanna `django.contrib ``a "
"thuilleadh mar chuid de thionscadal an úsáideora. Dá bhrí sin, ní "
"theastaíonn an maisitheoir ``@skipIfCustomUser`` a thuilleadh chun "
"tástálacha a mhaisiú i ``django.contrib.auth``."

msgid ""
"If you customized some :ref:`error handlers <error-views>`, the view "
"signatures with only one request parameter are deprecated. The views should "
"now also accept a second ``exception`` positional parameter."
msgstr ""
"Má shaincheapann tú roinnt: ref: `láimhseálaithe earráide <error-views>`, "
"díchuirtear na sínithe amharc nach bhfuil ach paraiméadar iarratais amháin "
"acu. Ba chóir go nglacfadh na tuairimí anois leis an dara paraiméadar suímh "
"```eisceacht'."

msgid ""
"The ``django.utils.feedgenerator.Atom1Feed.mime_type`` and "
"``django.utils.feedgenerator.RssFeed.mime_type`` attributes are deprecated "
"in favor of ``content_type``."
msgstr ""
"Tá na tréithe ``django.utils.feedgenerator.atom1feed.mime_type`` agus "
"``Django.utils.feedgenerator.rssfeed.mime_type`` a dhíchur i bhfabhar "
"``content_type``."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.core.signing.Signer` now issues a warning if an invalid "
"separator is used. This will become an exception in Django 1.10."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.core.signing.signer` rabhadh anois má úsáidtear "
"deighilteoir neamhbhailí. Beidh sé seo ina eisceacht i Django 1.10."

msgid ""
"``django.db.models.Field._get_val_from_obj()`` is deprecated in favor of "
"``Field.value_from_object()``."
msgstr ""
"``Django.db.Models.Field. Tá _get_val_from_obj () ``díluaite i bhfabhar "
"``field.value_from_object ()``."

msgid ""
"``django.template.loaders.eggs.Loader`` is deprecated as distributing "
"applications as eggs is not recommended."
msgstr ""
"Tá ``Django.Template.Loaders.Eggs.Loader`` a dhíchur mar iarratais a "
"dháileadh mar ní mholtar uibheacha."

msgid ""
"The ``callable_obj`` keyword argument to "
"``SimpleTestCase.assertRaisesMessage()`` is deprecated. Pass the callable as "
"a positional argument instead."
msgstr ""
"Tá an argóint eochairfhocal ``callable_obj`` chuig "
"``simpletestCase.assertRaisesMessage () ``a dhíchur. Rith an glaoch mar "
"argóint seasmhach ina ionad sin."

msgid ""
"The ``allow_tags`` attribute on methods of ``ModelAdmin`` has been "
"deprecated. "
"Use :func:`~django.utils.html.format_html`, :func:`~django.utils.html.format_html_join`, "
"or :func:`~django.utils.safestring.mark_safe` when constructing the method's "
"return value instead."
msgstr ""
"Tá an tréith `allow_tags`` ar mhodhanna ``ModelAdmin`` a dhíchur. Úsáid: "
"func: `~django.utils.html.format_html`, :func: "
"`~django.utils.html.format_html_join`, nó:func: "
"`~django.utils.safestring.mark_safe` agus luach tuairisceáin an mhodha á "
"thógáil ina ionad sin."

msgid ""
"The ``enclosure`` keyword argument to ``SyndicationFeed.add_item()`` is "
"deprecated. Use the new ``enclosures`` argument which accepts a list of "
"``Enclosure`` objects instead of a single one."
msgstr ""
"Tá an argóint eochairfhocal ``enclosure`` chuig `SyndicationFeed.add_item () "
"``díluachtaithe. Úsáid an argóint nua ``enclosures`` a ghlacann le liosta de "
"rudaí ``Inclosure`` in ionad ceann amháin."

msgid ""
"The ``django.template.loader.LoaderOrigin`` and "
"``django.template.base.StringOrigin`` aliases for "
"``django.template.base.Origin`` are deprecated."
msgstr ""
"Tá na hainmneacha `Django.Template.Loader.LoaderOrigin`` agus "
"``Django.Template.Base.StringOrigin`` do `Django.Template.Base.Origin`` a "
"dhíchur."

msgid "Features removed in 1.9"
msgstr "Gnéithe bainte i 1.9"

msgid ""
"These features have reached the end of their deprecation cycle and are "
"removed in Django 1.9. See :ref:`deprecated-features-1.7` for details, "
"including how to remove usage of these features."
msgstr ""
"Tá na gnéithe seo tar éis deireadh a dtimthriall díscrúdaithe bainte amach "
"agus baintear iad i Django 1.9. Féach: Ref: `deprecated-features-1.7` le "
"haghaidh sonraí, lena n-áirítear conas úsáid na ngnéithe seo a bhaint."

msgid "``django.utils.dictconfig`` is removed."
msgstr "Baintear ``django.utils.dictconfig``."

msgid "``django.utils.importlib`` is removed."
msgstr "Baintear ``django.utils.importlib``."

msgid "``django.utils.tzinfo`` is removed."
msgstr "Baintear ``django.utils.tzinfo``."

msgid "``django.utils.unittest`` is removed."
msgstr "Baintear ``django.utils.unittest``."

msgid "The ``syncdb`` command is removed."
msgstr "Baintear an t-ordú ``syncdb``."

msgid ""
"``django.db.models.signals.pre_syncdb`` and "
"``django.db.models.signals.post_syncdb`` is removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear ``django.db.models.signals.pre_syncdb`` agus "
"``django.db.models.signals.post_syncdb``."

msgid "Support for ``allow_syncdb`` on database routers is removed."
msgstr "Baintear tacaíocht do `allow_syncdb`` ar ródairí bunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"Automatic syncing of apps without migrations is removed. Migrations are "
"compulsory for all apps unless you pass the :option:`migrate --run-syncdb` "
"option."
msgstr ""
"Baintear sioncrónú uathoibríoch aipeanna gan imirce. Tá imirce éigeantach do "
"gach aip mura rachaidh tú ar an roghna:option: `migration --run-syncdb`."

msgid ""
"The SQL management commands for apps without migrations, ``sql``, "
"``sqlall``, ``sqlclear``, ``sqldropindexes``, and ``sqlindexes``, are "
"removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear na horduithe bainistíochta SQL le haghaidh aipeanna gan imirce, "
"``sql``, `sqlall``, `sqlclear``, `sqldropindexes``, agus ``sqlindexes``."

msgid ""
"Support for automatic loading of ``initial_data`` fixtures and initial SQL "
"data is removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear tacaíocht do luchtú uathoibríoch daingneáin ``initial_data ``agus "
"sonraí tosaigh SQL."

msgid ""
"All models need to be defined inside an installed application or declare an "
"explicit :attr:`~django.db.models.Options.app_label`. Furthermore, it isn't "
"possible to import them before their application is loaded. In particular, "
"it isn't possible to import models inside the root package of an application."
msgstr ""
"Caithfear gach samhail a shainiú taobh istigh d'fheidhmchlár suiteáilte nó "
"sainmhíniú: attr: `~django.db.models.options.app_label` a dhearbhú. Ina "
"theannta sin, ní féidir iad a iompórtáil sula luchtaítear a n-iarratas. Go "
"háirithe, ní féidir samhlacha a iompórtáil taobh istigh de phacáiste fréimhe "
"feidhmchláir."

msgid ""
"The model and form ``IPAddressField`` is removed. A stub field remains for "
"compatibility with historical migrations."
msgstr ""
"Baintear an tsamhail agus an fhoirm ``Ipaddressfield``. Tá réimse stub fós "
"ann le haghaidh comhoiriúnachta le himirce stairiúla."

msgid "``AppCommand.handle_app()`` is no longer supported."
msgstr "Ní thacaítear le ``AppCommand.handle_app () ``a thuilleadh."

msgid ""
"``RequestSite`` and ``get_current_site()`` are no longer importable from "
"``django.contrib.sites.models``."
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir ``requestsite`` agus ``get_current_site () ``a iompórtáil ó "
"``django.contrib.sites.models`` a thuilleadh."

msgid "FastCGI support via the ``runfcgi`` management command is removed."
msgstr "Baintear tacaíocht FastCGI tríd an ordú bainistíochta ``runfcgi`."

msgid "``django.utils.datastructures.SortedDict`` is removed."
msgstr "Baintear ``Django.utils.DataStructures.Sorteddict``."

msgid "``ModelAdmin.declared_fieldsets`` is removed."
msgstr "Baintear ``ModelAdmin.Declared_FieldSets``."

msgid "The ``util`` modules that provided backwards compatibility are removed:"
msgstr "Baintear na modúil ``util`` a sholáthraíodh comhoiriúnacht ar ais:"

msgid "``ModelAdmin.get_formsets`` is removed."
msgstr "Baintear ``ModelAdmin.get_FormSets``."

msgid ""
"The backward compatible shims introduced to rename the "
"``BaseMemcachedCache._get_memcache_timeout()`` method to "
"``get_backend_timeout()`` is removed."
msgstr ""
"Tugadh isteach na shims comhoiriúnacha ar chúl chun an ``BaseMemcachedCache "
"a athainmniú. Baintear modh _get_memcache_timeout () ``chun "
"``get_backend_timeout ()``."

msgid ""
"The ``--natural`` and ``-n`` options for :djadmin:`dumpdata` are removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear na roghanna ``--natural`` agus ``-n`` le haghaidh: djadmin: "
"`dumpdata`."

msgid ""
"The ``use_natural_keys`` argument for ``serializers.serialize()`` is removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear an argóint ``use_natural_keys`` do `serializers.serialize () ``."

msgid "Private API ``django.forms.forms.get_declared_fields()`` is removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear API príobháideach ``django.forms.forms.get_declared_fields () ``."

msgid ""
"The ability to use a ``SplitDateTimeWidget`` with ``DateTimeField`` is "
"removed."
msgstr "Baintear an cumas ``SplitDateTimeWidget`` le `DateTimeField`` a úsáid."

msgid "The ``WSGIRequest.REQUEST`` property is removed."
msgstr "Baintear an maoin `WSGIrequest.request``."

msgid "The class ``django.utils.datastructures.MergeDict`` is removed."
msgstr "Baintear an rang ``Django.utils.DataStructures.Mergedict``."

msgid "The ``zh-cn`` and ``zh-tw`` language codes are removed."
msgstr "Baintear na cóid teanga `zh-cn`` agus `zh-tw``."

msgid "The internal ``django.utils.functional.memoize()`` is removed."
msgstr "Baintear an ``django.utils.functional.memoize () ``inmheánach."

msgid "``django.core.cache.get_cache`` is removed."
msgstr "Baintear ``django.core.cache.get_cache``."

msgid "``django.db.models.loading`` is removed."
msgstr "Baintear ``django.db.models.loading``."

msgid "Passing callable arguments to querysets is no longer possible."
msgstr "Ní féidir argóintí inghlaonta a chur chuig ceisteanna a thuilleadh."

msgid ""
"``BaseCommand.requires_model_validation`` is removed in favor of "
"``requires_system_checks``. Admin validators is replaced by admin checks."
msgstr ""
"Baintear ``BaseCommand.requires_model_validation`` i bhfabhar "
"``requires_system_checks``. Cuirtear seiceálacha riaracháin in ionad "
"bailíochtóirí riaracháin."

msgid ""
"The ``ModelAdmin.validator_class`` and ``default_validator_class`` "
"attributes are removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear na tréithe ``ModelAdmin.Validator_Class`` agus "
"``default_validator_class``."

msgid "``ModelAdmin.validate()`` is removed."
msgstr "Baintear ``ModelAdmin.validate () ``."

msgid ""
"``django.db.backends.DatabaseValidation.validate_field`` is removed in favor "
"of the ``check_field`` method."
msgstr ""
"Baintear ``Django.db.backends.databaseValidation.validate_field`` i bhfabhar "
"an modh ``check_field``."

msgid "The ``validate`` management command is removed."
msgstr "Baintear an t-ordú bainistíochta `bailíochta`."

msgid ""
"``django.utils.module_loading.import_by_path`` is removed in favor of "
"``django.utils.module_loading.import_string``."
msgstr ""
"Baintear ``django.utils.module_loading.import_by_path`` i bhfabhar "
"``django.utils.module_loading.import_string``."

msgid ""
"``ssi`` and ``url`` template tags are removed from the ``future`` template "
"tag library."
msgstr ""
"Baintear clibeanna teimpléad ``ssi`` agus `url ``ón leabharlann clib "
"teimpléad ``todhcha``."

msgid "``django.utils.text.javascript_quote()`` is removed."
msgstr "Baintear ``django.utils.text.javascript_quote () ``."

msgid ""
"Database test settings as independent entries in the database settings, "
"prefixed by ``TEST_``, are no longer supported."
msgstr ""
"Ní thacaítear le socruithe tástála bunachar sonraí mar iontrálacha "
"neamhspleácha i socruithe bunachar sonraí, réamhshocraithe ag ``TEST_``, a "
"thuilleadh."

msgid ""
"The ``cache_choices`` option to :class:`~django.forms.ModelChoiceField` "
"and :class:`~django.forms.ModelMultipleChoiceField` is removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear an rogha ``cache_choices`` to:class: "
"`~django.forms.ModelChoiceField` agus:class: "
"`~django.forms.ModelMultipleChoiceField`."

msgid ""
"The default value of the :attr:`RedirectView.permanent "
"<django.views.generic.base.RedirectView.permanent>` attribute has changed "
"from ``True`` to ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Tá luach réamhshocraithe den tréith: attr: `RedirectView.permanent "
"<django.views.generic.base.RedirectView.permanent>`athraithe ó ``True`` go "
"``False``."

msgid ""
"``django.contrib.sitemaps.FlatPageSitemap`` is removed in favor of "
"``django.contrib.flatpages.sitemaps.FlatPageSitemap``."
msgstr ""
"Baintear ``Django.Contrib.SiteMaps.FlatPageSitemap`` i bhfabhar "
"``Django.Contrib.FlatPages.Sitemaps.FlatPageSitemap``."

msgid "Private API ``django.test.utils.TestTemplateLoader`` is removed."
msgstr "Baintear API príobháideach ``Django.Test.utils.TestTemplateLoader``."

msgid "The ``django.contrib.contenttypes.generic`` module is removed."
msgstr "Baintear an modúl ``django.contrib.contenttypes.generic``."

msgid "Django 1.9.1 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.9.1"

msgid "Django 1.9.1 fixes several bugs in 1.9."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.9.1 roinnt fabhtanna i 1.9."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``BaseCache.get_or_set()`` with the ``DummyCache`` backend "
"(:ticket:`25840`)."
msgstr ""
"Seasta ``BaseCache.get_or_set () ``leis an gcúltaca ``DummyCache`` (:ticket: "
"`25840`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression in ``FormMixin`` causing forms to be validated twice "
"(:ticket:`25548`, :ticket:`26018`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraíodh aischéimniú in `FormMixin`` a fhágann go ndéanfaí foirmeacha a "
"bhailíochtú faoi dhó (:ticket: `25548`, :ticket: `26018`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a system check crash with nested ``ArrayField``\\s (:ticket:`25867`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste seiceála córais le ``Arrayfield``\\ s neadaithe (:ticket: "
"`25867`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression in ``CommonMiddleware`` causing ``If-None-Match`` checks "
"to always return HTTP 200 (:ticket:`25900`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú in ``CommonMiddleware`` ina chúis go gcuirfeadh "
"seiceálacha ``If-None-Match`` HTTP 200 ar ais i gcónaí (:ticket: `25900`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed admin's delete confirmation page's summary counts of related objects "
"(:ticket:`25883`)."
msgstr ""
"Líon achoimre ar rudaí gaolmhara ar leathanach deimhnithe scriosadh "
"riaracháin seasta (:ticket: `25883`)."

msgid ""
"Added ``from __future__ import unicode_literals`` to the default ``apps.py`` "
"created by ``startapp`` on Python 2 (:ticket:`25909`). Add this line to your "
"own ``apps.py`` files created using Django 1.9 if you want your migrations "
"to work on both Python 2 and Python 3."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh `from __future__ allmhairiú unicode_literals`` leis an "
"réamhshocraithe ``apps.py`` a chruthaigh ``startapp`` ar Python 2 (:ticket: "
"`25909`). Cuir an líne seo le do chuid comhad ``apps.py` féin a cruthaíodh "
"ag baint úsáide as Django 1.9 más mian leat go n-oibreoidh d'imirce ar "
"Python 2 agus Python 3 araon."

msgid ""
"Prevented ``QuerySet.delete()`` from crashing on MySQL when querying across "
"relations (:ticket:`25882`)."
msgstr ""
"Chuir sé cosc ar ``QuerySet.delete () ``titim ar MySQL agus tú ag fiosrú ar "
"fud caidrimh (:ticket: `25882`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed evaluation of zero-length slices of ``QuerySet.values()`` "
"(:ticket:`25894`)."
msgstr ""
"Meastóireacht sheasta ar slisní nialas-fad de ``QuerySet.Values () "
"``(:ticket: `25894`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``TypedChoiceField`` change detection with nullable fields "
"(:ticket:`25942`)."
msgstr ""
"Braite athraithe seasta ``TypedChoiceField`` le réimsí neamhnaithe (:ticket: "
"`25942`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed incorrect timezone warnings in custom admin templates that don't have "
"a ``data-admin-utc-offset`` attribute in the ``body`` tag. (:ticket:`25845`)."
msgstr ""
"Rabhadh crios ama míchearta socraithe i dteimpléid riaracháin saincheaptha "
"nach bhfuil tréith ``data-admin-utc-offset`` acu sa chlib ``body`. (:ticéad: "
"`25845`)."

msgid ""
"Avoided hiding some exceptions, like an invalid ``INSTALLED_APPS`` setting, "
"behind ``AppRegistryNotReady`` when starting ``runserver`` "
"(:ticket:`25510`). This regression appeared in 1.8.5 as a side effect of "
"fixing :ticket:`24704` and by mistake the fix wasn't applied to the ``stable/"
"1.9.x`` branch."
msgstr ""
"Seachnaíodh roinnt eisceachtaí a cheilt, cosúil le socrú ``INSTALLED_APPS`` "
"neamhbhailí, taobh thiar de `AppregistryNotready`` agus tú ag tosú "
"``runserver`` (:ticket: `25510`). Bhí an aischéimniú seo le feiceáil i 1.8.5 "
"mar fho-éifeacht de shocrú: ticket: `24704` agus trí dhearmad níor cuireadh "
"an socrú i bhfeidhm ar an mbrainse `stable/1.9.x``."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``migrate --fake-initial`` detection of many-to-many tables "
"(:ticket:`25922`)."
msgstr ""
"Braite seasta ``migrae--fake-initial`` ar go leor táblaí (:ticket: `25922`)."

msgid ""
"Restored the functionality of the admin's ``list_editable`` add and change "
"buttons (:ticket:`25903`)."
msgstr ""
"Athchóirigh feidhmiúlacht cnaipí cuir agus athraithe ``list_editable`` an "
"riaracháin (:ticket: `25903`)."

msgid "Fixed ``isnull`` query lookup for ``ForeignObject`` (:ticket:`25972`)."
msgstr ""
"Cuardach ceist seasta ``isnull`` le haghaidh ``ForeignoBject`` (:ticket: "
"`25972`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed incorrect object reference in "
"``SingleObjectMixin.get_context_object_name()`` (:ticket:`26006`)."
msgstr ""
"Tagairt réad mícheart socraithe i "
"``SingleObjectMixin.get_Context_Object_name () ``(:ticket: `26006`)."

msgid ""
"Restored ``contrib.auth`` hashers compatibility with ``py-bcrypt`` "
"(:ticket:`26016`)."
msgstr ""
"Comhoiriúnacht hashers ``contrib.auth`` athchóirithe le `py-bcrypt`` "
"(:ticket: `26016`)."

msgid "Django 1.9.10 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.9.10"

msgid "Django 1.9.10 fixes a security issue in 1.9.9."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.9.10 saincheist slándála i 1.9.9."

msgid "Django 1.9.11 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.9.11"

msgid "Django 1.9.11 fixes two security issues in 1.9.10."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.9.11 dhá shaincheist slándála i 1.9.10."

msgid "Django 1.9.12 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.9.12"

msgid "Django 1.9.12 fixes a regression in 1.9.11."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.9.12 aischéimniú i 1.9.11."

msgid "Django 1.9.13 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.9.13"

msgid ""
"Django 1.9.13 fixes two security issues and a bug in 1.9.12. This is the "
"final release of the 1.9.x series."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.9.13 dhá shaincheist slándála agus fabht i 1.9.12. Is é "
"seo an scaoileadh deiridh den tsraith 1.9.x."

msgid "Django 1.9.2 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.9.2"

msgid ""
"Django 1.9.2 fixes a security regression in 1.9 and several bugs in 1.9.1. "
"It also makes a small backwards incompatible change that hopefully doesn't "
"affect any users."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.9.2 aischéimniú slándála i 1.9 agus roinnt fabhtanna i "
"1.9.1. Déanann sé athrú beag neamh-chomhoiriúnach ar chúl freisin nach "
"ndéanfaidh sé difear d'úsáideoirí ar bith."

msgid ""
"Security issue: User with \"change\" but not \"add\" permission can create "
"objects for ``ModelAdmin``’s with ``save_as=True``"
msgstr ""
"Saincheist slándála: Is féidir le húsáideoir le cead “athrú” ach ní “cuir "
"leis” rudaí a chruthú do `ModelAdmin`` le `save_as = true``"

msgid ""
"If a ``ModelAdmin`` uses ``save_as=True`` (not the default), the admin "
"provides an option when editing objects to \"Save as new\". A regression in "
"Django 1.9 prevented that form submission from raising a \"Permission "
"Denied\" error for users without the \"add\" permission."
msgstr ""
"Má úsáideann ``ModelAdmin`` ``save_as = True`` (ní an réamhshocraithe), "
"soláthraíonn an riarachán rogha agus rudaí á eagarthóireacht chuig “Sábháil "
"mar nua”. Chuir aischéimniú i Django 1.9 cosc ar an aighneacht foirme sin "
"earráid “Cead Diúltaithe” a ardú d'úsáideoirí gan an cead “cuir leis”."

msgid ""
"Backwards incompatible change: ``.py-tpl`` files rewritten in project/app "
"templates"
msgstr ""
"Athrú neamh-chomhoiriúnach ar ais: comhaid ``.py-tpl`` a athscríobh i "
"dteimpléid tionscadal/app"

msgid ""
"The addition of some Django template language syntax to the default app "
"template in Django 1.9 means those files now have some invalid Python "
"syntax. This causes difficulties for packaging systems that unconditionally "
"byte-compile ``*.py`` files."
msgstr ""
"Ciallaíonn comhréir teanga roinnt teanga teimpléad Django a chur leis an "
"teimpléad app réamhshocraithe i Django 1.9 tá roinnt comhréireachta Python "
"neamhbhailí ag na comhaid sin anois. Is cúis leis seo deacrachtaí do chórais "
"phacáistithe a thiomsaíonn comhaid ``*.py`` gan choinníollacha."

msgid ""
"To remedy this, a ``.py-tpl`` suffix is now used for the project and app "
"template files included in Django. The ``.py-tpl`` suffix is replaced with "
"``.py`` by the ``startproject`` and ``startapp`` commands. For example, a "
"template with the filename ``manage.py-tpl`` will be created as "
"``manage.py``."
msgstr ""
"Chun é seo a leigheas, úsáidtear iarmhír ``.py-tpl`` anois do na comhaid "
"teimpléad tionscadail agus aip atá san áireamh i Django. Cuirtear na "
"horduithe ``startproject`` agus ``startapp`` in ionad `.py`` iarmhír `.py``. "
"Mar shampla, cruthófar teimpléad leis an ainm comhaid ``manage.py-tpl`` mar "
"`manage.py``."

msgid ""
"Please file a ticket if you have a custom project template containing ``.py-"
"tpl`` files and find this behavior problematic."
msgstr ""
"Déan ticéad a chomhdú má tá teimpléad tionscadail saincheaptha agat ina "
"bhfuil comhaid `.py-tpl`` agus faigh an t-iompar seo fadhbanna."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression in ``ConditionalGetMiddleware`` causing ``If-None-Match`` "
"checks to always return HTTP 200 (:ticket:`26024`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú in ``ConditionalGetMiddleware`` ina chúis go gcuirfeadh "
"seiceálacha ``If-None-Match`` HTTP 200 ar ais i gcónaí (:ticket: `26024`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression in the admin's edit related model popup that caused an "
"escaped value to be displayed in the select dropdown of the parent window "
"(:ticket:`25997`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú i gcnaipe samhail a bhaineann le heagarthóireacht an "
"riaracháin a d'fhág go dtaispeánfaí luach éalaithe i roghnaigh an fhuinneog "
"tuismitheora (:ticket: `25997`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression where defining a relation on an abstract model's field "
"using a string model name without an app_label no longer resolved that "
"reference to the abstract model's app if using that model in another "
"application (:ticket:`25858`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú nuair nach réitigh caidreamh a shainiú ar réimse "
"samhail teibí ag baint úsáide as ainm samhail teaghrán gan app_label an "
"tagairt sin d'aip an tsamhail teibí a thuilleadh má úsáideann tú an tsamhail "
"sin i bhfeidhmchlár eile (:ticket: `25858`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when destroying an existing test database on MySQL or "
"PostgreSQL (:ticket:`26096`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste agus bunachar sonraí tástála atá ann cheana a scriosadh ar "
"MySQL nó PostgreSQL (:ticket: `26096`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed CSRF cookie check on POST requests when ``USE_X_FORWARDED_PORT=True`` "
"(:ticket:`26094`)."
msgstr ""
"Seiceáil fianán CSRF seasta ar iarratais POST nuair a bheidh "
"`use_x_forwarded_port=true`` (:ticket: `26094`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a ``QuerySet.order_by()`` crash when ordering by a relational field of "
"a ``ManyToManyField`` ``through`` model (:ticket:`26092`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste ``QuerySet.Order_by () ``agus tú ag ordú le réimse "
"coibhneasta de mhúnla ``ManyTomanyField`` ``trí`` (:ticket: `26092`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression that caused an exception when making database queries on "
"SQLite with more than 2000 parameters when :setting:`DEBUG` is ``True`` on "
"distributions that increase the ``SQLITE_MAX_VARIABLE_NUMBER`` compile-time "
"limit to over 2000, such as Debian (:ticket:`26063`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú a d'fhág eisceacht agus ceisteanna bunachar sonraí á "
"dhéanamh ar SQLite le níos mó ná 2000 paraiméadar nuai:setting: `DEBUG` "
"``True`` ar dháileadh a mhéadaíonn teorainn ama tiomsaithe "
"``SQLITE_MAX_VARIABLE_NUMBER`` go breis agus 2000, mar Debian (:ticket: "
"`26063`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when calling the ``migrate`` command in a test case with the "
"``available_apps`` attribute pointing to an application with migrations "
"disabled using the ``MIGRATION_MODULES`` setting (:ticket:`26135`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste agus tú ag glaoch ar an ordú ``migrate`` i gcás tástála "
"leis an tréith ``available_apps`` ag díriú ar fheidhmchlár le himirce faoi "
"dhíchumasú ag baint úsáide as an socrú ``MIGRATION_MODULES`` (:ticket: "
"`26135`)."

msgid ""
"Restored the ability for testing and debugging tools to determine the "
"template from which a node came from, even during template inheritance or "
"inclusion. Prior to Django 1.9, debugging tools could access the template "
"origin from the node via ``Node.token.source[0]``. This was an undocumented, "
"private API. The origin is now available directly on each node using the "
"``Node.origin`` attribute (:ticket:`25848`)."
msgstr ""
"Athchóirigh sé an cumas chun uirlisí a thástáil agus a dhífhabhtú chun an "
"teimpléad as a tháinig nód a chinneadh, fiú le linn oidhreachta teimpléid nó "
"Roimh Django 1.9, d'fhéadfadh uirlisí dífhabhtaithe rochtain a fháil ar "
"thionscnamh teimpléid ón nód trí ``Node.Token.source [0] ``. Ba API "
"príobháideach neamhdhoiciméadaithe é seo. Tá an bunús ar fáil anois go "
"díreach ar gach nód ag baint úsáide as an tréith ``Node.origin`` (:ticket: "
"`25848`)."

msgid ""
"Always included ``geometry_field`` in the GeoJSON serializer output "
"regardless of the ``fields`` parameter (:ticket:`26138`)."
msgstr ""
"Cuir “geoimetry_field” san áireamh i gcónaí san aschur serializer GeoJSON "
"beag beann ar an paraiméadar ``fields ``(:ticket: `26138`)."

msgid ""
"Made invalid forms display the initial of values of their disabled fields "
"(:ticket:`26129`)."
msgstr ""
"Taispeánann foirmeacha neamhbhailí tosaigh luachanna a gcuid réimsí faoi "
"mhíchumas (:ticket: `26129`)."

msgid "Django 1.9.3 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.9.3"

msgid "Django 1.9.3 fixes two security issues and several bugs in 1.9.2."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.9.3 dhá shaincheist slándála agus roinnt fabhtanna i "
"1.9.2."

msgid ""
"Skipped URL checks (new in 1.9) if the ``ROOT_URLCONF`` setting isn't "
"defined (:ticket:`26155`)."
msgstr ""
"Seiceálacha URL scipeáilte (nua i 1.9) mura bhfuil an socrú `ROOT_URLCONF`` "
"sainmhínithe (:ticket: `26155`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression for cases where "
"``ForeignObject.get_extra_descriptor_filter()`` returned a ``Q`` object "
"(:ticket:`26153`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú do chásanna inar chuir "
"``ForeignObject.get_EXTRA_descriptor_filter () ``réad ``Q`` ar ais (:ticket: "
"`26153`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed regression with an ``__in=qs`` lookup for a ``ForeignKey`` with "
"``to_field`` set (:ticket:`26196`)."
msgstr ""
"Aischéimniú seasta le cuardach ``__in=qs`` le haghaidh ``ForeignKey`` le "
"tacar ``to_field`` (:ticket: `26196`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when filtering by a ``Decimal`` in ``RawQuery`` "
"(:ticket:`26219`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste agus tú ag scagadh le ``Decimal`` i `RawQuery`` (:ticket: "
"`26219`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed some crashing deprecation shims in ``SimpleTemplateResponse`` that "
"regressed in Django 1.9 (:ticket:`26253`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh roinnt shimanna díphléasaithe i ``SimpleTemplateResponse`` a "
"tháinig ar ais i Django 1.9 (:ticket: `26253`)."

msgid ""
"Changed the admin's \"permission denied\" message in the login template to "
"use ``get_username`` instead of ``username`` to support custom user models "
"(:ticket:`26231`)."
msgstr ""
"Athraigh sé teachtaireacht “cead diúltaithe” an riaracháin sa teimpléad "
"logála isteach chun ``get_username`` a úsáid in ionad ```username`` chun "
"tacú le samhlacha úsáideora saincheaptha (:ticket: `26231`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when passing a nonexistent template name to the cached "
"template loader's ``load_template()`` method (:ticket:`26280`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste nuair a chuirtear ainm teimpléad nach bhfuil ann ar "
"aghaidh chuig modh ``load_template () ``an lódóra teimpléad taisceáilte "
"(:ticket: `26280`)."

msgid ""
"Reverted a change in Django 1.9.2 (:ticket:`25858`) that prevented relative "
"lazy relationships defined on abstract models to be resolved according to "
"their concrete model's ``app_label`` (:ticket:`26186`)."
msgstr ""
"Aisghairm athrú i Django 1.9.2 (:ticket: `25858`) a chuir cosc ar chaidrimh "
"coibhneasta leisciúil a shainigh ar mhúnlaí teibí a réiteach de réir "
"`app_label`` (:ticket: `26186`) a mhúnla coincréite."

msgid "Django 1.9.4 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.9.4"

msgid ""
"Django 1.9.4 fixes a regression on Python 2 in the 1.9.3 security release "
"where ``utils.http.is_safe_url()`` crashes on bytestring URLs "
"(:ticket:`26308`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.9.4 aischéimniú ar Python 2 sa scaoileadh slándála 1.9.3 "
"ina dtiocfaidh ``utils.http.is_safe_url () ``ar URLanna bytestring (:ticket: "
"`26308`)."

msgid "Django 1.9.5 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.9.5"

msgid "Django 1.9.5 fixes several bugs in 1.9.4."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.9.5 roinnt fabhtanna i 1.9.4."

msgid ""
"Fixed a race condition in ``BaseCache.get_or_set()`` (:ticket:`26332`). It "
"now returns the ``default`` value instead of ``False`` if there's an error "
"when trying to add the value to the cache."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh coinníoll rása i ``Basecache.get_or_set () ``(:ticket: `26332`). "
"Tugann sé an luach ``default`` ar ais anois in ionad ``False`` má tá earráid "
"ann agus tú ag iarraidh an luach a chur leis an taisce."

msgid ""
"The forms in ``contrib.auth`` no longer strip trailing and leading "
"whitespace from the password fields (:ticket:`26334`). The change requires "
"users who set their password to something with such whitespace after a site "
"updated to Django 1.9 to reset their password. It provides backwards-"
"compatibility for earlier versions of Django."
msgstr ""
"Ní dhéantar na foirmeacha i `contrib.auth`` a thuilleadh a tharraingt spás "
"bán a thuilleadh ó na réimsí pasfhocal (:ticket: `26334`). Éilíonn an t-"
"athrú ar úsáideoirí a shocraíonn a gcuid pasfhocal ar rud éigin le spás bán "
"den sórt sin tar éis suíomh a nuashonrú go Django 1.9 a bhfocal faire a "
"athshocrú Soláthraíonn sé comhoiriúnacht cúil do leaganacha níos luaithe de "
"Django."

msgid "Fixed a memory leak in the cached template loader (:ticket:`26306`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh sceitheadh cuimhne sa lódóir teimpléad taisceáilte (:ticket: `26306 "
"`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression that caused ``collectstatic --clear`` to fail if the "
"storage doesn't implement ``path()`` (:ticket:`26297`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú a d'fhág gur theip ar `collectstatic --clear ``mura "
"gcuireann an stóráil ``path () `i bhfeidhm (: ticket: `26297`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when using a reverse lookup with a subquery when a "
"``ForeignKey`` has a ``to_field`` set to something other than the primary "
"key (:ticket:`26373`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste nuair a úsáidtear cuardach droim le fo-cheist nuair a "
"bhíonn `to_field`` ag `ForeignKey`` socraithe ar rud éigin eile seachas an "
"príomh-eochair (:ticket: `26373`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression in ``CommonMiddleware`` that caused spurious warnings in "
"logs on requests missing a trailing slash (:ticket:`26293`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraíodh aischéimniú in `CommonMiddleware` a d'fhág rabhaidh bréige i logaí "
"ar iarratais ar iarratais ar iarratais a eascraíonn slasc rianúil (:ticket: "
"`26293`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression with abstract model inheritance and explicit parent links "
"(:ticket:`26413`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú le oidhreacht mhúnla teibí agus naisc shoiléire "
"tuismitheoirí (:ticket: `26413`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a migrations crash on SQLite when renaming the primary key of a model "
"containing a ``ForeignKey`` to ``'self'`` (:ticket:`26384`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste imirce ar SQLite nuair a athainmnítear príomh-eochair "
"mhúnla ina bhfuil ``ForeignKey`` go ``féin`` (:ticket: `26384`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``JSONField`` inadvertently escaping its contents when displaying "
"values after failed form validation (:ticket:`25532`)."
msgstr ""
"Seasta ``JsonField`` ag éalú a ábhar de thaispeántas agus luachanna á "
"thaispeáint tar éis bailíochtú foirme theip (:ticket: `25532`)."

msgid "Django 1.9.6 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.9.6"

msgid "Django 1.9.6 fixes several bugs in 1.9.5."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.9.6 roinnt fabhtanna i 1.9.5."

msgid ""
"Added support for relative path redirects to the test client and to "
"``SimpleTestCase.assertRedirects()`` because Django 1.9 no longer converts "
"redirects to absolute URIs (:ticket:`26428`)."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíocht bhreise le haghaidh atreoruithe coinne coibhneasta chuig an "
"gcliant tástála agus chuig ``simpletestCase.assertRedirects () `toisc nach "
"ndéanann Django 1.9 athreoruithe a thuilleadh go URIs iomlána (:ticket: "
"`26428`)."

msgid ""
"Prevented ``makemigrations`` from generating infinite migrations for a model "
"field that references a ``functools.partial`` (:ticket:`26475`)."
msgstr ""
"Chuir sé cosc ar ``makemigrations`` imirce gan teorainn a ghiniúint do "
"réimse samhail a thagann tagairt do ``functools.partial`` (:ticket: `26475`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression where ``SessionBase.pop()`` returned ``None`` rather than "
"raising a ``KeyError`` for nonexistent values (:ticket:`26520`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú nuair a d'fhill ``SessionBase.pop () ```None`` seachas "
"`KeyError`` a ardú le haghaidh luachanna nach raibh ann (:ticket: `26520`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression causing the cached template loader to crash when using "
"template names starting with a dash (:ticket:`26536`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraíodh aischéimniú ina chúis leis an lódóir teimpléid taisceáilte nuair a "
"bhíonn ainmneacha teimpléad á n-úsáid ag tosú le sraigh (:ticket: `26536`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a ``makemessages`` regression where temporary ``.py`` extensions were "
"leaked in source file paths (:ticket:`26341`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraíodh aischéimniú ``makemessages`` inar sceitheadh síntí sealadacha "
"``.py`` i gcosáin comhad foinse (:ticket: `26341`)."

msgid "Django 1.9.7 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.9.7"

msgid "*June 4, 2016*"
msgstr "*4 Meitheamh, 2016*"

msgid "Django 1.9.7 fixes several bugs in 1.9.6."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.9.7 roinnt fabhtanna i 1.9.6."

msgid ""
"Removed the need for the ``request`` context processor on the admin login "
"page to fix a regression in 1.9 (:ticket:`26558`)."
msgstr ""
"Baineadh an gá atá leis an bpróiseálaí comhthéacs ``iarrata`` ar an "
"leathanach logála isteach riaracháin chun aischéimniú in 1.9 a shocrú "
"(:ticket: `26558`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed translation of password validators' ``help_text`` in forms "
"(:ticket:`26544`)."
msgstr ""
"Aistriúchán seasta de bhailíochtóirí pasfhocal “`help_text`` i bhfoirmeacha "
"(:ticket: `26544`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression causing the cached template loader to crash when using "
"lazy template names (:ticket:`26603`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú ina chúis leis an lódóir teimpléid taisceáilte nuair a "
"bhíonn ainmneacha teimpléad leisciúla á úsáid agat (:ticket: `26603`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``on_commit`` callbacks execution order when callbacks make "
"transactions (:ticket:`26627`)."
msgstr ""
"Ordú forghníomhaithe aisghlaonna ``on_commit`` seasta nuair a dhéanann "
"aisghlaonna idirbhearta (:ticket: `26627`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``HStoreField`` to raise a ``ValidationError`` instead of crashing on "
"non-dictionary JSON input (:ticket:`26672`)."
msgstr ""
"Seasta ``hStorefield`` chun ``ValidationError`` a ardú in ionad titim ar "
"ionchur JSON neamh-fhoclóir (:ticket: `26672`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``dbshell`` crash on PostgreSQL with an empty database name "
"(:ticket:`26698`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste seasta ``dbshell`` ar PostgreSQL le ainm bunachar sonraí folamh "
"(:ticket: `26698`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression in queries on a ``OneToOneField`` that has ``to_field`` "
"and ``primary_key=True`` (:ticket:`26667`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú i gceisteanna ar `OneTooneField`` a bhfuil ``to_field`` "
"agus ``primary_key=true`` (:ticket: `26667`)."

msgid "Django 1.9.8 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.9.8"

msgid "Django 1.9.8 fixes a security issue and several bugs in 1.9.7."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 1.9.8 saincheist slándála agus roinnt fabhtanna i 1.9.7."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``makemessages`` crash on Python 2 with non-ASCII file names "
"(:ticket:`26897`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste seasta ``makemessages`` ar Python 2 le hainmneacha comhaid neamh-"
"ASCII (:ticket: `26897`)."

msgid "Django 1.9.9 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 1.9.9"

msgid "Django 1.9.9 fixes several bugs in 1.9.8."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 1.9.9 roinnt fabhtanna i 1.9.8."

msgid ""
"Fixed invalid HTML in template postmortem on the debug page "
"(:ticket:`26938`)."
msgstr ""
"Seasta HTML neamhbhailí i dteimpléad postmortem ar an leathanach "
"dífhabhtaithe (:ticket: `26938`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed some GIS database function crashes on MySQL 5.7 (:ticket:`26657`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh roinnt timpeanna feidhme bunachar sonraí GIS ar MySQL 5.7 (:ticket: "
"`26657`)."

msgid "Django 2.0 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoileadh Django 2.0"

msgid "Welcome to Django 2.0!"
msgstr "Fáilte go dtí Django 2.0!"

msgid ""
"These release notes cover the :ref:`new features <whats-new-2.0>`, as well "
"as some :ref:`backwards incompatible changes <backwards-incompatible-2.0>` "
"you'll want to be aware of when upgrading from Django 1.11 or earlier. "
"We've :ref:`dropped some features<removed-features-2.0>` that have reached "
"the end of their deprecation cycle, and we've :ref:`begun the deprecation "
"process for some features <deprecated-features-2.0>`."
msgstr ""
"Clúdaíonn na nótaí scaoilte seo na:ref: `gnéithe nua <whats-new-2.0>`, chomh "
"maith le roinnt: ref: `athruithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha ar chúl<backwards-"
"incompatible-2.0>` a mbeidh tú ag iarraidh a bheith ar an eolas fúthu agus "
"tú ag uasghrádú ó Django 1.11 nó níos luaithe. <deprecated-"
"features-2.0>Chuireamar: Ref: `thit roinnt <removed-features-2.0>gnéithe `a "
"bhfuil deireadh a dtimthriall díghníomhaíochta bainte amach acu, agus "
"chuireamaire:ref: `thosaigh muid ar an bpróiseas díghníomhaíochta do roinnt "
"gnéithe`."

msgid ""
"This release starts Django's use of a :ref:`loose form of semantic "
"versioning <internal-release-cadence>`, but there aren't any major backwards "
"incompatible changes that might be expected of a 2.0 release. Upgrading "
"should be a similar amount of effort as past feature releases."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann an scaoileadh seo tús le húsáid Django as :ref:`foirm scaoilte de "
"leagan séimeantach <inmheánach-scaoileadh-cadence>`, ach níl aon athruithe "
"móra ar gcúl neamh-chomhoiriúnach a mbeifí ag súil leo ó eisiúint 2.0. Ba "
"cheart go mbeadh an oiread céanna iarrachta le huasghrádú agus a bhí "
"eisiúintí gné-ailt roimhe seo."

msgid ""
"Django 2.0 supports Python 3.4, 3.5, 3.6, and 3.7. We **highly recommend** "
"and only officially support the latest release of each series."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn Django 2.0 le Python 3.4, 3.5, 3.6, agus 3.7. Molaimid** go hard** "
"agus ní thacaímid go hoifigiúil ach leis an scaoileadh is déanaí de gach "
"sraith."

msgid "The Django 1.11.x series is the last to support Python 2.7."
msgstr ""
"Is é an tsraith Django 1.11.x an ceann deireanach a thacaíonn le Python 2.7."

msgid ""
"Django 2.0 will be the last release series to support Python 3.4. If you "
"plan a deployment of Python 3.4 beyond the end-of-life for Django 2.0 (April "
"2019), stick with Django 1.11 LTS (supported until April 2020) instead. "
"Note, however, that the end-of-life for Python 3.4 is March 2019."
msgstr ""
"Beidh Django 2.0 an tsraith scaoilte deireanach chun tacú le Python 3.4. Má "
"phleanálann tú Python 3.4 a imscaradh níos faide ná deireadh na saoil do "
"Django 2.0 (Aibreán 2019), cloí le Django 1.11 LTS (tacaíocht go dtí Aibreán "
"2020) ina ionad sin. Tabhair faoi deara, áfach, gurb é deireadh saoil Python "
"3.4 Márta 2019."

msgid "Third-party library support for older version of Django"
msgstr "Tacaíocht leabharlainne tríú páirtí le haghaidh leagan níos sine de D"

msgid ""
"Following the release of Django 2.0, we suggest that third-party app authors "
"drop support for all versions of Django prior to 1.11. At that time, you "
"should be able to run your package's tests using ``python -Wd`` so that "
"deprecation warnings do appear. After making the deprecation warning fixes, "
"your app should be compatible with Django 2.0."
msgstr ""
"Tar éis Django 2.0 a scaoileadh, molaimid go scaoilfidh údair aip tríú "
"páirtí tacaíocht do gach leagan de Django roimh 1.11. Ag an am sin, ba "
"cheart go mbeadh tú in ann tástálacha do phacáiste a reáchtáil ag baint "
"úsáide as `python -Wd`` ionas go mbeidh rabhaidh dífhabhtaithe le feiceáil. "
"Tar éis duit na socruithe rabhaidh díghrádaithe a dhéanamh, ba chóir go "
"mbeadh d'aip comhoiriúnach le Django 2.0."

msgid "What's new in Django 2.0"
msgstr "Cad atá nua i Django 2.0"

msgid "Simplified URL routing syntax"
msgstr "Comhréir ródaithe URL simplithe"

msgid ""
"The new :func:`django.urls.path()` function allows a simpler, more readable "
"URL routing syntax. For example, this example from previous Django releases::"
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn an fheidhm nua:func: `django.urls.path () `comhréir ródaithe URL "
"níos simplí, níos inléite. Mar shampla, an sampla seo ó eisiúintí Django "
"roimhe seo:"

msgid "could be written as::"
msgstr "d'fhéadfaí a scríobh mar:"

msgid ""
"The new syntax supports type coercion of URL parameters. In the example, the "
"view will receive the ``year`` keyword argument as an integer rather than as "
"a string. Also, the URLs that will match are slightly less constrained in "
"the rewritten example. For example, the year 10000 will now match since the "
"year integers aren't constrained to be exactly four digits long as they are "
"in the regular expression."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn an comhréireacht nua le cineál éigeantach ar pharaiméadair URL. Sa "
"sampla, gheobhaidh an dearcadh an argóint eochairfhocal ``blian` mar "
"shláimhir seachas mar shreang. Chomh maith leis sin, tá na URLanna a "
"mheaitseálfaidh sé beagán níos lú srianta sa sampla athscríofa. Mar shampla, "
"meaitneoidh an bliain 10000 anois ós rud é nach bhfuil sláimhreacha na "
"bliana srianta go díreach ceithre dhigit ar fad mar atá siad san abairt "
"rialta."

msgid ""
"The ``django.conf.urls.url()`` function from previous versions is now "
"available as :func:`django.urls.re_path`. The old location remains for "
"backwards compatibility, without an imminent deprecation. The old "
"``django.conf.urls.include()`` function is now importable from "
"``django.urls`` so you can use ``from django.urls import include, path, "
"re_path`` in your URLconfs."
msgstr ""
"Tá an fheidhm ``django.conf.urls.url () ``ó leaganacha roimhe seo ar fáil "
"anois mar: func: `django.urls.re_path`. Tá an sean-áit fós le haghaidh "
"comhoiriúnacht ar ais, gan díghabháil atá le teacht. Is féidir an sean-"
"fheidhm ``django.conf.urls.include () `allmhairithe anois ó ``django.urls "
"``ionas gur féidir leat ``ó django.urls allmhairiú include, path, re_path`` "
"a úsáid i do URLConfs."

msgid ""
"The :doc:`/topics/http/urls` document is rewritten to feature the new syntax "
"and provide more details."
msgstr ""
"Athscríobhtar an doiciméad:doc: `/topics/http/urls` chun an comhréiteach nua "
"a thaispeáint agus tuilleadh sonraí a sholáthar."

msgid "Mobile-friendly ``contrib.admin``"
msgstr "`contrib.admin`` atá cairdiúil don soghluaiste"

msgid ""
"The admin is now responsive and supports all major mobile devices. Older "
"browsers may experience varying levels of graceful degradation."
msgstr ""
"Tá an riarthóir sofhreagrach anois agus tacaíonn sé le gach mórghléas "
"soghluaiste. D’fhéadfadh leibhéil éagsúla díghrádaithe a bheith ag "
"brabhsálaithe níos sine."

msgid "Window expressions"
msgstr "Nathanna fuinneoige"

msgid ""
"The new :class:`~django.db.models.expressions.Window` expression allows "
"adding an ``OVER`` clause to querysets. You can use :ref:`window functions "
"<window-functions>` and :ref:`aggregate functions <aggregation-functions>` "
"in the expression."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an léiriú nua:class: `~django.db.Models.Expressions.Window` clásal "
"``OVER`` a chur le fiosraitheanna. <aggregation-functions>Is féidir "
"leat:ref: `feidhmeanna fuinneog <window-functions>`agus:ref: `feidhmeanna "
"comhiomlána` a úsáid sa abairt."

msgid ""
"The new :attr:`.ModelAdmin.autocomplete_fields` attribute "
"and :meth:`.ModelAdmin.get_autocomplete_fields` method allow using a "
"`Select2 <https://select2.org/>`_ search widget for ``ForeignKey`` and "
"``ManyToManyField``."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn an modh nua :attr:`.ModelAdmin.autocomplete_fields` "
"agus :meth:`.ModelAdmin.get_autocomplete_fields` giuirléid cuardaigh "
"`Select2 <https://select2.org/>`_ a úsáid le haghaidh ``ForeignKey` agus` "
"`ManyToManyField``."

msgid ""
"The default iteration count for the PBKDF2 password hasher is increased from "
"36,000 to 100,000."
msgstr ""
"Méadaítear an líon athraithe réamhshocraithe don hasher pasfhocal PBKDF2 ó "
"36,000 go 100,000."

msgid ""
"Added MySQL support for "
"the :class:`~django.contrib.gis.db.models.functions.AsGeoJSON` "
"function, :class:`~django.contrib.gis.db.models.functions.GeoHash` "
"function, :class:`~django.contrib.gis.db.models.functions.IsValid` "
"function, :lookup:`isvalid` lookup, and :ref:`distance lookups <distance-"
"lookups>`."
msgstr ""
"<distance-lookups>Cuireadh tacaíocht MySQL leis an bhfeidhm: class: "
"`~django.contrib.gis.db.models.functions.asgeojson`, :class: "
"`~django.contrib.gis.db.models.functions.geohash` feidhm, :class: "
"`~django.contrib.db.models.functions.is` feidhm, :lookup: `validisvalid`, "
"lookup agus:ref: `cuardach achair `."

msgid ""
"Added the :class:`~django.contrib.gis.db.models.functions.Azimuth` "
"and :class:`~django.contrib.gis.db.models.functions.LineLocatePoint` "
"functions, supported on PostGIS and SpatiaLite."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh se:class: `~django.contrib.gis.db.models.functions.azimuth` "
"agus:class: `~django.contrib.gis.db.models.functions.lineLocatePoint` "
"feidhmeanna, le tacaíocht ar PostGIS agus Spatialite."

msgid ""
"Any :class:`~django.contrib.gis.geos.GEOSGeometry` imported from GeoJSON now "
"has its SRID set."
msgstr ""
"Aon: Class: `~django.contrib.gis.geos.geosgeometry` allmhairithe ó GeoJSON "
"tá a tacar SRID anois."

msgid ""
"Added the :attr:`.OSMWidget.default_zoom` attribute to customize the map's "
"default zoom level."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh tréith: attr: `.osmwidget.default_zoom` leis chun leibhéal súmáil "
"réamhshocraithe an léarscáileáin a shaincheapadh."

msgid ""
"Made metadata readable and editable on rasters through "
"the :attr:`~django.contrib.gis.gdal.GDALRaster.metadata`, :attr:`~django.contrib.gis.gdal.GDALRaster.info`, "
"and :attr:`~django.contrib.gis.gdal.GDALBand.metadata` attributes."
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh meiteashonraí inléite agus in-eagarthóireachta ar rasters trí:attr: "
"`~django.contrib.gis.gdal.gdalraster.metadata`, :attr: "
"`~django.contrib.gis.gdal.gdalraster.info`, agus:attr: "
"`~django.contrib.gis.gdalband.metadata`."

msgid ""
"Allowed passing driver-specific creation options "
"to :class:`~django.contrib.gis.gdal.GDALRaster` objects using "
"``papsz_options``."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaítear roghanna cruthaithe tiománaí go sonrach a rith chuig: aicme: "
"`~django.contrib.gis.gdal.gdalraster` rudaí ag baint úsáide as "
"`papsz_options``."

msgid ""
"Allowed creating :class:`~django.contrib.gis.gdal.GDALRaster` objects in "
"GDAL's internal virtual filesystem. Rasters can now be :ref:`created from "
"and converted to binary data <gdal-raster-vsimem>` in-memory."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaítear rudaí a chruthó:class: `~django.contrib.gis.gdal.gdalraster` i "
"gcóras comhaid fíorúil inmheánach GDAL. <gdal-raster-vsimem>Is féidir le "
"Rasters a bheith anois: ref: `cruthaithe ó shonraí dénártha `i gcuimhne agus "
"a thiontú go sonraí dénártha."

msgid ""
"The new :meth:`GDALBand.color_interp() "
"<django.contrib.gis.gdal.GDALBand.color_interp>` method returns the color "
"interpretation for the band."
msgstr ""
"<django.contrib.gis.gdal.GDALBand.color_interp>Tugann an modh nua:meth: "
"`gdalband.color_interp () `an léirmhíniú datha don bhanda ar ais."

msgid ""
"The new ``distinct`` argument "
"for :class:`~django.contrib.postgres.aggregates.ArrayAgg` determines if "
"concatenated values will be distinct."
msgstr ""
"Cinneann an argóint nua ``distint`` do:class: "
"`~django.contrib.postgres.aggregates.ArrayAgg` an mbeidh luachanna "
"comhtháite ar leith."

msgid ""
"The new :class:`~django.contrib.postgres.functions.RandomUUID` database "
"function returns a version 4 UUID. It requires use of PostgreSQL's "
"``pgcrypto`` extension which can be activated using the "
"new :class:`~django.contrib.postgres.operations.CryptoExtension` migration "
"operation."
msgstr ""
"Tugann an fheidhm bunachar sonraí nua:class: "
"`~django.contrib.postgres.functions.randomuuid` leagan 4 UUID ar ais. "
"Éilíonn sé síneadh `pgcrypto`` PostgreSQL a úsáid ar féidir a ghníomhachtú "
"ag baint úsáide as an oibríocht imirce nua:class: "
"`~django.contrib.postgres.operations.cryptoextension`."

msgid ""
":class:`django.contrib.postgres.indexes.GinIndex` now supports the "
"``fastupdate`` and ``gin_pending_list_limit`` parameters."
msgstr ""
":class: Tacaíonn `django.contrib.postgres.indexes.ginIndex` anois leis na "
"paraiméadair ``fastupdate`` agus ``gin_pending_list_limit``."

msgid ""
"The new :class:`~django.contrib.postgres.indexes.GistIndex` class allows "
"creating ``GiST`` indexes in the database. The "
"new :class:`~django.contrib.postgres.operations.BtreeGistExtension` "
"migration operation installs the ``btree_gist`` extension to add support for "
"operator classes that aren't built-in."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn an rang nua:class: `~django.contrib.postgres.indexes.gistIndex` "
"innéacsanna `Gist`` a chruthú sa bhunachar sonraí. Suiteálann an oibríocht "
"imirce nua:class: `~django.contrib.postgres.operations.btreeGistExtension` "
"an síneadh ``btree_gist`` chun tacaíocht a chur le haghaidh ranganna "
"oibreora nach bhfuil ionsuite."

msgid ""
":djadmin:`inspectdb` can now introspect ``JSONField`` and various "
"``RangeField``\\s (``django.contrib.postgres`` must be in "
"``INSTALLED_APPS``)."
msgstr ""
":djadmin: Is féidir le `inspectdb` ``Jsonfield`` agus ``Rangefield``\\ s "
"éagsúla a ionchur anois (caithfidh ``django.contrib.postgres`` a bheith i "
"``INSTALLED_APPS``)."

msgid ""
"Added the ``protocol`` keyword argument to "
"the :class:`~django.contrib.sitemaps.GenericSitemap` constructor."
msgstr ""
"Chuir an argóint eochairfhocal ``protocol` leis an tógálaí:class: "
"`~django.contrib.siteMaps.GenericSiteMap`."

msgid ""
"``cache.set_many()`` now returns a list of keys that failed to be inserted. "
"For the built-in backends, failed inserts can only happen on memcached."
msgstr ""
"Tugann ``cache.set_many () ``liosta eochracha ar ais anois ar theip orthu a "
"chur isteach. Maidir leis na cúltaca ionsuite, ní féidir iontráil theip a "
"tharlú ach ar memcached."

msgid ""
":meth:`File.open() <django.core.files.File.open>` can be used as a context "
"manager, e.g. ``with file.open() as f:``."
msgstr ""
":meth: Is féidir `file.open () <django.core.files.File.open>`a úsáid mar "
"bhainisteoir comhthéacs, m.sh. `with file.open () mar f: ``."

msgid ""
"The new ``date_attrs`` and ``time_attrs`` arguments "
"for :class:`~django.forms.SplitDateTimeWidget` "
"and :class:`~django.forms.SplitHiddenDateTimeWidget` allow specifying "
"different HTML attributes for the ``DateInput`` and ``TimeInput`` (or "
"hidden) subwidgets."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn na hargóintí nua ``date_attrs`` agus ``time_attrs`` do:class: "
"`~django.forms.splitDateTimeWidget` agus:class: "
"`~django.forms.splithiddendateTimeWidget` tréithe HTML éagsúla a shonrú do "
"na fo-ghuirdeanna `DateInput`` agus `TimeInput`` (nó i bhfolach)."

msgid ""
"The new :meth:`Form.errors.get_json_data() "
"<django.forms.Form.errors.get_json_data>` method returns form errors as a "
"dictionary suitable for including in a JSON response."
msgstr ""
"Tugann an modh nua:meth: `form.errors.get_json_data () "
"<django.forms.Form.errors.get_json_data>`earráidí foirme ar ais mar fhoclóir "
"atá oiriúnach lena n-áireamh i bhfreagra JSON."

msgid ""
"The new :attr:`.ContextMixin.extra_context` attribute allows adding context "
"in ``View.as_view()``."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn an tréith nua:attr: `.contextMixin.extra_context` comhthéacs a "
"chur i ``View.as_view () ``."

msgid ""
":djadmin:`inspectdb` now translates MySQL's unsigned integer columns to "
"``PositiveIntegerField`` or ``PositiveSmallIntegerField``."
msgstr ""
": djadmin: aistríonn `inspectdb` anois colúin sláimhir neamhshínithe MySQL "
"go ``PositiveIntegerField`` nó ``PositiveSmallIntegerField``."

msgid ""
"The new :option:`makemessages --add-location` option controls the comment "
"format in ``.po`` files."
msgstr ""
"Rialaíonn an rogha nua:option: `makemessages --add-location` an fhormáid "
"tráchta i gcomhaid ``.po``."

msgid ""
":djadmin:`loaddata` can now :ref:`read from stdin <loading-fixtures-stdin>`."
msgstr ""
"<loading-fixtures-stdin>:djadmin: Is féidir le `loaddata` anois:ref: `léamh "
"ó stdin `."

msgid ""
"The new :option:`diffsettings --output` option allows formatting the output "
"in a unified diff format."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an rogha nua:option: `diffsettings --output` an t-aschur a "
"fhormáidiú i bhformáid diff aontaithe."

msgid ""
"On Oracle, :djadmin:`inspectdb` can now introspect ``AutoField`` if the "
"column is created as an identity column."
msgstr ""
"Ar Oracle, is féidir le: djadmin: `inspectdb` iontráil anois ``Autofield`` "
"má chruthaítear an colún mar cholún aitheantais."

msgid "On MySQL, :djadmin:`dbshell` now supports client-side TLS certificates."
msgstr ""
"Ar MySQL, tacaíonn: djadmin: `dbshell` le deimhnithe TLS ar thaobh an "
"chliaint anois."

msgid ""
"The new :option:`squashmigrations --squashed-name` option allows naming the "
"squashed migration."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an rogha nua:option: `squashmigrations --squashed-name` an imirce "
"squashed a ainmniú."

msgid ""
"The new :class:`~django.db.models.functions.StrIndex` database function "
"finds the starting index of a string inside another string."
msgstr ""
"Faigheann an fheidhm bunachar sonraí nua:class: "
"`~django.db.models.functions.strIndex` innéacs tosaigh teaghrán taobh istigh "
"de shreang eile."

msgid ""
"On Oracle, ``AutoField`` and ``BigAutoField`` are now created as `identity "
"columns <https://docs.oracle.com/en/database/oracle/oracle-database/21/"
"drdaa/ intro-to-tools-and-products-supporting-migraiton.html#GUID-14E4817B-"
"F3BC-4D99 -B471-A0ACDC303CC9>`__."
msgstr ""
"< https://docs.oracle.com/en/database/oracle/oracle-database/21/drdaa/ intro-"
"to-tools-and-products-supporting-migraiton.html #GUID -14E4817B-F3BC-4D99 "
"-B471-A0ACDC303CC9>Ar Oracle, cruthaítear ``AutoField`` agus "
"``BigAutoField`` anois mar `colúin aitheantais `__."

msgid ""
"The new ``chunk_size`` parameter of :meth:`.QuerySet.iterator` controls the "
"number of rows fetched by the Python database client when streaming results "
"from the database. For databases that don't support server-side cursors, it "
"controls the number of results Django fetches from the database adapter."
msgstr ""
"Rialaíonn an paraiméadar nua ``chunk_size`` de:meth: `.queryset.iterator` "
"líon na sraitheanna a fhaigheann cliant bunachar sonraí Python agus torthaí "
"á sruthú ón mbunachar sonraí. Maidir le bunachair sonraí nach dtacaíonn le "
"cúrsóirí taobh an fhreastalaí, rialaíonn sé líon na dtorthaí a fhaigheann "
"Django ón oiriúnóir bunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
":meth:`.QuerySet.earliest`, :meth:`.QuerySet.latest`, "
"and :attr:`Meta.get_latest_by <django.db.models.Options.get_latest_by>` now "
"allow ordering by several fields."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.Options.get_latest_by>:meth: `.querySet.Earliest`, :meth: "
"`.queryset.latest`, agus:attr: `Meta.get_latest_by `ceadaíonn ordú anois ag "
"roinnt réimsí."

msgid ""
"Added the :class:`~django.db.models.functions.ExtractQuarter` function to "
"extract the quarter from :class:`~django.db.models.DateField` "
"and :class:`~django.db.models.DateTimeField`, and exposed it through "
"the :lookup:`quarter` lookup."
msgstr ""
"Chuir an fheidhm: class: `~django.db.Models.Functions.ExtractQuarter` leis "
"chun an ráithe a bhaint ó:class: `~django.db.models.dateField` agus:class: "
"`~Django.db.Models.DateTimeField`, agus nochtaigh sé tríd an cuardach: "
"`quarter`."

msgid ""
"Added the :class:`~django.db.models.functions.TruncQuarter` function to "
"truncate :class:`~django.db.models.DateField` "
"and :class:`~django.db.models.DateTimeField` to the first day of a quarter."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an fheidhme:class: `~django.db.models.functions.truncQuarter` leis "
"an bhfeidhm chuig: class: `~Django.db.Models.DateField` agus:class: "
"`~Django.db.Models.DateTimeField` go dtí an chéad lá den ráithe."

msgid ""
"Added the :attr:`~django.db.models.Index.db_tablespace` parameter to class-"
"based indexes."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh paraiméadar: attr: `~django.db.models.index.db_TableSpace` le "
"hinnéacsanna aicme-bhunaithe."

msgid ""
"If the database supports a native duration field (Oracle and "
"PostgreSQL), :class:`~django.db.models.functions.Extract` now works "
"with :class:`~django.db.models.DurationField`."
msgstr ""
"Má thacaíonn an bunachar sonraí le réimse dúchasach fad (Oracle agus "
"PostgreSQL), oibríonn:: class: `~Django.db.Models.Functions.Extract` anois "
"len:class: `~Django.db.Models.DurationField`."

msgid ""
"Added the ``of`` argument to :meth:`.QuerySet.select_for_update()`, "
"supported on PostgreSQL and Oracle, to lock only rows from specific tables "
"rather than all selected tables. It may be helpful particularly "
"when :meth:`~.QuerySet.select_for_update()` is used in conjunction "
"with :meth:`~.QuerySet.select_related()`."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an argóint `of ``chuig: meth: `.queryset.select_for_update () `, le "
"tacaíocht ar PostgreSQL agus Oracle, chun sraitheanna amháin a ghlasáil ó "
"tháblaí ar leith seachas gach tábla roghnaithe. D'fhéadfadh sé a bheith "
"cabhrach go háirithe nuair a úsáidtear: meth: `~.queryset.select_for_update "
"() `i gcomhar le:meth: `~.queryset.select_related ()`."

msgid ""
"The new ``field_name`` parameter of :meth:`.QuerySet.in_bulk` allows "
"fetching results based on any unique model field."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann paraiméadar nua ``field_name`` de:meth: `.queryset.in_bulk` torthaí "
"a fháil bunaithe ar aon réimse samhail uathúil."

msgid ""
":meth:`.CursorWrapper.callproc()` now takes an optional dictionary of "
"keyword parameters, if the backend supports this feature. Of Django's built-"
"in backends, only Oracle supports it."
msgstr ""
": meth: `.cursorWrapper.callProc () `glacann foclóir roghnach de "
"pharaiméadair eochairfhocal anois, má thacaíonn an cúltaca leis an ngné seo. "
"De chúltaca ionsuite Django, ní thacaíonn ach Oracle leis."

msgid ""
"The new :meth:`connection.execute_wrapper() "
"<django.db.backends.base.DatabaseWrapper.execute_wrapper>` method "
"allows :doc:`installing wrappers around execution of database queries </"
"topics/db/instrumentation>`."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn an modh nua:meth: `connection.execute_wrapper () </topics/db/"
"instrumentation> <django.db.backends.base.DatabaseWrapper.execute_wrapper>`: "
"doc: `fillteáin a shuiteáil timpeall ceisteanna bunachar sonraí a "
"fhorghníomhú."

msgid ""
"The new ``filter`` argument for built-in aggregates allows :ref:`adding "
"different conditionals <conditional-aggregation>` to multiple aggregations "
"over the same fields or relations."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn an argóint nua ``scagair`` le haghaidh comhiomláin ionsuite: ref: "
"`coinníollacha éagsúla a chur leis na comhiomlánaithe iolracha thar na "
"réimsí nó na caidrimh cé <conditional-aggregation>anna."

msgid ""
"Added support for expressions in :attr:`Meta.ordering "
"<django.db.models.Options.ordering>`."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.Options.ordering>Tacaíocht bhreise le haghaidh abairtí "
"in:attr: `Meta.ording `."

msgid ""
"The new ``named`` parameter of :meth:`.QuerySet.values_list` allows fetching "
"results as named tuples."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn an paraiméadar nua ``ainmnithe ``de:meth: `.queryset.values_list` "
"torthaí a fháil mar tuples ainmnithe."

msgid ""
"The new :class:`.FilteredRelation` class allows adding an ``ON`` clause to "
"querysets."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn an rang nua:class: `.filteredRelation` clásal ``ON`` a chur le "
"fiosraitheanna."

msgid "Pagination"
msgstr "Leathanaigh"

msgid ""
"Added :meth:`Paginator.get_page() "
"<django.core.paginator.Paginator.get_page>` to provide the documented "
"pattern of handling invalid page numbers."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh leis: Meth: `Paginator.get_page () "
"<django.core.paginator.Paginator.get_page>`chun an patrún doiciméadaithe "
"maidir le láimhseáil uimhreacha leathanaigh neamhbhailí a sholáthar."

msgid "The :djadmin:`runserver` web server supports HTTP 1.1."
msgstr "Tacaíonn freastalaí gréasáin djaDmin: `runserver` le HTTP 1.1."

msgid ""
"To increase the usefulness of :meth:`.Engine.get_default` in third-party "
"apps, it now returns the first engine if multiple ``DjangoTemplates`` "
"engines are configured in ``TEMPLATES`` rather than raising "
"``ImproperlyConfigured``."
msgstr ""
"Chun úsáideacht: meth: `.engine.get_default` a mhéadú in aipeanna tríú "
"páirtí, filleann sé an chéad inneall anois má chuirtear ilinnill "
"``DjangoTemplates ``cumraithe i `TEMPLATES`` seachas "
"``ImproperlyConfigured`` a ardú."

msgid "Custom template tags may now accept keyword-only arguments."
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh clibeanna teimpléid saincheaptha glacadh le hargóintí "
"eochairfhocail amháin."

msgid "Added threading support to :class:`~django.test.LiveServerTestCase`."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh tacaíocht snáithe leis chuig: class: "
"`~django.test.liveservertestcase`."

msgid ""
"Added settings that allow customizing the test tablespace parameters for "
"Oracle: :setting:`DATAFILE_SIZE`, :setting:`DATAFILE_TMP_SIZE`, :setting:`DATAFILE_EXTSIZE`, "
"and :setting:`DATAFILE_TMP_EXTSIZE`."
msgstr ""
"Socruithe breise a cheadaíonn na paraiméadair spás tábla tástála a "
"shaincheapadh do Oracle: :setting: `DATAFILE_SIZE`, :setting: "
"`DATAFILE_TMP_SIZE`, :setting: `DATAFILE_EXTSIZE`, agus:setting: "
"`DATAFILE_TMP_EXTSIZE`."

msgid ""
"The new :class:`.ProhibitNullCharactersValidator` disallows the null "
"character in the input of the :class:`~django.forms.CharField` form field "
"and its subclasses. Null character input was observed from vulnerability "
"scanning tools. Most databases silently discard null characters, but "
"psycopg2 2.7+ raises an exception when trying to save a null character to a "
"char/text field with PostgreSQL."
msgstr ""
"Ní cheadaíonn an nua:class: `.prohibitNullCharactersValidator` an carachtar "
"null i ionchur an réimse foirme:class: `~django.forms.charfield` agus a fho-"
"aicmí. Breathnaíodh ionchur carachtar null ó uirlisí scanadh leochaileachta "
"Caitheann an chuid is mó de na bunachair sonraí carachtair neall go ciúin, "
"ach ardaíonn psycopg2 2.7+ eisceacht agus tú ag iarraidh carachtar neall a "
"shábháil i réimse char/téacs le PostgreSQL."

msgid "Backwards incompatible changes in 2.0"
msgstr "Athruithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha ar ais i 2.0"

msgid "Removed support for bytestrings in some places"
msgstr "Tacaíocht bainte le haghaidh bytestrings in áiteanna áirithe"

msgid ""
"To support native Python 2 strings, older Django versions had to accept both "
"bytestrings and Unicode strings. Now that Python 2 support is dropped, "
"bytestrings should only be encountered around input/output boundaries "
"(handling of binary fields or HTTP streams, for example). You might have to "
"update your code to limit bytestring usage to a minimum, as Django no longer "
"accepts bytestrings in certain code paths. Python's :option:`-b` option may "
"help detect that mistake in your code."
msgstr ""
"Chun tacú le teaghráin dúchasacha Python 2, b'éigean do leaganacha níos sine "
"Django glacadh le teaghráin bytestrings agus teaghráin Unicode araon. Anois "
"go bhfuil tacaíocht Python 2 titim, níor cheart teacht le bytestrings ach "
"timpeall teorainneacha ionchuir/aschuir (láimhseáil réimsí dénártha nó "
"sruthanna HTTP, mar shampla). B'fhéidir go mbeidh ort do chód a nuashonrú "
"chun úsáid bytestring a theorannú go dtí a laghad, mar ní ghlacann Django le "
"bytestrings i gcosáin cód áirithe a thuilleadh. Python's:option: d'fhéadfadh "
"rogha `-b` cabhrú leis an botún sin i do chód a bhrath."

msgid ""
"For example, ``reverse()`` now uses ``str()`` instead of ``force_text()`` to "
"coerce the ``args`` and ``kwargs`` it receives, prior to their placement in "
"the URL. For bytestrings, this creates a string with an undesired ``b`` "
"prefix as well as additional quotes (``str(b'foo')`` is ``\"b'foo'\"``). To "
"adapt, call ``decode()`` on the bytestring before passing it to "
"``reverse()``."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, úsáideann ``reverse () ``anois ``str ()`` ``in ionad "
"``force_text ()`` chun na `args`` agus `kwar`gs`` a fhaigheann sé a chur "
"faoi iallach sula gcuirtear iad a shocrú sa URL. Maidir le bytestrings, "
"cruthaíonn sé seo sreang le réimír ``b`` neamh-inmhianaithe chomh maith le "
"luachana breise (``str (b'foo') ``is ````b'foo'\"``). Chun oiriúnú, glaoigh "
"ar `decode () ``ar an mbytestring sula ndéantar é a chur chuig ``reverse "
"()``."

msgid ""
"The ``DatabaseOperations.datetime_cast_date_sql()``, "
"``datetime_cast_time_sql()``, ``datetime_trunc_sql()``, "
"``datetime_extract_sql()``, and ``date_interval_sql()`` methods now return "
"only the SQL to perform the operation instead of SQL and a list of "
"parameters."
msgstr ""
"Ní fhilleann na modhanna ``DatabaseOperations.dateTime_Cast_Date_SQL () ``, "
"`datetime_cast_time_sql ()``, `datetime_trunc_sql () ``, "
"`datetime_extract_sql ()``, agus ``date_interval_sql () ``ach an SQL a "
"dhéanamh chun an oibríocht a dhéanamh in ionad SQL agus SQL liosta de na "
"paraiméadair."

msgid ""
"Third-party database backends should add a ``DatabaseWrapper.display_name`` "
"attribute with the name of the database that your backend works with. Django "
"may use it in various messages, such as in system checks."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go gcuirfeadh cúltaca bunachar sonraí tríú páirtí tréith "
"``DatabaseWrapper.display_name`` leis ainm an bhunachar sonraí a oibríonn do "
"chúltaca leis. Féadfaidh Django é a úsáid i dteachtaireachtaí éagsúla, mar "
"shampla i seiceálacha córais."

msgid ""
"The first argument of ``SchemaEditor._alter_column_type_sql()`` is now "
"``model`` rather than ``table``."
msgstr ""
"An chéad argóint de ``SchemaEditor. Is é _alter_column_type_sql () ``anois "
"``samhail`` seachas ``tábla ``."

msgid ""
"The first argument of ``SchemaEditor._create_index_name()`` is now "
"``table_name`` rather than ``model``."
msgstr ""
"An chéad argóint de ``SchemaEditor. Is é _create_index_name () ``anois "
"``table_name`` seachas ``model``."

msgid ""
"To enable ``FOR UPDATE OF`` support, set "
"``DatabaseFeatures.has_select_for_update_of = True``. If the database "
"requires that the arguments to ``OF`` be columns rather than tables, set "
"``DatabaseFeatures.select_for_update_of_column = True``."
msgstr ""
"Chun tacaíocht ``FOR UPDATE OF ``a chumasú, socraigh`` "
"databaseFeatures.HAS_SELECT_FOR_UPDATE_OF = True``. Má éilíonn an bunachar "
"sonraí go mbeidh na hargóintí le `OF`` ná colúin seachas táblaí, socraigh "
"``databaseFeatures.select_for_update_of_column = True``."

msgid ""
"To enable support for :class:`~django.db.models.expressions.Window` "
"expressions, set ``DatabaseFeatures.supports_over_clause`` to ``True``. You "
"may need to customize the "
"``DatabaseOperations.window_start_rows_start_end()`` and/or "
"``window_start_range_start_end()`` methods."
msgstr ""
"Chun tacaíocht do: class: `~Django.db.Models.Expressions.Window` a chumasú, "
"socraigh ``DatabaseFeatures.supports_over_clause`` go ``True``. B'fhéidir go "
"mbeidh ort na modhanna ``databaseOperations.window_start_rows_start_end () "
"``agus/nó ``window_start_range_start_end ()`` a shaincheapadh."

msgid ""
"Third-party database backends should add a "
"``DatabaseOperations.cast_char_field_without_max_length`` attribute with the "
"database data type that will be used in "
"the :class:`~django.db.models.functions.Cast` function for a ``CharField`` "
"if the ``max_length`` argument isn't provided."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go gcuirfeadh cúltaca bunachar sonraí tríú tríú tríú tréith "
"``databaseOperations.cast_char_field_without_max_length ``leis an gcineál "
"sonraí bunachar sonraí a úsáidfear san fheidhm :class: "
"`~django.db.models.functions.cast` le haghaidh ``charfield`` mura gcuirtear "
"an argóint `max_length``."

msgid ""
"The first argument of ``DatabaseCreation._clone_test_db()`` and "
"``get_test_db_clone_settings()`` is now ``suffix`` rather than ``number`` "
"(in case you want to rename the signatures in your backend for consistency). "
"``django.test`` also now passes those values as strings rather than as "
"integers."
msgstr ""
"An chéad argóint de ``DatabaseCreation. Is é _clone_test_db () ``agus "
"``get_test_db_clone_settings ()`` anois ``suffix`` seachas ``uimhre`` (i "
"gcás gur mhaith leat na sínithe i do chúlcheann a athainmniú le haghaidh "
"comhsheasmhachta). Téann ``django.test`` anois ar na luachanna sin mar "
"shreangáin seachas mar shláimhreacha."

msgid ""
"Third-party database backends should add a "
"``DatabaseIntrospection.get_sequences()`` method based on the stub in "
"``BaseDatabaseIntrospection``."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go gcuirfeadh cúltaca bunachar sonraí tríú páirtí modh "
"``DatabaseIntrospection.get_sequences ()`` a chur leis bunaithe ar an stub i "
"``BaseDatabaseIntrospection`."

msgid "Dropped support for Oracle 11.2"
msgstr "Tacaíocht titim do Oracle 11.2"

msgid ""
"The end of upstream support for Oracle 11.2 is Dec. 2020. Django 1.11 will "
"be supported until April 2020 which almost reaches this date. Django 2.0 "
"officially supports Oracle 12.1+."
msgstr ""
"Is é deireadh na tacaíochta suas srutha do Oracle 11.2 ná Nollaig 2020. "
"Tacófar le Django 1.11 go dtí Aibreán 2020 a shroicheann beagnach an dáta "
"seo. Tacaíonn Django 2.0 go hoifigiúil le Oracle 12.1+."

msgid "Default MySQL isolation level is read committed"
msgstr "Léitear leibhéal aonrúcháin réamhshocraithe MySQL"

msgid ""
"MySQL's default isolation level, repeatable read, may cause data loss in "
"typical Django usage. To prevent that and for consistency with other "
"databases, the default isolation level is now read committed. You can use "
"the :setting:`DATABASES` setting to :ref:`use a different isolation level "
"<mysql-isolation-level>`, if needed."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh leibhéal aonrú réamhshocraithe MySQL, inléite athsheolta, a "
"bheith ina chúis le caillteanas sonraí i ngnáthúsáid Chun é sin a chosc agus "
"chun comhsheasmhacht le bunachair sonraí eile, léitear an leibhéal aonraithe "
"réamhshocraithe tiomanta <mysql-isolation-level>Is féidir leat an socrú: "
"setting: `DATABASES` a úsáid chó:ref: `úsáid leibhéal aonraithe difriúil `, "
"más gá."

msgid ""
":attr:`AbstractUser.last_name <django.contrib.auth.models.User.last_name>` "
"``max_length`` increased to 150"
msgstr ""
"<django.contrib.auth.models.User.last_name>:attr: `Abstractuser.last_name "
"```max_length ``méadaithe go 150"

msgid ""
"A migration for :attr:`django.contrib.auth.models.User.last_name` is "
"included. If you have a custom user model inheriting from ``AbstractUser``, "
"you'll need to generate and apply a database migration for your user model."
msgstr ""
"Tá imirce le haghaidh: attr: `django.contrib.auth.models.user.last_name` san "
"áireamh. Má tá samhail úsáideora saincheaptha agat ag oidhreacht ó "
"``AbstractUser`, beidh ort imirce bunachar sonraí a ghiniúint agus a chur i "
"bhfeidhm do do mhúnla úsáideora."

msgid ""
"If you want to preserve the 30 character limit for last names, use a custom "
"form::"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat an teorainn 30 carachtar d'ainmneacha deireanacha a chaomhnú, "
"bain úsáid as foirm saincheaptha:"

msgid ""
"If you wish to keep this restriction in the admin when editing users, set "
"``UserAdmin.form`` to use this form::"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat an srian seo a choinneáil sa riarachán agus tú ag "
"eagarthóireacht úsáideoirí, socraigh ``UserAdmin.form`` chun an fhoirm seo a "
"úsáid:"

msgid "``QuerySet.reverse()`` and ``last()`` are prohibited after slicing"
msgstr "Tá cosc ar ``QuerySet.reverse () ``agus ``last ()`` tar éis slisnú"

msgid ""
"Calling ``QuerySet.reverse()`` or ``last()`` on a sliced queryset leads to "
"unexpected results due to the slice being applied after reordering. This is "
"now prohibited, e.g.:"
msgstr ""
"Mar thoradh ar ``QuerySet.reverse () ``nó ``last ()`` a ghlaoch ar shraith "
"cheisteanna slisnaithe bíonn torthaí gan choinne mar gheall ar an slisnacht "
"á chur i bhfeidhm tar éis athordú. Tá cosc air seo anois, m.sh.:"

msgid "Form fields no longer accept optional arguments as positional arguments"
msgstr "Ní ghlacann réimsí foirme le hargóintí roghnacha a thuilleadh mar"

msgid ""
"To help prevent runtime errors due to incorrect ordering of form field "
"arguments, optional arguments of built-in form fields are no longer accepted "
"as positional arguments. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Chun cabhrú le hearráidí reatha a chosc mar gheall ar ordú mícheart argóintí "
"réimse foirme, ní ghlactar le hargóintí roghnacha réimsí foirme ionsuite mar "
"argóintí seasaim Mar shampla::"

msgid "raises an exception and should be replaced with::"
msgstr ""
"ardaíonn eisceacht agus ba chóir na nithe seo a leanas a chur in ionad:"

msgid "``call_command()`` validates the options it receives"
msgstr "Bailíonn ``call_command () ``na roghanna a fhaigheann sé"

msgid ""
"``call_command()`` now validates that the argument parser of the command "
"being called defines all of the options passed to ``call_command()``."
msgstr ""
"Bailíonn ``call_command () ``anois go sainmhíníonn parser argóint an "
"ordaithe atá á glaoch ar na roghanna go léir a chuirtear chuig "
"``call_command ()``."

msgid ""
"For custom management commands that use options not created using "
"``parser.add_argument()``, add a ``stealth_options`` attribute on the "
"command::"
msgstr ""
"Maidir le horduithe bainistíochta saincheaptha a úsáideann roghanna nach "
"cruthaíodh ag baint úsáide as `parser.add_argument () `, cuir tréith "
"``stealth_options`` ar an ordú:"

msgid "Indexes no longer accept positional arguments"
msgstr "Ní ghlacann innéacsanna le hargóintí seasaimh a thuil"

msgid "Foreign key constraints are now enabled on SQLite"
msgstr "Tá príomhshrianta eachtracha cumasaithe anois ar SQLite"

msgid ""
"This will appear as a backwards-incompatible change (``IntegrityError: "
"FOREIGN KEY constraint failed``) if attempting to save an existing model "
"instance that's violating a foreign key constraint."
msgstr ""
"Beidh sé seo le feiceáil mar athrú neamh-chomhoiriúnach ar chúl "
"(``IntegrityError: theip ar srian EOCHAIR FOREIGN ``) má dhéanann iarracht "
"samhail shampla atá ann cheana a shábháil atá ag sárú srian eochair "
"eachtrach."

msgid ""
"Foreign keys are now created with ``DEFERRABLE INITIALLY DEFERRED`` instead "
"of ``DEFERRABLE IMMEDIATE``. Thus, tables may need to be rebuilt to recreate "
"foreign keys with the new definition, particularly if you're using a pattern "
"like this::"
msgstr ""
"Cruthaítear eochracha eachtracha anois le ``DEFERRABLE INICIALLY ATFERRED`` "
"in ionad ``IDIRLEABLE IMMEDIATE``. Dá bhrí sin, b'fhéidir go gcaithfear "
"táblaí a atógáil chun eochracha eachtracha a athchruthú leis an sainmhíniú "
"nua, go háirithe má tá patrún mar seo á úsáid agat:"

msgid ""
"If you don't recreate the foreign key as ``DEFERRED``, the first "
"``create()`` would fail now that foreign key constraints are enforced."
msgstr ""
"Mura ndéanann tú an eochair eachtrach a athchruthú mar ``DEFERRED`, theip ar "
"an gcéad ``create () ``anois go ndéantar srianta eochairí eachtracha i "
"bhfeidhm."

msgid ""
"Backup your database first! After upgrading to Django 2.0, you can then "
"rebuild tables using a script similar to this::"
msgstr ""
"Cúltaca do bhunachar sonraí ar dtús Tar éis duit uasghrádú a dhéanamh go "
"Django 2.0, is féidir leat táblaí a atógáil ag baint úsáide as script cosúil "
"leis seo:"

msgid ""
"This script hasn't received extensive testing and needs adaption for various "
"cases such as multiple databases. Feel free to contribute improvements."
msgstr ""
"Níor fuair an script seo tástáil fhairsing agus teastaíonn oiriúnú de dhíth "
"le cásanna éagsúla mar iolracha bunachair Ná bíodh leisce ort feabhsuithe a "
"chur leis."

msgid ""
"In addition, because of a table alteration limitation of SQLite, it's "
"prohibited to perform :class:`~django.db.migrations.operations.RenameModel` "
"and :class:`~django.db.migrations.operations.RenameField` operations on "
"models or fields referenced by other models in a transaction. In order to "
"allow migrations containing these operations to be applied, you must set the "
"``Migration.atomic`` attribute to ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, mar gheall ar theorannú athraithe tábla ar SQLite, tá sé "
"toirmiscthe oibríochtaí: Class: "
"`~Django.db.Migrations.Operations.RenameModel` agus:class: "
"`~django.db.migrations.operations.RenameField` a dhéanamh ar mhúnlaí nó "
"réimsí dá dtagraíonn samhlacha eile in idirbheart. D'fhonn ligean imirce ina "
"bhfuil na hoibríochtaí seo a chur i bhfeidhm, ní mór duit an tréith "
"``Migration.Atomic` a shocrú go `False`."

msgid ""
"The ``SessionAuthenticationMiddleware`` class is removed. It provided no "
"functionality since session authentication is unconditionally enabled in "
"Django 1.10."
msgstr ""
"Baintear an rang ``SessionAuthenticationMiddleware`` as. Níor chuir sé "
"feidhmiúlacht ar bith ar fáil ós rud é go bhfuil fíordheimhniú seisiún "
"cumasaithe gan choinníoll in Django 1.10."

msgid ""
"The default HTTP error handlers (``handler404``, etc.) are now callables "
"instead of dotted Python path strings. Django favors callable references "
"since they provide better performance and debugging experience."
msgstr ""
"Tá na láimhseálaithe réamhshocraithe earráide HTTP (`` láimhseálaí404``, "
"etc.) inghlaoite anois in ionad teaghráin chonair Python poncaithe. Is fearr "
"le Django tagairtí inghlaoite toisc go soláthraíonn siad feidhmíocht níos "
"fearr agus taithí dífhabhtaithe."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.views.generic.base.RedirectView` no longer silences "
"``NoReverseMatch`` if the ``pattern_name`` doesn't exist."
msgstr ""
":class: `~Django.Views.Generic.Base.RedirectView` ní thostaíonn "
"``NoReverseMatch`` a thuilleadh mura bhfuil an ``pattern_name`` ann."

msgid ""
"When ``USE_L10N`` is off, :class:`~django.forms.FloatField` "
"and :class:`~django.forms.DecimalField` now "
"respect :setting:`DECIMAL_SEPARATOR` and :setting:`THOUSAND_SEPARATOR` "
"during validation. For example, with the settings::"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhíonn `USE_L10N`` as, :class: `~django.forms.floatfield` "
"agus:class: `~django.forms.decimalfield` anois:setting: `DECIMAL_SEPARATOR` "
"agus:setting: `THOUSAND_SEPARATOR` agus: setting: `THOUSAND_SEPARATOR` le "
"linn bailíochtaithe. Mar shampla, leis na socruithe::"

msgid ""
"an input of ``\"1.345\"`` is now converted to ``1345`` instead of ``1.345``."
msgstr ""
"déantar ionchur de ``\"1.345\"` a thiontú anois go ``1345`` in ionad ``1.345 "
"``."

msgid ""
"Subclasses of :class:`~django.contrib.auth.models.AbstractBaseUser` are no "
"longer required to implement ``get_short_name()`` and ``get_full_name()``. "
"(The base implementations that raise ``NotImplementedError`` are removed.) "
"``django.contrib.admin`` uses these methods if implemented but doesn't "
"require them. Third-party apps that use these methods may want to adopt a "
"similar approach."
msgstr ""
"Níl fo-aicmí de :class:`~django.contrib.auth.models.AbstractBaseUser` ag "
"teastáil a thuilleadh chun ``get_short_name()`` agus ``get_full_name()`` a "
"chur i bhfeidhm. (Baintear na bunfheidhmithe a ardaíonn "
"``NotImplementedError``.) Úsáideann ``django.contrib.admin`` na modhanna seo "
"má chuirtear i bhfeidhm iad ach níl siad de dhíth. B’fhéidir gur mhaith le "
"haipeanna tríú páirtí a úsáideann na modhanna seo cur chuige comhchosúil a "
"ghlacadh."

msgid ""
"The ``FIRST_DAY_OF_WEEK`` and ``NUMBER_GROUPING`` format settings are now "
"kept as integers in JavaScript and JSON i18n view outputs."
msgstr ""
"Coinnítear na socruithe formáide ``FIRST_DAY_OF_WEEK`` agus "
"``NUMBER_GROUPING`` anois mar shláimhreacha in aschuir amharc JavaScript "
"agus JSON i18n."

msgid ""
":meth:`~django.test.TransactionTestCase.assertNumQueries` now ignores "
"connection configuration queries. Previously, if a test opened a new "
"database connection, those queries could be included as part of the "
"``assertNumQueries()`` count."
msgstr ""
":meth: `~django.test.transactionTestCase.assertNumQueries` neamhaird anois "
"ar cheisteanna cumraíochta nasc. Roimhe seo, má d'oscail tástáil nasc nua "
"bunachar sonraí, d'fhéadfaí na ceisteanna sin a áireamh mar chuid den "
"chomhaireamh ``assertNumQueries () ``."

msgid ""
"The default size of the Oracle test tablespace is increased from 20M to 50M "
"and the default autoextend size is increased from 10M to 25M."
msgstr ""
"Méadaítear méid réamhshocraithe spáis tábla tástála Oracle ó 20M go 50M agus "
"méadaítear an méid réamhshocraithe uathoibríoch ó 10M go 25M."

msgid ""
"To improve performance when streaming large result sets from the "
"database, :meth:`.QuerySet.iterator` now fetches 2000 rows at a time instead "
"of 100. The old behavior can be restored using the ``chunk_size`` parameter. "
"For example::"
msgstr ""
"Chun feidhmíocht a fheabhsú agus tacair mhóra torthaí á sruthú ón mbunachar "
"sonraí, faigheann: meth: `.queryset.iterator` 2000 sraitheanna ag an am "
"anois in ionad 100. Is féidir an sean-iompar a athbhunú ag baint úsáide as "
"an paraiméadar ``chunk_size``. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"Providing unknown package names in the ``packages`` argument of "
"the :class:`~django.views.i18n.JavaScriptCatalog` view now raises "
"``ValueError`` instead of passing silently."
msgstr ""
"Ardaíonn ainmneacha pacáiste anaithnid a sholáthar san argóint ``packages`` "
"den :class: `~django.views.i18n.javascriptCatalog` amharc ``valueError`` "
"anois in ionad dul go ciúin."

msgid ""
"A model instance's primary key now appears in the default "
"``Model.__str__()`` method, e.g. ``Question object (1)``."
msgstr ""
"Tá príomh-eochair samhail le feiceáil anois sa réamhshocraithe ``Samhail. "
"__str__ () ``modh, m.sh. ``Rud ceist (1)``."

msgid ""
"``makemigrations`` now detects changes to the model field "
"``limit_choices_to`` option. Add this to your existing migrations or accept "
"an auto-generated migration for fields that use it."
msgstr ""
"Aimsíonn ``makemigrations`` athruithe anois ar an réimse samhail "
"``limit_choices_to`` rogha. Cuir é seo le do imirce atá ann cheana nó glac "
"le himirce a ghintear go huathoibríoch do réimsí a úsáideann é."

msgid ""
"Performing queries that require :ref:`automatic spatial transformations "
"<automatic-spatial-transformations>` now raises ``NotImplementedError`` on "
"MySQL instead of silently using non-transformed geometries."
msgstr ""
"Ardaíonn fiosrúcháin a dteastaíonn uathoibrí:ref: `claochluithe spásúla "
"uathoibríoch <automatic-spatial-transformations>`anois "
"`NotImplementederror`` ar MySQL in ionad geoiméadraí neamh-chlaochlaithe a "
"úsáid go ciúin."

msgid ""
"``django.core.exceptions.DjangoRuntimeWarning`` is removed. It was only used "
"in the cache backend as an intermediate class in ``CacheKeyWarning``'s "
"inheritance of ``RuntimeWarning``."
msgstr ""
"Baintear ``Django.Core.Exceptions.djangoruntimeWarning``. Ní úsáideadh é ach "
"sa chúltaca taisce mar rang idirmheánach in oidhreacht ```CachekeyWarning`` "
"de `RuntimeWarning``."

msgid ""
"Renamed ``BaseExpression._output_field`` to ``output_field``. You may need "
"to update custom expressions."
msgstr ""
"Athainmníodh ``BaseExpression. _output_field`` go ``output_field``. "
"B'fhéidir go mbeidh ort nathanna saincheaptha a nuashonrú."

msgid ""
"In older versions, forms and formsets combine their ``Media`` with widget "
"``Media`` by concatenating the two. The combining now tries "
"to :ref:`preserve the relative order of elements in each list <form-media-"
"asset-order>`. ``MediaOrderConflictWarning`` is issued if the order can't be "
"preserved."
msgstr ""
"I leaganacha níos sine, comhcheanglaíonn foirmeacha agus foirmeacha a gcuid "
"``Meáin ``le giuirléid ``Meáin`` tríd an dá cheann a chomhcheangal. <form-"
"media-asset-order>Déanann an comhcheangal iarracht anois:ref: `ord "
"coibhneasta eilimintí i ngach liosta a chaomhnú `. Eisítear "
"``MediaOrderConflictwarning`` mura féidir an t-ordú a chaomhnú."

msgid ""
"``django.contrib.gis.gdal.OGRException`` is removed. It's been an alias for "
"``GDALException`` since Django 1.8."
msgstr ""
"Baintear ``Django.contrib.gis.gdal.ogrexception``. Is ailias é do "
"``GdalException`` ó Django 1.8."

msgid "Support for GEOS 3.3.x is dropped."
msgstr "Titeann tacaíocht do GEOS 3.3.x."

msgid ""
"The way data is selected for ``GeometryField`` is changed to improve "
"performance, and in raw SQL queries, those fields must now be wrapped in "
"``connection.ops.select``. See the :ref:`Raw queries note<gis-raw-sql>` in "
"the GIS tutorial for an example."
msgstr ""
"Athraítear an bealach a roghnaítear sonraí le haghaidh ``GeometryField` chun "
"feidhmíocht a fheabhsú, agus i gceisteanna SQL amh, caithfear na réimsí sin "
"a fhilleadh anois in `connection.ops.select``. Féach na:ref: `Nóta "
"ceisteanna amh <gis-raw-sql>`sa rang teagaisc GIS mar shampla."

msgid "Features deprecated in 2.0"
msgstr "Gnéithe atá díscríofa i 2.0"

msgid ""
"``context`` argument of ``Field.from_db_value()`` and "
"``Expression.convert_value()``"
msgstr ""
"Argóint ``context`` de `Field.from_DB_Value () ``agus "
"``Expression.convert_Value ()``"

msgid ""
"The ``context`` argument of ``Field.from_db_value()`` and "
"``Expression.convert_value()`` is unused as it's always an empty dictionary. "
"The signature of both methods is now::"
msgstr ""
"Ní úsáidtear an argóint ``context`` de `Field.from_DB_Value () ``agus "
"``Expression.convert_VALUE ()`` mar is foclóir folamh é i gcónaí. Is é síniú "
"an dá mhodh anois:"

msgid ""
"Support for the old signature in custom fields and expressions remains until "
"Django 3.0."
msgstr ""
"Fanann tacaíocht don seanshíniú i réimsí saincheaptha agus nathanna go dtí "
"Django 3.0."

msgid ""
"The ``django.db.backends.postgresql_psycopg2`` module is deprecated in favor "
"of ``django.db.backends.postgresql``. It's been an alias since Django 1.9. "
"This only affects code that imports from the module directly. The "
"``DATABASES`` setting can still use "
"``'django.db.backends.postgresql_psycopg2'``, though you can simplify that "
"by using the ``'django.db.backends.postgresql'`` name added in Django 1.9."
msgstr ""
"Tá an modúl ``django.db.backends.postgresql_psycopg2`` a dhíchur i bhfabhar "
"``django.db.backends.postgresql``. Tá sé ina ainm ó Django 1.9. Ní théann sé "
"seo ach ar chód a allmhairíonn ón modúl go díreach. Is féidir leis an socrú "
"``DATABASES`` ``django.db.backends.postgresql_psycopg2'` a úsáid fós, cé gur "
"féidir leat é sin a shimpliú tríd an ainm "
"``'django.db.backends.postgresql'`` a chuirtear i Django 1.9 a úsáid."

msgid ""
"``django.shortcuts.render_to_response()`` is deprecated in favor "
"of :func:`django.shortcuts.render`. ``render()`` takes the same arguments "
"except that it also requires a ``request``."
msgstr ""
"Tá ``django.shortcuts.render_to_response () ``luasghabháilte i bhfabhr:func: "
"`django.shortcuts.render`. Glacann ``render () ``na hargóintí céanna ach "
"amháin go dteastaíonn ``iarraidh` uaidh freisin."

msgid ""
"The ``DEFAULT_CONTENT_TYPE`` setting is deprecated. It doesn't interact well "
"with third-party apps and is obsolete since HTML5 has mostly superseded "
"XHTML."
msgstr ""
"Tá an socrú ``DEFAULT_CONTENT_TYPE`` imithe i léig. Ní idirghníomhaíonn sé "
"go maith le haipeanna tríú páirtí agus tá sé imithe i léig toisc gur tháinig "
"HTML5 in ionad XHTML den chuid is mó."

msgid ""
"``HttpRequest.xreadlines()`` is deprecated in favor of iterating over the "
"request."
msgstr ""
"Tá ``HttpRequest.xReadLines ()`` a dhíchur i bhfabhar athraithe thar an "
"iarratas."

msgid ""
"The ``field_name`` keyword argument to :meth:`.QuerySet.earliest` "
"and :meth:`.QuerySet.latest` is deprecated in favor of passing the field "
"names as arguments. Write ``.earliest('pub_date')`` instead of "
"``.earliest(field_name='pub_date')``."
msgstr ""
"Tá an argóint eochairfhocal `field_name`` to:meth: `.querySet.Earliest` "
"agus:meth: `.queryset.latest` a dhíchur i bhfabhar ainmneacha na réimse a "
"rith mar argóintí. Scríobh ``.early ('pub_date') ``in ionad ``.early "
"(field_name='pub_date')``."

msgid "Features removed in 2.0"
msgstr "Gnéithe bainte i 2.0"

msgid ""
"These features have reached the end of their deprecation cycle and are "
"removed in Django 2.0."
msgstr ""
"Tá na gnéithe seo tar éis deireadh a dtimthriall díscrúdaithe bainte amach "
"agus baintear iad i Django 2.0."

msgid ""
"See :ref:`deprecated-features-1.9` for details on these changes, including "
"how to remove usage of these features."
msgstr ""
"Féach: Ref: `deprecated-features-1.9` le haghaidh sonraí faoi na hathruithe "
"seo, lena n-áirítear conas úsáid na ngnéithe seo a bhaint."

msgid ""
"The ``weak`` argument to ``django.dispatch.signals.Signal.disconnect()`` is "
"removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear an argóint ``lag`` chuig "
"``Django.Dispatch.Signals.Signal.Disconnect () ``."

msgid ""
"``django.db.backends.base.BaseDatabaseOperations.check_aggregate_support()`` "
"is removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear "
"``Django.db.backends.base.basedatabaseOperations.check_aggregate_support () "
"``."

msgid "The ``django.forms.extras`` package is removed."
msgstr "Baintear an pacáiste ``django.forms.extras``."

msgid "The ``assignment_tag`` helper is removed."
msgstr "Baintear an cúntóir ``assignment_tag``."

msgid ""
"The ``host`` argument to ``SimpleTestCase.assertsRedirects()`` is removed. "
"The compatibility layer which allows absolute URLs to be considered equal to "
"relative ones when the path is identical is also removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear an argóint ``óst`` chuig ``simpletestCase.assertsRedirectes () ``. "
"Baintear an ciseal comhoiriúnachta a ligeann URLanna iomlána a mheas "
"comhionann le cinn coibhneasta nuair a bhíonn an cosán comhionann freisin."

msgid "``Field.rel`` and ``Field.remote_field.to`` are removed."
msgstr "Baintear ``Field.rel`` agus ``Field.remote_field.to``."

msgid ""
"The ``on_delete`` argument for ``ForeignKey`` and ``OneToOneField`` is now "
"required in models and migrations. Consider squashing migrations so that you "
"have fewer of them to update."
msgstr ""
"Tá an argóint `on_delete`` le haghaidh `ForeignKey`` agus ``Onetoonefield`` "
"ag teastáil anois i samhlacha agus imirce. Smaoinigh ar imirce a scrúdú "
"ionas go mbeidh níos lú díobh agat le nuashonrú."

msgid "``django.db.models.fields.add_lazy_relation()`` is removed."
msgstr "Baintear ``django.db.models.fields.add_lazy_relations () ``."

msgid ""
"When time zone support is enabled, database backends that don't support time "
"zones no longer convert aware datetimes to naive values in UTC anymore when "
"such values are passed as parameters to SQL queries executed outside of the "
"ORM, e.g. with ``cursor.execute()``."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a chumasaítear tacaíocht crios ama, ní thiontaíonn cúltaca bunachar "
"sonraí nach dtacaíonn le criosanna ama amanna dáta feasacha go luachanna "
"naif i UTC a thuilleadh nuair a chuirtear luachanna den sórt sin mar "
"pharaiméadair chuig ceisteanna SQL a fhorghníomhaítear lasmuigh den ORM, "
"m.sh. le `cursor.executar () `."

msgid "``django.contrib.auth.tests.utils.skipIfCustomUser()`` is removed."
msgstr "Baintear ``django.contrib.auth.tests.utils.skipifCustomUser () ``."

msgid "The ``GeoManager`` and ``GeoQuerySet`` classes are removed."
msgstr "Baintear na ranganna ``Geomanager`` agus ``GeoquerySet``."

msgid "The ``django.contrib.gis.geoip`` module is removed."
msgstr "Baintear an modúl ``django.contrib.gis.geoip``."

msgid "The ``supports_recursion`` check for template loaders is removed from:"
msgstr ""
"Baintear an seiceáil ``supports_recursion`` le haghaidh luchtaitheoirí "
"teimpléad as:"

msgid "``django.template.engine.Engine.find_template()``"
msgstr "``Django.Template.Engine.Engine.Find_Template () ``"

msgid "``django.template.loader_tags.ExtendsNode.find_template()``"
msgstr "``Django.Template.Loader_Tags.ExtendSnode.Find_Template () ``"

msgid "``django.template.loaders.base.Loader.supports_recursion()``"
msgstr "``Django.Template.Loaders.Base.Loader.Supports_Recursion () ``"

msgid "``django.template.loaders.cached.Loader.supports_recursion()``"
msgstr "``Django.Template.Loaders.Cached.Loader.Supports_Recursion () ``"

msgid ""
"The ``load_template`` and ``load_template_sources`` template loader methods "
"are removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear na modhanna lódóra teimpléad ``load_template`` agus "
"``load_template_sources``."

msgid "The ``template_dirs`` argument for template loaders is removed:"
msgstr ""
"Baintear an argóint ``template_dirs`` le haghaidh luchtaitheoirí teimpléad:"

msgid "``django.template.loaders.base.Loader.get_template()``"
msgstr "``Django.Template.Loaders.Base.Loader.Get_Template () ``"

msgid "``django.template.loaders.cached.Loader.cache_key()``"
msgstr "``Django.Template.Loaders.Cached.Loader.Cache_key () ``"

msgid "``django.template.loaders.cached.Loader.get_template()``"
msgstr "``Django.Template.Loaders.Cached.Loader.Get_Template () ``"

msgid "``django.template.loaders.cached.Loader.get_template_sources()``"
msgstr "``Django.Template.Loaders.Cached.Loader.Get_Template_Sources () ``"

msgid "``django.template.loaders.filesystem.Loader.get_template_sources()``"
msgstr "``Django.Template.Loaders.FileSystem.Loader.Get_Template_Sources () ``"

msgid "``django.template.loaders.base.Loader.__call__()`` is removed."
msgstr "``Django.Template.Loaders.Base.Loader. Baintear __call__ () ``."

msgid ""
"Support for custom error views that don't accept an ``exception`` parameter "
"is removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear tacaíocht do thuairimí earráide saincheaptha nach nglacann le "
"paraiméadar ``eisceacht'."

msgid ""
"The ``mime_type`` attribute of ``django.utils.feedgenerator.Atom1Feed`` and "
"``django.utils.feedgenerator.RssFeed`` is removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear an tréith ``mime_type`` de `Django.Utils.FeedGenerator.Atom1Feed`` "
"agus ``Django.Utils.FeedGenerator.rssFeed``."

msgid "The ``app_name`` argument to ``include()`` is removed."
msgstr "Baintear an argóint ``app_name`` le `include () ``."

msgid ""
"Support for passing a 3-tuple (including ``admin.site.urls``) as the first "
"argument to ``include()`` is removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear tacaíocht chun 3 tuple a rith (lena n-áirítear ``admin.site.urls``) "
"mar an chéad argóint le `include () ``."

msgid ""
"Support for setting a URL instance namespace without an application "
"namespace is removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear tacaíocht chun spás ainmneacha sampla URL a shocrú gan spás "
"ainmneacha feidhmchláir."

msgid "``Field._get_val_from_obj()`` is removed."
msgstr "``Réimse. Baintear _get_val_from_obj () ``."

msgid "``django.template.loaders.eggs.Loader`` is removed."
msgstr "Baintear ``Django.Template.Loaders.Eggs.Loader``."

msgid ""
"The ``current_app`` parameter to the ``contrib.auth`` function-based views "
"is removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear an paraiméadar ``current_app`` chuig na tuairimí bunaithe ar "
"fheidhm ``contrib.auth``."

msgid ""
"The ``callable_obj`` keyword argument to "
"``SimpleTestCase.assertRaisesMessage()`` is removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear an argóint eochairfhocal ``callable_obj`` chuig "
"``simpletestCase.assertRaisesMessage () ``."

msgid ""
"Support for the ``allow_tags`` attribute on ``ModelAdmin`` methods is "
"removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear tacaíocht don tréith `allow_tags`` ar mhodhanna ``ModelAdmin``."

msgid ""
"The ``enclosure`` keyword argument to ``SyndicationFeed.add_item()`` is "
"removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear an argóint eochairfhocal ``enclosure`` le `SyndicationFeed.add_item "
"() ``."

msgid ""
"The ``django.template.loader.LoaderOrigin`` and "
"``django.template.base.StringOrigin`` aliases for "
"``django.template.base.Origin`` are removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear na hainmneacha ``Django.Template.LoaderOrigin`` agus "
"``Django.Template.Base.StringOrigin`` le haghaidh "
"``Django.Template.Base.Origin``."

msgid "See :ref:`deprecated-features-1.10` for details on these changes."
msgstr ""
"Féach:ref: `deprecated-features-1.10` le haghaidh sonraí faoi na hathruithe "
"seo."

msgid "The ``makemigrations --exit`` option is removed."
msgstr "Baintear an rogha ``makemigrations --exit``."

msgid ""
"Support for direct assignment to a reverse foreign key or many-to-many "
"relation is removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear tacaíocht do shannadh díreach le heochair eachtrach droim nó gaol "
"go leor."

msgid ""
"The ``get_srid()`` and ``set_srid()`` methods of "
"``django.contrib.gis.geos.GEOSGeometry`` are removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear na modhanna ``get_srid () ``agus ``set_srid ()`` de "
"`django.contrib.gis.geos.geosgeometry``."

msgid ""
"The ``get_x()``, ``set_x()``, ``get_y()``, ``set_y()``, ``get_z()``, and "
"``set_z()`` methods of ``django.contrib.gis.geos.Point`` are removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear na modhanna ``get_x () ``, `set_x ()``, `get_y () ``, `set_y ()``, "
"`get_z () ``, agus ``set_z ()`` modhanna ``django.contrib.gis.geos.point``."

msgid ""
"The ``get_coords()`` and ``set_coords()`` methods of "
"``django.contrib.gis.geos.Point`` are removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear na modhanna ``get_coords () ``agus ``set_coords ()`` de "
"`django.contrib.gis.geos.point``."

msgid ""
"The ``cascaded_union`` property of ``django.contrib.gis.geos.MultiPolygon`` "
"is removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear maoin ``cascaded_union`` de `Django.contrib.gis.geos.multipolygon``."

msgid "``django.utils.functional.allow_lazy()`` is removed."
msgstr "Baintear ``django.utils.functional.allow_lazy () ``."

msgid "The ``shell --plain`` option is removed."
msgstr "Baintear an rogha ``shell --plain ``."

msgid ""
"The ``django.core.urlresolvers`` module is removed in favor of its new "
"location, ``django.urls``."
msgstr ""
"Baintear an modúl ``django.core.urlresolvers`` i bhfabhar a shuíomh nua, "
"``django.urls``."

msgid ""
"``CommaSeparatedIntegerField`` is removed, except for support in historical "
"migrations."
msgstr ""
"Baintear ``CommaseParatedIntegerField``, ach amháin le haghaidh tacaíochta "
"in imirce stairiúla."

msgid "The template ``Context.has_key()`` method is removed."
msgstr "Baintear an modh teimpléad ``Context.has_key () ``."

msgid ""
"Support for the ``django.core.files.storage.Storage.accessed_time()``, "
"``created_time()``, and ``modified_time()`` methods is removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear tacaíocht do na modhanna ``django.core.files.storage.accessed_Time "
"() ``, `created_time ()``, agus `modified_time () ``."

msgid ""
"Support for query lookups using the model name when "
"``Meta.default_related_name`` is set is removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear tacaíocht le haghaidh cuardaigh fiosrúcháin ag baint úsáide as ainm "
"an tsamhail nuair a shocraítear ``Meta.default_RELATED_NAME``."

msgid "The MySQL ``__search`` lookup is removed."
msgstr "Baintear an cuardach MySQL ``__search``."

msgid ""
"The shim for supporting custom related manager classes without a "
"``_apply_rel_filters()`` method is removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear an shim chun tacú le ranganna bainisteora saincheaptha gan modh "
"``_apply_rel_filters () `."

msgid ""
"Using ``User.is_authenticated()`` and ``User.is_anonymous()`` as methods "
"rather than properties is no longer supported."
msgstr ""
"Ní thacaítear a thuilleadh le `User.is_Authenticated () ``agus "
"``User.is_Anonymous ()`` a úsáid mar mhodhanna seachas airíonna."

msgid "The ``Model._meta.virtual_fields`` attribute is removed."
msgstr "An ``Samhail. Baintear tréith _meta.virtual_fields``."

msgid ""
"The keyword arguments ``virtual_only`` in ``Field.contribute_to_class()`` "
"and ``virtual`` in ``Model._meta.add_field()`` are removed."
msgstr ""
"Na hargóintí eochairfhocal ``virtual_only`` i `field.contribute_to_class () "
"``agus ``fíorúil`` i `Samhail. Baintear _meta.add_field () ``."

msgid "The ``javascript_catalog()`` and ``json_catalog()`` views are removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear na tuairimí `javascript_catalog () ``agus ``json_catalog ()``."

msgid "``django.contrib.gis.utils.precision_wkt()`` is removed."
msgstr "Baintear ``django.contrib.gis.utils.precision_wkt () ``."

msgid ""
"In multi-table inheritance, implicit promotion of a ``OneToOneField`` to a "
"``parent_link`` is removed."
msgstr ""
"In oidhreacht il-tábla, baintear cur chun cinn intuigthe ``OneToonefield`` "
"go ``parent_nasc``."

msgid "Support for ``Widget._format_value()`` is removed."
msgstr "Tacaíocht do ``Giuirléid. Baintear _format_value () ``."

msgid ""
"``FileField`` methods ``get_directory_name()`` and ``get_filename()`` are "
"removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear modhanna ``filefield`` `get_directory_name () ``agus ``get_filename "
"()``."

msgid ""
"The ``mark_for_escaping()`` function and the classes it uses: "
"``EscapeData``, ``EscapeBytes``, ``EscapeText``, ``EscapeString``, and "
"``EscapeUnicode`` are removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear an fheidhm ``mark_for_escaping () ``agus na ranganna a úsáideann "
"sé: ``EscapeData``, `EscapeBytes``, `EscapeText``, `EscapeString``, agus "
"``EscapeUnicode``."

msgid ""
"The ``escape`` filter now uses ``django.utils.html.conditional_escape()``."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann an scagaire ``escape`` anois "
"``django.utils.html.conditional_escape () ``."

msgid "``Manager.use_for_related_fields`` is removed."
msgstr "Baintear ``Manager.Use_for_Related_Fields``."

msgid ""
"Model ``Manager`` inheritance follows MRO inheritance rules. The requirement "
"to use ``Meta.manager_inheritance_from_future`` to opt-in to the behavior is "
"removed."
msgstr ""
"Leanann oidhreacht mhúnla ``Bainiste`` rialacha oidhreachta MRO. Baintear an "
"riachtanas chun `Meta.Manager_Inheritance_From_Future`` a úsáid chun roghnú "
"isteach san iompar."

msgid ""
"Support for old-style middleware using ``settings.MIDDLEWARE_CLASSES`` is "
"removed."
msgstr ""
"Baintear tacaíocht do middleware sean-stíl ag baint úsáide as "
"`settings.middleware_classes``."

msgid "Django 2.0.1 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoileadh Django 2.0.1"

msgid "Django 2.0.1 fixes several bugs in 2.0."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 2.0.1 roinnt fabhtanna i 2.0."

msgid ""
"Reallowed filtering a queryset with ``GeometryField=None`` (:ticket:`28896`)."
msgstr ""
"Scagadh athshlánaithe tacar fiosrúcháin le ``GeometryField=None`` (:ticket: "
"`28896`)."

msgid ""
"Corrected admin check to allow a ``OneToOneField`` in "
"``ModelAdmin.autocomplete_fields`` (:ticket:`28898`)."
msgstr ""
"Seiceáil riaracháin ceartaithe chun `OneTooneField`` a cheadú i "
"`ModelAdmin.autocomplete_fields`` (:ticket: `28898`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression on SQLite where ``DecimalField`` returned a result with "
"trailing zeros in the fractional part truncated (:ticket:`28915`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú ar SQLite inar thug ``Decimalfield`` toradh ar ais le "
"nialais rianaithe sa chuid codánach a ghearrthaíodh (:ticket: `28915`)."

msgid "Fixed crash in the ``testserver`` command startup (:ticket:`28941`)."
msgstr "Timpiste seasta sa tosú ordaithe ``testserver` `(:ticket: `28941`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed crash when coercing a translatable URL pattern to ``str`` "
"(:ticket:`28947`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste seasta agus patrún URL inaistrithe á iallach chuig `str` (:ticket: "
"`28947`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed crash on SQLite when renaming a field in a model referenced by a "
"``ManyToManyField`` (:ticket:`28884`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste seasta ar SQLite nuair a athainmnítear réimse i samhail dá "
"dtagraíonn ``ManyTomanyField`` (:ticket: `28884`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when chaining ``values()`` or ``values_list()`` after "
"``QuerySet.select_for_update(of=(...))`` (:ticket:`28944`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste nuair a chuirtear `luachanna () ``nó `values_list ()`` a "
"shlánú tar éis ``QuerySet.Select_for_Update (of= (...)) ``(:ticket: `28944`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed admin changelist crash when using a query expression in the page's "
"ordering (:ticket:`28958`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste liosta athraithe riaracháin seasta agus tú ag úsáid abairt "
"fiosrúcháin in ordú an leathanaigh (:ticket: `28958`)."

msgid "Django 2.0.10 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 2.0.10"

msgid "Django 2.0.10 fixes a security issue and several bugs in 2.0.9."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 2.0.10 saincheist slándála agus roinnt fabhtanna i 2.0.9."

msgid ""
"Prevented repetitive calls to ``geos_version_tuple()`` in the ``WKBWriter`` "
"class in an attempt to fix a random crash involving ``LooseVersion`` since "
"Django 2.0.6 (:ticket:`29959`)."
msgstr ""
"Cosc ar ghlaonna athchleachtacha chuig ``geos_version_tuple () ``sa rang "
"``WKBwriter`` mar iarracht timpiste randamach a shocrú a bhaineann le "
"`LooSeversion`` ó Django 2.0.6 (:ticket: `29959`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a schema corruption issue on SQLite 3.26+. You might have to drop and "
"rebuild your SQLite database if you applied a migration while using an older "
"version of Django with SQLite 3.26 or later (:ticket:`29182`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh saincheist éillithe scéime ar SQLite 3.26+. B'fhéidir go mbeidh ort "
"do bhunachar sonraí SQLite a scaoileadh agus a atógáil má chuir tú imirce i "
"bhfeidhm agus tú ag úsáid leagan níos sine de Django le SQLite 3.26 nó níos "
"déanaí (:ticket: `29182`)."

msgid ""
"Prevented SQLite schema alterations while foreign key checks are enabled to "
"avoid the possibility of schema corruption (:ticket:`30023`)."
msgstr ""
"Cosc ar athruithe scéime SQLite agus cumasaítear seiceálacha eachtracha chun "
"féidearthacht éilliú scéime a sheachaint (:ticket: `30023`)."

msgid "Django 2.0.11 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 2.0.11"

msgid "Django 2.0.11 fixes a security issue in 2.0.10."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 2.0.11 saincheist slándála i 2.0.10."

msgid "Django 2.0.12 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 2.0.12"

msgid "Django 2.0.12 fixes a packaging error in 2.0.11."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 2.0.12 earráid pacáistithe i 2.0.11."

msgid "Corrected packaging error from 2.0.11 (:ticket:`30175`)."
msgstr "Earráid pacáistithe ceartaithe ó 2.0.11 (:ticket: `30175`)."

msgid "Django 2.0.13 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 2.0.13"

msgid "*February 12, 2019*"
msgstr "*12 Feabhra, 2019*"

msgid "Django 2.0.13 fixes a regression in 2.0.12/2.0.11."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 2.0.13 aischéimniú i 2.0.12/2.0.11."

msgid ""
"Fixed crash in ``django.utils.numberformat.format_number()`` when the number "
"has over 200 digits (:ticket:`30177`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste seasta i ``django.utils.numberformat.format_number () ``nuair a "
"bhíonn os cionn 200 dhigit ag an uimhir (:ticket: `30177`)."

msgid "Django 2.0.2 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 2.0.2"

msgid "Django 2.0.2 fixes a security issue and several bugs in 2.0.1."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 2.0.2 saincheist slándála agus roinnt fabhtanna i 2.0.1."

msgid ""
"Fixed hidden content at the bottom of the \"The install worked successfully!"
"\" page for some languages (:ticket:`28885`)."
msgstr ""
"Ábhar i bhfolach seasta ag bun an “D'oibrigh an suiteáil go rathúil!” "
"leathanach le haghaidh roinnt teangacha (:ticket: `28885`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed regression in the use of ``QuerySet.values_list(..., flat=True)`` "
"followed by ``annotate()`` (:ticket:`29067`)."
msgstr ""
"Aischéimniú seasta maidir le ``QuerySet.values_list (..., flat=True) ``agus "
"``annotate ()`` ina dhiaidh sin (:ticket: `29067`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression where a queryset that annotates with geometry objects "
"crashes (:ticket:`29054`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú ina dtiocfaidh tacar fiosrúcháin a anótáil le rudaí "
"geoiméadrachta (:ticket: `29054`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression where ``makemigrations`` crashes if a migrations "
"directory doesn't have an ``__init__.py`` file (:ticket:`29091`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú ina dtiteann ``makemigrations`` mura bhfuil comhad "
"``__init__.py` ag eolaire imirce (:ticket: `29091`)."

msgid "Django 2.0.3 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 2.0.3"

msgid ""
"Django 2.0.3 fixes two security issues and several bugs in 2.0.2. Also, the "
"latest string translations from Transifex are incorporated."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 2.0.3 dhá shaincheist slándála agus roinnt fabhtanna i "
"2.0.2. Chomh maith leis sin, corpraítear na haistriúcháin teaghráin is "
"déanaí ó Transifex."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression that caused sliced ``QuerySet.distinct().order_by()`` "
"followed by ``count()`` to crash (:ticket:`29108`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú a chúis le ``QuerySet.Distinct () .order_by () "
"``slisnéithe a chruthaigh ``count () `tar éis titim (: ticket: `29108`)."

msgid ""
"Prioritized the datetime and time input formats without ``%f`` for the Thai "
"locale to fix the admin time picker widget displaying \"undefined\" "
"(:ticket:`29109`)."
msgstr ""
"Tosaíocht a thabhairt do na formáidí ionchuir dáta agus ama gan ``%f`` do "
"shuíomh Téalainnis chun an giuirléid roghnóra ama riaracháin a shocrú a "
"thaispeánann “neamhshainithe” (:ticket: `29109`)."

msgid "Fixed crash with ``QuerySet.order_by(Exists(...))`` (:ticket:`29118`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste seasta le ``QuerySet.Order_by (Existents (...)) ``(:ticket: "
"`29118`)."

msgid ""
"Made ``Q.deconstruct()`` deterministic with multiple keyword arguments "
"(:ticket:`29125`). You may need to modify ``Q``'s in existing migrations, or "
"accept an autogenerated migration."
msgstr ""
"Rinneadh ``Q.deconstruct () ``deirmitheach le hargóintí eochairfhocal "
"iolracha (:ticket: `29125`). B'fhéidir go mbeidh ort ``Q`` a mhodhnú sna "
"himirce atá ann cheana, nó glacadh le himirce uathghinithe."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression where a ``When()`` expression with a list argument "
"crashes (:ticket:`29166`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú ina dtiocfaidh abairt ``When () ``le argóint liosta "
"(:ticket: `29166`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed crash when using a ``Window()`` expression in a subquery "
"(:ticket:`29172`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste seasta nuair a úsáidtear abairt ``Fuinneog () ``i bhfo-cheist "
"(:ticket: `29172`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``AbstractBaseUser.normalize_username()`` crash if the ``username`` "
"argument isn't a string (:ticket:`29176`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste seasta ``AbstractBaseUser.Normalize_UserName () ``mura bhfuil an "
"argóint ``ainm úsáideora`` teaghrán (:ticket: `29176`)."

msgid "Django 2.0.4 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 2.0.4"

msgid "Django 2.0.4 fixes several bugs in 2.0.3."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 2.0.4 roinnt fabhtanna i 2.0.3."

msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when filtering with an ``Exists()`` annotation of a queryset "
"containing a single field (:ticket:`29195`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh timpiste agus tú ag scagadh le anótáil ``Existents () ``de thacar "
"ceisteanna ina bhfuil réimse amháin (:ticket: `29195`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed admin autocomplete widget's translations for ``zh-hans`` and ``zh-"
"hant`` languages (:ticket:`29213`)."
msgstr ""
"Aistriúcháin giuirléid uathchomhlánaithe riaracháin seasta do theangacha "
"``zh-hans`` agus `zh-hant`` (:ticket: `29213`)."

msgid ""
"Corrected admin's autocomplete widget to add a space after custom classes "
"(:ticket:`29221`)."
msgstr ""
"Giuirléid uathchomhlánaithe riaracháin ceartaithe chun spás a chur leis tar "
"éis ranganna saincheaptha (:ticket: `29221`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``PasswordResetConfirmView`` crash when using a user model with a "
"``UUIDField`` primary key and the reset URL contains an encoded primary key "
"value that decodes to an invalid UUID (:ticket:`29206`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste seasta ``PasswordResetConfirmView ``nuair a úsáideann tú samhail "
"úsáideora le príomheochair ``UUIDField`` agus tá luach príomhúil "
"ionchódaithe sa URL athshocraithe a dhíchódóidh go UUID neamhbhailí "
"(:ticket: `29206`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression in Django 2.0 where ``OpenLayersWidget`` deserialization "
"ignored the widget map's SRID and assumed 4326 (WGS84) (:ticket:`29116`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú i Django 2.0 nuair a rinne díshealú "
"``OpenLayersWidget`` neamhaird ar SRID na léarscáileanna giuirléid agus "
"ghlac sé le 4326 (WGS84) (:ticket: `29116`)."

msgid "Django 2.0.5 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 2.0.5"

msgid "Django 2.0.5 fixes several bugs in 2.0.4."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 2.0.5 roinnt fabhtanna i 2.0.4."

msgid ""
"Corrected the import paths that ``inspectdb`` generates for "
"``django.contrib.postgres`` fields (:ticket:`29307`)."
msgstr ""
"Ceartaigh na cosáin allmhairithe a ghineann ``inspectdb`` do réimsí "
"``django.contrib.postgres`` (:ticket: `29307`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression in Django 2.0.4 where ``QuerySet.values()`` or "
"``values_list()`` after combining an annotated and unannotated queryset with "
"``union()``, ``difference()``, or ``intersection()`` crashed due to "
"mismatching columns (:ticket:`29286`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú i Django 2.0.4 nuair a tháinig ``QuerySet.values () "
"``nó `values_list ()`` tar éis tacar ceisteanna anótaithe agus gan anótáilte "
"a chomhcheangal le ``union () ``, `difríocht ()``, nó ``crosbhall () ``mar "
"gheall ar cholúin mímheaitseála (:ticket: `29286`)."

msgid "Django 2.0.6 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 2.0.6"

msgid "*June 1, 2018*"
msgstr "*1 Meitheamh, 2018*"

msgid "Django 2.0.6 fixes several bugs in 2.0.5."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 2.0.6 roinnt fabhtanna i 2.0.5."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression that broke custom template filters that use decorators "
"(:ticket:`29400`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú a bhris scagairí teimpléad saincheaptha a úsáideann "
"maisitheoirí (:ticket: `29400`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed detection of custom URL converters in included patterns "
"(:ticket:`29415`)."
msgstr ""
"Braite seasta tiontairí URL saincheaptha i bpatrúin san áireamh (:ticket: "
"`29415`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression that added an unnecessary subquery to the ``GROUP BY`` "
"clause on MySQL when using a ``RawSQL`` annotation (:ticket:`29416`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú a chuir fo-cheist gan ghá leis an gclásal ``GROUP BY`` "
"ar MySQL nuair a úsáideann anótáil ``RawSQL`` (:ticket: `29416`)."

msgid "Django 2.0.7 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 2.0.7"

msgid "Django 2.0.7 fixes several bugs in 2.0.6."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 2.0.7 roinnt fabhtanna i 2.0.6."

msgid ""
"Fixed admin changelist crash when using a query expression without ``asc()`` "
"or ``desc()`` in the page's ordering (:ticket:`29428`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste liosta athraithe riaracháin seasta nuair a úsáidtear abairt "
"fiosrúcháin gan ``asc () ``nó ``desc ()`` in ordú an leathanaigh (:ticket: "
"`29428`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed admin check crash when using a query expression in "
"``ModelAdmin.ordering`` (:ticket:`29428`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpiste seiceála riaracháin seasta agus tú ag úsáid abairt fiosrúcháin i "
"``ModelAdmin.Ordering`` (:ticket: `29428`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed ``__regex`` and ``__iregex`` lookups with MySQL 8 (:ticket:`29451`)."
msgstr ""
"Cuardaigh seasta ``__regex`` agus ``__iregex`` le MySQL 8 (:ticket: `29451`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed migrations crash with namespace packages on Python 3.7 "
"(:ticket:`28814`)."
msgstr ""
"Timpeann imirce seasta le pacáistí spás ainmneacha ar Python 3.7 (:ticket: "
"`28814`)."

msgid "Django 2.0.8 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 2.0.8"

msgid "Django 2.0.8 fixes a security issue and several bugs in 2.0.7."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn Django 2.0.8 saincheist slándála agus roinnt fabhtanna i 2.0.7."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression in Django 2.0.7 that broke the ``regex`` lookup on "
"MariaDB (even though MariaDB isn't officially supported) (:ticket:`29544`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú i Django 2.0.7 a bhris an cuardach ``regex`` ar MariaDB "
"(cé nach dtacaítear le MariaDB go hoifigiúil) (:ticket: `29544`)."

msgid ""
"Fixed a regression where ``django.template.Template`` crashed if the "
"``template_string`` argument is lazy (:ticket:`29617`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh aischéimniú nuair a thit ``django.template.template`` má tá an "
"argóint ``template_string`` leisciúil (:ticket: `29617`)."

msgid "Django 2.0.9 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 2.0.9"

msgid "Django 2.0.9 fixes a data loss bug in 2.0.8."
msgstr "Socraíonn Django 2.0.9 fabht caillteanas sonraí i 2.0.8."

msgid "Django 2.1 release notes"
msgstr "Nótaí scaoilte Django 2.1"

msgid "Welcome to Django 2.1!"
msgstr "Fáilte go dtí Django 2.1!"

msgid ""
"These release notes cover the :ref:`new features <whats-new-2.1>`, as well "
"as some :ref:`backwards incompatible changes <backwards-incompatible-2.1>` "
"you'll want to be aware of when upgrading from Django 2.0 or earlier. "
"We've :ref:`dropped some features<removed-features-2.1>` that have reached "
"the end of their deprecation cycle, and we've :ref:`begun the deprecation "
"process for some features <deprecated-features-2.1>`."
msgstr ""
"Clúdaíonn na nótaí scaoilte seo na:ref: `gnéithe nua <whats-new-2.1>`, chomh "
"maith le roinnt: ref: `athruithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha ar chúl<backwards-"
"incompatible-2.1>` a mbeidh tú ag iarraidh a bheith ar an eolas fúthu agus "
"tú ag uasghrádú ó Django 2.0 nó níos luaithe. <deprecated-"
"features-2.1>Chuireamar: Ref: `thit roinnt <removed-features-2.1>gnéithe `a "
"bhfuil deireadh a dtimthriall díghníomhaíochta bainte amach acu, agus "
"chuireamaire:ref: `thosaigh muid ar an bpróiseas díghníomhaíochta do roinnt "
"gnéithe`."

msgid ""
"Django 2.1 supports Python 3.5, 3.6, and 3.7. Django 2.0 is the last version "
"to support Python 3.4.  We **highly recommend** and only officially support "
"the latest release of each series."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn Django 2.1 le Python 3.5, 3.6, agus 3.7. Is é Django 2.0 an leagan "
"deireanach chun tacú le Python 3.4. Molaimid** go hard** agus ní thacaímid "
"go hoifigiúil ach leis an scaoileadh is déanaí de gach sraith."

msgid "What's new in Django 2.1"
msgstr "Cad atá nua i Django 2.1"

msgid "Model \"view\" permission"
msgstr "Cead “féach” samhail"

msgid ""
"A \"view\" permission is added to the model :attr:`Meta.default_permissions "
"<django.db.models.Options.default_permissions>`. The new permissions will be "
"created automatically when running :djadmin:`migrate`."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.Options.default_permissions>Cuirtear cead “amharc” leis an "
"tsamhail:attr: `Meta.default_Permissions `. Cruthófar na ceadanna nua go "
"huathoibríoch agus iad ag rith: djadmin: `migrate`."

msgid ""
"This allows giving users read-only access to models in the "
"admin. :meth:`.ModelAdmin.has_view_permission` is new. The implementation is "
"backwards compatible in that there isn't a need to assign the \"view\" "
"permission to allow users who have the \"change\" permission to edit objects."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann sé seo rochtain léite amháin a thabhairt d'úsáideoirí ar mhúnlaí sa "
"riarachán. :meth: Tá `.modeladmin.has_view_permission` nua. Tá an cur i "
"bhfeidhm comhoiriúnach ar ais sa mhéid nach gá an cead “amharc” a shannadh "
"chun ligean d'úsáideoirí a bhfuil an cead “athraithe” acu rudaí a chur in "
"eagar."

msgid ""
"There are a couple of :ref:`backwards incompatible considerations "
"<view_permission_backwards_incompatible>`."
msgstr ""
"<view_permission_backwards_incompatible>Tá cúpla de:ref: `breithnithe neamh-"
"chomhoiriúnacha ar ais `."

msgid ""
":attr:`.ModelAdmin.search_fields` now accepts any lookup such as "
"``field__exact``."
msgstr ""
":attr: `.modeladmin.search_fields` glacann anois le haon chuardach mar "
"``field__exact``."

msgid "jQuery is upgraded from version 2.2.3 to 3.3.1."
msgstr "tá jQuery uasghrádaithe ó leagan 2.2.3 go 3.3.1."

msgid ""
"The new :meth:`.ModelAdmin.delete_queryset` method allows customizing the "
"deletion process of the \"delete selected objects\" action."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an modh nua:meth: `.modeladmin.delete_querySet` próiseas scriostha "
"na gníomhaíochta “scrios rudaí roghnaithe” a shaincheapadh."

msgid ""
"You can now :ref:`override the default admin site <overriding-default-admin-"
"site>`."
msgstr ""
"<overriding-default-admin-site>Is féidir leat anois:ref: `an suíomh "
"riaracháin réamhshocraithe a shárú `."

msgid ""
"The new :attr:`.ModelAdmin.sortable_by` attribute "
"and :meth:`.ModelAdmin.get_sortable_by` method allow limiting the columns "
"that can be sorted in the change list page."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an modh nua:attr: `.modelAdmin.sortable_by` agus:meth: "
"`.modelAdmin.get_sortable_by` teorannú ar na colúin is féidir a shórtáil ar "
"leathanach an liosta athraithe."

msgid ""
"The ``admin_order_field`` attribute for elements "
"in :attr:`.ModelAdmin.list_display` may now be a query expression."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh go mbeadh an tréith `admin_order_field`` le haghaidh eilimintí "
"in:attr: `.modelAdmin.list_display` anois ina léiriú fiosrúcháin."

msgid ""
"The new :meth:`.ModelAdmin.get_deleted_objects()` method allows customizing "
"the deletion process of the delete view and the \"delete selected\" action."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an modh nua:meth: `.modeladmin.get_deleted_objects () `próiseas "
"scriostha an radharc scriosta agus an ghníomh “scrios roghnaithe” a "
"shaincheapadh."

msgid ""
"The ``actions.html``, ``change_list_results.html``, ``date_hierarchy.html``, "
"``pagination.html``, ``prepopulated_fields_js.html``, ``search_form.html``, "
"and ``submit_line.html`` templates can now be :ref:`overridden per app or "
"per model <admin-templates-overridden-per-app-or-model>` (besides overridden "
"globally)."
msgstr ""
"<admin-templates-overridden-per-app-or-model>Is féidir leis na teimpléid "
"``actions.html``, `change_list_results.html``, `date_hierarchy.html``, "
"`pagination.html``, `prepopulated_fields_js.html``, `search_form.html``, "
"agus ``submit_line.html`` a bheith anois:ref: `athsháraithe in aghaidh an "
"aip nó in aghaidh an tsamhail `(seachas a athsháraítear ar fud an domhain)."

msgid ""
"The admin change list and change form object tools can now "
"be :ref:`overridden per app, per model, or globally <admin-templates-"
"overridden-per-app-or-model>` with ``change_list_object_tools.html`` and "
"``change_form_object_tools.html`` templates."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leis an liosta athraithe riaracháin agus na huirlisí réad foirme a "
"athrú anois:ref: `athsháraithe in aghaidh an aip, in aghaidh an tsamhail, nó "
"ar fud an domhain `le teimpléid ``change_list_object_tools.html`` agus "
"``change_form_object_tools.html`<admin-templates-overridden-per-app-or-"
"model>`."

msgid ""
":meth:`.InlineModelAdmin.has_add_permission` is now passed the parent object "
"as the second positional argument, ``obj``."
msgstr ""
":meth: `.inlineModelAdmin.has_Add_Permission` cuirtear an tuismitheoir réad "
"anois mar an dara argóint seasmhach, ``obj ``."

msgid ""
"Admin actions may now :ref:`specify permissions <admin-action-permissions>` "
"to limit their availability to certain users."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le gníomhartha riaracháin anois :tag:`ceadanna a shonrú <admin-"
"action-permissions>` chun a infhaighteacht a theorannú d'úsáideoirí áirithe."

msgid ""
":djadmin:`createsuperuser` now gives a prompt to allow bypassing "
"the :setting:`AUTH_PASSWORD_VALIDATORS` checks."
msgstr ""
":djadmin: Tugann `createsuperuser` pras anois chun ligean seiceálacha: "
"setting: `AUTH_PASSWORD_VALIDATORS` a sheachaint."

msgid ""
"The new :meth:`.GEOSGeometry.buffer_with_style` method is a version "
"of :meth:`~.GEOSGeometry.buffer` that allows customizing the style of the "
"buffer."
msgstr ""
"Is é an modh nua:meth: `.geosgeometry.buffer_with_style` leagan de:meth: "
"`~.geosgeometry.buffer` a cheadaíonn stíl an maoláin a shaincheapadh."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.contrib.gis.forms.widgets.OpenLayersWidget` is now based on "
"OpenLayers 4.6.5 (previously 3.20.1)."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.contrib.gis.forms.widgets.openLayersWidget` bunaithe anois "
"ar OpenLayers 4.6.5 (roimhe seo 3.20.1)."

msgid ""
"Added the :setting:`SESSION_COOKIE_SAMESITE` setting to set the ``SameSite`` "
"cookie flag on session cookies."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an socrú:setting: `SESSION_COOKIE_SAMESITE` leis chun an bratach "
"fianán ``SameSite`` a shocrú ar fhianáin seisiúin."

msgid ""
"The :ref:`local-memory cache backend <local-memory-caching>` now uses a "
"least-recently-used (LRU) culling strategy rather than a pseudo-random one."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann an:ref: `cúltaca taisce cuimhne áitiúil <local-memory-"
"caching>`straitéis chaillú (LRU) is lú a úsáidtear le déanaí seachas ceann "
"bréag-randamach."

msgid ""
"The new :meth:`~django.core.cache.cache.touch` method of the :ref:`low-level "
"cache API <low-level-cache-api>` updates the timeout of cache keys."
msgstr ""
"<low-level-cache-api>Nuashonraíonn an modh nua:meth: "
"`~django.core.cache.touch` den: ref: `Leas-leibhéal taisce API `an t-am na "
"heochracha taisce."

msgid ""
"Added the :setting:`CSRF_COOKIE_SAMESITE` setting to set the ``SameSite`` "
"cookie flag on CSRF cookies."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an socrú: socrú: `CSRF_COOKIE_SAMESITE` leis chun an bratach fianán "
"``SameSite`` a shocrú ar fhianáin CSRF."

msgid ""
"The widget for ``ImageField`` now renders with the HTML attribute "
"``accept=\"image/*\"``."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an giuirléid le haghaidh ``ImageField`` anois leis an tréith HTML "
"``accept=\"image/*\"``."

msgid ""
"Added the :meth:`~django.utils.translation.get_supported_language_variant` "
"function."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an fheidhme:meth: "
"`~django.utils.translation.get_supported_language_variant` leis."

msgid ""
"Untranslated strings for territorial language variants now use the "
"translations of the generic language. For example, untranslated ``pt_BR`` "
"strings use ``pt`` translations."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann teaghráin neamhaistrithe le haghaidh leaganacha teanga chríochach "
"aistriúcháin na teanga chineálach Mar shampla, úsáideann teaghráin ``pt_br`` "
"neamhaistrithe aistriúcháin ``pt``."

msgid ""
"The new :option:`inspectdb --include-views` option allows creating models "
"for database views."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an rogha nua:option: `inspectdb --include-views` samhlacha a chruthú "
"le haghaidh tuairimí bunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.core.management.BaseCommand` class now uses a custom "
"help formatter so that the standard options like ``--verbosity`` or ``--"
"settings`` appear last in the help output, giving a more prominent position "
"to subclassed command's options."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann an rang:Class: `~Django.Core.Management.BaseCommand` "
"formáiditheoir cabhrach saincheaptha anois ionas go mbeidh na roghanna "
"caighdeánacha mar ``--verbosity`` nó ``--settings`` le feiceáil dheireanach "
"san aschur cabhrach, ag tabhairt suíomh níos suntasaí do roghanna ordaithe "
"fo-aicmithe."

msgid "Added support for serialization of ``functools.partialmethod`` objects."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíocht bhreise le haghaidh sraitheadh rudaí ``functools.partialmethod``."

msgid ""
"To support frozen environments, migrations may be loaded from ``.pyc`` files."
msgstr ""
"Chun tacú le timpeallachtaí reoite, féadfar imirce a luchtú ó chomhaid "
"``.pyc``."

msgid "Models can now use ``__init_subclass__()`` from :pep:`487`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le samhlacha ``__init_subclass__ () ``a úsáid anois ó:pep: `487`."

msgid ""
"A ``BinaryField`` may now be set to ``editable=True`` if you wish to include "
"it in model forms."
msgstr ""
"Féadfar ``Binaryfield`` a shocrú anois go ``editable=true`` más mian leat é "
"a chur san áireamh i bhfoirmeacha samhlacha."

msgid ""
"A number of new text database functions are "
"added: :class:`~django.db.models.functions.Chr`, :class:`~django.db.models.functions.Left`, :class:`~django.db.models.functions.LPad`, :class:`~django.db.models.functions.LTrim`, :class:`~django.db.models.functions.Ord`, :class:`~django.db.models.functions.Repeat`, :class:`~django.db.models.functions.Replace`, :class:`~django.db.models.functions.Right`, :class:`~django.db.models.functions.RPad`, :class:`~django.db.models.functions.RTrim`, "
"and :class:`~django.db.models.functions.Trim`."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear roinnt feidhmeanna bunachar sonraí téacs nua leis: :class: "
"`~django.db.models.functions.chr`, :class: "
"`~django.db.models.functions.left`, :class: "
"`~django.db.models.functions.lpad`, :class: "
"`~django.db.models.functions.ltrim`, :class: "
"`~django..db.Models.Functions.Ord`, :class: "
"`~django.db.models.functions.repeat`, :class: "
"`~django.db.models.functions.replace`, :class: "
"`~django.db.models.functions.right`, :class: "
"`~Django.db.Models.Functions.rpad`, :class: "
"`~django.db.db.Models.Functions.rTrim`, agus:aicme: "
"`~Django.db.Models.Functions.Trim`."

msgid ""
"The new :class:`~django.db.models.functions.TruncWeek` function "
"truncates :class:`~django.db.models.DateField` "
"and :class:`~django.db.models.DateTimeField` to the Monday of a week."
msgstr ""
"An feidhm nua:class: `~django.db.models.functions.truncWeek` truncats:class: "
"`~Django.db.Models.DateField` agus:class: `~Django.db.Models.DateTimeField` "
"go dtí an Luan seachtaine."

msgid "Query expressions can now be negated using a minus sign."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir nathanna ceisteanna a dhiúltú anois ag baint úsáide as comhartha "
"lúide."

msgid ""
":meth:`.QuerySet.order_by` and :meth:`distinct(*fields) "
"<.QuerySet.distinct>` now support using field transforms."
msgstr ""
":meth: `.queryset.order_by` agus:meth: `different (* fields) "
"<.querySet.Distinct> `tacaíonn anois le hathrú allamuigh a úsáid."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.db.models.BooleanField` can now be ``null=True``. This is "
"encouraged instead of ``NullBooleanField``, which will likely be deprecated "
"in the future."
msgstr ""
":class: Is féidir `~django.db.models.booleanfield` a bheith ``Null=True`` "
"anois. Spreagtar é seo in ionad ``Nullbooleanfield``, rud is dócha go "
"ndéanfar dlús amach anseo."

msgid ""
"The new :meth:`.QuerySet.explain` method displays the database's execution "
"plan of a queryset's query."
msgstr ""
"Taispeánann an modh nua:meth: `.querySet.explain` plean forghníomhaithe an "
"bhunachar sonraí ar cheist tacar fiosrúcháin."

msgid ":meth:`.QuerySet.raw` now supports :meth:`~.QuerySet.prefetch_related`."
msgstr ""
": meth: `.queryset.raw` tacaíonn anois:meth: `~.queryset.prefetch_related`."

msgid "Added :meth:`.HttpRequest.get_full_path_info`."
msgstr "Cuireadh leis: Meth: `.httpRequest.get_full_path_info`."

msgid ""
"Added the ``samesite`` argument to :meth:`.HttpResponse.set_cookie` to allow "
"setting the ``SameSite`` cookie flag."
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an argóint ``samesite`` leis: meth: `.httpResponse.set_cookie` chun "
"an bratach fianán ``SameSite`` a shocrú."

msgid ""
"The new ``as_attachment`` argument for :class:`~django.http.FileResponse` "
"sets the ``Content-Disposition`` header to make the browser ask if the user "
"wants to download the file. ``FileResponse`` also tries to set the ``Content-"
"Type`` and ``Content-Length`` headers where appropriate."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn an argóint nua ``as_attachment`` do:class: "
"`~django.http.fileResponse` an ceannteideal ``Content-Disposition`` chun an "
"brabhsálaí a iarraidh an bhfuil an t-úsáideoir ag iarraidh an comhad a "
"íoslódáil. Déanann ``FileResponse`` iarracht na ceannteidil ``Content-Type`` "
"agus ``Content-Length`` a shocrú nuair is cuí."

msgid ""
"The new :tfilter:`json_script` filter safely outputs a Python object as "
"JSON, wrapped in a ``<script>`` tag, ready for use with JavaScript."
msgstr ""
"<script>Aisíonn an scagaire nua:tfilter: `json_script` réad Python go "
"sábháilte mar JSON, fillte i gclib ````, réidh le húsáid le JavaScript."

msgid ""
"Added test :class:`~django.test.Client` support for 307 and 308 redirects."
msgstr ""
"Breise tástáil: class: `~django.test.client` tacaíocht do 307 agus 308 "
"atreoraithe."

msgid ""
"The test :class:`~django.test.Client` now serializes a request data "
"dictionary as JSON if ``content_type='application/json'``. You can customize "
"the JSON encoder with test client's ``json_encoder`` parameter."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an tástála:class: `~django.test.client` sraitheach foclóir sonraí "
"iarratais mar JSON má tá ``content_type = 'application/json'``. Is féidir "
"leat an t-ionchódóir JSON a shaincheapadh le paraiméadar ``json_encoder ``an "
"chliaint tástála."

msgid ""
"The new :meth:`.SimpleTestCase.assertWarnsMessage` method is a simpler "
"version of :meth:`~unittest.TestCase.assertWarnsRegex`."
msgstr ""
"Is leagan níos simplí de:meth: `~UnitTest.TestCase.AssertWarnsMessage` an "
"modh nua:meth: `~UnitTest.TestCase.AssertWarnsRegex`."

msgid "Backwards incompatible changes in 2.1"
msgstr "Athruithe neamh-chomhoiriúnacha ar ais i 2.1"

msgid ""
"To adhere to :pep:`249`, exceptions where a database doesn't support a "
"feature are changed from :exc:`NotImplementedError` "
"to :exc:`django.db.NotSupportedError`."
msgstr ""
"Chun cloí le:pep: `249`, athraítear eisceachtaí nuair nach dtacaíonn "
"bunachar sonraí le gné ó:exc: `NotImplementederror` to:exc: "
"`django.db.notSupportedError`."

msgid ""
"Renamed the ``allow_sliced_subqueries`` database feature flag to "
"``allow_sliced_subqueries_with_in``."
msgstr ""
"Athainmníodh an bratach gné bunachar sonraí `allow_sliced_subqueries`` go "
"`allow_sliced_subqueries_with_in``."

msgid ""
"``DatabaseOperations.distinct_sql()`` now requires an additional ``params`` "
"argument and returns a tuple of SQL and parameters instead of an SQL string."
msgstr ""
"``DatabaseOperations.Distinct_SQL ()`` teastaíonn argóint `params`` breise "
"anois agus tugann sé tuple SQL agus paraiméadair in ionad teaghrán SQL."

msgid ""
"``DatabaseFeatures.introspected_boolean_field_type`` is changed from a "
"method to a property."
msgstr ""
"Athraítear ``databaseFeatures.introspected_boolean_field_type`` ó mhodh go "
"maoin."

msgid "Support for SpatiaLite 4.0 is removed."
msgstr "Baintear tacaíocht do SpatiaLite 4.0."

msgid "Dropped support for MySQL 5.5"
msgstr "Tacaíocht titim do MySQL 5.5"

msgid ""
"The end of upstream support for MySQL 5.5 is December 2018. Django 2.1 "
"supports MySQL 5.6 and higher."
msgstr ""
"Is é deireadh na tacaíochta suas srutha do MySQL 5.5 ná Nollaig 2018. "
"Tacaíonn Django 2.1 le MySQL 5.6 agus níos airde."

msgid "Dropped support for PostgreSQL 9.3"
msgstr "Tacaíocht titim do PostgreSQL 9.3"

msgid ""
"The end of upstream support for PostgreSQL 9.3 is September 2018. Django 2.1 "
"supports PostgreSQL 9.4 and higher."
msgstr ""
"Is é Meán Fómhair 2018 deireadh na tacaíochta suas srutha do PostgreSQL 9.3. "
"Tacaíonn Django 2.1 le PostgreSQL 9.4 agus níos airde."

msgid ""
"Removed ``BCryptPasswordHasher`` from the default ``PASSWORD_HASHERS`` "
"setting"
msgstr ""
"Bainte ``BCryptPasswordHasher`` ón socrú réamhshocraithe ``PASSWORD_HASHERS``"

msgid ""
"If you used bcrypt with Django 1.4 or 1.5 (before "
"``BCryptSHA256PasswordHasher`` was added in Django 1.6), you might have some "
"passwords that use the ``BCryptPasswordHasher`` hasher."
msgstr ""
"Má d'úsáid tú bcrypt le Django 1.4 nó 1.5 (sular cuireadh "
"``BCryptsha256PasswordHasher`` i Django 1.6), b'fhéidir go mbeadh roinnt "
"pasfhocail agat a úsáideann an ``BCryptPasswordHasher`` hasher."

msgid "You can check if that's the case like this::"
msgstr "Is féidir leat a sheiceáil an bhfuil sin an cás mar seo:"

msgid ""
"If you want to continue to allow those passwords to be used, you'll have to "
"define the :setting:`PASSWORD_HASHERS` setting (if you don't already) and "
"include ``'django.contrib.auth.hashers.BCryptPasswordHasher'``."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat leanúint ar aghaidh ag ceadú na pasfhocail sin a úsáid, beidh "
"ort an socrú:setting: `PASSWORD_HASHERS` a shainiú (mura bhfuil tú cheana "
"féin) agus ``django.contrib.auth.hashers.bcryptPasswordHasher'` a chur san "
"áireamh."

msgid "Moved ``wrap_label`` widget template context variable"
msgstr "Athróg comhthéacs teimpléad giuirléid ``wrap_label`` aistrithe"

msgid ""
"To fix the lack of ``<label>`` when using ``RadioSelect`` and "
"``CheckboxSelectMultiple`` with ``MultiWidget``, the ``wrap_label`` context "
"variable now appears as an attribute of each option. For example, in a "
"custom ``input_option.html`` template, change ``{% if wrap_label %}`` to "
"``{% if widget.wrap_label %}``."
msgstr ""
"Ch <label>un an easpa ```a shocrú nuair a úsáidtear ``RadioSelect`` agus "
"``CheckboxSelectMultiple`` le ``MultiWidget``, tá an t-athróg comhthéacs "
"``wrap_label`` le feiceáil anois mar thréith de gach rogha. Mar shampla, i "
"dteimpléad saincheaptha ``input_option.html``, athraigh ``{% if wrap_label%}"
"`` go ``{% if widget.wrap_label%}``."

msgid "``SameSite`` cookies"
msgstr "Fianáin ``Samesite``"

msgid ""
"The cookies used for ``django.contrib.sessions``, "
"``django.contrib.messages``, and Django's CSRF protection now set the "
"``SameSite`` flag to ``Lax`` by default. Browsers that respect this flag "
"won't send these cookies on cross-origin requests. If you rely on the old "
"behavior, set the :setting:`SESSION_COOKIE_SAMESITE` and/"
"or :setting:`CSRF_COOKIE_SAMESITE` setting to ``None``."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn na fianáin a úsáidtear le haghaidh ``django.contrib.sessions``, "
"`django.contrib.messages``, agus cosaint CSRF Django anois an bhratach "
"``SameSite`` go `Lax`` de réir réamhshocraithe. Ní sheolfaidh brabhsálaithe "
"a bhfuil meas acu leis an bhratach seo ar na fianáin seo ar iarratais "
"trasbhunús Má tá tú ag brath ar an sean-iompar, socraigh an socrú:setting: "
"`SESSION_COOKIE_SAMESITE` agus/nó :setting: `CSRF_COOKIE_SAMESITE` go "
"``None``."

msgid "Considerations for the new model \"view\" permission"
msgstr "Breithnithe maidir leis an gcead “féach” samhail nua"

msgid "Custom admin forms need to take the view-only case into account"
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh foirmeacha riaracháin saincheaptha an cás amharc amháin a chur san "
"áireamh"

msgid ""
"With the new \"view\" permission, existing custom admin forms may raise "
"errors when a user doesn't have the change permission because the form might "
"access nonexistent fields. Fix this by "
"overriding :meth:`.ModelAdmin.get_form` and checking if the user has the "
"\"change\" permissions and returning the default form if not::"
msgstr ""
"Leis an gcead nua “amharc”, d'fhéadfadh foirmeacha riaracháin saincheaptha "
"atá ann cheana earráidí a ardú nuair nach bhfuil an cead athraithe ag "
"úsáideoir mar d'fhéadfadh an fhoirm rochtain a fháil ar réimsí nach bhfuil "
"Déan é seo a shocrú trí:meth: `.modeladmin.get_form` agus seiceáil an bhfuil "
"na ceadanna “athraithe” ag an úsáideoir agus an fhoirm réamhshocraithe a "
"thabhairt ar ais mura bhfuil:"

msgid "New default view permission could allow unwanted access to admin views"
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh cead amharc réamhshocraithe nua rochtain nach dteastaíonn a che"

msgid ""
"If you have a custom permission with a codename of the form "
"``view_<modelname>``, the new view permission handling in the admin will "
"allow view access to the changelist and detail pages for those models. If "
"this is unwanted, you must change your custom permission codename."
msgstr ""
"Má tá cead saincheaptha agat le ainm cóid den fhoirm ``view_ <modelname>``, "
"ligfidh an láimhseáil cead amharc nua sa riarachán rochtain amharc ar an "
"liosta athraithe agus ar leathanaigh mionsonraithe do na samhlacha sin. Mura "
"dteastaíonn sé seo, ní mór duit d'ainm cóid cead saincheaptha a athrú."

msgid ""
"The minimum supported version of ``mysqlclient`` is increased from 1.3.3 to "
"1.3.7."
msgstr ""
"Méadaítear an leagan íosta tacaithe de `mysqlclient`` ó 1.3.3 go 1.3.7."

msgid "Support for SQLite < 3.7.15 is removed."
msgstr "Baintear tacaíocht do SQLite <3.7.15."

msgid ""
"The date format of ``Set-Cookie``'s ``Expires`` directive is changed to "
"follow :rfc:`7231#section-7.1.1.1` instead of Netscape's cookie standard. "
"Hyphens present in dates like ``Tue, 25-Dec-2018 22:26:13 GMT`` are removed. "
"This change should be merely cosmetic except perhaps for antiquated browsers "
"that don't parse the new format."
msgstr ""
"Athraítear formáid dáta treoir ```Expires`` `Set-Cookie`` go dtí seo a "
"leanas: rfc: `7231 #section -7.1.1.1` in ionad caighdeán fianán Netscape. "
"Baintear na hiphens atá i láthair i ddátaí mar ``Máirt, 25-Nollaig 2018 "
"22:26:13 GMT``. Níor chóir go mbeadh an t-athrú seo ach cosmaideach ach "
"amháin b'fhéidir do bhrabhsálaithe seanmhara nach ndéanann an formáid nua a "
"pháirseáil."

msgid ""
"``allowed_hosts`` is now a required argument of private API "
"``django.utils.http.is_safe_url()``."
msgstr ""
"Is argóint riachtanach é `allowed_hosts`` anois de API príobháideach "
"``django.utils.http.is_safe_url () ``."

msgid ""
"The ``multiple`` attribute rendered by "
"the :class:`~django.forms.SelectMultiple` widget now uses HTML5 boolean "
"syntax rather than XHTML's ``multiple=\"multiple\"``."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann an tréith ``multiple`` a rinneadh ag an n:class: "
"`~django.forms.SelectMultiple` giuirléid anois comhréir boolean HTML5 "
"seachas ``multiple=\"multiple\"`` XHTML."

msgid ""
"HTML rendered by form widgets no longer includes a closing slash on void "
"elements, e.g. ``<br>``. This is incompatible within XHTML, although some "
"widgets already used aspects of HTML5 such as boolean attributes."
msgstr ""
"<br>Ní chuimsíonn HTML a rindreáiltear ag giuirléidí foirme scall deiridh ar "
"eilimintí neamhní a thuilleadh, m.sh. ``` Níl sé seo comhoiriúnach laistigh "
"de XHTML, cé gur úsáid roinnt giuirléidí gnéithe de HTML5 cheana féin mar "
"thréithe boolean."

msgid ""
"The value of :class:`~django.forms.SelectDateWidget`'s empty options is "
"changed from 0 to an empty string, which mainly may require some adjustments "
"in tests that compare HTML."
msgstr ""
"Athraítear luach roghanna folmha: Class: `~django.forms.SelectDateWidget` ó "
"0 go sreang folamh, a d'fhéadfadh roinnt coigeartúcháin a bheith ag teastáil "
"go príomha i dtástálacha a dhéanann comparáid idir HTML."

msgid ""
":meth:`.User.has_usable_password` and "
"the :func:`~django.contrib.auth.hashers.is_password_usable` function no "
"longer return ``False`` if the password is ``None`` or an empty string, or "
"if the password uses a hasher that's not in the :setting:`PASSWORD_HASHERS` "
"setting. This undocumented behavior was a regression in Django 1.6 and "
"prevented users with such passwords from requesting a password reset. Audit "
"your code to confirm that your usage of these APIs don't rely on the old "
"behavior."
msgstr ""
":meth: `.user.has_usable_password` agus an:func: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.hashers.is_password_usable` ní fhilleann feidhm "
"``False`` a thuilleadh má tá an pasfhocal ``None`` nó teaghrán folamh, nó má "
"úsáideann an pasfhocal hasher nach bhfuil sa socrú: `PASSWORD_HASHERS`. Ba "
"aischéimniú é an t-iompar neamhdhoiciméadaithe seo i Django 1.6 agus chuir "
"cosc ar úsáideoirí a raibh pasfhocail den sórt sin acu athshocrú pas Déan "
"iniúchadh ar do chód chun a dhearbhú nach bhfuil do úsáid na n-APIs seo ag "
"brath ar an sean-iompar."

msgid ""
"Since migrations are now loaded from ``.pyc`` files, you might need to "
"delete them if you're working in a mixed Python 2 and Python 3 environment."
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é go bhfuil imirce luchtaithe anois ó chomhaid `.pyc``, b'fhéidir go "
"mbeidh ort iad a scriosadh má tá tú ag obair i dtimpeallacht measctha Python "
"2 agus Python 3."

msgid ""
"Using ``None`` as a ``django.contrib.postgres.fields.JSONField`` lookup "
"value now matches objects that have the specified key and a null value "
"rather than objects that don't have the key."
msgstr ""
"Meaitseálann luach cuardaigh ```None`` mar luach cuardaigh "
"``Django.contrib.postgres.fields.jsonField`` anois rudaí a bhfuil an eochair "
"sonraithe acu agus luach null seachas rudaí nach bhfuil an eochair acu."

msgid ""
"The admin CSS class ``field-box`` is renamed to ``fieldBox`` to prevent "
"conflicts with the class given to model fields named \"box\"."
msgstr ""
"Athainmnítear an rang CSS riaracháin ``field-box`` go `fieldbox`` chun "
"coimhlintí leis an rang a thugtar do réimsí samhail darb ainm “bosca” a "
"chosc."

msgid ""
"Since the admin's ``actions.html``, ``change_list_results.html``, "
"``date_hierarchy.html``, ``pagination.html``, "
"``prepopulated_fields_js.html``, ``search_form.html``, and "
"``submit_line.html`` templates can now be overridden per app or per model, "
"you may need to rename existing templates with those names that were written "
"for a different purpose."
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é go bhfuil ``gníomhaíochtaí.html``, ``change_list_results.html``, "
"``date_hierarchy.html``, ``page.html``, ``prepopulated_fields_js.html``, "
"``search_form.html``, `` search_form.html`` , agus is féidir teimpléid "
"``submit_line.html`` a shárú anois in aghaidh na haipe nó in aghaidh na "
"samhla, seans go mbeidh ort teimpléid reatha a athainmniú leis na "
"hainmneacha sin a bhí scríofa chun críche eile."

msgid ""
"``QuerySet.raw()`` now caches its results like regular querysets. Use "
"``iterator()`` if you don't want caching."
msgstr ""
"``QuerySet.raw () ``a thorthaí a choscann anois cosúil le ceisteanna rialta. "
"Úsáid ``iterator () ``mura dteastaíonn caching uait."

msgid ""
"The database router :meth:`allow_relation` method is called in more cases. "
"Improperly written routers may need to be updated accordingly."
msgstr ""
"Tugtar modh ar an ródaire bunachar sonraí: meth: `allow_relations `i "
"gcásanna níos mó. B'fhéidir go gcaithfear ródairí scríofa míchuí a nuashonrú "
"dá réir."

msgid ""
"Translations are no longer deactivated before running management commands. "
"If your custom command requires translations to be deactivated (for example, "
"to insert untranslated content into the database), use the "
"new :ref:`@no_translations decorator <management-commands-and-locales>`."
msgstr ""
"Ní dhíghníomhaítear aistriúcháin a thuilleadh sula ndéantar orduithe "
"<management-commands-and-locales>Má éilíonn d'ordú saincheaptha aistriúcháin "
"a dhíghníomhachtú (mar shampla, chun ábhar neamhaistrithe a chur isteach sa "
"bhunachar sonraí), bain úsáid as an nua:ref: `@no_translations decorator`."

msgid ""
"Management commands no longer allow the abbreviated forms of the ``--"
"settings`` and ``--pythonpath`` arguments."
msgstr ""
"Ní cheadaíonn orduithe bainistíochta foirmeacha giorraithe na n-argóintí ``--"
"socruithe ``agus ``--pythonpath`` a thuilleadh."

msgid ""
"The private ``django.db.models.sql.constants.QUERY_TERMS`` constant is "
"removed. The :meth:`~.RegisterLookupMixin.get_lookup` "
"and :meth:`~.RegisterLookupMixin.get_lookups` methods of the :ref:`Lookup "
"Registration API <lookup-registration-api>` may be suitable alternatives. "
"Compared to the ``QUERY_TERMS`` constant, they allow your code to also "
"account for any custom lookups that have been registered."
msgstr ""
"Baintear an tairiseach príobháideach "
"``Django.db.Models.sql.Constants.Query_Terms``. <lookup-registration-"
"api>B'fhéidir gur roghanna oiriúnacha iad na modhanna: Meth: "
"`~.registerlookupMixin.get_lookupMixin.get_lookupMixin.get_lookups.get_lookups` "
"agus:ref: `Lookup Clárúcháin API `. I gcomparáid leis an tairiseach "
"``QUERY_TERMS``, tugann siad deis do chód cuntas a thabhairt ar aon "
"chuardach saincheaptha atá cláraithe."

msgid ""
"Compatibility with ``py-bcrypt`` is removed as it's unmaintained. "
"Use :pypi:`bcrypt` instead."
msgstr ""
"Baintear comhoiriúnacht le `py-bcrypt`` toisc nach bhfuil sé cothabháilte. "
"Úsáid: pypi: `bcrypt` ina ionad."

msgid "Features deprecated in 2.1"
msgstr "Gnéithe atá díscríofa i 2.1"

msgid ""
"The ``ForceRHR`` GIS function is deprecated in favor of the "
"new :class:`~django.contrib.gis.db.models.functions.ForcePolygonCW` function."
msgstr ""
"Tá an fheidhm GIS ``ForcerHR`` díluaite i bhfabhar an fheidhm nua:class: "
"`~django.contrib.gis.db.models.functions.forcePolygOncw`."

msgid ""
"``django.utils.http.cookie_date()`` is deprecated in favor "
"of :func:`~django.utils.http.http_date`, which follows the format of the "
"latest RFC."
msgstr ""
"Tá ``django.utils.http.cookie_date () `díscoilte i bhfabhr:func: "
"`~django.utils.http.http_date`, a leanann formáid an RFC is déanaí."

msgid ""
"``{% load staticfiles %}`` and ``{% load admin_static %}`` are deprecated in "
"favor of ``{% load static %}``, which works the same."
msgstr ""
"Tá ``{% load staticfiles%}`` agus ``{% load admin_static%}`` a dhíchur i "
"bhfabhar ``{% load static%}``, a oibríonn mar an gcéanna."

msgid ""
"``django.contrib.staticfiles.templatetags.static()`` is deprecated in favor "
"of ``django.templatetags.static.static()``."
msgstr ""
"Tá ``django.contrib.staticfiles.templatetags.static () ``díluachtaithe i "
"bhfabhar ``django.templatetags.static.static ()``."

msgid ""
"Support for :meth:`.InlineModelAdmin.has_add_permission` methods that don't "
